1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Margaret Douglas:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2349.htm#i23484
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Douglas [1]
2 CONT *F, #23484
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Aug 2012
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.0%
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Douglas was the daughter of Sir James Douglas, 7th of Drumlanrig and Christian Montgomerie.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Edward Crichton, 7th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar, son of William Crichton, 5th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar and Elizabeth Fleming, circa 4 June 1561.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, William Graham, 5th Earl of Menteith, son of John Graham, 4th Earl of Menteith and Marion Seton, circa 16 May 1571.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, thirdly, Robert Wauchope on 22 May 1593.
2 CONT
2 CONT From circa 4 June 1561, her married name became Crichton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As a result of her marriage, Margaret Douglas was styled as Countess of Menteith circa 16 May 1571. From 16 May 1571, her married name became Graham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Wauchope.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Margaret Douglas and Edward Crichton, 7th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar
2 CONT *1. Robert Crichton, 8th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar+[2] b. c 1568, d. 29 Jun 1612
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Margaret Douglas and William Graham, 5th Earl of Menteith
2 CONT *1. John Graham, 6th Earl of Menteith+[1] b. c 1574, d. Dec 1598
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2752. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 601.
