1 OCCU Sir, Knighted by Kings James VI in 1608, See McGregor pedigree
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} More About William Grierson and Nichola Maxwell: Marriage: 09 May 1593, Dumfrieshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of William Grierson and Nichola Maxwell is: 
2 CONT  	528	i.	 	Sir James Greer, born Abt. 1600 in Capenoch, Dumfrieshire, Scotland; died 1666 in Dumfrieshire, Scotland; married Mary Brown Abt. 1626.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir William Grierson of Lag was Knighted by James VI in 1608." (Information from the 1962 Yearbook of the American Clan Gregor Society, Inc, (page 24, # 1364, Robert Alan Temple), Washington, D.C. and other notes and charts from 
2 CONC Lois Temple, Dublin, Virginia.)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir William Grierson was the 9th Lord of Lag. In 1608, he was Knighted by the King, although [Lag Charter #159] refers to him as "Sir" on 23 March 1605. He also got sasine of Larglanley [11 May 1597], Windiehill [16 May 1609], an
2 CONC d Capenoch [26 Jun 1616]. He was the only son." (William Greer.)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir William Grierson was a Knight of Lag Castle, Dumfries. He was appointed keeper of certain rolls was shot and killed in 1629. From this time on the family called themselves Grier or Greer instead of Grierson. Sir William had t
2 CONC wo sons and was knighted by James VI." (The Historical Families of Dumfriesshire and the Border Wars by C.L. Johnstone. Appointed as Commissioner to Parliament representing Dumfriesshire 1617-1625; 1709-1711.)
2 CONT
2 CONT (NOTE FROM RALPH TERRY: William is shown by one source to have been born about 1550, but as his parents did not marry until 1566, and his sister, Grisel was not born until 1585, and her wife was not born until 1578, it is more pro
2 CONC bable that William Grierson was born about 1767 to 1675.)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth:  1550 Dumfries Dumfries and Galloway, Scotland  Death:  Jan. 21, 1629 Dumfries Dumfries and Galloway, Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Grierson, 9th Lord of Lag. Born: 1550/1567-1575 in Rock, Capenoch, Dumfriesshire, Scotland. Died: 21 Jan 1629 at Lag, Dumfriesshire, Lord of Lag, Scotland. He was shot and killed. From this time on the family called th
2 CONC emselves Grier or Greer instead of Grierson. He was invested as a Knight by James VI in 1608. He fought in the Battle of Dryfe Sands in 1593, escaped only by the fleetness of his horse. Sir William was Commissioner to Parliament f
2 CONC or Dumfriesshire 1617, 1621 and 1625, Sheriff of Dumfies 1615, 1617, and 1621 plus one of the Commissioners for the Borders in 1623. He built or rebuilt the house of Rockhall, giving it in liferent to his wife Nicolas, daughter of
2 CONC  John Maxwell and his wife Agnes, whom he married in 1593.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Roger Grierson. Mother: Helen Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Nichola Maxwell. Married: 09 May 1593 at Dumfriesshire, Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Roger Grierson (1529 - 1593)
2 CONT   Helen Douglas Grierson (1530 - 1578)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Nichola Maxwell Grierson (1578 - 1605)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   James Greer (1604 - 1666)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Old Dunscore Cemetery  Dunscore Dumfries and Galloway, Scotland Plot: Buried 17 Feb 1629 
2 CONT
