1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Robert Crichton:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2399.htm#i23984
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Crichton, 8th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar [1]
2 CONT *M, #23984, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1568, 
2 CONT *d. 29 June 1612
2 CONT *Last Edited=8 Feb 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.03%
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Crichton, 8th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar was born circa 1568.[1] He was the son of Edward Crichton, 7th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar and Margaret Douglas.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Anne Fermor, daughter of Sir George Fermor and Mary Curson, on 16 April 1608.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 29 June 1612 at Great Palace Yard, Westminster Hall, Westminster, London, England, hanged for his part in the assassination of John Turner, without legitimate issue.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career:
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 8th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar [S., 1488] on 23 May 1569.[1] 
2 CONT *Circa 1605 at Rycote, Oxfordshire, England, he lost an eye in a bout with a fencing master, John Turner, at Lord Norris’s house.[1] As revenge he plotted Turner’s murder for seven years, and on 11 May 1612 he had one Carlyle, kil
2 CONC l Turner by a pistol-shot.[1] 
2 CONT *Carlyle and several other accomplices were hanged by a hemp rope but Robert was granted a peer’s privilege of being hanged by a silk one, despite having as a Scottish peer been turned down for trial in the High Steward’s Court (i
2 CONC nstead being tried in the King's Court Bench as plain Robert Crichton).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Robert Crichton, 8th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar and Anne Fermor
2 CONT *1. William Crichton of Sanquhar [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 601. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
