1 NAME Benjamin /Jacob/
2 GIVN Benjamin
2 _MARNM Jacob
2 NICK Ben
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Shaarey Zedek Cemetery, Margaret Park Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 26 DEC 1891
2 PLAC Poland; Russia
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 OCT 1975
2 PLAC Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Memorable Manitobans: Benjamin “Ben” Jacob (1891-1975)
2 CONT Businessman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Russia in 1891, he came to Canada in 1910 and, three years later, he partnered with John Henry Crowley in establishing the garment manufacturing firm of Jacob-Crowley Manufacturing Company in Winnipeg. He played a key role
2 CONC  in introducing unionism in the city’s needle trade. During the Second World War, he was Chairman of the War Time Prices and Trade Commission for the garment industry in western Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13 May 1913, he married Dora Brown (c1895-1974) at Winnipeg and they had four children: Wilhelmina Berta “Minnie” Jacob (1914-1964, wife of Edward Wesley Newton Hesp), Helen Jacob (1915-1991, wife of Alan Abraham Klass), Isaac 
2 CONC Nathan Jacob (1917-1967), and Ted Jacob (1927-2003). He was a founding member of the Jewish Welfare Fund and an original member of the building committees of the YMHA and Shaarey Zedek Synagogue. He was the founding President of t
2 CONC he Glendale Golf and Country Club (1947).
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Winnipeg on 28 October 1975 and was buried in the Shaarey Zedek Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT Historic Sites of Manitoba: Keewayden Building / Crowley Building (138 Portage Avenue East, Winnipeg)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Marriage registration [Ben Jacob, Dora Brown], Manitoba Vital Statistics.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth registrations [Berta Jacob, Helen Jacob, Isaac Nathan Jacob], Manitoba Vital Statistics.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1921 Canada census, Ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage registration [Wilhelmina Berta Jacob, Edward Wesley Newton Hesp], Manitoba Vital Statistics.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary [Dora Jacob], Winnipeg Free Press, 11 March 1974, page 16.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary, Winnipeg Free Press, 29 October 1975, page 54.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary [Helen Jacob Klass], Winnipeg Free Press, 26 March 1991, page 46.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary [Ted Jacob], Winnipeg Free Press, 15 November 2003.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituaries and burial transcriptions, Manitoba Genealogical Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT This page was prepared by Gordon Goldsborough.
2 CONT
