1 TITL Lady Of Eglinton "Montgomerie'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Since created on 15 July 2012, this profile has not been sourced. Any scholarly sources one can provide would be much appreciated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikisource: ''Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900'', Vol. 38; [https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Dictionary_of_National_Biography,_1885-1900/Montgomerie,_Hugh_(1460%3F-1545) "Montgomerie, Hugh (1460?-1545)"], by Thomas Finlay
2 CONC son Henderson
2 CONT
2 CONT MONTGOMERIE, HUGH, third Lord Montgomerie and first Earl of Eglinton (1460?–1545), eldest son of Alexander, second lord Montgomerie, by his wife Catherine, daughter of Gilbert, lord Kennedy, was born about 1460....
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Helen, third daughter of Colin, first earl of Argyll, he had six sons and eight daughters: Alexander, master of Montgomerie, who died young; John, lord Montgomerie, killed in the skirmish in the High Street of Edinburg
2 CONC h called 'Cleanse the Causeway,' 2 May 1520, and father of Hugh, second earl; Sir Neil of Langshaw; William of Greenfield; Hugh, killed at the battle of Pinkie in 1547; Robert, first rector of Kirkmichael, and afterwards bishop of
2 CONC  Argyll; Margaret, married to William, second lord Semple; Marjory, to William, second lord Somerville; Maud, to Colin Campbell of Ardkinglass; Isobel, to John Mure of Caldwell; '''Elizabeth, to John Blair of that ilk'''; Agnes, t
2 CONC o John Ker of Kersland; Janet, to Campbell of Cessnock; and Catherine, to George Montgomerie of Skelmorlie.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Reg. Mag. Sig. Scot.; Exchequer Rolls of Scotl.; Pitscottie's Chron.; Balfour's Annals; Sir William Fraser's Earls of Eglinton; Paterson's Hist. of Ayr; Douglas's Scottish Peerage (Wood), i. 496-8.]
