2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Montgomerie [1]
2 CONT *F, #172441, 
2 CONT *d. from 31 July 1518 to 12 February 1522/23
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=1.0%
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Montgomerie married, secondly, John Campbell.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, William Sempill, 2nd Lord Sempill, son of John Sempill, 1st Lord Sempill and Margaret Colville, before 20 July 1517.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died from 31 July 1518 to 12 February 1522/23.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Montgomery-896
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Hugh Montgomerie, 1st Earl of Eglinton and Lady Helen Campbell.[1] 
2 CONT *Her married name became Campbell.[2] 
2 CONT *She was also known as Mariot.[2] 
2 CONT *From before 20 July 1517, her married name became Sempill.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Montgomerie and William Sempill, 2nd Lord Sempill
2 CONT *1. Helen Sempill+3 d. a 1547
2 CONT *2. Robert Sempill, 3rd Lord Sempill+1 b. c 1505, d. fr 1 Aug 1573 - 17 Jan 1575/76
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XI, page 622. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1279. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 104.
