2 CONT '''11 December 1548: Precept under the Privy Seal of remission to Robert, Master of Boyd, John Brisbane of Bishopland, David Fairlie younger of that ilk, Charles Mowat of Busby, Robert Boyd, junior, of Portincross, Robert Boyd in 
2 CONC Clerkland, Archibald Boyle and William Blair for absence from the army upon Gledsmuir, 20 Aug last for resistance to our old enemies of England and for art and part in the civil murder of the late Neil Montgomery of Lainshaw. Date
2 CONC d at Edinburgh, 11 Dec 1548. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f140&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=neil+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Paper
2 CONC s, reference GD8/140]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''January 1549: Extract from the Book of the Consistorial Court of Glasgow of disposition by William Muir of Glanderstone, brother german to John Muir of Caldwell, in favour of Patrick Montgomery and Agnes Mure, his spouse and th
2 CONC e longest liver of them two and the heirs gotten of their own bodies whatsoever of the twa part of the property of the lands and lordship of Giffyn with all profits belonging to him as assignee of unquhile John Montgomery, son and
2 CONC  heir of unquhile Sir Neil Montgomery of Langschaw, knight who had the gift thereof from the Queen and the Lord Governor for the space of 5 years after the 9th day of November then last past; which was the entry of the said Patric
2 CONC k and Agnes his spouse, to the said lands and profits of the same; reserving to Margaret Frissell, Lady of Giffen her reasonable terce and conjunct fee of the said lands Dated at Glasgow and registered 27 March 1549 [http://catalo
2 CONC gue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f30%2f20&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=neil+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls o
2 CONC f Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/30/20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 February 1560: Contract between Robert, Lord Boyd, for himself and taking burden on him for John Brisbane of Bishopton, Charles Mowat of Busby, David Fernielaw younger of that ilk, Robert Boyd in Clerkland, Archibald Boyle, 
2 CONC son of the late John Boyle of Kilburne, and William Blair in Henryscroft, on the one part, and Neil Montgomery, son and heir to the late Sir Neil Montgomery of Lainshaw, for himself, and taking burden on him for Dame Margaret Muir
2 CONC , his mother, Christine, Elizabeth and Helen Montgomery, his sisters german, and Thomas Montgomery, James and John, sons natural to the said Sir Neil, on the other part, for slaughter of Sir Neil Montgomery. Dated at Glasgow, 10 F
2 CONC eb 1560. (Boyd Papers). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=neil+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Bu
2 CONC rgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/167]'''
