2 CONT •Note: III. Sir Neil Montgomerie of Lainshaw, was the ancestor of the present lineal male representative of Montgomery ; the Lainshaw branch being heirs male to the representation of the family, and also to its estates and titles,
2 CONC  on the death of the fifth earl, but which latter were settled by that earl, under a new charter procured by him for that purpose, on the children of his aunt, Lady Margaret Montgomerie, Countess of Winton. The descent of this lin
2 CONC e will be found in full succeeding the account of the last named earl, (p. 62.) Genealogical History and Pedigree of The Family of Montgomery A Genealogical History of the Family of Montgomery, including The Montgomery Pedigree. c
2 CONC ompiled by Thomas Harrison Montgomery It was in truth a noble saying of the late Lord Clarendon, "that birth conveyed no merit, but much duty, to its inheritor." Lord Lindsay. Philadelphia: Printed for Private Circulation. 1863. H
