2 CONT '''Master William Montgomery of Stane, formerly Mr. William Montgomery of Greenfield, here treated is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/William-Montgomery-of-Giffen/6000000078847156002
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Master William Montgomery of Stane, formerly Mr. William Montgomery of Grenefield, is the seconf son of Hugh Montgomery, first Earl of Eglinton and his wife Lady Helen Campbell. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefou02pau
2 CONC lgoog/page/n452 The Scots Peerage III: p. 436] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mr. William Montgomery of Grenefield, who in terms of a contract dated 20 January 1507-08, married Elizabeth Francis, elder daughter of Robert Francis, Laird of Stane, and they had a charter for  the lands of Stane on 22 Januar
2 CONC y 1508-09. In 1522 William Montgomery was infeft by his father in the lands of Dreghorn. They had issue Arthur, who succeeded, and Hugh, who as Hugh Montgomery of Auchinhude, styles himself as son of Elizabeth Francis, Lady of Sta
2 CONC ne, who was then still alive on 21 March 1554-55. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog/page/n452 The Scots Peerage III: p. 436]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Master William Montgomery of Greenfield married Elizabeth Francis, the eldest daughter of Robert Francis of Stane: "Rob. Francys domini de Stane . . . . . filie sue naturali uxorique dicti Wil". [https://archive.org/stream/regi
2 CONC strummagnisi02scot#page/723/mode/1up RMS: 3381]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 January 1508: Charter by which Robert Francis of Stane confirms that he has given his lands of Stane, Sanctbridiskirk, and Bourtrehill, to his bastard daughter Elizabeth and her husband, Master William Montgomery of Greenfie
2 CONC ld. The charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 31 October 1509. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/723/mode/1up Registrum Magnii Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Sco
2 CONC tland, A. D. 1424-1513, charter number 3381 on p. 723]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 June 1526: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/115 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 513 on p. 115]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 June 1540: Charter by which James V King of Scots confirms that he has granted the ten pound lands of old extent of Stane in the bailliery of Cunningham to Arthur Montgomery, son and apparent heir of William Montgomery of Sta
2 CONC ne, and his wife Margaret Fairlie. The land of Stane had previously been resigned by William Montgomery of Stane, with the consent of his wife Elizabeth Francis. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/486 Registr
2 CONC um Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 2154 on p. 486]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog/page/n7 The Scots Peerage etc.By James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume III (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1906), 617 pp. For Montgomery Earl of Eglinton see pp. 420
2 CONC -65]
