1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JONET MONTGOMERY (otherwise JANET MONTGOMERY) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Jonet Montgomery, here treated, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Jonete-Montgomery/6000000221883488971 '''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jonet Montgomery, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Hugh-Montgomery-1st-Earl-of-Eglinton/6000000055745069238?through=6000000055745366955 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Helen-Campbell/6000000
2 CONC 183399368896?through=6000000055745366955 The Scots Peerage does not identify a date and place of birth or death for her. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/440/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 440]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jonet Montgomery, here treated, married George Campbell of Cessnock, who was killed at Flodden. On 7 November 1513 Hew, Earl of Eglintoun, was surety for his daughter Jonet: "that the goods and gear of her husband should be for
2 CONC thcoming to her son and other heirs". [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/440/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 440]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 October 1515: Charter of confirmation granted by James V under his Great Seal with advice, consent and assent of his dearest cousin and tutor, John, Duke of Albany Protector and Governor of his kingdom of the gifts made by H
2 CONC ugh, Earl of Eglinton, Lord Montgomery to his daughters of the wards and marriages following viz to Isabella Montgomery, his daughter of the ward and marriage of Robert Montgomery, son and heir of deceased Patrick Montgomery of Gi
2 CONC ffyn, and failing of the said Robert by his death unmarried of the marriage of any other heir or heirs of the said deceased Patrick who should happen to succeed to him in his heritage hold of the Earl; to Katherine Montgomery, his
2 CONC  daughter of the ward and marriage of George Montgomery, son and heir of deceased Cuthbert Montgomery of Skelmorlie, and the ward and marriage of Alexander Fergushill, son and heir of deceased Thomas Fergushill and Robert Fergushi
2 CONC ll of that ilk; to Janet Montgomery, his lawful daughter of the ward and marriage of John Ker, son and heir of deceased Robert Ker of Kerisland; and to Jonet Montgomery, his bastard daughter natural of the ward and marriage of the
2 CONC  heirs of Kellie. Dated at Edinburgh. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f30%2f18&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of S
2 CONC cotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/30/18]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This charter was printed in [https://archive.org/details/memorialsofmontg02fras/page/82/mode/1up Memorials of the Montgomeries. Vol. II, pp. 82-4] and in [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/404/mod
2 CONC e/1up Register of the Privy Council 1488-1529: entry number 2649]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/n9/mode/1up Registrum Secreti Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Privy Seal of Scotland. Vol I. A.D. 1488-1529. Edited by M. Livingstone, LSO. (HMSO, Edinburg
2 CONC h, 1908), 824 pp. including indices]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/memorialsofmonv100fras/page/n8/mode/1up Memorials of the Montgomeries Earls of Eglinton. Vol. I. By William Fraser (Edinburgh, MDCCCLIX), 400 pp.]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/memorialsofmontg02fras/page/n6/mode/1up Memorials of the Montgomeries Earls of Eglinton. Vol, II. By William Fraser (Edinburgh, MDCCCLIX), 424 pp. including indices]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogi
2 CONC cal account of the nobility of that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume III. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1906), 618 pp.]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research Notes and Commentary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT There seems to be confusion around Janets birthdate ,I have seen  1466 1488 1503
2 CONT
2 CONT ( I doubt whether even the prodigious Hugh Montgomerie born 1460 could have fathered her at 6 years of age !! - it remains a mystery !!)
2 CONT
2 CONT Also confusion about Spouse - also reported that she Married George Campbell of Loudon .
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents are generally agreed as : Daughter of Hugh Montgomerie of Hazelhead - 1st of Eglington  and  Helen Campbell b. 1465 ( daughter of Colin Campbell 1st of Argyll b. 1433  and Lady Isabel Stewart of Lorn )
2 CONT
2 CONT Married George Campbell of Cessnock 
2 CONT
