1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR WILLIAM EDMONSTONE OF DUNTREATH===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath is the eldest son of Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath and his wife Janet Schaw. He succeeded his father in 1502. [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/34/mode/1up Dun
2 CONC treath: 34]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath is reported to have been killed in action at the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513. [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/36/mode/1up Duntreath: 36] The fact that he d
2 CONC id is confirmed by three entries in the Exchequer Rolls of Scotland, which show that his son William benefited from the act of Parliament in favour of the heirs of those killed. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof14scot/
2 CONC page/579/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland 1513-22. Volume XIV, page 579] [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof14scot/page/580/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland 1513-22. Volume XIV, page 579] [https://archive.org/det
2 CONC ails/exchequerrollsof14scot/page/587/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland 1513-22. Volume XIV, page 587]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath married Sibylla Baillie daughter of William Baillie of Lamington and his wife Elizabeth Leslie. [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/35/mode/1up?view=theater Duntreath: 
2 CONC 35-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath married Dame Elizabeth Leslie.  [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/35/mode/1up?view=theater Duntreath: 35-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Third Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath married Katherine Forrest. [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/35/mode/1up?view=theater Duntreath: 35-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Fourth Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sie William Edmonstone of Duntreath married Sybilla Carmichael.  [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/35/mode/1up?view=theater Duntreath: 35-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
