2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Edmonstone/6000000037935462192?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1589145591855&through=6000000002187962824
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1515: Sasine of Redenach and other lands in Menteith to William Edmonstoun, in virtue of act in favour of heirs of persons killed in Northumberland. Menteth. Idem senescallus respondebit pro 16 It. 13 s. 4 d. de firmis terrarum
2 CONC  de Menteth. Redenach, Unschennach, Ergateis, et Lundeis cum pertinen. jacentium infra senescallatum suum, existentium in manibus regis per spatium 4 terminorum ult. elaps. sasina non recuperata, et pro 33 l. 6 s. 8 d. de relevio 
2 CONC earundem, regi debitis per sasinam datam Willelmo Edmonstoun de eisdem apud Edinburgh dicto 8 Nov. anno predicto, ratione dispensationis et statuti fact, per regem ult. defunctum heredibus interfectorum in Northummerland, ut in re
2 CONC tornatu continetur. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof14scot/page/579/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland 1513-22. Volume XIV, page 579]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1515: Sasine of Duntreth to William Edmonstoun, in virtue of act in favour of heirs of persons killed in Northumberland. Dunbertane. Vicecomes respondebit pro 200 li. de firmis baronie de Duntreth extendentis ad 55 marcat. terr
2 CONC arum antiqui extentus cum pertinen. jacentis infra balliam suam, existentis in manibus regis per spatium 2 annorum et 1 termini ult. elaps. sasina non recuperata, que firme se extendunt annuatim ad 100 li., et pro 2 h. piperis per
2 CONC  duplicationem albefirme earundem, regi debitis per sasinam datam Willelmo Edmonstoun de eisdem apud Edinburgh 30 Jan. a.r. predicto ratione dispensationis et statuti fact, per quondam regem ut predicitur, ut latius in retornatu c
2 CONC ontinetur. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof14scot/page/580/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland 1513-22. Volume XIV, page 579]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1516: Sasine of Arbaith, Lorne and Derre in Strathern to William Edmonstoun, in virtue of act in favour of heirs of persons killed in Northumberland. Stratherne. Senescallus respondebit pro 48 l. de firmis terrarum de Arbaith, 
2 CONC Lorn, et stratherne. Derre, cum pertinen. jacentium infra balliam suam, existentium in manibus regis per spatium 3 annorum ult. elaps. sasina non recuperata, et pro 16 li. de relevio earundem, regi debitis per sasinam datam Willel
2 CONC mo Edmonstoun de eisdem apud Edinburgh 29 Oct. a.r.4. ratione dispen- sationis et statuti quondam s. d. n. regis ult. defuncti heredibus interfectorum in suo exercitu gratiose concessorum, ut habetur in retornatu. [https://archive
2 CONC .org/details/exchequerrollsof14scot/page/587/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland 1513-22. Volume XIV, page 587]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 February 1539: Apud Edinburgh.Rex dedit literas legitimationis JACOBO EDMONSTOUN bastardo, filio naturali quondam Willelmi  E. de Duntreath militis. xxvi. 294. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/466/mode
2 CONC /1up RMS 1513-1546: charter number 2079]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 April 1541: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James V, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Newtoun of Downe in the Stewartry of Menteith and sheriffdom of Perth to James Edmonstoun, bastard 
2 CONC son of the deceased William Edmonstoun of Duntreith, knight. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/532/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 2324]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
