1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Chiefs of Clan Buchanan=
2 CONT *15th – George Buchanan,[76][77] (Guthrie Smith identifies him as 10th Chief and Buchanan of Auchmar identifies him as 17th Chief) succeed his grandfather, Walter 14th of Buchanan, in 1526 and died 1560. He first married '''Margar
2 CONC et Edmonstone''' and by her a son (John [Guthrie Smith identifies him as 11th Chief but then goes on to advise that the Chiefship passed from John’s father to John’s son[78] and Buchanan of Auchmar identifies him as 18th Chief[79 
2 CONC who married Elizabeth Livingston and by her had George[79] who succeeded his grandfather) and two daughters (Helen and Susanna). Second he married Janet Cunningham and by her had a son (William first ancestor of the cadets of Auch
2 CONC mar) and a daughter (Margaret).
2 CONT *16th – Sir George Buchanan,[78][79] (Guthrie Smith identifies him as 12th Chief and Buchanan of Auchmar identifies him as 19th Chief) succeed his grandfather, George 15th of Buchanan, in 1561, married Lady Mary Graham and by her 
2 CONC one son (John his successor) and two daughters (Helen and Susanna).
2 CONT *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Buchanan
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *''''''4. George Buchanan of that Ilk, c 1557
2 CONT *'''''' George Buchanan succeeded his grandfather in 1526. He married twice. (1) Margaret Edmonstone'''''', ( 2 ) Janet Cunningham. By his first wife he had John and by his second wife William  ( first of Auchmar ) , and Margaret.
2 CONC  George died 15 February 1560/61.
2 CONT * A shield of arms couché: Three ( boar's or bear's ) heads and necks erased. Crest unknown. Inscription illegible. Source, ( Leny and Bardowie Ch. ).
2 CONT *From: http://www.buchanan-heraldry.net.nz/body/seals.html
