2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Marjory Seytoun (1523)  Marjory Seytoun (1530) Mariotam Seutoun (1530) Marion Seton (1531) Lady Marjory Seytoun (1546) Lady Marjory Seytoun (1546) Dame Marion Seytoun (1548) Dame Marion Seton (1554) Dame Marion Seyt
2 CONC oun (1556) Lady Marion Seytoun (1557) Dame Marion Seytoun (1558)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Seton died between 1558 and 30 September 1558. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03paul/page/439/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 439]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Seton married Hugh, Earl of Eglinton. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03paul/page/439/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 439]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 Sep 1523: Charter granted by William, Lord Borthwick, in favour of his beloved son and heir apparent Arthur Borthuick, and Marjory Seytoun, his spouse and the longest liver of them two in conjunct infeftment and the heirs ma
2 CONC le lawfully procreated or to be procreated between them whom failing to the nearest and lawful heirs of the said Arthur whomsoever of the lands of Halkwood, Ovirgalcottis (Cauldcoats), Nethirgalcottis, Harschaw with the corn and w
2 CONC aulk mills thereof, and the lands of Rydding (Redding), lying within the barony of Avondaill; to hold of Andrew, Lord Avondaill his heirs and assignees for services used and wont reserving nevertheless 50 merks Scots from the said
2 CONC  lands to William, Lord Borthuick, for the time of the life of the said Arthur to be paid at two yearly terms Whitsunday and Martinmas in winter by equal portions  Dated at his castle of Borthuik Witnesses: William Borthuik of Cru
2 CONC ikstoun (Crookston), William Borthuik of Johnestoun, Richard Maitland of Lethingtoun and others [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f83&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Borthwick&k
2 CONC o=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Lands formerly belonging to the Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/10/83]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                   2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 February 1530: Precept granted by Hugh, Earl of Eglinton for infefting Hugh Montgomery, master of Eglinton and Marjory Seytoun, his spouse and the longest liever of them two in conjunct infeftment in the foresaid lands Dated 
2 CONC at Polnone [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f28%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marjory+seytoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Montgomerie Family,
2 CONC  Earls of Eglinton: Legal and Financial Papers, reference GD3/1/10/28/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 February 1530:Charter by Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Lord Montgomery, made in favour of Hugh, Master of Eglinton and Mariotam Seytoun, Lady of Borthwick, following from a marriage contract. [https://archive.org/details/registrumm
2 CONC agnisi03scot/page/218/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 993 on pp. 218-19]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 March 1530: Instrument of sasine followng on GD3/1/3615 in favour of Hugh Montgomery, master of Eglinton and Marjory Seytoun, his spouse and the longest liver of them two in conjunct infeftment of the foresaid lands. Patrick
2 CONC  Newton, notary [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f28%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marjory+seytoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Montgomerie Fam
2 CONC ily, Earls of Eglinton: Legal and Financial Papers, reference GD3/1/10/28/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 January 1530-31: Dispensation by Gavin, archbishop of Glasgow as judge delegate, for marriage of Hugh Montgomery and Marion Seton [later 2nd earl of Eglinton and the sister of George, lord Seton, formerly wife of Thomas, mas
2 CONC ter of Borthwick. 'Scots Peerage' iii, 439.]. (2 examples; one carries archbishop's round seal, good condition). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f3%2f15&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp
2 CONC =n&k=thomas%2c+master+of+borthwick&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton: Legal and Financial Papers, reference GD3/2/3/15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 May 1546: Procuratory of resignation by Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Lord Montgomery in favour of George, Lord Seytoun, Malcolm, Lord Flemyng, Thomas Niven of Monkredding and others for resigning the foresaid lands and barony and
2 CONC  also the lands and barony of Robertoun extending to 37lib 13s 4d of land of old extent lying in the bailliary of Cunningham and sheriffdom of Ayr in the hands of James, Earl of Arran, Lord Hamilton, tutor protector and governor o
2 CONC f Queen Mary and her kingdom, as in her hands, princess and stewartess of Scotland, his lady superior for new infeftment to be given thereof by the governor to Hugh, Earl of Eglinton and Lady Marjory Seytoun, his spouse, and the l
2 CONC ongest liver of them two in conjunct infeftment and the heirs lawfully procreated or to be procreated between them whom failing to the nearest and lawful heirs and assignees of the said Earl whomsoever. Dated at Glasgow [http://ca
2 CONC talogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f41%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marjory+seytoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton: Le
2 CONC gal and Financial Papers, reference GD3/1/10/28/3]'''
2 CONT
