1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARGARET CHARTERIS===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 March 1572: Charter by which Alexander Kirkpatrick of Kirkmichael confirms, with the consent of Roger Kirkpatrick of Closeburn and Thomas Kirkpatrick of Alisland, his curators, that he has given the ten pound lands of Kirkmi
2 CONC chael to his wife Margaret Charteris in liferent. His charter follows from a marriage contract dated 23 January 1571, in which Margaret is identified as the lawful daughter of John Charteris of Amisfeild. The charter was witnessed
2 CONC  by John Charteris of Amisfeild, John Charteris his son and heir, John Kirkpatrick, son and heir of Thomas Kirkpatrick of Alisland, Roger Kirkpatrick of Audgirth, James Gordon of Kirkconnell, and Henry alias Harry Kirkpatrick. Ale
2 CONC xander Kirkpatrick of Kirkmichael and his wife Margaret Charteris obtained a charter of confirmation under the Great Seal of Scotland on 9 June 1575. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/651/mode/1up RMS 1546-8
2 CONC 0, charter number 2423]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Printed Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/n5/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1546-1580. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. (H. M. Ge
2 CONC neral Register House, Edinburgh, 1886), 1180 pp. including indexes and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
