1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10958.htm#i109573  SCOTS PEERAGE.COM
2 CONT
2 CONT "<strong>Robert Maxwell, 4th Lord Maxwell</strong> (1493–1546) was a member of the council of Regency (1536) of the Kingdom of Scotland, Regent of the Isle of Arran and like his father before him patriarch of the House of Maxwell 
2 CONC \ clan Maxwell. A distinguished Scottish nobleman, politician, soldier and in 1513 Lord High Admiral, Lord Maxwell was a member of James V of Scotland's royal council and served as Lord Provost of Edinburgh in 1524, 1527 and 1535.
2 CONC  He was also an Extraordinary Lord of Session in 1533. In 1537, he was one of the ambassadors sent to the French Court to negotiate the marriage of James to Mary of Guise, whom he espoused as proxy for the King...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He was the eldest son of John Maxwell, 3rd Lord Maxwell, killed at the battle of Flodden, 9 September 1513, his mother being Lady Agnes Stewart, illegitimate daughter of James Stewart, 1st Earl of Buchan...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...On 3 June 1546 he was appointed warden of the west marches. He died on 9 July of the same year...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...By his first wife, Janet Douglas, daughter of Sir William Douglas of Drumlanrig, he had three children:
2 CONT * Robert Maxwell, 6th Lord Maxwell
2 CONT * Sir John Maxwell, married Agnes Maxwell, 4th Lady Herries
2 CONT *Margaret, married firstly to Archibald Douglas, 6th Earl of Angus, and secondly to Sir William Baillie of Lamington."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/maxwell1445.htm#MAXWELL_1445_4
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert [Maxwell], 4th Lord Maxwell, PC born c. 1494 
2 CONT
2 CONT mar. (1) after 4 Jul 1509 Janet Douglas, dau. of Sir William Douglas of Drumlanrig, by his wife Elizabeth Gordon, dau. of Sir John Gordon of Lochinvar
2 CONT
2 CONT children by first wife
2 CONT *1. Hon Robert Maxwell, later 5th Lord Maxwell
2 CONT *2. Hon Sir John Maxwell, jure uxoris Lord Herries of Terregles, mar. bef. 18 Mar 1547/8 Hon Agnes Herries, suo jure Lady Herries of Terregles, and had issue
2 CONT *1. Hon Margaret Maxwell (d. 1593), mar. (1) bef. 9 Apr 1543 as his second wife Archibald [Douglas], 6th Earl of Angus, and (2) bef. Sep 1560 Sir William Baillie of Lamington
2 CONT
2 CONT mar. (2) betw. 1520 and 15 Nov 1525 Lady Agnes Home (widow of (1) Adam [Hepburn], 2nd Earl of Bothwell and (2) Alexander [Home], 3rd Lord Home; mar. (4) bef. 13 Dec 1549 Cutherbert Ramsay, son of Nicholas Ramsay of Dalhousie; legi
2 CONC timated 31 Oct 1552; d. Feb 1557), illeg. dau. of James [Stewart], 1st Earl of Buchan, by his mistress Margaret Murray of Philiphaugh
2 CONT
2 CONT died 9 Jul 1546 suc. by son by first wife
2 CONT
