1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Grierson-205
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sir James "of Capenoch" Greer of Lag formerly Grierson Born 1604 in Capenock, Dumfries-shire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William (Grierson) Greer and Nichola (Maxwell) Grierson
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Helena (Grierson) Douglas, Robert Grierson, Agnes (Grierson) Laurie, Sarah Grierson and Lancelot Grierson	
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary Anne (Browne) Grier — married 1626 in Lag, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Henry Greer, James Greer, Anne (Greer) Turner, Nicola Grier, John Greer, Henry Greer and Anne Greer 	
2 CONT Died 29 Jan 1666 in Capenoch, Dumfries-shire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT  Biography Sir Knight James Grier
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial, Dumfrieshire, Scotland, probably Lag Tower, photo of the Tower built 1460. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James Grierson, son of Sir William and Nichola (Maxwell) Grierson was born circa 1604; died in 1666. Designated as The Rock and Capenoch, Dumfriesshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1626, he married Mary Browne, daughter of the Reverend John Browne of Glencairn, the first minister after the Reformation and Mary was, at the time of this marriage, the widow of Thomas Greer, of Barjang Tower of the same count
2 CONC y.
2 CONT
2 CONT From this union to his wife's Greer family, Sir James Grier, originated several Greer branches known as of Tullylagen, Grange and Sea Park. Many of these accepted the Quaker faith and removed to Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The known children of Sir James and Mary (Browne) Greer, three: i. James Greer ... . ii. Henry Greer ... . iii. Ann Greer ... ." (From a lithographed Family Chart prepared by Thomas Greer, of Ireland, in 1855 as given in GREGOR, M
2 CONC acGREGOR, MacGHEE, MAGRUDER, GRIERSON, GRIER, GREER --- A HISTORY OF THE ORIGIN OF THE ABOVE FAMILIES AND MANY OF THEIR DESCENDANTS, 1954, compiled by Robert M. Torrence, A.B., F.G.S.P., F.I.A.G., 110 Edgevale Road Baltimore 10, M
2 CONC aryland, page 41.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James Grier, Knight., of Capenoch, Dumfriesshire and Rock Hall, Alnwick, Northumberland, 5th son of Sir William Grier. James succeded his brother, John in Capenoch. In a discharge, dated 1630, James signs Grier and brother Ale
2 CONC xander signs Grierson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James removed to Cumberland and changed his surname to Grier. On 6 August 1630 [Lag Charter #214], James Greirsone (NOT SIR), brother of Sir Robert Greirsone of Lag, witnessed his brother Lancelot Greirsone's sasine to Dalskai
2 CONC rth." (William Greer, Illinois.) (Excerpts taken from the Ralph Terry Family Tree) Children
2 CONT
2 CONT     Henry Greer b: ABT 1627 in Capenoch, Dumfriesshire, Scotland
2 CONT     John Grier b: ABT 1635 in Capenoch, Dumfriesshire, Scotland
2 CONT     Anne Grier b: 1633
