1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Mary Fleming
2 CONT *Birth: say  1565 or 1566. Her parents married in May 1562, and she is historically noted as their fourth daughter.  
2 CONT * Death: say  1635.
2 CONT * Parents: Daughter of John Fleming, 5th Lord Fleming, and Elizabeth Ross.
2 CONT * Marriage: Married Sir James Douglas, 8th Baron of Drumlanrig. The marriage contract is dated 9 December 1581.  
2 CONT * Sir James Douglas was born circa 1559 and died on 16 October 1615. He was the son of Sir William Douglas (who died in 1572) and Margaret Gordon.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT # William Douglas, 1st Earl of Queensberry: Succeeded his father in 1615; created Viscount of Drumlanrig in 1628 and Earl of Queensberry in 1633; married Lady Isabel Kerr and died in 1640.
2 CONT # Sir James Douglas, 2nd of Mouswald: Received the Barony of Mouswald from his father in 1608; married Helena Grierson by contract dated 2 November 1615.
2 CONT # George Douglas: Documented as a younger son and noted in the Privy Council records for his activity in local border disputes.
2 CONT # David Douglas: Named alongside his brothers in contemporary family legal and property transactions.
2 CONT # Janet Douglas: Married William Livingstone of Jerviswood.
2 CONT # Helen Douglas: Married John Menzies of Castlehill.
2 CONT
2 CONT You may occasionally encounter a John Douglas (of Killyvarrane) in these records. The Scots Peerage clarifies that he was an older, natural (illegitimate) son of Sir James Douglas, born before the 1581 marriage to Mary Fleming. He
2 CONC  should not be attached as a biological child of Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 5th Lord Fleming married on 10 May 1562, Elizabeth Ross (died after 14 April 1578), only child of Robert, Master of Ross, son of Ninian, Lord Ross, by his wife Agnes Scott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Fleming, later 6th Lord Fleming later 1st Earl of Wigtown
2 CONT # Margaret Fleming, married after 19 April 1588, Sir James Forrester of Garden
2 CONT # Elizabeth Fleming (died after 24 September 1579)
2 CONT # Jane Fleming (died October 1630), married after 1582/3 William Bruce of Airth
2 CONT # Mary Fleming, married after 9 December 1581, Sir James Douglas, 8th of Drumlanrig,[14] and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Fleming also had a daughter with an unknown mother, Lucrece Fleming, who married firstly, John Stewart of Rosland, a royal valet, and secondly, at Stirling on 4 August 1593,[15] Robert Graham of the Fauld, an English borderer
2 CONC  who died in 1600.[16]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Fleming,_5th_Lord_Fleming#Family
2 CONT **10.  Joseph Bain, Calendar of Border Papers, vol. 2 (Edinburgh, 1894), p. 663 [https://archive.org/details/borderpaperscale02grea/page/662/mode/2up Archive.Org] 
2 CONT ** 14.  HMC Buccleuch Drumlanrig, vol. 1 (London, 1897), pp. 29-30.
2 CONT *Because her marriage spans two different noble houses, her family details are split across two volumes of *The Scots Peerage*:
2 CONT ** For her husband's family line (Douglas of Drumlanrig): Paul, James Balfour, Sir. *The Scots Peerage*. Edinburgh: David Douglas, 1910. Vol. VII, pp. 132–134.
2 CONT **For her father's family line (Fleming, Lord Fleming): Paul, James Balfour, Sir. *The Scots Peerage*. Edinburgh: David Douglas, 1911. Vol. VIII, pp. 542, 544.
