1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Robert Montgomery, or Montgumry, of Skelmorlie</strong>, son of Robert Montgomery, of the same, by Dorothy, daughter of Robert (Sempill), 3rd Lord Sempill [S], was 5th male descent from George Montgomery, of Skelmorli
2 CONC e (d 1505), 2nd son of Alexander, 1st Lord Montgomery [S], succeeded his father in 1583, was Knighted by James I, and created a Baronet [S] 10 or 1 January, sealed 22 December 1628, the patent being not recorded in the Great Seal 
2 CONC Register, with rem. to heirs male whatsoever, and with a grant of, presumably 16,000 acres of Nova Scotia, of which he has seizin in December 1628. He was M.P. [S] for Buteshire, 1644. He married Margaret, 1st daughter of Sir Will
2 CONC iam Douglas, of Drumlanrig, by Margaret, daughter of Sir James Gordon of Lochinvar. She died 1624. He died November 1651, having had 67 years tenure of the family estate."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n355/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 336
