1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on William Crichton:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p19229.htm#i192288
2 CONT
2 CONT William Crichton of Sanquhar [1]
2 CONT *M, #192288
2 CONT *Last Edited=8 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT William Crichton of Sanquhar was born in France.[1] He is the son of Robert Crichton, 8th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar and Anne Fermor.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Sanquhar, Scotland.[1] On 8 August 1609 he was legitimated.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1614 his claim to the title and other estates failed.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15 July 1619 he was served heir to territorial Barony of Sanquhar.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 601. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
