1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on John Graham:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p1307.htm#i13065
2 CONT
2 CONT John Graham, 4th Earl of Menteith [1]
2 CONT *M, #13065, 
2 CONT *d. January 1564/65
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Aug 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT John Graham, 4th Earl of Menteith was the son of William Graham, 3rd Earl of Menteith and Margaret Moubray.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marion Seton, daughter of George Seton, 4th Lord Seton and Elizabeth Hay, on 8 October 1548.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in January 1564/65.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career: He fought in the Battle of Solway Moss on 24 November 1542, where he was captured by the English and held priosoner until July 1541 when he was ransomed.[1] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 4th Earl of Menteith [S., 1427] circa 1544.[1] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland] before June 1545.[1] 
2 CONT *He was a Lord of the Congregation in 1558.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Graham, 4th Earl of Menteith and Marion Seton
2 CONT *1. William Graham, 5th Earl of Menteith+[3] d. Sep 1578
2 CONT *2. George Graham [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2751. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
