1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2978.htm#i29778 Darryl Lundy's Peerage] page on William Graham
2 CONT
2 CONT William Graham, 7th Earl of Menteith [1]
2 CONT *M, #29778, 
2 CONT *b. after July 1589, 
2 CONT *d. after 13 April 1661
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Aug 2012
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.2%
2 CONT
2 CONT William Graham, 7th Earl of Menteith was born after July 1589.[1] He was the son of John Graham, 6th Earl of Menteith and Maria Campbell.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Agnes Gray, daughter of Patrick Gray, 6th Lord Gray and Lady Mary Stewart, after 30 March 1612.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died after 13 April 1661.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career:
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 7th Earl of Menteith [S., 1427] in December 1598.[1] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland] in 1626/27.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Lord Justice General in 1628.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Extra Lord of Session between 1628 and 1633.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Lord President of the Council [Scotland] between 1628 and 1633.[1] 
2 CONT *On 13 August 1629 he waived his rights to the title of Earl of Strathearn.[1] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) in 1630.[1] 
2 CONT *He was created 1st Earl of Airth [Scotland] on 28 March 1633, with precedency of 6 September 1428.[3] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Lord President of the Council [Scotland] between 1639 and 1661.[1] 
2 CONT *On 11 January 1643/44 he was regranted the title of Earl of Menteith with remainder to his heirs male whomsoever.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He has an extensive biographical entry in the Dictionary of National Biography.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of William Graham, 7th Earl of Menteith
2 CONT # Sir James Graham+[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Graham, 7th Earl of Menteith and Agnes Gray
2 CONT # Lady Mary Graham+[2] d. 28 Jan 1653
2 CONT # Lady Margaret Graham+[3]
2 CONT # John Graham, Lord Graham of Kinpont+[4] b. c 1613, d. 6 Sep 1644
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
