1 NAME Archibald /Stewart/
2 GIVN Archibald
2 SURN Stewart
2 _MARNM Stewart
1 NAME Sir Archibald Stewart of Burray, 1st Baronet
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 MAY 1689
1 BURI
2 DATE 17 MAY 1689
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Archibald Stewart, of Burray</strong>, in Orkney, 4th but last surv. s. of William Stewart, of Mains, in Galloway, by Barbara, da. and h. of James Stewart, of Burray aforesaid, which William was only br. to Alexander, 1st
2 CONC  Earl of Galloway [S.], was in Hamilton's army, 1648, for the rescue of the King, being afterwards in that of Montrose ; held a command at the battle of Worcester, and was taken prisoner ; was in 1683 Lieut.-Col. of the Orkney mil
2 CONC itia, and, having suc. his elder br., William Stewart, in the estates of Mains and Burray, was cr. a Baronet [S.], as above, with rem. to heirs male whatsoever, the Privy Seal being dated 4 Nov. 1687, at  Whitehall. He m. firstly,
2 CONC  Isabel, da. of Sir William Murray, of Abercairny. She d. 3 Aug. 1683. He m. secondly, a few weeks later, 16 Sep. 1683, his maidservant, Katharine, da. of Patrick Rowsay, indweller in Stronsay. She d. in childbed s.p.m., 26 June 1
2 CONC 684. He d. at Burray 13, and was bur. there 17 May 1689.""
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n373/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 355
