1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY ISABELLE STEWART ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Stewart-Countess-of-Argyle/6000000000850596018
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Isabelle Stewart was one of the three daughters and co-heirs of John Stewart, Lord of Lorne. She married Colin, second Lord Campbell. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01paul/page/332 The Scots Peerage, Volume I
2 CONC , p. 332] She died at Dumbarton on 26 October 1510 and was buried at Kilmun in Argyllshire.[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01paul/page/334 Ibidem, p. 334]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 May 1466: Charter by which James III, King of Scots, confirms possession of various lands to Colin, Earl of Argyll, Lord Campbell, and his wife Isabelle Stewart, including the third part of various lands in Perthshire that h
2 CONC ad been resigned by Mariota Srewart, sister of Isabelle Stewart, daughters of the deceased John, Lord Lorn. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/185 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the G
2 CONC reat Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 877 on p. 185]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 January 1493: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms possession of Dollar Castle (alias Castle Gloum) and various lands to Archibald, Earl of Argyll, Lord Campbell and Lord. The lands were in the King's had becau
2 CONC se of the death of Earl Archibald's father Colin. Part of the land conveyed was held by Lady Isabelle Stewart, widow of Colin and mother of Archibald: "Domine Isabelle Stewart relicte dicti quondam Colini et matris dicti Arch." [h
2 CONC ttps://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/501 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 2354 on p. 501]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT #  [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft#page/356/mode/2up Sir James Balfour Paul (editor), The Scots Peerage etc., Volume I (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1904), pp. 332-33]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Commentary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Colin Campbell, 1st Earl of Argyll  married Isabelle Stewart, daughter of John Stewart, 2nd Lord Lorne in 1465, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Archibald Campbell, 2nd Earl of Argyll.
2 CONT # Thomas Campbell
2 CONT # Margaret Campbell, married George Seton, 4th Lord Seton
2 CONT # Isabel Campbell, married William Drummond, Master of Drummond, son to John Drummond, 1st Lord Drummond
2 CONT # Mary Campbell married Aonghas Óg Lord of the isles.
2 CONT # Helen Campbell, married to Hugh Montgomerie, 1st Earl of Eglinton
2 CONT # Elizabeth Campbell, married John Oliphant, 2nd Lord Oliphant
2 CONT # Catherine Campbell, married Lachlan Og Maclean
2 CONT
