1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ALEXANDER MONTGOMERY ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Montgomery: "styled second Lord Montgomerie, but who apparently never held the title. He was probably born about 1445, as he is said to be of lawful age in June 1466, when served heir to his father in the bailiary of 
2 CONC Cunningham. Little is known of his history, and it is doubtful if he survived his grandfather. It is certain he was never infeft in the great lordships of Ardrossan and Eglinton, with the smaller estates, which are enumerated in t
2 CONC he retour of his son Hugh as heir to his great-grandfather, the first Lord Montgomerie. Nor does he appear to have exercised the office of bailiary of Cunningham, to which he was served heir. He married, before 1459, Catherine, da
2 CONC ughter of Gilbert, Lord Kennedy, and had issue. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/434/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 434]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Birth ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of birth has not been identified for Alexander Montgomery, here treated. However, it is supposed that he must have been of lawful age on 17 June 1466, and if this was the case then it might reasonably be sugest
2 CONC ed that he was very likely born in or before about 1445.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Alexander Montgomery, here treated. However, he probably died before 30 August 1483, when his son Hugh is noticed acting as Lord Montgomery. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.go
2 CONC v.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f9%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1484&di=n NRS: GD3/1/10/9/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Montgomery, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-Kennedy/6000000009617281584?through=6000000002006366666. [https://archive.org/details/memorialsofmonv100fras/page/26/mode/1up Memorials of the Mo
2 CONC ntgomeries I: 26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 January 1448: Grant by James II as Stewart of Scotland in favour of Alexander Montgomery, eldest born son of the King's beloved cousin, Alexander, Lord Montgomery and his heirs of the said offices to which no fees were attac
2 CONC hed. On the resignation of the King said cousin made in his hands as Stewart of Scotland; to hold of the King as Stewart of Scotland for services used and wont. Given under the Privy Seal at Strivelyne (Stirling). [https://catalog
2 CONC ue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f15%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1484&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earl
2 CONC s of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/15/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 January 1465: Copy of Obligation by Robert Lord Boyd to Gilbert Lord Kennedy, by which the said Robert Lord Boyd obliges him during all the days of his life to aid assist supply and defend the said Gilbert Lord Kennedy, exce
2 CONC pting always his allegiance to the King, and the Bonds granted by him to John Lord Darnly, James Lord Hamilton, Robert Lord Lyle, Alexander Lord Montgomery, Alexander Montgomery grandson and heir of the said Alexander Lord Montgom
2 CONC ery, and Sir Alexander Boyd of Duncow, Knight, and also to be true and faithful to the said Gilbert Lord Kennedy so long as he shall have the keeping of the King's person, And further to cause with all convenient diligence solemni
2 CONC ze marriage between James Boyd his eldest son and Marian Kennedy daughter of the said Gilbert Lord Kennedy. Dated at Edinburgh. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f96&st=1&tc=y
2 CONC &tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1445&dt=1484&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD25/1/96]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 June 1466: Service before John of Culquhone of that ilk, knight, Royal Comptroller, and Mr David Guthrie of Kincaldrum, treasurer of the King, sheriffs of Ayr in that part, by Sir John of Achinlek of that ilk, Sir John Chamm
2 CONC yr of Gaitgard, knights, Robert Craufurd of Achynannys, John Colville, John Shaw, Quintin Mure, David Campbell, Hew Campbell, Edward de Cunninghame, George Mure, David Wallace, George Stewart, William de Achinlek, John de Hamilton
2 CONC , and George de Fullartoun of Alexander Montgomery, son of the deceased Alexander Montgomery, as heir of his said father, in the office of baillie of the barony of Cunningham, which office was valued yearly at its accustomed fees,
2 CONC  and held of the King, as Stewart of Scotland by the service pertaining to the office of bailliary in the name of blench ferm and had been in his hand since the decease of the said Alexander, 14 years before. At Linlithgow, in the
2 CONC  town hall. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f15%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1484&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of 
2 CONC the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/15/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 August 1483: Charter granted by Hugh, Lord Montgomery and Giffing in favour of Alexander Montgomery, son and apparent heir of Robert Montgomery of Giffyng and Janet of Dunlop, his spouse, in conjunct fee and the heirs male l
2 CONC awfully procreated or to be procreated of their bodies whom all failing to the said Robert his true nearest and lawful heirs male whomsoever for the true affection which he had towards them of the 5 merk lands of old extent of Bar
2 CONC  lying in the lordship of Giffyng, on the resignation of the said Robert; to hold of Hugh, Lord Montgomery for service used and wont. Dated the foresaid lands of Bar. Witnesses: John Montgomery, son and heir of Lord Montgomery, Ro
2 CONC bert Montgomery, Laird of Giffin, Master George Montgomery, rector of Eaglesham and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f9%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+m
2 CONC ontgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1484&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/10/9/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
