1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARGARET MURE (aka MARGARET MUIR)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Mure is the daughter of Quinton Mure of Skeldon. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n452/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, III, p. 436] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Mure married Sir Neil Montgomery of Lainshaw. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f3%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=neil+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=n NRS: 
2 CONC GD3/2/3/6] They had a dispensation on 21 July 1525 on account of their consanguinity, which states that she was only eleven years of age when she married Sir Neil Montgomery of Lainshaw, and was in ignorance of their close relatio
2 CONC nship. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n452/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, III, p. 436] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Montgomery-of-Lainshaw/6000000008571544852?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520867940444&through=6000000008517365038
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Neil-Montgomery-of-Lainshaw/6000000008517365038?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520868255949&through=6000000006444240847
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Christian-Montgomery/6000000008571309777?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520869209133&through=6000000008517365038
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Montgomery/6000000006444240863?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520869553046&through=6000000008517365038
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Helen-Montgomery/6000000076883095167?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520869675019&through=6000000076883095167
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Following the murder of her first husband, Margaret Mure married for a second time to John Kennedy of Skeldon. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n452/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, III, p. 436] They were a
2 CONC live in February 1560-61 and had two sons.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/N-N/6000000076882330551?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520869748570&through=6000000006444240847
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/N-N/6000000076882962890?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520869895480&through=6000000006444240847
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 July 1525: Dispensation by John Dingwall, archdeacon of Caithness and chancellor of Aberdeen, judge delegate, for marriage of Neil Montgomery and Margaret Muir. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.
2 CONC aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f3%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=neil+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/2/3/6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 February 1552: 	Precept of Clare constat by Gilbert Earl of Cassillis, to Dame Margaret Mure wife of John Kennedy (of Skeldon) as heir of the deceased Quintin Mure of Aird her father in the 6 merk land of Over Kilmoir and mil
2 CONC l thereof, lying in the bailiary of Carrick - to be holden blanch of the Earl and his successors Dated at Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f549&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&
2 CONC tp=n&k=John+Kennedy+of+Skeldon&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/549]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This Ladys mother was Dame Katharine Kennedy daughter of David 1st Earl of Cassillis, and who married Quintin Mure of Aird some time prior to 7th January 1510.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 April 1553: Instrument of Resignation ad perpetuam remanentiam, by the said Dame Margaret Mure with consent of John Kennedy of Skeldon her husband, in the hands of Gilbert Earl of Cassillis, of the 6 merk land and mill of Ov
2 CONC er Kilmoir, to remain with the Earl and his successors in all time coming, his Lordship having redeemed the same from her in due form - reserving the liferent thereof to Dame Katharine Kennedy her mother. Witnesses - Adam Boyd in 
2 CONC Pinkil, Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains, Thomas Kennedy of Coif and Gilbert Baird of Kilhenzie and James Ross, writer. Dated at Mayboll. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f552&st=1
2 CONC &tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Kennedy+of+Skeldon&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/552]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1560: Letter of Reversion by John Kennedy of Skeldon and Dame Margaret Mure his wife (See GD/25/1/552) to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis, bearing the Earl having infeft them in conjunct fee and liferent and the heirs procreate betwe
2 CONC en them whom failling the said John Kennedy his nearest heirs whatsoever, in an annualrent of 50 merks money of Scotland payable at two terms in the year Whitsunday and Martinmas by equal portions furth of the 4 merk land of Holms
2 CONC  of Dalrymple, lying in the bailiary of Kyle Stewart, yet nevertheless they oblige them and theirs aforesaid, upon the Earl or his successors making payment to them within the Church of Mayboll of the sum of 500 merks like money, 
2 CONC they shall immediately thereafter renounce and discharge the said annualrent and declare the same redeemed Witnesses - Mr Patrick Vaus parson of Wigton, James Kennedy of Ochterlour and Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains. [http://catalogu
2 CONC e.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f596&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Kennedy+of+Skeldon&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassill
2 CONC is (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/596]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 February 1560: Contract between Robert, Lord Boyd, for himself and taking burden on him for John Brisbane of Bishopton, Charles Mowat of Busby, David Fernielaw younger of that ilk, Robert Boyd in Clerkland, Archibald Boyle, 
2 CONC son of the late John Boyle of Kilburne, and William Blair in Henryscroft, on the one part, and Neil Montgomery, son and heir to the late Sir Neil Montgomery of Lainshaw, for himself, and taking burden on him for Dame Margaret Muir
2 CONC , his mother, Christine, Elizabeth and Helen Montgomery, his sisters german, and Thomas Montgomery, James and John, sons natural to the said Sir Neil, on the other part, for slaughter of Sir Neil Montgomery. Dated at Glasgow, 10 F
2 CONC eb 1560. (Boyd Papers). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=neil+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Bu
2 CONC rgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/167]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
