2 CONT '''10 February 1560-61: Contract between Robert, Lord Boyd, for himself and taking burden on him for John Brisbane of Bishopton, Charles Mowat of Busby, David Fernielaw younger of that ilk, Robert Boyd in Clerkland, Archibald Boyl
2 CONC e, son of the late John Boyle of Kilburne, and William Blair in Henryscroft, on the one part, and Neil Montgomery, son and heir to the late Sir Neil Montgomery of Lainshaw, for himself, and taking burden on him for Dame Margaret M
2 CONC uir, his mother, Christine, Elizabeth and Helen Montgomery, his sisters german, and Thomas Montgomery, James and John, sons natural to the said Sir Neil, on the other part, for slaughter of Sir Neil Montgomery. Dated at Glasgow, 1
2 CONC 0 Feb 1560. (Boyd Papers). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=neil+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers,
