1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR NEIL MONTGOMERY OF LAINSHAW===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n452/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, III, pp. 436-37] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/ancestralrecords01colo/page/222/mode/1up Ancestral Records and Portraits: Armorial Ensigns on Montgomery, Earl of Eglinton]
2 CONT
2 CONT MONTGOMERY OR MONTGOMERIE Arms Quarterly first and fourth azure three fleur de lis or for Montgomery second and third gul s Three annuUts or stoned azure for E glint on all within a border of the second charged with a double tress
2 CONC ure of the third Crest For Montgomery an arm embowed in armor the hand grasping a broken spear head drooping all ppr Motto Honeur sans Repos
2 CONT
2 CONT * The first Earl of Eglinton Hugh Montgomerie third Lord Montgomerie 
2 CONT ** died 1545 having 
2 CONT ** married Lady Helen the daughter of Colin the first Earl of Argyll 
2 CONT ** Their '''third son Sir Neil Montgomery''' married about 1500 Margaret 
2 CONT *** the '''daughter and heiress of''' Quintin Mure Laird of Skeldon 
2 CONT *** Their '''son Sir Neil Montgomery II of Lainshaw''' 
2 CONT **** married Jean, the daughter of John and Grisel (Betoun) Montgomery.
2 CONT * Mrs Charles Ridgely of Hampton erected in his memory and that of her brother the memorial church corner of Lafayette Avenue and Bolton Street Baltimore 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/ancestralrecords01colo/page/222/mode/1up Ancestral Records and Portraits: 222-23]
2 CONT
