2 CONT '''9 June 1622: Contract of marriage between Hugh Montgomery and Marion Montgomery. Contract of marriage between Hugh Montgomery, younger of Auchinhood with consent of Hugh Montgomery, elder of Auchinhood, his father on the one pa
2 CONC rt and Marion Montgomery, lawful daughter of unquhile Neill Montgomery of Langschaw with consent of Marion Mure, her mother and spouse to unquhile Neill and Neill Montgomery then of Langschaw (Lainshaw) her brother whereby in cont
2 CONC emplation of the marriage to be solemnised between Hew Montgomery, younger and Marion Montgomery, Hew Montgomery, elder binds himself to infeft Marion Montgomery, future spouse to his said son in liferent during all the days of he
2 CONC r lifetime in the just and equal half of the lands of Auchinhud, the just and equal half of the 16s 8d land of Park and the just and equal half of the 20s 4d land of old extent of Bordland both lying in the parish of Eaglesham and
2 CONC  sheriffdom of Renfrew and to infeft Hew Montgomery, younger and the heirs male lawfully to be proceate between him and his future spouse, which failing the said Hew Montgomery, younger his heirs male and assignees whomsoever heri
2 CONC tably in the haill lands of Auchinhood, Park and Bordland, reserving always to Hew Montgomery, elder and Janet Peebles, his spouse their liferent of the said half of the said lands which was not provided to the said Marion Montgom
2 CONC ery. Dated at Irvine. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f45%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hugh+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, P
2 CONC apers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference 9 June 1622]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 and 14 April 1654: Extract disposition by Neill Montgomery of Langschaw with consent of John Montgomery, younger, of Langschaw, his eldest son, and Margaret Lockhart, his spouse, to David Montgomery of Cockilbie, of 10 merkla
2 CONC nd of Langschaw and others in bailiery of Cuninghame, sheriffdom of Air, and others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH15%2f44%2f154&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+lockhart&ko=p&r
