3 TEXT Eaglesham generations Lord Montgomerie The third lord was created Earl of Eglintoun in 1507 and Hugh the fifth Earl dying in 1612 the title went to his nephew Sir Alexander Se ton The representation of the male line then reverted 
4 CONC to the heirs of the next son of the first Earl who was Mr Niel Montgomery of Lainsliaw His grandson Niel had sons Niel of Lainshaw and William of Brigend 1652 William had John who had Hugh who had William of Brigand This last was 
4 CONC the emigrant to New Jersey about 1710 The Lainshaw line expired in the person of John who died between 1669 and 1687 at least there is every reason to believe that he had no children That estate however went to the heirs of two yo
4 CONC unger branch by purchase and the American family being overlooked the representation was supposed to have gone with it J he emigrant however seems to have valued his pedigree highly and to have preserved the records so that we bel
4 CONC ieve the claim is well substantiated and that we may say that the present head of the family is John T Montgomery of Philadelphia 
