1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>George Montgomerie of Skelmorlie</strong>, was under age at his father's death, and his wardship was assigned by the crown to Lady Catherine Montgomerie, youngest daughter of the first Earl of Eglinton. This lady afterwar
2 CONC ds became his wife. In 1535, his name occurs as one of the assize on the trial of Patrick and Adam Colquhoun, brothers of the Laird of Luss, for being concerned in the slaughter of William Stirling of Glorat. He had two sons, and 
2 CONC died in 1561."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhist00mont#page/136/mode/2up A genealogical history of the family of Montgomery]; by Thomas Harrison Montgomery; 1863; page 137
