2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 March 1564: Charter granted in obedience to a decree arbitral by Hugh Montgomery of Stane in favour of John Fairly of that ilk his heirs and assignees of his lands called Bowhous of old extent lying in the lordship of Stane i
2 CONC n special warrandice to relieve John his heirs executors and assignees of the whole of his intromissions with the rents and duties of 20 merks of old extent of the lands of Dreghorn in whatever way intromitted with by John of the 
2 CONC years 1547 and 1558 and interevening years at the hands of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Hugh Montgomery of Auchinhood and any others whomsoever having interest; tohold in special warrandice of him and his heirs in blench for payment ye
2 CONC arly of a penny Scots on the ground of the said lands in name of blench farm if asked only. Dated at the burgh of Irvine. [Charter granted in obedience to a decree arbitral by Hugh Montgomery of Stane in favour of John Fairly of t
2 CONC hat ilk his heirs and assignees of his lands called Bowhous of old extent lying in the lordship of Stane in special warrandice to relieve John his heirs executors and assignees of the whole of his intromissions with the rents and 
2 CONC duties of 20 merks of old extent of the lands of Dreghorn in whatever way intromitted with by John of the years 1547 and 1558 and interevening years at the hands of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Hugh Montgomery of Auchinhood and any oth
2 CONC ers whomsoever having interest; tohold in special warrandice of him and his heirs in blench for payment yearly of a penny Scots on the ground of the said lands in name of blench farm if asked only. Dated at the burgh of Irvine. [h
2 CONC ttps://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f15%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=auchinhood&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Ear
2 CONC ls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/10/15/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1570: Charter granted by Hugh Montgomery of Stane and Margaret Montgomery, his spouse with consent of Laurence Lyn of Bourtrehill in favour of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Lord Montgomery and Dame Agnes Drummond, his spouse and the 
2 CONC longest liver of them two in conjunct infeftment, their heirs and assignees of the superiority of the said lands: to hold of the King as Prince and Stewart of Scotland for payment yearly of a penny Scots at the feast of Whitsunday
2 CONC  on the ground of the said lands in name of blench farm if asked only. Witnesses: Robert Ker of Kersland, Hugh Montgomery of Auchinhood, [ ], Hugh Montgomery of Stane, Peter Montgomery, Robert Craufurd, Alexander Michell and James
2 CONC  McIntairis. Signed by Margaret Montgomery in her own hand, notary Robert Craufurd. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f67%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=auchinhood&ko=p&r=&
2 CONC ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/67/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1570: Procuratory of resignation granted by Hugh Montgomery and his spouse, with consent of Laurence Lyn for resigning the superiority of the said lands in the hands of the King as Prince and Stewart of Scotland or in the hands
2 CONC  of Matthew, Earl of Levinax, Lord Darnly, Regent as in the hands of the superior in favour of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, his spouse and the longest liver of them two in conjunct infeftment. Witnesses: Robert Kerr of Kerrisland, Hugh
2 CONC  Montgomery of Auchinhuid, Thomas Montgomery, brother german of Hugh Montgomery of Stane and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f67%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+A
2 CONC uchinhuid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/67/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 September 1570: Assignation by Hugh Montgomery, Laird of Stane in favour of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton of a reversion by Hugh Montgomery of Auchinhuid and Bessie Blair, hi spouse for redemption of an annualrent of 20 merks furth 
2 CONC of the two merk land of Bowhouse lying within the lordship of Stane on payment of 100 merks dated at Irvine 24 March 1572; another reversion made by Hugh Montgomery of Auchinhuid and his spouse to Hugh Montgomery, Laird of Stane a
2 CONC nd his spouse, their heirs and assignees for redemption of an annualrent of 20 merks Scots furth of the said lands upon payment of 200 merks. Dated at Irvine, 8 Sept 1570 and a reversion granted by William Berclay of Perstoun and 
2 CONC Margaret Montgomery, his spouse made to unquhile Arthur Montgomery, Laird of Stane for the redemption of the 20s land called Fensydik and Litilbrydis Kirk on payment of 8 score merks dated [ ] 1546. Date of the assignation at Egli
2 CONC nton. Witnesses: Gawand Baillie in Garthamlock, son of Alexander Baillie of Carfyn, Hugh Montgomery, sometime of the Gard and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f66&
2 CONC st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+Auchinhuid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/66]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 April 1574: Instrument of Sasine under the hand of John Mvr, clerk of the diocese of Glasgow, notary public, following upon and narrating a precept from the chancery of King James VI (dated at Edinburgh 2nd February a.r. 7, 
2 CONC 1573-4) addressed to the bailie of Conynghame and his deputes, for infefting John Dunlope as heir of Henry Dunlope, his father, in 1/7th part of the nine merklands of old extent of Watterlandis and Halkattis, lying in the parish o
2 CONC f Dunlope, bailiary of Conynghame and sheriffdom of Air, taking security for £96:10:6 for the ferms of said lands which were in the hands of the Crown for the space of 17 years or thereby (viz:- for 17 years by reason of ward and 
2 CONC for one year without sasine being recovered) and for £5: 6: 8 of relief. Sasine given by Hugh Montgomerie of Auchinhuid, bailie depute of Conynghame, on 22nd April 1574, upon the ground of the lands of Watterlandis. [https://catal
2 CONC ogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f238&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+Auchinhuid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/238]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 September 1589: Transference by Hew Montgomery, younger of Auchinhuid having the full right of the ward, relief and non entry of the foresaid lands of Lochliboside (disponed to him and unquhile Dorothy Sempill his deceased sp
2 CONC ouse and to the longest liver of them two by Robert, Master of Eglinton, assignee of Sir John Maitland of Thirlestane, secretary to the King and Master Thomas Lyoun of Balduky, Master of Glamis, the King's treasurer equal and prin
2 CONC cipal donators to the King of the ward of all lands which pertained of before to the deceased Hew, Earl of Eglinton, holden by him of the King for services of ward and relief of which the said lands of Lochliboside are part) in fa
2 CONC vour of Robert Montgomery of Skelmorlie his heirs and assignees one or more of the ward of the foresaid lands since the death of the unquhile Earl until the lawful entry of the righteous heir or heirs thereto being of lawful and p
2 CONC erfect age with the relief thereof when it should happen. Dated at the burgh of Irvine. Witnesses: John Montgomery of Brigend and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f7%2
2 CONC f7%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=auchinhood&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/7/7/13]'''
2 CONT
