2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 August 1559: Instrument of Sasine by Thomas Kennedy of Bargany propitis manibus to his sister Jonet Kennedy wife of John Mure of Cauldwell, in liferent and to the heirs lawfully begotton of her and the said John heritably of
2 CONC  the above subjects. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f18&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Famil
2 CONC y of Bennan and Finnarts, reference GD60/18]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 July 1562: Letter of reversion granted by Jonet Kennedy, spouse to John Mure of Caulduell with his consent, whereby she declares that although Hugh, Earl of Eglinton had sold to her, her heirs and assignees, an annualrent of
2 CONC  50 merks Scots furth of the barony of Robertoun, yet on the said Earl paying to her 500 merks in the parish kirk of Irvine on 40 days warning before any term of Whitsunday or Martinmas she would discharge the said annualrent. [ht
2 CONC tps://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f57%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family
2 CONC , Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/57/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Books of the Town Clerks of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 November 1567: "In presens of me, notar and witnes underwrittin, personalie comperit Andro Arbukle, Johne Warnok, and Robert Cowper, tenentis in Westir Kittokside, and in presens of David Lyndsaye of Kittokside, of thair awn
2 CONC e consentis, dividit thair malyngis thairof, and wes content to stand to the samyn divisioun in all tymes cuming during thair lyvetymes; quhilk persones thre malynges ar of the v merkland of Wester Kittokside, on the south side of
2 CONC  ten merk land of Westir Kittokside, pertenyng heretablie to Johne Mure of Calduell, knycht, as eftir followis, viz., the said Robert Cowper, for his quarter of the said v merkland, extending to 16 s. 8 d. land, to ly in the Caste
2 CONC lhill Quarter nixt adjacent to the myldam, with the pertinentis, tofting, crofting and inland, conforme to the merchis affixt thairto; and that for the said Robertis malyng, he biggand his pairt of the merche dykis, and using wthe
2 CONC r nychtbourheid as nychtbouris suld do. And the saidis Andro Arbukle and Johne Warnok, ilkane of thame haveand xxv s. land of the samyn Hand in the nether pairt thairof, betuix the Castlehill and Cadzilburne, the said Androis xxv 
2 CONC s. land Hand on the west pairt of the said v merkland, wp and downe thu Cadzillmriiesido; and .lohne Warnokis xxv s. land Hand in the mid jiairt of the said v merkland rownd about the crukit bank, with half waiter of Cadzilburne, 
2 CONC betuix Michaelmes and Aprile yeirlie, he makand half labour thairfore, and als the draucht of the watter fra the Henry raedo to cum unstoppit to the said .Johne Warnokis pairt; togidder to ilkane of thaim tofting, crofting and inl
2 CONC and pertenyng to thair malvngis respective, conforme to the merchis sett and affixt be thair consentis thairupon. And ilkane of the saidis thre persones to keip nychtbourheid to wtheris lik fis thai aucht and suld do in all sortes
2 CONC . And heirto thai oblist thame ilkane of thame to wtheris to abide at the samyn but fraude and gyle. Upone the quhilkis ilkane of thame requirit instrumentis of me notar underwrittin. This wes done in the tolbuyth of Glasgw about 
2 CONC thre eftir none or thairby befoir thir witnes: the said David Lyndsay, Patrik Laucht, tailyour, Mungo Knok, fischer, and Johiio Wilsoun in Kittokside." [https://archive.org/details/abstractsofproto05glas/page/98/mode/1up Glasgow P
2 CONC rotocols V: protocol number 1572]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/abstractsofproto05glas/page/n8/mode/1up Abstracts of Protocols of the Town Clerks of Glasgow. Edited by Robert Renwick, Depute Town Clerk. Vol. V. Henry Gibsone's Protocols, 1555-1568. (Carson & Nic
2 CONC ol, Glasgow, MDCCCXCVII.), 135 pp. including indices]'''
2 CONT
