2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 October 1509: Charter by which William Schaw of Polkemmet confirms that he has sold the two merk land of old extent of Dalloy in the Bailliery of Kyle and sheriffdom of Ayr, to George Campbell of Cessnock. On 6 February 1522
2 CONC  possession of this land was confirmed to John Campbell, son and heir of the deceased George Campbell of Cessnock by a charter issued under the Great Seal of Scotland. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/48/mo
2 CONC de/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 218]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 November 1510: A Lettre maid to GEORGE CAMPBELL of Sexnock, for his gude and thankfull service done to the king,— of  the gift  of xl  lib. to be pait to him be the thesaurare that now is and beis for the tyme, of the coffer
2 CONC is, at the termez of Martimes and Witsonday and quhill he be rewardit be the king for his service,  etc. Per Signaturam.  xs. iv. 94. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/329/mode/1up RSSRS 1488-1529: entry 
