1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===4===
2 CONT John Schaw of Alva, who, with his father, had an appointment from the King for the custody of Stirling Castle on 20 January, 1489. He held the office of Sheriff of Clackmannan which he resigned in favour of Sir William Menteith of
2 CONC  Kerse who had a charter of confirmation on 25 September, 1489.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Northern Notes & Queries, Volumes 1-4 page 9 [https://books.google.com/books?id=YNtZAAAAIAAJ&dq=christian%20bruce%20james%20schaw&pg=RA1-PA9#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Schaw of Knockhill, the father of Margaret Schaw or Younger, was grandson of John Schaw of Alva and Knockhill, second son of Sir James Schaw of Sauchie (alive 1483), who was grandson of Sir James Schaw of Greenock, who marr
2 CONC ied Mary, second daughter and co-heiress of Islay de Annand of Sauchie, who was the lineal descendant of Islay de Annand (alive 1296). See ‘General Notes anent some Ancient Scottish Families, by David Marshall, F.S.A.Scot., privat
2 CONC ely printed.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * “Genealogical notes anent some ancient Scottish families, with index.” By David Marshall. “Schaw of Sauchie.” Pedigree, Page 119.  [https://archive.org/details/anent1884/page/119/mode/1up  Archive.Org] Page 104.  [https://archiv
2 CONC e.org/details/anent1884/page/104/mode/1up Archive.Org] Page 108 [https://archive.org/details/anent1884/page/108/mode/1up Archive.Org] Margaret Shaw might have been aunt to Alexander Shaw of Sauchy.
