1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR WILLIAM EDMONSTONE OF DUNTREATH ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath is reported to have died in 1486. He cerainly died before 20 April 1487, the date upon which his son, Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, was served heir to his deceased father. [https://a
2 CONC rchive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/33/mode/1up Duntreath: 33]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/parishofstrathbl00smit#page/102/mode/1up John Guthrie Smith, FSA (Scot).,The Parish of Strathblane and its Inhabitants from Early Times : A Chapter of Lennox History (Glasgow : James Maclehose and 
2 CONC Sons, Publishers to the University, 1886), pp. 102-24]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ee/edmonstone1.php Stirnet: Edmonstone 1]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ee/edmonstone2.php Stirnet: Edmonstone 2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=179005751-8-9339&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-4b48e0dfd693fdff2adc0a389f71d2c5&mrid=1b89a2323fd2812713c32bcb6c8042eb MyHe
2 CONC ritage Family Trees] via daughter [http://www.geni.com/profile-34677600271 Mariote Edmonstone] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 3 2015, 5:25:49 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=535803-16-5616&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-3110377944c892dbc420ef25e9aa9035&mrid=f5ae143337ba84ce6ba2c5a47e274618 MyHeri
2 CONC tage Family Trees] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 3 2015, 5:28:36 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Sir William Edmonstone1 
2 CONT *M, #65494
2 CONT *Father      Sir William de Edmonstone, Captain of Threave Castle1 d. c 1460
2 CONT *Mother     Mary Stewart1 b. c 1378, d. a Feb 1462
2 CONT *''''''     Sir William Edmonstone was born at of Duntreath, Stirlingshire, Scotland.1 He married Matilda Stewart, daughter of Sir James 'the Gross' Stewart, Master of Lennox and (Miss) MacDonald.1
2 CONT *''''''Family      Matilda Stewart 
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir Archibald Edmonstone, 3rd Laird Edmonstone+1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 908.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2180.htm#i65494
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William, 2nd of Duntreath, 1460-1486.*
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Matilda, dau. of Lord James Stewart (surviving son of Murdoch, Duke of Albany.)
2 CONT
2 CONT By her he had 6 sons & 1 daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT     1  Sir Archibald who succeeded him.
2 CONT
2 CONT     2  James. 
2 CONT
2 CONT         m. 1stly Elizabeth, dau & heiress of Alexander Cunningham of Polmaise,
2 CONT
2 CONT         m. 2ndly Helen, dau of John Murray of Touchadam.
2 CONT
2 CONT     3  James, Became Prior of Collegiate church of Kirkheugh at St. Andrews.
2 CONT
2 CONT     4  John. m. dau. of Sir John Stewart of Ardgowan & Blackhall.
2 CONT
2 CONT     5  George.
2 CONT
2 CONT     6  William, deputy-master of household to James IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT and
2 CONT
2 CONT     1 daughter, m. Lawrence, 1st Lord Oliphant..
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William died in 1486 & was succeeded by his eldest son
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.edmonstone.com/
2 CONT
