2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 July 1493: Witnesses: Arch. Edmondstoun de Duntrith, and Jac. Edmondstoun de Polmays, and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/466/mode/1up RMS: 2205]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 April 1495: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/476/mode/1up RMS: 2249]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 August 1505: Attested copy special retour in favour of John Haldene [Haldane] of Glenegas [Gleneagles], kt., as heir of deceased James Haldene [Haldane] of Glenegas [Gleneagles], kt., his father, in half lands of Thome, half 
2 CONC lands of three Lanerkynnis [Lanrick], half 4 merkland of land of old called Conlathe, now called Schaquhythome with fishing of water of Tethe [River Teith] and half mill of Lanerk and its aquaduct, with half of lands of Rusky [Rus
2 CONC kie] and lands of Auchinreg, in stewartry of Menteth [Menteith], sheriffdom of Perth. Sheriff of Perth: William Edmonstone [Edmiston] of Duntreth [Duntreath], stewart of Menteth. Members of inquest; Alexander, earl of Menteth, Dun
2 CONC can Forrest of Gardoun [Garden], JJAMES EDMONSTONE [EDMISTON] OF BUCHQUHADROK, Walter Forrest of Torwod [Torwood], Robert More [Muir] of Boquhoppil [Boquhapple], Patrick Menteth [Menteith] of Ratho, Robert Balfour of Boquhoppil [B
2 CONC oquhapple], William Menteth [Menteith] of Gallecat, James Stewart of Garthael, John Kinlouch [Kinloch] of Broklands [Brooklands], James Dog [Doig] of Domrobyne, James Menteth [Monteith], Walter Laur, Patrick Stewart, Patrick Bouch
2 CONC quhanane [Buchanan] of Lane [Leny], Alexander Balfour and George Stewart. Copy attested by Thomas Miller, substitute for James Dundas, depute of James St. Clair Erskine, earl of Rosslyn, director of chancery. [http://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f69&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+edmonstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Haldane Family of Gleneagles, Perthshire, re
2 CONC ference GD198/69]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 February 1510: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/791/mode/1up RMS: 3660]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 February 1511-12: Instrument of resignation by Helen Murray, spouse of James Edmondstoun of Buchquhadroch, with consent of her husband, in hands of Oliver Sinclare of Rosling, kt., lord of the barony of Herbertschir, of 40s. 
2 CONC lands lying in the town and territory of Donypace in said barony, sheriffdom of Striveling. Notary: Alexander Kowe, priest of St. Andrews diocese. Witnesses: Alexander Levingstoun of Donypace, Edward Spittaill, notary public, Andr
2 CONC ew [Stewart], residing with said James Edmondstoun in his service, sir Robert Edmondstoun, sir William Anderson, chaplains, Robert Sinclare, James Sinclare, Matthew Sinclare, John Mude, James Murray, and John Bichat. [http://catal
2 CONC ogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f529%2f23&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Buchquhadroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Title Deeds and other papers relating to Dunipace, St
2 CONC irlingshire, reference GD1/529/23]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 February 1511-12: Instrument of sasine in favour of Helen Murray and James Edmondstoun of Buchquhadroch, her spouse, and the survivor in conjunct infeftment of lands specified in GD1/529/23. Notary: Alexander Kowe, priest of 
2 CONC St. Andrews diocese. Witnesses: Alexander Levingstoun of Donypaiss, sir Robert Edmondstoun and sir William Andersoun, chaplains, Robert Sinclare, James Sinclare, Matthew Sinclare, John Mude, James Murray, Andrew Steward and John B
2 CONC ichat. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f529%2f24&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Buchquhadroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Title Deeds and other papers rela
2 CONC ting to Dunipace, Stirlingshire, reference GD1/529/24]'''
