1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == NINIAN ROSS, Lord Ross of Hawkhead ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ninian Ross, Lord Ross of Hawkhead, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Ross-2nd-Lord-of-Halkhead/6000000002188078971?through=6000000003646015147 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Christian-Edmonstone/60000000
2 CONC 05069829346?through=6000000003646015147. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/251/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 251]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ninian Ross, Lord Ross of Hawkhead, died in February 1555-56. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/251/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 251]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 December 1523: Charter by which Ninian, Lord Ross and Melville, confirms that he has given certain lands to Elizabeth Ruthven, Countess of Errol. The lands in question were to be held by Elizabeth and the male heirs procreate
2 CONC d between her and Ninian, Lord Ross and Melville. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 12 December 1523. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/55/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 24
2 CONC 4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 October 1529: Ninian, Lord Ros of Halkheid served on an assize. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/270/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 1234, note 1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 February 1540-41: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James V, King of Scots, confirms possession of two tenements in the Burgh of Linlithgow to James Hamilton, son and heir apparent of James Hamilton, formerly 
2 CONC of Kincavill. the tenements in question lay on the south side of the burgh between the tenements belonging to Ninian, Lord Ross of Hawkhead, and John Thomson. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/516/mode/1up R
2 CONC MS 1513-46: charter number 2265]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot., and John Maitlan
2 CONC d Thomson, MA., Advocates. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1883), 1067 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility
2 CONC  of that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume VII. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1910), 592 pp.]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/qr/ross03.php Stirnet: Ross 03]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninian_Ross,_3rd_Lord_Ross Biographical Summary by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ross married four times:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Stewart, daughter of Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox
2 CONT
2 CONT (contract 12 December 1523) Elizabeth, youngest daughter of William Ruthven, 1st Lord Ruthven, and widow of 
2 CONT
2 CONT William, 5th Earl of Erroll
2 CONT
2 CONT (contract 9 December 1529) Elizabeth Stewart, daughter of the Earl of Atholl and widow of the Earl of Lennox
2 CONT     Janet Montgomery
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Ross had issue:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, Master of Ross, who was killed in 1547 at the Battle of Pinkie Cleugh and left a daughter, Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Ross, 4th Lord Ross<br/>
2 CONT Hugh Ross<br/>
2 CONT William Ross
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Ross, who married first (1543) John Mure of Caldwell, secondly (5 November 1552) Nicholas Ramsay of Dalhousie and thirdly (before 8 July 1555) John Weir, and died before February 1556/7<br/>
2 CONT (a natural son) John Ross of Tartraven, ancestor of the family of Ross of Kirkland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT NINIAN, second lord Ross of Halk∣head, who, in the minority of king James V. was, by the estates of the nation, nominated one of the ambassadors to the court of France, to endeavour to get Scotland included in their treaty of peac
2 CONC e with the English,*anno 1515.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also one of the Scotch commissi∣oners at the court of England, when a peace was concluded, anno 1534.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 1st,* lady Janet Stewart, daugh∣ter of John earl of Lennox, by whom he had a son,
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, master of Ross, who was slain at the battle of Pinkie, anno 1547, his father being then alive, leaving issue a daughter, E∣lizabeth, married to John lord Fleming;* he had also another daughter Agnes, married to John Boyle 
2 CONC of Kelburn, ancestor of the earl of Glasgow.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 2dly, Elizabeth, daughter of William lord Ruthven, widow of William fifth earl of Errol, by whom he had a son,
2 CONT
2 CONT XIII. JAMES, who succeeded to his father's estate and honours, and was third lord Ross of Halkhead.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896980.0001.000/1:212?rgn=div1;view=fulltext
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses/Children: 1. Stewart, Janet [766]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ross, Robert Master of Ross [28537]
2 CONT     Ross, dau. [28538]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Ruthven, Elizabeth [7278]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ross, James 4th Lord of Halkhead [2880]+
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Stuart, Elizabeth (or Anne) [773]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/in.ernet.dli.2015.210885/2015.210885.The-Complete#page/n609/mode/2up/search/Ross
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Unknown, Partner(s) [28540]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ross, Christian [8457]+
2 CONT     Ross, Hugh (4th son) [28541]
2 CONT     Ross, William (5th son) [28542
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://clanmacfarlane.100megsfree5.com/775.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I775&tree=CC 1 - Lady Janet Stuart (later Lady Ross of Halkhead), who was born circa 1499 and married Ninian, third Lord Ross of Halkhead. They ha
2 CONC d a charter dated 15 November 1515 (he later married the twelfth earl's widow). 2 - Ninian ROSS of Halkhead b. C 1482; d. Feb 1555/56 occ: 3rd Lord Ross of Halkhead m1. Janet STEWART of Lennox children of Ninian ROSS and Janet STE
2 CONC WART: Robert, Master of Ross; unknown female m. MONCRIEF m2. contract 12 Dec 1523 Elizabeth RUTHVEN children of Ninian ROSS and Elizabeth RUTHVEN: James m3. contract 09 Dec 1529 Anne STEWART of Atholl m4. Janet MONTGOMERY other ch
2 CONC ildren of Ninian ROSS: Hugh (4th son); William (5th son); Christian m1. John MURE of Caldwell, m2. Nicholas RAMSAY of Dalhousie, m3. John WEIR
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT BARONY of ROSS of HALKHEAD (III) 1513
2 CONT
2 CONT Ninian Ross, Lord Ross of Halkhead, 1st son and heir, had sasine of the barony of Melville, of lands in Renfrew, and of Tarbert, 24 Oct and 24 Nov 1513, 24 Feb 1513/4; PC before 12 Jul 1514; sat frequently as a Lord of Parliament 
2 CONC from 1515 to 1540; one of the nobles, who, in 1515, despatched Ambassadors to France to endeavor to arrange for Scotland to be included in the pacification with England; summoned to be at Deridounlaws to resist the English, 25 Jun
2 CONC  1523; protested against Albany's departure for France, 25 May 1524; one of the Lords to accompany James V to the south parts of the realm, 27 Jun 1526; ratified a treaty with England, 30 Jun 1534; witnessed the ratification of th
2 CONC e forfeiture of John Lyon, Lord Glamis, 10 Dec 1540; summoned before the PC for "deforsing" two messengers, 13 Sep 1553.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 1stly, before 15 Nov 1515, when they had a charter of the lands of Tarbert, co. Ayr, Janet, probably a daughter of Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox. He m. 2ndly (contract 12 Dec 1523), Elizabeth, widow of William Hay, 5th
2 CONC  Earl of Erroll, youngest daughter of William Ruthven, 1st Lord Ruthven, by his 2nd wife, Christian, only daughter of William Forbes, 3rd Lord Forbes. She d. before 20 Jul 1529. He m. 3rdly (contract 9 Dec 1529), Elizabeth, widow 
2 CONC of John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Lennox, daughter of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl, uterine brother of James II, by his 2nd wife, Eleanor, daughter of William Sinclair, 1st Earl of Caithness. He m. 4thly, Janet Montgomery, who surv
2 CONC ived him. He d. in Feb 1555/6. [Complete Peerage XI:157-8]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of his father at the Battle of Flodden Field, Ross had by 1514 obtained sasines of his father's lands in Melville, Renfrew and Tarbert. He attended the parliaments of James V of Scotland frequently over the nex
2 CONC t 25 years. On 30 June 1534 he ratified Scotland's peace treaty with England. He was frequently present in the Parliaments of King James V between 1515 and 1540. Son of the 2nd Lord and Christian Edmonstone (b.?, d.1551), daughter
2 CONC  of Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath. He was married four times, the first three being to daughters of peers.
