2 CONT Name Meaning
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Scottish:
2 CONT
2 CONT from Older Scots baillie, baili. In Scotland, a baillie was a status name for any of various officials, including the chief magistrate in a barony and (later) the chief magistrate or administrative officer of a barony or district.
2 CONC  Etymologically, this is the same word as English Bailey , but the functions as well as the spelling of the two officials were different in England and Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT topographic name from Older Scots bailli ‘outer court of a castle’; see Bailey 3 and Bale 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dictionary of American Family Names © Patrick Hanks 2003, 2006.
