2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 June 1574: Charter by which James Edmonstoun of Ballingtone confirms that he has given the 20 merk land of Buchquhoppill and the 6 merk land of Cessintullie alias Ballingtone in the Stewartry of Menteith to his daughter Marj
2 CONC orie Edmonstoun and her husband Archibald Edmonstoun, portioner of Spittaltoun. His charter follows from a contact of marriage dated 22 August 1573. The lands in question were to be held by Archibald and Marjorie in conjunct fee a
2 CONC nd liferent, and by their legitimate heirs in fee, whom failing by Marjorie's lawful heirs, whom failing by Archibald's heirs and assignees. James Edmonstoun of Ballingtone reserved his own liferent and the terce of his wife Barba
2 CONC re Muschat. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 3 February 1575-76. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/674/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 2508]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 December 1608: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/800/mode/1up RMS: 2180]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 January 1613: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland which confirms possession of certain lands to Alexander Menteith, including the forty shilling land of Cammusbeg-Wester, located in the Stewartry of Menteith and sheriff
2 CONC dom of Perth, which had previously been resigned by Archibald Edmonstoun of Ballintone, his wife Marjorie Edmonstoun, and his eldest son and apparent heir John Edmonstoun: "quas Arch. Edmonstoun de Ballintone et Marjoria Edmonstou
2 CONC n ejus sponsa et Jo. E. eorum filius natu maximus et heres apparens resignaverunt". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/296/mode/1up RMS 1609-20: charter number 797]
