2 CONT F, #21438
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Janet Hepburn||p2144.htm#i21438|Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell|d. 18 Oct 1508|p10827.htm#i108262|Lady Janet Douglas|d. b 1490|p10827.htm#i108261|Adam Hepburn, Master of Hailes|b. c 1435\nd. c 1479|p482.htm#i4812|Helen 
2 CONC Home|d. a 1512|p482.htm#i4813|James Douglas, 1st Earl of Morton|d. 1493|p10825.htm#i108246|Joan Stewart|b. c 1428\nd. a 16 Oct 1486|p10533.htm#i105328|
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=25 Apr 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT      Lady Janet Hepburn was the daughter of Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell and Lady Janet Douglas.1 She married George Seton, 3rd Lord Seton, son of George Seton, 2nd Lord Seton and Lady Margaret Campbell, before 25 January
2 CONC  1506/7.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      From before 25 January 1506/7, her married name became Seton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Janet Hepburn and George Seton, 3rd Lord Seton
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton, 4th Lord Seton+ d. 17 Jul 15492 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariot Seton+ 3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Seton 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 572. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peera
2 CONC ge and Baronetage, 107th edition. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 1285. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct 
2 CONC or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 222. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Seton,_5th_Lord_Seton) says:
2 CONT
2 CONT Before January 1507, George Seton married Lady Janet Hepburn, daughter of Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell. They had one surviving son, who later succeeded as 6th Lord Seton, and a daughter, Mariota (or Marion), who married, 
2 CONC firstly Thomas, Master of Borthwick, secondly in 1530 she married Hugh Montgomerie, 2nd Earl of Eglinton, and thirdly, Alexander Graham of Wallacetown.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Flodden, Lady Seton lived as a widow for another forty-five years. A pious lady, she continued to make gifts to Seton Church, and had new extensions built. When her son, the young Lord Seton, came of age, she retired to the 
2 CONC Convent of Saint Catherine of Siena, at Edinburgh. This convent, founded 1517 by a bull of Pope Leo X, also benefited from Lady Seton's donations. She died there in 1558 and was buried next to her husband at Seton.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lady Janet Hepburn (born between 1481 and 1490; died after 10 May 1558) was the daughter of Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell and Lady Janet Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married George Seton, 3rd Lord Seton, son of George Seton, 2nd Lord Seton and Lady Margaret Campbell, before  25 January 1506/7. Her husband died at the Battle of Flodden in 1513. She later lived at the at Convent of St. Cathe
2 CONC rine of Sienna, Edinburgh, where she died. after 10 May 1558.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Jane (Janet) Hepburn was the daughter of Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell, and Janet Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband, George Seton, died at the Battle of Flodden Field. Lady Seton lived as a widow for another forty-five years. A pious lady, she continued to make gifts to Seton Church, and had new extensions built.
2 CONT
2 CONT When her son, the young Lord Seton, came of age, she retired to the Convent of Saint Catherine of Siena, at Edinburgh. This convent, founded 1517 by a bull of Pope Leo X, also benefited from Lady Seton's donations. She died there 
2 CONC in 1558 and then was buried next to her husband at Seton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Janet Hepburn and George Seton, 3rd Lord Seton
2 CONT
2 CONT George - died infant George Seton 4th Lord Seton died 17th July 1549 Archibald - died young Marion (Mariot) Seton
