2 CONT === George Seton III, 5th Lord Seton
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Seton,_5th_Lord_Seton
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton III, 5th Lord Seton (died 1513) was a Scottish nobleman.'' He is sometimes referred to as the 3rd Lord Seton because he was the 3rd Lord Seton with the name of George.''
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his father, the 4th Lord, on his death in 1508. During his brief tenure he carried out works at Seton Palace, the family seat in East Lothian, and made further donations to Seton Collegiate Church, which had been esta
2 CONC blished by his ancestors.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Seton was a companion of King James IV of Scotland, and went with him on the expedition into England in 1513. This campaign ended at the disastrous [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Flodden Battle of Flodden Field], whe
2 CONC re on 9 September, King James and Lord Seton were among the thousands of Scots who were killed. Lord Seton's body was returned to Scotland and interred at Seton Church beside that of his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Hepburn
2 CONT
2 CONT Before January 1507, George Seton married Lady Janet Hepburn, daughter of Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell. They had one surviving son, who later succeeded as 6th Lord Seton, and a daughter, Mariota (or Marion), who married, 
2 CONC firstly Thomas, Master of Borthwick, secondly in 1530 she married Hugh Montgomerie, 2nd Earl of Eglinton, and thirdly, Alexander Graham of Wallacetown.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Flodden, Lady Seton lived as a widow for another forty-five years. A pious lady, she continued to make gifts to Seton Church, and had new extensions built. When her son, the young Lord Seton, came of age, she retired to the 
2 CONC Convent of Saint Catherine of Siena, at Edinburgh. This convent, founded 1517 by a bull of Pope Leo X, also benefitted from Lady Seton's donations. She died here in 1558 and was buried next to her husband at Seton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations 
2 CONT #"George Seton, '''5th Lord''' Seton". The House of Seton of Scotland Family Website. Retrieved 3 September 2010. < [http://www2.thesetonfamily.com:8080/directory/Descents/lords_seton_descent.htm link] > 
2 CONT #"George Seton, '''3rd Lord''' Seton". thepeerage.com. Retrieved 3 September 2010. < [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2144.htm#i21433 link] >
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www2.thesetonfamily.com:8080/directory/Descents/lords_seton_descent.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT GEORGE SETON, LORD SETON
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton, 5th Lord Seton (d Flodden 09.09.1513),   and 3rd to be called "of the name George". 
2 CONT * m. (before 12.1506) Janet Hepburn (d 10.05.1558, dau of Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell) 
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton, 5th Lord Seton was the son of George (Seton) Seton, 4th Lord Seton and Lady Margaret Campbell.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lady Janet Hepburn, daughter of Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell and Lady Janet (Douglas) Hepburn, before Dec 1506.[1] They had issue:[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT #     George - died in infancy 
2 CONT #     George - heir 
2 CONT #     Archibald - died young 
2 CONT #     Marion - m. 1st Thomas, Master of Borthwick (annulled), m. 2nd Hugh Montgomerie, Master of Eglinton. , m. 3rd Alexander Graham of Wallastoun. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Seton on 25 Jan 1506/7.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Flodden at Flodden Field, Northumberland, England, and was killed in action on 9 September 1513
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2144.htm#i21433
2 CONT
2 CONT *George Seton, [3rd to be named George] 5th Lord Seton  
2 CONT *M, #21433, d. 9 September 1513
2 CONT *Last Edited=25 Apr 2008
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=2.59%
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton, 3rd Lord Seton was the son of George Seton, 2nd Lord Seton and Lady Margaret Campbell.1 He married Lady Janet Hepburn, daughter of Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell and Lady Janet Douglas, before 25 January 1506/
2 CONC 7.2 He died on 9 September 1513 at Flodden Field, Northumberland, England, killed in action.1
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton, 3rd Lord Seton succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Seton [S., 1451] circa 1507.1 He fought in the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of George Seton, 3rd Lord Seton and Lady Janet Hepburn
2 CONT
2 CONT # George Seton, 4th Lord Seton+ d. 17 Jul 15491  
2 CONT # Mariot Seton+ 3  
2 CONT # Margaret Seton 1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/105735750/george-seton
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton III, 5th Lord Seton was a Scottish nobleman. He is sometimes referred to as the 3rd Lord Seton because he was the 3rd Lord Seton with the name of George.
2 CONT
2 CONT He carried out his role at Seton Palace, the family seat in East Lothian. He also made significant contributions to the Seton Collegiate Church, which had been established by his ancestors.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton was with King James IV of Scotland, on the expedition into England in 1513. This campaign ended at the disastrous Battle of Flodden Field, where on Sep. 9, 1513, King James and Seton were among the thousands of Scots 
2 CONC who were killed. Lord Seton's body was returned to Scotland and interred at Seton Church beside that of his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton had married Lady Janet Hepburn, daughter of Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell in 1507. They had one surviving son, who later succeeded as 6th Lord Seton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton is buried at the Seton Collegiate Churchyard located on Fishergate Road, Tranent, East Lothian, Scotland, AND NOT AT Seton Church, Port Seton, East Lothian, Scotland, United Kingdom
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
