2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 222. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage
2 CONT #A Genealogical History of the Dormant: Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages of the British Empire By Sir Bernard Burke, LL.D., Ulster King of Arms, [etc.]. London:  Harrison, 59, Pall Mall, Bookseller to Her Majesty and H.R.R
2 CONC . the Prince of Wales.  1866.  page 486.  SETON -- BARONS SETON AND EARLS OF WINTOUN.   Earldom, by Charter, dated 16 November, 1600.  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=K3MaAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA486#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] >; 
2 CONC  [MTD] < [https://archive.org/details/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog/page/486/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] > 
