2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT George Seton, 4th Lord Seton was the son of George Seton, 3rd Lord Seton and Lady Janet Hepburn. He married, firstly, Elizabeth Hay, daughter of John Hay, 3rd Lord Hay of Yester and Elizabeth Douglas, circa 15 June 1527. He marrie
2 CONC d, secondly, Mary Pyerres circa February 1538/39. He died on 17 July 1549.  George succeeded to the title of 4th Lord Seton on 9 September 1513. He held the office of Extra Lord of Session in 1533. He was invested as a Privy Couns
2 CONC ellor (P.C.) [Scotland] in March 1542/43. He died in the abbey of Culross in July 17, 1549 and was buried there in the choir. At that time the English had invaded and occupied East Lothian When the English had left and peace was r
2 CONC estored his wife and friends removed his body from the Abbey and took it to Seton (Seytoun) where he was reburied in the choir of the college kirk, beside his father.  Succeeded by his son with his first wife.  Note: with the Scot
2 CONC tish Army before the Battle of Solway Moss 1542; fought at the Battle of Ancrum Moor 1544/5.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (1) circa. 15 Jun 1527 Hon. Elizabeth Hay, 1st daughter of John [Hay], 3rd Lord Hay of Yester, by his first wife Lady Elizabeth Douglas, sister of Archibald [Douglas], 6th Earl of Angus, and 1st daughter of Hon. George Dou
2 CONC glas, Master of Angus (by his wife Elizabeth Fleming, widow of Sir David Fleming of Monycabo and 2nd daughter of John [Drummond], 1st Lord Drummond), 1st son and heir apparent of Archibald [Douglas], 5th Earl of Angus.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by first wife 
2 CONT *     1. Hon. George Seton, later 5th Lord Seton. 
2 CONT *     2. Hon. John Seton of Cariston, mar. Isabel Balfour, niece and heiress of David Balfour of Carraldstoun, and had issue. 
2 CONT *     3. Hon. James Seton. (Note this seems an error to check) 
2 CONT *     4. Hon. Jean Seton (d. an infant.) 
2 CONT *     5. Hon. Marion Seton (d. 23 Jun 1567), mar. (1) after 8 Oct 1548 John [Graham], 4th Earl of Menteith, and (2) circa 1564 as his third wife John [Gordon], 11th Earl of Sutherland, and had issue by her first husband. 
2 CONT *     6. Hon. Margaret Seton (d. Jan 1564/5), mar. (1) after 10 Jan 1542/3 Robert Logan of Restalrig, and (2) David Hamilton of Ladyflat, son of Sir Robert Hamilton of Preston. 
2 CONT *     7. Hon. Beatrix Seton, mar. after 24 Feb 1556/7 George Ogilvy, 1st son and heir of Sir Walter Ogilvy of Dunlugus, and had issue. 
2 CONT *     8. Hon. Eleanor Seton (d. c. 1603), mar. after 11 Feb 1557 Hugh Somerville, 6th Lord Somerville, and had issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT mar. (2) circa Feb 1538/9 Marie Pierres, Lady-in-Waiting to Queen Mary of Lorraine (mar. (2) before 6 Oct 1554 Pierre de Clovis, Seigneur de Bryante; d. circa 1576), daughter of ..... Pierres. of Le Plessis Baudoin.  children by s
2 CONC econd wife 
2 CONT *     1. Hon. Robert Seton of Mylis (d. after 22 Feb 1562/3) 
2 CONT *     2. Hon. James Seton of Milton (d. before 29 Jan 1562/3) 
2 CONT *     3. Hon. Marie Seton (b. c. 1541; d. after 6 Apr 1615), a Maid-of-honour to Queen Mary I and later a nun at Rheims
