2 CONT She died on 9 April 1624.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Hugh Montgomerie, 3rd Earl of Eglinton and Agnes Drummond.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Seton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Margaret Montgomerie and Robert Seton, 1st Earl of Winton
2 CONT *1. Sir Thomas Seton2
2 CONT *2. Sir John Seton2
2 CONT *3. Robert Seton, 2nd Earl of Winton1 b. c 1583
2 CONT *4. George Seton, 3rd Earl of Winton+1 b. Dec 1584, d. fr 15 Dec 1650 - 17 Dec 1650
2 CONT *5. Alexander Montgomerie, 6th Earl of Eglinton+1 b. 1588, d. 7 Jan 1661
2 CONT *6. Lady Isabel Seton+2 b. 30 Nov 1593
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1280. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 1284.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT When Lady Margaret Montgomerie was born in 1566, in Beith, Ayrshire, Scotland, her father, Hugh Montgomerie, Third Earl Of Eglinton, was 35 and her mother, Agnes Drummond of Innerperrfray, was 43. She married Robert Seton Sixth Ea
2 CONC rl of Seton First Earl of Winton on 19 May 1583, in Ayrshire, Scotland. They were the parents of at least 11 sons and 4 daughters. She died on 9 April 1624, in Seton, Haddingtonshire, Scotland, at the age of 58, and was buried in 
2 CONC Port Seton, Haddingtonshire, Scotland, United Kingdom. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Thomas Seton 1578–1603 Isabel Seton of Winton, Countess of Perth 1579–1638 Isabel deSeton 1580–Deceased Robert Seton [2nd Earl of Winton] 1583–1609 Robert Seton 1583–1634 George Seton 3rd Earl Of Winton 1584–1650 Alexande
2 CONC r Seton 1588–1660 Alexander Seton Montgomery 6th Earl of Eglinton 1588–1661 Sir Thomas Seton 1589–1609 John Seton 1591–1634 Hugh Seton 1593–1669 Margaret Seton 1595–Deceased Margaret Seton 1595–Deceased Agnes Seton Deceased John S
2 CONC eton Deceased
