2 CONT '''20 May 1598: Instrument of Resignation and Sasine under the hand of John Masoun, town clerk of Air, notary public, narrating that John Mure of Auchendrane, in implement of a contract (of even date herewith) entered into between
2 CONC  him, on the one part, and Adam Johnestoun, burgess of Air, and Giles Fergushill, his spouse, on the other part, and in consideration of the sum of £1000 Scots paid to him, resigned one-half of his 20 shilling land of old extent o
2 CONC f Twastanecroce with meadow and pertinents, which he now occupies and formerly had in tack, lying in the territory of the Burrowfeild of the burgh of Air, into the hands of Alexander Lokhert, one of the bailies of the said burgh, 
2 CONC in favour of the said Adam Johnestoun and spouse, and the longer liver of them in conjunct infeftment, and the heirs lawfully procreated or to be procreated between them, whom failing, the heirs and assignees of the said Adam whom
2 CONC soever, to whom the bailie gave sasine accordingly; to be held of the provost, bailies and community of the said burgh for payment of eight shillings Scots yearly, viz:- three shillings for the one-half of the said twenty shilling
2 CONC  land and five shillings for the one-half of the meadow. Done quoad the resignation in the lodging of Margaret Kennedy in the burgh of Air on 20th May 1598, and quoad the sasine upon the ground of said lands on 22nd May 1598. Witn
2 CONC esses, William Montgomerie, writer, William Rysyd and William Roger, co-burgesses of Air, John Mure in Carcluy, servitor of the said John Mure, John Rankene, John Dalrimpill, Peter Hammiltoun, Alexander Lokhert, walker, John Maksp
2 CONC edden, John Cwnigham, carpenter, co-burgesses of Air, George Tennent, Andrew Miller and John McGrane, sergeants of said burgh. The instrument is written by George Masoun, son of the notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrso
2 CONC nlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f324&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df= National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/324]'''
