2 CONT '''8 May 1590: Contract of marriage between Thomas Kennedy of Bargeny and Dame Helen Kennedy, Countess of Eglinton, his daughter on one part and John Graham of Knockdolian on the other part, whereby John Graham of Knockdolian obli
2 CONC ges himself to infeft his future wife in liferent in various lands therein specified, and in general in all the lands and heritages of which he is now possessed or shall be possessed during his marriage, and that the male heir of 
2 CONC the marriage shall succeed him in all his lands, the said Dame Helen being obliged to maintain him during her lifetime at the rate of one third of the rent of the lands to be liferented by her; and if there is only a female heir o
2 CONC f the marriage then John shall be obliged to pay to her £6000 when she reaches the age of 14, if two daughters then 10,000 merks, and if three or more then £10,000 equally amongst them; for which causes Thomas obliges him to pay 5
2 CONC 000 merks of tocher at the terms and in the manner specified. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f1%2f5%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt
2 CONC =1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/B/1/5/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 September 1591: Letters of reversion granted by Dame Helen Kennedy, Countess of Eglinton with the consent of John Graham of Knockdolian, then her spouse in favour of Hugh, 5th Earl of Eglinton and Robert, Master of Eglinton,
2 CONC  his tutor whereby that they agree on payment being made to them of 4000 merks, within the parish kirk of Ayr they would discharge the annualrent of 400 merks furth of the Barony of Ardrossan. Dated at Anstruther. Witnesses: Alexa
2 CONC nder Kennedy, younger of Bargany, Hugh Kennedy of Bennane amd others. 2 pendant seals of Dame Helen Kennedy and John Graham of Knokdolian, poor impressions. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refer
2 CONC ence=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f1%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/1/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 December 1591: Notarial copy of a charter granted in implement of a decree arbitral by Hugh, 5th Earl of Eglinton with the consent of Robert, Master of Eglinton in favour of Dame Helen Kennedy, Countess of Eglinton etc of an
2 CONC  annualrent of 400 merks furth of the Barony of Ardrossan [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f1%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nationa
2 CONC l Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/1/6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 May 1600: Contract of Alienation between John Grahame of Knokdoliane, with consent of Dame Helen Kennedy, Countess of Eglinton, his spouse, and John McAlexander of Dalreoch, as son and heir of deceased Fargus McAlexander of 
2 CONC Dalreoch, whereby said John Grahame binds himself to infeft said John McAlexander in the 30s. land of Greirstoun and Quhytfarding, in parish of Colmonell, earldom of Carrick and sheriffdom of Ayr [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.u
2 CONC k/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD27%2f1%2f45&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Kennedy of Dalquharran Writs and Inventories, reference GD27/1/45]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 August 1613: Judicial ratification of renounciation granted by Dame Helen Kennedy, relict of unquhile Hew, Earl of Eglinton father to unquhile Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, that last deceased with the consent of Alexander Kennedy, 
2 CONC called of Craigneill, then her spouse and also with the consent of Josias Stewart of Bonytoun as Principal and Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmaynes as Cautioner in favour of Alexander, Earl of Eglinton as heir of tailzie and provision to 
2 CONC deceased Hugh, 5th Earl of Eglinton, of annualrent from the Barony of Ardrossan [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f1%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=
2 CONC s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/1/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 August 1613: Renunciation granted by Dame Helen Kennedy relict of unquhile Hew, Earl of Eglinton father to unquhile Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, that last deceased with the consent of Alexander Kennedy, called of Craigneill, then 
2 CONC her spouse and also with the consent of Josias Stewart of Bonytoun as Principal and Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmaynes as Cautioner in favour of Alexander, Earl of Eglinton as heir of tailzie and provision to deceased Hugh, 5th Earl of 
2 CONC Eglinton, of annualrent from the Barony of Ardrossan. Dated at the Burgh of Ayr. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f1%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Dame+helen+kennedy&ko=p&
2 CONC r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/1/8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 March 1616: Decreet before the Lords of Session at the instance of Helen Graham, one of the three female heirs of the deceased John Graham of Knockdolian, born of the marriage between John and Dame Helen Kennedy, Countess of
2 CONC  Eglinton, his wife, and at the instance of Robert Dunbar, brother to David Dunbar of Enterkine, her husband, against Robert Graham of Grugar, brother and male heir of tailzie to the deceased John Graham, and against Mr Alexander 
2 CONC Gibson of Durrie, one of the clerks of Session in whose hands the contract of marriage (GD220/1/B/1/5/1) was waiting to be registered that diligence might pass thereupon at the instance of the said Helen and her husband for recove
2 CONC ry of her third of the £10,000 thereby provided to the three female heirs born of the marriage; the contract is insert in the decreet. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f1
2 CONC %2f5%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+dunbar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/B/1/5/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
