2 CONT '''1 May 1598: Precept from chancery in favour of Gilbert Kennedy of Bargany as heir of deceased Thomas Kennedy of Bargany, his father, in lands of Bargany, Arstincher and Ballantra. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinec
2 CONC atalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f15&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gilbert+kennedy+of+bargany&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1590&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, refe
2 CONC rence GD109/15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 April 1600: Charter by Gilbert Kennedy of Bargany, and Jean Stewart, his spouse, in fulfillment of contract with Quintin Crawffurd of Camlarg, 26 April, 1600, whereby said Gilbert and Jean dispone to said Quintin, £3 land of
2 CONC  their lands of Newwerk of old extent. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f656&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gilbert+Kennedy+of+Bargany&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1600&di=n National Rec
2 CONC ords of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/656]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 March 1602: Ratification by Jean Stewart, relict of Gilbert Kennedy of Bargany, tutor testamentar of Thomas Kennedy, son and heir, or at least apparent heir of said Gilbert, of promise of tack by him to David Kennedy, younge
2 CONC r in Maxwellistoun, and Agnes Mcalexander, his spouse, of 40s. land of Maxwellistoun, in barony of Bargany for lifetime of said David and Agnes and their heir male. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.a
2 CONC spx?reference=GD109%2f2939&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gilbert+Kennedy+of+Bargany&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1475&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/2939]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 April 1603: Transumpt, dated 18 Feb. 1634 of Instrument of Sasine in favour of Thomas Kennedy now of Bargany of the 40s. land of the kirklands of Mayboill with the patronage of the parish kirk of Mayboill, in parish of Mayboi
2 CONC ll, bailiary of Carrick and sheriffdom of Ayr; following on Crown Precept of Sasine, dated 26 March 1603, in favour of said Thomas Kennedy, as heir of Gilbert Kennedy of Bargany, his father. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nr
2 CONC sonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD27%2f1%2f48&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gilbert+kennedy+of+bargany&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1590&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Kennedy of Dalquharran, reference GD27/1/48]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 September 1605: Gift under quarter seal in favour of Josias Stewart of Wester Polquharne, of tutorship of Thomas Kennedy, son and apparent heir of deceased Gilbert Kennedy of Bargany, as Thomas Kennedy of Drummurchye, neares
2 CONC t agnate relation of said Thomas, [his uncle] who succeeded to tutorship de jure, was convicted by parliament of lésè majesté and attainted. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f25
2 CONC 21&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gilbert+Kennedy+of+Bargany&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1475&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/2521]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Description: [A.P.S. IV. pp. 267 - 270]. In dorso: notarial note, 12 September, 1605, of compeirance of Josias Stewart, with caution when he undertook office of tutor.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 June 1620 :Signet letters at instance of Thomas Kennedy of Barganie, charging Josias Stewart of Bonytoun, now called of Blarquhen, his uncle, to compeir and answer for his intromissions with goods and gear of deceased Jean S
2 CONC tewart, spouse of deceased Gilbert Kennedy of Bargany, father of said Thomas. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f2529&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gilbert+Kennedy+of+Bargany&ko=p&r
2 CONC =&ro=s&df=1475&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/2529]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 June 1622: Signet letters at instance of Sir John Hammiltoun of Lettrik, kt., charging Josias Stewart of Bonytoun, now called of Blairquhan, to answer for his intromissions as tutor of Thomas Kennedy of Bargany and as execut
2 CONC or of deceased Jean Stewart, mother of said Thomas, sister of Josias. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f60&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jean+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n 
2 CONC National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/60]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 October 1625: Assignation by Gilbert Fergussoun in Mcclecheistoun, third son of deceased Gilbert Fergussoun of Dalduff, with consent of Mr John Ferguson of Kilkerane, for his interest, to John Hamiltoune, servitor of Sir Joh
2 CONC n Hamiltoune of Lettrick, kt., of contract, 20 May, 1599, between deceased Gilbert Kennedie of Barganie and deceased Jean Stewart, his spouse, on one part, and said deceased Gilbert on other part, whereby said deceased Gilbert Fer
2 CONC gussoun was infeft in annualrent of 80 merks scots from 50s. land of Barbe, parish of Gervane. [Assignation by Gilbert Fergussoun in Mcclecheistoun, third son of deceased Gilbert Fergussoun of Dalduff, with consent of Mr John Ferg
2 CONC uson of Kilkerane, for his interest, to John Hamiltoune, servitor of Sir John Hamiltoune of Lettrick, kt., of contract, 20 May, 1599, between deceased Gilbert Kennedie of Barganie and deceased Jean Stewart, his spouse, on one part
2 CONC , and said deceased Gilbert on other part, whereby said deceased Gilbert Fergussoun was infeft in annualrent of 80 merks scots from 50s. land of Barbe, parish of Gervane. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/det
2 CONC ails.aspx?reference=GD109%2f864&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jean+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/864]'''
2 CONT
