2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1467 or 1513? Check sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Old''':
2 CONT
2 CONT Angus married four times:
2 CONT
2 CONT *    1. Catherine Seton, a natural daughter of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly
2 CONT *    2. on 4 March 1467: Elizabeth, daughter of Robert Boyd, 1st Lord Boyd
2 CONT *    3. about 1498: Janet, daughter of John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy
2 CONT *    4. in 1500: Katherine Stirling.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Douglas,_5th_Earl_of_Angus Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Angus (Wikipedia)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Archibald led the noble's rebellion against James III which ended in the defeat and death of the King at the Battle of Sauchieburn n 1488.  When the nobles asked who was willing to lead the rebellion against the kind, Sir Arch
2 CONC ibald volunteered by saying "I will bell the cat".  This earned him his nickname.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Angus was born circa 1453.1 He was the son of George Douglas, 4th Earl of Angus and Isabel Sibbald.1 He and Catherine Seton were engaged on 30 September 1461.1 He married, firstly, Elizabeth Boyd, da
2 CONC ughter of Robert Boyd, 1st Lord Boyd of Kilmarnock and Mariot Maxwell, on 4 March 1467/68.1 He married, secondly, Janet Kennedy, daughter of John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy and Lady Elizabeth Gordon, circa 1498.1 He married, thirdl
2 CONC y, Katherine Stirling, daughter of Sir William Stirling, 2nd of Keir and Margaret Crichton, on 1 June 1500.2 He and Katherine Stirling were separated before 1513.1 He died between 29 November 1513 and 31 January 1514 at Priory of 
2 CONC St. Ninian, Galloway, Scotland.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Angus also went by the nick-name of 'The Great Earl'.1 Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Angus also went by the nick-name of 'Bell the Cat' for his courage in initiating opposition to King James III's f
2 CONC avourites at court.1 He succeeded to the title of 5th Earl of Angus [S., 1389] on 14 November 1462.1 He was created 1st Lord Douglas [Scotland] in 1475/76.3 He held the office of Warden of the East Marches on 11 April 1481.1 He wa
2 CONC s invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.).1 He held the office of High Chancellor [Scotland] between 1493 and 1498.1 His marriage to Janet Kennedy was annulled circa 1499.1 Cokayne writes that "his advice to the King against the fat
2 CONC al engagement at Flodden being insultingly received, he quitted the field shortly before the fight, bidding his two sons remain, both of whom were there slain, with their King."1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Angus and Elizabeth Boyd:
2 CONT
2 CONT George Douglas, Master of Angus+ b. c 1469, d. 9 Sep 1513
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Douglas+ b. bt 1470 - 1475, d. 9 Sep 1513 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Marion Douglas+ b. bt 1470 - 1477 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Douglas b. bt 1471 - 1478 
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Douglas b. bt 1472 - 1480
2 CONT
2 CONT Gavin Douglas b. c 1475, d. Sep 1522
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Archibald Douglas b. a 1475, d. c 1536
2 CONT
2 CONT =Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, ''The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinc
2 CONC t or Dormant'', new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 156. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, ''Burke's Peerage and Baronetage'', 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 1283. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baroneta
2 CONC ge, 106th edition. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, ''Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage'', 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1742. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] Cokayne, and others, ''The Complete Peerage'', volume I, page 157. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] Cokayne, and others,'' The Complete Peerage'', volume I, page 159. 
