3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU Bishop of Dunkeld
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gavin Douglas was born circa 1475. He was the son of Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Angus and Elizabeth Boyd. He died in September 1522
2 CONT
2 CONT Gavin Douglas wrote the book The Palace of Honour, published 1501,, an allegorical poem, which was not published until 1553. He held the office of Bishop of Dunkeld in 1515. He translated Virgil's Æneid.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/12086415/gavin-douglas
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial - Savoy Chapel Churchyard
2 CONT Strand, City of Westminster, Greater London, England
2 CONT Plot - Brass in aisle
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Death''' https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gavin_Douglas
2 CONT In 1522 Douglas was stricken by the plague which raged in London, and died at the house of his friend Lord Dacre. During the closing years of exile he was on intimate terms with the historian Polydore Vergil, and one of his last a
2 CONC cts was to arrange to give Polydore a corrected version of Major's account of Scottish affairs. '''Douglas was buried in the church of the Savoy, where a monumental brass (removed from its proper site after the fire in 1864) still
2 CONC  records his death and interment.'''
