1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John, third Lord Hay of Yester</strong>, eldest son and heir of the last, had a charter under the Great Seal on 7 October 1509, to himself and Elizabeth Douglas his wife, of certain lands in Hoprew, co Peebles, and in Ugs
2 CONC town, co Haddington, resigned in his favour by his father, succeeded to the Peerage 9 September 1513, and, as Sir John Hay of Hoprew, had sasine of the lands and baonies of Yester, Locherworth, Hoprew, Snaid, 3 November following.
2 CONC  He was a Commissioner for holding Parliament 6 July 1525, 12 June 1526, 8 September 1528, and 12 March 1542-43, being present in Parliament 22 February 1524-25, 10 July 1525, 12 June 1526, 6 April 1531, 7 June 1535, 10 December 1
2 CONC 540, and 13 March 1542-43, and serving on the Committee of Dooms 10 July 1526 and 13 March 1542-43, and on that of Causes 13 June 1526; he was one of the Lords who signed the letter to Henry VIII refusing to remove the Duke of Alb
2 CONC any from the guardianship of King James V, 4 July 1516, and the Treaty with England 7 October 1517. On 22 June 1531 he sold his lands of Gammilstoun and Redischill in the barony of Yester to George, Lord Seton. He died before July
2 CONC  1543. He married, first, before 17 September 1509, Elizabeth, sister to Archibald (Douglas), sixth Earl of Angus, daughter of George, Master of Angus; secondly, (--) daughter and sole heiress of John Dickson of Smithfield, co Pee
2 CONC bles."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft#page/434/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VIII, page 434
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's page on John Hay of Yester:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10961.htm#i109604
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hay, 3rd Lord Hay of Yester [1]
2 CONT *M, #109604, 
2 CONT *d. between 12 May 1543 and 19 July 1543
2 CONT *Last Edited=8 May 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hay, 3rd Lord Hay of Yester married Elizabeth Douglas, daughter of George Douglas, Master of Angus and Elizabeth Drummond, in 1509.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died between 12 May 1543 and 19 July 1543.2
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of John Hay, 2nd Lord Hay of Yester and Elizabeth Crichton.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 7 October 1509 he had a charter of the lands of Hoprew, Peebles-shire.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was invested as a Knight before 10 June 1510.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Hay of Yester [S., 1488] on 9 September 1513.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Hay, 3rd Lord Hay of Yester and Elizabeth Douglas
2 CONT *1. Elizabeth Hay+3
2 CONT *2. Mary Hay+4
2 CONT *3. Beatrice Hay2
2 CONT *4. John Hay, 4th Lord Hay of Yester+2 b. c 1510, d. b 30 Jan 1555/56
2 CONT *5. Thomas Hay2 b. a 1511, d. fr 30 Jan 1555/56 - 2 May 1558
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 1282. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baroneta
2 CONC ge, 106th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 3, page 3960. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 1285.
2 CONT *4. [S6286] Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealogy, online http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info. Hereinafter cited as Clan MacFarlane.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The third Lord, who also was named JOHN, was twice married. His first wife was Elizabeth Douglas, daughter of the Master of Angus, and sister of Archibald, sixth Earl of Angus. He took for his second wife the daughter of John Dick
2 CONC son of Smithfield, with whom he received that estate. It was inherited by William Hay, the elder of the two sons whom this lady bore to Lord Yester. He was the ancestor of the present family of Smithfield and Hairtoune, who were a
2 CONC dvanced to the dignity of Baronets of Nova Scotia by James VI., in 1624.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Of Colstoun, co. Haddington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two sons called John?
