2 TITL Margaret Tudor of England
2 NOTE Margaret Tudor was the elder of the two surviving daughters of Henry VII of England and Elizabeth of York, and the elder sister of Henry VIII. In 1503, she married James IV, King of Scots, thus becoming the mother of James V and g
3 CONC randmother of Mary, Queen of Scots. Most important of all, Margaret's marriage to James led directly to the Union of the Crowns. Fate, it was once argued, had intended Margaret to be Queen of Scots. Born on 29 November, 1489, she 
3 CONC was christened on the 30th — St. Andrew's Day — in St. Margaret's Church, Westminster, sharing a name with Scotland's only royal saint. In all, Margaret married three times.
3 CONT
3 CONT Read more about Margaret in her profile.
