1 OCCU 6th Lord Glamis, 6th Lord of Glamis, 5th Lord of Glamis
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From [http://thepeerage.com/p10964.htm#i109633 thepeerage.com]: '''John Lyon, 6th Lord Glamis''' was born circa 1491&sup1;. He was the son of John Lyon, 4th Lord Glamis and Elizabeth Gray. He married Janet Douglas,
2 CONC  daughter of George Douglas, Master of Angus and Elizabeth Drummond, before 12 December 1527&sup1;. He died on 8 April 1528 at Leith, Scotland.&sup1;
2 CONT
2 CONT The title Lord Glamis was created in 1445 for Sir Patrick Lyon (1402–1459), grandson of Sir John. John Lyon, 6th Lord Glamis, married Janet Douglas, daughter of the Master of Angus, at a time when King James V was feuding with the
2 CONC  Douglases. In December 1528 Janet was accused of treason for bringing supporters of the Earl of Angus to Edinburgh. She was then charged with poisoning her husband, Lord Glamis, who had died on 17 September 1528. Eventually, she 
2 CONC was accused of witchcraft, and was burned at the stake at Edinburgh on 17 July 1537. James V subsequently seized Glamis, living there for some time.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Lyon, 6th Lord Glamis and Janet Douglas
2 CONT ># George Lyon d. a 1542 
2 CONT ># Margaret Lyon d. 15 Jun 1610 
2 CONT ># Elizabeth Lyon &sup2;
2 CONT ># John Lyon, 7th Lord Glamis+ d. b 18 Sep 1559 
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT # Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 1282. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106
2 CONC th edition.
