1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://homepages.rootsweb.com/~slkarner/PS14/PS14_193.HTML
2 CONT
2 CONT Name	Robert BLACKADDER Laird of East Blackadder [1074], [1075], M
2 CONT Birth	1475 [1055]
2 CONT Death	9 Sep 1513, Killed At Flodden. [1054], [212] Age: 38
2 CONT Death Memo	The anonymous pedigree chart says he was killed at Bronnoton by Dacre, in 1514., ,
2 CONT Father	Andrew BLACKADDER Of The Ilk, M (1430-)
2 CONT Mother	Elizabeth JOHNSTONE of Johnstone, F (~1430-)
2 CONT Misc. Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT It appears that the barony of Blackadder was, for a while divided into two parts, East and West Blackadder. The two brothers Robert and Stephen were Lairds of East and West Blackadder, repectively.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Blackadar fell at Flodden leaving a widow and two daughters, Beatrix and Margaret. The unprotected state of his family opened a way for scenes of cruelty and fraud, which involved the house of Blackader in the most calamito
2 CONC us feud with the Humes of Wedderburn, who cast avaricious eyes on the lands of East Blackader. The Prior of Coldingham, and six domestics, along with the Dean of Dunblane and others were murdered by the Humes (Chambers Caled Vol. 
2 CONC II). Widow Alison and daughters shut themselves in Castle Blackader. Hume assaulted the castle and seized the women. Sir David Hume of Wedderburn married the widow. The two daughters were contracted to David's brothers John and Ro
2 CONC bert in 1518, and as they were only in their eighth year, they were confined by John Hume in the Castle Blackadar until they became of age. (Douglas Peerage, Vol. II, p. 174.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Castle Blackadar was entailed to male heirs and should have passed to Sir John of Tulliallan, Cousin and Tutor to the ladies. Hume refused to quit the lands or deliver up the Castle fortress. Sir John applied to the legislature, b
2 CONC ut due to anarchy and misrule, there was no administration of just claims. According to Taylor, Sir John was murdered by the Humes to prevent the castle and lands from being threatened.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses
2 CONT 1	Alison DOUGLAS [1076], F
2 CONT Birth	bef 1491 [153]
2 CONT Death	aft 1540 [212] Age: 49
2 CONT Father	George DOUGLAS Master Of Angus, M (ca1469-1513)
2 CONT Mother	Elizabeth DRUMMOND, F
2 CONT Marriage	13 Mar 1510-11, SCOT [213], [1077]
2 CONT Marriage Memo	This was the date of the "contract" of marriage
2 CONT Children	Beatrix, F
2 CONT Margaret, F
