1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Name: David Scott Suffix: Sir Sex: M David Scott of Buccleugh.
2 CONT
2 CONT David Scott hailed from Branxholm and was the ancestor of the Duke of Buccleuch and Queensberry. He was M. P. at Edinburgh in 1487. Birth: BEF 1440  Death: MAR 1491/92 _SDATE: 15 MAR 1491 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Holy Cross Church, Peebles, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir David Scott, 1st of Buccleuch was the son of Sir Walter Scott of Branxholm.
2 CONT He died in March 1491/92.1 He was created Baron of Buccleuch [Scottish Barony] on 21 May 1488 He lived at Branxholm, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife seen as https://www.geni.com/people/NN-Somerville/6000000009049700453?through=6000000007267045529 “but no evidence is forthcoming.” [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08paul#page/9/mode/1up TSP]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir David Scott, 1st of Buccleuch
2 CONT #Janet Scott+1
2 CONT #David Scott of Buccleuch, younger+ d. b 1491
2 CONT #Margaret Scott+2
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir of Branxholme, 7th Laird of Bucceleuch Scott
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir David, son and heir of Sir Walter Scott was concerned in most of the public transections in the reign of James III. He was instrumental in suppressing insurrections on the Borders, and was a conservator of peace with England. 
2 CONC He sat in Parliament 1431 as David Scott of Kirkurd, and in the Parliament of 1487, being then styled “Dominus de Bucluche”. For his services at the battle of Blackness he received Branxholm, Eckford and others into the barony of 
2 CONC Branxholm 1488. He died March 1492, and was buried in the church of the Holy Cross at Peebles. (Walter Scott Cameron)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
