1 NAME Alexander /Scott/ Rector of Wigton and Lord Register
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN Scott
2 NSFX Rector of Wigton and Lord Register
2 _MARNM Scott
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 JUN 1488
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sauchieburn
3 CTRY Kingdom of Scotland (not part of the United Kingdom)
1 OCCU
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR ALEXANDER SCOTT===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Rector of Wigton; Lord Register===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Alexander Nisbet, Sir Alexander Scott, here treated, is the son of Sur David Scott of Branholm and his Somerville wife. [https://archive.org/details/systemofheraldry02nisbuoft/page/280/mode/1up A System of Heraldty
2 CONC  etc. II: 280] He and his elder brother David, identified as the son of Sir Walter Scott of Kirkurd, are noticed in each others company on 28 November 1463, in the witness list of a charter in favour of Robert Scott of Hanyng: "Da
2 CONC v. Scot, Alex. Scot, fratribus germanis, fllis D. Walt. Scot de Kirkurde militis". [ https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/165/mode/1up RMS, 1424-1513: 771]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Alexander Scott, who was Rector of Wigton, and Lord Register in the reign of King James III. from the 1483 till the 1488, lost his life, with the king his master, at the unhappy field of Bannockburn. [https://archive.org/de
2 CONC tails/systemofheraldry02nisbuoft/page/280/mode/1up A System of Heraldty etc. II: 280] The unhappy event referred to is the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Sauchieburn Battle of Sauchieburn]'''
