1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Douglas, 4th of Drumlanrig, was killed at the Battle of Kirtle, between Lochmaben and Carlisle, fighting under the royal banner in the engagement with the Duke of Albany (the King's brother) and his cousin,
2 CONC  the 9th Earl of Douglas, when those noblemen invaded Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 22 JUL 1484 in Battle of Kirtle
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Sir William Douglas, 3rd Baron of Drumlanrig
2 CONT Mother: Margaret Carlyle, dau of Sir William Carlyle
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Elizabeth, dau of Sir Robert Crichton of Sanquhar.  She married secondly James Campbell of West Loudon and 3rdly Sir William Colville of Ochiltree.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT  Sir James Douglas, 5th Baron of Drumlanrig
2 CONT Archibald Douglas, ancestor of the Douglases of Cashogle
2 CONT George Douglas, ancestor of the Douglases of Penziere   
2 CONT Robert Douglas
2 CONT John Douglas
2 CONT  Margaret Douglas = John, 2nd Lord Cathcart
2 CONT Janet Douglas = (1) William, Master of Somerville = (2) Sir John Gordon of Lochinvar
2 CONT Elizabeth Douglas = John Campbell of Wester Loudoun
2 CONT  daughter m. Sir Simon Carruthers, 8th of Mouswald (d 1504) (unconfirmed)
2 CONT
