1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/maxwell1445.htm#MAXWELL_1445_4
2 CONT
2 CONT John Maxwell married (in 1491 or 1492) Agnes, the daughter of Sir Alexander Stewart of Garlies ,[3][4] She was still living on 25 July 1530. They had at least eight children, including: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Maxwell, who married Robert Charteris of Amisfield
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Maxwell was the daughter of John Maxwell, Fourth Lord Maxwell (of Dumfries, Scotland), and Agnes Stewart, eldest daughter of Sir Alexander Steward of Garlies.[1] Her birth date is not certain. It would be after 1490 when her
2 CONC  parents married, and before 1513 when her father died.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Robert Charteris of Amisfield, Scotland. They had one son John.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT *1.  Sir William Fraser, "The Book of Carlaverock" (Edinburgh: unknown, 1873), p. 172, Available at Archive.org. (accessed 28 July 2022). < [https://archive.org/details/bookofcarlaverv100fras/page/172/mode/1up?view=theater Archive
2 CONC .Org] >
