1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY AGNES HERRIES ==
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Agneti Hereis (1549-50) Agneti Hereis (1561) Agneti Hereis (1562) Agneti Hereis (1566) Dominam Agnetam Hereis (1577) Agnetem dominam Herreis (1593) Dame Agnes Hareis, Lady Herries (1598)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 19 December 1598. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar of  Dame Agnes Hareis, Lady Herries, reference CC8/8/32]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Agnes, Lady Herries, died at Terregles on 14 March 1593-94. She made her will the day before; being "seik in body bot haill in mynd and saull," she desired to be buried beside her husband. After leaving legacies to her children
2 CONC , she took kindly thought for her servants and tenants. Not being "habill to writt" herself, she ordered Mr. Thomsoun, reader of the kirk of Terregles, to "subscryve" the will, which was confirmed at Edinburgh on 19 December 1598.
2 CONC  [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/411/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 411]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 February 1549-50: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which the Queen confirms possession of one third part of the lands and barony of Herries, one third part of the lands and barony of Teregles, and various other lan
2 CONC ds, to John, Master of Maxwell, and his wife Agneti Hereis, otherwise Agnes Herries, eldest daughter and one of the three heirs of the deceased William, Lord Herries. Agnes Herries had previously resigned these lands to the crown 
2 CONC in order to obtain a new grant in favour of her husband and herself. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/91/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 405]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 March 1561: Charter by which Archibald Herries of Madinpaup, identified as the male heir of the deceased William, Lord Herries, confirms that he has sold the lands of Reidcastle in the Stewartry of Kirkcudbright to Sir John 
2 CONC Maxwell of Teregles and his wife Agneti Hereis, otherwise Agnes Herries. For greater security, it might be supposed, Sir John Maxwell of Teregles and his wife obtained a charter of confirmation under the Great Seal of Scotland on 
2 CONC 17 August 1562. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/322/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 1426]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 October 1561: Charter by John Maxwell of Terregles kt (with consent of Agnes, Lady Herries, his spouse) in favour of John Irvine, grandson and heir of late John Irvine of Scalis, of the £5 lands of old extent of Scalis, in th
2 CONC e parish of Ranepatrick [ie Redkirk], and the £5 lands of Woodhouselees, in the barony of Kirkandrews and parish of Canonbie. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f403%2f19&st=1&tc=y&t
2 CONC l=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lady+herries&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Graham of Mossknowe Papers, reference GD1/403/19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 May 1566: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which the King and Queen confirm that they have incorporated the baronies of Teregles and Kirkgunzean into the free barony of Teregles for John Maxwell of Teregles and his
2 CONC  wife Agneti Hereis. John and Agnes, who had previously resigned these lands in order to receive a new grant in their favour, were to hold the new barony in conjunct fee and liferent. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi0
2 CONC 4scot/page/423/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 1728]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 February 1577 and 26 February 1577: Charter by which William Baillie of Lamington, with the consent of his wife, Lady Margaret Maxwell, Countess of Angus, confirms that he has given the lands and barony of Lamington, togethe
2 CONC r with other lands, to his daughter Margaret Baillie and her husband Edward Maxwell. His gift follows from a contract between John, Lord Hereis, his spouse DOMINAM AGNETAM HEREIS, and their son Edward Maxwell, on the one part, and
2 CONC  William Baillie of Lamington and his wife Margaret, and their eldest daughter Margaret Baillie, on the other part. Edward Maxwell and his wife Margaret were to hold in conjunct fee and liferent. William Baillie of Lamingtom and h
2 CONC is wife Margaret reserved their own liferent. For greater security Edward Maxwell and his wife Margaret obtained a charter under the Great Seal of Scotland on 2 March 1577-78. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/pa
2 CONC ge/760/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 2780]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 May 1593: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/798/mode/1up RMS 1580-93: charter number 2321]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Terregles  is a village and civil parish near Dumfries, in Dumfries and Galloway, Scotland. It lies in the former county of Kirkcudbrightshire. The name Terregles, recorded as Travereglis in 1359.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/n5/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1546-1580. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, M.A., Advocate. (H. M. Ge
2 CONC neral Register House, Edinburgh, 1886), 1179 pp. including indexes and errata]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1580-1593. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, M.A., Advocate. (H. M. Ge
2 CONC neral Register House, Edinburgh, 1888), 1156 pp. including indexes and errata]
2 CONT
2 CONT
