1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===EDWARD MAXWELL OF LAMINGTON===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Commendator of Dundrennan===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Edward Maxwell, Commendator of Dundrennan, died 29 September 1598. He married, before 1597, Margaret, daughter of William Baillie of Lamington. She married, secondly, John Livingston of West Quarter. For a pedigree of Edward's 
2 CONC descendants, Baillies of Lamington, and Maxwells of Newlaw and Breoch, see Book of Carlaverock; one son, however, Hew Maxwell, a highwayman, is there omitted. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/411/mode/1
2 CONC up The Scots Peerage IV: 412]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 February 1577 and 26 February 1577: Charter by which William Baillie of Lamington, with the consent of his wife, Lady Margaret Maxwell, Countess of Angus, confirms that he has given the lands and barony of Lamington, togethe
2 CONC r with other lands, to his daughter Margaret Baillie and her husband EDWARD MAXWELL. His gift follows from a contract between John, Lord Hereis, his spouse DOMINAM AGNETAM HEREIS, and their son Edward Maxwell, on the one part, and
2 CONC  William Baillie of Lamington and his wife Margaret, and their eldest daughter Margaret Baillie, on the other part. Edward Maxwell and his wife Margaret were to hold in conjunct fee and liferent. William Baillie of Lamingtom and h
2 CONC is wife Margaret reserved their own liferent. For greater security Edward Maxwell and his wife Margaret obtained a charter under the Great Seal of Scotland on 2 March 1577-78. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/pa
2 CONC ge/760/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 2780]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 November 1589: Extract instrument of redemption of certain tenements of land in Hamilton, redeemed by John Hamilton of Weston from Edward Maxwell, fiar of Lamington, for 2600 merks. Registered in Commissary's court books of H
2 CONC amilton. Endordsed: judicial ratification by Margaret Bailie, wife of Edward Maxwell of Lamington. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f12%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edward+ma
2 CONC xwell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/2/12/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/411/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 412]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00090313&tree=LEO Biographical Summary by Genealogics]===
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Maxwell1,2
2 CONT M, #41005, d. 29 September 1598
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Sir John Maxwell, Lord Herries3,4 b. c 1512, d. 20 Jan 1583
2 CONT Mother	Agnes Herries4 b. c 1534, d. 14 Mar 1594
2 CONT
2 CONT      Edward Maxwell married Margaret Baillie, daughter of Sir William Baillie and Margaret Maxwell, before 1597.1 Edward Maxwell died on 29 September 1598.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Margaret Baillie
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	 Sir William Baillie+1 d. 1615
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations [S11566] The Scots Peerage, Vol. IV, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 412. [S11584] The Scots Peerage, Vol. V, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 442. [S11585] The Scots Peerage, Vol. VI, edited by Sir James Balfou
2 CONC r Paul, p. 481. [S11566] The Scots Peerage, Vol. IV, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 409-413.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
