2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''July 1530: Draft signature for letters permitting Robert, Lord Maxwell, to resign his liferent of the lands of Cartisbrig and Feludar, Brume, Newtoun, Mawlatis-Houch, Crouk, Braidleyis, Hassaldan, Tetwad and Humby, Kirkbrig and
2 CONC  the Schaw, Kirkhill, Blakhous, Brumehous and Sufeild, in the lordship of the Meirnis and sheriffdom of Renfrew, in favour of Beatrice Douglas, daughter of James, earl of Mortoun, notwithstanding Lord Maxwell's danger of forfeitur
2 CONC e. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f284&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrice+douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, refer
2 CONC ence GD150/284]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 July 1530: Testimonial by Thomas Maxwell, vicar of Carlaverock, informing the curatus of the parish church of Dalketh that he has published the three banns of marriage between Robert Maxwell, son and apparent heir of Robert,
2 CONC  Lord Maxwell, and Beatrice Douglas, daughter of James, earl of Morton. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f285&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrice+douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di
2 CONC =n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/285]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 June 1535: Acquittance by Robert, Lord Maxwell, to James, earl of Mortoun, for the tocher of Beatrix Douglas. Dated at Creichtoun. Witnesses: Mr. Hugh Ryge, sir George Heslehop, John Kylpatrik, John Chartouris, Gilbert Greso
2 CONC ne, sir Thomas Mychelsoun, William Trumbuyll and Richard Douglas. Notaries - John Gray, Hugh Rig and John Scot. [Seal]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f289&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n
2 CONC &tp=n&k=beatrix+douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/289]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/361/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 361]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://thepeerage.com/p2595.htm#i25947 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Beatrix Douglas was the daughter of James Douglas, 3rd Earl of Morton and Catherine Stewart.1 She married Robert Maxwell, 5th Lord Maxwell, son of Robert Maxwell, 4th Lord Maxwell and Janet Douglas, after 25 July 1530.2 She d
2 CONC ied after 31 October 1583.3
2 CONT
2 CONT From after 25 July 1530, her married name became Maxwell.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1562 she was certified a lunatic.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Beatrix Douglas and Robert Maxwell, 5th Lord Maxwell
2 CONT *Robert Maxwell, 6th Lord Maxwell4 b. bt 1549 - 1551, d. fr 21 Dec 1553 - 26 Jan 1554/55
2 CONT *John Maxwell, 7th Lord Maxwell+1 b. 24 Apr 1553, d. 6 Dec 1593
2 CONT
