1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/James-Greer-of-Gunpowder-River/6000000004871239894#/tab/discussion ——
2 CONT
2 CONT A tradition seems to have developed among a number of these families that they are descended from a James Grier of the family of Capenoch, son of Sir James Grier and Mary Browne, probably born in the early 1630s. He is mentioned o
2 CONC n the "Carrickfergus" tree as "James Grier M.D. of Edinburgh, died unmar." Whilst this tree is known to have many errors, this would appear to not be one of them. Recent research by Richard Miller has uncovered that James Grierson
2 CONC  of Capenoch was buried on 23 January 1662 in Greyfriars Church, Edinburgh. Contact with the Scottish Genealogical Society in Edinburgh confirmed that the burial was of James Grier(son) of Capenoch who was an MD (Apothecary) and d
2 CONC ied unmarried in Edinburgh. We will have to look elsewhere for the immigrant James Grier or Grear. There are, however, persistent rumours that members of the Capenoch family emigrated to Ireland at various times. It may be from th
2 CONC ose migrations that the American Greers spring. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familytreedna.com/public/GREER/default.aspx?section=news
