2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 March 1621: Precept of clare constat by William, Lord Creichtoun [Crichton], in favour of William Fergussoun [Ferguson], now of Craigdarroch, as brother german and heir of deceased John Fergussoun [Ferguson] of Craigdarroch,
2 CONC  of lands in GD77/98. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f103&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=craigdarroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the 
2 CONC Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/103]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 April 1621: Charter by Andrew Roresoun [Rorrison] of Bardannoch and John Roresoun [Rorrison], his eldest son, in favour of Elizabeth Fergussoun [Ferguson], sister of William Fergussoun [Ferguson] of Craigdarroch and future sp
2 CONC ouse of said John, of 2½ merk lands of Barboy [Barbuie] and corn mill called Bardannoch mill, in liferent. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f28&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=craigda
2 CONC rroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/28]''''
2 CONT
