2 CONC ails.aspx?reference=GD77%2f174%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD77%2f174&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/174/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 May 1624: Contract between William Fergusoune [Ferguson] of Craigdarroche [Craigdarroch] and John Fergusoune [Ferguson], now eldest son of deceased John Fergusoune [Ferguson], sometime in Corrochdow [Corrodow], whereby said 
2 CONC William sets in tack to John the lands of Corrochdow [Corrodow] and Chapelmark for his lifetime and 19 years, for yearly payment of 100 merks, and renunciation by said John of GD77/69.  [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonli
2 CONC necatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f75&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD77%2f75&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/75]'''
