1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Robert Henderson:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p43745.htm#i437445
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Henderson of Tunnygask [1]
2 CONT *M, #437445, 
2 CONT *d. 1622
2 CONT *Last Edited=2 Mar 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Henderson of Tunnygask was the son of James Henderson, 3rd of Fordell and Jean Murray.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Anna Kirkpatrick.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1622 at Bergen-op-Zoom, Brabant, The Netherlands, killed in action.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career:
2 CONT *He gained the rank of Colonel in the service of the Buccleuch's Regiment.[1] 
2 CONT *He fought in the Siege of Juliers.[1]
2 CONT *He was invested as a Knight in 1616.[1] 
2 CONT *He fought in the Siege of Bergen-op-Zoom in 1622.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1864. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
