2 CONT [http://thepeerage.com/p1489.htm#i14889 about - '''Andrew Kerr'''] - The Peerage .com
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Andrew Kerr was the son of Sir Robert Kerr and Christian Rutherford. He married Agnes Crichton, daughter of Sir Patrick Crichton, on 20 October 1487. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Murdered by Englishmen on 24 July 1526,' Sir Andrew Ker, with the Earl of Angus, Lord Home, and other Border chiefs, while escorting the young King James v. to Edinburgh were attacked near Melrose by Sir Walter Scott of Branxholm,
2 CONC  whose object was to free the King from the hands of the Douglases.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 18 July 1526 at Melrose, Roxburghshire, Scotland, killed while escorting King James V to London.  Sir Andrew Kerr lived at Cessford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Andrew Kerr and Agnes Crichton
