2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Kerr-166
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Kerr was the daughter of Sir Andrew Kerr of Cessford[1] and Agnes Crichton. She married Sir John Kerr of Ferniehirst, son of Sir Andrew Kerr of Ferniehirst and Janet Home.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had six children:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir Thomas Ker of Ferniehirst.
2 CONT # Andrew Ker of Nethergogar, who is mentioned in a minute of the Regality Court of Cavers (d bef 1541)
2 CONT # William Ker who was a great Royalist, and adhered firmly to the interest of Queen Mary. (dsp after 1561)
2 CONT # John, alive 31 October 1581, when a gift of a pension of 500 merks to him out of the profits of the Abbey of Kelso, by Mary, Queen Regent, was ratified by Queen Mary.
2 CONT # Margaret Kerr, married to William, Lord Hay of Yester.
2 CONT # Elizabeth Kerr married to Andrew, younger son of Walter Lundin of that Ilk.
2 CONT
