1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ROBERT KER OF WOODHEID ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 October 1543: Charter by Robert Ker of Wodheid, son of Andrew K. of Farnyhyrst, selling to his mother Janet Hume, wife of said Andrew, an annualrent of 3 li. and 12d. from the tenement of William Smyth lying on north side of 
2 CONC the Cawsegait of Jedburgh, between tenement of David Dawgles on west and tenement of John Clerk on east: and that for a sum which she has paid to him. Signed "Robart Ker", and seal of George Moscrop, burgess of Jedburgh, procured 
2 CONC and appended. Dated at Jedburgh. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f1%2f181&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=janet+hume&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Paper
2 CONC s of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), reference GD40/1/181]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 November 1576: Componitour for remission to Thomas Ker of Caveris dwelling in sheriffdom of Roxburgh for resetting of William Ker, son and apparent heir of Robert Ker of Ancrum Wodheid, and other rebels guilty of crimes of s
2 CONC laughter, etc against inhabitants of the burgh of Jedburgh in time of the latest troubles. [Componitour for remission to Thomas Ker of Caveris dwelling in sheriffdom of Roxburgh for resetting of William Ker, son and apparent heir 
2 CONC of Robert Ker of Ancrum Wodheid, and other rebels guilty of crimes of slaughter, etc against inhabitants of the burgh of Jedburgh in time of the latest troubles. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx
2 CONC ?reference=RH1%2f5%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ker+of+ancrum&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: RH1/5/6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
