2 CONT * 6. John Rutherford I of Hunthill (c.1510-1577)
2 CONT
2 CONT >John Rutherford succeeded in 1529 as a minor. The Treasurer's accounts for 1530 mention a composition for his relief and marriage. (Accounts of the Lord High Treasurer of Scotland, ed. T . Dickson and Sir J.B. Paul, 13 vols. (187
2 CONC 7-1978) V, 344).
2 CONT
2 CONT >On March 12, 1529/30 he was seised of Nether Chatto and other lands and four marklands of Scraisburgh that were in the king's hands since Martinmas. (The Exchequer rolls of Scotland, ed. J. Stuart etc., 23 vols. (1878-1908) XVI, 
2 CONC 520).
2 CONT
2 CONT >The Littleheuch line of Capehope and Kirkraw derives its name from the word Littleheuch which is a a small glen with steep sides.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/cu31924092516248/page/n387/mode/2up?q=Rutherford archive. org pg 371-373]<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT >Mr. John, Professor of Philosophy, Divinity, and Medicine in the College of Coimbra in Portugal, the Sorbonne in France, and elsewhere abroad. Probably identical with Mr. John Rutherfurd, Provost of St. Salvator's College, St. An
2 CONC drews, who resigned 30 August and died December 1577. He married Christian Forsyth, i" and had issue :—<br/>
2 CONT i. Mr. John, minister of Denino 14 October 1577, of Kemback 3 September 1579, St. Andrews July 1584, and died of the pest 4 October 1585. He married Janet, daughter of David Inglis of Ardit, and had issue :—
2 CONT * (i) David, served heir to his father 22 March 1606.
2 CONT * (ii) Mr. John, born 1565, Minister of Cupar 1590, and of Kilconquhar 21 July 1594. He was deposed 1603, and took to the study of medicine ; was re- instated and became minister of Dairsie in 1611, of Monifieth 24 June 1626, and 
2 CONC died 8 June 1632, aged sixty seven. He married, before 1606, Barbara Sandilands, relict of Thomas Dischington of Ardross, and had issue : —
2 CONT ** a. Mr. John, minister of Kirkden circa 1628, died March 1656. He married Isobel, daughter of Auchmuttie of Drumeldrie, and had issue : —
2 CONT *** (a) John, advocate, served heir to his grandfather 29 March 1664, married Janet Muschett, and had issue : —
2 CONT **** a. James, baptized 11 January 1657.
2 CONT **** b. Margaret, baptized 22 March 1658, married David Auchmouttie of Drumeldrie.
2 CONT *** (b) Janet. ii. William, owner and captain of a ship in Leith, and merchant burgess of Edinburgh, who died 4 November 1587. He had issue :—
2 CONT * (i) William of Wrightslands, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, who had a charter under the Great Seal of lands of Easter and Wester Quarrelholes, in the barony of Restalrig, 23 November 1621, and died 14 November 1624.  He married 
2 CONC Giles Stewart, who survived him, and had issue : —
2 CONT ** a. Robert of Wrightslands, served heir-general to his father 7 June 1625, and in the lands of Easter and Wester Quarrelholes, near Edinburgh, 22 July 1631, became a major-general in the Army, and Governor of Majorca. He had iss
2 CONC ue : —
2 CONT *** (a) William, Treasurer to the King of Spain
2 CONT *** (b) Robert, Count Rutherfurd, Governor of Ostend.
2 CONT ** b. William, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, who had a charter under the Great Seal of the lands of Quarrelholes on his brother Robert's resignation 1 August 1634, and sold the same to the City of Edinburgh. He died about 1656, h
2 CONC aving married Margaret, daughter of Alexander Guthrie, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, and sister to Sir Henry- Guthrie of Colliston, Knight, but had no issue.
2 CONT *** c. Andrew, created LORD RUTHEBFURD and EARL OF TEVIOT.
2 CONT *** d. Isabel, married Archibald Wilkie of Harlawmuir, merchant in Edinburgh, and had issue: —
2 CONT **** (a) Mr. Archibald, served heir to his uncle, the Earl of Teviot, 9 September 1671.
2 CONT ** e. Christine, married to Robert Durie of  Grange, mariner in Leith. He died in March 1625, and had issue John, his heir, William, who succeeded his brother, and Christian.
