2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page for Alexander Montgomerie:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p2070.htm#i20698
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Montgomerie, 6th Earl of Eglinton [1]
2 CONT *M, #20698, 
2 CONT *b. 1588, 
2 CONT *d. 7 January 1661
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=2.05%
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Montgomerie, 6th Earl of Eglinton was born in 1588.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Lady Anne Livingstone, daughter of Alexander Livingstone, 1st Earl of Linlithgow and Lady Helen Hay, on 22 June 1612.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Margaret Scott, daughter of Sir Walter Scott, 1st Lord Scott of Buccleuch and Mary Ker, between November 1642 and March 1644.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 7 January 1661.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was baptised with the name of Alexander Seton.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Robert Seton, 1st Earl of Winton and Lady Margaret Montgomerie.[1],[2] 
2 CONT *He gained the title of 6th Earl of Eglinton [S., 1507] on 4 September 1612.[1] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 7th Lord Montgomerie [S., 1445] on 4 September 1612.[1] 
2 CONT *On 24 March 1615 he resigned his titles, and had a regrant.[1] 
2 CONT *He fought in the Battle of Marston Moor in 1644, for the Parliamentarians.[1] 
2 CONT *He fought in the Captain in 1650, Horse Guards. for King Charles II.[1] 
2 CONT *Between 1651 and 1660 he was imprisoned.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Alexander Montgomerie, 6th Earl of Eglinton and Lady Anne Livingstone
2 CONT *1. Colonel James Montgomerie+2 d. 18 Oct 1675
2 CONT *2. Maj.-Gen. Robert Montgomerie+4 d. 1684
2 CONT *3. Hugh Montgomerie, 7th Earl of Eglinton+1 b. 8 Apr 1613, d. Feb 1669
2 CONT *4. Sir Henry Montgomerie5 b. 26 Jun 1614, d. 3 May 1643
2 CONT *5. Lady Margaret Montgomerie+4 b. 20 Feb 1616/17, d. 27 Jan 1664/65
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1280. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 560.
