1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Margaret Hay:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p2427.htm#i24263
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Margaret Hay [1]
2 CONT *F, #24263, 
2 CONT *d. circa 19 April 1695
2 CONT *Last Edited=31 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.66%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Margaret Hay married, firstly, Henry Ker, Lord Ker, son of Robert Ker, 1st Earl of Roxburghe and Jane Drummond, on 3 February 1638.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, John Kennedy, 6th Earl of Cassillis, son of Hew Kennedy, Master of Cassillis and Katherine Macdowall, on 15 March 1643/44.[1] A contract for the marriage of Lady Margaret Hay and John Kennedy, 6th Earl of Ca
2 CONC ssillis was signed on 20 February 1643/44.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died circa 19 April 1695.[3] She was buried on 22 April 1695 at St. Martin-in-the-Fields Church, Covent Garden, London, England.[2] Her will was probated on 4 July 1695.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of William Hay, 10th Earl of Erroll and Lady Anne Lyon.[2] 
2 CONT *From 3 February 1638, her married name became Ker. 
2 CONT *From 15 March 1643/44, her married name became Kennedy. As a result of her marriage, Lady Margaret Hay was styled as Countess of Cassillis on 15 March 1643/44. 
2 CONT *Her last will was dated 12 April 1695.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lady Margaret Hay and Henry Ker, Lord Ker
2 CONT *1. Jean Ker+
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lady Margaret Hay and John Kennedy, 6th Earl of Cassillis
2 CONT *1. John Kennedy, 7th Earl of Cassillis+2 b. Nov 1653, d. 23 Jul 1701
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 76. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 77.
2 CONT *3. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1336. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
