1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES SOMERVILLE, LORD SOMERVILLE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08paul#page/20/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 20-22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James, fifth Lord Somerville, born about 1518...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He died at Cowthally, in December 1569, and was buried in Carnwarth Church, being the last Lord Somerville there interred. He married, first, in or before 1529, Jean, natural daughter of James, first Earl of Arran, but by her h
2 CONC ad apparently no issue; secondly, Agnes, daughter of Sir James Hamilton of Finnart."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft#page/20/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VIII, page 20-21
2 CONT
2 CONT == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James Somerville, 6th Lord Somerville</strong>, (c.1518-1569) was a Lord of the Parliament of Scotland...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...James was the son of Hugh Somerville, 5th Lord Somerville and Jonet Maitland. He married Agnes, daughter of James Hamilton of Finnart in 1536 at Craignethan Castle."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'James Somerville, 6th Lord Somerville', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 27 February 2011, 22:27 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=James_Somerville,_6th_Lord_Somerville&old
2 CONC id=416276162> [accessed 15 October 2012]
2 CONT
