1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN TWEEDIE tutor of Drumelzier===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''John Tuedye, tutor of Drummelzeare (1577) John Twedie, tutor of Drumalzear (1579) Twedie tutoris de Drummelzear (1606) John Tuedye tutor of Drummelyear (1658)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 August 1554: Charter by John, Lord St. John, preceptor of Torphichen, to John Twedy of the Templelands of Kyrkwrd with 19, soumes grass in the common pasture of the town of Kyrkwrd in the sheriffdom of Peblis and with the wh
2 CONC ole non-entry duties of said lands since the death of James Twedy, last possessor thereof. At Edinburgh, 18 August, 1554. Witnesses: James Tenent, Alexander Coichran, Arthur Cleland, Sir John Brown, notary public. Fragment of Seal
2 CONC  remaining. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD89%2f1%2f377&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD89%2f1%2f377&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Carmichael Fa
2 CONC mily of Skirling, reference GD89/1/377]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 November 1577: Charter by said John Tuedye to John Tuedye, tutor of Drummelzeare, and Katherine Stewart, his spouse, of lands in GD89/1/377. At Edinburgh, 24 November, 1577. Witnesses: John Forsyth, writer, Hugh Somervell, y
2 CONC ounger of Spittell, James Cant, burgess of Edinburgh, and James Bellenden. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD89%2f1%2f378&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Tuedye&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di
2 CONC =n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Carmichael Family of Skirling, reference GD89/1/378]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 January 1579: John Twedie, tutor of Drumalzear, was a member of an assize. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/827/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: note 1 on p. 828]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 and 18 June 1580: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/119/mode/1up RMS 1580-93: charter number 383]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 December 1588: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/549/mode/1up RMS 1580-93: charter number 1605]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 February 1606: REX, — cum avisamento &c. (127.), — ad feudifirmam dimisit et quitteclamavit MARIOTE TWEDIE filie legit, quondam Joannis T. tutoris de Drummelzear, heredibus ejus et assignatis quibuscuuque . . . . . [https://
2 CONC archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/616/mode/1up RMS: charter number 1706]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 August 1658: (145) Aug. 6, 1658. PETER DUNLOPE son to umquhill Mr. William Dunlope apothicar burges of Edinburgh, heir of Mareon Twedye daughter to John Tuedye tutor of Drummelyear, his goodame, - in the tempel-landis of Kirk
2 CONC urde, and 15 sowthes of grasse upon the common pasturage, with the teynd sheaves, with the parochine of Kirkurde.- E. 3s. xxv. 91. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=
2 CONC qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=dunlope&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc. II]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/historyoftweedi00twee/page/n8/mode/1up The History of the Tweedie, or Tweedy, Family. A  Record of Scottish Lowland Life & Character. By Michael Forbes Tweedie. (W. P. Griffith & Sons, London, 1902)
2 CONC , 231 pp.]'''
