1 OCCU 4th Laird of Crichton, 7th Lord of the Isles
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Laird of Kirkpatrick (1472 - 1513)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Robert Crichton:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2397.htm#i23967
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Crichton, 2nd Lord Crichton of Sanquhar [1]
2 CONT *M, #23967, 
2 CONT *d. between 13 July 1513 and 6 November 1513
2 CONT *Last Edited=8 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Crichton, 2nd Lord Crichton of Sanquhar was the son of Robert Crichton of Kinnoull and Lady Marion Stuart.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marion Maxwell circa 1491.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died between 13 July 1513 and 6 November 1513, probably killed Flodden on 9 September 1513.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Crichton of Sanquhar [S., 1488] circa February 1494/95.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Robert Crichton, 2nd Lord Crichton of Sanquhar and Marion Maxwell
2 CONT *1. Robert Crichton, 3rd Lord Crichton of Sanquhar+[1] d. fr 12 Jul 1516 - 16 Oct 1520
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 601. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
