1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM CUNNINGHAM Earl of Glencairn===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Cunningham, Ear of Glencairn. On 24 August 1549 he had a charter from his father to himself and his wife of certain lands in the earldom of Glencairn. He was a member of the Privy Council as Master of Glencairn as early
2 CONC  as 1569 ; his first appearance on that body as Earl is in November 1575. He was dead before 18 October 1580, when his son James was sworn in as a Privy Councillor under the title of Earl of Glencairn. He married (contract 20 Augu
2 CONC st 1547) Janet Gordon, daughter of Sir John Gordon of Lochinvar. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/241/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: pp. 242-3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[http://thepeerage.com/p15057.htm#i150565 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage]===
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cuninghame, 6th Earl of Glencairn [1]
2 CONT *M, #150565, 
2 CONT *b. 1535, 
2 CONT *d. from 1576 to 24 February 1579/80
2 CONT *Last Edited=20 Feb 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.04%
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cuninghame, 6th Earl of Glencairn was born in 1535. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Janet Gordon, daughter of Sir John Gordon of Lochinvar and Margaret Crichton, on 24 August 1549.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died from 1576 to 24 February 1579/80.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Alexander Cuninghame, 5th Earl of Glencairn and Lady Janet Hamilton.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 6th Earl of Glencairn [S., 1488] on 23 December 1574.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 6th Lord Kilmaurs [S., 1464] on 23 December 1574.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of William Cuninghame, 6th Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT *1. Lady Jean Cunningham2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Cuninghame, 6th Earl of Glencairn and Janet Gordon
2 CONT *1. Lady Margaret Cuninghame2
2 CONT *2. Lady Elizabeth Cuninghame2
2 CONT *3. Lady Susannah Cuninghame+4
2 CONT *4. unknown son Cuninghame5
2 CONT *5. James Cuninghame, 7th Earl of Glencairn+2 b. c 1552, d. a Mar 1630
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 493. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 994.
2 CONT *4. [S4592] Penelope Thomson, "re: Thomson Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger LUNDY (101053), 19 April 2010. Hereinafter cited as "re: Thomson Family."
2 CONT *5. [S47] Hugh Montgomery-Massingberd, editor, Burke's Irish Family Records (London, U.K.: Burkes Peerage Ltd, 1976), volume 1, page 994. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Irish Family Records.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Cunningham,_6th_Earl_of_Glencairn Biographical Summary by Wikipedia]===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Cunningham, 6th Earl of Glencairn''' (after 1530 – circa 1578)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Alexander Cunningham, 5th Earl of Glencairn and Janet Hamilton, daughter of James Hamilton, 1st Earl of Arran. He married sometime before 24 August 1549 to Janet Gordon of Lochinvar (died 18 November 1596). She w
2 CONC as the daughter of Sir James Gordon of Lochinvar and Margaret Crichton. They had the following children:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT * James Cunningham, 7th Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT * John Cunningham, Laird of Ross
2 CONT * Lady Jean Cunningham who married George Haldane of Gleneagles (died 18 October 1574). After his death she married Roger Kirkpatrick of Closeburn.
2 CONT * Lady Katherine Cunningham who married Robert Fergusson, 9th Laird of Craigdarroch (died about 1613).
2 CONT * Lady Margaret Cunningham who married Sir Lachlan Mor Maclean of Duart (died 5 August 1598)
2 CONT * Lady Elizabeth Cunningham who married (1) in 1579 to James Crawford of Auchinames. After his death she married Alexander Cuninghame, 5th Laird of Craigends. Elizabeth died before 7 September 1614.
2 CONT * Lady Susannah Cunningham who married John Napier of Kilmahew
2 CONT
2 CONT William died between 1576 and 24 February 1579/80.
2 CONT
2 CONT William is a 14th great-grandfather of Prince William, Duke of Cambridge.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References===
2 CONT
