1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN CUNNINGHAM OF ROSS===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Cunningham of Ross is mentioned in a MS. genealogy of the family. He witnessed a sasine in favour of his brother James on 9 July 1576, and he had a sasine from his brother the Earl 2 May 1581. His son James appears as a su
2 CONC bstitute in an entail of the lands of Kilmaronok by William, eighth Earl, as Master of Glencairn. Douglas confuses this John with his nephew of the same name. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/241/mode/1
2 CONC up The Scots Peerage IV: pp. 242-3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 May 1579: Instrument of Seisin dated 13 July 1579 in favor of Susannah Cunningham in an annualrent corresponding to the sum of 50 merks payable from the lands of Glencross, redeemable on payment of said sum in the church of 
2 CONC Kilmaurs proceeding on a charter by William Earl of Glencairn and Dame Janet Gordon his wife. Witnesses, John Cunningham of Ross, son of the Earl, Mr. John Porterfield, minister, and William Cochrane, at Kilmaronock 28 May 1579. [
2 CONC http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f103&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+cunningham+of+ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=yNational Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, referenc
2 CONC e GD39/1/103]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 December 1584: Decree arbitral given and pronounced by Alexander Commendator of Kilwinning and William Cunningham of Caprington as Judges Arbiters in the submission entered into between James Earl of Glencairn on the one par
2 CONC t and William Porterfield of that ilk and Alexander Porterfield his son (and apparent heir) (see GD39/1/113) for themselves and taking burden on them for Marion and Jean Porterfield's daughters of the said William Porterfield on t
2 CONC he other part anent the demolishing and down casting of the Castle of Duchal, away taking of the jewels, goods and gear therein and in the peilhouse thereto adjoining by the Earl and his complices, and what homage the said William
2 CONC  Porterfield should make to the Earl for the slaughter of umquhile Ninian Lindsay (brother german of John Lindsay of Blacketholme) his servant and to the kin and friends of the said Ninian etc. All actions by the Porterfields are 
2 CONC to be stopped against the Earl, John Cunningham of Ross, his brother and others; the Earl is not to proceed in putting the Porterfields to the horn, etc. etc. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?ref
2 CONC erence=GD39%2f1%2f118&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+cunningham+of+ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y  National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/118]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 March 1585: Charter by James Earl of Glencairn to Alexander Commendator of Kilwinning (his cousin) whereby in implement of a contract entered into between them, dated (blank) Feby 1585 the Earl dispones to the commendator in 
2 CONC liferent and Jean Cunningham, his daughter and her heirs, the 8 merk land of Shaw, the 4 merkland of Bowieston and 5 merk land of Lambrochton,lying in the barony of Kilmaurs (under reversion for £500). Witnesses, David Cunningham 
2 CONC of Robertland, Alexander Cunningham of Aiket, John Cunningham of Ross and John Cunningham of Caldwell. At Finlayson. (John Cunningham of Ross does not sign as witness, the others do so). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonli
2 CONC necatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f121&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+cunningham+of+ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/121]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 July 1592: Instrument of Seisin in favour of James Cunningham (son of late Alexander commendator of Kilwinning) (See GD39/1/121) in (the 8 merk land of Shaw) the 4 merk land of Bowieston and 5 merk land of Lambrochton, proce
2 CONC eding on a precept of clare constat by James Earl of Glencairn to the said James Cunningham as heir of Jean Cunningham his sister, daughter of Alexander commendator of Kilwinning. Witnesses to the precept, John Cunningham of Ross,
2 CONC  brother german of the Earl, Hugh Glen of Linthill and Robert Cunningham servitor to the Earl, dated at Finlayston 23 July 1592 (23 July 1592 was the last day of 25th Jas. VI. Do. 25 Jas. VI., 28 July 1592 was in 26 Jas. ). Witnes
2 CONC ses in the Instrument Thomas Smith in Shaw and Hugh Patrick Servitor to (John Blair) the Laird of Montgrenan. (James Cunningham is called "Adolescens"). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference
2 CONC =GD39%2f1%2f132&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+cunningham+of+ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/132]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 September 1596: Contract between John Napier, fiar of Merchiston and John Cunningham of Ross by which Napier leases to Cunningham and his sub-tenants, not of name Logan or Cunningham of house of Drumquhassle, the 4 poundland
2 CONC s of Blairour for 19 years. Witnesses: Alexander Menteith; Walter Buchanan in Milton; and James Baillie. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD430%2f148&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+cun
2 CONC ningham+of+ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of Napier Family, reference GD430/148]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1599: Letters of reversion by John Cunningham of Ross and Margaret Cunningham, his spouse, in favour of Archibald Napier, fiar of Merchiston, with consent of John Napier, his father, over 28 bolls oat meal and £20 Scots from 4 
2 CONC poundlands of Blairour, in earldom of Lennox and sheriffdom of Dumbarton. Witnesses: John Napier, apparent of Kilmahew; Alexander Menteith; John Dunlop; James Balloch, servants of said John Napier; and Robert Alexander, notary. Ta
2 CONC g, no seal. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD430%2f152&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+cunningham+of+ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of Napier 
2 CONC Family, reference GD430/152]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 May 1609: Tack by Mr William Fullerton parson of Dreghorn, with consent of King James VI, to James Earl of Glencairn and Dame Margaret Campbell his wife and longest liver of them, (and their heirs) of the teind sheaves of the
2 CONC  10 merk land of Bowieston and Bowiestonhead, the 5 merk land of Titwood, 5 merk land of Lambrochton, 5 merk land of Third part, 4 merk land of Whiterig, 4 merk (and 10/-) land of Langlands, 32 shilling land of Alton, 12 merk land
2 CONC  of Southwick and 16 shilling land of Shawmilbushes, all lying in the parish of Dreghorn and barony of Kilmaurs (for 19 years from the Feast of "Lambmass" (1 Augt) last past).Witnesses, Alexander Cunningham of Crosshill, James Cun
2 CONC ningham of Aiket, John Cunningham of Ross, Gabriel Cunningham of Carcuran. At Kilmaurs. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f148&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+cunningham+of+ros
2 CONC s&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/148]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 May 1609: Contract between James Earl of Glencairn and Mr William Fullerton parson of Dreghorn, whereby for the sum of 2000 merks, the Earl obliges him to infeft the said Mr William Fullerton his heirs and assignees in an ann
2 CONC ual rent of 200 merks payable from the barony of Kilmaurs or any part thereof. Witnesses (Alexander Cunningham of Corsehill) James Cunningham of Aiket, John Cunningham of Ross etc. (Gilbert Cunningham (probably error of copying fo
2 CONC r Gabriel C.) At Kilmaurs. (Recorded in Books of Council Edinburgh 13 July 1614). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f149&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+cunningham+of+ross&ko=p
2 CONC &r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/149]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11-26 July 1618: Disposition by William Lord Kilmaurs with consent of Dame Janet Ker, his wife and William Cunningham writer donator to his liferent escheat to Alexander Cunningham of Crosshill his heirs and assignees of the la
2 CONC nds of Lambrochton and Thirdpart, Whiterig and Lochend, with the Mill called Crumshawmill, the parts of the lands of Alton and Outroddings, Langlands and Burnside occupied as stated, all lying in the barony of Kilmaurs. But redeem
2 CONC able on payment by Lord Kilmaurs his heirs and successors to said Alexander Cunningham and his foresaid of £10,160 of fine gold and silver containing procuratory of resignation. Quotes contract of 21 May last at Kilmaurs between W
2 CONC illiam Lord K, Dame Janet Ker his wife, Sir William Cunningham of Caprington Knt and Alexander Cunningham of Corsehill. Witnesses, John Cunningham of Ross (Rawn or Rawe)? William Cunningham, William Cunningham of Clonbeith, Mr Dav
2 CONC id Cunningham, minister at Kilmalcolm, David Fullerton of Knockinlaw and William Maxwell, son of the Laird of Newark. At Edinburgh and Finlayston. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%
2 CONC 2f1%2f187&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+cunningham+of+ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/187]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
