1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LADY JEAN CUNNINGHAM===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Bogus Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''According to the family history published in 1858, Lady Jean Cunningham, here treated, married Sir Roger Kirkpatrick of Closeburn. This history refers to Sir Roger and the claimed marriage in the following terms: "S
2 CONC ir Roger succeeded his uncle, and married The Right Honorable Lady Jean Cunningham, daughter of William Earl of Glencairne, grand-aunt to James, first Duke of Hamilton, and to William Earl of Glencairne, Lord High Chancellor of Sc
2 CONC otland". [https://archive.org/details/kirkpatrickofclo00kirk/page/40/mode/1up Kirkpatrick of Closeburn: p. 41] This is wrong. Jean Cunningham actually married Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/n
2 CONC rsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD19%2f18&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jean+cunningham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD19/18]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Poor Scholarship and Unreliable Copyology'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''In his account of the Cunningham Earls of Glencairn for the Scots Peerage, the Reverend John Anderson correctly reported that Lady Jean Cunningham, here treated, was married  first to George Haldane of Gleneagles, a
2 CONC nd secondly to Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/243/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: p. 243] For reasons that cannot presently be explained, Sir Bernard Burke misreported 
2 CONC these facts in his History of the Peerage and Baronetage, where he claimed that Lady Jean had actually married Roger Kirkpatrick of Closeburn. This was not not the only error made by Burke, he also identified Roger Kirkpatrick of 
2 CONC Closeburn as the son of Henry Kirkpatrick of Closeburn. [https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_Pf8cAAAAYAAJ/page/n1331/mode/1up Burke (1914), pp. 1136-38]. Seemingly without question, Burke's careless errors have been followed by a n
2 CONC umber of modern copyologists. For example. [http://www.thepeerage.com/p49180.htm Darryl Lundy's Peerage] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Cunningham,_6th_Earl_of_Glencairn Wikipedia]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of Identity===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Cunningham, here treated, is the daughter of William, Earl of Glencairn, and his wife Janet Gordon.  [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/242/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: p. 243]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Jean Cunningham, here treated married (contract 15 February 1572) George Haldane of Gleneagles. He died before October 1574. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/242/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: p
2 CONC . 243]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Jean Cunningham, here treated, married,Thomas, Kirkpatrick of Closeburn.  [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/242/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: p. 243]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 April 1573: Charter by George Haldane of Glenneagles to JANET CUNNINGHAM (Conynghame), daughter of William, Master of Glencairn (Glencarne), his future spouse, in liferent, of the lands and barony of Ruskie (Ruskye) and Lanr
2 CONC ik in the sheriffdom of Perth and, because Elizabeth Londie, mother of said George, is infeft in said lands in liferent, of the lands of Baturrycht Minor, Kirkgour, Baturrycht Major, Barlosk, Blayrneile, Wester Auchinkerocht, Ladr
2 CONC ischebeg, Catteris Easter (Eister), Wester and Middle Drumdasche, Treynbeg, Fynwiktennent, Ros, Lurg and Calyemoir in the barony of Haldane and sheriffdom of Perth in real warrandice during the lifetime of said Elizabeth. [Cf RMS,
2 CONC  1593 - 1608, no 264n.] [Seal.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD19%2f16&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD19%2f16&ro=m&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the
2 CONC  family of Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, Dumfries-shire, reference GD19/16]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 August 1577: REX &c., concessit THOME KIRKPATRIK filio et heredi apparenti Rogeri K. de Closburne, JEHANNE CUNYNGHAME ejus spouse future, filie legitime Willelmi com. de Glencarne, in ejus viduitate, — 10 librat. terrarum an
2 CONC tiqui extentus de Auchinlek, cum tenentibus &c., vic. Drumfreis ; — quas dictus Rog. resignavit : — Tenend. dictis Tho. et Jehanne in con- juncta infeodatione eorumque alteri diutius viventi, heredibusque inter eos legitime procre
2 CONC andis, quibus deficientibus, legit, et propinquioribus heredibus et assignatis dicti Thome quibuscunque : — Test, ut in aliis cartis &c. xxxiv. 536
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 September 1577: Charter by Roger Kirkpatrick of Closeburn to Thomas Kirkpatrick, his son and heir apparent, of the lands and barony of Closeburn and Newton under reservation of liferent, in implement of a marriage contract da
2 CONC ted [blank] 1577 between said Roger and Thomas Kirkpatrick, and JEAN CUNNINGHAM (Cunynghame), relict of George Haldane (Halden) of Glennages (Glennegas), with consent of William, lord of Glencairn her father. [Seal.] (With instrum
2 CONC ent of sasine dated 5 September 1577.) [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD19%2f18&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jean+cunningham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Pape
2 CONC rs of the family of Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, Dumfries-shire, reference GD19/18]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 April 1599: Notarial instrument narrating that Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn demanded possession of the lands and barony of Ruskie and Lanrik (Lanerik) in the sheriffdom of Perth, in fulfilment of the marriage contract of J
2 CONC EAN CUNNINGHAM, now spouse of said Thomas, which demand James Haldane of Glennages (Glenhageis) agreed to, in token whereof he handed over the keys of the manor place thereof, the said Thomas renouncing on his side all claim to th
2 CONC e lands of the barony of Haldane in the Lennox. [Cf GD19/16.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD19%2f31&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=closeburn&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Reco
2 CONC rds of Scotland, Papers of the family of Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, Dumfries-shire, reference GD19/31]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Printed Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/n5/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1546-1580. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. )H. M. Ge
2 CONC reral Register House, Edinburgh, 1886), 1180 pp. including indexes and errata]'''
2 CONT
