2 CONT ----
2 CONT Agnew, Andrew (d. 1547) of Lochnaw.  Only son of Patrick Agnew (d. 1513) and his wife Katherine, daughter of Sir Robert Gordon of Lochinvar.  Hereditary Sheriff of Wigtownshire from 1513; outlawed in 1527 with Sir Robert Gordon of
2 CONC  Lochinvar, his uncle, for the murder in Edinburgh of Sir Thomas Maclellan of Bomby; outlawry remitted 1538.  He married Agnes, daughter of Sir Alexander Stewart of Garlies and had issue: 
2 CONT * (1) Patrick Agnew (1529-91) (q.v.); 
2 CONT * (2) Gilbert Agnew (c.1530-c.1600) of Galdenoch; m. Margaret, co-heiresws of Uchtred MacDowell of Baraj, and had issue one son;
2 CONT * (3) Alexander Agnew of Ardoch, sheriff depute; 
2 CONT * (4) Helen Agnew, m. John MacCulloch of Torhouse.
2 CONT * He inherited Lochnaw Castle from his father in 1513.
2 CONT * Killed in action at the Battle of Pinkie in 1547. https://landedfamilies.blogspot.com/2013/07/57-agnew-of-lochnaw-castle-baronets.html<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
