1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Margaret Gordon:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p15040.htm#i150397
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Gordon [1]
2 CONT *F, #150397
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 May 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Gordon married Sir Hugh Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell of Loudoun, son of Sir Matthew Campbell of Loudoun and Isabel Drummond, in 1572. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Sir John Gordon of Lochinvar and Juliana Home.[1],[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1572, her married name became Campbell.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Gordon and Sir Hugh Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell of Loudoun
2 CONT *1. Isabel Campbell d. 1612
2 CONT *2. George Campbell, Master of Loudoun+[2] d. Mar 1611/12
2 CONT *3. Juliana Campbell [1] b. c 1581, d. a 1648
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume II, page 283. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2406. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 2407.
2 CONT
