1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===GILBERT ADAIR===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gilbert Adair is the brother of William Adair of Kinhilt.  The name of his mother has not been identified. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD141%2f89&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gilb
2 CONC ert+adair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD141/89]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 May 1611: Precept of Clare Constat by John McDowell of Logane, directed to David Asloane, dwelling in Logane as bailie to infeft Andrew Agnew as son and heir to the deceased Walter Agnew of Killumquha in the 2½ merkland of K
2 CONC illumquha-Agnew and the 20/- lands of Nether Grenane in the barony of Logane, held in feu of the said John McDowell according to the charter given to the said deceased Walter Agnew. Wit:- Gilbert Adair, brother to William Adair of
2 CONC  Kinhilt, Gilbert Agnew, burgess of Stranraer, Andrew McDowell in Culcossane and James Glover notary. Signed by granter and witnesses. No tag or seal. Endorsed with abbreviate of sasine, 20 June 1612. Wit:- William Agnew of Croach
2 CONC , Gilbert Adair, brother to Wm. Adair of Kinhilt, Gilbert Agnew, son of said Wm. Agnew and John Agnew, dwelling at Grenane. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD141%2f89&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn
2 CONC =n&tp=n&k=gilbert+adair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, McDouall family of Logan, Wigtownshire, reference GD141/89]'''
