2 ADDR
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2037.htm#i20362
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Archibald Douglas was born after 1604. He was the son of William Douglas, 1st Earl of Queensberry and Lady Isabel Kerr.1   He lived at Dornock, Dumfries-shire, ScotlandG.1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Archibald Douglas
2 CONT
2 CONT William Douglas+2
2 CONT Major James Douglas+1 b. 1634, d. a 1663
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Douglas-1069#:~:text=Sir%20Archibald%20Douglas%20was%20a,of%20the%20Douglases%20of%20Dornock.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Archibald Douglas was the son of William Douglas, the 1st Earl of Queensberry, and Isabel (Kerr) Douglas. He had to have been born either in or before his mother died in 1628. He was the founder of the Douglases of Dornock. He
2 CONC  filed his Will on December 11, 1679, and died either on or after that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT It looks as if there is confusion on who the sons of Sir Archibald were, and how many he had. Together, the 2 sources list 3 sons for Sir Archibald:-
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.) William Douglas of Dornock: Johnston states that he has multiple Wills and that they were recorded on May 25, 1717, March 29, 1736, and February 22, 1750. Johnston says that he married Alison Pennycook, who recorded her Will i
2 CONC n January of 1698. thepeerage.com also lists a William Douglas who is a son of Sir Archibald, which means they are one and the same.
2 CONT
2 CONT thepeerage.com gives the following descendants: William Douglas of Dornock sires William who sires James who sires brothers William and James, of the 2 brothers, only James has children, who are the siblings Clementine, Archibald,
2 CONC  Philidelphia, William, William. (No, that is not a typo, James really did have 2 sons named William, the first of them listed probably died before the other was born, allowing the name to be used again, which was not unheard of.)
2 CONT
2 CONT George Harvey Johnston gives the following descendants: William Douglas of Dornock sires James who sires brothers James, John, and William. Of the 3 brothers, only James had any children. One of them was Archibald Douglas, who die
2 CONC d without children. Archibald did have sisters, however, who inherited from him.
