1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JEAN MONTGOMERY===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from Paterson's History of Ayrshire===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The testament, testamentar, and inventar of the guidis, geir, debts, and sowmes of money, quhilks perteint to vmquhile Jeane Montgomerie, spous to Robert Boyd of Portincross, within the parochin of Kilbryd, the time of hir dece
2 CONC is, quha deceist in the moneth of December, the zeir of God Jai vi c. twentie ane zeiris, ffaithfullie maid and gevin vp be hir awin mouth, as hir latterwill and testament, of the date vnderwrittin, mair fullie proports.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inventar'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Item, the defunct and hir said spous had, the tyme foirsaid, perteining to thame, and in their possessioun, the guids and geir vnderwrittin, of the availls, qualities and pryces efterspecifit, viz. ane quhyt hors, pryce xl lib.
2 CONC  Item, ane dvne hors, pryce xl lib. Item, four auld pleughe naigis, pryce of the peice x lib., inde xl lib. Item, audit tydie ky, pryce of thame all Ixxxxvi lib. Item, auchtein zoung quoyis, pryce of thame all Ixxxx lib. Item, sax
2 CONC  stirks, pryce of them all xii lib. Item, of aittis in the borne and bornezaird, thrie- scoir bolls aitts, pryce of the boll iiii lib., inde ii c. xl lib. Item, of beir in the borne and borne- zaird, togidder with the ferme beir r
2 CONC estand awand be the tennents, extends to ane hundrit and xii bolls, pryce of the boll vi lib., inde of beir and ferme inde v c. Ixxii lib. Item, ane boitt, with her graith, pryce Ixvi lib. xiii s. iiii d. Item, ane skout, (?) pryc
2 CONC e x lib. Item, pleughe and pleughe irnes, with carris and harrowis, pryce viii lib. Item, ten feddir beddis and vii bowsters, estimat to i c. lib. Item, twelf pair of blankettis, pryce of the pair thrie lib., iude xxxvilib. Item, 
2 CONC thrie caddayis, pryce of thame xxiiii lib. Item, four sewit coveringis, pryce of thame xxvi lib. xiii s. iiiicl. Item, four ould caddais, pryce of thamo x lib. Item, sax aukl coveringis, pryce of thame vi lib. Item, tlirie pair of
2 CONC  courtingis, pryce x lib. Item, ten pair of lyning scheitts, pryce xllib. Item, of round scheittis and hardin claith, csti r mat to xx lib. Item, thrie pair of held scheittis, ostimat to sax pundis money. Item, twelf cod- waris, p
2 CONC ryce v lib. Item, fyve buirdclaithis, pryce x lib. Item, four dussane of serveittis, pryce x lib. Item, aucht breid claitliis, pryce vilib. Item, four lang towallis, pryce iii lib. Item, ane comp- ter claith, pryce xiilib. Item, n
2 CONC ync [cutihornis] pryce iii [or viii] lib. Item, thric chancleris, twa bassingis, ane lawer, ane pewldir stoip pryce of thame all xiii lib. vi s. viii d. Item, twa dussane twa plaittis, twentie ane truncheours, twa salsours, and an
2 CONC e saltfalt, twa wattir potts, prycc of thame all xv lib. Item, four pottis, thric speitts, with ane pair of raids, pryco of thame xvi lib. Item, ane litle caldroune, ane kettill, thrie pannis, ane girdill, thrie cruiks, ane chymna
2 CONC y, pryce of all xxxvi lib. Item, of kistis, beddis, and vther in- spret within the defunct's hous, with the abuilze- ment of his bodie, estimat to Ixvi lib. xiii s. iiii d.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Summa of the inventar, jaj vi c.lxxv lib.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Legacie.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''At Portincors, the xix day of December, the zeir of God jaivic. and twentie ane zeiris, the uhilk day Jeane Montgomerie nominat Robert Boyd of Portincors, hir husband, executour. em, my will, and I ordane my husband, to help ur
2 CONC  bairnes, Nans, Elspeth, and Barbara Boyds, in this manor, viz. to Nans viii c. merks, to Elspeth vii c. merkis, and to Barbara fyve hundrith merks. And to our eldest sone Robert, ane undrith merks, and ane broune naig, to George,
2 CONC  ie hundrith merkis, to Archibald tlirie hunrith merkis, to Gavin thrie hundrith merks, and James thrie hundrith merks. And farder, I quiest my husband, for the love that has been betwixt my husband and me, and for the favour he b
2 CONC eiris to our bairnes abonewritin, to give the thrid part of the movabill guidis and geir that apperteins to ws, to be equallie devydit amangis our four zoungcst sones, George, Archibald, Williame and James, and our thrie doehters,
2 CONC  Nans, Elspeth, and Barbara Boydis. And I leif my brother, Sir Robert Montgomerie of Skelmorlie, and George Montgomerie, our brother, to be overseers to my bairnes ; and ordanes thame, with my husband, to gif the portioun that is 
2 CONC left to ony of my dochteris to the rest of our bairnes, incais, as God forbid, ony of thame abuis their bodeys in harlotrie, &c. [https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyo02pateuoft/page/134/mode/1up History of Ayrshire II: 136
2 CONC -7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 21 October 1623. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory, of Jeane Montgomerie spous to Robert Boyd of Portincorss, parish of Kilbryd, reference C
2 CONC C9/7/19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''c. 1580: Marriage contract of ROBERT BOYD, SON OF ARCHIBALD OF PORTINCROSS, and Jean Montgomery, daughter of Sir Robert Montgomery of Skelmorlie. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3
2 CONC %2f2%2f10%2f26&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=portincross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/2/10/26]'''
2 CONT
