1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Richard Murray, of Cockpool</strong>, 6th son of Sir Charles Murray, of the same, by Margaret, daughter of Hugh (Somerville) Lord Somerville [S], succeeded, in 1620, his elder brother Sir James Murray in that estate, 
2 CONC and was created a Baronet [S], 19 July 1625, sealed 20 October 1625, with rem. to heirs male whatsoever, and a grant of , presumably, 16,000 acres in Nova Scotia, entitled the Barony of Cockpool, of which he had sasine in October 
2 CONC following. In 1635 he had sasine of the lands of Lockerbie, Hutton, Hoddam etc. He died s.p. probably unmarried, in 1636."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n311/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 292
2 CONT
2 CONT "(403) <strong>Sir Richard Murray of Cockpool</strong>, died s.p. 1636. He was served heir to his brother, Sir James (No. 402), 28th March 1621 and 1st June 1630. On 19th July 1625 he was created a BARONET. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ARMS in Font's MS., c. 1624. Same as Sir Charles (No. 401). 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his brother."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/98/mode/2up The heraldry of the Murrays: with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees], by G. Harvey Johnston, 1910, 
2 CONC page 99, paragraph 403
