1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARGARET FLEMING, COUNTESS OF ATHOLL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 September 1579: Vicecomes respondebit pro £64 de relevio omnium et singularum TERRARUM ET BARONIE DE RETTRAY, cum molendinis, silvis, piscariis, tenentibus, tenandriis, et liberetenentium servitiis earundem, et pro £20 de rel
2 CONC evio bine partis ville et terrarum de Inverchroekie et Chapeltoun, bine partis ville et terrarum de Murtclarie, bine partis terrarum de Dalrilyeane, bine partis ville de terrarum de Dalma, bine partis ville et terrarum de Leanoch,
2 CONC  bine partis terrarum de Petcurrane, alias Pitbrane et Glengleneth, et bine partis ville et terrarum de Kynnarde, cum molendinis, silvis, piscariis, partibus, pendiculis, tenentibus, tenandriis, et liberetenentium servitiis omnium
2 CONC  et singularum terrarum et villarum particulariter superius expressatarum ; ac tertie partis terrarum de Glenschie, cum silvis earundem, jacentium infra bondas de Strathardill et Glenschie ac balliam suam ; regi debitis per sasina
2 CONC m datam dicto JOANNI ATHOLIE COMITIi, reservato tamen vitali redditu omnium et singularum dictarum terrarum et baronie ac aliarum particulariter prescriptarum domine MARGARETE FLEMYNG, COMITISSE ATHOLIE, pro toto tempore vite sue,
2 CONC  secundum tenorem sui infeofamenti earundem. (Edinburgh, 7 September.] [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollss00exchgoog/page/554/mode/1up RSRS XX: 554]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 September 1579: Vicecomes respondebit pro £166 13e. 4d. de firmis dominii de Balvany, cum castro et fortalicio ejusdem, tenentibus, tenandriis, et liberetenentium servitiis earundem, et omnium et singularum terrarum et baroni
2 CONC arum de Botrophin, Bocharme, et Aberlour, unacum advocatione et donatione ecclesie de Aberloure et capellaniarum de Bocharme, et omnium et singularum terrarum de Buquhomie et Kynnynvie unacum molendinis et multuris predictarum ter
2 CONC rarum, jacentium infra balliam suam, existentium in manibus supremi domini nostri regis termini Penthecostes ultime preteriti sasina non recuperata ; et pro quatuor rubeis rosis per duplicationem albefirme dicti dominii de Balvany
2 CONC , cum castro et fortalicio ejusdem, tenentibus, tenandriis, et liberetenentium servitiis earundem, et dictarum terrarum de Botrophin, Bocharme, et Aberloure, unacum advocatione et donatione ecclesie et capellaniarum prescriptarum 
2 CONC ; necnon pro 2d. per duplicationem albefirme dictarum terrarum de Bukquhomie et Kynnynvie, cum molendinis et multuris ; regis debitis per sasinam datam JOANNI ATHOLIE COMITI, salvo tamen vitali redditu unius davate terrarum de Edi
2 CONC nglassie, unius davate terrarum de Ardbrek, unius davate terrarum de Auchloncartie, unius davate terrarum de Edinvillie, unius davate terrarum de Kynnynvie, et unius davate terrarum de Towiemoir et Towiebeg, demptis molendinis, mu
2 CONC lturis, et sequelis earundem, domine MARGARETE FLEMYNG, COMITISSE ATHOLIE, pro toto tempore vite sue, secundum tenorem sui infeofamenti earundem. (Edinburgh, 7 September. ] [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollss00exchgoog/pa
2 CONC ge/554/mode/1up RSRS XX: 554]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollss00exchgoog/page/n10/mode/1up Rotuli Scaccarii Regum Scotorum. The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland. Vol. XX. 1568-1579. Edited by George Powell McNeill, MA., LL.B., Advocate (H. M. General
2 CONC  Register House, Edinburgh, 1898), 685 pp. including index]’’’
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Fleming-160
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Fleming was born c. 1528, daughter to Malcolm Fleming, 3rd Lord Fleming and his wife Janet Stewart, natural daughter of King James IV. by Isabel Stewart, Countess of Bothwell, daughter of James, third Earl of Buchan.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, first, to Robert Graham, Master of Graham, who was killed at the Battle of Pinkie Cleugh on 10 September 1547 along with her father and a brother in law. This marriage likely occurred c. 1545.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly (contract 30 January 1549), to Thomas Erskine, Master of Erskine, without issue. She had a charter in her viduity (widowhood) in liferent from John Cunningham of Drumquhassell on 1 March 1549 in implement of 
2 CONC her marriage-contract with Thomas, Master of Erskine.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, thirdly, (contract 1 April 1557), to John Stewart, fourth Earl of Atholl, Lord Chancellor. They had a charter of the lands of Inglassey.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is said to have possessed powers of incantation, and at the birth of James VI. cast the pains of labour from the Queen on the Lady Hires.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was dead before 15 March 1587.
2 CONT
