1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Barnabas O'Brien:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2399.htm#i23987
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnabas O'Brien, 5th Earl of Thomond (actually, 6th Earl of Thomond, his brother Henry was the 5th Earl)
2 CONT *M, #23987, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1590, 
2 CONT *d. 1657
2 CONT *Last Edited=17 Dec 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.83%
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnabas O'Brien, 5th Earl of Thomond was born circa 1590. He was the son of Donough O'Brien, 3rd Earl of Thomond and Helen Roche.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Anne Fermor, daughter of Sir George Fermor and Mary Curson, on 17 July 1615 at Easton Neston, Northamptonshire, England.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1657. He was buried on 15 November 1657.
2 CONT
2 CONT Career:
2 CONT *He was educated BNC Oxford.[3] 
2 CONT *He was Member of Parliament (M.P.) (I Parl) Coleraine , Carlow and Ennis 1634, knighted 1615 in 1613.[3] 
2 CONT *He was Privy Counsellor (P.C.) (I ) in 1639.[3] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 5th Earl of Thomond [I., 1552] before 22 April 1639. 
2 CONT *In 1641 having been neutral between the Confederate Irish and the English forces , he came out in support of Parliament during the full English Civil War 1646, gave up Bunratty Castle and retired to England.[3] 
2 CONT *On 3 May 1645 a document creating him Marquess of Billing passed the Privy Seal but Letters Patent were never completed and he never took up that peerage designation.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Barnabas O'Brien, 5th Earl of Thomond
2 CONT *1. Lady Mary O'Brien+[4] d. 1686
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Barnabas O'Brien, 5th Earl of Thomond and Anne Fermor
2 CONT *1. Penelope O'Brien+[1]
2 CONT *2. Henry O'Brien, 6th Earl of Thomond+[1] b. c 1620, d. 2 May 1691
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003). Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Bar
2 CONC onetage, 107th edition. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United K
2 CONC ingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XII/1, page 709. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage. [S37] Charles Mosl
2 CONC ey, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 2033. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 406.
