2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Graham-5958
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert Graham was born about 1516, the 4th son of William Graham, 3rd Earl of Menteith and Margaret Moubray.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, sometime before 1562 Helen Kincaid, daughter of John Kincaid of Warristown and widow of Robert Crauford.[2] .
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert and Helen had at least 5 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # A daughter, Marion[2]
2 CONT # Eldest son and heir William[2]
2 CONT # 2nd son John[2]
2 CONT # 3rd son James[2]
2 CONT # 4th son Andrew[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Family Records'', By Ashworth Peter Burke.  Page 272.  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=MZRAAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA272&ots=24QRVTAor0&dq=Gilbert%20of%20Gartrenich%2C%20the%20second%20son&pg=PA272#v=onepage&q=Gilbert%20of%20Gartrenic
2 CONC h,%20the%20second%20son&f=false GoogleBooks] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT The representative of this family claims, as heir male of the illustrious and noble family of GRAHAM, Earls of Strathearn, Menteith and Airth, descended from the Royal family of Scotland, the ancient earldoms of that family, which
2 CONC  have remained dormant since the death s.p. of William, 8th Earl of Menteith in 1694. William, 3rd Earl of Menteith, d. 7 April, 1544, leaving with other issue (see STUART), a fourth son,
2 CONT
2 CONT GILBERT GRAHAM, of Gartavertane, who in 1572 resigned these lands to the Crown for a regrant in favour of William, his son and apparent heir. He also resigned, in 1576, the lands of Gartrenich, alias Auchmore, in the earldom of Me
2 CONC nteith, to the fifth earl, apparently for the purpose of a regrant in favour of his younger son, into whose possession they passed. In a lease of the lands of Tulliallan, .1551, he calls himself "brother-germane to ane nobill and 
2 CONC mychty lord, Johnne, Erll of Menteyth." Dying before 25 June, 1577, he left issue,
2 CONT
2 CONT I. William, of Gartavertane, who on that date was served heir to his uncle Robert, of Gartmore, and whose son, Robert, s. to that estate, and was father of Gilbert, last male of Gartmore, who was s. by his sister Agnes in said lan
2 CONC ds which she conveyed to her father-in-law, William, 1st Earl of Stirling in 1636.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. GILBERT, of whom presently.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Marion, m. Alexander Alexander, of Menstry.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Agnes, m. Jasper Graham, of Blaircessnock, from whom the Grahams, of Gartur (extinct since 1818). He was murdered by the Grahams, of Duchray, in 1618.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
