2 CONT George Seton (c. 1531-1585/6), 5th [or 7th] Lord Seton.  He was the 5th George Seton and the 7th lord.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Seton V, 7th Lord Seton''' (1531–1586), was a Lord of the Parliament of Scotland, Master of the Household of Mary, Queen of Scots, and Provost of Edinburgh. He was the eldest son of George Seton, 6th Lord Seton, and Eliz
2 CONC abeth Hay, a daughter of John Hay, 3rd Lord Hay of Yester. His childhood and schooling were in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Seton,_7th_Lord_Seton
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page for George Seton, 5th Lord Seton:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10953.htm#i109521
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton, 5th Lord Seton [1]
2 CONT *M, #109521, 
2 CONT *b. 1531, 
2 CONT *d. 8 January 1585/86
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.43%
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton, 5th Lord Seton was born in 1531.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT A contract for the marriage of George Seton, 5th Lord Seton and Isabel Hamilton was signed on 2 August 1550.[4],[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 8 January 1585/86.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of George Seton, 4th Lord Seton and Elizabeth Hay.[3] 
2 CONT *He was educated at France.[3] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 5th Lord Seton [S., 1451] on 17 July 1549.[1]
2 CONT *He partipicated in an ordinance between 1557 and 1559; Provost of Edinburgh.[3] 
2 CONT *On 17 December 1557 he was appointed by the Scottish Parliament to attend the marriage of Mary Queen of Scots with the Dauphin of France.[3] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Master of the Household to Mary Queen of Scots in 1563.[3] 
2 CONT *In 1568 he fled to Low Countries after Mary Queen of Scots defeat at the Battle of Langside.[3] He was a waggoner between 1568 and 1570.[3] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland] in 1573.[3] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Scottish Ambassador to France in 1583.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of George Seton, 5th Lord Seton and Isabel Hamilton
2 CONT *1. George Seton, Master of Seton3 d. Mar 1562
2 CONT *2. Sir William Seton+3 d. Jul 1635
2 CONT *3. Margaret Seton+1 b. bt 1551 - 1558, d. b 10 Feb 1615/16
2 CONT *4. Robert Seton, 1st Earl of Winton+5 b. 1552, d. 22 Mar 1603
2 CONT *5. Sir John Seton of Barns3 b. b 1555, d. b 11 Jun 1594
2 CONT *6. Alexander Seton, 1st Earl of Dunfermline+3 b. 1555, d. 16 Jun 1622
2 CONT
