1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN BUCHANAN OF THAT ILK===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://archive.org/stream/buchananbooklife00buchuoft#page/183/mode/1up Biographical Summary from The Buchanan Book]===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Buchanan, who married Annabel Erskine, daughter of Adam, Commendator of Cambuskenneth, son of the Master of Mar, had (1) George, his successor, and (2) Walter Buchanan. This Sir John Buchanan *' was," says Auchmar, "ac
2 CONC counted the worst, if not the " only bad one of all the Lairds of Buchanan;" and by his frequent travels into foreign nations and other extravagances had involved his estate in such an immense debt that his grandson at first found
2 CONC  it inconvenient to enter as heir. [https://archive.org/stream/buchananbooklife00buchuoft#page/183/mode/1up The Buchanan Book: p. 183]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Chiefs of Clan Buchanan= 
2 CONT *15th – [http://www.geni.com/people/George-Buchanan/6000000020945399669 George Buchanan],[76][77] (Guthrie Smith identifies him as 10th Chief and Buchanan of Auchmar identifies him as 17th Chief) succeed his grandfather, [http://w
2 CONC ww.geni.com/people/Walter-Buchanan/6000000002188091234 Walter 14th of Buchanan], in 1526 and died 1560. He first married [http://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Buchanan/6000000000769956432?through=6000000020945399669 Margaret Edmons
2 CONC tone] and by her a son ([http://www.geni.com/people/John-Buchanan/6000000011635910537?through=6000000000769956432 John] [Guthrie Smith identifies him as 11th Chief but then goes on to advise that the Chiefship passed from John’s f
2 CONC ather to John’s son[78] and Buchanan of Auchmar identifies him as 18th Chief[79 who married [http://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Buchanan/6000000011277818134 Elizabeth Livingston] and by her had [http://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Ge
2 CONC orge-Buchanan-16th-Laird-of-Buchanan/6000000020945965920?through=6000000011277818134 George] [79] who succeeded his grandfather) and two daughters (Helen and Susanna). Second he married [http://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Buchanan/6
2 CONC 000000020945759381?through=6000000020945399669 Janet Cunningham] and by her had a son ([http://www.geni.com/people/William-Buchanan/6000000020945837059 William] first ancestor of the cadets of Auchmar) and a daughter ([http://www.
2 CONC geni.com/people/Margaret-Buchanan/6000000020945709520?through=6000000020945399669 Margaret]). 
2 CONT *16th – [http://www.geni.com/people/Sir-George-Buchanan-16th-Laird-of-Buchanan/6000000020945965920?through=6000000011277818134 Sir George Buchanan],[78][79] (Guthrie Smith identifies him as 12th Chief and Buchanan of Auchmar ident
2 CONC ifies him as 19th Chief) succeed his grandfather, [http://www.geni.com/people/George-Buchanan/6000000020945399669  George 15th of Buchanan], in 1561, married [http://www.geni.com/people/Lady-Mary-Graham/6000000020945873262 Lady Ma
2 CONC ry Graham] and by her one son '''([http://www.geni.com/people/John-Buchanan/6000000020945892285 John] his successor''') and two daughters (Helen and Susanna).  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Buchanan
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Buchanan book. The life of Alexander Buchanan, Q.C., of Montreal, followed by an account of the family of Buchanan http://www.archive.org/details/buchananbooklife00buchuoft
2 CONT
2 CONT *   XVII. Sir George Buchanan, succeeded his grandfather, George, Laird of Buchanan, in 1561. He married Lady Mary Graham, daughter of John, Earl of Menteith, and '''had John''' and two daughters, (1) Helen, who married Alexander 
2 CONC Colquhoun of Luss, and (2) Susanna, who married John Macfarlane of that Ilk. https://archive.org/stream/buchananbooklife00buchuoft#page/183/mode/1up
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''   XVIII. Sir John Buchanan, who married Annabel Erskine''', daughter of Adam, Commendator of Cambuskenneth, son of the Master of Mar, '''had,''' (1) George, his successor, and (2) Walter Buchanan. '''This Sir John Buchanan "w
2 CONC as," says Auchmar, "accounted the worst, if not the "only bad one of all the Lairds of Buchanan;" and by his frequent travels into foreign nations and other extravagances had involved his estate in such an immense debt that his gr
2 CONC andson at first found it inconvenient to enter as heir. 
2 CONT *   XIX. Sir George Buchanan, was Colonel of the Stirlingshire Regiment, and lost a great many of his regiment and kinsmen at the battle of Ennerkeithing, in which he was taken prisoner, and died in 1651.  .... etc.https://archive
2 CONC .org/stream/buchananbooklife00buchuoft#page/185/mode/1up  Sir George married Elizabeth Preston, only daughter of Sir George Preston of Craigmillar. He had one son, John and three daughters, (1) Helen, who married Sir John Rollo of
2 CONC  Bannockburn, (2) Agnes, who married James Stewart of Rosyth (3) Jean or Janet, who married John Leckie of that Ilk.  .... etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT  _______________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Strathendrick and its inhabitants from early times; an account of the parishes of Fintry, Balfron, Killearn, Drymen, Buchanan, and Kilmaronock (1896) http://archive.org/details/cu31924028090698; https://archive.org/stream/cu319
2 CONC 24028090698#page/n337/mode/1up Pg.288
2 CONT *   XII. GEORGE BUCHANAN of Buchanan succeeded his grandfather in 1561. On 27th March 1561 George Buchanan was retoured heir of George Buchanan his grandfather in the lands of Buchanan, Auchmar, and Sallochy, with the islands of C
2 CONC lairinch and Kepinch, and also the bell and alms of St. Kessog.6 He married Lady Mary Graham, daughter of John, Earl of Menteith;7 and had issue: '''(1) John'''; and two daughters: (1) Helen, who married Alexander Colquhoun of Lus
2 CONC s (marriage contract dated 18th August 1595);8 and (2) Susanna, who was the first wife of John Macfarlane of that Ilk, by whom she had no children.9 https://archive.org/stream/cu31924028090698#page/n338/mode/1up Pg.289
2 CONT *'''      XIII. JOHN BUCHANAN of Buchanan had gift of the ward and non-entry of  all his estates since the death of his father''', Sir George, '''dated, Perth, 28th March 1599. On 26th October 1602 he is retoured heir of his fathe
2 CONC r''' Sir George Buchanan '''in Buchanan, and other lands, and in the same year he had a thirty-eight years' tack of the whole teinds of Kilmaronock from his father-in-law''', Adam, Commendator of Cambuskenneth, '''to him and his w
2 CONC ife Annabel Erskine. By Annabel Erskine he had at least two sons''': (1) George; and (2) Walter, who was at Glasgow College 7th March 1620.1 
2 CONT *   XIV. GEORGE BUCHANAN of Buchanan married Elizabeth Preston, only daughter of Sir George Preston of Craigmillar, Knt. He had an infeftment as heir-apparent of his father. Sir John Buchanan, in the estate of Buchanan, to him and
2 CONC  his wife, Elizabeth Preston, 10th July 1629. He and his father were dead before 1653. He left issue: one son John, and three daughters: (1) Helen, who became second wife of Sir John Rollo of Bannockburn;2  (2) Agnes, who married 
2 CONC James Stewart of Rosyth3  (marriage contract dated 7th July 1649);4 and (3) Jean or Janet,5  who married, 5th December 1661, John Leckie of that Ilk.6 
2 CONT * .... etc. _______________
