1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===KATHERINE RUTHVEN Lady Glenorchy===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Katherine Rutven is the daughter of William, Lord Ruthven, and Janet Halyburton. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#page/260/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 260]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Katherine Ruthven, lady Glenorchy. She was alive in February 1584 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f37%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n
2 CONC &tn=n&tp=n&k=ruthven&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1560&dt=1600&di=n NRS: GD112/37/1] but died in or before 1587. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f23%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ruthven&ko
2 CONC =p&r=&ro=s&df=1560&dt=1600&di=n NRS: GD112/23/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===EVIDENCE FROM THE NATIONAL RECORDS OF SCOTLAND===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 June 1551: Instrument of resignation by John Hammyltoun of Orbestoun, procurator for Colin Campbell of Glenurquhar, in hands of James, duke of Chattellarault, earl of Arran, lord Hammyltoun, tutor of Mary, queen of Scots, an
2 CONC d protector of the realm, and governor, of lands and barony of Fynlarg, (specified), for new infeftment in favour of said Colin and Katherine Ruthven, his spouse, 15 June 1551. Notary: Thomas Sinclare, clerk, St Andrews diocese. W
2 CONC itnesses: Mr Robert Auchmowtie, Mr John Borthuik and Mr Michael Nasmytht, and Neil Layng, notary. Done in hospice of the said governor in place of the friars of the Holy Trinity near burgh of Peblis, [Holy Cross]. [http://catalogu
2 CONC e.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f71&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ruthven&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1560&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (B
2 CONC readalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/71]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 May 1555: Copy contract between Colin Campbell of Glenurquhay and James Campbell of Laweris, whereby said James assigns to said Colin and Katherine Ruthven, and their heirs, tack to him and subtenants, by prior and convent of
2 CONC  Charterhouse near Perth, of 20 merks worth of lands of Hairthollonich with mill thereof, and 8 merks worth of lands of Craig, in lordship of Dischirre and Twoider, sheriffdom of Perth, for length of time said tack is yet to run, 
2 CONC provided that said Colin and his heirs keep said James and his heirs skaithless anent right and kindness of said tacks and lands contained therein at hands of heirs of deceased John Campbell of Glenurquhay, and said James binds hi
2 CONC mself to take a leal and true part with said Colin, etc. Witnesses: Mr Henry Kynross, George Crychttone, John Montreif, John Campbell of Murthlie, Alexander Menzies of Rannoch and Malcolm Robertsone of Corquhan. Containing note in
2 CONC  hand of Sir Colin Campbell of Glenorchy, bt, that this contract is registered in the official's books of Lothian, 7 May 1555. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f65%2f1&st=1&tc=y&
2 CONC tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=KATHERINE+RUTHVEN&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/65/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 February 1561-62: Instrument narrating contract, 1 February 1561/2, between Colin Campbell of Glenurquhay and John Scrymgeour of Glastir, constable of Dunde, whereby said John is to infeft said Colin and Katherine Ruthven, hi
2 CONC s spouse, in liferent, and Colin Campbell, their son, of Ardbaith, in fee, in £5 land of old extent of Edinkip in lordship of Balquhidder, sheriffdom of Perth, in return for 700 merks scots. Notary: Walter Ramsay, notary, St Andre
2 CONC ws diocese.Witnesses to contract: Patrick Eviot of Balhoussy, John Cambell, fiar of Lawaris, Hew Hering of Haltoune, Robert Menzes of Comry, Angus Leith in Dunde. Witnesses to instrument: Patrick Eviot, John Cambell, Hew Hering, R
2 CONC obert Menzes and Angus Campbell. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f1%2f116&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ruthven&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1560&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Pape
2 CONC rs of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/1/116]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
