1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John Blackader of Tulliallan</strong>, co Perth, son and heir of James Blackader, of the same, by Elizabeth, daughter of (--) Bruce (probably Archibald Bruce of Powfoulis, otherwise Batfoullis), was born the Sunday  after
2 CONC  Easter, 1596, and baptized June following; succeeded his father at the age of 14, in 1610, and was created a Baronet [S] as 'of Tulliallan', 28 July 1626, the patent being sealed 3 February 1627, with rem. to heirs male whatsoeve
2 CONC r, and with grant of, presumably, 16,000 acres in Nova Scotia, of which he had seizin in February  1627. He was one of the captains in the Scotch regiment levied for the King of France in 1642. He married Christian, daughter of Jo
2 CONC hn (Graham), Earl of Mentieth [S], by Mary, daughter of Sir Colin Campbell, of Glenorchy. 'By his foolish generosiy, wheredom, and every other unfortunate way, together with the prodigality and pride of his Lady he squandered away
2 CONC  an honourable and ancient estate of 3,000 merks or £2,000 sterling yearly.' He was living 1666 and died before 1675 leaving male issue, but after his death the Baronetcy became dormant."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n333/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 315
