3 CTRY Kingdom of Scotland (not yet part of the United Kingdom)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN STEWART ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parson of Kirkmahoe in Dumfriesshire===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Johanni S[tewart]. filio dicti Alex[ander] [Stewart of Garlies], senioris (1542) M. Joanne Stewart rectore de Kirkmaho (1569) Mr. John Stewart parson of Kirkmaho (1569-70) Jo. Stewart  de  Kirkmaho (1570) John Stewa
2 CONC rt parson and vicar of Kirkmaho  (1573-74) John Stewart rector of Kirkmaho (1576) John Stewart rector of Kirkmaho (1577) John Stewart rector of Kirkmaho (1580-81) Johnne Stewart parson of Kirkmaho (1594)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stewart, parson of Kirkmahoe, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Alexander-Stewart-of-Garlies/6000000008212240737?through=6000000005243250038  [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/155/mod
2 CONC e/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 155] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD138%2f1%2f132&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kirkmaho&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD138/1/132] His mother is reported
2 CONC  to be https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Dunbar-lady-of-Clugston/6000000008212255434?through=6000000005243250038 [https://archive.org/details/fastiecclesiu02scotuoft/page/n292/mode/1up Fasti II; 281] On 23 October 1542 he was n
2 CONC amed as the principal heir-in-remainder to his elder brother https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Alexander-Stewart-of-Garlies/6000000012633148669?through=6000000005243250038 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/655
2 CONC /mode/1up RMS 1513-46: 2820-21]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stewart, parson of Kirkmahoe, died on 10 August 1592. He made his last will and testament at the Larg on 9 August 1592. He nominated his wife, Margaret Stewart, and his eldest son Alexander to be his executors. He also nom
2 CONC inated and appointed the Laird of Garlies to be tutor and administrator to his son Alexander. At the time of his death his son John Stewart owed him twenty-two pounds. He left small legacies to his daughters, Barbara Stewart, Marg
2 CONC aret Stewart, and Jonet Stewart. Confirmation was granted to Margaret Stewart and her son Alexander on 5 February 1594. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Johnne S
2 CONC tewart parson of Kirkmaho, reference CC8/8/26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000195709870871 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000195710458825 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000195710025833 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stewart, parson of Kirkmahoe, died on 10 August 1592. He probably died at Larg in Dumfriesshire, Scotland, where he made his last will and testament. [NRS: CC8/8/26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stewart, parson of Kirkmahoe, married https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Stewart/6000000186683538834?through=6000000005243250038 [NRS: CC8/8/26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
