2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 October 1542: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James V, King of Scots, confirms that he has given a new grant of the land and barony of Garlies and Glenmunnock to Alexander Stewart of Garlies and his son and
2 CONC  apparent heir, also Alexander Stewart. Alexander, senior, is the hold in liferent, and Alexander, junior, is to hold in fee. Alexander Stewart of Garlies, senior, who previously resigned the barony in favour of his son Alexander,
2 CONC  reserved the liferent of his wife Margaret Dunbar. In the event of the death of Alexander, junior, the land and barony of Garlies and Glenmunnock was to pass to his younger brother John: "Johanni S. filio dicti Alex, senioris et 
2 CONC heredibus." In the event  of the death of Alexander Stewart of Garlies, senior, without a lawful male heir, the barony was to pass to Walter Stewart of Barkly and his lawful male heirs, whom failing to Archibald Stewart of Fintela
2 CONC cht and his lawful male heirs; whom failing to John Stewart of Minto and his lawful male heirs; whom failing to Robert Stewart, citizen of Glasgow. In the event of the failure of all the previously mentioned  people, the barony wa
2 CONC s to pass to Alexander senior's nearest lawful male heir whatsoever bearing the name and arms of Stewart of Garlies. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/655/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 2820]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 October 1542: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James V, King of Scots, confirms 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/655/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 2821]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 December 1569: Charter by which Robert, commendator of Whithorn, confirms that he has given certain lands to Andrew Stewart, Master of Ochiltree. His charter was witnessed by Magister John Stewart, rector of Kirkmahoe and ot
2 CONC hers: "M. Joanne Stewart rectore de Kirkmaho." His charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 10 September 1578. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/766/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 2797
2 CONC ]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 March 1569-70: Tack by Robert Commendator of Quhitherne with consent of the Convent, to Mr. John Stewart parson of Kirkmaho, of the parsonage of the parish of Mochrum for 19 years, paying yearly 160 merks scots. At St. Andrew
2 CONC s. wit:- David Fraser, Robert Land and Andrew Grief, N.P. Signed by granter and Dom. George Steinstoun Dom. John Kay Dom. John Stewart Dom. Adam Flemyng, vicar of Quhithern tag, no seal. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonl
2 CONC inecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD138%2f1%2f124&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kirkmaho&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Stewart family, Earls of Galloway (Galloway Charters), reference GD138/1
2 CONC /124]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 February 1571: Charter by which James Stewart of Cardonald has sold the twenty shilling land of Wrightsland, the five pound land of Cardonald, the eight pound land of Easter Henderson, and the five merk land of Over Darnly, t
2 CONC o Robert Stewart and his wife Marie Stewart. His charter was witnessed by John Stewart of Kirkmahoe and others. His charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 3 October 1572. [https://archive.org/details/registrumma
2 CONC gnisi04scot/page/548/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 2098]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 February 1573-74: Tack by John Stewart parson and vicar of Kirkmaho to his deceased father Sir Alexander Stewart of Garroleis for his lifetime of the teind sheaves and emoluments of the parsonage and vicarage of the Kirk, gle
2 CONC be and Kirklands for 40 merks yearly. At Quhitherne. wit: Sir John Dunbar of Mochrum, Patrick Agnew sheriff of Wigton, Mr. Patrick Vaus of Barnbarroch and William Gordoun of Myrfad. [endorsed 1574]. Signed by granter and witnesses
2 CONC . tag, no seal. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD138%2f1%2f132&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kirkmaho&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Stewart famil
2 CONC y, Earls of Galloway (Galloway Charters), reference GD138/1/132]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 January 1576: Instrument of Sasine at the hand of William Makgowin N.P. narrating that John Glendonning of Drumrasche, Stewart Depute of Kirkcudbright, conform to Crown precept from Chancery dated 17 Feb. 1575 infeft Alexande
2 CONC r Stewart of Garoles yr., as heir to his father the deceased Alexander Stewart of Dalswinton in the lands and baronies of Garleis and Glenmanoche with the office of Steward within their bounds with the mills lie crevis and the fis
2 CONC hings, held in chief of the Crown; reserving to Alexander Stewart of Garleis elder eques auratus grandfather of the said Alexander the liferent thereof. Wit:- John Stewart rector of Kirkmaho, Anthony Stewart of Clarie, Mr. John St
2 CONC ewart of Barclay, Patrick Stewart his son and George Murheid conotary. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD138%2f1%2f135&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kirkmaho&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n Na
2 CONC tional Records of Scotland, Papers of the Stewart family, Earls of Galloway (Galloway Charters), reference GD138/1/135]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 December 1577: Charter by Sir Alexander Stewart of Garleis elder and Katharine Stewart spouses conform to a contract dated at Clarie 28 April 1577 and registered at Edinburgh 28 Oct. 1577, between Anthony Robert and William 
2 CONC Stewart sons of said Sir Alexander on the one part and Alexander Stewart younger of Garleis son and heir of the deceased Sir Alex. Stewart of Dalswinton on the other part, in favour of the said Alex. Stewart younger of Garleis, of
2 CONC  the 21 merkland of Grenane reserving the granter's liferent in a 4 merkland of Mains of Grenane, the 1 merkland of Stewartoun, 1 merkland of Carstubbane, 1 merkland of Stronrie, 1 merkland of Meikle Auchraa, 1 merkland of Benbrek
2 CONC , 1 merkland of Blakcraig and 1 merkland of Munquhill extending in all to 11 merklands; held from the granters of John [Maxwell] Earl of Mortoun by ward and relief. At Wigton. wit:- William Gordoun of Murifad, Alexander Gordoun of
2 CONC  Barquhill,John  Stewart rector of Kirkmaho, Archibald Muir in Arawlane, John Dunbar brother german to the Laird of Enterkyn and Dom. Herbert Andersoun vicar of Keltoun. 2 tags, 1 seal. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonli
2 CONC necatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD138%2f1%2f144&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kirkmaho&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Stewart family, Earls of Galloway (Galloway Charters), reference GD138/1/
2 CONC 144]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 March 1580-81: Instrument of Sasine at the hand of William Makgowyne N.P. narrating that John Stewart rector of Kirkmaho as bailie on precept by Elizabeth and Margaret Stewart daughters of deceased James Stewart Earl of Moray
2 CONC  with consent of James Stewart now Earl of Moray spouse of said Elizabeth and of Colin Earl of Argyle tutor dative to said Margaret, and of Dame Anne Keyt their mother now spouse to the said Colin, dated 13th and 18th Feb. 1580, a
2 CONC nd witnessed by Hew Kennedy of Barquhanie, Mr. Thomas Craig advocate, John Guthrie, Robert Burne Heidar of Dolar, Alexander McKie, Thomas Murdoch, Neill Montgomerie of Langschaw, John Richartson, John Gray, David Phynie, Mr. James
2 CONC  Stewart and James Cunnynghame - infeft Alexander Stewart of Garroleis and Cristine Douglas spouses in the £10 lands of Mains of Quhitherne called Knokcandochane with its teinds. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatal
2 CONC ogue/details.aspx?reference=GD138%2f1%2f156&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kirkmaho&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Stewart family, Earls of Galloway (Galloway Charters), reference GD138/1/156]'''
2 CONT . 
2 CONT
