2 ADDR
3 CITY Mochrum
3 STAE Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 AUG 1586
2 PLAC Scotland
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT 74. Sir John Dunbar, nat. circa Anno 1522, of Mochrum. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He obtained a Commission under the Great Seal, from Queen Mary, appointing him Judiciary within the Barony of Mochrum, with the Jurisdiction of punishing theft, and all other crimes committed within the said Barony, in as ample a 
2 CONC manner as any other Justiciar in Scotland. Dated in 1545. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By a Charter dated 5th August, 1556, Andrew Dunbar, a descendant of Patrick Dunbar (No. 40), conveyed to Sir John Dunbar, of Mochrum, a portion of the Barony of Mochrum, called " Mochrum Lock." 
2 CONT
2 CONT He afterwards obtained a Commission and Charter from the Queen, appointing him Coroner within the Shire of Wigton, to him or his heirs or assignees, with all the fees and emoluments thereunto belonging, to be holden of the Majesty
2 CONC  in Ward. Dated 1557. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He acquired from the Prior of St Mary's Isle the lands of Parkhill, in 1559. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth, daughter of Mungo Mure, of Rowallan (by Isabel, his wife, daughter of Sir Hugh Campbell, of Loudoun, High Sheriff of the County of Ayr, and Ancestor of the Earl of Loudoun). By her he had two daughters. 
2 CONT * <strong>Grisel Dunbar</strong>, born at Mochrum about Anno 1545. She married in 1565, Alexander Dunbar (No. 80), the younger, of Canzie, son of Alexander Dunbar (No. 79), of Canzie. 
2 CONT * Euphemia Dunbar, born at Mochrum about Anno 1550. She married first Alexander Vanse, of Barnbarroch. by whom she had no issue; and secondly, to ---  Macdowal, of Garthland, and had. issue. Names not given. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Dunbar, having no male issue, in order to keep his Estate in his own Name and Family, gave his eldest daughter, Grisel, in marriage to his cousin, Alexander Dunbar (No. 80), third son and apparent heir of Alexander Dunbar
2 CONC , of Canzie (see No. 79), and put him in fee of his Estate, so that in all after writs he was designated "Fiar of Mochrum," which Alexander was lineally descended from Alexander Dunbar, of Canzie and Kilbuiach, third son of the fi
2 CONC rst Sir Alexander Dunbar, of Westfield, Sheriff of Murray ; thus continuing the direct male line.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Welles, Albert. [http://archive.org/stream/dunbarfamily00well#page/n55/mode/2up Dunbar family]. N.Y., Society Lib. 1880. page
