1 NAME Alexander /Dunbar/ II
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN Dunbar
2 NSFX II
2 _MARNM Dunbar
2 NICK Dunbar of Canzie
1 NAME Sir Alexander Dunbar of Conzie
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1550
2 PLAC Grange Hill, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1585
2 PLAC Moray, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT 80. <strong>Sir Alexander Dunbar</strong>, his apparent heir, nat. circa Anno 1540. He succeeded to his father at his death, in the Estate of Canzie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married in 1565 to Grisel Dunbar, daughter and heiress of Sir John Dunbar (No. 74), of Mochrum, and by her he obtained the Barony of Mochrum ; which marriage was confirmed by vouchers, particularly a Charter proceeding upon
2 CONC  a Contract entered into between her father, on the one part, and Alexander Dunbar, of Canzie on the other part, whereby it was agreed that the said Alexander should marry the said Grisel, upon which the said Alexander and Grisel 
2 CONC wer put in fee of the whole Barony of Mochrum, with its pertinents, the ten merk lands of Culingrot and and Glentriploch, all lying in the Shire of Wigton. This Contract and Charter are dated 17th November, 1564, and confirmed by 
2 CONC a Charter, under the Great Seal, the 17th of November, 1565. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Dunbar died in Anno 1585, and by the said Grisel left issue three sons — 
2 CONT * Sir John Dunbar, born at Canzie about Anno 1566. 
2 CONT * Alexander Dunbar, born at Canzie about Anno 1568. 
2 CONT * William Dunbar, born at Canzie about Anno 1570. William was the Progenitor of the Dunbar Family, of Hempriggs and Northfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Welles, Albert. [http://archive.org/stream/dunbarfamily00well#page/n57/mode/2up Dunbar family]. N.Y., Society Lib. 1880. page 237
