1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT 83. <strong>William Dunbar, of Canzie and Hempriggs</strong>, born about Anno 1570, third son of Alexander Dunbar (No. 80), of Canzie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT " He was the Progenitor of the Dunbar Family of Hempriggs and Northfield, Scotland." 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first Sheriff of Kilbuiach (not Canzie, although he afterwards got Canzie, but which only remained a short time in the Family). 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Dunbar was paternally descended from the Dunbars, Earls of Moray, Earls of March, and Earls of Dunbar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Seven Royal Charters and two Matriculations of Arms are recorded in this line, the last of each in favor of William Dunbar, of Hempriggs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His son was — 
2 CONT * Alexander Dunbar
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Welles, Albert. [http://archive.org/stream/dunbarfamily00well#page/n67/mode/2up Dunbar family]. N.Y., Society Lib. 1880. page 242
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT * Likely to be  duplicate of [http://www.geni.com/people/William-Dunbar-1st-of-Hemprigg/6000000013469225240 William Dunbar, 1st of Hempriggs] - though according to Albert Welles, the Progenitor of the Dunbar Family of Hempriggs wa
2 CONC s the grandson of Hon. Elizabeth Forbes, not the son.
