1 NAME Alexander /Stewart/
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN Stewart
2 _MARNM Stewart
1 NAME Alexander Stewart 1st in Auchtow
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1610
2 PLAC Glenogle, Balquhidder, Perthshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 AUG 1645
2 PLAC Kilsyth, Stirlingshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~rykbrown/glenogle.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander STEWART, 1st in Auchtow, b. ABT 1610 in Glenogle, Balquhidder, Perthshire, Scotland.  Alexander is suggested to be a younger son of Duncan MacRobert STEWART, 3rd in Glenogle. Alexander's name and identity is inferred fro
2 CONC m the 1684 testament of his suggested son, James Stewart in Wester Auchtow.  It is suggested that Alexander was the father of:
2 CONT
2 CONT     "Duncan" STEWART, b. ABT 1630 in Auchtow, Balquhidder, Perthshire, Scotland.  There is no evidence to show the existence of any such son as "Duncan".  His name and identity are suggested based solely on onomastics.  If he exis
2 CONC ted at all then it is suggested that he probably died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Alexander STEWART, 2nd in Auchtow, b. ABT 1632, in Auchtow, Balquhidder parish, Perthshire, Scotland.  Alexander is described in the 1684 testament as a predeceased brother of James Stewart in Wester Auchtow.  Whether he was a
2 CONC n older or younger brother is unknown and does not adversely affect the accounting of this family.  However, the fact that he died before James would lend a small weight to the suggestion that Alexander was older.  It is presently
2 CONC  suggested that Alexander was the older brother and that the property of Auchtow would have passed firstly to him, and, presumably with heirs failing, then latterly to his brother James.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Has Children James STEWART, 3rd in Wester Auchtow, b. ABT 1635, in Auchtow, Balquhidder parish, Perthshire, Scotland.  He died in 1684.  His testament is presented above.
2 CONT         Alexander STEWART, 4th in Wester Auchtow, b. ABT 1660, probably in Wester Auchtow, Balquhidder, Perthshire, Scotland.  Alexander is described in the 1684 testament as the son of James Stewart in Wester Auchtow.  His sugges
2 CONC ted descendants are described below.
2 CONT         Isabel STEWART, b. ABT 1664, probably in Wester Auchtow, Balquhidder, Perthshire, Scotland.  Isabel is described in the 1684 testament as a daughter of James Stewart in Wester Auchtow.
2 CONT         Robert STEWART, 5th in Wester Auchtow, b ABT 1665
2 CONT     Has Children "Son" STEWART, predecessor to Cuill and Achra, (POSSIBLY IDENTICAL WITH JAMES STEWART 3RD IN WESTER AUCHTOW) b. ABT 1638 in Auchtow, Balquhidder, Perthshire, Scotland.  There is no documentary evidence for the exi
2 CONC stence of this unknown son.  He is suggested as the most likely place for the Cuill and Achra branches to descend from.  It is suggested that this unknown son may have been the father of:
2 CONT
2 CONT         Has Children Alexander STEWART, predecessor of Cuill, b. 1663 in Balquhidder parish, Perthshire, Scotland.  It is suggested that this Alexander may have been a grandson of Alexander Stewart, 1st in Auchtow, by an unknown s
2 CONC on, although it is possible that he could be descended from an earlier line.  However the fact that Cuill is located adjacent to Auchtow suggests that the Cuill family descend from Auchtow.  Furthermore, as the Achra branch, a lat
2 CONC er cadet branch, also descends from Auchtow then it would seem that Cuill must descend from Auchtow in order to remain senior to the Achra branch.  It is entirely possible that this Alexander could be identical with Alexander 4th 
2 CONC in Wester Auchtow.  Alexander's descendants are presented below under 7 Line - The Stewarts in Cuill.
2 CONT
2 CONT         Has Children Duncan STEWART, in Wester Auchtow, predecessor of Achra, b. ABT 1665 in Balquhidder parish, Perthshire, Scotland.  It is shown below that the Achra Stewarts descend from the Wester Achtow branch and this would
2 CONC  seem to be the most likely place.  The descendants of Duncan are presented below under 9 Line - The Stewarts in Achra.
