1 NAME Samuel /Grove/
2 GIVN Samuel
2 SURN Grove
2 _MARNM Grove
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1735
2 ADDR
3 CITY Halesowen
3 STAE Worcestershire
3 CTRY UK
1 BURI
2 DATE 3 JAN 1800
2 PLAC Halesowen, Shropshire
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 JAN 1800
2 ADDR
3 CITY Halesowen
3 STAE Worcestershire
3 CTRY UK
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Bio notes: Biography of Samuel Grove
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Grove is not found in the IGI but his brother Joseph is [1]. Likewise, his baptism is not recorded but he is mentioned in his father's will and Davenport has concluded after an intensive study that Samuel, son of Joseph and
2 CONC  Hannah, was born at Hawn in Halesowen married Esther Taylor at Halesowen on 4 February 1760 [2]. In 1771, he was farming his father's tenancy in Frankley south of Halesowen township but in the parish of Frankley in the county of 
2 CONC Worcester [3]. They had 10 children [4]. He died in January 1800 and was buried in Halesowen on 3 January 1800 [4].
2 CONT
2 CONT [1] IGI  www.familysearch.org accessed on 30/03/2006
2 CONT Joseph Grove
2 CONT Birth: about 1735,  Halesowen, Worcester, England
2 CONT Death: 03 JAN 1800 Halesowen, Worcestershire
2 CONT Father: Joseph Grove
2 CONT Mother: Hannah Stringer
2 CONT Spouse: Esther Taylor [Tayler in another citation]
2 CONT Marriage: 04 FEB 1760
2 CONT [2]. James Davenport, The Grove Family of Halesowen, Methuen and Co, 1912
2 CONT "Ninth Generation
2 CONT The family of Joseph (Grove) by Hannah Stringer consisted of
2 CONT 1. Joseph bap 23 Mar 1734
2 CONT 2. Samuel, mentioned in father's will
2 CONT 3. Thomas bap 7 Mar 1741
2 CONT 4. Benjamin bap 20 May 1744
2 CONT 5. Matthew bap 6 May 1759
2 CONT ......
2 CONT 2. Samuel (son of Joseph)
2 CONT Samuel described as a bachelor married 4 Feb.1760, as the followijng considerations show, Esther Taylor who was bap 29 May 1737 as daughter of Henry and Judith Taylor of ye Hill. The case of Samuel presents some difficulty, becaus
2 CONC e his baptism is not to be found at Halesowen like those of his four other brothers, and the only proof that he was the son of Joseph and Hannah is the reference to him in his father's will as tenant of Frankley [see Joseph Grove'
2 CONC s will]. Unfortunately that will is not help as to date because the words Samuel and Benjamin in the will are in large thick type and have been substituted for other names scratched out probably some time after the Will was made i
2 CONC n 1771 and before it was proved in 1784. It looks as though some time after 1771 the loan of 20 pounds and also the Frankley tenancy had been transferred from one son to another and the father had before his death altered the name
2 CONC s accordingly. "
2 CONT Davenport goes on at some length to show that our Samuel is not the Samuel Grove who married Susanna Parks in Halesowen in 1767, He then goes on to show that two other Samuel Grove's who married in Halesowen in 1760 and 1766 could
2 CONC  not have been our Samuel and concludes:
2 CONT The fact remains that some other Samuel not recorded as baptized at Halesowen must have been Esther's husband. Clearly the happy bridegroom was Samuel, Joseph's son and younger brother of the Joseph bap. 23 Mar 1734, whose baptism
2 CONC  probably did take place at Halesown but was through inadvertence never recorded. This conclusion seems incontestable to the writer after a careful and prolonged study of the register and the marriage accordingly in the pedigree s
2 CONC heet but it will be remembered tha the conslusion arrived at not of course by direct proof but by process of elimination of the three and only other Samuels whose existence there is trace of."
2 CONT [3]. See Joseph Grove's will - notes of his father
2 CONT [4]. James Davenport, The Grove Family of Halesowen, Methuen and Co, 1912
2 CONT "The family of Samuel and Esther
2 CONT 1. William bap 29 Nov 1761 as s. of Samuel and Esther
2 CONT 2. Thomas bap 18 May 1766 do
2 CONT 3. Harry bap 9 Oct 1768 do
2 CONT 4. James bap 31 May 1773 do
2 CONT 5. Edward bap 26 Nov 1778
2 CONT 6. Joseph bap. 26 Nov 1780 as son of Esther
2 CONT 7. Anne bap 31 JaN 1790 as dau. of Samuel and Esther
2 CONT 8. Josiah bap 28 Dec 1781 do
2 CONT 9. Thomas bap 3 Sep 1783 as son of Esther
2 CONT 10. Phoebe bap 31 Jan 1790 as dau. of Samuel and Esther
2 CONT The father Samuel was apparently the Samuel buried 3 Jan 1800
2 CONT The mother Esther was buried 23 April 1815 aged 78
2 CONT A stone showed that the son Josiah died 26 july 1830 aged 49, and his wife, Mary, on 13 March 1844, aged 66 at Wednesbury"
