1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====ELIZABETH SOMERVILLE
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Disputed Name and Ancestry'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''The name and ancestry of Elizabeth Somerville, here treated, is disputed. According to James, eleventh Lord Somerville (1652-82), writing in volume one of his account of the family (Published in 1815), Janet Somervi
2 CONC lle, daughter of Thomas, Lord Somerville: "was marryed upon Neill or either Duncan Campbell, the first Earle of Argyle. Lord Somerville's work was subsequently edited by Sir Walter Scott (1771-1832), who added the following note: 
2 CONC "Douglas and Crawford, I observe, name this lady Elizabeth, and wed her with Archibald, son and heir of Sir Duncan Campbell of Lochern. This Archibald, according to these genealogists, died before his father, leaving issue, Sir Co
2 CONC lin Campbell, first Earl of Argyle, so created by James II. in 1457." [https://archive.org/details/memorieofsomerv11815some/page/134/mode/1up Memorie of the Somervilles, Volume I, page 134] The late George William Campbell, appear
2 CONC s to have folowed Douglas and Crawford. Writing in his account of the the family of Somerville, Lord Somerville (Published in 1911), he claims that Elizabeth Somerville, here treated, is the daughter of John, third Lord Somerville
2 CONC , and his wife Helen Hepburn. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/12/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 12]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/memorieofsomerv11815some/page/134/mode/1up Memorie of the Somervilles. Volume I, page 134]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/12/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 12]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LT5V-LMN/lady-elizabeth-somerville-1415-1460 FamilySearch]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://gw.geneanet.org/gsprague?lang=en&n=somerville+baroness+campbell&oc=0&p=lady+elizabeth+de Geneanet]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of John, third lord Somerville of Carnwath.  Birth and death dates are not documented.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Lady Elizabeth Somerville
2 CONT
2 CONT Seen as '''Birth:''' 23 April 1415 in Carnwath, Lanarkshire, Scotland (or about 1422)
2 CONT
2 CONT Seen as '''Death:''' 4 March 1460 (Age 44), Lochawe, Argyll, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SPOUSES AND CHILDREN:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Lord Archibald Gillespic Campbell (1405-1440) • Marriage: 13 January 1432, Carnwath, Lanarkshire, Scotland
2 CONT * Lady Elizabeth Somerville
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children (6)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # Lady Elizabeth Campbell (1430-1485)
2 CONT # Anne Campbell (1431-?)
2 CONT # Duncan Campbell (1431-?)
2 CONT # Lady Catherine Campbell (1432-1482)
2 CONT # Sir Colin Campbell 1st Earl of Argyll (1433-1493)
2 CONT # Margaret Campbell (1440-1530)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''PARENTS AND SIBLINGS:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''John Somerville''' (d 1491)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: 10 Jul 1446, Hailes Castle, Prestonkirk, East Lothian, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Helen Hepburn''' (1420-1457)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children (8)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # Lady Elizabeth Somerville (1415-1460)
2 CONT # Jean Somerville (1440-1495)
2 CONT # Catherine Somerville (1447- ?)
2 CONT # John Somerville (1450-?)
2 CONT # William Somerville, Master of Somerville (1451-1491)
2 CONT # Lady Helen Somerville (1453-?)
2 CONT # Elizabeth Somerville of Carnwath (1455-1510)
2 CONT # Roberton Somerville
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
