2 CONT '''14 February 1571-72: Extract Charter under the Great Seal, granting to Torquil McLeod, son and heir apparent of Roderick McLeod of Lewis, the lands and baronies of Assynt and Cogarch, in the earldom of Ross and sheriffdom of In
2 CONC verness, the lands, isle and barony of Lewis with castle etc, the lands and isle of Waterness, in said sheriffdom; on said Rodorick's resignation. Reserving said Rodorick's liferent. To be held by said Torquil and the heirs male o
2 CONC f his body, whom failing, Gillecallum Garwie McLeod of Raisay and the heirs male of his body, whom failing, said Torquil's heirs male whomsoever bearing the arms and surname of McLeod, and their assignees, united into the free bar
2 CONC ony of Lewis as before. Provided that said Rodorick and Torquil remain faithful to the King and commit no treason. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2243&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k
2 CONC =Torquil&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register House Charters, reference RH6/2243]'''
