1 NAME Aonghas /Óg Eoin/
2 GIVN Aonghas
2 _MARNM Óg Eoin
2 NICK Angus of Ross Master of Ross
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1490
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aonghas Óg (died 1490) was a Scottish nobleman who was the last independent Lord of the Isles. Aonghas became a rebel against both his father and against the Scottish crown, in a civil clan war which would see the 
2 CONC end of the independent Lordship of the Isles.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Angus was born the bastard son of John of Islay, Earl of Ross (Eoin). In time, Aonghas would become a rebel against both his father and against the Scottish crown. He is not to be confused with his namesake, Aonghas Óg, Lord of Is
2 CONC lay, who fought alongside Robert the Bruce.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aonghas married Isobella Campbell daughter of Colin Campbell, 1st Earl of Argyll.  (name also seen as Mary)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1490 Aonghas had his throat cut while he was sleeping. The murderer was his Irish harpist, Art O'Carby, who carried out the act for reasons which remain unclear. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Refs
2 CONT * MacDougall, Norman, "Achilles' Heel? The Earldom of Ross, the Lordship of the Isles, and the Stewart Kings, 1449-1507", in Edward J. Cowan & R. Andrew McDonald (eds.), Alba: Celtic Scotland in the Medieval Era, (Edinburgh, 2000)
2 CONC , pp. 248–75
2 CONT * Oliver, Neil, A History of Scotland, Phoenix, London (2010) ISBN 0753826631
2 CONT * Oram, Richard, "The Lordship of the Isles, 1336-1545", in Donald Omand (ed.) The Argyll Book, (Edinburgh, 2005), pp. 123–39
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aonghas_Óg
2 CONT * http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2218.htm#i66660
