2 CONT ====Books and Links
2 CONT * '''Book:''' ''The Scots Peerage'', Vol. 1, [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01paul/page/336/mode/1up p. 336].
2 CONT * '''Book:''' ''The Book of the Thanes of Cawdor: A Series of Papers Selected From the Charter Room at Cawdor, 1236-1742''. [https://archive.org/details/bookthanescawdo02innegoog/page/170/mode/1up Archive, org, p. 170]. Transcript
2 CONC ion from [https://www.rps.ac.uk/trans/1543/3/20 "Records of the Parliaments of Scotland to 1707"]:—
2 CONT ** '''Procedure: household arrangements for the queen'''
2 CONT *** "[1543/3/20] The which day [James Hamilton, earl of Arran], my lord governor, with the advice of the lords of articles, thought it expedient that the lords underwritten be named and installed for the keeping of the queen's gra
2 CONC ce, or any two of them quarterly, and one to be installed and joined to them by my lord governor at his pleasure, that is to say [William Keith], earl Marischal, [William Graham], earl of Montrose, [John Erskine], lord Erskine, [W
2 CONC illiam Ruthven], lord Ruthven, [Alexander Livingston], lord Livingston, [John Lindsay], lord Lindsay [of the Byres], [George Seton], lord Seton and [John Campbell], laird of Cawdor."
2 CONT *** "[1543/3/21] Item, regarding the place, because the queen's grace was born in Linlithgow and, therefore, the transporting of her, being so tender of age, may do her harm, the lords think it expedient that she remain in the pal
2 CONC ace of Linlithgow or castle of Stirling at the pleasure of the queen's grace, her mother, with the advice of [James Hamilton, earl of Arran], my lord governor, and council to be had thereto; and the time of transporting her grace 
2 CONC be done with the advice of the queen's grace, her mother, my lord governor and lords of council."
2 CONT * '''Book:''' ''Peerage of Scotland: A Genealogical and Historical Account of all the Peers of that Ancient Kingdom; their Descents, collateral Branches, Births, Marriages, and Issue''. Vol. II, [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/p
2 CONC t?id=mdp.35112103424299&view=2up&seq=568 Hathitrust, pp. 414-15].
2 CONT * '''The Peerage''': [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10924.htm#i109236 Sir John Campbell, 1st of Cawdor]
2 CONT * '''Wikitree''': [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Campbell-190 John (Campbell) Campbell Ist of Cawdor (abt. 1490-1546)]
2 CONT ** "He married Muriel, daughter of John Calder of Cawdor. circa 1510.[1][2]"
2 CONT ** "He murdered his brother-in-law Lachlan Cattanach MacLean 10th Laird of Duart."
2 CONT ** "On 20 Mar 1543, he was appointed one of eight guardians of Mary, Queen of Scots, during her childhood.[3]"
2 CONT * '''Wikipedia''': [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Campbell_of_Cawdor_(nobleman) John Campbell of Cawdor (nobleman)]
2 CONT * '''Clan MacFarlane Genealogy:''' [https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I3157&tree=CC Sir John Campbell, 1st of Cawdor (Calder)]. • cites Stirnet with associated sources.
2 CONT * '''Patrick's People''': [https://www.patrickspeople.scot/ourfamily/8164.htm CAMPBELL, John 1st of Cawdor (Calder), jure uxoris, Sir]
2 CONT * '''FindAGrave®''': [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/197519991/john-campbell Sir John “of Cawdor” Campbell]
