2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children[edit] Maclean is said to have had at least six wives or mistresses. To cement his alliance, with the Argylls he married Katherine Campbell, daughter of Archibald Campbell, 2nd Earl of Argyll.[3] Although poli
2 CONC tically convenient, the marriage was not a success, as she tried to poison him and he arranged to have her drowned by placing her on a rock in the sound of Mull. She was rescued just before the high tide drowned her.
2 CONT
2 CONT His children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT Eachann Mor Maclean, his heir and successor Ailean Maclean, second son of Lachlan Catanach, but better known as Ailean nan Sop, or Allan o' the Wisp, because he set fire to buildings with straw, was a very noted character. Many le
2 CONC gends have been told concerning him, some of which can not be true, although they may contain a grain of truth.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Catherine Campbell1 
2 CONT *F, #39205
2 CONT *Father      Archibald Campbell, 2nd Earl of Argyll d. 9 Sep 1513
2 CONT *Mother     Elizabeth Stewart1
2 CONT *''''''     Catherine Campbell married Lachlan Og Maclean, 10th Laird of Duart, son of Lachlan Brannoc Maclean, 7th Chief of MacLean and Janet Stewart.1 Catherine Campbell married Archibald Campbell, son of Dugald Campbell and Agn
2 CONC es Lamont, circa 1524.2,1,3
2 CONT *''''''Family 1      Lachlan Og Maclean, 10th Laird of Duart d. 1484
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Anne Maclean+1
2 CONT *''''''Family 2      Archibald Campbell b. c 1480, d. 1542
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Alexander Campbell2
2 CONT *Citations
