2 CONC e, 106th edition.
2 CONT * 2.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 666. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p1945.htm#i19445
2 CONT *_____________
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Catherine Campbell survived a murder attempt by her husband, lachlan Maclean of Duart in 1527. Maclean rowed out to Lady's Rock in the Tirth of Lorn one night at low tide and left his wife.  source Wikipedia, the free encyclo
2 CONC pedia beyond Colin Campbell, 3rd Earl of Argyll.
2 CONT --------------------
