2 CONT George Seton, 4th Lord Seton (d 1507-8), and 2nd to be called "of the name George".  He was one of the conservators of treaties with the English, 30 Sept. 1497, and 12 July, 1499, and witnessed the assignation of the dower of Marg
2 CONC aret, Queen of Scotland, 24 May, 1503. m. Margaret Campbell (dau of Colin Campbell, 1st Earl of Argyll)
2 CONT
2 CONT [MTD note:  He was George Seton II, 4th Lord of Seton.  Sources mixed up his being 2nd George and 4th Lord.]]
