2 CONC ded to the title of 2nd Lord Seton on the death of his Grandfather, his father had died a few years earlier, circa July 1478. In 1493 he was the founder of the Collegiate Church of Seton. He was invested as a Privy Counsellor in S
2 CONC cotland in 1496. He died between 11 June 1507 and 6 April 1508.
