1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Drummond, Master of Drummond, was the son of William Drummond, Master of Drummond, and Lady Isabel Campbell.
2 CONT
2 CONT WALTER DRUMMOND, THE 2d MASTER OF DRUMMOND,
2 CONT Succeeded in 1490.Married in 1513.Died in 15l9.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Drummond, designed the second Master of Drummond, as he died before his grandfather, John, Lord Drummond, carried on the succession of the family, on the death of his father, William, and is reckoned the seventeenth head' o
2 CONC f the house of Drummond.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of this young nobleman, nothing memorable is recorded. He married, about the year 1513, Lady Elizabeth Graham, daughter of William, first earl of Montrose,  and by her, he had one son, David, who succeeded, on his great grandfathe
2 CONC r's death, to the estate and honours of the house of Drummond. He died very young, and was buried in the family burial-place at Innerpaffray, in 1519.
2 CONT
2 CONT ("Genealogical memoir of the most noble and ancient house of Drummond" by David Malcolm pub. 1808)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Drummond, Master of Drummond (Engagement / Contract)
2 CONT Contract Date: January 1502.
2 CONT Details: As a wealthy and prominent widow (following the death of Lord Glamis), a formal marriage contract was drawn up between Elizabeth Gray and Walter Drummond (born c. 1492). However, this union never culminated in a wedding. 
2 CONC Walter ultimately went on to marry Elizabeth Graham in February 1514, while Elizabeth Gray pursued other matches.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on standard peerage timelines and secondary genealogical tracking, Walter Drummond, Master of Drummond, is typically estimated to have been born around 1492 (rather than 1497).
2 CONT
2 CONT This lines up better with a January 1502 marriage contract involving Elizabeth Gray, as it would place him around 10 years old at the time of the betrothal contract—a completely typical age for high-status, strategic child betroth
2 CONC als in the early 16th-century Scottish nobility designed to secure land and alliances well before a formal church wedding could legally take place.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/dd/drummond01.php#link3 Stirnet - Drummond01’] 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 	(b)	Sir William, Master of Drummond (dvp 1490) 	m1. Isabel Campbell (d before 1493, dau of Colin Campbell, 1st Earl of Argyll)
2 CONT **	((1))	Walter, Master of Drummond (d 1518) m. (02.1513-4) Elizabeth Graham (dau of William Graham, 1st Earl of Montrose)
2 CONT *** 	((A))	David Drummond, 2nd Lord (d 1571) 	m1. Margaret Stewart (possibly dau of Alexander Stewart, Bishop of Moray)
2 CONT *** 	(B)	John Drummond, Dean of Dunblane (a 1478)
2 CONT *** 	(C)	Walter Drummond of Ledcrieff or Ladecrief
2 CONT *** 	(D)	Mariota Drummond (b c1424, a 1466) possibly of this generation	m. (1444) Alexander Ouchterlony (b c1424, dvp c05.1466)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
