1 OCCU Created 1st Lord Kennedy 20th March 1457/58, Keeper of the Castle of Lochdoun, Constable of Stirling Castle, Regent of Scotland, Laird of Dunure, office of Constable of Stirling Castle 1466, Lord, Regent
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p2150.htm#i21499 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilbert_Kennedy,_1st_Lord_Kennedy Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, 1st Lord Kennedy (22 February 1405 – 27 March 1489) was a Scottish lord, a son of Sir James Kennedy, Younger of Dunure, and Lady Mary Stewart, daughter of Robert III, King of the Scots. He served as one 
2 CONC of six Regents during the early reign of James III of Scotland, after the 1460 death of James II. 
2 CONT Personal life
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert married Catherine Maxwell, daughter of Herbert Maxwell, 1st Lord Maxwell.
2 CONT
2 CONT     John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy, father of David Kennedy, 1st Earl of Cassilis.
2 CONT     Catherine Kennedy, mother of Hugh Montgomerie, 1st Earl of Eglinton.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, after 1460, Isabel Ogilvy, daughter of Sir Walter Ogilvy of Lintrathen and Isabel Glen, and widow of Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis. In 1484 she sued John Kennedy for silver ware which he claimed to have bough
2 CONC t from Gilbert Kennedy, 1st Lord Kennedy. Gilbert was then said to be deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices and titles
2 CONT Kennedy, created 1st Lord of Kennedy between 27 March 1457 and 20 March 1458, in addition held the office of Keeper of the Castle of Lochdoun and the office of Constable of Stirling Castle, bestowed upon him in 1466. By that time,
2 CONC  he was already Regent of Scotland, having secured the position on the death of James II. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://www.venitap.com/Genealogy/WebCards/ps34/ps34_058.htm Venitab]
2 CONT *[http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~lelandva/kenne009.htm#id3905 Free Genealogy rootsweb]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Kennedy-1392
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LZBZ-3M4/gilbert-kennedy-1st-lord-kennedy-1405-1479
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/272928220/gilbert-kennedy
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure was created the 1st Lord Kennedy c.1457. in addition, he held the Office of Keeper of the Castle of Lochdoun and the Office of Constable of Stirling Castle, bestowed upon him in 1466. By that time, he was
2 CONC  already Regent of Scotland, having secured the position on the death of James II.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a son of Sir James Kennedy of Dunure and Lady Mary Stewart, daughter of Robert III, King of the Scots. He served as one of six Regents during the early reign of James III of Scotland, after the 1460 death of James II.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Gilbert married Catherine Maxwell, daughter of Herbert Maxwell, 1st Lord Maxwell. Their children included :
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy
2 CONT Catherine Kennedy Montgomerie.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1460 he married Isabel Ogilvy, daughter of Sir Walter Ogilvy of Lintrathen and Isabel Glen, and widow of Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis.
