1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN, LORD KENNEDY ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for John, Lord Kennedy, here treated. He appears to have been alive on 24 July 1508, the date upon which Sir David Kennedy, Bailie of Carrick, accounted for ten pounds in rent w
2 CONC hich John, Lord Kennedy, paid for one half of the barony of Trabeauch in the Earldom of Carrick, [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof13scot/page/41/mode/1up ER XIII: 41-2] but he died before 23 May 1509, when his son Davi
2 CONC d was retoured as heir to his deceased father in various lands in the Earldom of Carrick, including Trabeauch. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f215&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&
2 CONC k=john+lord+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1510&di=y NRS: GD25/1/215]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 April 1475: Instrument of Seisin in favor of John Lord Kennedy, in the Barony of Dalrymple lying in Kyle-regis, and County of Ayr; Proceeding on a Precept from Chancery. The seisin given by Sir George Campbell of Louden Knig
2 CONC ht Sheriff of the County, to Quintin Mure of Aird as Attorney for Lord Kennedy. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f118&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+lord+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=
2 CONC s&df=&dt=1475&di=y  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/118]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 July 1508: Compotum David  Kennedy, militis, ballivi de Carrik, Leswalt, et Menebrig, et aliarum terrarum subscriptarum, . . . . . Et eidem de decem libris firmarum medie partis de Trabeauch  spectantis antis Johanni domino 
2 CONC Kennedy, ut patet in rotulo anni precedentis, de anno compoti, xli. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof13scot/page/41/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland XIII: 41-2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 May 1509: Copy of Precept from Chancery for infefting Sir David Kennedy of Leswalt Knight, as heir served and retoured to the deceased John Lord Kennedy his father, in the barony of Dalrymple extending to a 48 merk land and 
2 CONC lying in Kyle-regis, the 15 merk 6 shilling 8 penny land of Coif, Kileckie and Ellerkennoch, lying in the Earldom of Carrick - the half of the barony of Dalcharn extending to an 18 merk 6 shilling 8 penny land, and comprehending t
2 CONC he 5 merk land of Dalcharn, the 5 merk land of Arnshean, the merk land of Dirthroil, 6 shilling 8 penny land of Craigfin, the 20 shilling land of Kilicrosscan and 3 merk land of Dalchangan; the half of the barony of Traboyack exte
2 CONC nding to a 10 pound land called Glengenet, and Bennan, with the keeping of the castle of Lochdown and 5 pound land of Pennyland of Lochdown for keeping of the said castle all lying in the Earldom of Carrick. [https://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f215&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+lord+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1510&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ail
2 CONC sa Muniments), reference GD25/1/215]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/456/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 456-7]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/historicalaccoun1849cowa#page/n32/mode/1up Historical Account of the Noble Family of Kennedy, Marquess of Ailsa and Earl of Cassillis, with Notices of Some of the Principal Cadets Thereof  (Edinbur
2 CONC gh MDCCCXLIX), p. 27]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summaries ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. John10 Kennedy (Gilbert9, James8, Gilbert7, John6, Gilbert5de Carrick, Gilbert4, Roland3, Nicol,2, Duncan1) was born circa 1436 Scotland.36 He married Elizabeth Gordon after 12 Jul 1471 Scotland.37 He died after 24 Jul 1508 Sc
2 CONC otland.38 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also known as John Kennedy, second Lord Kennedy.39 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John10 Kennedy and Elizabeth Alexander were as follows: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. i. David11 3rd Lord Kennedy, b. circa 1460; m. Agnes Borthwick. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Katherine; b. circa 1460;40 m. Thomas Kennedy, son ofGilbert Kennedy of Bargany, circa 1470.41
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=pC8njhobGxQC&pg=PA282&lpg=PA282&dq=Kennedy+of+Dunure&source=bl&ots=LPK7YWCzo2&sig=VK2uWD_SBFxjhCf6wxmbnTwdnKo&hl=en&sa=X&ei=j46OUcKUFsfUqAGli4GoDw&ved=0CDkQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q=Kennedy%20of%20Dunu
2 CONC re&f=false Medieval Scotland:] Crown, Lordship and Community.  edited by Alexander Grant, K. Keith John Stringer.  "The Kin of Kennedy."
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10928.htm#i109277
2 CONT
2 CONT John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy1 
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #109277, b. before 12 October 1454, d. between 24 July 1508 and 13 May 1509
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=29 Jun 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT      John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy was born before 12 October 1454.2 He was the son of Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, 1st Lord Kennedy and Catherine Maxwell.2 He married, firstly, Elizabeth Montgomerie, daughter of Alexander Montgome
2 CONC rie, 1st Lord Montgomerie and Margaret Boyd, before 25 March 1460.2 He married, secondly, Lady Elizabeth Gordon, daughter of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly and Elizabeth Crichton, between 24 August 1467 and 12 August 1471.2 
2 CONC He married, thirdly, Elizabeth Kennedy after 1500.2 He died between 24 July 1508 and 13 May 1509.2
2 CONT
2 CONT      John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Kennedy [S., 1458] circa 1480.2 He was a Commissioner to treat with the English in 1484.2 He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland] to King James
2 CONC  III.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy and Elizabeth Montgomerie
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir David Kennedy, 1st Earl of Cassillis+ d. 9 Sep 15133 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy and Lady Elizabeth Gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Kennedy+ d. a Dec 15434 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Kennedy+ b. b 1485, d. 15421 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct 
2 CONC or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XII/1, page 274. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VII, page 121. 
