1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY MARGARET MONTGOMERY Countess of Lennox ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Lady Margaret Montgomery, Countess of Lennox, here treated, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Montgomery/6000000173871977161 Lady Margaret Montgomery, here treated, is noticed as the wif
2 CONC e of John, Earl of Lennox, on 20 July 1461; [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%2f3%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1500&di=n 
2 CONC NRS: GD220/1/F/5/3/7] and again on 1 June 1490. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%2f5%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1500&d
2 CONC i=n NRS: GD220/1/F/5/5/1] https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Montgomery/6000000173871977161 is noticed as the wife of Alexander, first Lord Home, on 10 September 1459, [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/deta
2 CONC ils.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f41%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1500&di=n NRS: GD3/1/1/41/8] and again on 4 May 1478. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.a
2 CONC spx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f38%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1500&di NRS: GD3/1/1/38/1]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Margaret Montgomery, here treated, is the daughter of Alexander Montgomery, first Lord Montgomery, and his wife Margaret Boyd. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/435/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III
2 CONC : 435] She was contracted to marry John, first Earl of Lennox, on 15 May 1438, at which time she and her future husband were not of lawful age. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/349/mode/1up The Scots Pe
2 CONC erage V: 349]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 July 1461: Charter by King James III in favour of John Lord Darnley and Margaret Montgomery, his spouse, of the lands of Tarbolton [Darnley, Dreghorn and Raguillhill deleted] lying in the sheriffdom of Ayr, proceeding on res
2 CONC ignation by Lord Darnley; dated 20 Jul 1461, the 1st of the King's reign. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%2f3%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomery&ko=p
2 CONC &r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/F/5/3/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 July 1461: Charter by King James III to the said John Lord Dernele and Margaret Montgomery, his spouse, in conjunct fee, and the survivor of them, of the dominical lands of Torboltone, Drumley, Dregarne, and Ragalhill, in th
2 CONC e shire of Ayr, which belonged to the said John Lord Dernele heritably, and had been resigned by him: to be held by the said grantees, and the lawful heirs of their bodies; whom failing, by the nearest lawful heirs of the said Joh
2 CONC n Lord Dernele whosoever, of the King, as Steward of Scotland, in feu and heritage, for rendering the services due and wont. Dated at Edinburgh. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%
2 CONC 2f2%2f1%2f52&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/2/1/52]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 June 1490: Charter of resignation by King James IV in favour of Matthew Stuart, son and apparent heir to John, Earl of Lennox, Lord Darnley, of the whole earldom of Lennox and lordship of Darnley called Crucksfu, the lands of
2 CONC  Galston with its pertinents, with the patronage of the churches and chapels belonging to the earldom, lying in the sheriffdoms of Dunbarton, Stirling, Ayr and Renfrew, to be held ward of the King, proceeding on resignation by Joh
2 CONC n, Earl of Lennox, reserving the liferent to the Earl and the liferent of a third part of the lands to Margaret Montgomery, his spouse, for her lifetime; dated at Linlithgow. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue
2 CONC /details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%2f5%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), 
2 CONC reference GD220/1/F/5/5/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/435/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 435]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/349/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 349]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00006267&tree=LEO Genealogy Proposed by Genealogics] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart, 1st Earl of Lennox. (b. bef. 1430, d. 8 Jul/11 Sep 1495) Was created Lord Darnley and Earl of Lennox. Stewart was the son of Catherine Seton and Sir Alan Stuart, a grandson of Alexander Stewart, 4th High Steward of S
2 CONC cotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT His marriage has been a source of genealogical confusion. He is recorded as having on 15 May 1438 contracted to marry Margaret, the daughter of Alexander Montgomerie, 1st Lord Montgomerie, and Margaret Boyd, by indenture as both p
2 CONC arties were underage. She however appears to have deceased young. However, ultimately he married in 1460 Margaret Montgomerie, who was not the same individual, but her fraternal niece, daughter of Alexander, Master of Montgomerie,
2 CONC  by his wife Elizabeth Hepburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT They (earl John and the younger Margaret Montgomerie) had eight children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Marion Stuart. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Stuart, 4th Seigneur d'Aubigny, b. c. 1470, d. 1543. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Stewart, Seigneur d'Oison, b. bef. 1446, d. c. 1512. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Stuart, b. bef. 1476. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox, b. bef. 5 May 1488, d. 9 Sep 1513, Flodden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Stewart, Seigneur d'Oison, b. bef. 1495, d. bef. 1504. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Stewart, b. bef. 1495, d. bef. 1509. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Elizabeth Stewart, b. bef. 1495. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Since John and Margaret were too young to marry in 1438, he was 10 and she was 4, they were married by their parents in what was called "Indenture". At this time Margaret's name became Stewart (Stuart) Later they were man and wife
2 CONC  and had eight children together.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Complete Peerage of Scotland, Ireland, Great Britian and the United Kingdom
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_Toc253996205
2 CONT
2 CONT King Robert III had one illegitimate child by Mistress (2): 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir JOHN Stewart of Ardgowan and Blackhall .  His father gave him charters for land at Auchingoun in 1390, Blackhall in 1395 and Ardgowan in 1403, all in Renfrewshire.  He was ancestor of the SHAW-STEWART family, Baronetcy created
2 CONC  27 Mar 1667[1138].  m ---.  The name of Sir John´s wife is not known.  Sir John & his wife had --- children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         MARGARET Stewart (-after Aug 1442).  Her marriage is confirmed by the charter dated 12 Mar 1440 under which her grandson "Sir Duncan le Cambel knight Lord of Lochawe" donated alms from "his lands of Ardenaslate" to the 
2 CONC church of Dunovyng [Dunoon], for the souls of "his grandfather Celestin Cambel and Isabella Lamont [Laigmani] his lawful wife…Colin Cambel his father and Mariote filie M´Cwill Cambel matris quondam nostre…his late wife Marcellina 
2 CONC Stewart and Margaret Stewart his present wife"[1139].  m (before 12 Mar 1440) as his second wife, Sir DUNCAN Campbell of Lochow, son of Sir COLIN Campbell of Lochow, Argyllshire & his wife Mariot Campbell (-1453, bur Kilmun).  He 
2 CONC was created Lord Campbell in 1445.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Stewart,_1st_Earl_of_Lennox
2 CONT
2 CONT His marriage has been a source of genealogical confusion. He is recorded as having contracted to marry Margaret, the daughter of Alexander Montgomerie, 1st Lord Montgomerie, and Margaret Boyd, by indenture on 15 May 1438 as both p
2 CONC arties were under age. She, however, appears to have died young. Ultimately, he married another Margaret Montgomerie in 1460, who was not the same individual, but her fraternal niece, daughter of Alexander, Master of Montgomerie (
2 CONC son of the 1st Lord), by his wife Elizabeth Hepburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Margaret Montgomerie had eight recorded children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Marion Stuart. Lady Elizabeth Stewart, b.  c. 1464, married Archibald Campbell, 2nd Earl of Argyll Robert Stuart, 4th Seigneur d'Aubigny, b. c. 1470, d. 1544. Sir John Stewart, Seigneur d'Oison, b. bef. 1446, d. c. 1512. Eliz
2 CONC abeth Stuart, b. bef. 1476. Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox, b. bef. 5 May 1488, d. 9 Sep 1513, Flodden. Sir William Stewart, Seigneur d'Oison, b. bef. 1495, d. bef. 1504. Alexander Stewart, b. bef. 1495, d. bef. 1509. Parents
2 CONC  and simlings Margaret: n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Montgomerie,_1st_Lord_Montgomerie _____________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p26157.htm#i261561
