2 CONT '''4 May 1478: Notarial instrument relating to the delivery to Sir James Flemyng, rector of Chergraple as procurator for Alexander, Lord Home and Lady Margaret Montgomery, his spouse of 48 cows by the tenants of the lands of Galow
2 CONC bereis, lordship of Stewarton and their delivery by said sir James as procurator foresaid to Thomas Home, natural son of Alexander and Margaret. Witnesses: Robert Mungumry of Bradstan, Constantine Dunlop of that ilk, John Arnot, A
2 CONC rthur Boyd, Andrew Dunlop and William Redpath with others. John Reid, notary. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f38%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomery&ko=p&
