2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 April 1493: Instrument of Resignation by William Chanslar Lord of Quodquhen Nether, of his lands of Quodquhen and Cormestone, in the hands of his superior, John Lord Somervill, (John Somervill of Cambusnathane, tutor of the 
2 CONC said Lord, being present), reserving to the said William the free tenement and whole profit of the said lands of Quodquhen, with the free tenement and whole profit of 4 merks of the said lands of Cormestowne, for the whole time of
2 CONC  his life; and reserving the lawful third part of the said lands of Quodquhen only to Jonet Geddas, his spouse, for the whole time of her life. Done in the chapel of the manor of Quodhaly. Witnesses: Thomas Somerwill of Blakpull, 
2 CONC John Browne of Cultyremanys, Patrick Moyre of Anandstowne and others. William Hunter, Notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD118%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=SOMERVILL&ko=p&r=&ro=
2 CONC s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Chancellor family of Shieldhill, Lanarkshire, reference GD118/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 April 1493: Instrument of Sasine given propriis manibus by John Somervile of Cambusnathane, tutor of John Lord Somervill, Baron of the Barony of, Carnwyth, to John Chanslare, eldest son and apparent heir of William Chanslare
2 CONC  of Quodquen, of the lands of Quodquen Nether, according to the resignation of the said William Chanslare, and according to the tenor of the old infeftment: The said John Chanslare being placed in the house of his said father, all
2 CONC  others being expelled, and the doors closed. Witnesses, Mr William Creichtowne, Vicar of Walestowne, Sir William Lyndessay, Vicar of Knokbryd, Notary Public, and others. William Hunter, Notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk
2 CONC /nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD118%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=SOMERVILL&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Chancellor family of Shieldhill, Lanarkshire, reference GD118/8]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John, third Lord Somerville, born about 1484...He died before 27 October 1522, having married Agnes, daughter of Humphrey Colquhoun of Luss.  [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft#page/14/mode/2up The Scots peer
2 CONC age VIII, page 15]'''
