1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR ROBERT BRUCE OF AIRTH ==
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000213388482825&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n44/mode/1up
2 CONT [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/bruce08.php Stirnet: Bruce 08]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summaries ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Susceeded his grandfather in Airth Killed at Battle of Flodden 2 sons 1 daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT ref ILG
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight of Stanehouse & Airth 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.brucefamily.com/GroupC.html The DNA of Robert De Brus]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes:==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://books.google.com/books?id=v0lmAAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA187&ots=D52l-2voUF&dq=william%20livingston%20married%20janet%20bruce&pg=PA187#v=onepage&q=william%20livingston%20married%20janet%20bruce&f=false The Scots Peerage:] Founded
2 CONC  on Wood's Edition of Sir Robert Douglas ..., Volume 5  edited by James Balfour Paul.  Page 187-188
2 CONT
2 CONT "Janet, second daughter of Sir John Bruce of Stenhouse and Airth ... married William Livingston, younger, of Kilsyth ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert died on 9 September 1513 at Flodden Field, Northumberland, England, and was killed in action.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.robertsewell.ca/pdf/024Livingston2.pdf Livingston: Bruce of Airth]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/bookofbruceances00week/page/n12/mode/1up Book of Bruce: 352 pp. including index]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Robert, the eldest son of Sir John Bruce, was served heir  to his father, 8 October 1488. At the time of his father's death he could not have been more than eleven years old, or at his grandfather's more than sixteen, if, as is st
2 CONC ated, his parents were married in 1471. In 1488-89 he had a precept for a certain sum in the Lord Treasurer's accounts " For biggin of his place of Ercht that was brynt " before the battle of Sauchie by the forces of James in., at
2 CONC  that time the house of Keir was also burnt. He was a knight, and probably the principal part of the present Castle of Airth was built by him after the burning before mentioned. On 29 June 1489, he had a charter of confirmation fr
2 CONC om King James iv. of the charter of King James ii. to his grandfather Alexander. Sir Robert married  Euphame, daughter of Alexander, Lord Montgomerie, and sister of Hugh, first Earl of Eglintoun, and was killed at Flodden, 1513, l
2 CONC eaving issue: four sons and one daughter, viz. : —
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Robert, succeeded his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. John, mentioned as being dead 1512.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Edward
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. James
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Isobel,married 1505 Andreas de Methven de eodem.
2 CONT
2 CONT *[https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n44/mode/1up The Bruces of Airth and their cadets by Armstrong, William Bruce p 13]
2 CONT ----
