1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JEAN BLAIR Lady Montgreenan ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Blair, here treated, is the daughter of John Blair of that Ilk. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f257&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Jeane+Blair&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=y NRS:
2 CONC  GD86/257]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Blair died before 9 January 1624, the date upon which her grandson, Alexander Cunningham of Montgrennan, was served as her heir. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=b
2 CONC l&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=montgrennan&f=false Inquisitiones Generales]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Blair married Alexander Cunningham, Commendator of Kilwinning. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f11%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Jean+Blair&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=y 
2 CONC NRS: GD3/2/11/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Blair, widow of Alexander Cunningham, Commendator of Kilwinning, married John Stewart of Ardmalloch, Sheriff of Bute. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/242 The Scots Peerage IV: 242]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 January 1581-82: Letters of Tack (much injured by damp) by Jeane Blair, daughter of Johnne Blair of that Ilk, tackswoman of the parsonage teinds of the kirk of Stewartoun, with consent of Alexander, commendator of Killwyninge
2 CONC , her spouse, in favour of David Conynghame of Robertland of the teind sheaves of the following lands, viz:- the six merkland of Fullschawis, which pays 19 bolls meal and 2 bolls bear, the twenty shilling land of Spittell, which p
2 CONC ays 3 bolls meal, the four merkland of Braidieland, which pays 4 bolls meal and one-half boll bear, the 2½ merkland of Robertland, which pays 4½ bolls bear, the 40 shilling land of Over Lochrige, which pays 5 bolls meal, the 6 mer
2 CONC kland of Over and Nether Cassillton which pays 11 bolls meal and the 14 shilling land of Horsmwre, which pays 3 bolls meal all lying in the parish of Stewartone and the 2½ merkland of the Hoilhous lying in the parish of Irvin, whi
2 CONC ch pays 5 bolls meal, all lying in the bailiary of Conynghame and sheriffdom of Air, for 19 years from Lammas 1581 at a yearly rent of 16/8 for each boll of the above 58(?) bolls of victual, extending altogether to £48: 6: 8. At K
2 CONC illwyning 4 January 1581-2. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f257&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Jeane+Blair&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser
2 CONC  Charters, reference GD86/257]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 November 1582: Charter by which Hugh Cunningham of Watterstoun confirms that he has sold the ten merk lands of old extent to Alexander Cunningham, Commendator of Kilwinning, and his wife Jeanne Blair. The land is to be held b
2 CONC y Alexander and Jeanne in conjunct fee and liferent, and is to descend to their lawful male heirs, whom failing by Alexander's nearest heirs. The contract of sale was concluded at Irvine on 31 July 1582 and the charter was confirm
2 CONC ed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 2 March 1582-83. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/160 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-1593, charter numbe
2 CONC r 526 on p. 160]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5-6 December 1582: Tack by Alexander, commendator of Killwynninge (Kilwinning) with consent of the convent thereof, setting to Thomas master of Boyde, and to Thomas Boyde his second son liberal and the survivor of them and afte
2 CONC r their decease to the heirs and assignees whomsoever of said Thomas younger for nineteen years from Lammas last bypast, the teind sheaves and teind bolls of vitual of the following lands, viz Monefode-Boyde, the Newtoun, the land
2 CONC s Under the hill, the Manis of the Law, Blakschaw and the Brewlands alias lcus Roberti Boyde, Arneill-Boyde, Huntarstoun and Campbellstoun, all lying in the parish of Kilbryde, bailiery of Conynghame (Cunningham) and sheriffdom of
2 CONC  Ayr and yielding yearly 57 bolls victual, meal and bear, of teind. Paying yearly for each of the said bolls 6s 8d, in all 9lib Scots; beginning payment for Huntarstoun, Campbellstone and Manis of Law betwixt Yule and Candlemas ne
2 CONC xt, for Arneill-Boyde after the ish of a nineteen years tackset to William Cunningham, son of Hew Cunningham of Walterstone and for the others after the decease of Alexander Cunningham, son and heir apparent of James Cunningham of
2 CONC  Clonbeith; all conform to contract dated at Irwin, 30th November 1582. At Kilwinning, 5th December 1582. Witnesses Robert Blair, brother german of John Blair of that ilk, William Stevinstone, Gavin Nasmythe and Alexander Michell 
2 CONC younger, notaries and comburgesses of Irwin with others divers. Signed Alexander Commendarius a Kilwynige, Deyn James Mechell, Deyne Robart Curry, Deyne Jhone Deyne. In dorso Jeane Blair, spouse of said commendator and tacksman of
2 CONC  the parsonage teinds of the kirk of Kilbryde, ratifies said tack in presence of said notaries. Whereupon William Stevinstone, burgess of Irwin, in name of said master of Boyde asked instruments.Witnesses Robert Blair aforesaid, J
2 CONC ames Cowpar in Kilwinning, Thomas Eset, messenger, Alexander Michell, younger notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2648&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Jeane+Blair&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=
2 CONC &dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/2648]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 October 1583: Contract between Alexander, commendator of Kilwinning, and Jean Blair his wife on the one part and James Hamilton of Ardoch and his wife Elizabeth on the other about fishings on the water of Garnock. [http://ca
2 CONC talogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f11%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Jean+Blair&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton
2 CONC , reference GD3/2/11/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 August 1591: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the forty shilling lands of old extent of Hullerhill in the Regality of Kilwinning, Bailliery of Cunningham and Sheriffdom of Ayr, together wi
2 CONC th various other lands, to Jean Blair, daughter of John Blair of that Ilk. These lands are to be held in feuferme by Jean and by her lawful heirs by Alexander Cunningham, Commendator of Kilwining, whom failing by Alexanders neares
2 CONC t heirs and assignees. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/648 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-1593, charter number 1918 on pp. 648-49]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 February 1592: Decreet of lords at instance of Mr William Melville, commendator of Kilwinning, senator of the college of justice, against Jean Blair, lady Montgreenan and others, and dene James Michel subprior of Kilwinning, 
2 CONC because of their refusal to hand over certain registers of the abbey and the seal. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f12%2f11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Jean+Blair&ko=p&r=&ro=m&
2 CONC df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/2/12/11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 January 1624: (1104) ALEXANDER CUNYNGHAME filius legitimus Magistri Jacobi Cunynghame de Montgrennan, haeres Jeannae Blair, aviae. viii. 241. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyl
2 CONC e&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=montgrennan&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum ets. II: Inquisitiones General
2 CONC es]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
