2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Hunter Papers ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 June 1547: Letter by William, Lord Semple, and Dame Marioun his spouse, undertaking on pavment of a certain sum to reconvey to MUNGO HWNTAR OF HUNTERISTOUN the teyne shilling land of HOLHOUS AND BLAKFALD, the lands callit MY
2 CONC LNEAKYR and meadow callit QUHYTTOCH MEDOW, with the pertinents, in the lordschip of Hunteristoun, with Charter and Sasine maid to them thereupon by the said Mungo Huntar, dated and sealed by William, Lord Semple, and by Sir David 
2 CONC Neill, Notar Public, for Dame Marioun Montgomery, Lady Semple, with her hand on the pen led by him, the 21st June 1547. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso45scotuoft/page/24/mode/1up Hunter Papers: pp. 24-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 December 1581: The Testament-Dative and Inventar of the goods geir soumes of money and dettis perteining to Umquhile Robert Hunter of Hunterstoun within the Sherefdome of Air the tyme of his deceis quha deceist upoun the nynt
2 CONC  day of August the yeir of God l m vc lxxxj yeirs Faythfullie made and gevin vp be Margaret Craufurd Lady Hunterstoun his relict In name and behalf of Jane, Marioun, Katherine, Elizabeth, and Hew Hunteris, yr lauchtfull barnes by 
2 CONC the air and executours Dativis decernit to their said Umqle. father be decreit of the Commissars of Ed r. as the samyn decreit of the dait the first day of December the yeir of God i m v c lxxxj yeirs at lenth proportis. . . . . .
2 CONC  Followis the dettis awand to the deid. . . . . . Item be Dame Marioun Montgumrie lady Sempill ane hundreth merk. Item mair be hir of Lent money fiftie merk and Johne Gray in Corsbie myln and Thomas Scyir in Corsbie cautioun thair
2 CONC fore. Item mair be the said Dame Marioun Montgumrie lady Sympill tua hundreth and fiftie merk qlk. soum she confest befoir witnesses . . . . . Item mair be the said Dame Marioun Montgomery lady Sympill of byrun annuellis ane hundr
2 CONC eth merk mair be hir of lent money ane hundreth merk. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso45scotuoft/page/32/mode/1up Hunter Papers: 32]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 November 1555: Dame Mariota Montgomery, Lady Symple, [Note] Came in the Queen's Will for Ratihabition of the Slaughter of Gilbert Rankyne in Lecheland, committed by the fervants of the faid Lady, Mar. 17, 1553, under filence 
2 CONC of night: And for Ratihabition of the cruel Hurting and Wounding  of John  Fynn, and Mutilation of his arm; and for Hurting  and Wounding of John Roger in fundry parts of his body, to the effufion of his blood, committed at the fa
2 CONC me time — by Refetting of her fervants, who had committed the faid crimes, red-hand, that fame night, within THE Castle  of Laven, immediately after the perpetration thereof: And alfo for Ratihabition of the taking and apprehendin
2 CONC g of Humphry  Malcolmefoun  and  Archibald  Scherare, they being conducted by her fervants on the fame night to the Caftle of Laven, feeing she received  them into her faid Caftle; Item, for Incarceration and fubjection of the fai
2 CONC d perfons in the forefaid Caftle by the fpace of twenty-four hours, without food or drink; thereby Ufurping the Queen's  authority.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note by Robert Pitcairn:  She was eldest daughter of Hugh first Earl of Eglintoun; and was, at the time of this Trial, relict of William second Lord Sempill, who died anno 1548. There seems no doubt that her name was Mariota, s
2 CONC he having been named after her mother, Mariota Seytoun, Mistress of Borthwick, and sister of Gerge  Iord Seytoun. [https://archive.org/details/criminaltrialsin01pitc/page/n428/mode/1up Ancient Criminal Trials I - II: 381*]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 June 1559: Reversion by John Campbell of Skippininche and Marian Montgomery, his spouse, to Hugh Montgomery of Hasilhead, and Margaret Fressell, his mother, of the 10 mark lands of Lyoncros, containing the reversion price of
2 CONC  250 marks. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f164&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marian+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kil
2 CONC marnock, reference GD8/164]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 August 1569: Procuratory by Marion Montgomery, widow of late William Lord Semple, with consent of John Campbell, provost of Kilmun, now her husband, for renouncing all claims to lands of Spango Campbell. [http://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f7%2f15&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=William+lord+Semple&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton: Titles, refere
2 CONC nce GD3/2/7/15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Books of the Town Clerks of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 June 1559: Charter by which Hugh Mungumry of Hasilhead confirms that he has sold the ten merk lands of old extent of Liandcross in the barony of Renfrew to John Campbell of Skippinche and his wife Lady Marion Mungumry. [https
2 CONC ://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto05glas#page/12/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols V: 1349]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 January 1559-60: Acknowledgement by John Campbell of Skippinche and his wife Marion Mungumry, that they had received from Hugh Mungumry of Hasilheid, 250 merks in a reversion for the redemption of the ten merk lands of old ex
2 CONC tent of Lyencors. Witnessed by George Mungumry, brother of Hugh Mungumry of Hasilheid. [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto05glas#page/14/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols V: 1352]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Commissary Records of Edinburgh ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Marion Montgomery, Lady Sempill, was still alive when her husband https://www.geni.com/people/John-Campbell-of-Skipnish-Provost-of-Kilmun/6000000006444052875 died on 18 September 1573. He did not refer to her by name in hi
2 CONC s last will and testament, which was made shortly before he died, but he left legacies to "my spous" and to "my lady my spous." [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of 
2 CONC Johne Campbell, Provost of Kilmun, reference CC8/8/3]'''
2 CONT
