1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert 3rd Lord Sempill ... By his second wife, Elizabeth Carlyle, he had a son '''John''', ancestor of the Sempills of Beltrees, and English Born, married Mary Livingston in March 1565. She was one of the Four Mar
2 CONC ys who were ladies in waiting to Mary, Queen of Scots.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From  "John Semple of Beltrees" The Scots Peerage by Paul, James
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 548 – John Sempill, who was legitimated as above in 1546, seems to have gone to France in 1560. He is described as ‘an Englishman born.’ As John Sempill of Beltries, he was called as one of the substitutes in the conveyance w
2 CONC hich his father made of his estates on 8 November 1572. The Regent Morton is said to have coveted the aftermentioned lands granted by Queen Mary, and to have endeavoured to reduce the gift. Having used intemperate threats, Sempill
2 CONC  was arrested on a suspicion of conspiring against the life of the Regent, and on being tortured with the boot, confessed. He had certain jewels and furs belonging to Queen Mary, and was imprisoned in Blackness because he wouln no
2 CONC t deliver them to the Earl of Lennox. On 15 June 1577 he was convicted of treasonably conspiring for the slaughter of the Earl of Morton, the Regent. He died on 25 August 1579, having married (contract 3 March 1564-65) Marie, daug
2 CONC hter of Alexander, fifth Lord Livingstone. They had a grant from Queen Mary, 20 March 1564-65, of the lands of Over Drumdelgie and others in the barony of Stratbogie, on the forfeiture of the Earl of Huntly; but in 1567, Huntly ha
2 CONC ving been restored to the lands, they got instead the Island of Little Cumbrae and others. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By her, who survived him, he had issue;-
2 CONT * Capt. John Semple abt 1564 - Bet 1646
2 CONT * Dorathie Semple
2 CONT * Sir James Semple, 2nd Lord Sempill 'of Beltrees' 1565 - 1626
2 CONT * Arthur Semple
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Livingston
2 CONT
2 CONT In March 1565, Mary Livingston married John Sempill of Bruntschiells and Beltrees, a son of Robert Sempill, 3rd Lord Sempill (c. 1505–1576), who had been born in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT The leading preacher of the Scottish Reformation, John Knox, disapproved of Queen Mary's court, and included some remarks on the marriage in his History of the Reformation in Scotland. According to Knox, Sempill was called the "Da
2 CONC ncer", and Livingstone was known as "Lusty" and pregnant before their wedding. A grant of lands made by Queen Mary to the couple in 1565 was renewed to Mary Livingstone by James VI of Scotland in 1581. Knox singled out the barony 
2 CONC of Auchtermuchty which was included in this grant as one of the rewards given by the Queen to courtiers of whom he disapproved, rather than to hard-working administrators.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The 19th-century writer Agnes Strickland researched the marriage, noting that it was delayed rather than "shame-hastened" as Knox suggested, and had been discussed in autumn 1564. It was celebrated at Court during the Shrove-Tide 
2 CONC feast on 5 March, called "Fasterins Eve" in Scotland. The diplomat Thomas Randolph called it the "great marriage of this happie Englishman that shall marrie lustie Livingston." Randolph heard of a plan to invite the Earl of Bedfor
2 CONC d who was Governor of Berwick-upon-Tweed to the wedding because Sempill's mother was English. The Earl of Bedford had not previously visited Edinburgh.[3] Queen Mary gave "Mademoyselle de Sanple" a present of a bed made from scarl
2 CONC et and black velvet, with embroidered taffeta curtains and silk fringes.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2. Laing, David, ed., Works of John Knox: History of the Reformation, vol. 2, Wodrow Society (1846), 415–16 and footnotes
2 CONT * 3. Strickland, Agnes, Lives of the Queens of Scotland, vol.4, Blackwood (1853), pp.94-6, citing Thomson, Thomas, Collection of Inventories, (1815): see also Calendar State Papers Scotland, vol. 2 (1900), p. 113, 125, 133
2 CONT * 4. Robertson, Joseph, ed., Inventaires de la Royne Descosse, (1863), p. 31, 153
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-312443951-1-588042/john-semple-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-6679e341a80eb334f1f7f57033ea549d&mrid=dccbafb0965433510baf8b38aba837de MyHeritage Family
2 CONC  Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 30 2017, 23:56:16 UTC''
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Sempill,_3rd_Lord_Sempill
2 CONT
