1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LADY JEAN SEMPILL (aka DOMINE JEANNE SEMPILL)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Jean Sempill, here treated, is the daughter of Robert, Lord Sempill and his wife Isabel Hamilton, daughter of William Hamilton of Sanquar. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/550/mode/1up The Scots
2 CONC  Peerage V: 550]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Jean Sempill, here treated is reported died on the last day of February 1592-93. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/550/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 550]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 21 January 1594. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Dame Jane Sempill, Lady Ross, reference CC8/8/26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Additional Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 20 April 1601. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Dame Jane Sempill, lady Ross. reference CC8/8/35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Jean Sempill, here treated, married James, Lord Ross of Hawkhead. She and her deceased husband are mentioned in a quitclaim charter dated 23 March 1582-83 which was issued by her daughter Elizabeth and Elizabeth's husband,
2 CONC  Alan Lockhart, son and apparent heir of Mungo Lockhart of Cleghorn.  [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi05scot#page/164/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 15
2 CONC 80-1593, charter number 538 on page 164]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 March 1582: Service of terce of Lady Jean Semple, relict of James, Lord Rois of Halkheid and Malvile, in barony of Malvile, in sheriffdoms of Edinburgh, Linlithgow and Stirling; Lady Jean obtains the shadow part by lot, and 
2 CONC chooses the tower of Malvile as her second mansion. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD199%2f39&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jean+semple&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of
2 CONC  Scotland, Papers of the Ross Family of Pitcalnie, reference GD199/39]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 March 1582-83: REX  concessit  et  quitteclamavit  ALLANO LOCKART  filio  et  heredi  apparenti  Quintigerni  L.  de  Cleghorne,  et  ELIZABETHS ROS  ejus  sponse  future  (filie  legitime quondam  Jacobi  dom.  Ros  de  Hal
2 CONC ket  et Mailwell  et  Domine  Jeanne  Sempll  domine Ros  ejus  sponse),  eorumque  alteri  diutius viventi  in  conjuncta  infeodatione,  et heredibus  masc.  inter  eos  legit,  procreandis, quibus  deficientibus,  heredibus  ma
2 CONC sc.  sive assignatis  dicti  Allani  quibuscunque, — terras  de  Grugfute,  in  jiarochia  de  Carriddin,  vic.  Linlithgow;  32  solidat.  terrarum  de  Hill  de  Cleghorne,  molendinum granorum  de  Cleghorne  cum  terris  molen
2 CONC dinariis  etc.,  in  baronia  et  dominio  de  Kilbryde  per  annexationem,  vic.  de  Lanerk; quatuor  librat.  terrarum  antiqui  extentus de  Langbyris,  Lonerig,  Boithuilescheillis, ex  dicti  Quint.  10  libratis  de  Boithu
2 CONC ile, in  dominio  et  baronia  de  Boithuile,  vic. Lanerk  ; — necnon  dicto  Allano,  et  heredibus supradictis,  —  reliquam  partem  diet. 10  libratarum  de  Boithuill  cum  manerie et  mansione,  lie  Park  de  Boithuill, te
2 CONC rtia  parte  molendini  granarii  de  B. situati  sub  aqua  de  Calder,  cum  tertia parte  terrarum  molendinariarum  &c., extenden.  ad  6  librat.  ant.  ext.;  reliquam partem  diet.  10  libratarum  ant.  ext.  de Cleghorne,
2 CONC   extenden.  ad  8  librat.  8  sol. ant.  ext. ; — quas  dictus  Quint,  resignavit : — Reservato  dicto  Quint,  vitali  redditu  diet. 8  librat.  8  sol.  de  Cleghorne  et  6  librat.  de Boithuile  : — Tenend.  Cleghorne  de
2 CONC   rege tanquam  principe  et  senescallo  Scotie, ceteras  de  rege: — Preterea  rex  voluit quod  unica  sasina  apud  maneriem  seu mansionem  de  Cleghorne  capienda  pro omnibus  diet,  terris  &c.  de  Cleghorne  et Boithuile
2 CONC   staret: — Test,  ut  in  aliis  cartis &c.  xxxv.  790. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi05scot#page/164/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-1593, cha
2 CONC rter number 538 on page 164]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
