1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == GRISSEL SEMPILL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Grissel Sempill here treated is not the same person as''' https://www.geni.com/people/Grizel-Semple-Lady-Stanehous/6000000002979961425?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1493104527329&through=6000000017845335924
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms, Grizzel Sempill is the bastard daughter of Robert, third Lord Semple. He was unable to identify her mother but suggested that she may have been the daughter of an Eng
2 CONC lish woman named Elizabeth Carlile. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft#page/550/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 550]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Grissell Sempill, here treated, married John Blair of that Ilk.  [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/572/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: 2179] They were contracted on 11 May 1565. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeer
2 CONC agefoun07pauluoft#page/550/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 550]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 February 1574: Charter by which Robert Graham of Knockdolian confirms possession of the ten merk land of old extent of Thornlie-Wallace in the sheriffdom of Renfrew to John Blair of that Ilk and his wife Grissillide Simple. T
2 CONC he contract of marriage between John Blair of that lk and his wife Grissillide Simple was signed at Edinburgh on 19 February 1573. For greater security a charter of confirmation under the Great Seal of Scotland was obtained on 8 F
2 CONC ebruary 1573-74. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/572/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D. 1546-1580, charter number 2179 on page 572]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 July 1589: A charter by which John Blair of that Ilk confirms that he has given the six shilling eight penny lands of old exten of Bogton in the Renfrewshire parish of Cathcart to his son and heir John Blair and his wife Isa
2 CONC belle Boyd, daughter of Thomas, Master of Boyd. The marriage contract for John Blair junior and Isabelle Boyd was signed at Glasgow on 5 July 1589. John Blair of that Ilk reserved his own liferent and that of his wife Grisillidi S
2 CONC emple. For greater security a charter under the Great Seal of Scotland was obtained on 2 February 1598-99. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi06scot#page/278/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D.  1593-16
2 CONC 08, charter number 853 on page 278]'''
