1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===ROBERT, MASTER OF SEMPILL===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Sempill, Master of Sempill''' 
2 CONT * Son of Robert Sempill, 3rd Lord Sempill and Isabel Hamilton.
2 CONT * Married Elizabeth Hamilton, daughter of James Hamilton, 1st Earl of Arran, before 27 May 1543.
2 CONT * Married Barbara Preston, daughter of Archibald Preston, before 30 April 1569.
2 CONT * Died before 16 December 1569.
2 CONT
2 CONT Supported MARY QUEEN OF SCOTS. He was styled as Master of Sempill. He murdered William Crichton, 5th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar on 11 June 1550 at the house of Governor Arran, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland, stabbed to death in a 
2 CONC quarrel by the 3rd Lord Semphill.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Child of Robert Sempill, Master of Sempill and Elizabeth Hamilton''' Robert Sempill, 4th Lord Sempill+3 b. b 1569, d. 25 Mar 1611
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Reference''' http://www.thepeerage.com/p11034.htm#i110338
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Murder of William Crichton'''
2 CONT >Robert, Lord Sempill, was said to have murdered William Crichton, 5th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar on 11 June 1552. According to the story recorded by John Lesley, Lord Sempill was in the private lodging of Regent Arran in Edinburgh
2 CONC , and was moved by rage to stab Lord Sanquhar with his sword. Sempill was arrested and taken to Edinburgh Castle, and would have been beheaded, but his influential friends secured his release.
2 CONT
2 CONT >It was said by Robert Lindsay of Pitscottie that Sempill's daughter, Grizzel called 'Lady Gilton', who was the widow of James Hamilton of Stenhouse a former Provost of Edinburgh, was particularly helpful in securing help for Semp
2 CONC ill. She was the mistress of John Hamilton, Archbishop of St Andrews, Regent Arran's brother. A record survives of a pardon granted in September 1552 to Lord Sempill's eldest son, '''Robert Master of Sempill, for his part in the m
2 CONC urder.'''
