3 POST EH21 8RY
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://thepeerage.com/p20951.htm#i209505
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan Cathcart, 3rd Lord Cathcart was the son of Alan Cathcart, Master of Cathcart and Agnes Lyle.[1][2][3] He succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Cathcart in December 1535.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Helen Sempill, daughter of William Sempill, 2nd Lord Sempill and Margaret Montgomerie.[1][2][4] They had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan, 4th Lord Cathcart (only son) b. c 1537, d. Dec 1618[1][5]
2 CONT He also had a natural son also named Alan.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Pinkie on 10 September 1547 where he was killed in action.[1][4][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT Clan MacFarlane: Alan Cathcart
2 CONT The Peerage: Alan Cathcart
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 Paul, James Balfour. "The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom", Edinburgh: Davi
2 CONC d Douglas,1905, Vol. II, Archive.org, pp. 512-3
2 CONT ↑ 2.0 2.1 Crawfurd, George, "The peerage of Scotland : containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom", Edinburgh: George Crawfurd, 1716, Archive.org, p. 77
2 CONT ↑ MacGregor, Gordon, The Red Book of Scotland, Scotland, private, 2022, Ed. 3, Vol. II. p. 927
2 CONT ↑ 4.0 4.1 Cokayne, George Edward, "The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom", London: St. Catherine Press, 1913, Ed. 2 Vol III, Archive.org, p. 104
2 CONT ↑ 5.0 5.1 Burke, John Bernard, "Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the peerage, baronetage, and knightage, Privy Council, and order of preference" , London: Harrison & Sons, 1915, 77th ed., Archive.org, p. 410
