1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN KENNEDY OF SKELDON===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n452/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, III, p. 436] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 February 1552: 	Precept of Clare constat by Gilbert Earl of Cassillis, to Dame Margaret Mure wife of John Kennedy (of Skeldon) as heir of the deceased Quintin Mure of Aird her father in the 6 merk land of Over Kilmoir and mil
2 CONC l thereof, lying in the bailiary of Carrick - to be holden blanch of the Earl and his successors Dated at Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f549&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&
2 CONC tp=n&k=John+Kennedy+of+Skeldon&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/549]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This Ladys mother was Dame Katharine Kennedy daughter of David 1st Earl of Cassillis, and who married Quintin Mure of Aird some time prior to 7th January 1510.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 April 1553: Instrument of Resignation ad perpetuam remanentiam, by the said Dame Margaret Mure with consent of John Kennedy of Skeldon her husband, in the hands of Gilbert Earl of Cassillis, of the 6 merk land and mill of Ov
2 CONC er Kilmoir, to remain with the Earl and his successors in all time coming, his Lordship having redeemed the same from her in due form - reserving the liferent thereof to Dame Katharine Kennedy her mother. Witnesses - Adam Boyd in 
2 CONC Pinkil, Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains, Thomas Kennedy of Coif and Gilbert Baird of Kilhenzie and James Ross, writer. Dated at Mayboll. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f552&st=1
2 CONC &tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Kennedy+of+Skeldon&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/552]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1560: Letter of Reversion by John Kennedy of Skeldon and Dame Margaret Mure his wife (See GD/25/1/552) to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis, bearing the Earl having infeft them in conjunct fee and liferent and the heirs procreate betwe
2 CONC en them whom failling the said John Kennedy his nearest heirs whatsoever, in an annualrent of 50 merks money of Scotland payable at two terms in the year Whitsunday and Martinmas by equal portions furth of the 4 merk land of Holms
2 CONC  of Dalrymple, lying in the bailiary of Kyle Stewart, yet nevertheless they oblige them and theirs aforesaid, upon the Earl or his successors making payment to them within the Church of Mayboll of the sum of 500 merks like money, 
2 CONC they shall immediately thereafter renounce and discharge the said annualrent and declare the same redeemed Witnesses - Mr Patrick Vaus parson of Wigton, James Kennedy of Ochterlour and Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains. [http://catalogu
2 CONC e.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f596&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Kennedy+of+Skeldon&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassill
2 CONC is (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/596]'''
