1 NAME Hugh /Kennedy of Ochterlure/
2 GIVN Hugh
2 SURN Kennedy of Ochterlure
2 _MARNM Kennedy of Ochterlure
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HUGH KENNEDY OF OCHTERLURE===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1560: 	Decree and Final sentence given and pronounced by Thomas Abbot of Glenluce, bearing his being chosen by James Kennedy of Ochterlour at request of Gilbert Earl of Cassillis, to decide about the heritable right of the land
2 CONC s of Ochterlour and others, lying in the County of Wigton, belonging to the said James Kennedy, and that conform to his obligation dated at Mayboll 12th January then last 1560 and subsuming that having undertaken to decide in the 
2 CONC matter and having respect for the well and honour of the House of Cassillis and considering that James Kennedy having no heirs male of his body, but only two daughters and that Agnes Johnston his wife was not likely to have more c
2 CONC hildren and also considering that he had and has great support and assistance yearly from the Earl (his brother's son) therefore ordains him to infeft the Earl and his heirs male in the lands of Ochterlour and 5 merk land of Stran
2 CONC raer and Marscluvy - reserving his liferent and the liferent of the said Agnes Johnston his wife and decerns the Earl to dote his two daughters according to their rank at the sight of four landed gentlemen nearest of him to the Ho
2 CONC use of Cassillis [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f594&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD25%2f1%2f594&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Archives of Scotland, Papers of the Ken
2 CONC nedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/594]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 May 1576: Precept by Gilbert Earl of Cassillis for infefting Hugh Kennedy of Ochterlure and Beseta Kennedy his wife (See GD25/1/594) in conjunct fee and liferent, in the 4 merk land of Dalrympleholm - 6 merk land of Kilmore 
2 CONC with the mill thereof and 5 merk land of Bernardston Lindsayston and Drumroyhill, lying in the Earldom of Carrick and baronies of Dalrymple and Cassillis respective - To be holden blanch of the Earl and his successors - reserving 
2 CONC the free tenement of the said lands of Kilmore and mill thereof, and lands of Bernardston Lindsayston and Drumroyhill to John Kennedy sometime of Skeldon father of the said Hugh Kennedy, for all the days of his life. Witnesses - J
2 CONC ames Kennedy son of William Kennedy of Monersion, John Kennedy in Baltersan Hugh Kennedy in Anees Nevin Agnew in Crackloch and Sir Herbert Anderson Notary. Dated at Inch. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/deta
2 CONC ils.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f844&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=skeldon&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/844]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 November 1576: Instrument of Seisin in favors of Hugh Kennedy of Ochterlure and Beseta Kennedy his wife, in the 4 merk land of Dalrympleholm 6 merk land of Kilmore with the mill there of, and 5 merk land of Bernardston Linds
2 CONC ayston, and Drumroyhill - proceeding on Precept by Gilb. Earl of Cassillis 13th May then last.  Witnesses Gilbert Baird of Kilquhenzie and Quintin Dick. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference
2 CONC =GD25%2f1%2f847&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=BESETA+KENNEDY&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/847]'''
1 FAMC @F6000000076882879997@
1 FAMS @F6000000076937555494@
1 RFN geni:6000000076938948386
1 SUBM @S6000000008879398364@
1 CHAN
2 DATE 15 MAR 2018
3 TIME 06:24:09
0 @I6000000002188028731@ INDI
1 NAME Katherine /Kennedy/
2 GIVN Katherine
2 SURN Kennedy
2 _MARNM Kennedy
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 9 JUL 1489 AND 9 AUG 1509
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1534
1 TITL Dame
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===DAME KATHERINE KENNEDY===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Katherine Kennedy is the daughter of David, Earl of Cassillis, and his first wife Agnes Borthwick. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/463/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, page 463] It is not possible to ide
2 CONC ntify the place and precise date of her birth. However, her mother appears to have married her father shortly before 9 July 1489 [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/395/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Sc
2 CONC otland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 1876 on page 395] and to have died before 9 August 1509 [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/721/mode/1up Ibidem, charter number 3371 on page 721] the date upon which her f
2 CONC ather gave certain lands to his second wife Margaret Boyd. Presumably, therefore, she was born during the intervening period.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Katherine Kennedy was married first, contract 4 October 1510, to Quintin Mure of the Aird. He and his wife had a precept of sasine for the lands of Kilmore on 7 January 1510-11. They had one child, a daughter named Margare
2 CONC t who was married first to Neil Montgomery of Lainshaw, and second to John Kennedy of Skeldon. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/461/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, page 461]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Child of the First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Mure/6000000071862225925?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1513022989980&through=6000000011750396693
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Katherine Kennedy married, as her second husband, Sir William Hamilton of Sorn and Sanquar before 11 May 1524 [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/61/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D.
2 CONC  1513-1546, charter number 272 on page 61] and was still married to him on 4 December 1556. It follows, therefore, that she is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Kennedy/6000000006902434632?from_flash=1&f
2 CONC session_id=1513019123432&through=6000000006902434632 who married her second husband John Wallace before 21 August 1545. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/740/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A
2 CONC .D. 1513-1546, charter number 3151 on page 740]''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to James Anderson, Catherine Kennedy and her husband had a charter for the lands of Ovir-Sorne and Nether-Sorne dated 3 May 1533 [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/382/mode/1up Historical and Gene
2 CONC alogical Memoirs of the House of Hamilton, page 382]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''G. Harvey Johnston follows Anderson and calls her Catherine Kennedy rather than Katherine Kennedy. He too says that  she and her husband had a charter for the lands of Ovir-Sorne and Nether-Sorne dated 3 May 1533. [https://arch
2 CONC ive.org/stream/heraldryofhamils00john#page/122/mode/1up G. Harvey Johnston, FSA (Scot)., The Heraldry of the Hamiltons with Notes on all the Males of the Family, Descriptions of the Arms, Plates and Pedigrees (W. & A. K. Johnston 
2 CONC Limited, Edinburgh & London, MCMIX), pp. 122]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 January 1510: Copy of Precept by David Earl of Cassillis for infefting Quintin Mure of Aird (See GD25/1/191) and Katherine Kennedy his wife, daughter of the Earl in the 6 merk land of Nether Kilmore with the mansion house the
2 CONC reof lying in the barony of Cassillis. Witnesses - Sir John Kennedy prebend of Mayboll, Sir Jasper Home Chaplain, James Kennedy son of Sir John Kennedy of Blairquhan and Thomas Corry of Kelwood. Dated at Aird [http://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f222&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Katherine+Kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa M
2 CONC uniments), reference GD25/1/222]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: It follows from the precept that David Lord Kennedy became Earl of Cassillis, between 25th July 1509, and 7th January 1510. See note immediately after GD25/1/215.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 June 1523: Letter of Reversion by William Hamilton of Maknariston and Katharine Kennedy his wife, to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis bearing the Earl having infeft them in the 40 shilling land of Barbiston and merk land of Brackenh
2 CONC ill, lying in the barony of Dalrymple, Kyle-regis, yet nevertheless they oblige them after the lapse of 3 years from the date of the said Letter, upon the Earl making payment to them, within the church of Ayr of the sum of 200 mer
2 CONC ks money of Scotland, that they shall resign in the hands of his Lordship and his successors the said lands of Barbiston and Brackenhill with all right and title which they had thereto and declare the same lawfully redeemed. Witne
2 CONC sses - Sir George Blair Chaplain, James Brown burgess of Ayr, and Adam Hamilton. Dated at Crossragwell. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f266&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=adam+h
2 CONC amilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/266]'''
