2 CONT '''4 December 1556: Charter by which William Hamilton, elder of Sorn and Sanquar confirms that he has given the lands and barony of Sanquar and others to his son and heir William Hamilton of Glenmure. The land conveyed is to be he
2 CONC ld by William Hamilton of Glenmure and his lawful male heirs, and in the event of his failure by James Hamilton, the brother of William the elder, and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by Bernard Hamilton, brother of William the
2 CONC  elder, and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by George Hamilton, brother of William the elder, and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by Patrick Hamilton, the bastard brother of William the elder, and his lawful male heirs who
2 CONC m failing by John Hamilton of Cambuskeith, whom failing by any of the lawful male heirs of William Hamilton the elder who bear the name and arms of Hamilton. William Hamilton, elder of Sorn and Sanquar, reserved his own liferent a
2 CONC ns that of his wife Katherine Kennedy. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on  9 December 1556. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/250/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A
2 CONC .D. 1546-1580, charter number 1125 on pages 250-51]'''
