2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 and 14 April 1654: Extract disposition by Neill Montgomery of Langschaw with consent of John Montgomery, younger, of Langschaw, his eldest son, and Margaret Lockhart, his spouse, to David Montgomery of Cockilbie, of 10 merkla
2 CONC nd of Langschaw and others in bailiery of Cuninghame, sheriffdom of Air, and others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH15%2f44%2f154&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+lockhart&ko=p&r
2 CONC =&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of David Ross, Accountant to the GPO, Edinburgh, reference RH15/44/154]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 November 1661: Charter granted by David Montgomery of Langshaw in favour of John Montgomery, his brother german, second lawful son of the deceased John Montgomery of Cockilbie, his heirs and assignees, of the said lands rese
2 CONC rving nevertheless the free tenement and liferent of Helen Houstoun, spouse of John Montgomery, late of Langshaw, during all the days of her life, if it should happen through her said husband deceasing she surviving; to hold of hi
2 CONC m for performance to the said Alexander, Earl of Eglinton and his heirs and successors, of ward and relief as often as they shall happen. Dated at Glasgow 28 November 1661. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/d
2 CONC etails.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f12%2f10&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+houstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/12/10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
