1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===NEIL MONTGOMERY===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Neil Montgomery, here treated, is the son of Neil Mobtgomery of Lainshaw. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Dative and Inventory of Neil Montgomerie lawful son to the deceased Neill M. of Lang
2 CONC shaw, reference CC8/8/76]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Neil Montgomery, here treated, is reported in error to have died intestate in January 1668. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Dative and Inventory of Neil Montgomerie lawful son to the decease
2 CONC d Neill M. of Langshaw, reference CC8/8/76] That this is an error is proved by the fact that he and Elizabeth Kirkwood had twin children whose baptism was registered at Edinburgh on 11 April 1673. Possibly, therefore, the year1668
2 CONC  was written in error for 1678.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Testament Dative and Inventory===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The testament dative and inventory of Neil Montgomery, here treated, was given up by his widow Elizabeth Kirkwood., who was recognised as her deceased husband's only executrix dative and creditrix. No provision was made for chi
2 CONC ldren, from which circumstance it would appear that none were alive when the testament dative and inventory was given up. Confirmation was granted to the widow on 5 May 1680.  [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Co
2 CONC urt, Testament Dative and Inventory of Neil Montgomerie lawful son to the deceased Neill M. of Langshaw, reference CC8/8/76]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000154872124867 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000154871832858 Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Neil Montgomery, here treated, married Elizabeth Kirkwood. A marriage contract dated 6 September 1665: "past betwixt the sd umqull Neill Montgomerie on the ane pairt & the sd Elizabeth Kirkwood wit consent of Margaret ffoules h
2 CONC er mother on the other pairt". [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Dative and Inventory of Neil Montgomerie lawful son to the deceased Neill M. of Langshaw, reference CC8/8/76]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Their intention to marry was proclaimed in the church of Canongate parish near Edinburgh on 3 October 1665, and 10 October 1665, [National Records of Scotland, Canongate Marriages, reference OPR.685/3/13] and they were married 
2 CONC "in the kirk of Halyrood hous be Mr. Patrick Hepburne, minister" on 30 October 1665. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso34scotuoft/page/284/mode/1up Canongate Register of Marriages, 1564-1800: 284]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
