2 CONT '''9 March 1564: Charter granted in obedience to a decree arbitral by Hugh Montgomery of Stane in favour of John Fairly of that ilk his heirs and assignees of his lands called Bowhous of old extent lying in the lordship of Stane i
2 CONC n special warrandice to relieve John his heirs executors and assignees of the whole of his intromissions with the rents and duties of 20 merks of old extent of the lands of Dreghorn in whatever way intromitted with by John of the 
2 CONC years 1547 and 1558 and interevening years at the hands of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Hugh Montgomery of Auchinhood and any others whomsoever having interest; tohold in special warrandice of him and his heirs in blench for payment ye
2 CONC arly of a penny Scots on the ground of the said lands in name of blench farm if asked only. Dated at the burgh of Irvine. [Charter granted in obedience to a decree arbitral by Hugh Montgomery of Stane in favour of John Fairly of t
2 CONC hat ilk his heirs and assignees of his lands called Bowhous of old extent lying in the lordship of Stane in special warrandice to relieve John his heirs executors and assignees of the whole of his intromissions with the rents and 
2 CONC duties of 20 merks of old extent of the lands of Dreghorn in whatever way intromitted with by John of the years 1547 and 1558 and interevening years at the hands of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Hugh Montgomery of Auchinhood and any oth
2 CONC ers whomsoever having interest; tohold in special warrandice of him and his heirs in blench for payment yearly of a penny Scots on the ground of the said lands in name of blench farm if asked only. Dated at the burgh of Irvine. [h
2 CONC ttps://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f15%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=auchinhood&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Ear
