2 CONT '''1570: Charter granted by Hugh Montgomery of Stane and Margaret Montgomery, his spouse with consent of Laurence Lyn of Bourtrehill in favour of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Lord Montgomery and Dame Agnes Drummond, his spouse and the 
2 CONC longest liver of them two in conjunct infeftment, their heirs and assignees of the superiority of the said lands: to hold of the King as Prince and Stewart of Scotland for payment yearly of a penny Scots at the feast of Whitsunday
2 CONC  on the ground of the said lands in name of blench farm if asked only. Witnesses: Robert Ker of Kersland, Hugh Montgomery of Auchinhood, [ ], Hugh Montgomery of Stane, Peter Montgomery, Robert Craufurd, Alexander Michell and James
2 CONC  McIntairis. Signed by Margaret Montgomery in her own hand, notary Robert Craufurd. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f67%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=auchinhood&ko=p&r=&
