2 CONT '''3 September 1589: Transference by Hew Montgomery, younger of Auchinhuid having the full right of the ward, relief and non entry of the foresaid lands of Lochliboside (disponed to him and unquhile Dorothy Sempill his deceased sp
2 CONC ouse and to the longest liver of them two by Robert, Master of Eglinton, assignee of Sir John Maitland of Thirlestane, secretary to the King and Master Thomas Lyoun of Balduky, Master of Glamis, the King's treasurer equal and prin
2 CONC cipal donators to the King of the ward of all lands which pertained of before to the deceased Hew, Earl of Eglinton, holden by him of the King for services of ward and relief of which the said lands of Lochliboside are part) in fa
2 CONC vour of Robert Montgomery of Skelmorlie his heirs and assignees one or more of the ward of the foresaid lands since the death of the unquhile Earl until the lawful entry of the righteous heir or heirs thereto being of lawful and p
2 CONC erfect age with the relief thereof when it should happen. Dated at the burgh of Irvine. Witnesses: John Montgomery of Brigend and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f7%2
