2 CONT '''9 June 1622: Contract of marriage between Hugh Montgomery, younger of Auchinhood with consent of Hugh Montgomery, elder of Auchinhood, his father on the one part and Marion Montgomery, lawful daughter of unquhile Neill Montgome
2 CONC ry of Langschaw with consent of Marion Mure, her mother and spouse to unquhile Neill and Neill Montgomery then of Langschaw (Lainshaw) her brother whereby in contemplation of the marriage to be solemnised between Hew Montgomery, y
2 CONC ounger and Marion Montgomery, Hew Montgomery, elder binds himself to infeft Marion Montgomery, future spouse to his said son in liferent during all the days of her lifetime in the just and equal half of the lands of Auchinhud, the
2 CONC  just and equal half of the 16s 8d land of Park and the just and equal half of the 20s 4d land of old extent of Bordland both lying in the parish of Eaglesham and sheriffdom of Renfrew and to infeft Hew Montgomery, younger and the
2 CONC  heirs male lawfully to be proceate between him and his future spouse, which failing the said Hew Montgomery, younger his heirs male and assignees whomsoever heritably in the haill lands of Auchinhood, Park and Bordland, reserving
2 CONC  always to Hew Montgomery, elder and Janet Peebles, his spouse their liferent of the said half of the said lands which was not provided to the said Marion Montgomery. Dated at Irvine.  [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlin
2 CONC ecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f45%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=auchinhood&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/10/45/2]'''
