1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR JOHN MURE OF CALDWELL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/selectionsfromfa01mait/page/9/mode/1up Selections from the Family Papers Preserved at Caldwell, Part First, pp. 9-11]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 May 1529: Dispensation by Gilbert Strathauchin canon of Aberdeen and Moray, by authority of Laurence cardinal-bishop of Praenests, to John Mure of Caldwell and Jonet Stewart of Culzane [sc. relict of Sir John Kennedy of Culz
2 CONC ean] for their marriage, they being within the forbidden degrees. Procurators for the parties, James Montgummery of Brigend and Thomas Corry of Kelwod. Witnesses: Mr Patrick Arbuthnay, sir David Fergushill, Sir Robert Hammiltoune,
2 CONC  chaplains, David Bonar, Christopher Seytoune, Mr James Kennedy vicar of Monyboll, and James Kennedy. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+stewart&
2 CONC ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Family of Bennan and Finnarts, reference GD60/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 25 January 1535 James V, King of Scots, confirmed possession of the ten merk land of old extent to John Mure of Caldwell and his wife Jonete Stewart. John Mure of Caldwell had previously resigned this land to the King in ord
2 CONC er to obtain a new grant in favour of himself and his wife. The land in question was to be held in conjuct fee and liferent by John and Jonete, and thereafter by their male heirs. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03sco
2 CONC t/page/319/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 1443]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 June 1536: Precept of Sasine by John Kennedy of Bardrochit in favour of John Mure of Cauldwel and Jonet Stewart, his spouse, of the 20s. land of Clauchryebayne, in the bailiary of Carrik and sheriffdom of Ayr. [http://catalog
2 CONC ue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD27%2f1%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Kennedy of Dalquharran, reference GD27/1/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 April 1537: Instrument of sasine on a precept from John Kennedy of Culzane dated at Culzane 7 March last, to John Mure of Cawldwell and Jonet Stewart his wife conjunctly of the 40s land of Changand and Laggand in the barony 
2 CONC of Glenstynchel and bailiary of Carryk occupied by the said John and Jonet. Witnesses: Thomas McClenen and Gilbert McCumstine. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&t
2 CONC n=n&tp=n&k=jonet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Family of Bennan and Finnarts, reference GD60/6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 October 1537: Charter by John Kennydy of Culzane to John Mwre of Cauldwell and Jonet Stewart his wife conjunctly of the 20s land of Auchyndunnann, inhabited by John Wallace in the bailiary of Kilsteuart, and the 12s 6d land 
2 CONC of Goldryng, inhabited by Robert Geddy, in the lordship of Goldring, and same bailiary, in consideration of a sum of money paid to him by the said John and Jonet in his urgent need; reddendo 1d yearly for each of the two lands to 
2 CONC be held in blench farm; with clause of warrandice. t Dalquharran. Witnesses: James Hannay, James Park, and sir David Fergusson, chaplain. Signed "Jhon Kenyde of Culzane wyt my hand". [Seal gone.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.u
2 CONC k/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Family of Bennan and Finnarts, reference GD60/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot., and John Maitl
2 CONC and Thomson, MA., Advocates. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1883), 1067 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/selectionsfromfa01mait/page/n8/mode/1up Selections from the Family Papers Preserved at Caldwell MCCCCXCVI - MDCCCLII.  Part First. (Glasgow, MDCCCLIV), 317 pp.]'''
