2 DATE BEF 12 MAY 1552
1 TITL Dame
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAME JONET STEWART ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Janet Stewart, here treated, the Lady of Culzean, may be the daughter of Matthew Stewart, Earl of Lennox. The name of her mother has not been identified. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/mm4fz/mure02.php Stirnet
2 CONC : Mure 02]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Dame Jonet Stewart, here treated, who died before 12 May 1552, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Stewart-Lady-Ross-of-Halkhead/6000000078406505695, who probably died before 9 December 1523.
2 CONC '''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Jonet Stewart, here treated, died before 12 May 1552. [NRS: CC9/7/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation is thought to have been granted on 12 May 1552 [date of entry on p. 160 used]. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Jonet Stewart, lady of Culzane, referen
2 CONC ce CC9/7/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000198970418836 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Jonet Stewart, here treated, married Sir John Kennedy of Culzean.  She is noticed as his widow on 20 May 1529. On 20 May 1529 they had a dispensation to marry. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details
2 CONC .aspx?reference=GD60%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y NRS: GD60/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Jonet Stewart. here treated, married Sir John Mure of Caldwell. On 20 May 1529 they had a dispensation to marry. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp
2 CONC =n&k=jonet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y NRS: GD60/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Third Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Jonet Stewart, here treated, married Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn. She and her husband had a tack for the teinds of the church of Dalgarnock on 25 June 1546. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/detail
2 CONC s.aspx?reference=GD19%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=roger+kirkpatrick&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1590&di=n NRS: GD19/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Book of Gavin Ros ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[14] May 1529: Instrument narrating that John Mur of Cald(well) obliged himself and his heirs to fulfil all things specified in a contract of marriage between him and Dame Jonet Stewart, lady of Culzeane, and also in letters of
2 CONC  obligation made to Dame Jonet, Egidia Kennedy and Jonet K., daughters of Dame Jonet ; moreover, he obliges himself to reform and better the said contract and obligation in any point or points if it seem expedient to Dame Jonet, b
2 CONC y the advice of lawyers. Done at Dalquhorran . . . May 1529. Witnesses, Archibald Stewart and Alexander Ross. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso10scotuoft/page/178/mode/1up Protocol Book of Gavin Ross 1412-32: Protocol 
2 CONC number 990]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''!4 May 1529: Instrument narrating that Hugh, Earl of Eglintoun, superior of the lands of Thorntoun, affirmed and approved these grants,"for the natural affection he has towards her," contained in a charter of liferent of the te
2 CONC n-merk lands of Thorntoun made by the said Earl to Dame Jonet Stewart, relict of the late John Kennedy of Culzean, Knight, notwithstanding an erasure of the same in the eighth line of said charter from the head expressly contained
2 CONC , which words were erased in presence of the Earl, and John Mur of Caldwell likewise approved the same words and the erasure of the same. Done at Eglintoun 14 May 1529. Witnesses, Robert Mungumbri of . . . William Symonton and Sir
2 CONC  George Baxter. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso10scotuoft/page/179/mode/1up Protocol Book of Gavin Ross 1412-32: Protocol number 991]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 May 1529: Instrument to the effect that Archibald (Stewart), attorney for said Jonet, obliges himself on her behalf, if any reason shall be found between her and John Mure of Caldwell for any cause now not manifest, to obtai
2 CONC n a lawful dispensation from the Apostolic See at the cost of said Dame Jonet, or at least to again resign the ten-merk lands of Thorntoun, which she has in liferent, in the hands of the superior in favour of the said John M. of C
2 CONC aldwell. Same date and witnesses as preceding, [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso10scotuoft/page/179/mode/1up Protocol Book of Gavin Ross 1412-32: Protocol number 992]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 May 1529: On the same day John Mur of Caldwell resigned the ten-merk lands of Thorntoun, lying in the bailiary of Cunygham, in the hands of Hugh, Earl of Eglintoun, overlord of the same, in favour of Dame Jonet Stewart, lady
2 CONC  of Culzean ; which resignation made, the Earl regave the lands to Archibald Stewart, attorney of Dame Jonet, in terms of her charter. 14 May 1529. Same witnesses as preceding. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso10scotuo
2 CONC ft/page/179/mode/1up Protocol Book of Gavin Ross 1412-32: Protocol number 993]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[14] May 1529: Instrument narrating that Alexander Knox, bailie of Hugh, Earl of Eglintoun, in terms of a precept by the Earl, passed to the lands of Thorntoun, and there gave sasine and possession of the (10) merk lands of Tho
2 CONC rntoun, with mansion and orchard in the bailiary of Cunigham, sheriffdom of Air, to Archibald Stewart, attorney of Dame Jonet Stewart, relict of the late John Kennedy of Culzean, Knight, in liferent, according to her charter, by d
2 CONC elivery of thatch and beam ("tecti et tigni ") gave and delivered to Dame Jonet for her lifetime. Done on the ground of the lands . . . May 1529. Witnesses, John Kennedy of Culzean, John Mur of Caldwall, Constantine Caldwall, Alex
2 CONC ander Ross and Thomas Caldwall, [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso10scotuoft/page/179/mode/1up Protocol Book of Gavin Ross 1412-32: Protocol number 994]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 May 1529: Dispensation by Gilbert Strathauchin canon of Aberdeen and Moray, by authority of Laurence cardinal-bishop of Praenests, to John Mure of Caldwell and Jonet Stewart of Culzane [sc. relict of Sir John Kennedy of Culz
2 CONC ean] for their marriage, they being within the forbidden degrees. Procurators for the parties, James Montgummery of Brigend and Thomas Corry of Kelwod. Witnesses: Mr Patrick Arbuthnay, sir David Fergushill, Sir Robert Hammiltoune,
2 CONC  chaplains, David Bonar, Christopher Seytoune, Mr James Kennedy vicar of Monyboll, and James Kennedy. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+stewart&
2 CONC ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Family of Bennan and Finnarts, reference GD60/4]'''
