2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 October 1537: Charter by John Kennydy of Culzane to John Mwre of Cauldwell and Jonet Stewart his wife conjunctly of the 20s land of Auchyndunnann, inhabited by John Wallace in the bailiary of Kilsteuart, and the 12s 6d land 
2 CONC of Goldryng, inhabited by Robert Geddy, in the lordship of Goldring, and same bailiary, in consideration of a sum of money paid to him by the said John and Jonet in his urgent need; reddendo 1d yearly for each of the two lands to 
2 CONC be held in blench farm; with clause of warrandice. At Dalquharran. Witnesses: James Hannay, James Park, and sir David Fergusson, chaplain. Signed "Jhon Kenyde of Culzane wyt my hand". [Seal gone.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.
2 CONC uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Family of Bennan and Finnarts, reference GD60/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 June 1546: Tack by Robert, commendator of Holyrood, Alexander, abbot of Cambuskenneth (Cambuskynneth), his co-adjutor and administrator thereof, and the convent thereof to Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, LADY JANET STEWART,
2 CONC  LADY CALDWELL (Cauldwell), HIS SPOUSE, Roger Kirkpatrick, his son and heir apparent, and James and John Kirkpatrick, also his sons of the teinds etc of the church of Dalgarnock. [Tag; signatures of convent.] [http://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD19%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=roger+kirkpatrick&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1590&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, Dumfr
2 CONC ies-shire, reference GD19/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 May 1592: Renunciation by Hugh Kennedy now of Girvanmains to Thomas Kennedy son and apparent heir of Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culean Knight, by which for certain sums of money paid to him the said Hugh Kennedy by Mr David Makgi
2 CONC ll of Cranston-riddel Advocate to our Sovereign Lord, in behalf of the said Thomas Kennedy his oy (grandson) he renounces, quit-claims and overgives to the said Thomas Kennedy his heirs and assignees, all right title and interest 
2 CONC which he said Hugh Kennedy had to the 20 pound land of Culean, with the manor place woods and fishings thereof, and ratifies and approves the Charter of the same (No. preceding) granted by Margaret Kennedy his mother relict of Gil
2 CONC bert Kennedy of Girvanmains his father to the said Thomas Kennedy and his aforesaid, in the whole heads, articles, and clauses and obliges him to warrand the same both from his own and the proper facts and deeds of his said Umquhi
2 CONC l father - and whereas the merk land of Dunbog, which is part of the said 20 pound land of Culean was disponed by Elizabeth Kennedy relict of [ ] Kennedy of Culean to Umquhil Janet Stewart relict of Sir John Kennedy of Culean Knig
2 CONC ht her heirs and assignees, and that the right of the said merk land now pertains to him the said Hugh Kennedy as heir of his said Umquhil father, therefore he obliges him to warrand the said merk land of Dunbog to the said Thomas
2 CONC  Kennedy and his aforesaid, from the alienation thereof by the said Umquhil Janet Stewart. Witnesses-John Kennedy of Bogend, John Baird of Kilquhenzie, Alexander Lockhart younger of Boghall and Hugh Kennedy in Craigneil. Dated at 
2 CONC Mayboll. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f1018&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=janet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Fami
2 CONC ly, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/1018]'''
2 CONT
