2 CONT
2 CONT == Supporting evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT From “History of the County of Ayr: With a Genealogical Account of the ...,” Volume 2 By James Paterson.  Page 281. [https://books.google.com/books?id=BIXSAAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA281&dq=%22Janet%20Stewart%22%20Culzean&pg=PA281#v=onepage&q&
2 CONC f=true GoogleBooks] 
2 CONT
2 CONT >We have before us the substance of the testament of "quondam Domine Jonete Stewart, Domine de Culzeane," who died on the 24 of December 1551.  She appointed as her executors, JOHN GREIR OF LAG, Patrick Kennedy, her son, and Alexa
2 CONC nder Stewart of Garrulas.
2 CONT
2 CONT From From The Scots Peerage, Vol 4, page 152 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/152 Archive.Org]
2 CONT
2 CONT >"The eldest son, is designed of the Grenane, and son and heir apparent of Alexander Stewart of Garlies, knight, in the records of parliament, 1495. According to some accounts, he fell at the battle of Flodden, 9th September 1513 
2 CONC ; but, according to others, he predeceased his father, who was the person killed at Flodden."
2 CONT
2 CONT >"They had one son, Alexander, and sixteen daughters: '''the eldest Janet married to Sir John Kennedy of Cullean'''; the second, Christian, to Sir James Stewart of Cardonald; the third to Towers of Innerldth; the fourth to Douglas
2 CONC  of Pompherstoun; the fifth to Moutray of Seafield; the sixth to Lundy of Balgony; the seventh .to Hannay of Sorbie; the eighth to Alexander Adair of Kilhill; the ninth to Finlay Campbell of Corsiehill; the tenth to Thomas Kennedy
2 CONC  of Bargenny; the eleventh to Lockhart of Barr; the twelfth to Kennedy of Blairquhan; the thirteenth to Crichton of Naughton; the fourteenth to Johnston of Johnston; the fifteenth to Cairns of Orchardtoun; and the sixteenth, Elisa
2 CONC beth, to Thomas, son and heir apparent of Uchtred Macdowall of Garthland."
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *http://genealogy.kirkpatrickaustralian.com/archives/getperson.php?personID=I7456&tree=TKA daughter of Alexander Stewart and Christian Douglas [n.b. This is a Jean, daughter of Alexander Stewart of Garlies, born after 1576, so can
2 CONC not have been this Jonet.  Ref: [https://archive.org/details/historylandsand01mackgoog/page/n306 Archive.Org] 
2 CONT * http://genealogy.kirkpatrickaustralian.com/archives/getperson.php?personID=I6794&tree=TKA
2 CONT *”History of the Lands and Their Owners in Galloway. With Historical Sketches of the District ...” Author Peter Handyside MacKerlie.  Page 284 [https://archive.org/details/historylandsand01mackgoog/page/n304 Archive.Org] Jonet, pe
2 CONC rhaps the daughter of Alexander Stewart of Greenan (d 1513 at Flodden) & Elizabeth Blairquhan; sister of Alexander Stewart of Garlies.
2 CONT * seen as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stewart/6000000064408263249?through=6000000003275349031 & https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Douglas/6000000064409262876?through=6000000003275349031
2 CONT * seen as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stuart-1th-Earl-of-Lennox/6000000002991797769?through=6000000043048859990
