2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''January 1549: Extract from the Book of the Consistorial Court of Glasgow of disposition by William Muir of Glanderstone, brother german to John Muir of Caldwell, in favour of Patrick Montgomery and Agnes Mure, his spouse and th
2 CONC e longest liver of them two and the heirs gotten of their own bodies whatsoever of the twa part of the property of the lands and lordship of Giffyn with all profits belonging to him as assignee of unquhile John Montgomery, son and
2 CONC  heir of unquhile Sir Neil Montgomery of Langschaw, knight who had the gift thereof from the Queen and the Lord Governor for the space of 5 years after the 9th day of November then last past; which was the entry of the said Patric
2 CONC k and Agnes his spouse, to the said lands and profits of the same; reserving to Margaret Frissell, Lady of Giffen her reasonable terce and conjunct fee of the said lands Dated at Glasgow and registered 27 March 1549 [http://catalo
2 CONC gue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f30%2f20&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=giffen&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1560&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Egl
2 CONC inton, reference GD3/1/1/30/20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 January 1589: Charter by which Patrick Sempill of Craigbait confirms (in completion of a marriage contract between his mother Margaret Lindsay and Agnes Mure, widiow of Patrick Montgomery of Giffen, and their daughter Grissi
2 CONC l Montgomery, and Agnes Mure's husband Hugh Montgomery of Hessilhead for his interest) that he has given his twenty shilling lands of Craigbait in liferent to Grissil Montgomery, his future spouse    [https://archive.org/stream/re
2 CONC gistrummagnisi05scot#page/618/mode/1up Registrum Magnii Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-1593, charter number 1822 on pp. 618-19]'''
