1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM MURE OF GLANDERSTON===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This laird of Glanderstone left two sons — William his successor, and James of Ballybregach in the county of Down, who was a captain in his uncle Clanboyes' regiment of horse in 1642. He also left six daughters, all of whom wer
2 CONC e married: Janet was the wife of the Rev. John Carstairs;....Ursula, married to William Ralston of that ilk ; Jean, to John Hamilton of Hallcraigs, nephew of Lord Clanboyes, and her first cousin ; Margaret, who married, first, the
2 CONC  Rev. Zachariah Boyd, minister of the barony of Glasgow,... secondly, the Rev. James Durham, a little less celebrated minister of the same church ; Agnes married William Porterfield of Quarrelton ; Elizabeth married the Rev. Alex.
2 CONC  Dunlop, her son by whom was William Dunlop, principal of the university of Glasgow... [https://archive.org/details/selectionsfromf01muregoog/page/n67/mode/1up Family Papers I: pp. 25-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22  August 1646: WILLIELMUS MURE de Glanderstoun, haeres Willelmi Mure de Glanderstoun, patris; - in 33 solidatis et 6 denariatis terrarum de Dumgraine in baronia et regalitate de Pasleto. E. 40s. 6d.etc. feudiferme. xviii. 320
2 CONC . [Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc., Volume II, Inquisitiones Speciales. Renfrew, inquisition number 125]'''
2 CONT
