2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 August 1559: Instrument of Sasine by Thomas Kennedy of Bargany propitis manibus to his sister Jonet Kennedy wife of John Mure of Cauldwell, in liferent and to the heirs lawfully begotton of her and the said John heritably of
2 CONC  the above subjects (10 merkland of Thornetoune). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f18&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Papers of the Family of Bennan and Finnarts, reference GD60/18]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 July 1562: Letter of reversion granted by Jonet Kennedy, spouse to John Mure of Caulduell with his consent, whereby she declares that although Hugh, Earl of Eglinton had sold to her, her heirs and assignees, an annualrent of
2 CONC  50 merks Scots furth of the barony of Robertoun, yet on the said Earl paying to her 500 merks in the parish kirk of Irvine on 40 days warning before any term of Whitsunday or Martinmas she would discharge the said annualrent. [ht
2 CONC tps://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f57%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family
2 CONC , Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/57/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 November 1566: Instrument of redemption by Robert Crawford of Clolymand, procurator for Hugh, Earl of Eglinton from Lady Janet Kennedy of Caldwell and John Muir of Caldwell, knight, her spouse, of the barony of Robertoun lyi
2 CONC ng in the bailliary of Cunningham from an annual rent of 50 merks furth thereof by payment of 500 merks. Dated 10th November 1566. Witnesses John Mure of Rowallan, James Kincaid of that ilk, Thomas Caldwell of that ilk and others.
2 CONC  John Muir, notary. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f19%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Janet+Kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers o
2 CONC f the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/10/19/3]'''
