1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR ROBERT MURE OF CALDWELL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Mure of Caldwell, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Mure-of-Caldwell/6000000010437836860?through=6000000003043297800 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Jonet-Kennedy/60000001989693308
2 CONC 67?through=6000000003043297800 [https://archive.org/details/selectionsfromfa01mait/page/14/mode/1up Caldwell, Part First, pp. 14-17]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 October 1573: Contract between Hugh, master of Eglinton, and Robert Mure of Caldwell by which former dispones to latter the nonentries etc. of lands of Thornton and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalo
2 CONC gue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f8%2f12&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+mure+of+caldwell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/2/8/12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Books of the Town Clerks of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 February 1573-74: John Arbunkle produced a charter whereby Robert Mwre of Cauldwell granted to him a 12s. 6d. land, part of the granter's 10 merk land of old extent of Kittoksyd, lying in the parish of Kilbryd and shire of La
2 CONC nerk. Charter subscribed and sealed at Glasgow, 28 January, 1573-4, in presence of Thomas Spreull of Coldoun, James Kinkaid, junior, of that Ilk, John Stewart of Neilstounsyd, Robert Blair, notary, James Robisoun, servitor to the 
2 CONC said Robert, and Archibald Hegate. Sasine given by John Wilsoun, bailie in hoc parte. Witnesses: John Wamok in Phillipsmilne, Robert Wamok, there, James Cowpar in Kittoksyd, John Aikinheid there, John Arbunkle there, John Wamok in
2 CONC  Kittoksyde, John Dwning there, William Dwning there, and John Rid there. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsprotoc08robegoog/page/n30/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols IV: protocol number 1031]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 February 1573-74: William Dwning produced a charter whereby Robert Mure of Cauldwell granted to him an 11s, 1 and one half penny land, part of the granter's 10 merk land of Kittoksyde, lying in the parish of Kilbryd and shire
2 CONC  of Lanark. Charter subscribed and sealed, and sasine given as in No. 1031. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsprotoc08robegoog/page/n30/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols IV: protocol number 1032]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 February 1573-74: James Wilsoun produced a charter whereby Robert Mwre of Caulduell granted to him the 11s. 1p. land, part of the grantor's 10 merk land of Kittoksyde, lying in the parish of Kilbryd and shire of Lanark . . . 
2 CONC . . [Note] [https://archive.org/details/abstractsprotoc08robegoog/page/n30/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols IV: protocol number 1033]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: One or more leaves— probably two, forming the centre sheet of a section— are wanting here. At the top of the next preserved page there are three lines forming the end of another protocol and containing the names of these 
2 CONC witnesses: John Ride, John Wamok, Robert Cowpar, and Bartholomew Symmer.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 June 1575: Bartholomew Summyr in Holmeberne produced a charter whereby Robert Mwre of Cauldewell granted to him the 11s. Id. land of old extent of Kittoksyide, lying in the parish of Kilbryid and shire of Lanark. Charter subs
2 CONC cribed and sealed at Cauldewell, 20 May, 1575, in presence of Thomas Sprewile of Coulden, David Mwre, King's messenger, and Robert Arthwire. Sasine given by Gavin Grahame, bailie in hoc parte. Witnesses: Walter Stewarde in Castelt
2 CONC oune, John Flemynge in Mwrray, John Reid in Kittoksyide, John Wamok there, and Robert Couper there. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsprotoc08robegoog/page/n36/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols IV: protocol number 1047]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 February 1597-98: Andrew Warnok, son of Andrew Warnok in Phippismihie, in Kittoksyde, produced a feu-charter whereby Robert Mure of Caldwell granted to him a house, with yard and pertinents, and two half acres of land, Iving
2 CONC  discontiguous, in the shire of Lanerk and parish of Kilbryde, one of which half acres lay on the west side of the water of Kittok, at the back of the dwelling-house of Robert Warnok at Philpismilne, and the other lay opposite on 
2 CONC the east side of the said water ; and also a cow's grazing on the 25 s. land of Kittoksyde, heritably belonging to John Warnok in Kittoksyde. Sasine given by John Ardbucle in Kittoksyde, as bailie in hac parte of Robert Mwre. Witn
2 CONC esses : Robert Warnok in Philpismilne, John Warnok, there, Gilbert Gray, brothcr of William Gray, citizen of Glasgow, and Patrick Ardbucle in Cors. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsofproto10glas/page/71/mode/1up Glasgow Proto
2 CONC cols X: protocol number 3192]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/abstractsprotoc08robegoog/page/n7/mode/1up Abstracts of Protocols of the Town Clerks of Glasgow. Edited by Robert Renwick, Depute Town Clerk. Vol. IV. William Hegait’s Protocols, 1568-76. With App
2 CONC endix (including Michael Fleming’s Protocols), 1530-7. (Carson & Nicol, Glasgow, MDCCCXCVII.), 152 pp. including appendix and indices]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/abstractsofproto10glas/page/n8/mode/1up Abstracts of Protocols of the Town Clerks of Glasgow. Edited by Robert Renwick, Depute Town Clerk. Vol. X.  Archibald Hegate's Protocols, 1587-1600.  John R
2 CONC os' Protocols, 1588-9. George Huchesone's Protocols, 1586-91. (Carson & Nicol, Glasgow, MDCCCC), 164 pp. including indices]'''
2 CONT
