1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == GEORGE CAMPBELL OF CESSNOCK elder ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Campbell of Cessnock. elder, here treated, is noticed on 6 October 1484, as a member of an assize which returned Thomas Kennedy as heir to his deceased father, Gilbert Kennedy of Bargany. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.go
2 CONC v.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f780&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cesnok&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=n NRS: GD109/780] He is noticed again on 25 February 1490, in the witness list of a charter made in favour of
2 CONC  William Schaw of Polkamet and his wife Margaret Campbell. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/491/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2315]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Campbell of Cessnock, elder, here treated, died before 29 April 1508, the date upon which James IV, King of Scots, exempted his son George from paying the relief due for the lands of Cessnock following the death of his f
2 CONC ather. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/246/mode/1up RSSRS 1488-1529: entry number 1663]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/George-Campbell-of-Cessnock-younger/6000000055731602900?through=6000000183415019821
