2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 October 1484: Retour in favour of Thomas Kennide as heir of Gilbert Kennide of Bargany, his father, in a 40s. land comprising one merkland of Sannass, one merkland of Assyss and one merkland of Berwanach in parish of Kyrkcubr
2 CONC y de Entertig; lands held of lord of Carnlok, under reddendo of a gift of silver plate (argenteim) at feast of St John the Baptist. Inquest: Sir George Cambell of Lowdoun, sheriff of Are, Sir Robert Colwill of Huchiltre, John Cath
2 CONC kert of Carltoun, kt., James Kennide of Rowe, Quintin Mure of Ard, George Cambell of Cesnok, John Red of Barskymmyn, William Schaw of Crage, David Barcla of Ladyland, Cuthbert Dunbar of Blantyre, Andrew Campbell of Skeringtoun, Wi
2 CONC lliam Craffurd of Beax, Roger Mure of Cloncard, Fergus Fergusson of Kilkeran, John Hoggeson of Barchare, Lambert Wallas of Scheualtone, John Kennide of Knokreoch and John Arnot of Lochrig. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrso
2 CONC nlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f780&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cesnok&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/780]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 February 1490: Charter made in favour of William Schaw of Polkamet and his wife Margaret Campbell. Witnessed by George Campbell of Cesnok, and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/491/mode/1up RMS
2 CONC  1424-1513: charter number 2315]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 Jul 1500: Instrument of Seisin propriis manibus in favor of Margaret Campbell daughter of George Campbell of Cesnock, and wife of Sir John Kennedy Knight son and apparent heir of John Kennedy of Blairquhan, in the 2 merk lan
2 CONC d of Cloywarranach and 6 merk land of Carrickalla lying in the Lordship of Galloway and County of Wigton, and in the 12 merk land of Trounan, lying in the Earldom of Carrick given by the said Sir John Kennedy. Witnesses- John Kenn
2 CONC edy in Nemone of Cree, John Maclunan, Robert Man, and Fergus Macnaught. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f171&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+campbell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1
2 CONC 520&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/171]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 April 1503: Preceptum Remissionis GEORGEI CAMPBELE, filii et heredis apparentis Georgei  Campbele de Cesnok, et quatuor aliorum, pro captione et detentione Thome Huchon junioris absque auctoritate regia, et pro omnibus aliis
2 CONC , etc.,  ….., - proditoria traditione, murthuro, incendio,homicidio, raptu mulierum, et furto exceptis. Per Signetum. xs. iii.  5. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/137/mode/1up RSSRS 1488-1529: entry num
2 CONC ber 931]’’’
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 May 1503: Preceptum  Remissionis  JOHANNIS CAMPBELE  de  Lowdoun,  et  sex [aliorum],  [pro]  captione  Johannis Bathcate  extra  domum  suam  propriam ejusdem  absque  auctoritate  et mandato  regis,  et  pro  precogitata  
2 CONC felonia [per]  ispos  facta  Georgeo  Campbele,  filio domini  de  Cesnok,  et  pro [ blank space ] que eis  ratione  omnium  et  singulorum  premis- sorum  imputari  poterit  tantum.  Per Signetum.     iii  lib.  xs.  iii.  5. [h
2 CONC ttps://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/138/mode/1up  RSSRS 1488-1529: entry number 938]’’’
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 May 1503: Preceptum  Remissionis  ARCHIBALDI LOKERT  et  Thome  Zoung,  pro  precogitata  felonia  facta  Georgeo  Campbele,  filio domini  de  Cesnok,  et  suis  complicibus,  et pro  omnibus  aliis  actionibus,  etc.,  .  
2 CONC .  .  , — proditoria  traditione,  murthuro,  inoen- dio,  homicidio,  raptu  mulierum  et  furto exceptis.     Per  Signetum.     xxs.       iii.  5. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/138/mode/1up  RSSRS
2 CONC  1488-1529: entry number 938]’’’
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 March 1504-05: REX, - quia  literas vicecomiti de Aire direxerat ad distringendum Tho. Somervale de Braxfeld pro 500 mercis Jonete Kennedy domine Boithuil persolvendis; - et  Geo. Campbele vicecomes deputatus, quia dictus Tho
2 CONC . in bonis mobilibus distringibilis non erat, terras subscriptas pro dicta summa appreciari fecit et dicte Jonete vendi; - igitur, tanquam senescallus Scotie et dominus superior, concessit dicte JONETE KENNEDY DOMINE BOITHUIL, et 
2 CONC heredibus ejus, - terras de Prestwikschawis,extendentes ad 10 libratas terrarum antiqui extentus,- exceptis theoloneo finis pontis, viz. le fholl de le Brigand de Are,  piscationibus  dictarum terrarum, et 20 solidis annui redditu
2 CONC s, - in domino de Kilestewart, vic. Aire; - et  voluit quod  dictus Tho. et heredes ejus haberent regressum quandocunque diet, summam, etc., persolverent infra septennium. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/6
2 CONC 03/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2836]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1507: Instrument of Seisin in favor of John Kennedy son of Sir John Kennedy of Blairquhan in the whole lands mentioned in the above Precept and proceeding thereon. Attorney Matthew Campbell son of George Campbell of Ce
2 CONC ssnock. Witnesses - James and Gilbert Kennedies, William Mure and James Boyd. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f208&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=campbell+of+cessnock&ko=p&r=&ro
2 CONC =s&df=&dt=1520&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/208]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 December 1507: Charter made in favour of Thome Fentoun of Ogill. Witnessed by John Campbell, son of George Campbell of Cesnok, and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/675/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: c
2 CONC harter number 3158]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 April 1508: A  Lettre made to GEORGE CAMPBELL of Sexnok [Cesnok], dischargeand  him of the hale releyf of his landis of Sexnok with thair pertinentis, quhilkis perteniisss to the King be the deces  of his fader, that he may 
2 CONC intromett thairwith, and dispone thairapoun as he thinkis maste eicpedient, — dischargeing al schireffis and balzeis of thair officis in that parte Per Signaturam manu Regis subscriptam. xs. solut. per aquittantiam in mense Novemb
2 CONC ris proximo sequentis.  iii.  176.[https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/246/mode/1up RSSRS 1488-1529: entry number 1663]'''
2 CONT
