1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JANET CAMPBELL Lady of Cessnock ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 10 April 1551. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Jonet Campbell, lady of Cessnock, spouse of Edward Creichtoune, reference CC9/7/1]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 February 1533: Charter by which James V, King of Scots, confirms possession of the forty shilling land of old extent of Gallisholmis, in the Bailliery of Kyle-Stewart and sheriffdom of Ayr, to John Campbell of Cessnock and h
2 CONC is wife Jonet Campbell. Cessnock had previously resigned this land in order to obtain a new grant in favour of himself and his wife. They were to hold this land in conjunct fee and liferent.[https://archive.org/details/registrumma
2 CONC gnisi03scot/page/297/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 1350]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/cc4aq/campbell26.php Stirnet: Campbell 26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Unattributed Pedigree ==
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN LOCKHART OF BAR (as above), b. 1510 - d. 1575; in 1531 was granted Bar, Stewart Gallishomes; in 1568 was at the horn for destroying church images in the church of Ayr; in 1570, was at the election of Matthew Stewart as regent
2 CONC ; was a supporter of John Knox; it is after his death, that the Castle of Galston becomes associated with the Lockharts of Bar;
2 CONT
2 CONT married JANET CAMPBELL, Lady Cessnock, about 1535; she was the widow of (1) George Ross of Hanyng, and (2) John Campbell of Cessnock.....She and her 3rd husband had ward of the Campbell lands, and it must have been through Janet C
2 CONC ampbell (Ross) (Campbell) Lockhart that the family of Lockhart became associated with Galston Tower. Robert Ross after the turn of the century, sued her descendants -- evidently for the Ross share of their inheritance of her holdi
2 CONC ngs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. John Lockhart of Bar, b. ca. 1535 - d. April 16, 1614; married (1) by 1549 Alison Muir who had died by 1586. Married (2) Janet Gordan, relict of John Mure of Auchindrane. Married (3) Agnes Cunningham. ---CHILDREN: (1) a son nam
2 CONC ed Andrew Lockhart who about 1590 entered the Church; (2) a daughter Janet who had married John Cunningham by 1624......With no male heirs, he made grants of some of his lands to his brother George Lockhart of Ayr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. George Lockhart of Ayr, b. by 1540 -d. after 1626; married (1) Marion Hamilton who has a will dated 1592; married (2) Marion Campbell who died after 1614 and before 1625; was buried at Ayr. His daughter Margaret Lockhart marrie
2 CONC d Alexander Lockhart, burgess of Ayr, and their line continued as the Lords of Bar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Moses Lockhart, who in 1602 was "brother of the Lord of Bar". 
