2 CONT '''12 November 1490: Confirmation by James IV, King of Scots, made in favour of Paisley Abbey, following upon an action raised against Sir John the Ross of Hawkhead by George, Abbot of Paisley, for: "the wrangwis detentioun and wi
2 CONC thholding fra the sadis abbot and convent of xj chalder of mele and iiij bollis, price of the boll x s. aucht to thame of ane yerelie annuell of the landis of Ingliston".  [https://archive.org/details/registrummonaste00mait/page/6
2 CONC 0 Registrum: 60-1]'''
