2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Murray,_John_(d.1510)_(DNB00)_ “ Murray, John (d.1510)“]  Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900, Volume 39. by Thomas Finlayson Henderson.
2 CONT
2 CONT MURRAY, JOHN (d. 1510), laird of Falahill, the so-called 'out law' of the old border ballad, was the son of Patrick Murray, sixth of Falahill. ... Murray was slain in 1510 by Andrew Ker of Gateschaw and Thomas Scott, brother of Ph
2 CONC ilip Scott of Aidschaw. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Janet Forrester (Exchequer Rolls, x.732, 757), widow of Schaw of Knockhill (ib. p. 727), he had, besides other children, four sons; 
2 CONT *John, who succeeded him; 
2 CONT *James, who succeeded John; 
2 CONT *William, ancestor of the Murrays of Romano; and 
2 CONT *Patrick, who became laird of Broadmeadows. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It was his son John—not he, as usually stated–who was married to Lady Margaret Hepburn, daughter of the first Earl of Bothwell.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/mm4fz/murray07.php Stirnet Murray7]
2 CONT
2 CONT (A)	John Murray of Falahill 'the Outlaw' m. Janet Forrester
2 CONT *(i)	James Murray of Falahill (d c1529) 	m. '''Margaret Home'''
2 CONT **(a)	Patrick Murray of Falahill (d 1580) 	m1. Margaret Fleming (possibly dau of John Fleming, 2nd Lord) 	m2. _ Borthwick 	m3. Elizabeth (dau of Andrew Scloter, widow of Mr. Ormiston)
2 CONT *(ii)	William Murray
2 CONT *(iii)	Elizabeth Murray	m. (1537) Sir James Douglas, 5th of Cavers (d 28.09.1545)
2 CONT
