1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''James Schaw of Sauchie''' was in the late 1400's commander of the garrison of Stirling Castle during a difficult time in Scotland's history. He was Knighted for his services by the Scottish king.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT James Schaw was born  in Sauchie, Clackmannshire, Scotland, and died JAN 1528.  He was the son of John Shaw of Alveth and heir to his grandfather, James Schaw of Sauchie (d 1491).  Of age in 1502. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT
2 CONT # ? Christian Bruce, daughter of Sir David Bruce and Marion Herries
2 CONT
2 CONT #Alison Home, daughter of Patrick Home and Margaret St. Clair. She was born in Polwarth, Berwickshire, Scotland, and was living in 1526.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Schaw are:
2 CONT *Alexander Schaw of Sauchie was born in Sauchie, Clackmannshire, Scotland, and died BEF JUL 1549.  Married 2) Elizabeth Cunningham of Glengarnock
2 CONT * John Schaw of Broich  was born in Sauchie, Clackmannshire, Scotland, and died ?  .  
2 CONT * Elizabeth Schaw, died 1559.  Mistress of James V.  Married Robert Gib of Carribber.
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gordon A. MacGregor writes: "SIR JAMES SCHAW OF SAUCHIE, succeeded his father and had a charter from James, Lord Haliburton, for the lands of Auchengownie, in the barony of Forgandenny, on 2 February, 1502. He m. Alison, daughter 
2 CONC of Sir Patrick Home of Polwarth, with whom he had a charter under the Great Seal for the lands of Greenock-Schaw on 4 December, 1506, and d. in January of 1528. He was father of 
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Alexander Schaw of Sauchie who had a charter under the Great Seal for the lands of Westerton of Tillicoultry on 8 May, 1513, and succeeded his father in the lands of Sauchie. He m. Elizabeth, daughter of William Cunningham of 
2 CONC Glengarnock, with whom he had a charter of confirmation under the Great Seal for the lands of Wester Greenock-schaw on 14 January, 1540. He d. by July of 1549. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *2. John Schaw, witness to an instrument of Sasine for the lands of Greenock-schaw in favour of his brother Alexander Schaw of Sauchie, on 21 February, 1540."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir James Schaw, grandson of the aforementioned James Schaw, whilst Keeper of Stirling Castle, denied James III access to his son the Duke of Rothesay and was later implicated in the conspiracy which ultimately led to the kings d
2 CONC emise at Sauchieburn. James was pardoned by James IV and reinstated as Keeper of Stirling Castle."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Alexander Shaw of Sauchie gave the Lands of Greenock in Patrimony to John Shaw, his eldest son, by his 2nd wife, Elizabeth, daughter of William Cunningham of Glengarnock."
2 CONT ——-
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Schaw
2 CONT
2 CONT William Schaw was the second son of John Schaw of Broich, and grandson of Sir James Schaw of Sauchie.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://groups.google.com/forum/m/#!topic/soc.genealogy.medieval/QDDWQCx8iio
2 CONT
2 CONT >Can someone point me toward good sources of information about SirJames Shaw of Sauchie, father of Janet Shaw who married Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath in about 1479? He appears to have been Governor of Stirling Castle, ro
2 CONC yal guardian, and Ambassador to England during the 1470s.  I'm guessing he was born say about 1430.  And, he may have married Christian Bruce of Clackmannan.  ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT
2 CONT * The Scots peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom.  Paul, James Balfour, Sir, 1846-1931.  “Hume, Earl of Marc
2 CONC hmont.” Page 4.  [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/4/mode/1up Archive.Org] Alison Home married to Sir James Shaw of Sauchie. 
2 CONT
