2 CONT * “Old Greenock from the Earliest Times to the Early Part of the Nineteenth ...“  By George Williamson.  Page 275.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=wA3mAAAAMAAJ&dq=christian%20bruce%20james%20schaw&pg=PA275#v=onepage&q=christia
2 CONC n%20bruce%20james%20schaw&f=false GoogleBooks] Greenock was not the original family estate. The original family were the Shaws of Sauchie, and they acquired the Barony of Wester Greenock in the reign of Robert III., by intermarria
2 CONC ge with the daughter and heiress of Galbraith of Greenock.” After referring to Craufurd's “ History of Renfrewshire,” and Douglas's “Baronage,” in corroboration of the foregoing statements, the pedigree proceeds—“By Charter dated 
2 CONC 4th December, 1506, James IV. grants to Sir James Shaw of Sauchie and Alison Hume, his spouse, the lands of Greenock-Shaw, &c. Sir James seems to have married, second, Christian, daughter of Sir David Bruce of Clackmannan the ance
2 CONC stor of the Earls of Elgin, and descended from an uncle of King Robert the Bruce. Alexander Schaw, designed son and heir of Sir James Schaw of Sauchy . . on 14th January 1539 obtained a charter to himself and Elizabeth Cunninghame
2 CONC , his spouse, of the lands of Wester Greenock-Shaw and others. This lady was his second wife, and daughter of William Cunninghame of Glengarnock. .... For further information regarding the Schaws of Sauchie and Greenock we refer t
2 CONC o “Genealogical notes anent some ancient Scottish Families, with index by David Marshall, F.S.A. Scot., Lochleven Place, Kinross; introduction and annotations by John Brown Brown-Morrison of Finderlie, F.R.S.E., F.S.A. Scot., priv
2 CONC ately printed at Perth in 1884," a work of deep interest and great research.
2 CONT * “Genealogical notes anent some ancient Scottish families, with index.” By David Marshall.  “Schaw of Sauchie.”  Page 106 [https://archive.org/details/anent1884/page/106/mode/1up Archive.Org] James Shaw, heir of deceased James Sh
2 CONC aw of Sauchy, his grand father (died 1491), probably by John Shaw of Alva, his son.  Spouse of Alison Hume in 1506.  Alexander Shaw, their son in 1508. ... Elison Hume his spouse in 1526 ...
2 CONT *[http://redbookofscotland.co.uk/bruce-of-clackmannan Red Book of Scotland] 4. Christina Bruce married Sir James Schaw of Sauchie, and had issue.  
2 CONT * “ The Origins of Freemasonry: Scotland's Century, 1590-1710.”  By David Stevenson.  Page 27.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=6WzkgXaSSeIC&lpg=PA27&dq=james%20schaw%20of%20sauchie&pg=PA27#v=onepage&q=james%20schaw%20of%20sauc
2 CONC hie&f=false GoogleBooks] John Schaw of Broich, father of James Schaw, master of works, was the younger son of James Schaw of Sauchie, died 1528.
2 CONT * [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4as/shaw01.php#top Stirnet: Shaw 01] Does not list Christian Bruce.
