1 NAME Sir Patrick Home of Polwarth, Kt.
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1434
2 ADDR
3 CITY Wedderburn
3 STAE Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE NOV 1503
2 ADDR
3 CITY Polwarth
3 STAE Scotland
1 OCCU Laird of Polwarth, Baron Sir of Home-Polworth, Sir Baron
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Patrick Home was born ABT 1434 in Wedderburn, Berwickshire, Scotland, and died NOV 1503 in Polwarth, Berwickshire, Scotland. He was the son of 2. David Home and 3. Elizabeth Carmichael. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret St. Clair, daughter of John St. Clair and Katherine Home. She was born ABT 1440 in Polwarth, Berwickshire, Scotland, and died ? 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Helen Schaw, daughter of James Schaw and Isabel Unknown. She was born ABT 1450 in Sauchie, Clackmannshire, Scotland, and died AFT 1541.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Patrick</strong>, known familiarly as <em>Lang Patrick of Pollart</em>, married, first, Margaret, younger daughter and co-heiress with her sister Marion of John Sinclair of Herdmanston, in the lands of Polwarth and Kimmer
2 CONC ghame...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He held also the following appointments, viz.:
2 CONT * Chamberlain of Stirling and Strathern, 1489
2 CONT * Comptroller, 1499
2 CONT * Chamberlain of Fife and Kilmarnock, 1501
2 CONT * Keeper of Stirling Castle, 1494 and 1501
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He died in November 1503.  He married, first, as above stated, Margaret Sinclair; and secondly, previous to 24 March 1490, Ellen, daughter of Sir James Shaw of Sauchie, <em>lady of Dirletoun</em>, widow of Archibald Halyburton,
2 CONC  Master of Halyburton.  She survived him, and was married, thirldy, to Sir Patrick Houston of that Ilk, and fourthly, in 1516, to Sir Robert Hamilton of Fingalton, and was still alive in 1541."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/2/mode/2up The Scots Peerage], Vol. VI, pages 2-3
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ancestor of the Barons Polwarth and the extinct Earls of Marchmont (see POLWARTH, B.)"
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, pg. 1256.
