1 NAME Robert /Hamilton of Preston/
2 GIVN Robert
2 SURN Hamilton of Preston
2 _MARNM Hamilton of Preston
1 SEX M
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===SIR ROBERT HAMILTON OF PRESTON===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Hamilton of Preston is the eldest son of Sir Robert Hamilton of Fingalton. [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/345/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs: 345]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Hamilton of Fingalton and Preston married 1st Margaret, daughter of Sir John Mowat of Stonehouse; married 2nd Marion, daughter of Sir David Crighton of Cranstonriddell; married 3rd 1516 Helen, daughter of Sir James S
2 CONC chaw of Sauchy. [Burke's Peerage]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 Octobert 1470: Charterby which David, Earl of Crawfurdie confirms that he has given the lands of the Mains of Kinblathment, in the barony of Kinblathment and sheriffdom of Forfar, to William Guthrie. The principal witnesses a
2 CONC re James, Lord Hamilton, and Sir Robert Hamilton of Preston, knight: "D. Rob. Hammyltoun de Prestoun, milite." [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/769/mode/1up Registrum Magnii Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Regis
2 CONC ter of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 3575 on p. 769]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 May 1515: Charter by which James V, king of Scots, confirms possession of the lands of Clowburn and Mylhill to Hugh Muir and his heirs. The lands of Clowburn are said to be held by Master John lindsay of Colbyntoun, and one 
2 CONC bovate of land there is said to be held by Margaret Weir, relict of the deceased John Hamilton, brother german of Sir Robert Hamilton of Preston: "Margareta Weir relicta quondam Johannis Hammiltoun fratris germani Roberti H. de Pr
2 CONC estoun, militis." [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/16/mode/1up Registrum Magnii Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 75 on p. 16]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/339/mode/1up Historical and Genealogical Memoirs of the House of Hamilton, pp. 339-63 for Hamilton of Preston]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Pedigree 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/hamilton/hamilton14.html
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sir John Hamilton of Fingalton, *ca 1337, +ca 1402; m.N Keith, dau.of Sir William Keith of Galston; They had issue:
2 CONT ** A1. Sir John Hamilton of the Ross; 1m: Jane Lyddell, dau.of Sir James Lyddell of Preston; 2m: Anna Seton, dau.of Sir William Seton
2 CONT *** B1. Sir James Hamilton of Fingalton and Preston; m.Agnes Hamilton, dau.of Sir James Hamilton, 5th of Cadzow
2 CONT **** C1. Sir Robert Hamilton of Fingalton and Preston, +ca 1488; m.Margaret Johnstone, dau.of Sir John Johnstone of Johnstone
2 CONT ***** D1. Sir Robert Hamilton of Fingalton and Preston, +by 1522; all or at least most of Robert's children were by his first marriage but one or two might have been by his second marriage; 1m: Margaret Mowat, dau.of Sir John Mowa
2 CONC t of Stonehouse; 2m: Marion Crichton, dau.of Sir David Crichton of Cranstonriddell; 3m: 1516 Helen Schaw, dau.of Sir James Schaw of Sauchie
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
