1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM EDMONSTONE===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Lord Edmonstone of Culloden===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Edmonstone, Lord Edmonstone of Culloden, here treated, is the son and heir of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Archibald-Edmonstone/6000000008010804618?through=6000000019640840942 [https://archive.org/details/genealo
2 CONC gicalacco00inedmo/page/28/mode/1up Duntreath: 28]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath died in or before 1460, the year upon which he was succeeded by his son by Princess Mary Stewart, Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath. [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#pag
2 CONC e/32/mode/1up Genealogical Account of the Family of Edmonstone of Duntreath, p. 32]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Cited by Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 November 1421: Resignation by John de Annandia of the lands of Myles, "reverendo et superiori domino suo Johanni domino Settoni. Witnesses:  Archibaldo de Edmistone, milite, et Willielmo, filio suo et heredi ; Willielmo de A
2 CONC nnandia consanguineo meo, Johanni et Hugoni de Lindesay, armigeris." [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/28/mode/1up Genealogical Account of the Family of Edmonstone of Duntreath. By Sir Archibald Edmonstone
2 CONC  of Duntreath, Baronet: 28]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 July 1414: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland made in favour of Michael of Ramsay. Witnessed by WIL. DE EDMONDSTOUN and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/12/mode/1up RMS, 1424-1513: charte
2 CONC r number 70]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 November 1429: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland made in favour of John of Arnutis. Witnessed by WIL. DE EDMUNDYSTOUN, SCUTIFER, and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/26/mode/1up RMS, 141
2 CONC 4-1513: charter number 135] [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/46/mode/1up See pp. 47-8 for key to the witness lost of Royal Charters WiL. de Edmudystoun, Scutifer
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 February 1449-50: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland made in favour of Alexander Lyon, son and heir of Patrick, Lord Glamis. Witnessed by WIL. DE EDMONDSTOUN DE CULLODIN, MILES, and others. [https://archive.org/details
2 CONC /registrummagnisi02scot/page/72/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 318] [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/158/mode/1up See pp.158-60 for the key to the witness list of Royal Charters. William Edmonstoun 
2 CONC of Culloden is number 128]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 December 1450-51: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland made in favour of John Maxwell of Calderwood. Witnessed by WIL. DE EDMONDSTOUN DE CULLODIN, MILES, and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/pag
2 CONC e/92/mode/1up RMS, 1424-1513: charter number 404] [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/158/mode/1up See pp.158-60 for the key to the witness list of Royal Charters. William Edmonstoun of Culloden is number 128]
2 CONC '''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 February 1450: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland made in favour of Walter Scot of Kirkurde. Witnessed by WIL. DE EDMONDSTOUN DE CULLODIN, MILES, and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/158
2 CONC /mode/1up See pp.158-60 for the key to the witness list of Royal Charters. William Edmonstoun of Culloden is number 128]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 April1452: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland made in favour of Charles of Moravia of Cokpule. Witnessed by WILLELMUS, DOMINUS EDMONSTOUN OF CULLODIN, MILES, and others.  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02
2 CONC scot/page/121/mode/1up RMS, 1424-1513: charter number 546] [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/159/mode/1up Key to the witness list of Royal Charters. William, Lord Edmonstoun of Culloden is number 199]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/n8/mode/1up Genealogical Account of the Family of Edmonstone of Duntreath, 95 pp.]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/parishofstrathbl00smit#page/102/mode/1up John Guthrie Smith, FSA (Scot).,The Parish of Strathblane and its Inhabitants from Early Times : A Chapter of Lennox History (Glasgow : James Maclehose and Son
2 CONC s, Publishers to the University, 1886), pp. 102-24] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Sir William de Edmonstone, Captain of Threave Castle1,2,3,4 
2 CONT *''''''M, #39473, d. circa 1460
2 CONT *Father     Sir Archibald Edmonstone1
2 CONT *''''''     Sir William de Edmonstone, Captain of Threave Castle was born at of Duntreath, Stirlingshire, Scotland.1 He married Mary Stewart, daughter of Sir Robert III Stewart, King of Scotland, Earl of Atholl & Carrick and Annab
2 CONC ella Drummond, in 1425; They had 1 son (William) and 1 daughter (Elizabeth, wife of Humphrey Cunningham of Glengarnock).2,3,4 Sir William de Edmonstone, Captain of Threave Castle died circa 1460.2,3,4
2 CONT *''''''Family      Mary Stewart b. c 1378, d. a Feb 1462
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir William Edmonstone+1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 908.
2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 573-574.
2 CONT * 3.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 651-652.
2 CONT * 4.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 644-645.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1314.htm#i39473
2 CONT
