2 CONC tage Family Trees] via son [http://www.geni.com/profile-34677600317 William Edmonston] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 3 2015, 5:28:36 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial #50192776
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Edmonstone of Culloden, 1st of Duntreath. d. 1460
2 CONT
2 CONT m. 1425 the Lady Mary, 2nd dau. of King Robert III by Annabella, dau. of Sir John
2 CONT
2 CONT      Drummond of Stobhall.
2 CONT
2 CONT      She had been married previously to, 
2 CONT
2 CONT        1stly, The Earl of Angus. 
2 CONT
2 CONT        2ndly Sir James Kennedy, ancestor of the Marquess of Ailsa, by whom she had a son 
2 CONT
2 CONT             James, who becaume Bishop of St Andrews and one of the most powerful men in 
2 CONT
2 CONT             Scotland in the reign of James II. 
2 CONT
2 CONT        3rdly Sir William Graham of Kincardine (ancestor of Dukes of Montrose).
2 CONT
2 CONT By her he had 1 son William (see below) and 1 dau., Mary, who married Humphrey Cunningham of Glengarnock.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William first acquired the lands of Duntreath in 1434, or slightly earlier, when they were granted to his wife and himseld by James I.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1460 & was succeeded by his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT  https://www.edmonstone.com/
