1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN SOMERVILLE OF CAMBUSNETHAN===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, is the son and heir apparent of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Somerville-of-Cambusnethan/6000000004148910101?through=6000000011338274353 [https://archive.org/details/registrumma
2 CONC gnisi02scot/page/805/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 3716]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Hepburn/6000000042064880358?through=6000000011338274353 On 12 March 1511 his father gave him and his wife the lands of Gilmertoun and Gutt
2 CONC eris in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh, to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/805/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 3716]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 March 1511: REX confirmavit cartam Joh. Somervale de Cambusnethane militis, — [qua, — pro speciali amore  etc.,  et pro satisfactione dotis et nonnullis  magnis pecuniarum summis per Adam Hepburne de Craggis pro contractu ma
2 CONC trimonii inter suum filium et ejus filiam solempnisati  persolutis,— concessit  filio suo et  heredi  apparenti JOHANNI SOMERVALE, et JONETE HEPBURNE ejus sponse,— terras suas de Gilmertoun et Guttaris,  vic,  Edinburgh, — terris 
2 CONC et loco de Drum  exceptis  : — Tenend. dictis Joh. filio  et Jon. et  eorum alteri diutius viventi in conjuncta infeodatione,et beredibus inter ipsos  legit, procreatis, quibus deficientibus, legit, et  propinquioribus heredibus  
2 CONC dicti  Joh. filii  de corporo legit, procreandis, quibus omnibus del, dicto Joh. patri  et  heredibus  suis  quibuscunque  reversuras, de  rege in  feodo: — Test. M.   Jac. Hering  thesaurario  Rossen.,  Jac. Somervall,  M.  Micha
2 CONC ele  Somervell  rectore de  Libertoun,  D.   Hen. Lausoun  capellano, David Somervell,  Alex. Young,  et  Alex. Clerk, notariis  publicis  : —  cum subscriptione manuali  : —  Apud Edinburgh, 12 Mar. 1511] [https://archive.org/det
2 CONC ails/registrummagnisi02scot/page/805/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 3716]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 May 1514: Special retour in favour of John Somervell as heir to his father, Sir John Somervell of Cambusnethane, in the barony of Cambusnethane and lands of the town and territory of Carnwith etc. in the barony thereof, both 
2 CONC in the sheriffdom of Lanark, and part of the lands of Gilmertoun in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh, under reservation of liferent of the barony of Cambusnethane to Marion Ballie, relict of John, Lord Somervell. Inquest: William Cokbu
2 CONC rn of Scraling, James Fawle of Braid, John Carmichell of Medoflatt, Alexander Dalmahoy of that ilk, Robert Grame of Westhall, Andrew Wardelaw of Warestoun, Thomas Lowrestoun of that ilk, William Balye of Cormestoun, John Chancella
2 CONC r of Quodquen, James Cunnynghame, son of John Cunnynghame of Bonnytoun, Andrew Straton, John Pomfraye, Andrew Wardlaw. (Engrossed in the document is copy of the commission for executing a brieve for this service and a brieve of te
2 CONC rce in favour of ELIZABETH CARMICHELL, relict of said John Somervell.) [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f4%2f107&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=156
2 CONC 0&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), Somerville Writs, reference GD40/4/107]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 May 1514: Lanark. Vicecomes respondebit pro duobus paribus calcarium alborum per duplicationem albefirme terrarum et baronie de Cambusnethane cum tenentibus etc., et suis pertinen., et  pro 50 li. de firmis terrarum  ville e
2 CONC t territorii de Carnweth, Cawlo, Carlinden, Murhall, Torbrekkis, Blakcastell, Grenesyde,  Auchingray, Moishatt, Croftbill, Estirsidewod, Westirsidewod, Cleuch, et Hisewod, termini S. Martini  ultimo preteriti, existentium in manib
2 CONC us regis sasina non recuperata, que firme se extendunt annuatim ad 100 marcas,  et  pro  2 denariis argenti per duplicationem albefirme  earundem, regi debitis per sasinam datam Johanni Somervel de eisdem 12 Maii a.r.l. [https://a
2 CONC rchive.org/details/exchequerrollsof14scot/page/546/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls XIV: 546]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 May 1514: Edinburgh.Vicecomes respondebit pro 23 marcis 3 s. 4 d. de firmis cujusdam partis terrarum de  Gilmertoun olim Johanni quondam domino Somervel pertinentis, et pro xlvj  marcis  6 s. 8 d. de  relevio ejusdem, regi d
2 CONC ebitis per sasinam datam dicto Johanni Somervel de eisdem dictis die mense et anno. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof14scot/page/546/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls XIV: 546]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 July 1527: At  Edinburgh. Ane Lettre to WILLIAM  SOMERVILE broder germane to Johne  Somervile  of Cambusnethane, — of gift of all gudis movable and unmovable qubilkis pertenit to William Somervile in the Nuke,  pertening to t
2 CONC he king as his eschete throw byding fra the oist and raid apoun the thevis in the southland, etc. Per Signaturam manu Regis subscriptam. vi.  69  et  vii.  78. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/564/mode/1
2 CONC up Register of the Privy Seal of Scotland, 1488-1529. number 3830]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 February 1562-63: Contract between John Creichtoun of Ryhill, tutor of Sanchar, and CHRISTINE DALZELL, relict of John Somervell of Camnethane, now his spouse, on one part, and Bessie Inglis and James Moffet, her spouse, on o
2 CONC ther part, whereby said John and Christine are to enter said Bessie and James to peaceable possession of steading of Newmains in barony of Carnweth, sheriffdom of Lanerk, from which deceased Janet Kello, mother of said Bessie, was
2 CONC  forcibly removed. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH15%2f39%2f119&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Haddington Pap
2 CONC ers, reference RH15/39/119]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John 'Red Bag' Somerville, 2nd of Cambusnethan (d 1553) was called 'Red Bag' on account of the red satin satchel he carried while hawking. Red-Bag would later be involved in rivalry over the Somerville family estates. * m1. (by
2 CONC  13.03.1511, divorced 1515-6) Janet Hepburn (dau of Sir Adam Hepburn of Craigs) i.+ issue * m2. (mcrt 10.07.1510) Margaret Graham (dau of William Graham, 1st Earl of Montrose) * m3. Christian Dalzell Divorced: BEF 1539. It is not 
2 CONC clear which wife is the mother of which children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT #  John (James) Somerville , 3rd of Cambusnethan Married 1) Katherine Carmichael 2) Katherine Murray
2 CONT # William, 2nd son.  
2 CONT #  Agnes, oldest daughter.  Married 1) John Fleming, 2nd Lord Fleming  2) George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes.
2 CONT # Helen? 2nd daughter.  Married Lockhardt, Lord of Cleghorn.
2 CONT #  youngest daughter, Flora.  Married James Johnstone.  Mother of James Johnstone, "... one of the most famous border raiders of his time."
2 CONT
2 CONT Stirnet says Nov 2004 " THE FOLLOWING IS PROVISIONAL / DRAFT AND SUBJECT TO CHANGE. " at http://www.stirnet.com/HTML/genie/british/ss4as/somerville02.htm
