1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN SOMERVILLE OF CAMBUSNETHAN ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Somerville, here treated, is the grandson of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Somerville-of-Cambusnethan/6000000004148910101 On 27 March 1561 he had sasine of the the ten pound lands of  Prestuikschawis in the Kyle-Stewart
2 CONC  division of Ayrshire, which lands had been in the hands of the crown since his grandfather had been killed in action at the Battle of Flodden. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollss03exchgoog/page/468/mode/1up Exchequer Rol
2 CONC ls of Scotland XIX: 468]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Somerville of Cambusnethan is reported to have died in February 1594. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4as/somerville02.php Stirnet: Somerville 02] He certainly died before 22 May 1594, the date upon which Hug
2 CONC h, Lord Somerville, raised letters of horning against his widow, Katherine Murray, and their eldest son John. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f4%2f158&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k
2 CONC =Katherine+Murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD40/4/158]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children of First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, married, as his second wife, https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Murray/6000000181524204826?through=6000000181523170874 They are noticed as man and wife on 10 September 1554, the
2 CONC  date upon which he gave her the lands and barony of Cambusnethan in liferent. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/226/mode/1up RMS 1580-1593: charter number 733]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children of Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
