2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 October 1539: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James V, King of Scots, confirms that he had give the lands and barony of Cambusnethan anew to John Somerville of Cambusnethan and his wife Hatherine Carmichael,
2 CONC  to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent, and thereafter by their lawful male heirs, whom failing by John's nearest lawful heirs whatsoever. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/455/mode/1up RMS 1513-15
2 CONC 46: charter number 2027]'''
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 September 1554: Charter by which John Somerville of Cambusnethan confirms that he has given the barony of Cambusnethan in the sheriffdom of Lanark in liferent to his wife KATHERINE MURRAY, who obtained a charter of confirmat
2 CONC ion under the Great Seal of Scotland on 4 September 1584. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/226/mode/1up RMS 1580-1593: charter number 733]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 February 1560: Charter by John Somervell of Cambusnethan, [ to ] John Somervell, his son, of the lands and barony of Cambusnethan. Dated at Cambesnethan, 25 Feb 1560. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/d
2 CONC etails.aspx?reference=GD8%2f169&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Cambusnethan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, reference GD8/169]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 February 1560: Bond by John Somerville of Cambusnethan, to deliver the reversion for redemption of the lands and barony of Cambusnethan, from his son, John Somerville, dated at Cambusnethan, 25 Feb 1560.(Contains mention of 
2 CONC a piece of gold called 'A Portingall Docat' which money the said John Somerville elder had received from Thomas, now Lord Boyd). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f360&st=1&tc=y&tl
2 CONC =n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Somerville+of+Cambusnethan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, reference GD8/360]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 June 1560: Charter by which John Somerville of Cambusnethan confirms that he has given the barony of Cambusnethan to John Somerville, his son, procreated between him and his wife KATHERINAM MURRAY. John junior's charter, whi
2 CONC ch was witnessed by Patrick Murray, son of Patrick Murray of Fallahill, and others, was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 19 January 1580-81. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/27/mode/1up RMS 158
2 CONC 0-1593: charter number 87]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1560: Charter by John Somervell of Cambusnethan to John Somervell, his son, procreate, between him and KATHERINE MURRAY, his spouse, of the lands of Quiodquen. Dated at Cambesnethan, 31 Jul 1560.  [https://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f168&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Cambusnethan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, reference GD8/168]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 March 1561: Ballivus de Kile respondebit pro £1900 de firmis decem libratarum terrarum antiqui extentus de Prestuikschawis etc., jacentium infra balliam suam et vicecomitatum de Air, existentium in manibus regine et quondam 
2 CONC sui patris tanquam senescallorum Scotie per spatium quadraginta septem annorum et unius termini ultimo retroactorum ratione warde et sasina non recuperata respective, et pro £40 de relevio earundem, regine tanquam senescalle presc
2 CONC ripte debitis per sasinam datam Johanni Somervile de Cambusnethane, cujus avus obiit in bello de Flowdoun. (Edinburgh, 27 March.] [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollss03exchgoog/page/468/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland
2 CONC  XIX: 468]'''
2 CONT                   8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 April 1574: Charter by John Somervell of Cambusnethan to John Somervell, his eldest son, of the lands of Guttaris in the lordship of Gilmertoun. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=G
2 CONC D40%2f4%2f145&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Cambusnethan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian, Somerville Writs, reference GD40/4/145]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 June 1574: Charter issued by David Neisbit of Dalzell. Witnessed by William Somerville, brother german of John Somerville of Cambusnethan: "Wil. Somerwell fratre germano Joannis S." [https://archive.org/details/registrummagn
2 CONC isi04scot/page/824/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 3006]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 May 1575: Lanark. Idem vicecomes respondebit pro £5600 de firmis omnium et singularum terrarum subscriptarum, videlicet, ville et territorii de Carnweth, extendentium ad decem libratas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de 
2 CONC Cowlo et Carlingden extendentium ad decem marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, [terrarum de] Murehall extondentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de Torbrekis et Blaikcastell extendentium ad quinque marcata
2 CONC s terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de Grenefeild extendentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de Auchingray extendentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, [terrarum de] Moshatt et Crofthill 
2 CONC extendentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de Eistir Sydwod et Westir Sydwod exten- dentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de Hywod et Cleuch extendentium ad quinque marcatas terr
2 CONC arum antiqui extentus, extendentium in integro ad quadraginta libratas terrarum antiqui extentus, jacentium in baronia de Carnweth infra balliam suam, existentium in manibus supremi domini nostri regis et suorum predecessorum resp
2 CONC ective per spatium triginta quinque annorum ultime elapsorum sasina non recuperata, que firme extendunt annuatim ad centum sexaginta libras; et pro 2d. argenti per duplieationem albefirme earundem ; regi debitis per sasinam datam 
2 CONC Joanni Somerville de Cambusnethaine. [Edinburgh, 10 May.] [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccarii01mcnegoog/page/480/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland. Volume XX. 1568-1579, pp. 480-81]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 May 1578: Precept of sasine under the Quarter Seal in favour of Hugh, Lord Somervell, in respect of the lands of Gilmertoun, Drum and Gutteris, following on decree of declarator of redemption against John Somervell of Cambus
2 CONC nethem, KATHERINE MURRAY, his spouse, James Somervell younger of Cambusnethem and Margaret Hammiltoun, his spouse, and John Somervell, son of said John and Katherine. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details
2 CONC .aspx?reference=GD40%2f4%2f146&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Katherine+Murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), reference GD40/4/146]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    12
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 May 1580: Et de £5600 de firmis omnium et singularum terrarum subscriptarum, videlicet, vile et terrarum de  Carnvath, cum pertinentiis, extendentium ad decem  libratas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de Cowbo et Carling
2 CONC den, extendentium ad decem marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, [terrarum de] Murehall, extendentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de Torbrekis et Blakcastell, extendentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum ant
2 CONC iqui extentus, terrarum de Grenfeild, extendentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de  Auchingray, extendentium ad quinque  marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, [terrarum de] Moschat et Crofthill, extendenti
2 CONC um ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de Eister Sydwod et Vestir Sydwod, extendentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiqui extentus, terrarum de Hywod et Cleuch, extendentium ad quinque marcatas terrarum antiq
2 CONC ui extentus, cum singulis earundem pertinentiis, extendentium in integro ad quadraginta libratas terrarum antiqui extentus, jacentium in baronia de Carnvath infra balliam computantis existentium in manibus regis et suorum predices
2 CONC sorum respective per spatium triginta quinque annorum ultime elapsorum sasina non recuperata, que firme extendunt annuatim ad centum sexaginta libras ; et de 2d. argenti per duplicationem albefirme earundem; regi debitis per sasin
2 CONC am datam Joanni Somervall de Cambusnethaine, decimo Maii, anno regni regis octavo. [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccarii00mcnegoog/page/81/mode/1up The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland XXI: pp. 81-2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    13
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 May 1580: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland in favour of John Lummisdane of Blanerne which mentions John Somerville, son of John Somerville of Cambusnethan, and KATHERINE MURRAY his mother: "Jo  Somerwel filius Joanni
2 CONC s S. de Cambusnethane, Katherina Murray ejus mater". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/827/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 3015]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    14
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 May 1581: Contract between John Somerville of Cambusnethan, and KATHERINE MURRAY, his spouse, on the one part and John Somerville, their son, on the other part, whereby the said John Somerville younger, binds himself that he 
2 CONC shall not appoint, transact nor agree with James Somerville, eldest son to the said John Somerville, of Cambusnethan towards the disposition of the lands and barony of Cambusnethan, in favour of the said James, without the special
2 CONC  consent of his father. Charter at Cambusnethan, 4 May 1581. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f310&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Somerville+of+Cambusnethan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n 
2 CONC National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, reference GD8/310]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    15
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 May 1594: Copy of letters of horning at the instance of Hugh, Lord Somervell, against KATHERINE MURRAY, relict of John Somervell of Cambusnethane, John Somervell, their eldest son, and James Somervell now of Cambusnethane in
2 CONC  terms of a decree of redemption of part of the lands of Gilmertoun dated 18 Dec. 1577. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f4%2f158&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Katherine+Murray&ko=p
2 CONC &r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), Somerville Writs, reference GD40/4/158]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Books of the Town Clerks of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 August 1560: John Somyrvaile of Cambusneithan gave sasine to John Kello, junior, attorney, and in name of John Somyrvaile (son of the said John Somyrvaile and Katherine Murray, his spouse), of (1) a cottage land (terram eota
2 CONC giam) of the lower town of Quodquen; (2) his lands of the upper town of Quodquen, extending to a £7 10 s. farm (firme) ; (3) 44 acres of land, commonly called the New Maynes, lying on the north side of the common pasturage and of 
2 CONC the lands of Quodquen ; and (4) the lands of Kerswell, extending to a ten merk land of old extent, lying in the barony of Carnwetht and shire of Lanark. Witnesses: William Selkirk, in Pedder; Symone Feichear in Libertoune, and Tho
2 CONC mas Franche in Neddirtowne. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsprotoc04robegoog/page/n104/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols II: 578]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
