1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ROBERT, MASTER OF ROSS ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert, Master of Ross, was killed in action at the Battle of Pinkie Cleugh, on 10 September 1547. He married Agnes Moncrieff, relict of Thomas Scott of Abbotshall, by whom he left a daughter Elizabeth, who married, 10 May 1562
2 CONC , Lord Fleming. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/252/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 252]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Inventory of his Moveable Estate ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 13 January 1550. [National Records of Scotland, St. Andrews Commissary Court, Inventory of Robertus (Robert), Master of Ross, dated 10 September 1547, sometime spouse of Agnes Moncrief, relict of Tho
2 CONC mas Scott, of Abbotshall, parish of Kirkcaldy, killed at Battle of Pinkecleuch, reference CC20/4/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninian_Ross,_3rd_Lord_Ross Biographical Summary by Wikipedia] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert, Master of Ross, who was killed in 1547 at the Battle of Pinkie. He married Agnes Moncrieff and left a daughter, Elizabeth Ross. She was a lady in waiting to Mary, Queen of Scots, and married on 10 May 1562, John Fleming
2 CONC , 5th Lord Fleming. Mary paid for the wedding banquet. The celebrations were held in Holyrood park at the side of the loch and there were "great triumphs", shows and masques involving a staged sea-battle or naumachia. The ambassad
2 CONC or from Sweden attended.''''
