1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN ROSS OF TARTRAVEN ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Ross of Tartraven, here treated, is the bastard son of https://www.geni.com/people/Ninian-Ross-3rd-Lord-of-Halkhead/6000000003646015147?through=6000000221719448883. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/s
2 CONC cotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/252/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 252] The name of his mother has not been identified. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/175/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 776]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 April 1553: Apud Edinburgh. REGINA etc., dedit literas legitimationis WILLELMO STEWART bastardo, filio naturali quondam Willelmi S. in Paslay, et JOANNI ROS bastardo, naturali filio Niniani dom. de R. [https://archive.org/de
2 CONC tails/registrummagnisi04scot/page/175/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 776]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                       2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 November 1562: Sasine, dated 16 November 1562, given by John Ros [Ross], in Tartrewane [Tartraven], as bailie of James Lord Ross of Halkheid [Halkhead] and Melvile [Melville], in favour of John Tailzeour [Taylor] of the one-
2 CONC fourth part of the half of the one-eighth part of the £10 lands of Morovinside [Muiravonside] called Cokishill [Coxhill], now occupied by said John Tailzeour [Taylor], following on charter by said Lord Ross, dated at Melvile [Melv
2 CONC ille] 13 November 1562; witnesses to charter, Mr Alexander Mauchane [Mauchan], advocate, John Mayne, his servitor, John Lawsone [Lawson] and Alan Wauch [Waugh], in Morvinside [Muiravonside]. Witnesses to sasine, William Merschell 
2 CONC [Marshall], in Cokishil [Coxhill], Archibald Tailzeour [Taylor], James Gryntoun [Grinton], Peter Leirmonth [Learmonth], in Crahill, Henry Ross and James Martyne [Martin]. Notary, George Freir [Freer], M.A. [https://catalogue.nrsco
2 CONC tland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD332%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=tartraven&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Calder Family of Redford, Stirlingshire, reference GD332/1
2 CONC ]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Book of Gilbert Grote ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 December 1569: Instrument narrating that Patrik Hammiltoun, son of James Hammiltoun of Kincavill, superior of the lands after-mentioned, passed to the personal presence of his father and there overgave and purely and simply 
2 CONC resigned by staff and baton four oxengang of land of the Mains of Kincavill (occupied by Thomas Borthuik and James Borthuik, his son), lying in the town and territory of Kincavill and sheriffdom of Lynlithquhow, in favour of Aliso
2 CONC un Blair. John Ros in Tortraven, brother of Lord Ros, Halket, and Mauile [Malvile ?] asked instruments on behalf of the said Alisoun. Done on 10th December 1569 in the chamber of the said James Hammiltoun within the burgh of Edinb
2 CONC urgh. Witnesses, the said John Ros, John Hammiltoun and Alexander Hammiltoun, sons of the Laird of Kincavill, and William Archibald, servitor of Lord Ros, 127. [https://dn790006.ca.archive.org/0/items/scottishrecordso31scotuoft/sc
2 CONC ottishrecordso31scotuoft_bw.pdf Protocol Book of Mr. Gilbert Grote: protocol number 284]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
