1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography==
2 CONT Lady Elizabeth Leslie, married in 1485 to William, third Earl of Errol.  Their marriage-contract is dated at Lindores, 14th October 1485, and by it the Earl of Rothes bound himself to pay to the Earl of Errol the sum of 1000 merks
2 CONC , to be invested in land for the benefit of the said Lady Elizabeth and her heirs.  William, Earl of Errol, had a charter to himself, and Elizabeth his spouse, of the lands of Inchescheray, in the barony of Errol, 26th March 1501;
2 CONC  and another to himself, and Elizabeth his spouse, of the barony of Glendovik, in the shire of Perth, about 1503.  '''The issue of this marriage was a daughter, Lady Mariana, married to David, seventh Earl of Crawford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Countess Consort of Crawford?
2 CONT
2 CONT also known as '''Mariana (or Marianna) Hay
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT Note by Ed Wyse on Dec 18, 2011: This woman is named "Lady Mariana" in Leslie Family records.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Given name has also been reported to be '''Elisabeth'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * http://books.google.com/books?id=vqgxAQAAIAAJ&pg=PA27#v=onepage&q=&f=false pages  27 - 28
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
