1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/hh4aa/halyburton1.php#linklo
2 CONT
2 CONT TCP (Rothes) notes that TSP (Haliburton) shows Christina as dau of the younger Sir Walter by Mary Douglas whilst TSP (Rothes) shows her as dau of the elder Sir Walter by his 2nd wife, Isabel Stewart, "which seems more likely".
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/334/mode/1up?view=theater The Scots Peerage] shows as daughter of the 2nd Walter Haliburton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Christina, married, as his second wife, in 1440, to George, Earl of Rothes. Nineteen years later the Earl raised an action of divorce against his wife on the ostensible ground that they were within the forbidden degrees of cons
2 CONC anguinity, but his reasons for so doing are not apparent.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://www.thepeerage.com/p10799.htm#i107989
2 CONT *Christian Haliburton1
2 CONT *F, #107989
2 CONT *Last Edited=20 May 2007
2 CONT *     Christian Haliburton is the daughter of Walter Haliburton and Isabella Stewart.1 She married George Leslie, 1st Earl of Rothes, son of Sir Norman Leslie of Rothes and Christian Seton.1
2 CONT *     Christian Haliburton was also known as Christian Halyburton. Her married name became Leslie.1
2 CONT *Children of Christian Haliburton and George Leslie, 1st Earl of Rothes
2 CONT *1.Lady Elizabeth Leslie+
2 CONT *2.Andrew Leslie, Master of Rothes+ d. b 3 Aug 1473
2 CONT *3.Christina Leslie+
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 219. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *<nowiki>-------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p100.htm#i2986
2 CONT *Christian Halyburton
2 CONT *Father Sir Walter Haliburton d. b 10 May 1447 
2 CONT *Mother Isobel Stewart 
2 CONT *     Christian Halyburton and George Leslie, 1st Earl of Rothes, Lord Leslie were divorced. Christian Halyburton was born at of Dirleton, Berwickshire, East Lothian, Scotland. She married George Leslie, 1st Earl of Rothes, Lord L
2 CONC eslie, son of Norman Leslie and Christian Seton, in 1440.
2 CONT *Family George Leslie, 1st Earl of Rothes, Lord Leslie b. b 2 Sep 1416, d. bt 31 Aug 1489 - 24 May 1490 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT *◦Christian Leslie+ d. a 20 Feb 1492
2 CONT *◦Andrew Leslie, Master of Rothes+ d. b 3 Aug 1473
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S212] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. XI, p. 188; The Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles, by Gerald Paget, Vol. 2, p. 470.
2 CONT *<nowiki>------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *Full text of "Historical records of the family of Leslie from 1067 to 1868-69. Collected from public records and authentic private sources" 
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/historicalrecord02lesluoft/historicalrecord02lesluoft_djvu.txt
2 CONT *(Please excuse the Typo's from this web site)
2 CONT *George, Earl of Kothes, married, secondly, in 1440, ''''''Christian, daughter of Walter, Lord Halyburton of Dirleton, by Lady Isabel Stewart, eldest daughter of Eobert, Duke of Albany, and relict of Alexander Leslie, Earl of Eoss
2 CONC ''''''. By Christian Halyburton the Earl of Eothes had issue 
2 CONT **I. ANDREW, Master of Rothes, of whom hereafter. 
2 CONT **II. LADY ELIZABETH LESLIE, married in 1485 to William, third Earl of Errol. .... Etc. 
2 CONT *<nowiki>------------------------------------</nowiki>—
