2 CONT > Sir William Baillie of Hoprig and Lamington, his son, in 1492, had a charter under the great seal to him and Marion Home his wife, in conjunct fee and infeftment. This lady was the daughter of Sir Patrick Home of Polwarth, compt
2 CONC roller of Scotland in the reign of James the Fourth, and ancestor of the earls of Marchmont, by whom he bad Sir William Baillie, his son and heir, and John Baillie, of whom descended the Baillies of St. John’s Kirk, Lanarkshire, o
2 CONC f whom are come the Baillies of Jerviswood and Walston. Sir William Baillie, the eldest son, married his cousin Elizabeth, daughter and one of the heirs of line of John Lord Lindsay of the Byres, by whom he had Sir William his son
2 CONC  and heir, and a daughter, Janet, married to Sir David Hamilton of Preston. 
2 CONT
