2 CONT '''1557: Copy contract between Colin Campbell of Glenurquhay, on one part, and Marion Edmestoun, relict of John Campbell of Glenurquhay, Christine and Marion Campbell, daughters and heirs of said deceased John, with consent of Edw
2 CONC ard Reddocht of Cultebragane, their curator, on other part, whereby said Marion gives up to said Christine and Marion her conjunct fee of £15 worth of land of the Port of Lochtay, with the place, isle and fishings of the same, in 
2 CONC lordship of Descher and Toyer, and £8 land of Ardbayicht and Dery with Mill thereof, in stewartry of Stratherne, without prejudice of her liferent therein, so that her said daughters may enter thereto as heirs of said deceased Joh
2 CONC n, and thereafter they are to dispone said lands to said Colin, reserving their mother's liferent, and they oblige themselves to dispone to said Colin by the first of May next to come, the superiority of £8 land of Drumlart and Bl
2 CONC airvoyak, in earldom of Menteith, said sheriffdom, said Marion giving said Colin a tack of her conjunct lands, for her lifetime except £8 land of Ardbaycht and Derye, (blank) 1557. Witnesses: Robert Menzeis of Comre, Edmond Moncri
2 CONC f, James Tuthane, John McVir, William Ruthane, Alexander McNab, John McConye Roy, John Reddocht, William Reddocht, John McEwin. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f135&st=1&tc=
2 CONC y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmestoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane, reference GD112/2/135]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 December 1558: Charter by Christina Campbell, one of two daughters and heirs of deceased John Campbell of Glenurquhay, with consent of Edward Reidheugh of Cultebragan, her curator, to Colin Campbell of Glenurquhay, her uncle
2 CONC , of half ten merkland of Lie Port of Lochtay with half island and fishing thereof, island and loch of Lochtay, half 8 merkland of easter end of Eddirogoll next lands of Balloch, and half four merk 6s 8d land of Collelloquhane, 11
2 CONC  December 1558. Witnesses: John McCoule of Dunollycht, Duncan Campbell of Glenlyoun, Alexander Hume fiar of Lundeis, Patrick Eviot of Balhoussy, Alexander Ruthven, prebendary of Forgoune, and David Hume. Two seals on tags. [http:/
2 CONC /catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f135&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmestoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breada
2 CONC lbane, reference GD112/2/135]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
