1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARIOTE FORESTER (aka MARION FORESTER)===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mariote Forester, here treated, married James Edmonstone of the Newton. On 16 March 1544-45 she and her husband had a charter under the great seal of Scotland confirming their possession of the five merk land of Wester Rowis lo
2 CONC cated in the Stewartry of Menteith and sheriffdom of Perth, to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent, and thereafter by their lawful male heirs, whom failing by James Edmonstone's own heirs and assignees. James had previous
2 CONC ly resigned this land to the crown in order to obtain a new grant to him and his wife. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/721/mode/1up RMS: 3078] Her husband died in April 1575. [National Records of Scotland,
2 CONC  Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar of James Edmestoun of the Newtoun, parish of Kilmadok, sheriffdom of Perth, reference CC8/8/20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Her Husband's Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Edmonstone of the Newton made his last will and testament at Newton, probably at his house there, on 19 April 1575. The witnesses present included his sons-in-law, David Home of Argadie, and William Muschett of Spitteltou
2 CONC n. He nominated and appointed his wife Marion Forester as his executrix, and charged her to intromit with his goods and gear, including the house, for her own benefit and for the benefit of their four youngest children: "To wit  A
2 CONC ndro, James, Marion and Marjorie Edmestoun". At the time of his death he owed one hundred pounds to William Muschett in Spitteltoun: "for his tocher guide wit Mgratt Edmestoun dochter to the defunct" and eighty pounds to David Hom
2 CONC e of Argadie, money that was still owed to him: "for his tocher guide wt Cristiane Edmestoun his spous". Eighteen pounds was also owed to: "Mungo Edmestoun, sone to the defunct" for a horse that he purchased for his father. Confir
2 CONC mation was granted on 26 November 1589. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar of James Edmestoun of the Newtoun, parish of Kilmadok, sheriffdom of Perth, reference CC8/8/20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138749166986& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138750344821& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138749553902& Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Mungo-Edmonstone/6000000138697877830?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1591867486127&through=6000000037935462192
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Edmonstone/6000000138698012821
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Edmonstone-of-Newton/6000000138698094821?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1591867771742&through=6000000037935462192
