2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Father's Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Edmonstone of the Newton made his last will and testament at Newton, probably at his house there, on 19 April 1575. The witnesses present included his sons-in-law, David Home of Argadie, and William Muschett of Spitteltou
2 CONC n. He nominated and appointed his wife Marion Forester as his executrix, and charged her to intromit with his goods and gear, including the house, for her own benefit and for the benefit of their four youngest children: "To wit  A
2 CONC ndro, James, Marion and Marjorie Edmestoun". At the time of his death he owed one hundred pounds to William Muschett in Spitteltoun: "for his tocher guide wit Mgratt Edmestoun dochter to the defunct" and eighty pounds to David Hom
2 CONC e of Argadie, money that was still owed to him: "for his tocher guide wt Cristiane Edmestoun his spous". Eighteen pounds was also owed to: "Mungo Edmestoun, sone to the defunct" for a horse that he purchased for his father. Confir
2 CONC mation was granted on 26 November 1589. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar of James Edmestoun of the Newtoun, parish of Kilmadok, sheriffdom of Perth, reference CC8/8/20]'''
2 CONT
