2 CONT '''16 June 1612: Procuratory of resignation by James Edmonstoun of Newtoun, of the Place of Garden with the mains and mill thereof, the lands of Middle Garden, and the thirled multures of the lands of Eister and Wester Myis, Blair
2 CONC grottis, Blairfachane, and Offerance of Cashlie astricted to the mill of Wester Garden, in the sheriffdom of Stirling, in favour of Sir Archibald Stirling of Keir, Dame Grissell Ross, his spouse, in liferent, and John Stirling, th
2 CONC eir son, in fee, following on a contract between the said parties for the apprising of the lands of Sir James Forrester, sometime of Garden, warranting that no one had made or would make disposition of the said lands to the prejud
2 CONC ice of the said lands excepting the said contract, and the minute of contract between the said Sir Archibald and his foresaids on the one part and Sir James Forester, sometime of Garden, Dame Margaret Flemyng, his spouse, with con
2 CONC sent of John, Earl of Wigtoun, Lord Flemyng, on the other, regarding the said Sir James' giving up of part of the said lands and his quitting of the legal reversion of another part. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecat
