1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == I WILLIAM BUCHANAN OF AUCHMAR ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1575: Charter by William Buchanan of Auchmar in favour of Walter Buchanan alias Leny and Isabel Henderson, his wife, and their heirs, failing which to the heirs of Walter, of an annualrent of £20 scots out of the 13 me
2 CONC rk land and half of the mill of Strathyre, to be held blench of William. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fD%2f6%2f3%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Buchanan+of+Auchmar&ko=p&
2 CONC r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/D/6/3/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 June 1587: Precept of clare constat by George Buchanan of that ilk in favour of Patrick Buchanan as heir to the deceased William Buchanan of Auchmar, his father, of the lands of Bailefuill, Kipp, Bad and Ardochmore with the 
2 CONC mill thereof extending to a 13 merk land lying in the barony of Strathyre and sheriffdom of Perth; dated at Innerzerick. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fD%2f6%2f3%2f4&st=1
2 CONC &tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Buchanan+of+Auchmar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/D/6/3/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Chiefs of Clan Buchanan=
2 CONT *15th – George Buchanan,[76][77] (Guthrie Smith identifies him as 10th Chief and Buchanan of Auchmar identifies him as 17th Chief) succeed his grandfather, Walter 14th of Buchanan, in 1526 and died 1560. He first married Margaret 
2 CONC Edmonstone and by her a son (John [Guthrie Smith identifies him as 11th Chief but then goes on to advise that the Chiefship passed from John’s father to John’s son[78] and Buchanan of Auchmar identifies him as 18th Chief[79 who ma
2 CONC rried Elizabeth Livingston and by her had George[79] who succeeded his grandfather) and two daughters (Helen and Susanna). Second he married Janet Cunningham and by her had a son ('''William first ancestor of the cadets of Auchmar
2 CONC ''') and a daughter (Margaret). http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Buchanan.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/historicalgeneal1820buch/page/135/mode/1up Essay upon the Family and Surname of Buchanan. By William Buchanan of Auchmar. (First published in the year 1723) (Glasgow, Printed for J. Wylie & Co., 1
2 CONC 820), 276 pp.] [https://archive.org/details/historicalgeneal1820buch/page/184/mode/1up For the family of Buchanan of Auchmar see pp. 184-92]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/strathendrickits00smit#page/n12/mode/1up Strathendrick and Its Inhabitants from Early Times: An Account of the Parishes of Fintry, Balfron, Killearn, Drymen, Buchanan, and Kilmaronock. By John Guth
2 CONC rie Smith, FSA. Scot. (J. Maclehose and sons, Glasgow, 1896) 410 pages including index] [https://archive.org/details/strathendrickits00smit/page/373/mode/1up For Buchanan of Auchmar see pp. 373-6]'''
