2 CONT '''9 December 1573: Instrument under the hand of John Muschett, clerk of the diocese of Dunblane and clerk of the commissariot thereof, notary public, narrating that Willeame Edmonstoun of Duntreycht, on the narrative that a subse
2 CONC quent contract had been entered into between Archibald Edmonston of Spittellton, his brother's son, and James Edmonston of Ballinton, his cousin, regarding a marriage between the said Archibald and Marjory Edmonston, only daughter
2 CONC  of the said James, and in order that the said marriage might take effect and the spouses be infeft in the lands aftermentioned, renounced, discharged and revoked (1) a former contract (dated at Edinburgh 12th June 1559), which he
2 CONC  had entered into with the said James Edmonston, who bound himself to infeft him in the lands of Kingis Boquhoppill and the 6 merkland of Cessintullie lying in the stewartry of Menteytht, and sheriffdom of Perthe, and (2) all acti
2 CONC on and cause which he might have in virtue of said contract. Done on 9th December 1573 in the "ovir chalmer" in Ballinton. Witnesses, James Muschet of Tolgarthe, Willieame Edmonstone, portioner of Row, David Home in Argatye, Archi
2 CONC bald Edmonston of Spittelton and James Edmonston, son of the said William. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f237&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ballinton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nat
2 CONC ional Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/237]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 June 1574: Charter by which James Edmonstoun of Ballingtone confirms that he has given the 20 merk land of Buchquhoppill and the 6 merk land of Cessintullie alias Ballingtone in the Stewartry of Menteith to his daughter Marj
2 CONC orie Edmonstoun and her husband Archibald Edmonstoun, portioner of Spittaltoun. His charter follows from a contact of marriage dated 22 August 1573. The lands in question were to be held by Archibald and Marjorie in conjunct fee a
2 CONC nd liferent, and by their legitimate heirs in fee, whom failing by Marjorie's lawful heirs, whom failing by Archibald's heirs and assignees. James Edmonstoun of Ballingtone reserved his own liferent and the terce of his wife Barba
2 CONC re Muschat. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 3 February 1575-76. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/674/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 2508]'''
2 CONT
