1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''''A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage and Baronetage'' (also known as ''Burke's Peerage'') and ''The Scots Peerage'' do not report a marriage to John Hay for this Janet.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Janet Douglas:
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10827.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Janet Douglas was the daughter of James Douglas, 1st Earl of Morton and Joan Stewart.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell, son of Adam Hepburn, Master of Hailes and Helen Home, before 1 February 1480/81.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died before 1490, without male issue.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Janet Douglas was also known as Joanna.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 1445, her married name became Erskine.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 1 February 1480/81, her married name became Hepburn.[1] As a result of her marriage, Lady Janet Douglas was styled as Countess of Bothwell on 17 October 1488.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Janet Douglas and Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell
2 CONT *1. Lady Janet Hepburn+2
2 CONT *2. Lady Margaret Hepburn4 d. 1542
2 CONT
