2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Hugh Campbell1
2 CONT * b. 1502
2 CONT * d. February 1561
2 CONT * Father	Sir Hugh Campbell2 d. b 4 Aug 1508
2 CONT * Mother	Isobel Wallace3 d. b 1530
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Hugh Campbell was born in 1502 at of Loudoun, Ayrshire, Scotland.1 He died in February 1561.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, first, Margaret Stewart, second daughter of Matthew, second Earl of Lennox, and had issue; 
2 CONT
2 CONT and secondly, Agnes, daughter of Sir John Drummond of Innerpeffray, s.p. She survived him and was married, secondly (banns proclaimed at Eaglesham Kirk 31 May, 7 and 14 June 1562, dispensation 10 August 1562), as his second wife, 
2 CONC to Hugh, third Earl of Eglinton;' and thirdly (contract dated 15 November 1585), to Patrick, third Lord Drummond, and died 21 January 1589-90. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue by first marriage :—
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Sir Matthew, his heir.
2 CONT * 2. Thomas, Commendator of Holywood, styled brother of Sheriff of Ayr 1561.8 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had also two natural children :— 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Alexander, charged before the Privy Council with his brother Sir Matthew with invading the lands of James Chalmers of Gatgirth 1 October 1575, and not appearing, was denounced rebel.'
2 CONT * 2. Margaret, had letters of legitimation under the Great Seal with her brother Alexander on 5 October 1572."  She married Alexander Nisbet of Bankhead." 
2 CONT
