1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://archive.org/details/historyofcountie32pate/page/339/mode/1up?q=Kersland History of the counties of Ayr and Wigton Volume 3 Cunninghame Part 2 by James Paterson Published 1866 Page 548]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Mathew Campbell of Loudoun, Sheriff of Ayr. He had a charter of the lands and lordship of Mauchline, and the church lands of Loudoun, 1 February 1566. Sir Mathew promoted the Reformation; but such was his sense of loyalty, tha
2 CONC t he fought on the side of Queen Mary at Langside, where he was taken prisoner. He married Isobel Drummond, daughter of Sir John Drummond of Innerpeffray, by whom he had issue —
2 CONT * 1st son. Hugh Campbell, his successor.
2 CONT * 2nd son. Mathew Campbell, who signalized himself in the German wars. He settled in Lavonia, and was ancestor of the celebrated Austrian FieldMarshal, Count Lauhdon.
2 CONT * 1st daughter. Jean Campbell, married, first, to Robert Montgomerie of Giffen, and had issue; secondly, to Ludovick, Duke of Lennox, without issue.
2 CONT * 2nd daughter. Margaret Campbell, married to Thomas Lord Boyd, and had issue.
2 CONT * 3rd daughter. Marion Campbell, married to Sir John Wallace of Craigie.
2 CONT * 4th daughter. Agnes Campbell, married to William Cuninghame of Caprington.
2 CONT * 5th daughter. Isabel Campbell, married to William Graufurd of Leifnorris.
2 CONT * 6th daughter. Anne Campbell, married to Lord Kirkcudbright.
2 CONT * 7th daughter. Annabella Campbell, married, first, to Daniel Ker of Kersland; secondly, to David Dunbar of Enterkine.
2 CONT
2 CONT
