1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "Sir John Drummond of Innerpeffrie his fourth daughter, with Lady Margaret Stuart, was <strong>Jean Drummond</strong>. She was married to his fourth Sir James Chisholm of Cromlix, and had to him Sir James, who succeeded ; William 
2 CONC Bishop of Vafon in France, and Sir John Chisholm, and Thomas Chisholm portioner of Buttergafk ; her daughters were, Helen Chisholm Lady Kinfauns, mother to Lodovick Lyndfay, Earle of Craufurd, Jean Chisholm Lady Maddertie, Agnes  
2 CONC Chisholm Lady Marchefton, and Margaret Chisholm Lady Mufchet."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/genealogyofmostd00drum#page/150/mode/2up The genealogy of the most noble and ancient House of Drummond]; 1889; page 151
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.thepeerage.com/p56421.htm#i564201
2 CONT Jean Drummond1 F, #564201 Last Edited=28 Jun 2014 Consanguinity Index=12.54%
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Drummond is the daughter of Sir John Drummond, 1st of Innerpeffray and Margaret Stewart.1 She married Sir James Chisholm of Cromlix.1 Her married name became Chisholm.1 Children of Jean Drummond and Sir James Chisholm of Crom
2 CONC lix
2 CONT #     Helen Chisholm+2
2 CONT #     Agnes Chisholm+1
2 CONT #     Sir John Chisholm of Cromlix1
2 CONT #     William Chisholm1
2 CONT #     Sir John Chisholm1
2 CONT #     Thomas Chisholm1
2 CONT #     Jean Chisholm1
2 CONT #     Margaret Chisholm1
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT #     [S6275] David Malcolm, A Genealogical Memoir of the Most Noble and Ancient Hosue of Drummond and of the Several Branches That Have Sprung From it (Edinburgh, Scotland: Graham Maxwell, 1808), page 79. Hereinafter cited as Hos
2 CONC ue of Drummond.
2 CONT #     [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Ex
2 CONC tinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 517. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
