2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Montgomerie, 5th Earl of Eglinton [1]
2 CONT *M, #21507, 
2 CONT *b. 1584, 
2 CONT *d. 4 September 1612
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.11%
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Montgomerie, 5th Earl of Eglinton was born in 1584.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT A contract for the marriage of Hugh Montgomerie, 5th Earl of Eglinton and Margaret Montgomerie was signed circa 3 May 1604.[1] He and Margaret Montgomerie were separated in June 1608.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 4 September 1612, without issue.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Hugh Montgomerie, 4th Earl of Eglinton and Giles Boyd.[2],[3] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 6th Lord Montgomerie [S., 1445] in April 1586.[2] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 5th Earl of Eglinton [S., 1507] in April 1586.[1] 
2 CONT *He bought the monastic Barony of Kilwinning in 1594.[2] 
2 CONT *He was contracted to marry Gabriela, daughter of the 1st Duke of lennox, but she became a nun.[2] 
2 CONT *On 28 November 1611 he resigned the Earldom and lands of Eglinton to the Crown for Charter of novodamus, which united the territorial lordship and barony of Kilwinning with the territorial Earldom of Eglinton, in favour of himsel
2 CONC f and with remainder to his cousin, Sir Alexander Seton of Foulstruther.[2] 
2 CONT *His marriage to Margaret Montgomerie was annulled on 11 March 1612.[2]
2 CONT
