1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT == Robert Seton, 2nd Earl of Winton (c. 1583 – 1634) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Seton''' was the eldest son and heir of Robert Seton, 1st Earl of Winton, and Lady Margaret Montgomerie. He succeeded his father in March 1603 as the 2nd Earl of Winton and 9th Lord Seton.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In February 1603, he married Anne Maitland, daughter of John Maitland, 1st Lord Thirlestane. The marriage was famously troubled; contemporary accounts and later peerage works (such as ''Burke's'') record that Robert suffered from 
2 CONC severe mental incapacity or "madness" that manifested on his wedding night. Following a petition for divorce by his wife on the grounds of impotence and his ongoing incapacity, he was kept in seclusion at Seton Palace.
2 CONT
2 CONT Due to his condition, he resigned the Earldom and family estates on 26 June 1606 in favor of his younger brother, George Seton, who became the 3rd Earl of Winton. Robert remained under the care of his family until his death in Jan
2 CONC uary 1634. He died without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Immediate Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Parents:''' Robert Seton, 1st Earl of Winton and Lady Margaret Montgomerie.
2 CONT * '''Spouse:''' Anne Maitland (m. 1603; later divorced/separated).
2 CONT * '''Siblings:''' George Seton, 3rd Earl of Winton; Alexander Seton, 6th Earl of Eglinton; and Thomas Seton of Oliveestob.
2 CONT * '''Relationship to the Dunfermline Branch:''' He was the nephew of Alexander Seton, 1st Earl of Dunfermline, and a first cousin to Lady Jean Seton and Charles Seton, 2nd Earl of Dunfermline.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://thepeerage.com/p2146.htm#i21455  Lundy, Darryl. "Robert Seton, 2nd Earl of Winton," The Peerage]
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft/page/596/mode/2up Paul, James Balfour. The Scots Peerage, Vol. 8, p. 596]
2 CONT * Mosley, Charles. ''Burke's Peerage and Baronetage'', 107th edition, Vol. 1, p. 1280.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
