2 CONT George Seton, 3rd Earl of Winton [1]
2 CONT *M, #21456, 
2 CONT *b. December 1584, 
2 CONT *d. from 15 December 1650 to 17 December 1650
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=2.05%
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton, 3rd Earl of Winton was born in December 1584.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Lady Anne Hay, daughter of Francis Hay, 9th Earl of Erroll and Elizabeth Douglas, on 26 April 1609.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Hon. Elizabeth Maxwell, daughter of John Maxwell, 6th Lord Herries of Terregles and Elizabeth Maxwell, before 1628.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died from 15 December 1650 to 17 December 1650.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Robert Seton, 1st Earl of Winton and Lady Margaret Montgomerie.[1] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 8th Lord Seton [S., 1451] on 26 June 1606.[1] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Winton [S., 1600] on 26 June 1606.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Burgess of Glasgow in 1618.1 He held the office of Justice-General of St. Andrews.[1] 
2 CONT *He was Temporary President of the Council between December 1625 and March 1626.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Member of the Council of War in February 1628.[1] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland].[1]
2 CONT
