1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY MARGARET DOUGLAS Countess of Arran ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Margaret Douglas, here treated, is the eldest daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Douglas-3rd-Earl-of-Morton-1st-Earl-of-Arran/6000000003876555042?through=6000000002459946278 and his wife https://www.geni.com/peo
2 CONC ple/Catherine-Stewart-Countess-of-Morton/6000000006444422042?through=6000000002459946278. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/361/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 361]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Margaret Douglas married in about 23 September 1532 to James Hamilton, Earl of Arran, afterwards Governor of Scotland. She and her husband, on 31 May and 3 October 1560, confirmed entails in favour of James, fourth earl of
2 CONC  Morton dated 22 April 1543. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/361/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 361] She survived her husband, and was still alive in 1579. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pa
2 CONC ul/page/368/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 368]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 March 1528: Instrument of sasine narrating that James, earl of Mortoun, gave sasine to Margaret Douglas, his daughter, of the lands of Sanderyggis, in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh, reserving terce to Katherine Stewart. Witness
2 CONC es: William Grahym, William Trumbuyll, Adam Wachup, John Boide, William Sandelandis, John Nymmyll, John Dalgless and Thomas Knokkis. Notary - John Gray, M.A., Dunkeld. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details
2 CONC .aspx?reference=GD150%2f781&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=MARGARET+DOUGLAS&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/781]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 February 1532: Discharge by Sir James Hammyltoun of Fynnart to James, earl of Mortoun. for money promised for the marriage between James, earl of Arran, and Margaret Douglas, daughter of said earl of Mortoun. At Edinburgh. W
2 CONC itnesses: George bishop of Dunkeld, Mr. William Douglas, chancellor of Dunkeld brother german of the earl of Morton, and William Gibsoun, dean of Lestalrig. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refer
2 CONC ence=GD150%2f286&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=MARGARET+DOUGLAS&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/286]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 September 1532: REX concessit MARGARETE DOWGLAS filie Jacobi com. de Mortoun dom. de Dalkeith, in vitali redditu, — turrim et fortalicium de Kinneill, terras de Ovirtoun et Nethirtoun earundem, Burustoun et Burnstounnes, cum
2 CONC  salinis et carbonariis earundem, Westir-Kers, Est-feild de Kinneil, Kers, Inveravane, in baronia de Kinneill, vic. Linlithqw ; — quas Jacobus com. Arranie dom. Hammyltoun personaliter resignavit. [https://archive.org/details/regi
2 CONC strummagnisi03scot/page/267/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 1225]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 September 1532: Instrument narrating that in presence of sir Thomas Mailvile, parson of Hutoun and commissary of Mr. James Symsoun, parson of Kirkforthir and official of Lothian Margaret Douglas, daughter of James, earl of M
2 CONC ortoun, in sua virginitate, asked that Robert Douglas and John Gyffert should be given to her as curators, and when, this had been done, renounced in favour of the said earl her liferent of the lands of Colden Wester and Sanderygi
2 CONC s, in view of her infeftment in 500 merks from the barony of Kynneill. Done in the parish church of Natoun. Witnesses: sirs John Scot and George Kynloch, chaplains, Robert Ramsay, George Elwand and sir John Wilsoun, curatus of the
2 CONC  said church. Notaries - John Gray and John Scot. [Seal]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f287&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=MARGARET+DOUGLAS&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y Nati
2 CONC onal Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/287]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 October 1532: Discharge by Sir James Hammyltoun of Fynnar to Mr. Thomas Bannatyne, on behalf of James, earl of Mortoun, for a sum of money paid for the marriage of James, earl of Arrane, to Margaret Douglas, daughter of the 
2 CONC earl of Mortoun and now countess of Arrane. Dated at Edinburgh. Witnesses Mr. John Chepman, William Chepman, Donald Foulartoun and William Reche. Notaries - John Chepman and Thomas Mailvile. [Signature; seal]. [http://catalogue.nr
2 CONC scotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f288&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=MARGARET+DOUGLAS&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/288]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 May 1560: Ratification by James, duke of Chattellarault, Margaret Douglas, his spouse, and James, earl of Arrane, their son, of the charter and infeftment by deceased James, earl of Mortoun, to James, now earl of Mortoun, of
2 CONC  the earldom of Mortoun. (3 seals) (Reg.ii. 301). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f332&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=MARGARET+DOUGLAS&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y National Rec
2 CONC ords of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/332]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1563-64: Letter from Margaret [Douglas], countess of Arran to 'my veilbelovit freind the lairde of Dowhill', asking him for payment of the balance of 100 crowns which she gave to him and his wife 'that was the laird of
2 CONC  Lochlevinis sistar'. Written from Hamilton. Part of Countess's signature, very faint. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD254%2f644&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=MARGARET+DOUGLAS&ko=p&r=&r
2 CONC o=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Lindsay family of Dowhill, reference GD254/644]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage; founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of 
2 CONC that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume VI (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1909), 601 pp. For Douglas, Earl of Morton see pp. 337-87]
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage; founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of 
2 CONC that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume IV (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1907), 597 pp. For Hamilton, Duke of Hamilton see pp. 339-97] 
2 CONT
