2 CONT <blockquote>'''The existence of Lady Margaret Hamilton, here treated, is uncertain. She may sometimes have been confused with https://www.geni.com/people/Barbara-Hamilton/6000000002116134514 For the suggestion that it was Lady Bar
2 CONC bara Hamilton who married Alexander Gordon, rather than Lady Margaret Hamilton, see [http://www.thepeerage.com/p11034.htm#i110339 Darryl Lundy's Peerage] For the suggestion that it was Lady Margaret Hamilton who married Alexander 
2 CONC Gordon see [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/118/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs, p. 118]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Lady Margaret Hamilton is said to be the daughter of James Hamilton, Earl of Arran, and his wife Lady Margaret Douglas. According to James Anderson: "Lady Margaret, married to Alexander, Lord Gordon, eldest son of G
2 CONC eorge,fourth Earl of Huntly, who died before his father without issue." Anderson cites Wood's Peerage, Volume I, page 648, [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/118/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs, p. 118] but this is 
2 CONC not reflected in Sir James Balfour Paul's Peerage accounts. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou00paulgoog#page/n393/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, IV, p. 370] [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#page/536/mode/1
2 CONC up Ibidem, p. 536]'''</blockquote>
