1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LADY BARBARA HAMILTON===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Spurious Pedigree'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Lady Barbara Hamilton here treated may sometimes have been confused with https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Hamilton/6000000008427827761?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521039152867&through=6000000002116134514 For the s
2 CONC uggestion that it was Lady Margaret Hamilton who married Alexander, Lord Gordon, rather than Lady Barbara Hamilton, see [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/118/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs, p. 118]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Barbara Hamilton is the daughter of James, Earl of Arran, and his wife Lady Margaret Douglas. [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/118/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs, p. 118]  [https://archive.org/stream/scot
2 CONC speeragefou00paulgoog#page/n393/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, IV, p. 370] On 14 December 1553 she had a charter by which her father gave her an income from various lands for her lifetime. A charter of confirmation under the Great Se
2 CONC al of Scotland was issued on 21 December 1553. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/196/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-1580, charter number 877 on p. 196]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Barbara Hamilton married Alexander, Lord Gordon, who died shortly after 18 September 1552. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/536 The Scots Peerage IV: 536]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Barbara Hamilton married James, Lord Fleming, who, when he gave certain of his lands to her brother John on 15 January 1557, reserved his wife's terce therein. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/277/mo
2 CONC de/1up Ibidem, charter number 1237 on p. 277]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[http://www.thepeerage.com/p11034.htm#i110339 Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Barbara Hamilton]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Barbara Hamilton [1]
2 CONT *F, #110339
2 CONT *Last Edited=17 Jan 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=1.15%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Barbara Hamilton is the daughter of James Hamilton, 2nd Earl of Arran and Lady Margaret Douglas.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Alexander Gordon, Lord Gordon, son of George Gordon, 4th Earl of Huntly and Elizabeth Keith, circa 1546.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, James Fleming, 4th Lord Fleming before 23 December 1553.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT From circa 1546, her married name became Gordon. From before 23 December 1553, her married name became Fleming.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lady Barbara Hamilton and James Fleming, 4th Lord Fleming
2 CONT *1. Jean Fleming+[3] b. c 1554, d. 23 Jun 1609
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 4. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage,
2 CONC  106th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume VI, page 679. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *3. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 76.
2 CONT
