1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR WILLIAM HAMILTON OF SORN AND SANQUAR===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Hamilton of Sorn and Sanquar is said by John Anderson  to be the second son of Alexander Hamilton of Cambuskeith [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/382/mode/1up Memoirs of the House of Hamilton]
2 CONC  G. Harvey Johnston concurs. [https://archive.org/stream/heraldryofhamils00john#page/122/mode/1up Heraldry of the Hamiltons]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Chamberlain of Kelso===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Hamilton of Sanquar is noticed acting as Chamberlain of the Monastery of Kelso on 17 October 1536 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f2%2f9%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k
2 CONC =sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD40/2/9/5] and on 25 February 1536-37. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f2%2f10%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+hamiltoun&ko=p&r=&r
2 CONC o=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD40/2/10/4] and again on 13 October 1537. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f2%2f11%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD4
2 CONC 0/2/11/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Brother of John Hamilton of Cambuskeith===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 1 April 1538 William Hamilton, brother of John Hamilton of Cambuskeith, witnessed a precept of sasine made in favour of John Hamilton of Cambuskeith and his wife Janet Stewart. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlineca
2 CONC talogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f179%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hamilton+of+cambuskeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD1/179/1]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Contract with Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 January 1547: Contract between Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis, and William Hammyltoune of Sanchar, whereby the latter is 1) to give to the Earl a letter of reversion re wadset on lands of Barburstoun, etc., redeemable for 300 me
2 CONC rks; 2) to occupy, with Katherine Kennedy, his spouse, the lands of Glenmolt, etc. in liferent, maill-free, and 3) to continue, after expiry of tack of Balzett, etc. in kindly tenancy till ended by payment of 100 merks Scots [http
2 CONC ://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f2%2f92&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GTD25/2/92]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Judgement by Sir William Hammiltoun of Sanquhar===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Hamilton of Sanquar is noticed on 4 September 1551, sitting in judgement at the burgh court of Ayr.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f159&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&
2 CONC k=sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD86/159]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Witness to a decree of division concerning the marches of Seton and Preston===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 15 January 1552 he witnessed a decree of division concerning the marches of Seton and Preston. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f11%2f3%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ham
2 CONC ilton+of+sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD3/1/11/3/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Remission for certain indwellers of Perth===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 17 July 1553 William Hamilton of Sanquar signed a remission in favour of certain indwellers in Perth for failing to join the king's army. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f
2 CONC 43%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD112/43/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sasine Witness===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 8 August 1554 he witnessed an instrument of sasine made in favour of George Seton.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f11%2f1%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hamilton+of+s
2 CONC anchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD3/1/11/1/13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Hamilton of Sorn and Sanquar died before 5 April 1565, he date upon which his last will and testament is reported to have been registered [https://archive.org/stream/heraldryofhamils00john#page/122/mode/1up Heraldry
2 CONC  of the Hamiltons]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence published by the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT           1
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 June 1523: Letter of Reversion by William Hamilton of Maknariston and Katharine Kennedy his wife, to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis bearing the Earl having infeft them in the 40 shilling land of Barbiston and merk land of Brackenh
2 CONC ill, lying in the barony of Dalrymple, Kyle-regis, yet nevertheless they oblige them after the lapse of 3 years from the date of the said Letter, upon the Earl making payment to them, within the church of Ayr of the sum of 200 mer
2 CONC ks money of Scotland, that they shall resign in the hands of his Lordship and his successors the said lands of Barbiston and Brackenhill with all right and title which they had thereto and declare the same lawfully redeemed. Witne
2 CONC sses - Sir George Blair Chaplain, James Brown burgess of Ayr, and Adam Hamilton. Dated at Crossragwell. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f266&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=adam+h
2 CONC amilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/266]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 October 1536: Discharge by William Hammyltoun of Sanchar and chamberlain of Kelso to Sir William Ker for £20 Scots, for the teind sheaves of Litill Newtoun, for the Lammas term of 1535 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrs
2 CONC onlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f2%2f9%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Lothian papers, Volume IX. Fernieherst, reference GD40/2/9/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT           3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 February 1536-37: Discharge by William Hamiltoun of Sanchar, Chamberlain of Kelso, to William Ker, brother german to Andrew Ker of Farnyhirst, for £20 for teinds of Newtoun, and £5 for maills of Neddyr Howdane [http://catalo
2 CONC gue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f2%2f10%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+hamiltoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Lothian papers, Volume X. Fernieherst, referenc
2 CONC e GD40/2/10/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT           4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 Ocrober 1537: Discharge by William Hammyltoun of Sanchar, Chamberlain of Kelso, to Sir James Bolden, chaplain, in name of William Ker, brother german to the Laird of Farnyhyrst, for £20 Scots, for teinds of Little Newtoun [h
2 CONC ttp://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f2%2f11%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Lothian papers, Volume X. Fernieherst, refere
2 CONC nce GD40/2/11/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT           5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 April 1538: Precept of sasine by William Cunynghame [Cunningham], knight, fiar of the earldom of Glencarne and lord of Kilmawris [Kilmaurs] in favour of '''John Hammiltoun of Cambuskeith and Janet Stewart, his spouse''' of th
2 CONC e lands of Ovirmure and Carlingcraig in the lordship of Lowdoun [Loudoun], bailiwick of Cunynghame, and sheriffdom of Ayr. At Edinburgh, 1 Apr, 1538. Witnesses: Patrick Hammiltoun of Bogsyd [Bogside], William Hammiltoun, brother o
2 CONC f the said John Hammiltoun of Cambuskeith, Robert Ormstone [Ormiston], Sir James Walker, and Andrew McTene. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f179%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ham
2 CONC ilton+of+cambuskeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Birkwood writs, Lesmahagow, Lanarkshire, reference GD1/179/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT           6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 January 1547: Contract between Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis, and William Hammyltoune of Sanchar, whereby the latter is 1) to give to the Earl a letter of reversion re wadset on lands of Barburstoun, etc., redeemable for 300 me
2 CONC rks; 2) to occupy, with Katherine Kennedy, his spouse, the lands of Glenmolt, etc. in liferent, maill-free, and 3) to continue, after expiry of tack of Balzett, etc. in kindly tenancy till ended by payment of 100 merks Scots [http
2 CONC ://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f2%2f92&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ai
2 CONC lsa Muniments), reference GD25/2/92]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT           7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 September 1551: Instrument under the hand of Stephen Prestoune, clerk of the diocese of Glasgow, notary public, narrating that Donald Campbell and Thomas Kennedy, burgesses of Air, who each claimed right to the yard-dike betw
2 CONC een their respective tenements in the said burgh, with consent of their co-burgesses, elected, nominated and ordained William Hammiltoun of Sanchar, knight, to determine and decreet between them to whom the foresaid dike and the l
2 CONC and upon which it was built, pertained and obliged themselves to abide by his decision and to implement and observe it in all points: The said William Hammiltoun thereupon pronounced and decreed that the foresaid yard-dike and the
2 CONC  land upon which it was built pertained to the said Donald Campbell and his heirs, but providing that they should keep the said Thomas and his heirs scathless and unmolested in time coming. Done in the cemetery of the Friars Minor
2 CONC  of said burgh on 4th September 1551 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f159&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William F
2 CONC raser Charters, reference GD86/159]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT           8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 January 1552: Decree of division of marches between Seton and Perstoun by James Achesoune, Alexander of Halybrintoun, Alexander Adesoun and sir Alexander Kow, chplain judges arbiters chosen for George, Lord Seton, Thomas Hun
2 CONC tar, Walter Hall, Gilbert Lindsay and John Eddelwod, judges for David Hamilton of Fingaltoun, and laird of Perstoun, and Richard Maitland of Lethington, Master David Hamilton of Elistob and Alexander Hamilton in Prestoun, oversmem
2 CONC  chosen by both the parties Witnesses: William Hamilton of Sanchar, knight, David Crawfurd of Kers and others [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f11%2f3%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&t
2 CONC p=n&k=hamilton+of+sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earldom of Winton Bundle 1, reference GD3/1/11/3/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT           9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 July 1553: Componitur for remission in favour of Donald Myllar, Finlay McIntalyour, Malcolm McNachtane, John Tailyeour Moyr, David Toscheauche, Donald Myllar, Finlay McCarquhayre, Gillefillan McGown, John McOleass, Duncan Mc
2 CONC Aworycht, Andrew McAwarycht, Donald McIntalyeour, John McYndoir, Donald McEwyn, Donald McOlcallum, Duncan McRobert, Donald McInwellycht, Dougal McCarreis, Terlach McKillip, Archibald McInlay McNab, Patrick McGilleyerly, John McAne
2 CONC moir, Duncan Fure alias Wrycht, Duncan Moyr, John Moyr, his son, Donald McGillequhonell, John Campbell alias Leyche, Donald McKnewane, John McKynnead, Gillepatrick McColayne, Donald McPatrik, Patrick McCarbre, Donald McGilleyerg, 
2 CONC Duncan McCoule, Gillespie McAwyre, Gillechrist McIntalyeour, Donald McAine, John McInstalker, Donald McKynnead, Donald McCay, Donald McGillequhoan, John Dow McRobert, Donald Dow McNab, Finlay McKnewane, John McCallequhoan, Finlay 
2 CONC McKyndoir, Donald McCarar, Nicholas Flegeir, Duncan Talyour, Patrick Mcconache McCarbre, John Reouche McAldonycht, Donald McNachtane, indwellers within sheriffdom of Perth, for failing to join the king's army, and for all other cr
2 CONC imes laid to their charge. Signed by John, lord Erskine, William, abbot of Culross, and William Hamilton of Sanchar. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f43%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&
2 CONC tp=n&k=sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, State Papers, reference GD112/43/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT          10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 August 1554: Instrument of sasine in favour of George Seyton of the lands and baronies of Seton and Winton and Tranent under specified reservations. Witnesses: William Hamilton of Sanchar, attorney, Mr David Hamilton of Elist
2 CONC ob, sheriff in that part Witnesses: Arthur Hall of Foulbar, James Aldinstoun of that ilk, sir Hector Sinclair, sir Alexander Bow and sir George Adesouns, prebendaries of the collegiate church of Seton and others
2 CONT Thomas Raith, notary [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f11%2f1%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hamilton+of+sanchar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earldo
2 CONC m of Winton Bundle 1, reference GD3/1/11/1/13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 September 1662: BIRTH BRIEVE with the authority of the Privy Council in favour of Adam Cunningham (who is intending to travel to Germany), certifying that the late Adam Cunnyngham, a lieutenant of a company of soldiers in Ger
2 CONC many, the father of Adam Cunningham, the bearer of these presents, is descended from Alexander Cunningham of Cullelan in Scotland, and Joanna Maxwell, daughter of the baron of Newark, his father and mother; and the late Alexander 
2 CONC Cunnynghame of Cullellan, and Issobella Mure, daughter of (Sir) Adam Mure, knight of Rowallan, his granfather and grandmother ; and the late Sir William Cunnyngham of Capringtoun, baron and knight (whose fourth son the said Sir Al
2 CONC exander was), and Jonet Hamiltoun, daughter of Sir William (Hamilton) of Sarn, knight, his great-grandfather and great-grandmother ; and that the said lord of Capringtoun and his progemitors come of the very noble and powerful fam
2 CONC ily of William, Earl of Glencairne, Lord Cunyngham and Kilmaweris, the chief of the family of Cunnunghame, and chancellor of Scotland. P.R. v. 262. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=njp.32101073592006;view=1up;seq=170 Regist
2 CONC er of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1660-1668, number 318 on p. 162]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                                        _____________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes: The assertion for Sir William Hamilton being Lord High Treasurer of Scotland is probably in error. There are only two Hamiltons that were listed as having held the position:
2 CONT *1. John Hamilton (brother of Regent, Abbot of Paisley, later Bishop of St Andrews) held the position in 1546
2 CONT *2. William Hamilton, 3rd Duke of Hamilton, held the position in 1686 as part of a committee.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_High_Treasurer_of_Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT He did, however, hold the post of Lord Provost of Edinburgh (see below).
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT
2 CONT GENEALOGY: The Scots Peerage; Page 29; Vol 1; G929.72; P291sc; Denver
2 CONT
2 CONT Public Library; Genealogy
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Hamilton of Sanquhar, High Treasurer of Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on William Hamilton of Sorn and Sanquhar:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p11023.htm#i110229
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Hamilton of Sorn and Sanquhar [1]
2 CONT *M, #110229
2 CONT *Last Edited=12 May 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Hamilton of Sorn and Sanquhar held the office of High Treasurer [Scotland]. He lived at Sanquhar, Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir William Hamilton of Sorn and Sanquhar
2 CONT *1. Isabel Hamilton+[1] b. c 1529, d. 13 Nov 1604
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume X, page 291. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the List of Lord Provosts of Edinburgh:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Lord_Provosts_of_Edinburgh
2 CONT
2 CONT The Rt. Hon. The Lord Provost of Edinburgh is the convener of the City of Edinburgh local authority. He is elected by the city council and serves not only as the chair of that body, but as a figurehead for the entire city. He is e
2 CONC x officio the Lord-Lieutenant of Edinburgh. He is equivalent in many ways to the institution of Mayor that exists in many other countries.
2 CONT
2 CONT While some of Scotland's local authorities elect a Provost, only the four main cities (Glasgow, Edinburgh, Aberdeen and Dundee) have a Lord Provost. In Edinburgh this position dates from 1667, when Charles II elevated the Provost 
2 CONC to the status of Lord Provost, with the same rank and precedence as the Lord Mayor of London. The title of Lord Provost is enshrined in the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994. The current Lord Provost is George Grubb, Liber
2 CONC al Democrat councillor for Almond ward.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lord Provost of Edinburgh is virtue officii Admiral of the Firth of Forth, the Provost of Leith is Admiral of the port thereof.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Provosts of Edinburgh
2 CONT
2 CONT *(1376) John de Quhitnes
2 CONT *...
2 CONT *(1551) William Craik
2 CONT *(1555) Sir William Hamilton of Sanquhar
2 CONT *(1554) Archibald Douglas of Kilspindie
2 CONT
2 CONT James Stewart, Earl of Arran held the lands for a time, however they passed to the Wallaces of Craigie and in 1583-4 it is recorded that William Wallace of Ellerslie held the lands of Mains of Helentoun and Bogend, together with t
2 CONC he tower, fortalice, and manor place of Helenton, together with half of the mill.[14]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:
2 CONT *13. ^ Paterson, Page 748
2 CONT *14. ^ Paterson, Page 749
2 CONT
2 CONT Paterson, James (1863–66). History of the Counties of Ayr and Wigton. V. - II - Kyle. Edinburgh: J. Stillie.
