2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 June 1523: Letter of Reversion by William Hamilton of Maknariston and Katharine Kennedy his wife, to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis bearing the Earl having infeft them in the 40 shilling land of Barbiston and merk land of Brackenh
2 CONC ill, lying in the barony of Dalrymple, Kyle-regis, yet nevertheless they oblige them after the lapse of 3 years from the date of the said Letter, upon the Earl making payment to them, within the church of Ayr of the sum of 200 mer
2 CONC ks money of Scotland, that they shall resign in the hands of his Lordship and his successors the said lands of Barbiston and Brackenhill with all right and title which they had thereto and declare the same lawfully redeemed. Witne
2 CONC sses - Sir George Blair Chaplain, James Brown burgess of Ayr, and Adam Hamilton. Dated at Crossragwell. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f266&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=adam+h
2 CONC amilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/266]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Book of Gavin Ros===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 October 1530: Instrument narrating that Adam Hamiltoun, brother-german of William Hamiltoun of Sanquhar, in name of and as procurator for his brother, as he asserted, compearing in the Tolbooth of the burgh of Air, required J
2 CONC ohn Craufurd of Drongan and James Taite, justiciars deputed in the action of perambulation moved between the burgesses and inhabitants of the burgh of Prestwick on one part and the said William H. on the other, concerning the divi
2 CONC sion of lands of property of Prestwick, lands of Sanquhar and of Clune, to give to Adam, in name of William H. an authentic copy of the commission in said cause, directed to said James (and John) in the behalf, which John Craufurd
2 CONC  and James Taite declared they had not the commission at the present time, because the opposing party had obtained it, as they assert, upon which Adam, in nameof William protested that it should not prejudice the latter. [https://
2 CONC archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso10scotuoft#page/194/mode/1up Protocol Book of Gavin Ros, N.P.,  1512-1532, Edited by the Reverend John Anderson, Curator of the Historical Department, H.M. General Register House, and Francis J. 
2 CONC Grant, W.S., (Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1908), protocol number 1067 on p. 194]'''
