2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 May 1574: Instrument of Seisin in favour of Alexander Earl of Glencairn, son and heir of William and grandson and heir of Cuthbert Earls of Glencairn, in the 5 merk land of Langmuir the lands of Alton Tilwood and Newlands (L
2 CONC ambrochton Third Part "Twa Hills") and annualrent of 2 shillings payable from Newlands, all lying in the barony of Kilmaurs and formerly wadset by Cuthbert and William Earls of Glencairn to Hugh Earl of Eglinton deceased (See GD39
2 CONC /1/36) and redeemed by the said Alexander Earl of Glencairn from Hugh then Earl of Eglinton [mentioned in the precept William Cunningham of Caprington, son and heir of the late John Cunningham of Caprington, Adam Cunningham brothe
2 CONC r german of the said William, witnesses to the instrument William Cunningham in Irvine], grandson and heir of the said Hugh Earl of Eglinton proceeding on a precept from Chancery dated 20 May 1574. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov
2 CONC .uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f76&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+cunningham+of+caprington&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/76]'''
2 CONT
