2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Please note that the quote below does NOT refer to Thomas Kennedy 5th Laird of Bargany. The correct web address for the quote below is http://www.electricscotland.com/history/domestic/    then look up Reign of King James VI part
2 CONC  D.   The quote below is dated 7th November 1597. Thomas Kennedy 5th of Bargany was dead by this time. His son also called Thomas became 6th Laird of Bargany''''''  from Stephen Johnson (Thomas Kennedy 5th of Bargany was my 11 x g
2 CONC reat grandfather)
2 CONT
2 CONT see   Notes
2 CONT * '.... it pleased God to tak the Laird of Bargeny in his mercy; wha was the nobillest man that ever was in that country [Carrick] in his time. He was endued with mony guid virtues. First he fearit God, and was fra the beginning o
2 CONC n the right side of religion. He was wise and courteous, and therewith stout and passing kind; and sic ane noble spender in outings with the best-halden house at hame that ever was in the land. He was never behind with na party, a
2 CONC nd keepit himself ever to the fore with his living. He had ever in his household twenty-four gallant gentlemen, double-horsit, and gallantly clad; with sic ane repair to his house, that it was ane wonder where the same was gotten 
2 CONC that he spendit [4, 5]
2 CONT
