2 CONT
2 CONT '''21  March 1623: Decreet of lords of council and session i.c. Dorothy Stewart, relict of Thomas Kennedie, sometime of Drummurchie, and Mr. James Inglis, minister at Daylie, her spouse, v. Thomas Kennedie of Barganie, son of dece
2 CONC ased Gilbert Kennedie of Barganie, narrating contract, 19 August, 1597, between said Gilbert and said deceased Thomas, his brother, whereby said Gilbert warranted to said Thomas, lands of Ardrossane, to be worth annualrent of 400 
2 CONC merks scots, till redemption thereof by Hew, earl of Eglintoun, when other lands are to be substituted, whereby said lords decern that said Dorothy has right to make requisition of sums remaining unpaid by said Thomas Kennedie of 
2 CONC Barganie. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f481&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drummurchie&ko=a&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-H
