1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN GRAHAM OF KNOCKDOLIAN===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Graham of Knockdolian married Dame Helen Kennedy, the widow of Hugh Montgomery, Earl of Eglinton, and Alexander Kennedy of Craigneill. She was his future wife on 25 April 1583.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrso
2 CONC nlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2660&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: RH6/2660]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the Third Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Graham/6000000086733905824?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1548857546438&through=6000000024091778829
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Graham/6000000086733575984?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1548857681111&through=6000000024091778829
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Helen-Graham/6000000086732679308?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1548857814912&through=6000000024091778829
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1583: Charter under Great Seal confirming a charter by Robert Grahame of Knokdoliane granting to John Grahame, his son and apparent heir and to Helen Kennedy, his future spouse, lawful daughter of Thomas Kennedy of Bar
2 CONC gany and the survivor of them in conjunct fee and the heirs to be lawfully begotten betwixt them, whom failing to said John's heirs male whomsoever, in implement of a marriage contract dated [ ] in the £10 lands of Craig, £5 lands
2 CONC  of Milanerdaill, 40 shilling lands called Ballaird and Altikaine, half merk land of Drumwachty (or Drumuauchtane), with mill and mill lands thereof, £10 lands of Auchindraine with manor place, mill and mill lands thereof, £10 lan
2 CONC ds of Ballachthrull (or Ballochtrule) and Corvar, 5 merk 10s lands of Tomlothre (or Tomlothie), Monunsioun and Balluig (or Moling), with manor, towers, fortalices, yards, orchards, tenants, tenandries and services of free tenants 
2 CONC thereof all lyng in the earldom of Carrick, sheriffdom of Air. To be held a me of the King rendering therefor service ought and wont. Reserving to said Robert the liferent of Craig, Ballaird, Altikane, Drumwachty, Auchindraine, To
2 CONC mlothre, Monunsioun and Balluig, Ballachthoull and Corvar. With precept of sasine addressed to James McCornok. Witnesses to the confirmed charter Barnard Fergusson of Kilkerran, Simon Fergusson, his son, Adam Hog and John Kennedy,
2 CONC  servitors of Thomas Kennedy of Barganye Witnesses to the charter of Confirmamus (which contains a clause of novodamus), Colin, Earl of Argyll, Lord Campbell and Lorne, Chancellor and Jusice General, Patrick, Archbishop of St Andr
2 CONC ews, Robert, commendator of Dunfermline, the King's secretary, Walter, commendator of Blantyre, Keeper of the Privy Seal, Alexander Hay of Eister Kennet, Clerk of the Rolls, Register and Council, Lewis Bellenden of Auchnoule, knig
2 CONC ht, Justice Clerk, Robert Scott, Director of Chancery [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2660&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/2660]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 May 1590: Contract of marriage between Thomas Kennedy of Bargeny and Dame Helen Kennedy, Countess of Eglinton, his daughter on one part and John Graham of Knockdolian on the other part, whereby John Graham of Knockdolian obli
2 CONC ges himself to infeft his future wife in liferent in various lands therein specified, and in general in all the lands and heritages of which he is now possessed or shall be possessed during his marriage, and that the male heir of 
2 CONC the marriage shall succeed him in all his lands, the said Dame Helen being obliged to maintain him during her lifetime at the rate of one third of the rent of the lands to be liferented by her; and if there is only a female heir o
2 CONC f the marriage then John shall be obliged to pay to her £6000 when she reaches the age of 14, if two daughters then 10,000 merks, and if three or more then £10,000 equally amongst them; for which causes Thomas obliges him to pay 5
2 CONC 000 merks of tocher at the terms and in the manner specified. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f1%2f5%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt
2 CONC =1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/B/1/5/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 September 1591: Letters of reversion granted by Dame Helen Kennedy, Countess of Eglinton with the consent of John Graham of Knockdolian, then her spouse in favour of Hugh, 5th Earl of Eglinton and Robert, Master of Eglinton,
2 CONC  his tutor whereby that they agree on payment being made to them of 4000 merks, within the parish kirk of Ayr they would discharge the annualrent of 400 merks furth of the Barony of Ardrossan. Dated at Anstruther. Witnesses: Alexa
2 CONC nder Kennedy, younger of Bargany, Hugh Kennedy of Bennane amd others. 2 pendant seals of Dame Helen Kennedy and John Graham of Knokdolian, poor impressions. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refer
2 CONC ence=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f1%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/1/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 May 1600: Contract of Alienation between John Grahame of Knokdoliane, with consent of Dame Helen Kennedy, Countess of Eglinton, his spouse and John McAlexander of Dalreoch, as son and heir of deceased Fargus McAlexander of D
2 CONC alreoch, whereby said John Grahame binds himself to infeft said John McAlexander in the 30s. land of Greirstoun and Quhytfarding, in parish of Colmonell, earldom of Carrick and sheriffdom of Ayr [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk
2 CONC /nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD27%2f1%2f45&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Kennedy of Dalquharran Writs and Inventories, reference GD27/1/45]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 June 1614: Discharge by Anna Graham, lawful daughter of the deceased Sir John Graham of Knockdolian having reached 21 years of age, in favour of John, Earl of Montrose as principal and Robert Graham of Gartmore as cautioner,
2 CONC  of the sum of 5000 merks which the Earl and Robert Graham had, by their bond dated at Glasgow 5 Nov 1607, obliged themselves to make forthcoming to her by Robert Graham of Grugar, now of Auchincloich, in full satisfaction of all 
2 CONC her rights through the decease of her father, Sir John or the decease of her grandfather, Robert Graham of Knockdolian, as one of their heirs portioners; discharging the said Earl and his cautioner of the said bond and the said Ro
2 CONC bert Graham of Auchincloich; at Glasgow. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f7%2f6%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+john+graham+of+knockdolian&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y N
2 CONC ational Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/A/7/6/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 June 1614: Discharge by Robert Graham of Auchincloich and Robert Graham his son with consent of his curators, in favour of John, Earl of Montrose as principal and Robert Graham of Gartmore as cautioner, of an obligation gran
2 CONC ted by them obliging them to cause Anna Graham, eldest lawful daughter of Sir John Graham of Knockdolian, upon reaching 21 years of age, to renounce (as one of the three heirs portioners of the said Sir John and Robert, his father
2 CONC ) in favour of the said Robert Graham of Auchincloich her right as heir foresaid, and granting them to have received the said renunciation from the said Anna Graham in the terms of the obligation; at Glasgow. [http://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f7%2f6%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+john+graham+of+knockdolian&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Duke
2 CONC s of Montrose, reference GD220/1/A/7/6/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 December 1618: Extract bond by Robert Graham younger of Auchincloich in favour of William Montgomery of Bridgend for £8000, and that in satisfaction of several sums paid to Robert's creditors: 5000 merks to Helen Graham, law
2 CONC ful daughter to Sir John Graham of Knockdolian and 4000 merks to Margaret Graham, sister to the said Robert and 500 merks to John Graham, natural son to the said Sir John etc; dated 30 Dec 1618 and registered in the Books of Sessi
2 CONC on 25 Mar 1620. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f1%2f1%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+john+graham+of+knockdolian&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotla
2 CONC nd, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose , reference GD220/1/B/1/1/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
