2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 September 1617: Extract contract of marriage between Hew Kennedie of Girvanemaynes, with consent of Anna Kennedie, his spouse, and Hew Kennedie, their eldest son, on the one part, and Thomas Kennedie of Bargany, with consent
2 CONC  of Josias Stewart of Bonytoune, his tutor, and Helen Kennedie, his sister, on the other part, for the marriage of the said Hew, younger, and Helen. Hew, elder, to infeft Hew, younger, and Helen in the 11 mark lands of Montgomries
2 CONC toune, McCroreistoune, McInvainstoune and Fardinewilliame in the parish of Kirkmichaell, the 9 mark lands of Dalquhorrane, 40/- lands of Thang, Mylne of Daljerberie in the parish of Dallie, 20/- lands of Dalquhornell in parish of 
2 CONC Calmonell, mark land of Glaik in parish of Girvane, and Mylne of Girvane Maynes in the parish of Kirkoswald, all in the earldom of Carrick, with some liferent reservations to '''the said Hew, elder, and Anna''' Registered: B. of C
2 CONC . and S., 16 December 1633. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD180%2f197&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hew+kennedie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ca
2 CONC thcart Family of Genoch and Knockdolian, reference GD180/197]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Date unknown: Minute of agreement between Sir John Hammiltoun of Lettrik on one part, and Josias Strewart of Ravinstoune, Margaret Stewart, lady Bargany his daughter, and Thomas, James and [blank] Kennedy, children of said Marg
2 CONC aret and Thomas Kennedy of Bargany, her spouse on other part, whereby said Josias and Margaret ratify contract of alienation of lands and barony of Bargany in favour of said Sir John; with notes of information thereanent. [http://
2 CONC catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f40&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+kennedy+of+bargany&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1620&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrympl
2 CONC e-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/40]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT 26 October 1619: Revocation by Thomas Kennedy of Bargany of all infeftments, charters, contracts, bonds etc., etc., made by him in favour of Margaret Stewart, daughter of Josias Stewart of Bonyntoun, his spouse and of William Stew
2 CONC art of Dunduff, especially their marriage contract in so far as it may be extended to all infeftments in favour of his said spouse and heirs of said marriage, and contract of tack GD109/23 tending to my [said Thomas's] utter wrak 
2 CONC and skaith. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f24&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+kennedy+of+bargany&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1620&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of th
2 CONC e family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/24]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 June 1622: Signet letters at instance of Sir John Hammiltoun of Lettrik, kt., charging Josias Stewart of Bonytoun, now called of Blairquhan to answer for his intromissions as tutor of T'homas Kennedy of Bargany and as execut
2 CONC or of deceased Jean Stewart, mother of said Thomas, sister of Josias.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f60&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+kennedy+of+bargany&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1
2 CONC 620&dt=1630&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/60]'''
2 CONT
