1 NAME Jonete /Maxwell/ Lady Boyd
2 GIVN Jonete
2 SURN Maxwell
2 NSFX Lady Boyd
2 _MARNM Maxwell
2 NICK Mariota
1 SEX F
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 18 JUN 1471 AND 16 JUN 1474
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JONETE MAXWELL (aka MARIOTA MAXWELL) Lady Boyd ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jonete Maxwell, here treated, is reported to be the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Maxwell-of-Calderwood/6000000019658638370 and his first wife https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Borthwick-Lady-Calderwood/600000
2 CONC 0011080081469?through=6000000006444357850. She is identified as Mariota Maxwell in both the Maxwell Memoirs [https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/465/mode/1up Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock I: 465] and the Sc
2 CONC ots Peerage, although the evidence cited by the Scots Peerage identifies her as Jonete Maxwell. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/145 The Scots Peerage V: 145]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jonete Maxwell, here treated, was alive on 18 June 1471, [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof08scot/page/53 Exchequer Rolls VIII: 53] but she died before 16 June 1474. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof08sco
2 CONC t/page/241 Ibidem: 241] The Marquis of Ruvigny was of the opinion that she died early in 1473: "She died after 25 June 1472, apparently early in 1473. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/145 The Scots Peer
2 CONC age V: p. 145]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jonete Maxwell, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Boyd-1st-Lord-Boyd-of-Kilmarnock/6000000000642082925?through=6000000006444357850: "and was by him mother of the first Earl of Arran, and Elizabeth Countes
2 CONC s of Angus". [https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/465/mode/1up Maxwell Memoirs I: 465]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 June 1471: Computum Rogeri de Foultoune et Johannis Dunlop, serjandorum dominii de Stewartoune, redditum apud Edinburgh decimo octavo die mensis Junii anno Domini etc. septuagesimo primo . . . . . et eisdem, per solucionem f
2 CONC actam Jonete Maxwell, sponse Roberti olim domini Boid predicti, et Jonete Kennedy, sponse quondam Alexandri Boid, militis, percipientibus annuatim de firmis dictarum terrarum de Stewartoune quadraginta libras, videlicet qualibet e
2 CONC arum viginti libras, ex gracia domini regis, de tribus ultimis terminis hujus computi, lx It. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof08scot/page/53 Exchequer Rolls VIII: 53]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 June 1474: Compotum Rogeri de Foultoune et Johannis Dunlop, serjandorum dominii de Stewartoune, [Edinburgh, 16 June  1474, from 25 June 1462] . . . . . Et per solucionem factam Jonete Maxwele, quondam sponse Roberti Boide, e
2 CONC x gracia domini regis, de primo termino hujus compoti. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof08scot/page/241 Exchequer Rolls VIII: 241]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/n6/mode/1up Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock, Vol. I. Memoirs & Charters (Edinburgh 1863), 497 pp.]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev200fras#page/n6/mode/1up Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock, Vol. II. Correspondence (Edinburgh 1863), 453 pp.]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/136 The Scots Peerage V: pp. 136-82]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes and Comments ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # married about 1445 in Calderwood, Lanark, Scotland to Thomas Boyd, 1st Lord Boyd (c 1425-c 1482)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 	
2 CONT # Thomas Boyd, Earl of Arran,  b. 1446, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland ,  d. Abt 1473, Antwerp, Brabant, Belgium, Netherlands 
2 CONT # Elizabeth Boyd,  b. Abt 1448, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland ,  d. Bef 1498
2 CONT # Sir. Alexander Boyd, Baron,  b. Abt 1452, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland ,  d. 23 Nov 1508
2 CONT # Archibald Boyd,  b. Abt 1454, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland , d. Bef 4 May 1507
2 CONT # John Boyd,  b. Abt 1456, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland
2 CONT # Annabella Boyd,  b. Abt 1460, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland
2 CONT # Margaret Boyd,  b. Abt 1462, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke's Peerage is not sure whether this person is named Janet or Mariota.  See below for an indication that there may have been two sisters, a Mariota and a Janet, that married different people--or the Mariota/Janet that married 
2 CONC Robert, 1st Lord Boyd came from a later generation of Maxwell as indicated by Burke's (see discussion below about inconsistancies in Burke's lineage) and the Mariota/Janet of this generation married William Porteous. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke's has a fairly major screw up with the ancestors of Mariota/Janet. In the Kilmarnock, Baron line which contains the Boyd lineage, the marriage of Robert, 1st Lord Boyd to Janet or Mariota Maxwell is given. Burke's states tha
2 CONC t Mariota/Janet's father is Robert Maxwell of Calderwood described in the Farnham, Baronet line.
2 CONT
2 CONT Under the Farnham line where the Maxwell of Calderwood line age is given, one would expect to find a Robert Maxwell of Calderwood with a daughter Mariota/Janet who married Robert, 1st Lord Boyd. Not only one, but two different gen
2 CONC erations, one (Robert) the grandson of the other (John), supposedly had daughters that married the "1st Lord Boyd".
2 CONT
2 CONT The "Robert" (grandson, who had an un-named daughter marrying 1st Lord Boyd) died in 1531 while his supposed daughter Mariota/Janet died by early 1473--58 years earlier?--not likely. The grandfather (John), which names his daughte
2 CONC r Mariota/Janet marrying 1st Lord Boyd, is the son of a marriage of 4 Dec 1450 and is dead by 1490--again born to a marriage and died way too late for Mariota/Janet and the wrong name (John-not Robert)! To compound matters, this "
2 CONC John" married Janet/Marion Boyd daughter of Thomas Boyd 5th Lord of Kilmarnock (who also happens to be father of Mariota/Janet's husband Robert, 1st Lord Boyd)-therefore having Mariota/Janet Maxwell marrying her mother's brother!
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a Robert Maxwell of Calderwood, married 1402, grandfather of the "John" and great great grandfather of the "Robert", who seems to be perfect--but in a screwed-up lineage, who knows? I have designated this Robert Maxwell o
2 CONC f Calderwood as father of Mariota/Janet and discounted the other Robert and John.
2 CONT
2 CONT My impression is that all of the mistakes are in the Farnham line--not in the Kilmarnock line.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://thepeerage.com/p20591.htm#i205908 Genealogy Proposed by Darryl Lundy's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Maxwell [1]
2 CONT *F, #205908
2 CONT *Last Edited=17 Sep 2006
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Maxwell married Sir William Carlyle, 2nd Lord Carlyle of Torthorwald, son of John Carlyle, Master of Carlyle, before 12 July 1487.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She is the daughter of John Maxwell, Master of Maxwell and Janet Crichton.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 12 July 1487, her married name became Carlyle.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Janet Maxwell and Sir William Carlyle, 2nd Lord Carlyle of Torthorwald
2 CONT *1. James Carlyle, 3rd Lord Carlyle of Torthorwald [1] d. b 15 Jan 1525/26
2 CONT *2. Michael Carlyle, 4th Lord Carlyle of Torthorwald+[1] d. Jun 1575
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 41. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
