1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ARCHIBALD BOYD OF BONSHAW (formerly ARCHIBALD BOYD OF NAIRSTON)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Archibald Boyd of Bonshaw is the second son of Robert, first Lord Boyd, and Lady Mariota Maxwell. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05paul#page/145/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 145-6] According to the Marquis of Ruvi
2 CONC gny, he is noticed for the first time on 7 August 1492. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05paul#page/145/mode/1up Ibidem: 145] This date is wrong, however. He is in fact noticed as: "Archibaldo Boyd de Narstoune" on 7 A
2 CONC ugust 1492, in the witness list of a discharge issued by Cuthbert, Lord Kilmaurs. [https://archive.org/details/douglasbookf03fras/page/135/mode/1up The Douglas Book. Vol IIII: charter number 130 on pp. 135-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Archibald Boyd of Bonshaw died before 4 May 1507. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05paul#page/146/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 46]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT
2 CONT Archibald Boyd of Bonshaw was born in 1454 at Kilmarnock, Renfrewshire, Scotland and died before May 1507.
2 CONT * Parents: Robert Boyd, 1st Lord Boyd of Kilmarnock (1485-1482) and Mariot Maxwell (1430-1472)
2 CONT # Married: Abt 1469 of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland to Christian Mure (1448-1523)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 	
2 CONT # Robert Boyd,  b. Abt 1470, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland ,  d. Bef 28 Jan 1523  
2 CONT # Miss Boyd,  b. Abt 1471, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland , 
2 CONT # Elizabeth Boyd, Countess of Loch,  b. Abt 1475, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland , 
2 CONT # Marion Boyd, Concubine of James IV, King of Scots.  b. Abt 1477, of, Bonshaw, Dumfries, Scotland,  d. Bef 31 Aug 1559
2 CONT #  Patrick Boyd,  b. Abt 1477, of, Kilmarnock, Ayr, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT # [S323] Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots Peerage: founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's The Peerage of Scotland (Edinburgh, Scotland: David Douglas, 1904), volume I, page 22. Hereinafter cited as The Scots Peerage.
2 CONT # [S1322] David Arathoon, "re: Acheson Family and Campbell Family," e-mail message to Darryl Lundy, 8 April 2005 - 14 July 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Acheson Family and Campbell Family."
2 CONT
