1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ADAM BOYD ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adam Boyd, here treated, is not mentioned in the Scots Peerage account of the family of Robert, Lord Boyd, and his wife Mariota Maxwell, [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/142/mode/1up The Scots Peerag
2 CONC e V: pp. 142-47] or in Stirnet's review of the published histories. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/boyd1.php Stirnet: Boyd 1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT From: "Mike Boyd" <mikejboyd@bigpond.com>  Subject: [BOYD] A new 6th Son for 1st Lord Robert Boyd - Adam Boyd and his second wife Joan Cuthbert who moved to Leeds, England.  Date: Thu, 28 May 2009 15:07:33 +1000
2 CONT
2 CONT I was given this family from a scroll that Linda Fairlie from the East  Ayrshire Council showed me in 2007 and gave a copy to me in May 2009.
2 CONT
2 CONT There was no date on this scoll - but it was on A4 page size, suggesting it  was done in the last 20 to 30 years - nor was there any name of the  researcher. This tree scroll spans 13 generations but has very little data  in ways 
2 CONC of dates and very few locations. Linda was uncertain when this  scroll was given to Dean Castle staff.
2 CONT
2 CONT It starts with an Adam Boyd born 1460, youngest son of Robert Boyd 1st Lord  Boyd (1414-1480) and Joan Cuthbert, 2nd wife) moved to Leeds, England his  home Kirk Bielston.
2 CONT
2 CONT This linkage to Adam Boyd son of first Lord Boyd - Robert Boyd - is  uncertain. When I first saw this I thought it was Adam Boyd of the Penkill  family which descends from Lord Robert Boyd's second son Alexcander Boyd.
2 CONT
2 CONT This tree would suggest that there was a NEW sixth son for the first Lord  Robert Boyd after his sons Robert [J0]; Thomas Boyd [J1]; Alexander [J2];  Archibald [J3] and John [J4], who was born in 1460.
2 CONT
2 CONT I would like to get in contact with the researcher who supplied this family  scroll to Dean Castle?
2 CONT
2 CONT This may be another reason why there are a number of Boyd families in NE  England including in Yorkshire. And it may explain why the 9th Lord Boyd  married someone from Newcastle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thank you Mike Boyd Historical Committee, HBS
2 CONT
2 CONT From: "Mike Boyd" <mikejboyd@bigpond.com>  Subject: Re: [BOYD] A new 6th Son for 1st Lord Robert Boyd - Adam Boyd andhis second wife Joan Cuthbert who moved to Leeds, England.  Date: Fri, 29 May 2009  Thanks Lauren. I had not thou
2 CONC ght about the paper supply aspect. So this would now suggest it was an UK or perhaps Australian or New Zealand source who provided this tree to Dean Castle - some time over the last 20 years or so..
2 CONT
2 CONT When I write this family chapter up, I will be careful about its introduction.
2 CONT
2 CONT I only arrived home on Tuesday, and still have to sorted out my papers. But I hope that in a few weeks to be able to search the IGI family connections in the IGI and to post the "given" generations to seeif anyone can connect to t
2 CONC hem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mike Boyd Historical Committee, HBS
2 CONT
2 CONT ----- Original Message <nowiki>-----</nowiki>  From: Lauren Boyd  To: Mike Boyd  Cc: ayrshire@rootsweb.com ; BOYD@rootsweb.com  Sent: Friday, May 29, 2009 3:28 AM Subject: Re: [BOYD] A new 6th Son for 1st Lord Robert Boyd - Adam B
2 CONC oyd and his second wife Joan Cuthbert who moved to Leeds, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mike:
2 CONT
2 CONT If I am following.... there were no sources for the information provided? So... this is THEORY and WISHFUL THINKING at this point in time? A sign post for more research?
2 CONT
2 CONT A4 would also suggest it was not submitted by an American. That is not a standard USA paper size.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aye,
2 CONT
2 CONT Lauren
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://news.rootsweb.com/th/read/BOYD/2009-05/1243552344
