1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == WILLIAM CUNNINGHAM Earl of Glencairn ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cunningham, 4th Earl of Glencairn; born about 1493;He was the son of Cuthbert Cuninghame, 3rd Earl of Glencairn and Lady Marion Douglas.2 He married (1) before 10 Jul 1509 to Katherine Borthwick (died after 17 Jan 1527/28)
2 CONC , daughter of William, 3rd Lord Borthwick; married (2) after Jan 1535/36 to Margaret or Elizabeth Campbell, daughter of John of West Loudoun and/or Stephenson. William died in Mar 1547/48.
2 CONT
2 CONT William was knighted before 10 July 1509. He was High Treasurer of Scotland in 1526 and went on an embassy to France in 1538. He was taken prisoner by the English after the Scottish defeat at the Battle of Solway Moss in late 1542
2 CONC , but was ransomed for £1000. In 1543, William was appointed plenipotentiary to negotiate a peace with England, and he became a promoter of English interests in Scotland and received a pension from the English. He was defeated by 
2 CONC the Earl of Arran in 1544 and had to flee to England with his eldest son. Nevertheless, he deserted the English cause in autumn 1544 (the English Lord Chancellor complained of the deceit of 'the old fox and his cub'). The Scottish
2 CONC  Parliament granted his a remission from all his treasons at the end of 1544, and he became a Privy Councillor in 1545. He was an early supporter of Protestantism in Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 - It is known that William had issue by both marriages but, other than to note that most of the children noted appeared to be adult by the time of the second marriage, it is not clear who if any of these was by the second marria
2 CONC ge.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sources 	
2 CONT # [S265] Colquoun_Cunningham.ged, Jamie Vans
2 CONT # [S295] Kennedy of Bargany Family History Report and other reports
2 CONT # [S280] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Cunningham02: The Scots Peerage (Glencairn), Burkes Extinc t Peerages 1883 (Cuningham of Kilmaurs and Glencairn), Burk es Peerages 1934 (Cuninghame of Corsehill). (Reliability: 3)
2 CONT # [S260] Burke's Landed Gentry of Great Britain 2001, Peter Beauclerk Dewar,, (2001.)
2 CONT # [S278] The Cuninghame family of Glencairn, Suzanne Doig
2 CONT # [S280] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Ferguson02 (Reliability: 3)
2 CONT # [S280] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Campbell01 (Reliability: 3) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT
2 CONT # http://webspace.webring.com/people/gu/um_8463/gene/glencairn.htm
2 CONT # http://thepeerage.com/p2853.htm#i28523
2 CONT # http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I2302&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cunningham-2058
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William "Fourth Earl of Glencairn" Fourth Earl of Glencairn formerly Cunningham Born 24 Mar 1493 in Glencairn, Dumfries-shire, Scotlandmap Son of Cuthbert Cunningham and Marion (Douglas) Cunningham Brother of Margaret Bellenty
2 CONC ne and	Alexander Cunningham Husband of Catherine (Borthwick) Cunningham — married [date unknown] [location unknown] Husband of Elizabeth Campbell — married Jan 1535 [location unknown] Father of Isabel Cuninghame of Glencairn, Andr
2 CONC ew Cunningham, Alexander (Cunningham) Fifth Earl of Glencairn, Janet Cunyngham and	Lady Elizabeth Cunningham Died 11 Mar 1548 in Battle of Pinkie, Musselburgh, Midlothian, Scotlandmap Profile manager: Terri Rick private message [s
2 CONC end private message] Cunningham-2058 created 18 Jun 2013 | Last modified 27 Jul 2016 This page has been accessed 1,369 times.
2 CONT
2 CONT Categories: Battle of Pinkie Cleugh | Earls of Glencairn | Clan Cunningham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clan Cunningham tartan.	William (Cunningham) Fourth Earl of Glencairn is a member of Clan Cunningham. If you are interested in this profile, please check out the Scottish Clans Project!
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cunningham (Cunninghame) was a Scottish nobleman and the Fourth Earl of Glencairn. He was active in the intriguing affairs of 16th century Scotland. His loyalties switched from Scottish to those of the English and later ba
2 CONC ck to Scottish.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in 1493. William Cunningham was the only son of Cuthbert Cunningham and Marion Douglas. He passed away in 1548. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT William first married Catherine Borthwick. Secondly, William married Elizabeth Campbell, of Wester Loudoun. Some sources indicate children were all from the second marriage, others have some of the children from the first marriage
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT The following are the children of WIlliam and Elizabeth:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander, the fifth Earl of Glencairn Andrew, progenitor of the Campbells of Corsehill Hugh of Watterstoun Robert of Montgrenane WIlliam, Bishop of Argyll Elizabeth, married john Cunningham of Caprington, Jean (Janet), married Ro
2 CONC bert Fergusson of Craigdarroch Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Mosley, Charles, editor. Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes. Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003 The Scots Peerage (Glencairn), Burkes Extinct Peerages 1883 (
2 CONC Cuningham of Kilmaurs and Glencairn) Wikipedia: William Cunningham, 4th Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/glencairn1488.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT William [Cunningham], 4th Earl of Glencairn, PC
2 CONT
2 CONT born
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1493
2 CONT
2 CONT mar. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT bef. 10 Jul 1519 Hon Catherine Home (widow of Alexander Home; d. after 17 Jan 1527/8), 2nd dau. of William [Borthwick], 3rd Lord Borthwick, by his wife Margaret Hay, 1st dau. of John [Hay], 1st Lord Hay of Yester, by his second wi
2 CONC fe Elizabeth Cunningham, dau. and eventual hrss. of George Cunningham, son and heir of Sir William Cunningham of Belton
2 CONT
2 CONT children by first wife
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hon Alexander Cunningham, later 5th Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Hon Andrew Cunningham of Corsehill (d. 1544), mar. Margaret Cunningham of Polmaise, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1a. Cuthbert Cunningham of Corsehill (d. 1575), mar. Maud Cunningham, dau. of John Cunningham of Aiket, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1b. Patrick Cunningham of Corsehill, concerned in the slaughter of the Earl of Eglinton 1586 and was himself killed by the Montgomeries (d. 1588)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2b. Alexander of Corsehill (d. May 1646), mar. Marion Porterfield, dau. of William Porterfield of that Ilk and Duchal, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1c. Alexander Cunningham of Corsehill (d. c. 1667), mar. Mary Houston, dau. of John Houston of that Ilk, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1d. Alexander Cunningham of Corsehill, mar. Anna Crawford, dau. of John Crawford of Kilbirnie. and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1e. Sir Alexander Cunningham of Corsehill, 1st Bt., mar. Mary Stewart, dau. of John Stewart of Blackhall, and had issue who in default of any nearer heirs-male would be heirs-male of the Earldom of Glencairn
2 CONT
2 CONT 2d. Cuthbert Cunningham of Cockilbie
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Hon Hugh Cunningham of Watterson (d. after 1541), ancestor of the Cunninghams of Carlung
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Hon Robert Cunningham of Davidstoun, Minister of Failford, co. Ayr (d. after 12 May 1546), mar. Mariota ...... and was the ancestor of the Cunninghams of Mountgrenan
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Hon William Cunningham, Bishop of Argyll 1539 and Dean of Brechin 1557 (b. 1513; d. bef. 26 Feb 1561/2)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Lady Elizabeth Cunningham, mar. Sir John Cunningham of Caprington, and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Lady Jean Cunningham, mar. Robert Fergusson of Craigdarroch
2 CONT
2 CONT mar. (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT after Jan 1535/6 Elizabeth Crichton (widow of (1) William Wallace the Elder, Tutor of Craigie, and (2) Robert [Crichton], 4th Lord Crichton of Sanquhar), dau. and hrss. of John Campbell of West Loudoun
2 CONT
