2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Genealogical Memoir of the Most Noble and Ancient House of Drummond" by David Malcolm, published in Edinburgh, Scotland, 1808. (price was 1 guinea to subscribers) 
2 CONT
2 CONT This book goes into the deep history of the Drummond family, and how they fit into the peerage of Scotland. Sir John Drummond, 1st Lord Drummond lived during the reigns of King James III, James IV, and James V from about the years
2 CONC  1470 to 1519. He was an important legal and political leader of that time. James IV was so enamoured with Lord Drummond's eldest daughter, Margaret, that he intended to make her his wife. The nobles and royal council did not appr
2 CONC ove of the marriage, so they poisoned Margaret and two of her sisters over breakfast one morning so that James would cooperate in an arranged marriage with the daughter of King Henry VIII of England. However, under promise of marr
2 CONC iage, she bore to the King a daughter, Lady Margaret Stewart from whom our family descends.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
