2 CONC died in 1491. The last ten years of his life were tainted by many outrages and accusations of being insane.  His grandson '''John''' succeeded to the title and became Vice-Admiral in the fleet of James IV (1488-1513); he was made 
2 CONC Lord Chamberlain in 1516. Eight years later, in 1524, the 2nd lord Fleming met his death in Kilbucho glen where he was killed by the Tweedies of Drumelzier as a result of a feud.
