2 CONT
2 CONT Eliza Douglas of Lochleven is the daughter of Sir Henry Douglas of Lochleven and Elizabeth Erskine.1 She married Sir John Drummond, 1st of Innerpeffray, son of John Drummond, 1st Lord Drummond and Lady Elizabeth Lindsay.1     Her 
2 CONC married name became Drummond.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Eliza Douglas of Lochleven and Sir John Drummond, 1st of Innerpeffray
2 CONT # Henry Drummond, 1st of Riccarton+1 d. a 1555. Married  Janet Crichton
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Elizabeth Douglas, a cousin [of her husband] of the house of Lochleven. [1]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was born about 1455 and thought the be the daughter of Henry Douglas of Lochleven. She married Sir John Drummond, 1st of Innerpeffray.
2 CONT
2 CONT In regard to her marriage The Scots Peerage states: "Sir John, of Innerpeffray, said to have married, first, the daughter of his uncle, James Drummond of Coldoch, and secondly, '''Eliza Douglas of Lochleven, but there is no proof 
2 CONC of this.'''
2 CONT
