2 CONT Scottish flag
2 CONT Henry Drummond was born in Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was born about 1500, the son of Sir John Drummond, 1st of Innerpeffray and Eliza, the daughter of Henry Douglas of Lochleven.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Janet Crichton, daughter of Henry Crichton and heiress of Riccarton.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had five sons and five daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Henry, the heir[2]
2 CONT # William, 2nd son, m. Margaret Drummond, heretrix of Piticairnes in 1580[2]
2 CONT # Sir David, 3rd son, Supreme Judge of the Bishop's Court of Vason in France[2]
2 CONT # Thomas, d. unm. in France[2]
2 CONT # Ninian, ministeer and parson of Kinnoull, m. Margaret Creichtone[2]
2 CONT # Margaret, m. George Drummond, 4th laird of Balloch[2]
2 CONT # unnamed, m. Laird of Cowstowne, Polwart[2]
2 CONT # unnamed, m. Laird of Logie[2]
2 CONT # unnamed, m. Laird of Bearlaw, Houstone[2]
2 CONT # unnamed, m. Laird of Bardige, Bruce[2]
2 CONT
