1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Margaret Livingston1
2 CONT * F, #459625
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p45963.htm#i459625
2 CONT * Last Edited=28 Nov 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Livingston''' is the daughter of William Livingston, 4th Lord Livingston.2 She married John Hay, 4th Lord Hay of Yester, son of John Hay, 3rd Lord Hay of Yester and Elizabeth Douglas, before 18 October 1533.1
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 18 October 1533, her married name became Hay.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Livingston and John Hay, 4th Lord Hay of Yester
2 CONT
2 CONT # Margaret Hay1
2 CONT # Christian Hay1
2 CONT # Elizabeth Hay+3 d. b Mar 1581
2 CONT # William Hay, 5th Lord Hay of Yester+1 b. 1538, d. Aug 1586
2 CONT # Thomas Hay1 b. a 1539, d. b 11 Jun 1584
2 CONT # James Hay1 b. a 1539
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Livingston-702
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of William Livingston, 4th Lord Livingston of Callendar, and his wife Agnes Hepburn, second daughter of Alexander Hepburn of Whitson. She was likely born c. 1510 else she would be considerably older than her h
2 CONC usband.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, shortly before 18 October 1533, John Hay, later Lord Hay of Yester, the son and heir of John Hay, third Lord Hay of Yester, and his first wife, Elizabeth Douglas, daughter of George, Master of Angus, and sister to Arc
2 CONC hibald (Douglas), sixth Earl of Angus.[2] He was born c. 1510.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died c. 1555 and she survived him an d was living 11 February 1567.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had children.
