2 CONT '''1583: (Draft) tack by George, earl of Cathnes (Caithness) (assignee of Beatrix Ruthven, daughter of William, Earl of Gowrie, donatrix of the ward, nonentries, etc. of the earldom of Cathnes, which pertained to the deceased John
2 CONC  Sinclair, Master of Cathnes, and fell to the crown by his decease,) with advice of his curators (John, Earl of Montrose, Mungo Grahame of Rathernes, Sir Patrick Hepburne of Lufneis and Patrick Hepburne of [Benestoun]), to his unc
2 CONC le, George, chancellor of Cathnes, of the four pennylands of Bordland of Murkill for the period during which they are in the king's hands. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD96%2f199&st
