2 CONT '''17 July 1585: Precept of clare constat by David, earl of Craufurd, lord Lyndsay addressed to Archibald Cullane, baillie in that part for infefting Thomas Wallace of Nather Collen, as heir to umquhile Robert Wallace, his father 
2 CONC in the lands of Nather Collen in the barony and regality of Scone and sheriffdom of Perth. Granted to said Earl by the king upon the forfeiture of umquhile William, earl of Gowrie, to whom they had been granted on the resignation 
2 CONC of the commendator and convent of Scone. Reserving the liferent of half said lands to Agnes Seytone, relict of said Robert and mother of said Thomas. At Brechin, 17th July 1585. Witnesses William Fullartoun of Ardoych, John Ramsay
2 CONC  of Jurdanstoun, Alexander Ramsay, burgess of Brechin (?), Robert Kynnere, baillie of Breychine, William Ogilvy, portioner of Idvie, [ ] Grahame, notary public cum diversis aliis. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatal
