2 CONT                    13
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 May 1590: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given an annualrent of two hundred and ten pounds from the lands of Cousland, in the Sheriffdom of Edinburgh, to James Richardson of Smeatoun and his s
2 CONC econd son Robert. The annualrent had been granted to James Richardson by William, Earl of Gowrie, who had borrowed money from him and used Cousland as security. His obligation passed first to his eldest son James, Earl of Gowrie, 
2 CONC and then to second son John, Earl of Gowrie. Earl John must have been a minor child when his father's obligation passed to him on 12 November 1589, for his mother was still acting as his tutrix testamentary on this date: "dicto Jo
2 CONC , et Dorathea Stewart comitissa de Gowry ejus matre et tutrice testamentaria". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/593/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-1593, charter number 1730 on p.
2 CONC  593]'''
