2 CONT '''24 July 1591: Transumpt of charter, dated at the monastery of Scone, 26 August 1559, by Patrick, bishop of Moray and commendator of Scone, and the convent thereof, to John Baxter, of the lands of Haltoune of Crwquhy; in action 
2 CONC at the instance of the said John Baxter and Alexander, his eldest son, against Dame Dorothy Stewart, Countess of Gowrie, John, Earl of Gowrie, now commendator of Scone and others, for the production of the register of the said abb
2 CONC ey for transumpt to be made; the original having been in the hands of David Bruce in Bandirrane and stolen from his house. [Charter not printed in the Liber de Scon]. [1569.173] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalog
