1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===GEORGE RUTHVEN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Ruthven is the son of Patrick, third Lord Ruthven. He and twenty-five other, including the Regent Lennox, were killed near Stirling on 4 September 1571. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#page/262/mode/1u
2 CONC p The Scots Peerage IV: 262] [https://archive.org/details/historieandlife00jamegoog/page/n130/mode/1up Historie of King James the Sext: 92]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Susan-Lynne-Schwenger/6000000019146876194 says: It appears the only George Ruthven at this general time died in 1571. However in an introduction to Muses Threnodie written by James Cant. there's a refer
2 CONC ence to a 92 year old George Ruthven who is in fact a subject of the poem which was published in 1638. The math works out if the George Ruthven born in 1544 or 1545 was the subject of Muses Threnodie.
