1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Lord Thomas Howard (1511 – 31 October 1537), courtier, was a younger son of Thomas Howard, 2nd Duke of Norfolk by his second marriage to Agnes Tilney.[1] He is chiefly known for his affair with Lady Margaret Dou
2 CONC glas (1515–1578), the daughter of Henry VIII's sister, Margaret Tudor, for which he was imprisoned in the Tower, where he died on 31 October 1537. The affair is immortalized in verses by his nephew, the poet Earl of Surrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord Thomas was at court in 1533 when his niece, Anne Boleyn married King Henry VIII as his second wife, and helped to bear the canopy at the christening of Anne's daughter, Princess Elizabeth. In the years which followed he wa
2 CONC s often at court, and it was there that he met Lady Margaret Douglas (1515–1578), the daughter of Henry VIII's sister, Margaret Tudor, and her second husband, Archibald Douglas, 6th Earl of Angus (c.1489–1557). By the end of 1535 
2 CONC Lord Howard and Lady Margaret Douglas had fallen in love and become secretly engaged.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord Howard's niece, Queen Anne Boleyn, fell from power in May 1536. This undoubtedly contributed to the King's fury when in early July 1536 he learned of the engagement of Lord Howard and Lady Margaret since Lady Margaret was 
2 CONC at the time next in the line of succession as a result of the King's bastardization of his daughters Princess Mary and Princess Elizabeth. Both Lord Howard and Lady Margaret were committed to the Tower, and on 18 July 1536 an Act 
2 CONC of Attainder accusing Lord Howard of attempting to 'interrupt ympedyte and lett the seid Succession of the Crowne' was passed in both houses of Parliament. The Act sentenced Howard to death, and forbade the marriage of any member 
2 CONC of the King's family without his permission.[3] The death sentence was not carried out, and Howard languished in the Tower despite the fact that Lady Margaret had broken off their relationship. While in the Tower Lady Margaret fel
2 CONC l ill with a fever, and the King allowed her to be moved to Syon Abbey under the supervision of the abbess. She was released from imprisonment on 29 October 1537. Lord Howard remained in the Tower, where he caught a fatal illness 
2 CONC and died on 31 October 1537. There is an unsubstantiated tradition that he was poisoned. His body was given to his mother, the Dowager Duchess of Norfolk, with the stipulation that it be buried ‘without pomp’. Lord Howard was inte
2 CONC rred at Thetford Abbey.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord Thomas' nephew, Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey, referred to his death in a poem to a lady who refused to dance with him:—[citation needed]
2 CONT * If you be fair and fresh, am I not of your hue? 
2 CONT * And for my vaunt I dare well say, *my blood is not untrue;
2 CONT * For you yourself doth know, it is not long ago
2 CONT * Sith that for love one of the race did end his life in woe,
2 CONT * In Tower both strong and high, for his assured truth,
2 CONT * Whereas in tears he spent his breath, alas, the more the ruth!
2 CONT * This gentle beast so died, whom nothing could remove,
2 CONT * But willingly to seek his death for loss of his true love.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1540 Lady Margaret Douglas was disgraced in a similar affair with Thomas Howard's nephew Sir Charles Howard, the son of Lord Thomas' elder half-brother Lord Edmund Howard, and a brother of Henry VIII's fifth Queen, Katherine
2 CONC  Howard.[5]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_Thomas_Howard ______________________________
2 CONT *'''Thomas Howard
2 CONT *'''M, #48567, b. circa 1505, d. 31 August 1536
2 CONT *Father     Sir Thomas Howard, Earl Marshal of England, 2nd Duke Norfolk, Sheriff of Norfolk & Suffolk, Lord High Treasurer b. 1443, d. 21 May 1524
2 CONT *Mother     Agnes Tilney
2 CONT *'''     Thomas Howard was born circa 1505. He died on 31 August 1536 at Tower Hill, London, Middlesex, England.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1616.htm#i48567 ______________________________
2 CONT *'''Lord Thomas Howard1
2 CONT *'''M, #105335, b. circa 1515, d. 1537
2 CONT *Last Edited=17 May 2002
2 CONT *'''     Lord Thomas Howard was born circa 1515. He married Lady Margaret Douglas, daughter of Archibald Douglas, 6th Earl of Angus and Lady Margaret Tudor.1 He died in 1537.1
