1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LADY MARGARET HAMILTON===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Hamilton is the daughter of John Hamilton of Clydesdale (aka John Hamilton of Samuelston) and his wife Janet Home. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft#page/363/mode/1up The Scots Peerage (Edinburgh 1
2 CONC 907) IV, p. 363]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Hamilton married John Johnstone of that Ilk. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun01paul#page/248/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, I, p. 248]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Hamilton married David Douglas, son of Sir George Douglas of Pittendreigh. The marriage contract was signed at Linlithgow on 8 May 1552. [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/472/mode/1up Hamilton Mem
2 CONC oirs, p. 472] [https://archive.org/stream/douglasbook02fras#page/622/mode/1up The Douglas Book, II, p. 296]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Third Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Following the death of her second husband in June 1557, Margaret Hamilton married Sir Patrick Whitelaw of that Ilk. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun01paul#page/193/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, I, p. 193]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-Johnstone-Marquis-of-Annandale/6000000000066816688?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1499238716583&through=6000000062135420893
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Johnstone/6000000062135420893?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1499238763116&through=6000000002501896109
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Archibald-Douglas-8th-Earl-of-Angus/6000000002187894993?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1499237178833&through=6000000002501896109
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Lady-Elizabeth-Douglas/6000000003897292957?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1499237184960&through=6000000002501896109
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Lady-Margaret-Douglas/6000000000769880470?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1499237298122&through=6000000002501896109
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1567: A charter by which Sir Patrick Whitelaw of that Ilk, with the consent of his wife, Lady Margaret Hamilton, has sold certain lands at Oldhamstocks in Berwickshire to William Arnot in Cocksburnspath and his wife Ma
2 CONC rgaret Wallace, and their son John Arnot, burgess of Edinburgh. The charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 12 July 1568. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/462/mode/1up Register of the Great
2 CONC  Seal of Scotland, A.D., 1546-1580, charter number 1823 on p. 462]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/n8/mode/1up John Anderson, Historical and Genealogical Memoirs of the House of Hamilton etc. (Edinburgh 1825), 476 pp. plus additions] [https://archive.org/stream/historica
2 CONC lgeneal00ande#page/371/mode/1up pp. 371-72 for Hamilton of Samuelstoun]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft#page/363/mode/1up Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms, The Scots Peerage (Edinburgh 1907), iv, p. 363 for John Hamilton of Clydesdale and his daughter Margaret]
2 CONT # [http://thepeerage.com/p10959.htm#i109582 Darryl Lundy's Peerage: Margaret Hamilton]
