1 NAME Sir Thomas Lyon, Master of Glamis
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1540
2 PLAC Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 FEB 1608
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU Master of Glamis, Lord High Treasurer of Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Thomas</strong>. Except for the period 1575-78 which intervened between the birth of his nephew Patrick, ninth Lord Glamis, and the death of Patrick's father John, eighth Lord Glamis, he was heir-presumptive to the ti
2 CONC tle, and was known as the <strong>Master of Glamis</strong>...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...On 20 January 1586-87 he was nominated one of the commissioners for considering grants out of the Crown lands, and on 9 February following one of the Extraordinary Lords of Session...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He died 18 February 1608. When the King heard of the event he is said to have observed that the boldest and hardiest man in his dominions was dead...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He married, first, after 1575, Agnes, third sister of Patrick, fifth Lord Gray...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He married, secondly, in 1586, Eupham, daughter of William, fifth Earl of Morton."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft#page/284/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VIII, page 284-288
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=grI2AAAAIAAJ An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII]; by George Brunton, David Haig; 1832; Page 203
2 CONT --------------------
