2 CONT == His Father's Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Campbell of Skipnish, Provost of Kilmun, here treated, made his last will and testament immediately before he died on 18 September 1573. In the first he nominated his sons, Archibald Campbell and Duncan Campbell, to be his
2 CONC  only executors and assignees. Because his sons were still minor children, he nominated and appointed the Earl of Argyll and the Master of Argyll to be their curators and tutors testamentar. His wife https://www.geni.com/people/Ma
2 CONC rion-Montgomery-Lady-Sempill/6000000011056651203?through=6000000006444052875 was still alive on 13 September 1573. He does not refere to her by name in his testament but he left legacies to "my spous" and "my lady my spous." Confi
2 CONC rmation was granted to his sons Archibald Campbell and Duncan Campbell on 10 February 1574. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Johne Campbell, Provost of Kilmun, r
2 CONC eference CC8/8/3]'''
2 CONT
