2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Hume_of_Godscroft David Hume or Home of Godscroft (1558–1629) was a Scottish historian and political theorist, poet and controversialist, a major intellectual figure in Jacobean Scotland. It h
2 CONC as been said that "Hume marks the culmination of the Scottish humanist tradition."[1] … He was the second son of Sir David Hume or Home, 7th Lord of Wedderburn, a Roman Catholic traditionalist of the Merse (now Berwickshire), who 
2 CONC had married an active Calvinist wife in Mary Johnston of Elphinstone.[3][4]
