2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT James Pringle of Whytbank was also known as James Pringle of Woodhouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Pringle-2371
2 CONT
2 CONT James Pringle was born around 1515 (estimated based on 1561 marriage of daughter). died 03 July 1563 [citation needed] / Nov 1563.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of David Pringle (of Smailholm) & Margaret Lundie. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited the lands of Whytbank, Selkirkshire; and Woodhouse, Peeblesshire. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He accompanied King James V at the 1542 Battle of Solway Moss, where he was taken prisoner, but late released. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret Kerr (of Linton, who married secondly Sir David Home of Wedderburn). [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 4 sons and 1 daughter: [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT # James Pringle (heir). [1]
2 CONT # George Pringle. [1]
2 CONT # Robert Pringle. [1]
2 CONT # William Pringle. [1]
2 CONT # Marian Pringle (married George Pringle of Blyndlee 1561). [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT David Home - Children by Margaret Ker
2 CONT
2 CONT # Patrick [disputed] (Burke’s has no children by her 2nd marriage)
2 CONT
