1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARGARET CAIRNES Lady Orchartoun ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Cairnes, Lady Orchartoun, here treated, is reported to be the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Cairnes-of-Orchardton-the-Younger/6000000093309390837?through=6000000073515113601 and his wife https://www.g
2 CONC eni.com/people/Janet-Kennedy/6000000019527392048 [https://kirkpatrickaustralian.com/getperson.php?personID=I17748&tree=No1 Kirkpatrick Family History]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 April 1587: Letters of Horning under the Signet of King James VI, addressed to Nicoll Newall, narrating that it was shewn by Margaret Cairnis, Lady Orchartoun, spouse of Edward Maxwall of Tynwald, and the said Edward, for hi
2 CONC s interest, that she was in peaceable possession of the lands of Dargavell since the decease of her last husband until two years ago when Johnne and David, sons of the late James Scott in Dargavill and Bessy Carrutheris, their mot
2 CONC her, after the burning of the complainers houses and dwelling in Dargavill by Johnne, lord Maxwall "his associatis and wageit men", set themselves down upon the room and possession of Dargavell with the assistance of Lord Maxwall 
2 CONC and intromitted with the corn and plenishing thereon; and that they still continue in their violent and wrongous possession thereof, and threaten to trouble and molest the complainers in their peaceable possession, notwithstanding
2 CONC  they had obtained letters and charges to possess the same again: The King therefore commands that the persons complained upon be charged to find sufficient and responsible sureties acted in the Books of the Secret Council that th
2 CONC e complainers, their tenants and servants, should be harmless and scatheless in their bodies, lands, tacks, possessions, goods and gear under the penalty of £100. At Halirudhous 29th April 1587. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk
2 CONC /nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f282&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Margaret+Cairnis&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/282]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 May 1587: Letters of Horning under the Signet of King James VI, addressed to Nicholl Newall, narrating that it was shewn by Margaret Cairnis, lady Orchartoun, spouse of Edward Maxwell of Tynwald, and the said Edward for his 
2 CONC interest, that Johnne and David, sons of the late James Scott, in Dergavill, and Bessy Carrutheris, their mother, were on 18th May denounced as rebels and put to the horn for not finding surety as directed in letters of horning No
2 CONC . GD86/282. The king therefore commands that the warden of the West Marche, the sheriff of Drumfreis, the provost and bailies of the burgh of Drumfreis and other judges and ministers of law be charged to search for and take the sa
2 CONC id rebels and to keep them in "sure firmance and captivitie" till they should be brought and presented to his justice and deputies. Given under the Signet at Haliruidhous 24th May 1587. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlin
2 CONC ecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f284&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Margaret+Cairnis&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/284]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Memorandum that upon 12 June 1587 Simone Johnston, Mathow Dicsone and Johne Merschell, bailies of Drumfres, were charged in terms of the above letters. Witnesses, Williame Maxwell apparent of Tyndwell, Robert Maxwell, his broth
2 CONC er and David McGhe, notary.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
