1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === William Kirkkpatrick, of Conheath, Last Lord of Kirkmichael
2 CONT * Death	9 Jun 1686 	Kirkmichael, Dumfries, Scotland 
2 CONT *Father  	KIRKPATRICK Sir Alexander, ,Lord of Kirkmichael and Conheath,   d. Yes, date unknown 
2 CONT *Mother  	KIRKPATRICK Margaret, ,daughter of Sir Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn,   d. Yes, date unknown 
2 CONT ===Children ===
2 CONT *1. KIRKPATRICK Major. George, ,of Knock,   b. 1671,   d. 24 Jun 1738, Dumfries, Dumfrieshire, Scotland Find all individuals with events at this location
2 CONT * 2. KIRKPATRICK James, ,of Cullompton, Devon,England,   b. Abt 1673,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT *3. KIRKPATRICK Robert, ,in Craigshields,of Over and Nether Glenkiln,   b. 1678,   d. 6 Oct 1746, Edinburgh, Scotland.
2 CONT * [http://genealogy.kirkpatrickaustralian.com/archives/getperson.php?personID=I6471&tree=TKA William Thomas Kirkpatrick] The old parish of Kirkmichael included the old Parish of Garrel or Garvald which were united about 1674 in sp
2 CONC ite of the vigorous protestations of the parishioners of Garrel. However, Garrel had been without a minister for several years. Some adjustments to the boundaries were made between the 1791 account and that of 1834, the eastern pa
2 CONC rt of the old Parish of Garrel being transferred to Lochmaben. With the recent conjoining with Tinwald and Torthorwald, the southern boundaries are taken care of by these two. Much of the north of the old parish is now afforested,
2 CONC  and marches upon Kirkpatrick Juxta, the west on Closeburn, and the east with Johnstone and Lochmaben.Ref:The Church of Scotland congregation of Kirkmichael, Tinwald and Torthorwald
2 CONT
