2 CONT Re: Above Note; By this illustrious alliance (the Princess having had, by her former husband, no male issue which survived after 1484) the heir of the house of Hamilton was for above a century the heir presumptive to the Throne [S
2 CONC .], though sometimes subject to the life of an infant child of one of the reigning monarchs, none of whom, till about 1600, had more than one child who survived infancy.
