1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on David Lyon of Baky and Cossins:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p1254.htm#i12536
2 CONT
2 CONT David Lyon of Baky and Cossins[1]
2 CONT *M, #12536, 
2 CONT *d. 9 September 1513
2 CONT *Last Edited=8 Apr 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT David Lyon of Baky and Cossins married Lady Elizabeth Lindsay, daughter of David Lindsay, 1st Duke of Montrose and Elizabeth Hamilton, circa September 1505.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 9 September 1513.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of John Lyon, 3rd Lord Glamis and Elizabeth Scrymgeour. 
2 CONT *He lived at Baikie, Scotland.[1] (Blaikie Castle?)
2 CONT *He lived at Cossins, Scotland.[2] (Ben M. Angel notes: Cossans, near Kirriemuir in Angus or Forfarshire)
2 CONT *He lived at Haltoun of Erse, Scotland.[2] (Ben M. Angel notes: this is probably Hatton Castle near Newtyle in Angus or Forfarshire. Refer to Wikipedia page on Hatton Castle)
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of David Lyon of Baky and Cossins and Lady Elizabeth Lindsay
2 CONT *1. John Lyon, 2nd of Cossins+
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 514. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 951. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT --------------------
