1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN LENNOX OF CALLY===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Lands of Cally===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''At the beginning of the 15th century Cally and other lands in the parish of Girthon, Kirkcudbrightshire, belonged to Sir John Stewart of Girthon. His daughter and heiress, Elizabeth, married firstly (1412) Alexander Stewart of 
2 CONC Torbane and secondly (c.1430) Donald Lennox, who is said to have been a natural son of Duncan, earl of Lennox. She died after 1471, having made over her lands to her younger son, William Lennox, MA, who appears to have been a grad
2 CONC uate of St Andrews University. William Lennox purchased Kirkennan and other lands in the parish of Buittle from Lord Monypenny in 1485 and thereby became involved in litigation in Scotland and France. He died in 1516 and was succe
2 CONC eded by his son, also called William, who married Margaret Chalmer. Their son William, who died in 1576, married Margaret Gordon, and had a son, John, and a daughter, Jonet, who married (1575) Andrew Lennox of Plunton. John's two 
2 CONC younger sons by his marriage with Agnes Maclellan, married (1607) Andrew Lennox's two younger daughters and co-heiresses. The eldest son, John Lennox, married (1612) Marion Lidderdale, daughter of James Lidderdale of Isle. John's 
2 CONC son, Alexander, married firstly (1639) Marion Gordon, eldest daughter of William Gordon of Penninghame, and secondly (1643) Margaret Lamb, relict of William Gordon of Kirkconnell. Alexander Lennox of Cally died in November 1657, l
2 CONC eaving an only daughter, Anna Lennox, married to Richard Murray, younger, of Broughton. In 1661 Richard Murray obtained a crown charter of the Cally estates on the resignation of John Lennox of Plunton, heir male of tailzie and pr
2 CONC ovision of Alexander Lennox.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD10&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of th
2 CONC e Murray Family of Broughton, reference GD10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                      1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 July 1598: Discharge by William Lennox, burgess in Wigton [Wigtown], to John Lennox of Callie [Cally] for 100 merks as his part of the assythment received by the said John for the slaughter of Robert Lennox of Creoch, the sai
2 CONC d William's brother, committed by Thomas Richart [Richard] and Martin Baillze [Baillie]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD10%2f658&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+lennox&ko=p&r=&ro
2 CONC =s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Murray Family of Broughton, reference GD10/658]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 November 1607: Note of contract of marriage between Thomas Lennox and William Lennox, sons of John Lennox of Callie [Cally], and Jean and Margaret Lennox, daughters of Andrew Lennox of Plunton. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.g
2 CONC ov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD10%2f354&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+lennox&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Murray Family of Broughton, reference GD10/354]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 November 1607: Charter by John Levenax [Lennox] of Calie [Cally], with consent of John Levenax [Lennox], apparent of Calie, his son, to William Levenax [Lennox], his son, and Margaret Levenax [Lennox], daughter of Andrew Lev
2 CONC enax [Lennox] of Pluntoun [Plunton], of the 3 merkland of Drumrukcalie [Drumruck], parish of Girthon, in implement of contract of marriage between William and Thomas Levenax [Lennox], the granter's sons, and Margaret and Jean Leve
2 CONC nax [Lennox], daughters of the said Andrew, dated 19 November 1607. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD10%2f110&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=plunton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National
2 CONC  Records of Scotland, Papers of the Murray Family of Broughton, reference GD10/110]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 February 1648: Summons of transferring, narrating extract contract of marriage between Thomas Lennox and William Lennox, sons of John Lennox of Calie, and Jean Lennox and Margaret Lennox, daughters of Andrew Lennox of Plunto
2 CONC n, dated 19 November 1607. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD10%2f369&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+lennox&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of th
2 CONC e Murray Family of Broughton, reference GD10/369]'''
