1 NAME Patrick /McKie/ of Larg
2 GIVN Patrick
2 SURN McKie
2 NSFX of Larg
2 _MARNM Mckie
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1495
2 PLAC CumlodenDumfries and Galloway, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1590
2 PLAC Minnigaff, Kirkcudbrightshire/Dumfries and Galloway , Scotland
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Patrick Sr McKie , b. abt. 1500/bef 1515 in Cumloden Scotland deceased in Minnigaff Kirkcudbright Scotland. He married abt. 1520 in Scotland, Janet MacDonall , b. bef. 1515/1520 in Garthland Scotland; deceased in S
2 CONC cotland, daughter of Uchtred MacDowall [born Abt. 1500 in Garthland] . Children of Patrick Sr McKie and Janet MacDonall were as follows: 
2 CONT * Archibald McKie born Abt. 1532 in Of Stranord, Scotland 
2 CONT * Patrick Jr McKie 
2 CONT ===============
2 CONT Listed as landowner in 1504 and 1530 (sasine) in Larg. An interesting relic is a monumental stone built into the wall of the old kirk of Minnigaff bearing the inscription: "Hic jacet--Patricus M'Ke de Caloda me fieri fecit" (Here 
2 CONC lies--Patrick M'Ke of Camloden [who]caused me to be made), per Book of Mackay p 354
2 CONT
2 CONT Book of McKee pg 325 calls this the "Minigaff stone" 
2 CONT
2 CONT ================================
2 CONT
2 CONT III.''' Patrick Makge of Larg, m. Janet, dau. of Uchtred
2 CONT Macdowall of Garthland, and widow of Alexr. Adair of Kinhilt''', as a charter under the Great Seal shows, dated 1529. An interesting relic of this couple, a monumental stone built into the wall of the old kirk of Minnigaff, bears 
2 CONC the inscription :—" Hie jacet—Patricus M'Kc de Caloda me fieri fecit" (Here lies—Patrick M'Ke of Camloden caused me to be made). The known issue of Patrick was two sons :—
2 CONT * Patrick, of whom follows ; and 
2 CONT * Archibald of Stranord who had three children (Alexr. ; Patrick of Craignyne ; and Margaret, m.
2 CONT   Patrick Heron of Kironghtree).
2 CONT
2 CONT pg. 354
2 CONT
2 CONT  THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University) Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH : NORMAN MACLEOD, -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY, ST. PETER'S MANSE, MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC VI [1906]
2 CONT
