1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NOTE - her birth date needs to be re-checked and verified - 
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of  Sir Alexander Stewart, 3rd Laird of Garlies and Dalswinton.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~wghannay/odohannay.html
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hannay of Sorbie, although he never possessed Sorbie, was the fifth son of Ethie. John married the renowned daughter of Sir Alexander Stewart of Garlies, by Elizabeth, the daughter of Sir Archibald Douglas of Culrow. This Eli
2 CONC zabeth or Isobel married John in approximatelly 1500, having all ready had five husbands: Thomas, son of Uthred McDowell of Gartland, Towers of Inerbith, Douglas of Pompertown, Moultry of Seafield and Lundy of Balgony. Nothing dau
2 CONC nted she bore John four more sons. John was a man of considerable consiquence in Galloway, and a baillie of Wigtown. He was a signatory of "Charter of Monuments of Holywood in Glasgow Diocese" on 17th of October 1522. He appears i
2 CONC n several documents from 1504, when he is baillie to the Abbott of Saulset until 1533. He died about 1544. His four sons were Andrew, Gilbert, George, and John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/hanna/2772/
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.... .... . John Hannay (son of Alexander Hannay) [?m: Elizabeth Stewart (daughter of Sir Alexander Stewart & Elizabeth Douglas; grand-daughter of sir William Stewart & Elizabeth UNKNOWN and sir Archibald Douglas of Cavers; g-gra
2 CONC nd-daughter of sir John Stewart of Garlies & Marion Stewart; 2g-grand-daughter of sir Walter Stewart of Garlies & Dalswinton) (reported by Lundin records)?]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke's has her as daughter of the 4th Laird of Garlies
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://thepeerage.com/p45546.htm#i455454
2 CONT
2 CONT Isobell Stewart is the daughter of Sir Alexander Stewart, 4th of Garlies.2 She married Thomas Macdowall, younger of Garthland, son of Uchtred Macdowall, 7th of Garthland and Isobell Gordon.1  Her married name became Macdowall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Isobell Stewart and Thomas Macdowall, younger of Garthland
2 CONT
2 CONT Uchtred Macdowall, 8th of Garthland+2 d. c 1531
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S32] BLG2001 volume 1, page 883. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S32] [S32] BLG2001. [S32]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Robert Lundie has no children by his second wife, Elizabeth Stewart, who was the daughter Sir Alexander Stewart, 3rd of Garlies, d. Abt 1500 & Elizabeth Douglas. She married 2nd to John Hannay, of Sorbie.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *[https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I23373&tree=CC Clan MacFarlane Geneology] shows parents as Sir Robert Lundie of Balgonie &  Helen Sibbald, heiress of Balgonie and cites 
2 CONT * [S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Lindsay04.
2 CONT * [S6][https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ll/lundin3.php Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Lundin3] 
