1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Robert Crichton:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2397.htm#i23963
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Crichton, 1st Lord Crichton of Sanquhar
2 CONT *M, #23963, 
2 CONT *d. from July 1494 to February 1494/95
2 CONT *Last Edited=8 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Crichton, 1st Lord Crichton of Sanquhar was the son of Sir Robert Crichton of Sanquhar and Elizabeth Erskine.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Margaret Hay.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Christian Erskine, daughter of Sir John Erskine of Kinnoull, before 1457.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died from July 1494 to February 1494/95.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Lochmaben in 1484, which he successfully defended for King James III against the 9th Earl of Douglas.[1]  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Lochmaben_Fair
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created 1st Lord Crichton of Sanquhar [Scotland] on 29 January 1487/88.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir Robert Crichton, 1st Lord Crichton of Sanquhar and Margaret Hay
2 CONT *1. Robert Crichton of Kinnoull+1 d. fr Feb 1483/84 - Feb 1491/92
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 601. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
