1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN CATHCART OF GLENDOWIS===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Title-Deeds for Carleton (from 1496): Allan Cathcart, son and heir of Sir John Cathcart of Carleton, who died 1510. Margaret and Sibyl Cathcart, his daughters, who each inherited half of the lands and barony. Margaret married (
2 CONC 1) the first-named Robert Cathcart above, (2) Hew Campbell, son and heir of Robert Campbell of Kilmanach. Sibyl married (1) John Cathcart of Glendowis, Robert's younger brother, who also fell at Flodden, (2) Gilbert Kennedy. Marga
2 CONC ret's son Robert inherited her half of Carleton and he and his posterity were thereafter styled "of Carleton", though they resided at Killochan. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD117&s
2 CONC t=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hew+cathcart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1700&dt=1800&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cathcart Family of Carleton and Killochan, reference GD117]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''24 February 1511: Charter of alienation granted by Sybilla Carthkert daughter and one of the heiresses of deceased Alan Carthkert of Carltoun and spouse of John Carthkert of Glendowyss in favour of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton and L
2 CONC ord Montgomery of those 10s of her lands of old extent of Drumlomford together with the house thereof lake and lands adjacent to the same which were then occupied by Donald Makmolrone; to hold of her in fee for payment yearly of o
2 CONC ne penny money of Scotland at the feast of Whitsunday in name of blench farm if asked only. Dated at Edinburgh. Witnesses: Patrick Montgomery of Giffyn and others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.asp
2 CONC x?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f39%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sybil+cathcart&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/10/39/1]'''
1 FAMC @F6000000017139347876@
1 FAMS @F6000000013823056047@
1 RFN geni:6000000013822926695
