1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES MAXWELL===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Maxwell, here treated, is the son of John, third Lord Maxwell, and his wife, Lady Janet Crichton. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/477 The Scots Peerage etc. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord 
2 CONC Lyon king of Arms. Volume VI (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1909), for the children of John, third Lord Maxwell, see pp. 477-78]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Maxwell, here treated, is said to be the ancestor of the family of Maxwell of Cavens, although the names of his immediate successors are not known. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/126 The Scot
2 CONC s Peerage etc. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon king of Arms. Volume III (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1906), p. 126]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/477 The Scots Peerage etc. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon king of Arms. Volume VI (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1909), for the children of John, third Lord Maxwe
2 CONC ll, see pp. 477-88]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/126 The Scots Peerage etc. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon king of Arms. Volume III (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1906), for Maxwell of Dirleton see pp. 126-3
2 CONC 1]'''
2 CONT # [http://archive.org/stream/maxwellhistoryge00hous#page/10/mode/1up Maxwell history and genealogy By Florence Wilson Houston, Laura Cowan Blaine, Ella Dunn Mellette] 
