0 @I6000000084332774255@ INDI
1 NAME Homer Aymer /Maxwell/ Ancestor of Portrack (caer.XIV)
2 GIVN Homer Aymer
2 NSFX Ancestor of Portrack (caer.XIV)
2 _MARNM Maxwell
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1460
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/477 The Scots Peerage etc. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon king of Arms. Volume VI (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1909), for the children of John, third Lord Maxwell
2 CONC , see pp. 477-78]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Maxwell family were for over two centuries in
2 CONT possession of the estate of Portrack. The Portrack Maxwells were a prominent branch of the
2 CONT family in the later 16th and early 17th centuries, suffering a sharp decline during the religious
2 CONT troubles from the 1630s to 1740s. The ancient tower house or Portrack and the house which
2 CONT replaced it are situated in the north-eastern corner of the parish of Holywood, close to the
2 CONT border with Dunscore parish. The estate at one time also included the lands of McWhanrick
2 CONT and Glengaber, also in the parish of Holywood. The estate was immediately adjacent to
2 CONT Cowhill on the south-east, and Dalswinton to the north.
2 CONT
2 CONT Homer (Aymer) Maxwell (c1460- )
2 CONT In the Book of Carlaverock Sir William Fraser states that the progenitor of the Maxwells of1
2 CONT Portrack was Homer Maxwell, son of John, Master of Maxwell and his wife Janet Crichton.
2 CONT We cannot discover any other authority for this statement apart from what is said in an old
2 CONT manuscript account of the Herries family, presented in the Herries Peerage Case in 1851,
2 CONT where the ancestor of Portack is called ‘Hary’ and is listed as a son of John, Master of
2 CONT Maxwell.2
2 CONT Among the defenders in an action by the Abbot of Holywood for ‘wrongous occupancy’ on 16
2 CONT March 1498/99 were “Amere of Maxvale, Robert Maxvale in Gleneslane and William3
2 CONT Maxwell of Stepfurd”. It is not clear whether this ‘Amere’ is one and the same as Homer, son
2 CONT of John, Master of Maxwell, but his designation ‘of Maxvale’ could indicate he was a senior
2 CONT member of the Maxwell family.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Book of Carlaverock, Sir William Fraser, Volume I, Page 155.
2 CONT 2 Sessional Papers of the House of Lords, Volume XVII, 1851: Evidence Before Lords Committees for
2 CONT Privileges, and Before the House, &c., Page 296.
2 CONT 3 Acta Dominorum Concilii (Acts of the Lords of Council in Civil Causes), Volume II (1496-1501), ed.
2 CONT George Neilson & Henry Paton, 1918, Edinburgh; Page 337.
