1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This profile does not belong here. As stated below, this would be a son of John Maxwell of Pollok, not 3rd Lord Maxwell. Robert Maxwell, son of 3rd Lord Maxwell was ancestor of Cowhill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Maxwell, a son of Sir John Maxwell of Pollock, was rector of Torbolton in the year 1521, and next was provost of Torbolton in the year 1521, and next was provost of the collegiate church in the town of Dunbarton, and at 
2 CONC last was promoted to this see of Orkney. He built the stalls in his catherdral, which are curiously engraven with the arms of several of his ancestors in his see; and he furnished the steeple with a set of excellent bells, which w
2 CONC ere cast within the castle of Edinburgh, by Robert Borthwick, as the inscription on them bears. In the year 1536, when the king made his famous progress through the isles belonging to his crown, his Majesty was nobly entertained b
2 CONC y this bishop at his own charges; and at this time the king was pleased to give the town of Kirkwall a confirmation of its royalty. [https://archive.org/details/historicalcatalo00keit/page/222/mode/1up A Historical Catalogue of th
2 CONC e Scottish Bishops down to the year 1688. By the Right Reverend Robert Keith. etc. (Bell & Bradfute, Edinburgh, 1824), p. 223]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===ROBERT MAXWELL===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===BISHOP OF ORKNEY===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/22/mode/1up Maxwell Memoirs, p. 22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/403/mode/1up Maxwell Memoirs, pp. 403-11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===ROBERT MAXWELL===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Maxwell, here treated, is the son of John, thord Lord Maxwell, and his wife, Lady Janet Crichton. He was living on 8 May 1485.  [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/477 The Scots Peerage etc. Edited b
2 CONC y Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon king of Arms. Volume VI (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1909), for the children of John, third Lord Maxwell, see pp. 477-78]'''
