2 DATE BET 17 JUL 1635 AND 22 JAN 1640
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===DAME JANET KERR Countess of Glencairn===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Dames Janet Kerr, Countess of Glencairn. She was alive on 17 July 1635, when letters of horning were issued against her at the instance of John Inglis, but she died before 2
2 CONC 2 January 1640, when her son William, Earl of Glencairn, had a gift of her escheat from the brow. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f273&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Janet+Ker+Co
2 CONC untess+of+Glencairn&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD39/1/273]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Janet Kerr married William, Earl of Glencairn.''' [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou00paulgoog#page/n263/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: p.246]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 December 1610: Charter by James Earl of Glencairn to William Master of Glencairn, his eldest son ("senior son and apparent heir") and Dame Jamet Ker his wife in liferent and the heirs male (procreated or) to be procreate betw
2 CONC een them, whom failing to the nearest lawful (heir) male of the Master of Glencairn mentioned in the new entail of the lordship and Earldom of Glencairn, of the lands and barony of Glencairn with the castle etc. lying in the count
2 CONC y of Dumfries and lands and barony of Kilmaurs lying in the county of Ayr the Charter granted in implement of a contract entered into between the Earl on the one part and William Master of Glencairn and Dame Janet Ker his wife, da
2 CONC ughter of the deceased Mark Earl of Lothian (on the 2nd part) and Dame Margaret Maxwell Countess of Lothian mother of the said Dame Janet Ker on the third part dated 24th November 1610, but with and under the reservations provisio
2 CONC ns and conditions mentioned in the said contract. (This only refers to the barony of Kilmaurs). Witnesses, Sir James Cunningham of Glengarnock, knight, William Barclay of Innergelly, George and James Cunninghams burgesses of Edinb
2 CONC urgh (Geo. C. burgess of Canongate, John C., merchant burgess of Edinburgh). Robert Fergusson, apparent of Craigdarroch, one of the baillies for the Earl of Glencairn. At Canongate. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecat
2 CONC alogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f156&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+maxwell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1620&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/156]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 February 1635: Letters of horning, John Inglis, elder, Merchant burgess of Edinburgh, against Dame Janet Ker Countess of Glencairn proceeding on letters obligatory granted by the countess to him for the sum of £1164:4:2 as th
2 CONC e price of goods and merchant ware furnished to her, dated 17 July 1633. The letters (of Horning) dated 2nd and  3 February 1635. (Dame Janet Ker Summoned 14 April 1635 and put to the Horn at Irvine 17 July 1635. Letters of Hornin
2 CONC g, registered in books of Council 23 July 1635). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f269&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD39%2f1%2f269&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of 
2 CONC Scotlland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/269]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 April 1637: Contract of marriage between William Earl of Glencairn with consent of Dame Janet Ker Countess of Glencairn his mother on the one part, and Mrs Anna Ogilvie (lawful) daughter of James Lord Deskfurd with consent of
2 CONC  the said James Lord Deskfurd her father and Dame Elizabeth Leslie her mother on the other part In contemplation of which marriage the Earl with consent of his mother obliges him his heirs as well male taillie and of provision etc
2 CONC  to infeft the said Mrs Anna Ogilvie his future spouse in liferent in the lands of Finlayston Cunningham with the castle etc For which causes Lord Deskfurd obliges him to pay to the Earl in name of Dote with the said Mrs Anna Ogil
2 CONC vie within the burgh of Edinburgh the sum of 40,000 merks etc. Witnesses, Sir William Cunningham of Robertland knight, baronet, Sir Alexander Abercrombie of Berkenbog knight baronet, Mr. William Cochrane of Coudon, Mr Robert Hepbu
2 CONC rn advocate and William Sharpe Sheriff Clerk of Banff. At Cullen. (Signature of Dame Janet Ker is to be obtained. Provision is made for the daughters of the marriage if no son thereof is born) (Failing Lord Deskford and his wife, 
2 CONC John Earl of Rothes, John Leslie of Newton, Sir Patrick Ogilvie, elder and younger of Inchmartin, and Alexander Ogilvie of Kempcairn, brother german of Lord Deskford are to fulfil the contract). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk
2 CONC /nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f271&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Janet+Ker+Countess+of+Glencairn&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotlland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/271]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 January 1640: Gift by King Charles 1st to William Earl of Glencairn, his heirs as assignees one or more, of the liferent escheat of all lands heritages etc pertaining to Dame Janet Ker Countess of Glencairn (his mother) of a
2 CONC ll years and terms bygone from the expiry of year and day after the said Countess her denunciation to the horn (which took place on 17 July 1635 at the instance of John Inglis (See GD39/1/269). Her letters obligatory being dated 1
2 CONC 7 July 1633 and registered in Books of Council 2 Feb. 1635), etc. At Holyroodhouse. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f273&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Janet+Ker+Countess+of+Glen
2 CONC cairn&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotlland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/273]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 January 1644: Decree of declarator obtained before the Lords of Council and Session at the instance of William Earl of Glencairn against Colonel Robert Cunningham (lawful) son of umquhile Dame Janet Ker Countess of Glencairn
2 CONC  and (Lady - Cunningham) Ladies Margaret, Jean, Anne and Marion Cunningham, (Lawful) daughters of the Countess, and nearest in kin to her, Sir Ludovick Stewart of Minto husband of Lady Cunningham , David Beton of Creick, husband o
2 CONC f Lady Margaret and John Blair of that ilk, husband of Lady Jean making mention that the Earl had by Gift of our sovereign Lord (See GD39/1/273) the liferent escheat of all lands heritages etc which pertained to the said Countess 
2 CONC with the maills farms annualrent etc of all years and terms bygone since the expiry of year and day after the Countess her denunciation to the horn, and of all years and terms thereafter during her lifetime, pertaining to his Maje
2 CONC sty by reason of the Countess having upon the 17 July 1635 been denounced rebel and put to the horn by virtue of letters of horning (See GD39/1/269) against her at the instance of John Inglish merchant burgess of Edinburgh for not
2 CONC  making payment to him of £770:4/2 (Sic but £1170) etc. as the letters of horning etc did at more length bear, and as the letters of gift to the said William Earl of Glencairn under the privy seal of date 22d January 1640 and also
2 CONC  more fully purport. By virtue whereof the Earl had good and undoubted right to the foresaid liferent escheat etc. (Edinburgh). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f285&st=1&tc=y
2 CONC &tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Janet+Ker+Countess+of+Glencairn&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotlland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/285]'''
