1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Robert Maxwell, of Orchardtoun</strong>, co. Kirkcudbright, as also of Ballycastle, co. Londonderry, s. of [Robert?] Maxwell ('who maintained a company of Foot, brought over at his own expense, in Ireland and also a troop
2 CONC  of horse') acquired Ballycastle from his wife's father (who held it from the Haberdashers' Company), but was obliged, in 1649, to surrender it to the Pari, forces ; acted as Lieut.-Col. under the Duke of Hamilton [S.] and was cr.
2 CONC  a Baronet [S.] as above, 30 June 1663, the patent not being, however, recorded in the Great Seal Register [S.]. He m., before Feb. 1639/40, Anne or Marion, only da. and h. of Robert (Maclellan) 1st Lord Kirkcudbright [S.] (who d.
2 CONC  13 Jan. 1638/9) by his first wife Anne, da. of Sir Matthew Campbell. She d. 1650. He was living 1669 but d. before 1673, probably about 1670."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524390#page/n359/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1903; Vol. III; page 340
2 CONT
2 CONT Baronet in 1663, died 1671.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sir Robert Maxwell of Spottis and Orchardton, first Baronet. He was retoured heir to his father in the lands of Spottis and others on 31st October 1615. He was created a Baronet in 1663. He had three sons. He died before 20th Oct
2 CONC ober 1
