1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Maxwell,_1st_Earl_of_Nithsdale
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Maxwell, 1st Earl of Nithsdale (after 1586 – May 1646), was a Scottish nobleman. He succeeded his brother as 10th Lord Maxwell in 1613, and was created Earl of Nithsdale in 1620. General of Scots in Danish-Norwegian service
2 CONC  during the Thirty Years' War. A loyal supporter of Charles I and a prominent Catholic, he lost his titles and estates in 1645, dying on the Isle of Man in 1646.
