1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ben M. Angel notes: Lundy's picture of George Seton and his family is in fact not of this family, accoring to the Seton family website: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www2.thesetonfamily.com:8080/history/7th_Lord_Seton_Epitaph.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT The likely source of the mis-identification, attributed to a 2008 E-mail by Caroline Maubois, comes from the mis-identification of George Seton, 7th Lord Seton, who was the 5th Lord Seton named George. Lundy has him listed as 5th 
2 CONC Lord Seton, apparently a common mistake made by those studying this family. The pic is actually of this person's paternal grandfather, along with this person's father, aunt, and uncles, all of whom were apparently alive after the 
2 CONC death of that generation's George in March 1562. The woman is actually the elder Seton's daughter, not his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Hon. Elizabeth Maxwell:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p2148.htm#i21471
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Elizabeth Maxwell [1]
2 CONT *F, #21471
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 May 2008
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=1.81%
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Elizabeth Maxwell married George Seton, 3rd Earl of Winton, son of Robert Seton, 1st Earl of Winton and Lady Margaret Montgomerie, before 1628.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of John Maxwell, 6th Lord Herries of Terregles and Elizabeth Maxwell.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 1628, her married name became Seton.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hon. Elizabeth Maxwell and George Seton, 3rd Earl of Winton
2 CONT *1. Lady Isabel Seton [2]
2 CONT *2. Lady Mary Seton+[1] d. 15 Jan 1697/98
2 CONT *3. Christopher Seton [2] b. 28 Jun 1631, d. Jul 1648
2 CONT *4. William Seton [2] b. 8 Jan 1633, d. Jul 1648
2 CONT *5. Lady Anne Seton+[2] b. 30 Sep 1634, d. a 23 Feb 1685/86
2 CONT *6. Sir John Seton of Garleton, 1st Bt.+[2] b. 29 Sep 1639, d. Feb 1686
2 CONT *7. Sir Robert Seton of Windygoul, 1st and last Bt. [2] b. 10 Nov 1641, d. Nov 1671
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 50. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1280. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John [Maxwell], 6th Lord Herries of Terregles married his second cousin '''Lady Elizabeth Maxwell''' (d. aft. Dec 1639), sister of Robert [Maxwell], 1st Earl of Nithsdale, and 1st dau. of John [Maxwell], 7th Lord Maxwell (sometime
2 CONC  Earl of Morton), by his wife Lady Elizabeth Douglas, 2nd dau. of David [Douglas], 7th Earl of Angus
