1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY MARGARET MAXWELL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Maxwell-1792
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Maxwell''', 3rd daughter
2 CONT * https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I5603&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes''': 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15th December 1597, John, eighth Lord Maxwell, with several cautioners, including John Maxwell of Kirkconnel and George Maxwell of Dramcoltram, became bound to pay to John Wallace, younger of Craigie, 7000 merks as dowry with h
2 CONC is sister Margaret Maxwell. The dowry was made payable on the 10th November 1599, and as it was not paid, the right of recovering the money was by Mrs John Wallace transferred to Catherine Wallace, one of her husband's sisters. By
2 CONC  a legal act this gentlewoman compelled George Maxwell of Drumcoltram, one of Lord Maxwell's cautioners, to pay the amount to her and her husband, William Wallace, younger of Elderslie. To Edward, son of George Maxwell of Drumcolt
2 CONC ram, the sum was, in January 1633, refunded by the grantor's brother, Robert, first Earl of Nithsdale. [The Book of Wallace by Rev.Charles Rogers pub.1889]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources''': 
2 CONT * [S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Wallace04: Vans Family Archive with support from GE Cockay n e's 'Baronetage' (volume IV).
2 CONT * [S841] The Book of Wallace, Rev. Charles Rogers, (Wallace -The Book of Wallace by Rev. Charles Rogers 1889.pdf in editors collection).
