2 CONT John died in 1639, supposedly murdered by John and Thomas Blake[10] whereafter by September 1641 Marion had remarried to Andrew Stewart (Burke, 1894, p. 1365) who was a legal writer.[11] In 1637, she appeared before Dumfries Kirk 
2 CONC session for failure to attend communion (Bryson & Veitch, 1825, p. 347), the implication being that she preferred to adhere to Roman Catholicism. Andrew Stewart died in 1662 and she survived him until 4 January 1674 (DGFHS, 2008).
