1 NAME Robert Baronet /Grierson/ (1st Baronet of Lag, Sir, Knight)
2 GIVN Robert Baronet
2 SURN Grierson
2 NSFX (1st Baronet of Lag, Sir, Knight)
2 _MARNM Grierson
2 NICK Auld Lag
1 NAME Sir Robert Grierson of Lag, 1st Baronet
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1657
2 ADDR
3 CITY Barquhar
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 29 DEC 1733
2 ADDR
3 STAE Rock Hall Estate Collin Dumfries-shire
3 CTRY Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Robert Grierson, of [Rock Hall, in] Lag</strong>, co. Dumfries, s. and h. of William Grierson, or Grier, of Farquhar, by Margaret (mar. contract June 1654), da. of Sir James Douglas, of Mouswald (which William was 2d s. o
2 CONC f Sir Robert Grierson, or Grier, of Lag, sometime, 1628-33, 1639-41, 1643, 1644-47 and 1648, M.P. [S.] for Dumfries Sheriffdom, who d. about 1654), was served h., 9 April 1669, to his cousin Robert (s. and h. of Sir John Grierson,
2 CONC  of Lag), who had d. 17 March 1666, at the age of 18; was M.P. [S.] for Dumfries Sheriffdom, 1678, 1681-82 and 1685-86 ; was Steward of Kirkcudbright, making himself notorious by his vehement persecution of the Covenanters, and wa
2 CONC s cr. a Baronet [S.], as above, 25 March 1685, with rem. to heirs male whatsoever and with a pension of £200 a year. In April 1685, he presided at the trial and execution for refusing to take the abjuration oath of the two women k
2 CONC nown as " the Wigtown martyrs." After the Revolution he suffered many fines and imprisonments. He executed various entails 26 Oct. 1713, 28 Aug. 1719, 22 Oct. 1725, and 20 Dec. 1733, chiefly in favour of his 4th and yst. s., Gilbe
2 CONC rt, and to the exclusion of his eldest son. He m. Henrietta, 3d da. of James (Douglas), 2d Earl of Queensberry [S.], by his 2d wife Margaret, da. of John (Stewart), 1st Earl of Traquair [S.]. He d. 15 April 1736."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n345/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 327
