1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN FERGUSSON OF CRAIGDARROCH ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Fake Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''At least two vanity pedigrees published on the internet claim that John Fergusson of Craigdarroch, here treated, was born on 27 April 1597, at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. See [https://ancestors.familysearch.o
2 CONC rg/en/KHBL-G3T/john-ferguson-1597-1628#:~:text=When%20John%20Ferguson%20was%20born%20on%2027%20April,were%20the%20parents%20of%20at%20least%201%20son FamilySearch] and [https://www.ancestry.co.uk/genealogy/records/john-fergussone-
2 CONC 24-2mzgz37?geo_a=r&o_iid=41013&o_lid=41013&o_sch=Web+Property Ancestry] This is wrong. A man named Robert Fergusone did have a son named John whose baptism was registered at Edinburgh on 27 April 1597, but he was a baker there. He
2 CONC  was not the Laird of Cardarroch .The baptism of this child reads as follows: "Robert Fergusone baxter A. S. N. Johne w. Johne Halliday advocat and Johne Watsone of Gorgie". [NRS: OPR.685/1/1] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?
2 CONC doc_id=6000000184131854895 Image of Baptismal Record]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''It follows, therefore, that John Fergusson of Craigdarroch, here treated, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/John-Fergusone/6000000184136121864 '''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Fergusson and Robert Menzies Fergusson, joint editors of the Fergusson Records, believed that John Fergusson of Craigdarroch, here treated, was the eldest son and heir of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Fergusson-of-Cr
2 CONC aigdarroch/6000000014585399699?through=6000000049134112844 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Cunningham/6000000177170383853 However, this proposition is not supported by the surviving record evidence, which shows 
2 CONC that https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Fergusson/6000000049134379853?through=6000000049134112844 was actually the eldest son of this marriage. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f
2 CONC 99&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD77&ro=s&df=1611&dt=1615&di=n NRS: GD77/99] It follows, therefore, that John Fergusson, here treated, is unlikely to be the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/John-Fergusson/600000018
2 CONC 3963675861 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''As noticed above, John Fergusson of Craigdarroch, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Fergusson-of-Craigdarroch/6000000014585399699?through=6000000049134112844 [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrs
2 CONC onlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f99&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD77&ro=s&df=1611&dt=1615&di=n NRS: GD77/99] However, the name of his mother has not been satisfactorily identified.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Fergusson of Craigdarroch, here treated, is the grandson and heir of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Fergusson-8th-Laird-of-Craigdarroch/6000000024871543697 from whom he inherited various lands in the barony of Glencairn 
2 CONC and sheriffdom of Dumfries. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f100&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=craigdarroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n NRS: GD77/100]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Fergusson of Craigdarroch, here treated, died before 18 March 1621. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f103&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+fergussoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&d
2 CONC t=1650&di=n NRS: GD77/103]'''
