1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''About the Keeling-Gouldman-Golden family relationship'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT There was an extremely close, familial relationship during this generation. HOWEVER, it is no longer thought that Gouldmans descend from Keelings. Different yDNA types make that almost impossible.
2 CONT
2 CONT For most accurate Gouldman genealogy, see https://goldengenealogy.com/wngb/gouldman-family-history/
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''IMPORTANT / READ / ERRORS IN GENI RELATIONSHIP'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''>> Thomas Gouldman c1640-1684 and his son Edward Keeling, d1710, is not son and grandson of Leonard Keeling.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT GEDMatch: A668333
2 CONT
2 CONT This line yDNA tested with multiple male family members with branches from 1780s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Our Goldens are R1b R-BY61503 R-FTB95535 R-BY70029 Y-111 Y-700
2 CONT
2 CONT --- Tester yDNA is not linked because GENI contains flaws in editing ancestor relationships. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --- It assumes that our yDNA R-BY70029 applies to the entire male line listed within GENI --- that line contains errors.
2 CONT
2 CONT The claimed direct lineage grandfathers of Edward Gouldman, Thomas Gouldman and Keeling are not our grandfathers ... HAVE TRIED to correct these relationship errors but GENI has disabled the REMOVE relationship functionality.
2 CONT
2 CONT Our constantly updated Golden family research is available at https://goldengenealogy.com/wngb/
2 CONT
2 CONT Our family's document beginning is 1760 in the Newberry, South Carolina area.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill Golden, Norfolk1956@gmail.com
