1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ANNIE LAURIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Annie Laurie is the daughter of Sir Robert Laurie of Maxwellton, and his second wife, Jean Riddell [http://www.thepeerage.com/p24760.htm#i247594 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.thepeerage.com/p24760.htm#i247594 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]
2 CONT # [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annie_Laurie Wikipedia: Annie Laurie]
2 CONT # [http://dna.cfsna.net/GEN/Scotland/Dumfries/Craigdarroch_Lairds.htm and Fergusson DNA Project. The Lairds of Craigdarroch] 
2 CONT # [http://dna.cfsna.net/GEN/Scotland/Dumfries/Alexander_F_and_Annie_Laurie.htm Fergusson DNA Project. The Lairds of Craigdarroch]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Lady John Scott Version of the Song: Maxwelton's Braes are Bonnie===
2 CONT
2 CONT Maxwelton's braes are bonnie,
2 CONT Where early fa's the dew, 'Twas there that Annie Laurie Gi'ed me her promise true Gi'ed me her promise true - Which ne'er forgot will be, And for bonnie Annie Laurie I'd lay me down and dee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her brow is like the snaw-drift, Her neck is like the swan, Her face it is the fairest, That 'er the sun shone on. That 'er the sun shone on - And dark blue is her e'e, And for bonnie Annie Laurie I'd lay me down and dee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Like dew on gowans lying, Is the fa' o' her fairy feet, And like winds, in simmer sighing, Her voice is low and sweet. Her voice is low and sweet - And she's a' the world to me; And for bonnie Annie Laurie I'd lay me down and dee.
