1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES HENDERSON OF FORDELL===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ee/elphinstone4.php Stirnet: Elphinstone 04]
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p43743.htm#i437430 BIOGRAPHICAL SUMMARY FROM DARRYL LUNDY'S PEERAGE]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Henderson, 3rd of Fordell was the son of William Henderson and Elizabeth Scott.[2] He married Jean Murray, daughter of Sir William Murray, 10th of Tullibardine.[1] He died between 1610 and 1612.[1] In 1565 he was excused 
2 CONC by Queen Mary and Lord Darnley from attending their army ‘ost' (assembly of landowners and their followers summoned by the sovereign(s) for military service), because of his minority, and from attending the wars all his life for t
2 CONC he good service of his predecessors.[1] In 1566 he was granted the hereditary Provostship of Inverkeithing.[1] Children of James Henderson, 3rd of Fordell and Jean Murray 1. Sir John Henderson, 4th of Fordell+[2] d. Jan 1618 2. Si
2 CONC r Robert Henderson of Tunnygask [2] d. 1622 3. Sir Francis Henderson of Easter Duvis in Newbottle [2] d. 1628 4. James Henderson [2] 5.Janet Henderson [2] 6. Grizel Henderson [2] 7Euphanie Henderson [2] 8.Barbara Henderson [2] 9. 
2 CONC Margaret Henderson [2] d. Dec 1649 10. Elizabeth Henderson [2] 11. Anne Henderson [2] b. 21 Dec 1567'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citations: 1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1864. Hereinafter cite
2 CONC d as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition. 2. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.'''
