2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 November 1603: Charter by which Thomas Livingstone of Hanyng confirms that he has given various lands in Stirlingshire, including Hanyng, to his son and heir Alexander Livingstone, and to Alexander's wife Janet Henderson, th
2 CONC e widow of William Elphinstone, sheriff of Orkney. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/547 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1593-1608, charter number 149
2 CONC 9 on p. 547]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 May 1608: Charter by which Alexander Livingston, fiar of Hanyng, which the consent of his wife Janet Henderson, confirms that he has sold the lands of Easter and Wester Ballinbreich, in the barony of Manuell and sheriffdom o
2 CONC f Stirling, to James Polworth, younger of Couston, and his wife Elizabeth Livingstone. James and Elizabeth's charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 15 September 1608. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnis
2 CONC i06scot/page/787 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1593-1608, charter number 2150 on p. 787]'''
2 CONT
