2 CONT [http://books.google.com/books?id=bS42AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA265&lpg=PA265&dq=Robert+Ker+1500&source=bl&ots=iOETQfgphY&sig=7toW2p9s8EXYlUzLwFF4DgAst0E&hl=en&ei=CvQ8TOnyKIbmsQP8rcnaCg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CCYQ6AEwBA#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Robert%20Ker%201500&f=false  The Universal magazine, Volume 60 Pg. 264 Pub. for J. Hinton, 1777]  has Christian as the daughter of Thomas' brother Philip, BUT [https://archive.org/details/rutherfurdsoftha00ruth/page/n23
2 CONC /mode/2up ''The Rutherfurds of that Ilk, and their cadets'' by Rutherfurd, Family of, of Rutherfurd; Cockburn-Hood, Thomas H pub 1884] has her as the daughter of Thomas; and [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera02byuburk/p
2 CONC age/1390/mode/2up?view=theater  ''Burke's Landed Gentry'' pub 1833] has Philip's daughter, Christian (who ''Rutherfords'' calls Catherine) marrying  James  Stuart, ancestor  to  the  Earls  of  Traquair.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT In [https://archive.org/details/rutherfurdsoftha00ruth/page/n23/mode/2up  
2 CONT (Rutherfurds of that Ilk, and their cadets by Thomas H. Cockburn-Hood, pub. 1884) pg x]
2 CONT
2 CONT He [James] died in the year 1493, and by the said Margaret, a daughter of the Lord Erskine, he had issue two sons and one daughter :
2 CONT &
2 CONT I. Philip, his apparent heir.
2 CONT II. '''Thomas, who at last became heir-male of the family, as will be shown hereafter.
2 CONT His daughter Christian was married to Sir Robert Ker''', only son and apparent heir of Sir Walter Ker of Cessford, ancestor of the Duke of Roxburgh. [1-Charta penes ducem de Roxburgh, ad annum 1484.]
2 CONT
