1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR PATRICK CRICHTON OF CRANSTON-RIDDELL===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Bogus Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Patrick Crichton of Cranston-Riddell, here treated, has been identified as the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Crichton-of-Sanquhar-Kt/6000000006444623396?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1605004019380&through=600
2 CONC 0000002005914231 but this is quite wrong [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/cc4rz/crichton03.php Stirnet: Crichton 03]''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of Identity===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Crichton of Cranston-Riddell, here treated, is the son and heir of https://www.geni.com/people/David-Crichton-of-Cranston-Riddell/6000000162117930821?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1604954436671&through=6000000162127350821 Hi
2 CONC s father resigned the lands of Cranston-Riddell in his favour and his charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 25 July 1468. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/198/mode/1up RMS, 1424-1513: 95
2 CONC 6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Crichton of Cranston-Riddell, here treated, married Katherine Turing. A date for the marriage has not been identified but they were married  before 14 July 1488, the date upon which the lands of Ralestoun were set in re
2 CONC ntal to them for three years. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof10scot/page/630/mode/1up RSRS 10: 630]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 July 1468: Charter by which James III, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Cranstoune-Redale in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh to PATRICIO DE CREICHTOUN son and heir of his household squire, DAVID de C. The l
2 CONC ands of Cranstoune-Redale had previously been resigned by DAVID CREICHTOUN, who reserved his own liferent and the terce of his wife MERGARETE SCHAW. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/198/mode/1up RMS, 1424-1
2 CONC 513: 956]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 January 1477-78: Nisbet: Instrument of resignation by David Creichtone of Cranstoune in the hands of the king of the lands of Nesbat in the constabulary of Haddington in favour of himself for annexation thereof to the barony
2 CONC  of Cranstone Riddale. Witnesses: Alexander Lesly, Receiver General, John Haldane of Rusky, Alexander Guthre of that ilk, James Shaw younger, James Balfoure, William Mane. Notary (imperial and royal): Thomas Colly. [http://catalog
2 CONC ue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f3%2f490&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Creichtone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothi
2 CONC an Muniments), reference GD40/3/490]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 April 1485:  Instrument of sasine in favour of Patrick Creichtoun as heir to David Creichtone of Cranstone Riddall, his father, in the lands of Nesbete, following on precept from Chancery. Witnesses: John Cokburne of Tempill
2 CONC hall, Mr James Crechtone, vicar of Cranstone, Mr William Creichtone, clerk, John Huntare, Richard Diesone, Thomas Warandare, Robert Eglyntone, William Cokburne, George Cokburne, John Crosare, (?) serjeant of the king. Sheriff in t
2 CONC hat part depute: John Hepburne. Notary (imperial and royal): William Henrison. [Sheriff's seal, defaced.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f3%2f491&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=crei
2 CONC chtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), reference GD40/3/491]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 July 1488: ASSEDACIO TERRARUM DE KlLMERNO, FACTA APUD STRIVELING XIIII 0 die mensis Julii anno etc. lxxxviii 0 , per venerabilem in Cristo patrem Henricum abbatem de Cambuskenneth, Robertum dominum Lile, Johannem dominum Dru
2 CONC mmond, justiciarios DOMINI REGIS, MAGISTRUM ALEXANDRUM INGLIS. . . . . . Ralestoun assedatur Katerine sponse Patricii Crechton de Cranstoun pro terminis trium annorum, inde pecunia xij li. cum serviciis debitis et consuetis, grass
2 CONC uma tantum. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof10scot/page/630/mode/1up RSRS 10: 630]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 January 1689: Kilmernok, xiij Januarii anno prescripto. Railstoun, quam Katrina Turing, nunc sponsa Patricii Crechton de Cranstoun Riddale, prius habuit - Railstoun - in assedacione, de expresso consensu ipsius Katrine ac ec
2 CONC iam per literas suppremi domini nostri regis suo secreto sigillo, assedatur Archibaldo Diksoun et Mariote Mowbra ejus sponse conjunctim et divisim pro terminis novemdecim annornm, etc. prout in dictis literis lacius continetur, qu
2 CONC e litere sunt de data primi Junii anni Domini etc. octuagesiminoni. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof10scot/page/661/mode/1up RSRS 10: 661]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 October 1490: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Nesbit in the [barony of Cranstoun-Riddale], constabulary of Haddington and sheriffdom of Edinburgh, to his familiar [gentleman]
2 CONC  PATRICIO CREICHTOUN DE CRANSTOUN-RIDDALE and KATERINE TURING his spouse. The lands were to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent and, following their decease, by any of Patricio's lawful heirs whatsoever. Patricio had prev
2 CONC iously resigned these land in order to ontain a new grant in favour of himself and his wife. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/414/mode/1up RMS, 1424-1513: 1975]'''
