2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT “Edinburgh Castle - The Medieval Documents”. [https://pub-prod-sdk.azurewebsites.net/api/file/5b6df16d-ed5e-4d46-beca-aae700b5c941 PDF] page 150
2 CONT
2 CONT >1495: In Yarrow, the fermes of the two places of Easter and Wester Mountberger (Montbergeris Estier et Westir Cranston Riddell (Captain of Edinburgh Castle) for £100 annually to be paid at St (£133 6s 8d), as appears in previous 
2 CONC accounts, allowing that it should pay £100 by remaining with Patrick Crichton above in the present account was allocated to him in part-payment of his fee for keeping of Edinburgh Castle, which is agreed upon with him (super quo c
2 CONC ompotandum est cum eodem), because Laurence, Lord Oliphant, then captain of the said castle, is fully paid up to Martinmas term 1493, and the said Patrick entered after him in the first week of Lent (ER x. 503 5). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Following on from an isolated hint in 1459, this shows that the captain of the Castles salary was being paid from the profits of sheep flocks of Border shillings; initially running the shielings in question as a commercial ventur
2 CONC e, and the king first reduced the royal profits, then simply demitted them back to him as his pay.
2 CONT
