2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Bogus Genealogy'''<blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Darryl Lundy's Peerage claims that Janet Crichton, here treated, is the granddaughter of a man named John Crichton, and a wife named Christian Grenislaw, and that she was the daughter of Patrick Crichton, who was th
2 CONC eir son.Evidence whivh might support this claim is not identified, but it appears to have been founded upon information byTim Boyle, who sent it by email to Darryl Lundy. This is quite wrong. [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2982.htm#i
2 CONC 29813 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of Identity===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the Scots Peerage, Janet Crichton, here, treated, is the dughter of Patrick Crichton of Cranstoun-Riddell. The evidence cited confirms that John, Earl of Mortoun, married a lady named Janet Crichton, [https://archi
2 CONC ve.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/655/mode/1up RMS: 3066] but it does not identify the name of her father. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/358/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 358]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Janet Crichton, here treate. She was still alive on 22 February 1506-07. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/655/mode/1up RMS: 3066]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 March 1501-02: Charter by Jonet Bell, sister and heir of deceased Thomas Bell, to John, earl of Mortoun, and Jonet Creichtoun, his spouse, of a tenement in Blackfriars' wynd in Edinburgh, lying between the abbot of Abirbroth
2 CONC ok's land on the south, deceased Thomas Broune's land on the north, said wynd on the east and tenement of abbot of Melrose on the west. Sealed with the seal of John Bissait, bailie giving sasine. Witnesses: James Giffert of Sheref
2 CONC hall, John Todrik, Thomas Beynstoun, William Giffert, Thomas Almeross, James Monynet, notary, William Thomsoun and Andrew Grahame, serjeants. [Seal.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD
2 CONC 150%2f773&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+earl+of+mortoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1480&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/773]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 February 1506-07: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Abirdour in the regality of Dalkeith and sheriffdom of Fife, to John, Earl of Mortoun, and his wife Jonete Creichtoun, to be
2 CONC  held by them in conjunct fee and liferent, and by their male heirs, whom failing by the Earl's nearest heirs whatsover. The Earl of Mortoun had previously resigned this land into the king's hands in order to obtain a new grant in
2 CONC  favour of himself and his wife.  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/655/mode/1up RMS, 1424-1513: 3066]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/358/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 358]
2 CONT # [https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00105287&tree=LEO Genealogics]
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2982.htm#i29813 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Janet Crichton was the daughter of Sir Patrick Crichton. She married John Douglas, 2nd Earl of Morton, son of James Douglas, 1st Earl of Morton and Joan Stewart, before 1493.1,2 She died after 1515.1 After her marriage, Janet C
2 CONC richton was styled as Countess of Morton before 1493. From before 1493, her married name became Douglas. Children of Janet Crichton and John Douglas, 2nd Earl of Morton Lady Elizabeth Douglas+ d. 2 May 1527 James Douglas, 3rd Earl
2 CONC  of Morton+2 d. Dec 1548 Richard Douglas3 Lady Agnes Douglas+3 b. c 1505'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''PLEASE NOTE: JANET CRICHTON DID NOT BECOME JANET DOUGLAS, FOLLOWING HER MARRIAGE TO JOHN DOUGLAS, EARL OF MORTON. TO SUGGEST THAT SHE ADOPTED DOUGLAS AS HER MARRIED NAME IS ABSURD!
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Crichton was the daughter of Sir Patrick Crichton.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married John Douglas, 2nd Earl of Morton, son of James Douglas, 1st Earl of Morton and Joan Stewart, before 1493[1],[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT As a result of her marriage, Janet Crichton was styled as Countess of Morton before 1493. From before 1493, her married name became Douglas.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She died after 1515.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Janet Crichton and John Douglas, 2nd Earl of Morton
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Elizabeth Douglas+ d. 2 May 1527
2 CONT James Douglas, 3rd Earl of Morton+[2] d. Dec 1548 Richard Douglas[3] Lady Agnes Douglas+[3] b. c 1505 Janet Crichton was born before 1500. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 231. ↑ 2.0 2.1 2.2 Mosley, Charles, editor. Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes.
2 CONC  Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003. Volume 2, page 2786. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Mosley, Charles, editor. Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, Volume 2, page 2787 ↑ http://www.thepeerage.com/p2982.
2 CONC htm#i29813 Royal Ancestry D. Richardson 2013 Vol. I p. 659 From earlier profile to be checked and incorperated in narrative above.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Douglas, 2nd Earl Morton, 4th Lord Dalkeith married Janet Crichton, daughter of Patrick Crichton; They had 2 sons (James, 3rd Earl of Morton; & Richard) & 2 daughters (Beatrice (Elizabeth), wife of Robert, Lord Keith; & A
2 CONC gnes, wife of Alexander, 5th Lord Livingston).2,3 Sir John Douglas, 2nd Earl Morton, 4th Lord Dalkeith was born before 1466 at of Dalkeith, Midlothian, Scotland.3 He and Elizabeth Graham were engaged on 30 June 1466.5 Sir John Dou
2 CONC glas, 2nd Earl Morton, 4th Lord Dalkeith died between 19 July 1511 and September 1515.3 Family 1 Janet Crichton d. a 28 Jul 1514 Children Elizabeth (Beatrix) Douglas+ d. b 25 Jul 1527 James Douglas, 3rd Earl Morton+2,3 d. b 4 Nov 
2 CONC 1550 Richard Douglas Agnes Douglas+6 Family 2 Elizabeth Graham b. c 1455
