1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARTIN CRICHTON OF CRANSTON-RIDDELL===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Martin Crechtoun (1526) Martin Creichtoun son of James Creichtoun of Cranstounriddell (1527) Martin Creichtoun son of James Creichtoun of Cranstounriddell (1528) Martino Creichtoun brother german of James Creichtoun
2 CONC  of Cranstoun-Riddale (1535) Martin Crichtoun (1540) Martin Crechtoun heir of his nephew James Crechtoun of Cranstoun Riddale (1551) Martino Creichtoun of Cranstoun Riddale (1558)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/n558/mode/1up SQUIRE OR GENTLEMAN IN THE HOUSEHOLD OF JAMES V KING OF SCOTS]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Martin Crichton, here treated, was appointed as a squire and gentleman in the household of James V, King of Scots, on 2 August 1526. His appointment was to last for his lifetime. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00sc
2 CONC otgoog/page/n558/mode/1up RSS I: 3463] He was the son of James Crichton of Cranston-Riddell.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD328%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=martin+crichtoun&ko=
2 CONC p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD328/30]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 20 February 1527 he had a precept of sasine for half the lands of Mychelstoun in the lordship of Weddale, resigned in his favour by Egidia Cranstoun, sister and heir of Patrick Cranston of Rochebyres,  [http://catalogue.nrsc
2 CONC otland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD328%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=martin+crichtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD328/30] which lands he subsequently gave to James Hoppringle. His charter in Hoppringl
2 CONC e's favour is dated 28 February 1528. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD328%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=martin+crichtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD328/30]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Martin Crichton, here treated, is identified as the son of James Crichton of Cranston-Riddell in a precept of sasine in his favour dated 20 February 1527, [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refe
2 CONC rence=GD328%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=martin+crichtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD328/30] and a charter in his favour dated 19 November 1535. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?referenc
2 CONC e=GD328%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=martin+crichtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD328/30] His brother James succeeded to Cranston-Riddell before 19 November 1535, upon which date Martin is noticed as the brother german of 
2 CONC James Crichton of Cranston-Riddell. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/337/mode/1up RMS, 1513-46: 1524]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Martin Crichton's elder brother, James Crechtoun of Cranstoun-Riddale, and his son and heir, also named James Crichton of Cranston-Riddell, both died before 4 August 1551, upon which date Martin Crichton is noticed as the heir 
2 CONC of his nephew, the deceased James Crechtoun of Cranstoun-Riddale. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=AD1%2f108&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cranstoun-riddale&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n Natio
2 CONC nal Records of Scotland, Crown Office Writs, reference AD1/108] On 20 June 1588 he is noticed as Martin Creichtoun of Cranstoun-Riddail. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/288/mode/1up RMS, 1546-1580: 1286]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 August 1526: Ane Lettre to MARTIN CRECHTOUN, - makand him squyar and gentilman in our soverane lordis hous for all the dais of his life : And for his gud service to be done thairin our soverane lord gevis and grantis to him i
2 CONC n his fee the soum of xl lib. . . . . . . to be payit to him yeirlie at Witsonday and Martimes in winter be even portionis of the reddiest of his casualiteis be his thesaurare . . . . . ; togidder with mete [and] drynk to himself,
2 CONC  his servand and twa hors . . . . . , and liveray claithis, to be pait to him zeirlie be his comptrollar . . . . . Per Signaturam manu Regis subscriptam. vi. 17 et vii. 16. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/pa
2 CONC ge/n558/mode/1up RSS I: 3463]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 February 1527: Precept of sasine, grant by Egidia Cranstoun, sister and heir of Patrick C. of Rochebyres, with consent of Edward Auchinlek of Kylbank her husband, of her half of the lands of Mychelstoun in the lordship of We
2 CONC ddale to MARTIN CREICHTOUN son of JAMES C. OF CRANSTOUNRIDDELL, reserving one house and one acre to the superior, 20 Feb. 1527. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD328%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=
2 CONC n&tn=n&tp=n&k=martin+crichtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Messrs Scott Moncrieff and Traills, W.S., reference GD328/30]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 February 1528: Charter by Egidia Cranstoun, sister and heir of Patrick C. of Rochebyres, with consent of Edward Auchinlek of Kylbank her husband, of her half of the lands of Mychelstoun in the lordship of Weddale to MARTIN C
2 CONC REICHTOUN son of JAMES C. OF CRANSTOUNRIDDELL, reserving one house and one acre to the superior, 23 Feb.1528. Instrument recording renunciation of right of redemption, 4 Apr. 1531. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecata
2 CONC logue/details.aspx?reference=GD328%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=martin+crichtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Messrs Scott Moncrieff and Traills, W.S., reference GD328/30]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 April 1561: Charter by which Martin Crichton of Cranston-Riddell confirms that he has sold the lands and barony of Cranston-Riddell in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh to his cousin [Note] Master James Crichton: "M. JACOBO CREYCHT
2 CONC OUN consobrino suo". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/345/mode/1up RMS, 1546-1580: 1505]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: The latin word consobrino is used but this term probably includes nephews.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 April 1561: Charter by which Martin Crichton of Cranston-Riddell has sold the lands of Catslak in the lordship of Ettrick Forrest and sheriffdom of Selkirk to his cousin [Note] Master James Cricton: "M. JACOBO CREYCHTOUN cons
2 CONC obrino suo". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/345/mode/1up RMS, 1546-1580: 1506]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: The latin word consobrino is used but this term probably includes nephews.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 November 1535: Charter by which James V, King of Scots, confirms possession of the barony of Frendraucht, the barony of Inverkeithnye, and the barony of Mailherb and Forgundeviny, to his household servant Sir James Creichtou
2 CONC n of Frendraucht, to be held by him and the lawful heirs male of his body, whom failing by George C., grandson of the deceased Gavin C. brother of the late William, Lord C., and his heirs, whom failing by James C. second son of Si
2 CONC r John C. of Strathurd, and his heirs, whom failing by Robert C. his brother, and his heirs, whom failing by MARTINO C[REICHTOUN]. brother german of JAC. C[REICHTOUN]. OF CRANSTOUN-RIDDALE, captain of Edinburgh Castle, and his hei
2 CONC rs, who failing to John C. of Innernyte, and his heirs. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/337/mode/1up RMS, 1513-46: 1524]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 February 1540: Charter by MARTIN CRICHTOUN to James Hoppringle, brother of Robert H. of Blindlee, of half of Michelstoun, 7 Nov. 1540. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD328%2f30&s
2 CONC t=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=martin+crichtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Messrs Scott Moncrieff and Traills, W.S., reference GD328/30]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 August 1551: Special retour before Mr. John Sinclare, sheriff depute of Edinburgh and sheriff of Selkirk in hac parte, by John Ker of Farnyhirst, kt., David Crechtoun of Nachtane, Gilbert Wauchope of Nudry Mershale, Robert Fa
2 CONC irlie of Braid, James Ker of Mersingtoun, John Hoppringle of that ilk, Thomas Fawside of that ilk, Patrick Crechtoun of Logtoun, Alexander Crechtoun of Newhall, William Crechtoun of Drylaw, John Rutherfurde of Hunthill, John Halde
2 CONC n of that ilk, Michael Tulloch of Hilcarny, David Kincaid of Coittis and Alexander Hume in Northberwik, in favour of MARTIN CRECHTOUN as heir to deceased JAMES CRECHTOUN OF CRANSTOUN RIDDALE, his nephew, in place and lands of Cats
2 CONC lak, places and lands of Eister and Wester Montberngear and place and lands of Blakgrane, in lordship of Ettrik forest, sheriffdom of Selkirk. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=AD1%2f108
