2 CONC iptam summam septuaginta librarum trium solidorum et iiijo' denariorum absque quibus- cunque ovibus seu bonis domini regis. Holele, xxiiij B. x s. , Thornelee, xxiiij B. X s., nunc assedantur in feodifirma Patricio Creichtoun fili
2 CONC o Patricii Creichtoun de Cranstoun Riddale, militis, inde solvendo annuatim videlicet pro dicto loco de Holole xxvj B. et pro dicto loco de Thornele XXV j B., absque introitu ex consideratione commissariorum. [https://archive.org/
2 CONC details/exchequerrollsof13scot/page/654/mode/1up RSRS XIII: 654]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 December 1507: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Gilbertoun in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh to Patrick Creichtoun, son of his househild [squire] Patrick Creichtpun of Cranston-r
2 CONC iddale. The lands of Gilbertoun had previously resigned by John Creichtoun of Burnistoun, who reserved his own liferent and the rerce of his wife Jonet Hammyltoun. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/677/mode/
2 CONC 1up RMS, 1424-1513: 3167]'''
2 CONT
