2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Book of John Foular===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 May 1528: William Rynd, bailie, passed to the back land of PATRICK CREICHTOUN, son and heir of the late PATRICK CREICHTOUN OF CRANSTON RIDDAILL, in which James McClzeane now dwells, on the north side of the High Street, with
2 CONC in a tenement of the late William Cranston of Rathobyres, and bounded as before described; and there the said PATRICK CREICHTOUN resigned the foresaid back-land, with halls, chambers, etc., in the hands of the bailie, who gave sas
2 CONC ine of the foresaid back-land, halls, chambers, cellars and kitchen thereof, to a prudent woman, Jonet Turing, relict of William Adamson, in life-rent, and to Alexander Adamson, son of the said Jonet, his heirs and assignees, in f
2 CONC ee, under reversion of £140 by the said Alexander and his heirs to the said PATRICK, upon the redemption being made of the said back-land. Witnesses: Sir David Youngm crate of St. Giles Kirk, George Ur, John Lyntoun, Robert Adamso
2 CONC n, Alexander Rynde, Robert Mason, John Bartilmo, and David Purves, serjeant. The same day etc., PATRICK CREICHTOUN obliged himself and his heirs, that whensoever it should happen him and his heirs to loose the said back-land from 
2 CONC the foresaid Alexander Adamson, his heirs or assignees, by payment of the said sum of £140, that then he shall resign the said land, and shall infeft KATHERINE TURING, his mother, therein in liferent. And thereupon Sir David Young
2 CONC , curate, asked instruments. [The Protocol Book of John Foular, 1528-1534. Edited by John Durkan, D.Litt. (Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1985) protocol number 11 on pp. 4-5]'''
2 CONT
