2 CONT Gen. III (this Generation: Sir William Kerr b. Scotland 16 May 1542. m. Mary Ann Clifford Carr, sister of Lord Somerset. Sir Wm changed the name to Kelso, then to Carr
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT William Ker, son of Sir John Kerr and Katherine (Kerr) Kerr, was a staunch Royalist, who was of good and faithful service to Queen Mary and was in 1561 settled with a pension of 500 merks. In 1554 he was mentioned in the minutes o
2 CONC f the Regality Court of Cavers. He was still living in 1561, when involved in a '''suit. He died without issue.'''[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Since he died childless he could not be the father of Benjamin Carr alleged parents of New England immigrants Robert and Caleb Carr or the other children attached at Wikitree.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
