2 CONT Biography source below from  :- Turnbull, Albert. (2018). The Turnbull Pedigree. Paragon Publishing. p. 25.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was born about 1520. He died about 1572.
2 CONT According to Turnbull (2018), “Sir Thomas 1520 -1572, Baron of Minto, married Mary Kerr. Because of a later court case his 9 sons and daughter were named: William1541; Hector c. 1542; Thomas 1550; James 1546; Margaret 1548; Mark 1
2 CONC 549; Patrick 1551; Andrew 1555; Robert 1558 and Walter 1560 -1623”.
2 CONT His father was George Turnbull (1453-1522), and his mother was Janet Kerr (1445- ). They were married about 1480. George is noted at the Battle of Sclaterford, in 1513, when he rallied 700 Turnbull, Kerr, Scott and Douglas rievers
2 CONC  and defeated Lord Dacre's army, reputedly some 5000 strong in the Rule valley. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional sources are available at :-
2 CONT Hawick Records Archives, Turnbull registrations in Roxburghshire. Land Owners and Tenants 
