1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN EDMONSTONE OF THAT ILK AND EDNAM===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Edam, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Edmonstone-of-that-Ilk-and-Ednam/6000000176594644857?through=6000000176594826851 and the grandson of https://www.geni.com/
2 CONC people/John-Edmonstone-of-Edmonstone-and-Ednam/6000000041815308823 His mother is https://www.geni.com/people/Alison-Cockburn/6000000176639722829?through=6000000176594826851 On 2 February 1594 he had a charter under the Great Seal 
2 CONC of Scotland which confirmed his possession of barony of Ednam in the sheriffdom of Roxburgh, and other lands in the sheriffdoms of Berwick and Edinburgh. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/17/mode/1up RMS 159
2 CONC 3-1608: 56]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, died before 15 July 1630, the date upon which Master James RaIth and his wife Elize Foullar were confirmed in their possession of Edmondstoun. [https://archive.org/detail
2 CONC s/registrummagnisi08scot/page/533/mode/1up RMS 1620-33: 1601]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 February 1593-94: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms possession of of the land and barony of Ednam in the sheriffdom of Roxburgh to JOANNI EDMONDSTOUN son and heir apparent of 
2 CONC Andree Edmondstoun fiar of that Ilk (feodatarii de eodem). The charter also confirms his possession of the lands of Ryislaw and Little Blakburne in the sheriffdom of Berwick, and a one third part of the land and mill of Nudrie-Mer
2 CONC schell in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh. The office of Coroner of Lothian was also confirmed to him. Andrew's father Sir John Edmondstoun of that Ilk continued to hold a liferent interest in these lands, and after his decease this w
2 CONC as to pass to Andrew. John Edmondstoun junior, and his lawful heirs, were to hold these lands, whom failing they were to pass to Patrick Edmondstoun, brother german of Sir John, whom failing they were to pass to Andrew's nearest m
2 CONC ale heir bearing the name and arms of Edmondstoun. John Edmonston, junior, is said to be the grandson of Sir John Cockburn of Ormiston by his daughter Alison Cockburn: "D. Joannis Cokburne de Ormestoun militis justiciarie clerici,
2 CONC  avi dicti Jo. E. minoris (ex quondam Alisona C. ejus filia legitima nati)". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/17/mode/1up RMS 1593-1608: 56]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 June 1614: Contract of Marriage between John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Anne Stirling. On 19 July 1614, Anne Stirling, identified as the future wife of John Edmonstone of that Ilk, had a charter confirming her liferent intere
2 CONC st in the lands of Ryslaw in the sheriffdom of Berwick, and the lands of Edmam in the sheriffdom of Roxburgh. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/579/mode/1up RMS 1609-20: charter number 1608]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 September 1627: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which King Charles I confirms that Mr. Alexander Morriesoun of Prestongrange has resigned in favour of Master Janes Raith, Advocate, and his wife Elize Fouller, the
2 CONC  ville and lands of Edmonstoun called the Maynes of Edmonstoun, and the lands of Cauldcoittis, in the regality of Mussleburgh and sheriffdom of Edinburgh, together with a one third part of the land and mill of Nudrie-Merschell. Hi
2 CONC s resignation was made with the consent of a number of interested parties, including Sir John Edmonstoun of that Ilk and his wife Lady Jean Lawson: "consensu D. Joannis Edmonstoun de eodem militis et Domine Jeanne Lawsoun ejus con
2 CONC jugis". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/401/mode/1up RMS 1620-33: charter number 1150]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 July 1630: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland made in favour of Master James Raith, Advocate, and his wife Elize Foullar, by which King Charles I confirms their possession of the town and lands of Edmondstoun. This lan
2 CONC d had previously been owned by the deceased Andrew Edmondstoun of that Ilk and his son, the also now deceased Sir John Edmondstoun of that Ilk, who had disposed of it to Master James Raith and his wife Elize: "per quond. And. Edmo
2 CONC ndstoun de eodem et quond. D. Jo. E. ejus filium edificatis et per dictum D. Jo. dictis Jac. et El. dispositis". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/533/mode/1up RMS 1620-33: charter number 1601]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 November 1633: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland in favour of Sir David Creichtoun of Lugtoun-Crichtoun, which identifies one of his tenants at Gilmertoun as John Edmonstone, now of Ednam, heir apparent of his grandfa
2 CONC ther, the deceased Andrew Edmonstone of that Ilk, and his father, the deceased Sir John Edmonstone of that Ilk as the son and heir apparent of the deceased Andrew: "que fuerunt Jo. Edmestoun tunc de Ednem, heredis apparentis quond
2 CONC am Andree E. de eodem ejus avi, saltern quond. D. Joannis E. de eodem filii et heredis apparentis dicti And. ac patris dicti Jo". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/759/mode/1up RMS 1620-33: charter number 22
2 CONC 54]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Printed Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/n5/mode/1up  Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1593-1608. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, M.A., Advocate (H. M. G
2 CONC eneral Register House, Edinburgh, 1890), 1142 pp. including indexes and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/n5/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1609-1620. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, M.A., Advocate (H. M. Ge
2 CONC neral Register House, Edinburgh, 1890), 1152 pp. including indexes and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/n5/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1620-1633. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, M.A., Advocate (H. M. Ge
2 CONC neral Register House, Edinburgh, 1894), 1075 pp. including indexes]'''
