2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Edmonstone of Newton, here treated, is the brother of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Edmonstone-of-that-Ilk-and-Ednam/6000000176594826851?through=6000000176609625884 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                       1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 November 1580: Letters of Reversion by Patrick Edmonstoun, portioner of Natoun, and Marion Hepburne, his spouse, to John Pennycuik, fiar of that ilk, and his spouse, of 85 merks annualrent furth of the lands of Slipperfield 
2 CONC called Yowthrid in the barony of Brochtoun, sheriffdom of Peblis. Dated at Edinburgh 21 November 1580. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=B48%2f19%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+e
2 CONC dmonstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Records of Linlithgow Burgh, B48/19/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 January 1583-84: Letters of Reversion granted by Patrick Edmestoun [Edmonstone] of Natoun [Newton] and Marion Hepburne [Hepburn], his spouse, to John Pennycuke [Penicuik], yr, of that ilk, and Euphamia Bruce, his spouse, of 
2 CONC subjects as in GD18/45 on delivery of 900 merks Scots together with 19 year tack of the said lands. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD18%2f48&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Edmonstone+of+N
2 CONC atoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of Clerk family of Penicuik, Midlothian, reference GD18/48]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 August 1589: Reversion by Patrick Edmonstoun [Edmiston] of Newtoune [Newton] and Marion Hepburne [Hepburn], his spouse, to John Sinclair, son and apparent heir of John Sinclair of Drydane [Dryden], of lands in GD18/522 on pa
2 CONC yment of 3,000 merks. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD18%2f524&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+edmonstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Clerk f
2 CONC amily of Penicuik, Midlothian, reference GD18/524]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                   4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 February 1593-94: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms possession of of the land and barony of Ednam in the sheriffdom of Roxburgh to JOANNI EDMONDSTOUN son and heir apparent of 
2 CONC Andree Edmondstoun fiar of that Ilk (feodatarii de eodem). The charter also confirms his possession of the lands of Ryislaw and Little Blakburne in the sheriffdom of Berwick, and a one third part of the land and mill of Nudrie-Mer
2 CONC schell in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh. The office of Coroner of Lothian was also confirmed to him. Andrew's father Sir John Edmondstoun of that Ilk continued to hold a liferent interest in these lands, and after his decease this w
2 CONC as to pass to Andrew. John Edmondstoun junior, and his lawful heirs, were to hold these lands, whom failing they were to pass to Sir John's brother Patrick Edmondstoun of Newton, and his heirs, whom failing they were to pass to An
2 CONC drew's nearest male heir bearing the name and arms of Edmondstoun. John Edmonston, junior, is said to be the grandson of Sir John Cockburn of Ormiston by his daughter Alison Cockburn: "D. Joannis Cokburne de Ormestoun militis just
2 CONC iciarie clerici, avi dicti Jo. E. minoris (ex quondam Alisona C. ejus filia legitima nati)". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/17/mode/1up RMS 1593-1608: 56]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 May 1598: Disposition by Patrick Edmonstoun [Edmonstone] of Natoun [Newton] and Marion Hepburn, his spouse, in favour of John Creichtoun [Crichton] of Brunstoun [Brunstane] of the west half of the lands of Auchincorth in prin
2 CONC cipal and lands of Newbiggingis [Newbigging] in warrandice all lying in the barony of Pennycuke [Penicuik] and sheriffdom of Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD18%2f72&st=1&t
