1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR WILLIAM SCOTT OF KIRKURD knight===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Sir Walter Scott of Kirkurd. However, he is known to have  died before 8 January 1550-51, upon which date his wife Grissel Betoun is noticed as his widow. [http://catalogue.
2 CONC nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=AD1%2f106&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+Scott+of+Kirkurd&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y NRS: AD1/106]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 January 1550-51: Royal letters, with consents of James, duke of Chattelarault, earl of Arrane, Lord Hammiltoun, protector and governor of the realm, and of William, commendator of Culross, comptroller, discharging Grissel Bet
2 CONC oun, relict of William Scott of Kirkurd, kt., of maills of steading and lands of Harterne (?) (£30), steading and lands of Fawsyid (40 merks), steading and lands of Williamhoip (£12), in lordship of Ettrik forest, in respect of ye
2 CONC ar 1550 and all preceding years. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=AD1%2f106&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+Scott+of+Kirkurd&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotlan
2 CONC d, Crown Office Writs, reference AD1/106]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 February 1551: Extract Registered Contract of Marriage between Andro Murray of Blackbarony and Dame Grissale Betoun [Beaton] relict of umquhile William Scott of Kyrkhurd [Kirkurd], kt, whereby the said Andro resigns for new i
2 CONC nfeftment in favour himself and his said wife "his gret lugeing bak land and foreland under and above with the pertinents lyand in Bells wynd within the Burgh of Edinburgh also the lands of Ballincrieff [Ballencrieff, Aberlady pa.
2 CONC , East Lothian] and Pvray (Poverhouse) with their pertinents". It contains an obligation by Walter Scott of Branxholm [Branxholme], kt, and Robert Betoun of Creith [Creich] to pay 1200 marks to the said Andro Murray. Recorded in t
2 CONC he Books of Counsel. Witnesses: John Bellenden of Auchnoull, Justice Clerk, Robert Betoun of Creith, Patrick Murray of Fallowhill [Falahill], Archybald Douglas of Kilspyndi [Kilspindie], Maister John Scrymgeour [Scrimgeour] of the
2 CONC  Myris, Maister Thomas Westoun [Weston] and James Nicolsoun [Nicholson]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD32%2f2%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Patrick+Murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1601
2 CONC &di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Viscounts and Barons of Elibank, reference GD32/2/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 March 1554-55: Instrument of Sasine following on a precept of clare constat by Walter Scot, grandson of deceased Walter Scot of Branxholm, knight, and son of deceased William Scot of Kirkurd, knight, with consent of Robert S
2 CONC cot of Allanhauch, his tutor, in favour of James Geddes as heir to Edward Geddes, his father, in lands in GD89/1/311.  Dated 19 March 1554[/5] and witnessed by William Gib, James Naper, John Melros and Sir John Allane, notary publ
2 CONC ic, 26 March, 1555. Witnesses: James Allane, William Thomsone, John Gib and James Murhouse. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD89%2f1%2f322&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kirkurd&ko=p&r=&ro
2 CONC =s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Carmichael Family of Skirling, reference GD89/1/322]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p1031.htm#i10306 BIOGRAPHICAL ACCOUNT COPIED FROM DARRYL LUNDY'S PEERAGE]
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Sir William Scott of Kirkurd and Buccleuch, younger1
2 CONT *'''M, #10306, b. circa 1525, d. before 19 May 1552
2 CONT *Last Edited=30 Mar 2007
2 CONT *'''     Sir William Scott of Kirkurd and Buccleuch, younger was born circa 1525.2 He was the son''' of Sir Walter Scott, 3rd of Buccleuch and Elizabeth Carmichael.3 '''He married Grizel Bethune''', daughter of Sir John Bethune, 2
2 CONC nd of Creich and Janet Hay, '''circa 1548.3,2 He died before 19 May 1552.3
2 CONT *'''     He fought in the Battle of Pinkie on 10 September 1547.3 He lived at Branxholm, Scotland.
2 CONT *'''Child of Sir William Scott of Kirkurd and Buccleuch, younger
