1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MAJOR-GENERAL ROBERT MONTGOMERY===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Montgomery, here treated, is the fifth son of Alexander, Earl of Eglinton, and his wife Anna Livingstone. According to the Scots Peerage he: "was enrolled as a student at the University of Glasgow on 1 March 1637. He ent
2 CONC ered the army, distinguished himself in the Civil Wars, and became a major-general. He commanded a brigade at Worcester in 1651, and was forced to retreat. He was confined in Edinburgh Castle, from which he escaped in 1658, and re
2 CONC tired to Holland, whence he returned with the King. After the Restoration he was appointed one of the Gentlemen of His Majesty's Bedchamber. He died in December 1684. He married (contract dated 4 September 1662) Elizabeth, daughte
2 CONC r of James Livingstone, Viscount of Kilsyth, who survived him and married, before 24 January 1688, Captain George Douglas, brother of Sir James Douglas of Kelhead. They had issue two sons, Alexander and James, and a daughter, who 
2 CONC all died without issue.'" [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/452/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: p. 450]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/memorialsofmonv100fras/page/79/mode/1up Memorials of the Montgomeries. By William Fraser (Edinburgh 1859): pp. 79-81]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Major-General the Hon. Robert Montgomery married Elizabeth Livingston. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft#page/192/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: p. 192]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
