2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/17 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 158-1593, charter number 50 on p. 17]
2 CONT ** 5 October 1580: Elizabeth Heriot, daughter of James Heriot of Trabroun, is named as the heir remainder to Marie Maitland, daughter of Richard Maitland of Lethington, in a charter by which William, Lord Ruthven, confirms that he
2 CONC  has given an annuity of one hundred merks to Marie Maitland, to be taken from his lands and barony of Ballerno and Kirknewton in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh.
2 CONT * [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD32%2f19%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Marie+Maitland&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Viscounts and Baron
2 CONC s of Elibank, reference GD32/19/9]
2 CONT ** 22 December 1596: Copy tack by Mr James Logane [Logan] in favour of Alexander Lauder of Haltoun [Halton] and Marie Maitland his spouse of the teinds of Eister [Easter] and Wester Wormiestoun [Wormiston], also called Cringiltie 
2 CONC [Cringletie] and Stewarton, for 19 years after Lammas 1586.
