1 OCCU 3rd Earl of Wigtown
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John Fleming, 3rd Earl of Wigton''' married Lady Jean Drummond, daughter of John Drummond, 2nd Earl of Perth and Jean Ker, on 10 March 1633. He died in February 1664/65. He was the son of John Fleming, 2nd Earl 
2 CONC of Wigton and Margaret Livingstone. He gained the title of 3rd Earl of Wigton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Fleming, 3rd Earl of Wigton and Lady Jean Drummond
2 CONT * William Fleming, 5th Earl of Wigton+ d. 8 Apr 1681
2 CONT * John Fleming, 4th Earl of Wigton d. Apr 1668
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ====Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT XVII. JOHN, third earl of Wigton, who, in his father's lifetime,* got a charter under the great seal, Johanni domino Fleming, ma∣gistro de Wigton, of the lands, lordship, and barony of Cumbernauld, de novo united, 1st February 163
2 CONC 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a man of untainted honour and loyalty. He joined the king's party in the very beginning of his troubles, and never de∣serted his interest.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was with Montrose at the unfortunate battle of Philiphaugh,* and made his escape with him to the Highlands; but afterwards, by the interest of his friends, he obtained li∣berty to return home, and lived a private and retired li
2 CONC fe till the restoration.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married lady Jean Drummond, daugh∣ter of John second earl of Perth, by whom he had six sons and two daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. John, his heir.
2 CONT *2. Sir Robert.
2 CONT *3. Henry.
2 CONT *4. James.  These last three died unmarried.
2 CONT *5. William, afterwards earl of Wigton.
2 CONT *6. Charles, who died young.
2 CONT *1st daughter, lady Margaret.
2 CONT *2. Lady Jean. They both died unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT The earl died anno 1663, and was succeeded by his eldest son, XVIII. JOHN, fourth earl of Wigton, who got a charter under the great seal,*Johanni domino Fleming, et Annae Ker sponsae suae, of the earldom of Wigton, lordship of Bal
2 CONC douie, &c. 10th May 1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Links to additional information:
2 CONT *http://thepeerage.com/p3062.htm#i30613
2 CONT
2 CONT * The peerage of Scotland: containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom, ... collected from the public records, and ancient chartularies of this nation, ... Illustrated with copper-plates. By R
2 CONC obert Douglas, Esq;. Douglas, Robert, Sir, 1694-1770. [https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896980.0001.000/1:252?rgn=div1;view=fulltext link]
2 CONT * [https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I21452&tree=CC MacFarland Genealogy] cites
2 CONT *1. [S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Fleming02:.
2 CONT *2. [S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Drummond02.
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earl_of_Wigtown
2 CONT *Balfour Paul, James (1904). The Scots Peerage. Edinburgh : D. Douglas. pp. 518-558. Retrieved 19 November 2018. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/518 Archive.Org]
2 CONT *Fraser, Vol I, pp328-30 [https://archive.org/stream/douglasbook01fras#page/839/mode/2up Archive.Org]
2 CONT * The Complete Peerage, 1st edition, Volume 8, page 139 [https://archive.org/stream/completepeerage00cokagoog#page/n147/mode/2up Archive.Org] 
