1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Fleming, 4th Earl of Wigton was the son of John Fleming, 3rd Earl of Wigton and Lady Jean Drummond. He married Anne Ker, daughter of Harry Ker, on 5 December 1660. He died in April 1668.  He gained the title o
2 CONC f 4th Earl of Wigton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of John Fleming, 4th Earl of Wigton and Anne Ker
2 CONT *Jean Fleming1 d. Apr 1683.  Married George Maule.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT XVIII. JOHN, fourth earl of Wigton, who got a charter under the great seal,*Johanni domino Fleming, et Annae Ker sponsae suae, of the earldom of Wigton, lordship of Baldouie, &c. 10th May 1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT By the said Anne, a daughter of Henry lord Ker, he had only one daughter,
2 CONT *Lady Jean, married to George third earl of Panmure.
2 CONT
2 CONT And dying without male-issue, anno 1668, his estate and honours devolved upon his next surviving brother, XVIII. WILLIAM, fifth earl of Wigton, a man of great worth and merit.
2 CONT
