1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === William Fleming, 5th Earl of Wigton 
2 CONT *M, #21241, d. 8 April 1681
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 Sep 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=2.11%
2 CONT
2 CONT William Fleming, 5th Earl of Wigton was the son of John Fleming, 3rd Earl of Wigton and Lady Jean Drummond. He married Lady Henrietta Seton, daughter of Charles Seton, 2nd Earl of Dunfermline and Lady Mary Douglas, on 8 September 
2 CONC 1670. He died on 8 April 1681.1  He gained the title of 5th Earl of Wigton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT XVIII. WILLIAM, fifth earl of Wigton, a man of great worth and merit. He was one of the lords of the privy council to king Charles II. and was constituted sheriff of the county of Dunbarton, and governor of the castle; which offic
2 CONC es he enjoyed as long as he lived.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married lady Henriet Seton, daughter of Charles earl of Dunfermline, by whom he had two sons and one daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. John, his heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Charles, afterwards earl of Wigton.
2 CONT
2 CONT His daughter, lady Mary, married to Mr. Harry Maule of Kelly, father of the present earl of Panmure.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died anno 1681, and was succeeded by his eldest son,
2 CONT
2 CONT XIX. JOHN, sixth earl of Wigton, a man of great honour and integrity.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
