2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Lindsay,_9th_Earl_of_Crawford
2 CONT
2 CONT David Lindsay, 9th Earl of Crawford (died 10 September 1558) was a Scottish peer and Member of Parliament. He married Secondly, Katherine Campbell, daughter of Sir John Campbell, 1st of Cawdor and Muriel Calde, irn 1550. and they 
2 CONC had a son, John Lindsay of Balcarres, Lord Menmuir. First known as David Lindsay of Edzell, he inherited the earldom from David Lindsay, 8th Earl of Crawford by nomination, and was succeeded by the 8th earl's grandson David Lindsa
2 CONC y, 10th Earl of Crawford.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I3958&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander the son of the 8th Earl was found guilty of constructive patricide which rendered him incapable of succession. The Earldom then passed to Sir David but then went back to Alexander's son. The 9th Earl re-conveyed the Earl
2 CONC dom back to his kinsman.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Info re: Earls of Crawford http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/crawford1398.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT David Lindsay, 9th Earl of Crawford [1] 
2 CONT *M, #109234, b. before 1513, d. 20 September 1558
2 CONT *Last Edited=22 May 2007
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.02%
2 CONT
2 CONT David Lindsay, 9th Earl of Crawford was born before 1513.[2] He was the son of Walter Lindsay and unknown daughter Erskine.[3],[2] He married, firstly, Janet Gray, daughter of Patrick Gray, Master of Gray and Annabella Forbes, bef
2 CONC ore 12 June 1535.[2] He married, secondly, Katherine Campbell, daughter of Sir John Campbell, 1st of Cawdor and Muriel Calder, in 1550.[4] He died on 20 September 1558 at Invermark Castle, Angus, Scotland.[2] He was buried at Edze
2 CONC ll, Scotland. [2] His will (dated 20 September 1558) was proven (by probate) on 1 October 1558.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT David Lindsay, 9th Earl of Crawford also went by the nick-name of 'the Interpolated Earl'.[2] He succeeded as the 9th Earl of Crawford [S., 1398] on 27 November 1542.[2] He was appointed Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland] in 1546.
2 CONC [2] On 2 May 1546 he reinstated the son of his cousin, Alexander Lindsay, Master of Crawford to the Earldom of Crawford.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of David Lindsay, 9th Earl of Crawford and Katherine Campbell
2 CONT *1. Sir David Lindsay, Lord Edzell+[2] d. Dec 1610
2 CONT *2. John Lindsay of Balcarres, Lord Menmuir+[5] d. 3 Sep 1590
2 CONT *3. Sir Walter Lindsay [6]
2 CONT *4. Lady Elizabeth Lindsay+[6] d. May 1585
2 CONT *5. Lady Margaret Lindsay+[1] d. a 16 Jun 1589
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT * Scotland, Deceased in 1541 - Dundee, Angus, Scotland age at death: 41 years old 
2 CONT **(Parents : M: David LINDSAY 1471-1542 &  F: Elizabeth HAY 1475-1511) with
2 CONT * M: David LINDSAY 1527-1574  
2 CONT **married to Margaret Bethune 1525-1583 with 
2 CONT ***F: Helen Lindsay LINDSAY 1558-1579 married in March 1570, Moonzie, Fife, Scotland, to David (SIR - EARL OF CRAWFORD) LINDSAY 1551-1610 
2 CONT ****with F: Margaret LINDSAY 1575-1614
2 CONT
