1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>William Douglas of Friarshaw</strong>, second son of No. 82, died 1575. He married Euphame Davidson, who died February 1578. They had issue : — 
2 CONT * John Douglas of Friarshaw, died without issue before 1603. 
2 CONT * James Douglas. He is supposed to have died unmarried before 1603, as his brother George then had the estate of Friarshaw. 
2 CONT * George (No. 98). 
2 CONT * Andrew Douglas. He married Marion Douglas, and is mentioned in a charter 1581. He had one son: — 
2 CONT ** George Douglas, living 1600. 
2 CONT * William Douglas, had son :
2 CONT ** Robert Douglas.
2 CONT * Robert Douglas."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/heraldryofdougla00john#page/34/mode/2up The heraldry of the Douglases: with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees], by G. Harvey Johnston, Publishe
2 CONC d 1907, page 34, paragraph 97
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT When William Douglas 1st of Friarshaw was born about 1519, in Roxburghshire, Scotland, United Kingdom, his father, Sir James Douglas 5th of Cavers, was 25 and his mother, Elizabeth Murray of Falahill, was 21. He married Lady Eupha
2 CONC me Davidson McCarston about 1560, in Melrose, Roxburghshire, Scotland, United Kingdom. They were the parents of at least 2 sons. He died before 29 November 1575.
2 CONT
