1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM ELIOTT OF STOBS===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ee/elliot01.php Elliot 1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ===
2 CONT William Eliott of Stobs was a prominent Scottish landowner, clan leader, and politician during the 17th century. He served as a Member of Parliament (MP) for Roxburghshire from 1640 until 1651, navigating the family through the En
2 CONC glish Civil War. As the head of the Stobs line, he transitioned the clan from the violent ''Border Reiver'' traditions into established regional political authority.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Vital Statistics and Core Identity ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Name: William Eliott of Stobs
2 CONT * Birth: Circa 1594–1600 in Stobs, Roxburghshire, Scotland.
2 CONT * Death: July 1654.
2 CONT * Occupation/Title: Member of Parliament (MP) for Roxburgh; Laird of Stobs.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Parentage and Lineage ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father: '''Sir Gilbert Eliott of Stobs''' (d. 1624), widely famous in Border lore as '''"Gibbie wi' the Gowden Gartins"''' (Gilbert with the Golden Garters).
2 CONT * Mother: '''Margaret Scott''' (c. 1567–1651), daughter of Walter Scott of Harden ("Auld Wat") and Mary Scott ("The Flower of Yarrow").
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage and Spouse ===
2 CONT William married '''Elizabeth Douglas''' of the Cavers family.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marriage Date: After November 28, 1621, in Scotland.
2 CONT * Identity Safe-Guard: Elizabeth was the daughter of the Laird of Cavers. She is the key generational firewall; ensuring she is linked as William's wife prevents the "Marchioness of Argyll" error from bleeding backward into this g
2 CONC eneration.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Issue ===
2 CONT William and Elizabeth had a large family that solidified the Eliott footprint across the Scottish Borders:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. '''Sir Gilbert Eliott, 1st Baronet of Stobs''' (c. 1621–1677) – Eldest son, knighted banneret in 1643, created Baronet of Nova Scotia in 1666. Married (1) Isabella Cranstoun and (2) Magdalen Nicolson.
2 CONT 2. '''Archibald Eliott''' of Craigend and Deanfoot.
2 CONT 3. '''Gavin Eliott''' – Whose wife was a Nicolson.
2 CONT 4. '''William Eliott''' of Grange.
2 CONT 5. '''Richard Eliott''' of Fallahill.
2 CONT 6. '''John Eliott'''.
2 CONT 7. '''Margaret Eliott''' – Married (1) William Bennet of Grubit and (2) James Scott of Bonnington.
2 CONT 8. '''Anna Eliott''' – Married John Maxwell of Cowhill.
2 CONT 9. '''Marie Eliott''' – Married John Young of Gulyhill.
2 CONT 10. '''Isobel Eliott''' – Married Francis Scott of Arkleton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT > '''Curator's Primary Source References:'''
2 CONT > * ''The Elliots: The Story of a Border Clan, a Genealogical History'' by the Dowager Lady Eliott of Stobs and Sir Arthur Eliott, 11th Bart. of Stobs.
2 CONT > * ''Roxburghshire Parliamentary Registers'' (1640–1651 blocks).
2 CONT > * ''Cavers/Eliott Marriage Contracts'' dated Nov 1621.
