1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HUGH SOMERVILLE 6th Lord Somerville===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 December 1591: Extract letters of horning at the instance of Mr Thomas Gilbert, advocate, against Hugh, Lord Somerwell, and Walter, Master of Somerwell, in terms of a contract dated 3 Oct. 1590 by which the said Hugh and Walt
2 CONC er bound themselves to infeft the said Mr Thomas, under reversion, in the £8 lands of Muirhall and Garwodend in the barony of Carnewath and to pay a yearly maill until the expiry of the reserved liferent of Dame Agnes Hammiltoun, 
2 CONC Lady Somerwell. (Execution dated 4 Dec. 1591.) (Registered P.R. Hornings Lanark, 11 March 1591/2.) [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f4%2f152&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Somerwell&k
2 CONC o=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), Somerville Writs, reference GD40/4/152]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft#page/22/mode/2up Biographical Summary by the Scots Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT "<strong>Hugh, sixth Lord Somerville</strong>, born 1547...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He died on 24 March 1597, at Raploch, the house of Gavin Hamilton, father-in-law of his son Hugh, and was buried in the choir of the old church of Cambusnethan...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He married (contract 11 January 1557-58) Elizabeth Seton, daughter of George, fourth Lord Seton, but separated from her for no reasonable cause in 1587."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft#page/22/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VIII, page 22-24
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1046.htm#i31403 Biographical Summary by Our Royal Ancestors] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Somerville, 6th Lord Somerville1
2 CONT M, #31403, b. 1547, d. 24 March 1597
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	James Somerville, 5th Lord Somerville b. c 1518, d. Dec 1569
2 CONT Mother	Agnes Hamilton d. a 2 Aug 1597
2 CONT
2 CONT      Hugh Somerville, 6th Lord Somerville was born in 1547. He married Eleanor Seton, daughter of George Seton, 4th Lord Seton and Elizabeth Hay, on 11 January 1558; They had six additional sons (only one of whom reached maturity)
2 CONC  and two other children who also predeased their father.2 Hugh Somerville, 6th Lord Somerville and Eleanor Seton were divorced in 1587.2 Hugh Somerville, 6th Lord Somerville died on 24 March 1597 at Raploch, Scotland (house of Gav
2 CONC in Hamilton).
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Eleanor Seton d. c 1603
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT     Jean Somerville2 b. c 1565
2 CONT
2 CONT     William Somerville, Master of Somerville b. c 1566, d. Jan 1592
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert Somerville b. c 1567, d. Jul 1587
2 CONT
2 CONT     Gilbert Somerville, 7th Lord Somerville b. c 1568, d. 1618
2 CONT
2 CONT     Hugh Somerville, 8th Lord Somerville+ b. 1573, d. Apr 1640
2 CONT
2 CONT     (Miss) Somerville2 b. c 1575
2 CONT
2 CONT     Elspeth Somerville2 b. c 1577
2 CONT
2 CONT     Janet Somerville2 b. c 1580
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT     [S9664] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. XII/1, p. 99; Scot's Peerage, by Sir James Balfour Paul.
2 CONT     [S11587] The Scots Peerage, Vol. VIII, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 24.
