1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARION TWEEDIE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Marione Tweidye (1653) Marion Tuedye (1656) Mareon Twedye (1658)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Tweedie, here treated, is the daughter of John Tweedie tutor of Drummelyear. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&h
2 CONC l=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=dunlope&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc. II]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Tweedie, here treated, died in October 1652. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD89%2f1%2f390&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=templelands+of+kirkurd&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: G
2 CONC D89/1/390]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Tweedie, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Dunlop-Writer-to-the-Signet/6000000177902555831?through=6000000177901167843 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Makdalene-Dunlop/6000000177905389904?through=6000000177901167843
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Dunlop-Writer-in-Edinburgh/6000000177901571824?through=6000000177901167843
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Dunlop-Apothecary-in-Edinburgh/6000000177901292821?through=6000000177901167843
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Dunlop-Merchant-in-Edinburgh/6000000177905257864?through=6000000177901167843
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Last Will and Testament of her husband Alexander Dunlop==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Dunlop made his last will and testament on 6 July 1619, at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. He nominated and appointed William Dunlop and Alexander Dunlop, his lawful sons from his second marriage to Marion Tweedie,
2 CONC  to be his only executors, and his wife Marion Tweedie was charged to give up the inventory of his moveable estate in their name and behalf.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In addition to this he nominated and appointed John Bayne, one of the Clerks of Session, David Foullertoun, James Speir, merchant, and Mr John Dunlop, Minister of the Gospel at Ratho, identified by Alexander as his brother-germ
2 CONC an, to be tutors testamentar to John Dunlop, his eldest son from his marriage to the deceased Ellizabeth Seytoune, his first wife. He also nominated and appointed his present wife Marion Tweedie to be tutor testamentar to James Du
2 CONC nlop, their eldest son, and to William Dunlop and Alexander Dunlop, his executors, and failing her by death or re-marriage, he nominated and constituted Mr. John Bayne, James Pringle, clerk, David Foullertoun, and Mr. John Dunlop,
2 CONC  his foresaid brother-german, to be tutors testamentar to their children, that is James Dunlop, William Dunlop and Alexander Dunlop.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Dunlop, here treated, left a number of small legacies. He left his part of the free goods and gear to his executors, William Dunlop and Alexander Dunlop, to be divided equally between them. To his bastard son John Dun
2 CONC lop he left the sum of six hundred merks, money that was owed to him by James Dunlop of that Ilk. To his bastard daughter Marion Dunlop he left the sum of five hundred merks, money that was owed to him by Robert Trotter, merchant 
2 CONC in Edinburgh. He also left the sum of one hundred merks to his servant (employee) William Young, the man who wrote his last will and testament.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Dunlop of that Ilk acted himself as cautioner for Marion Tweedie, and her sons William and Alexander Dunlop, and confirmation was granted to them on 8 June 1620. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, 
2 CONC The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Alexander Dunlop, Writer to the Signet, reference CC8/8/50]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000179892533830 Image of Testament 1]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000179892386840 Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000179892772844 Image of Testament 3]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000179892370894 Image of Testament 4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                       1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 September 1653: (130) 20 Sep. 1653. PEITTER DUNLOP heir of Marione Tweidye, his gudame, - in the Kirklands of Hopekailzeo, within the parochin of Kelzeo : - E. 40 s. - the Kirklands of Drummellzear with pastourag of 48 soume
2 CONC s cattell. - E. 5m. xxi. 220. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v
2 CONC =snippet&q=%20dunlop&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum etc. II]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 August 1658: (Extract) Retour of Special Service of said Peter Dunlop as heir to said Marion Tuedye, his gradmother, who died in October, 1652, in the Templelands of Kirkurd, described in GD89/1/377. 6 August, 1656. [http://c
2 CONC atalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD89%2f1%2f390&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=templelands+of+kirkurd&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Carmichael Family of Skirl
2 CONC ing, reference GD89/1/390]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 August 1658: (145) Aug. 6, 1658. PETER DUNLOPE son to umquhill Mr. William Dunlope apothicar burges of Edinburgh, heir of Mareon Twedye daughter to John Tuedye tutor of Drummelyear, his goodame, - in the tempel-landis of Kirk
2 CONC urde, and 15 sowthes of grasse upon the common pasturage, with the teynd sheaves, with the parochine of Kirkurde.- E. 3s. xxv. 91. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=
2 CONC qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=dunlope&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc. II]'''
