1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == THOMAS FERGUSSON OF CRAIGDARROCH ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 November 1514: Thomas Fergusson, son and heir to John Fergusson, is infeft in Jerbruch, etc. [https://archive.org/details/recordsofclannam00ferg/page/378/mode/1up Records: 378]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 December 1518: Charter made in favour of Johanni  Adamsoun, senior, witnessed by Tho. Fergussoun de Cragdarroch and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/628/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 271
2 CONC 8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 August 1522: Assignation by Robert, Lord Maxwell, having the gift of the ward lands and barony of Crauffurdstoune [Crawfordton], in favour of Thomas Fergussone [Ferguson] of Cragdarrauch [Craigdarroch], Robert, Matthew and A
2 CONC rthur Fergussone [Ferguson], his sons, and Margaret Gordoun [Gordon], their mother, of the ward lands of Cragdarrauch [Craigdarroch] and Gerburgh [Jarbruck] for the time of the said ward. [Tag, seal gone.] [https://catalogue.nrsco
2 CONC tland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f93&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Craigdarroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshir
2 CONC e, reference GD77/93]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 May 1534: Instrument of resignation by Thomas Fergusone [Ferguson] of Cragdarroch [Craigdarroch], in hands of William Cwnyghame [Cunningham], kt., Master of Glencarne [Glencairn], of £10 lands called Cadzelhauch [Caitloch], S
2 CONC troneba [Stronbae], Benboy [Benbuie], Corrochdowis [Corrodow] and Cannanell [Cammonell] in barony of Glencarne [Glencairn] and sheriffdom of Drumfreis [Dumfries], in favour of Robert Fergusone [Ferguson], son and apparent heir of 
2 CONC said Thomas, and Janet Cwynghame [Cunningham], daughter of deceased William Cunyghame [Cunningham] of Cragans and affianced spouse of said Robert. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77
2 CONC %2f108&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Corrodow&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/108]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 February 1563-64: Precept of clare constat by Edward, Lord Crychtone [Crichton], in favour of Robert Fergussone [Ferguson], as son and heir of deceased Thomas Fergussone [Ferguson] of Cragdarroch [Craigdarroch], of lands in 
2 CONC GD77/92. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f94&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Craigdarroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson fami
2 CONC ly of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/94]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 February 1563-64: Precept of clare constat by Edward, Lord Creychtoun [Crichton], in favour of Robert Fergussoun [Ferguson] as son and heir of deceased Thomas Fergussoun [Ferguson] of Cragdarraych [Craigdarroch], of 4 merk l
2 CONC ands of Jargburgh [Jarbruck] and Drummahallane [Dalmacallan]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f95&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Craigdarroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=n Natio
2 CONC nal Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/95]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 February 1574-75: Apud Halyrudhous. REX etc., dedit  literas  legitimationis  ROBERTO  FERGUSSOUN bastardo, filio naturali quondam Thome F. de  Cragdarroch.  xxxiv.  207. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/p
2 CONC age/630/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 2359]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-1580. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. (H. M. G
2 CONC eneral Register House, Edinburgh, 1886), 1180 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot., and John Maitl
2 CONC and Thomson, MA., Advocates. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1883), 1067 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
