1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ROBERT FERGUSSON OF CRAIGDARROCH ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Fergusson of Craigdarroch, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Fergusson-6th-Laird-of-Craigdarroch/6000000027635119956?through=6000000010050783414 On 1 May 1534 his father resigned various land
2 CONC s in the barony of Glencairn in favour of Robert, and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Cunningham/6000000027626394293?through=6000000010050783414 [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refer
2 CONC ence=GD77%2f108&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Corrodow&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD77/108]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 May 1534: Instrument of resignation by Thomas Fergusone [Ferguson] of Cragdarroch [Craigdarroch], in hands of William Cwnyghame [Cunningham], kt., Master of Glencarne [Glencairn], of £10 lands called Cadzelhauch [Caitloch], S
2 CONC troneba [Stronbae], Benboy [Benbuie], Corrochdowis [Corrodow] and Cannanell [Cammonell] in barony of Glencarne [Glencairn] and sheriffdom of Drumfreis [Dumfries], in favour of Robert Fergusone [Ferguson], son and apparent heir of 
2 CONC said Thomas, and Janet Cwynghame [Cunningham], daughter of deceased William Cunyghame [Cunningham] of Cragans and affianced spouse of said Robert. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77
2 CONC %2f108&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Corrodow&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/108]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 February 1563-64:Precept of clare constat by Edward, Lord Creychtoun [Crichton], in favour of Robert Fergussoun [Ferguson] as son and heir of deceased Thomas Fergussoun [Ferguson] of Cragdarraych [Craigdarroch], of 4 merk la
2 CONC nds of Jargburgh [Jarbruck] and Drummahallane [Dalmacallan]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f95&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+fergussoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1615&di=n Natio
2 CONC nal Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/95]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 February 1585-86: Charter by Robert Fergussoun [Ferguson] of Craigdarroch in favour of James Fergussoun [Ferguson] in Chapelmark, his son, of 1 merk land of Chapelmark. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue
2 CONC /details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f67&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=craigdarroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di= National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/67]'''
