1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN CUNNINGHAM OF CAMBUSKEITH===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Cunningham of Cambusketh, formerly John Cunningham of Kilmoronock, is the second son of James, Earl of Glencairn, and his wife Margaret Campbell. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou00paulgoog#page/n261/mode/1up The
2 CONC  Scots Peerage, iv, pp. 244-45]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Cunningham of Cambuskeith died at Kilmaurs on 9 February 1628. [https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyo02pateuoft/page/216 A History of the County of Ayr, etc., Vol, II., p. 216]''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Cunningham of Cambuskeith married Margaret Knox.[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/119 RMS: 358]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Cunningham-of-Cambuskeith-younger/6000000083380582356?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1540465858006&through=6000000018681432182
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Cunningham/6000000065645906964?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1540470116770&through=6000000018681432182
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Cunningham/6000000010986813031?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1540470196124&through=6000000018681432182
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Cunningham/6000000018681222301?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1540470268306&through=6000000018681432182
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1627: Charter of Sale (almost indecipherable) by Sir William Cunynghame of Caprintoun, knight, whereby, in implement of a contract (of the date of these presents) he sold to John Cunynghame, lawful second son of James,
2 CONC  Earl of Glencairne, and Margaret Knox, his spouse, in liferent, and to John Cunynghame, their lawful eldest son, his heirs and assignees whomsoever, in fee, the £10 land of old extent of Cambuskeith, lying on the north side of th
2 CONC e water of Irving, with tower, manor-place, mills etc. within the bailliary of Cunynghame and sheriffdom of Air: To be held a me for payment to the king, as prince and steward of Scotland, of £10 Scots and 13 shillings and 4 pence
2 CONC  of augmentation in name of feufarm, and doubling the feu-farm on the entry of heirs and assignees: With precept of sasine. At Edinburgh 25th April 1627 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference
2 CONC =GD86%2f496&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cambuskeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/496]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[17th Century] Bond by Alexander Cunynghame, brother germane to Sir David Cunynghame of Robertland, knight, by which said Alexander stands security for '''Anna Cunynghame, one of the three sisters and heirs portioners of umquhi
2 CONC le John Cunynghame of Cambuskeith''', and Mr. Robert Wallace, her future husband, son lawful of Mr. Michael Wallace, minister at Kilmarnock, in all sums of money, debts, and obligations of said Anna and Robert. [http://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD103%2f2%2f307&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cambuskeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of Society of Antiquaries of Scotland, refere
2 CONC nce GD103/2/307]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 May 1645: Certified Copy Retour of Inquest made in a court of the bailiary of Cunynghame held in the tolbooth of the burgh of Irwing on 6 May 1645 by Thomas Neving of Monkridding and Mr. John Gervane of Dalgain (?), depute ba
2 CONC ilies of the said bailiary, finding that''' Ann Cunynghame was one of the three lawful and nearest heirs of John Cunynghame of Cambuskeith, her brother''' in the £10 land of old extent of Cambuskeith, lying on the north side of th
2 CONC e Water of Irwing as the same now runs, with tower, manor-place, mill etc. within the bailiary of Cunynghame and sheriffdom of Air: which lands are held of the prince and steward of Scotland in feu-farm for payment of £10 Scots an
2 CONC d 13/4 in augmentation of rental (which sums are to be doubled in the first year of the entry of heirs of the said John) and are in the hands of the liferentrix Margaret Knox, mother of the said John Cunynghame, since his decease 
2 CONC in January 1637 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f578&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cambuskeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, r
2 CONC eference GD86/578]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 July 1664: Precept (faint) from the Chancery of King Charles I. addressed to the sheriff and his bailies of Air, for infefting the said David Cunynghame as nearest and lawful heir of Margaret Cunynghame, his mother, in one-t
2 CONC hird part of the £10 land of Cambuskeith described in the preceding writ; and commanding them to take security for the sum of £10:13:6 Scots due in name of feu-farm and augmentation for said lands which were in the hands of the su
2 CONC perior for 3 years (viz. £3:11:1½ for feu-farm and augmentation and £7: 2: 3 for a double thereof.) At Edinburgh 30th July a.r. 16, 1664 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f641&st=1
2 CONC &tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+cunynghame&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/641]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 December 1655: Precept of Sasine from the chancery of Oliver, Lord Protector, addressed to the sheriff of Ayr and his deputes, for infefting Elizabeth Cunynghame, as one of the three nearest and lawful heirs of John Cunyngha
2 CONC me of Cambuskeith, her brother-german,  in one-third part of the £10 land of old extent of Cambuskeithe, lying on the north side of the Water of Irving as the said water now runs, with tower, fortalice, manor place etc., within th
2 CONC e bailiary of Cunynghame and sheriffdom of Ayr, taking security for  [£7: 2] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f614&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cambuskeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=16 Nation
2 CONC al Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/614]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 July 1664: Certified Copy Retour of Inquest (defective) held on [8th July 1664] finding that David Cunynghame, lawful son of Alexander Cunynghame, was nearest and lawful, heir of his mother, Margaret Cunynghame, eldest sister
2 CONC -german and one of the three lawful and nearest heirs portioners of John Cunynghame of Cambuskeith in one-third part of the £10 land of old extent of Cambuskeith, lying on the north side of the Water of Irwing, as the same now run
2 CONC s, with tower, manor place, miln etc. within the bailiary of Cunynghame and sheriffdom of Air: Which lands are held of the prince and steward of Scotland in feu-farm for payment of £3: 6: 8 Scots and 4/5½ in augmentation of rental
2 CONC  (which sums are to be doubled in the first year of the entry of heirs) and are in the hands of the superior since the decease of the liferentrix Margaret Knox, mother of the said Margaret Cunynghame, in the month of November 1661
2 CONC  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f640&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cambuskeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, referenc
2 CONC e GD86/640]'''
2 CONT
