1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY MARGARET CUNNINGHAM ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Elizabeth Elphingstoun (1636)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Margaret Cunningham is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Cunningham-7th-Earl-of-Glencairn/6000000008333459792?through=6000000017786418799 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Cunningham/6000000
2 CONC 008630789485?through=6000000017786418799 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/245/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 245]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the late Reverend John Anderson, writing in his account of the Earls of Glencairn for the Scots Peerage, Margaret Cunningham: "As the future spouse ' of James Hamilton of Evandale, son and heir of James Hamilton of
2 CONC  Liberton, she had a charter of the liferent of the lands of Crawford John and others 23 December 15977 She must have been divorced from her husband, who was alive in 1611 as in a charter of 28 August 1610 she is described as the 
2 CONC 'future spouse' of Sir James Maxwell of Calderwood. She had certainly led a very unhappy life with her first husband, as she speaks in her will of the 'crosse of an unloving husband who proved most unnatural to me.'  She was there
2 CONC fore no doubt glad to marry, as his third wife, on 8 September 1610, Sir James Maxwell. She had issue by both marriages, and it is a curious fact that her eldest daughter by her first husband, Jean Hamilton, was married to James M
2 CONC axwell, afterwards the first baronet of Calderwood, the second son by his second wife of Margaret Cunningham's second husband." [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/245/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 245]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT CUNNINGHAME
2 CONT MARGARET
2 CONT 9 / 12 / 1623
2 CONT DAME, LADY CALDERWOOD, PARISH OF CARLUKE
2 CONT TESTAMENT TESTAMENTAR & INVENTORY
2 CONT LANARK COMMISSARY COURT
2 CONT CC14/5/2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The last will and testament of Dame Margaret Cunningham, Lady Calderwood, dated  2 October 1622, is printed in full in volume one of Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock. [https://archive.org/details/memoirsofmaxwev100fras/page/4
2 CONC 77/mode/1up Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock I: 477-80]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
