1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===THOMAS KIRKPATRICK OF CLOSEBURN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Roger-Kirkpatrick-of-Closeburn/6000000042760365552?through=6000000176770224849 [National Records of Scotland. Edinburgh Commissary Court, 
2 CONC Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Roger Kirkpatrick of Cloisburne, sheriffdom of Dumfries, reference CC8/8/13] The name of his mother is not certainly known, but it is thought likely, probable even, that he is the son of http
2 CONC s://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Hamilton/6000000057756305070 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Father's Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Roger Kirkpatrick of Closebur made his last will and testament on 9 January 1582. The witnesses present included, Thomas Kirkpatrick of Helisland, John Kirkpatrick, younger of Helisland, Alexander Kirkpatrick of Kirkmichael, Th
2 CONC omas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, his eldest son and heir, William Kirkpatrick and Roger Kirkpatrick, also his sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Roger Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, here treated, nominated and appointed Thomas Kirkpatrick, his son and apparent heir, Rogger Greirsoun of Lage, and Thomas Kirkpatrick of Aelisland, to be his executors testamentar. He also nomina
2 CONC ted and appointed John Gordon of [ Troquhan ] to be tutor testamentar and guardian to: "Alexr Kirkpatrik my sone & Mt Kirkpatrik my dochter the said Johnis awin systeris bairnes".
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Roger Kirkpatrick of Closeburn left individual legacies to the following, viz. Roger Kirkpatrick, his son, William Kirkpatrick, his son, Samuel Kirkpatrick, his son, Alexander Kirkpatrick, his son, and Margaret Kirkpatrick, his
2 CONC  daughter. He also left to his daughter Margaret: "all my wyffis claithis to the said Mt conforme to hir motheris letter will".'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted to Thomas Kirkpatrick on 29 June 1584. [National Records of Scotland. Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Roger Kirkpatrick of Cloisburne, sheriffdom of Dumfries, referenc
2 CONC e CC8/8/13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000177511973963 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000177511096904 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000177512105972 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000177511057913 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000177511046992 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000177515562855 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000177511189914 Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, here treated, married Jean Cunningham.  [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/242/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: p. 243]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Stirnet, Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn married Barbara Stewart in 1614. She is said to be the daughter of Sir Alexander Stewart of Garlies. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/kk/kirkpatrick2.php Stirnet:
2 CONC  Kirkpatrick 2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 February 1562: Tack by Robert, commendator of Haliecrois, and the convent thereof, to Roger Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, Thomas Kirkpatrick, his son and heir apparent, and William and Alexander Kirkpatrick, also his sons, of the
2 CONC  teinds etc of Dalgarnock. [Signatures of convent.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD19%2f12&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+kirkpatrick&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Re
2 CONC cords of Scotland, Papers of the family of Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, Dumfries-shire, reference GD19/12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 August 1577: REX &c., concessit THOME KIRKPATRIK filio et heredi apparenti Rogeri K. de Closburne, JEHANNE CUNYNGHAME ejus spouse future, filie legitime Willelmi com. de Glencarne, in ejus viduitate, — 10 librat. terrarum an
2 CONC tiqui extentus de Auchinlek, cum tenentibus &c., vic. Drumfreis ; — quas dictus Rog. resignavit : — Tenend. dictis Tho. et Jehanne in con- juncta infeodatione eorumque alteri diutius viventi, heredibusque inter eos legitime procre
2 CONC andis, quibus deficientibus, legit, et propinquioribus heredibus et assignatis dicti Thome quibuscunque : — Test, ut in aliis cartis &c. xxxiv. 536 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/736/mode/1up RMS 1546-80:
2 CONC  2702]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 September 1577: Charter by Roger Kirkpatrick of Closeburn to Thomas Kirkpatrick, his son and heir apparent, of the lands and barony of Closeburn and Newton under reservation of liferent, in implement of a marriage contract da
2 CONC ted [blank] 1577 between said Roger and Thomas Kirkpatrick, and Jean Cunningham (Cunynghame), relict of George Haldane (Halden) of Glennages (Glennegas), with consent of William, lord of Glencairn her father. [Seal.] (With instrum
2 CONC ent of sasine dated 5 September 1577.) [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD19%2f18&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jean+cunningham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Pape
2 CONC rs of the family of Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, Dumfries-shire, reference GD19/18]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 April 1585: Vicecomes respondebit pro £17 6s. 8d. de firmis totius et integre tertie partis omnium et singularum quatuor marcatarum terrarum de Dalbatie, necnon totius et integre tertie partis omnium et singu- larum novem ma
2 CONC rcatarum terrarum de Orcheartoun, cum molendinis, multuris, etc., jacentium in senescallatu de Kirkcudbricht et infra balliam suam, existentium in manibus supremi domini nostri regis per spatium duorum annorum aut eocirca ultime e
2 CONC lapsorum sasina non recuperata; et pro 2d. argenti per duplicationem albefirme earundem ; necnou pro £120 de firmis omnium et singularum decem libratarum terrarum de Brigbrycht antiqui extentus, et quadraginta solidatarum terrarum
2 CONC  de Aleisland antiqui extentus, jacentium infra balliam suam, necnon omnium et singularum terrarum de Newtoun, extendentium ad octo libratas terrarum antiqui extentus, jacentium infra baroniara de Tibberis et balliam suam predicta
2 CONC m, existentium in manibus dicti domini regis per spatium predictum ratione qua supra ; et pro £60 de relevio earundem ; regi debitis per sasinam datam Thome Kirkpatrik de Cloisbume. [Editiburgh, 16 April.] [https://archive.org/det
2 CONC ails/rotuliscaccarii00mcnegoog/page/n589/mode/1up RSRS 1480-88: p. 515]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 May 1585: Vicecomes respondebit pro £288 de firmis totarum et integrarum  terrarum et baronie de Cloisburne, extendentium ad quadraginta octo libratas terrarum antiqui extentus, cum tenentibus, tenandriis, et liberetenentium
2 CONC  servitiis earundem, jacentium infra balliam suam, existentium in manibus supremi domini nostri regis per spatium duonim annorum aut eocirca ultime elapsorum sasina non recuperata ; et pro £144 de relevio earundem ; regi debitis p
2 CONC er sasinam datam Thome Kirkpatrik. [Edinburgh, 27 May.] [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccarii00mcnegoog/page/n586/mode/1up RSRS 1580-88: p. 513]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 April 1599: Notarial instrument narrating that Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn demanded possession of the lands and barony of Ruskie and Lanrik (Lanerik) in the sheriffdom of Perth, in fulfilment of the marriage contract of J
2 CONC EAN CUNNINGHAM, now spouse of said Thomas, which demand James Haldane of Glennages (Glenhageis) agreed to, in token whereof he handed over the keys of the manor place thereof, the said Thomas renouncing on his side all claim to th
2 CONC e lands of the barony of Haldane in the Lennox. [Cf GD19/16.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD19%2f31&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=closeburn&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Reco
2 CONC rds of Scotland, Papers of the family of Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, Dumfries-shire, reference GD19/31]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 December 1614: Contract of marriage between BARBARE STEWART, widow of Joannis Kirkpatrik de Aleisland, and Sir Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/758/mode/1up RMS 1609-2
2 CONC 0: 2100]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11-12 January 1615: Instrument subscribed by Alberti Cunynghame, notary public, of a sasine in favour of Thomas Kitpatrick of Closeburn and BARBARE STEWART. Witnessed by William Kirkpatrick, son of BARBARE STEWART, Alexander Ki
2 CONC rkpatrick, brother of Sir Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn, John Kirkpatrick, son of Sir Thomas Kirkpatrick. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/758/mode/1up RMS 1609-20: 2100]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 January 1615: Charter by which Sir Thomas Kirkpatrick of Closeburn confirms that he has given various lands in liferent to BARBARE STEWART, his future wife. The lands conveyed were (1) the fourteen merk land of old extent of
2 CONC  Auchinleck and Sandrum in the parish of Dalgarnock; (2) the ten merk land of Schynnell; (3) the fifty shilling lands of Stronmuligano and Kilmark; (4) the two and one half merk land of old extent of Ma(r)gninain et Clachannoch)  
2 CONC in the parish if Tinrowe and barony of Glencairn; (5), the forty shilling Kirkland of old extent in the barony of Dalgarnock and sheriffdom of Dumfries. The charter was witnessed by Alexander Kirkpatrick, brother of Sir Thomas, Jo
2 CONC hn Kirkpatrick, son of Sir Thomas, and Henry Kirkpatrick in Kirkflat. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/758/mode/1up RMS 1609-20: 2100]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Printed Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/n5/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1546-1580. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. )H. M. 
2 CONC Gereral Register House, Edinburgh, 1886), 1180 pp. including indexes and errata]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/n5/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great seal of Scotland. A. D. 1609-1620. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. (H. M. 
2 CONC General Register House, Edinburgh, 1892), 1161 pp. including indexes and errata]'''
