1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == THOMAS FERGUSSON  ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Fergusson, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Fergusson-of-Craigdarroch/6000000014585399699?through=6000000183863738821 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Cunningham/6000000177
2 CONC 170383853?through=6000000183863738821  According to the deceased James Fergusson, and the deceased Robert Menzies Fergusson, joint editors of the Fergusson Records, https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Fergusson-of-Craigdarroch/6000
2 CONC 000014585399699?through=6000000183863738821 married https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Cunningham/6000000177170383853?through=6000000183863738821 : "and had by her John and William, Edward, Thomas, and Robert". [https://archive
2 CONC .org/details/recordsofclannam00ferg/page/378/mode/1up Fergusson Records: 378]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Contrary to what is suggested by the above mentioned quotation, it would seem to be the case that Thomas Fergusson, here treated, was actually the eldest son of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Fergusson-of-Craigdarroch/60000
2 CONC 00014585399699?through=6000000183863738821 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Cunningham/6000000177170383853?through=6000000183863738821 [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?referenc
2 CONC e=GD77%2f99&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=craigdarroche&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1620&di=n NRS: GD77/98]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Thomas Fergusson, here treated, He was alive on 31 October 1614, [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f99&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n
2 CONC &tp=n&k=craigdarroche&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1620&di=n NRS: GD77/99] but he died before 27 April 1625. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD77%2f105&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=craigdarroch&
2 CONC ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD77/105]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                      1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 October 1614: Charter by John Fergusone [Ferguson], now of Craigdarroche [Craigdarroch], son and heir of deceased Robert Fergusone [Ferguson] of Craigdarroche [Craigdarroch], in favour of Thomas Ferguson, eldest son of said 
2 CONC Robert by Catharine Cunyghame [Cunningham], now his relict, of an annualrent of 300 merks from lands of Courig and Graindes, under reversion of 3000 merks. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refer
2 CONC ence=GD77%2f99&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=craigdarroche&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1620&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Fergusson family of Craigdarroch, Dumfriesshire, reference GD77/99]'''
2 CONT
