1 NOTE {geni:about_me} was connected as sonbut have disconnected becaus he is refered to as son of Patrick M'Kie of Barjarrock - please see Patrick James MacKie (MacKey, McKee, M'Kie), Bailie In Minnigaf about me section https://www.geni
2 CONC .com/people/Patrick-MacKie-MacKey-McKee-M-Kie-Bailie-In-Minnigaf/6000000006843949641
2 CONT * Gender:	Male
2 CONT * Birth:	1620
2 CONT * Cumloden, Larg, Minnigaff,, Scotland, United Kingdom
2 CONT * Death:	circa 1680 (55-64)
2 CONT * Minnigaff, Kirkcudbrightshire, Scotland (United Kingdom)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Alexander (who predeceased his father in 1591, and whose widow m., secondly, Alexr. Gordon of Clanyard), m. Katherine, dau. of Sir Patrick Agnew of Lochnaw, hereditary sheriff of Wigton,contract dated 8 Oct., 1575, with issue: 
2 CONC — 
2 CONT # '''Patrick, of whom follows;'''
2 CONT # a son who had three sons (Alexr. ; Patrick, who succeeded to Larg,16-16 ; and   James of Crosbie, who had a son Robert, whose son John in 1691 succeeded to Larg and Palgown).
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Patrick, had a charter under the Great Seal, 4 March,  1598, as Patrick Makkie, eldest son of the late Alexr. Makkie, son and heir apparent of Patrick Makkie of Larg, of the lands of  Camloden, Barrawer, Calcathane, Biach, Cam
2 CONC den, Fyntillach with   the isle in the loch thereof, Clonlouchagach, Garser, Baryarrock, Barjargane, all in Wigtonshire, and Clonquhard in Kirkcudbrightshire, now created into the free barony of Larg with the fortalice of Culgour 
2 CONC as chief messuage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick, who was knighted before 1610, joined the regiment raised by Sir Donald Mackie of Strathnaver for service under the  King of Denmark, and was wounded at the battle of Oldenburgh. He returned from the Continent in 1628, and
2 CONC  that year became M.P.  for the stewartry of Kirkcudbright, a position which he filled till 1639. Sir Patrick, an ardent Covenanter, was chosen president of  the first meeting of Kirkcudbright stewartry War Committee on 27 June, 1
2 CONC 640, and soon afterwards commanded a regiment of Galloway  horse at the battle of Newburn, in which his only son Alexander fell  after capturing a standard from the enemy. Zachary Boyd in a long  poem entitled " Newburn Book" thus
2 CONC  deplores the fall of young M'Kie :—
2 CONT
2 CONT "In this conflict, which was a great pitie, We lost the son of Sir Patrick M'Ghie."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick m., first, Susanna, 3rd dau. of Sir Thomas Kennedy of  Culzean, no issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m., secondly, Mary, dau. of Sir Uchtred Macdowall of Garthland, issue five :—
2 CONT * Alexr., k. at Newburn in 1640; 
2 CONT * Jean, m. John Houston ofDrumastane, by whom she had a son Patrick ;
2 CONT *  a dau. m Alexr.Murdoch of Cumloden ; 
2 CONT * Agnes, m. George, son of John Gordon of Airds ; and
2 CONT *  Grizel.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m., thirdly, Isobel Kerr, Lady Greenheid, who survived him.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick d. in 1645, and was succeeded by his nephew, https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-M-Kie-bailie-in-Minnigaff/6000000024891366552, of whom follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT pg. 355-356  - - THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University) Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH : NORMAN MACLEOD, -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY, ST. PETER'S MANSE, MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC 
2 CONC VI [1906] 
2 CONT
2 CONT =================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick McKie b. after 1575 d. 1645; m. Susanna Kennedy b. abt. 1570 and she was of Culzeau, Scotland. He was of Larg, Minnigaff, Kircudbright, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT died 1645; married 8 October 1575 [-?-]
2 CONT
2 CONT It is said that Sir Patrick McKee of Larg was a staunch Presbyterian who heavily mortgaged his estates to aid the Protestant cause. He was a grantee of lands in Northern Ireland during the Ulster settlement 1610. 
2 CONT * Patrick MCKIE, born Abt. 1597 in Of Minnigaff, Kirkcudbright, , Scotland.
2 CONT * David MACKEY, born Abt. 1600 in Of Larg, Minnigaff, Kirkcudbright, Scotland; died in Prob Crosby, 
2 CONT * Wigtownshire, , Scotland.
2 CONT * Alexander MCKIE, born Abt. 1600 in Kirkcudbright, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir Patrick MacKie of Larg (1576 - 1645)m., first, Susanna, 3rd dau. of Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culzean, no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m., secondly, Mary, dau. of Sir Uchtred Macdowall of Garthland, issue five : — Alexr., k. at Newburn in 1640; Jean, m. John Houston of Drumastane, by whom she had a son Patrick ; a dau. m Alexr. Murdoch of Cumloden ; Agnes, m. 
2 CONC George, son of John Gordon of Airds ; and Grizel.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m., thirdly, Isobel Kerr, Lady Greenheid, who survived him. Sir Patrick d. in 1645, and was succeeded by his nephew, Patrick M'Kie, bailie in Minnigaf
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *”The book of Mackay”.  Author Mackay, Angus, 1860-1911.  Page 356.   [https://archive.org/details/bookofmackay00mack/page/356 Archive.Org]
