1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John's children were all baptized in Dumfries, which is very near to the "family seat" at Larg, Minnigaff.  This, despite clearly going fairly far afield to marry (best such record comes from Falkirk).  It seems th
2 CONC at lesser sons of noble families had to travel to find wives.  Likely these marriages were strategically arranged, which explains the distances involved.
2 CONT
2 CONT At least wife Marion had to travel an equal distance, from Aberdeen to Falkirk, to be wed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later in life, son John settled in Largo, Fifeshire, while son David settled in nearby Brechin, Angus.  John's wife was from Aberdeen, so I believe that in later years John and Marion left Dumfries and went East to Brechin, someti
2 CONC me after 1618.
