1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir William Purves, of Purves Hall</strong>, co. Berwick, only s. of Robert Purves, of Abbeyhill, co. Edinburgh, Burgess of that city (d. 1655), by Anne Douglas, his wife, was an officer in the Court of Session, holding a
2 CONC fterwards, 1656, an office in the Court of Exchequer; an Advocate, and, 13 Nov. 1662, Solicitor-Gen. [S.] ; was Knighted and subsequently cr. a. Baronet [S.], as above, 5, 6, or 25 July 1665, there being, however, no record of suc
2 CONC h creation in the Great Seal Register. He m. Margery, da. of Robert Flemming, of Restalrig. He d. in 1684 or 1685."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n263/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 244
