4 CONT
4 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
4 CONT
4 CONT
4 CONT Jump to: navigation, search 
4 CONT
4 CONT
4 CONT The Purves, later Purves-Hume-Campbell, later Home-Purves-Hume-Campbell Baronetcy, of Purves Hall in the County of Berwick, was a title in the Baronetage of Nova Scotia. It was created on 25 July 1665 for William Purves. The fourt
4 CONC h Baronet married Lady Anne, daughter of Alexander Hume-Campbell, 2nd Earl of Marchmont. Their grandson, the sixth Baronet, assumed the additional surnames of Hume and Campbell. The latter's son, the seventh Baronet, assumed the a
4 CONC dditional surname of Home. He sat as Member of Parliament for Berwickshire. The title became either extinct or dormant on the death of the eighth Baronet in 1960.
4 CONT
4 CONT Helen Purves-Hume-Campbell, daughter of the seventh Baronet, married Vice-Admiral Sir George Warrender, 7th Baronet, and was the mother of Victor Warrender, 1st Baron Bruntisfield.
4 CONT
4 CONT Purves, later Purves-Hume-Campbell, later Home-Purves-Hume-Campbell baronets, of Purves Hall (1665)[edit]
4 CONT Sir William Purves, 1st Baronet (died c. 1685)
4 CONT Sir Alexander Purves, 2nd Baronet (died 1701)
4 CONT Sir William Purves, 3rd Baronet (died 1730)
4 CONT Sir William Purves, 4th Baronet (1701–1762)
4 CONT Sir Alexander Purves, 5th Baronet (1739–1812)
4 CONT Sir William Purves-Hume-Campbell, 6th Baronet (1767–1833)
4 CONT Sir Hugh Purves-Hume-Campbell, 7th Baronet (1812–1894)
4 CONT Sir John Home-Purves-Hume-Campbell, 8th Baronet (1879–1960)
4 CONT
4 CONT See also[edit]
4 CONT Lord Polwarth
4 CONT Purves (Family Name)
