1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===DAME ELIZABETH RUTHVEN (aka ISABEL RUTHVEN)===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Dame Elizabeth Ruthven (1609) Dame Elizabeth Ruthven (1610) Dominiam Eliz Ruthven (1613) Deame Elizabethe Rwthvane, ladie Lowdoune (1617)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Elizabeth Ruthven is the daughter of William, Earl of Gowrie, and Dorothy Stewart. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#page/266/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 266]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 7 September 1617. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar of Deame Elizabethe Rwthvane, ladie Lowdoune, spouse to Hew, lord of Lowdowne, in the parish of th
2 CONC e same, reference CC9/7/14]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Elizabeth Ruthven married Hugh Campbell, first Earl of Loudoun. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f153&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+ruthven&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=
2 CONC &di=n NRS: GD39/1/153] The Scots Peerage misidentifies her husband as George, first Earl of Loudon. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#page/266/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 266]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/498/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 498]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1-9 June 1610: Contract between James Earl of Glencairn and William Lord Kilmaurs his eldest son as principal, and Sir James Cunningham of Glengarnock knight, Alexander Cunningham of Crosshill, David Cunningham of Robertland an
2 CONC d James Cunningham of Aiket, cautioners of the one part, and Hugh Lord Loudon and DAME ELIZABETH RUTHVEN, his wife, on the other part, by which for the sum of 10,000 merks paid by Lord Loudon to the Earl and his son, they dispone 
2 CONC to Lord Loudon and his wife their heirs and assignees the barony of Kilmaurs with the manor place etc. (patronage of churches etc.) But redeemable on payment of said sum of 10,000 merks and expenses by the Earl and his son to Lord
2 CONC  Loudon and his wife. At Edinburgh, Loudon and Glasgow 1st, 4th and 9th, June 1610. Witnesses, Alexander Cunningham son to said Laird of Corsehill. Witness to signatures Patrick Cunningham of Halpland (?) Mr Daniel Cunningham, Mun
2 CONC go Campbell. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f153&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+ruthven&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, ref
2 CONC erence GD39/1/153]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 July 1610: Instrument of Seisin in favour of Hugh Lord Loudon and DAME ELIZABETH RUTHVEN his wife, in the barony of Kilmaurs with the manor place etc. proceeding on a charter granted in implement of the contract dated 9th Ju
2 CONC ne 1610 (GD39/1/153). Witness to charter, Mr Malcolm Colquhoun, George Campbell of Dalloy. Instrument drawn by George Campbell, clerk of the diocese of Glasgow, notary public. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue
2 CONC /details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f154&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+ruthven&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/154]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 December 1613: . . . . . DOMINIAM ELIZ RUTHVEN . . . . .  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/352/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1609-1620, charter number 967 on pp. 352-54]
