1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Sir Hugh Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell of Loudoun:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p2514.htm#i25135
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Hugh Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell of Loudoun[1]
2 CONT *M, #25135, 
2 CONT *b. after 1561, 
2 CONT *d. 15 December 1622
2 CONT *Last Edited=27 May 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Hugh Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell of Loudoun was born after 1561.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Margaret Gordon, daughter of Sir John Gordon of Lochinvar and Juliana Home, in 1572.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Lady Isabel Ruthven, daughter of William Ruthven, 1st Earl of Gowrie and Dorothea Stewart, after 1608.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, thirdly, Margaret Home, daughter of Sir George Home of Wedderburn, circa 11 October 1617.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 15 December 1622.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Sir Matthew Campbell of Loudoun and Isabel Drummond.[2] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Knight in 1572.[3] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Sheriff of Ayr.[3] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Irvine in 1579.[3] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland] in 1601.[3] 
2 CONT *He was created 1st Lord Campbell of Loudoun [Scotland] on 30 June 1601.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Hugh Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell of Loudoun and Lady Isabel Ruthven
2 CONT *1. Jean Campbell2
2 CONT *2. Margaret Campbell2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Hugh Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell of Loudoun and Margaret Gordon
2 CONT *1. Isabel Campbell6 d. 1612
2 CONT *2. George Campbell, Master of Loudoun+2 d. Mar 1611/12
2 CONT *3. Juliana Campbell7 b. c 1581, d. a 1648
2 CONT
