2 CONT William Adair (d.1626) of Kinhilt and Ballymena. Eldest son of Ninian Adair (d. c.1606) of Kinhilt. Made a denizen of Ireland, 1624. He married 1st, Rosina, daughter of Sir Thomas McClellan of Bomby; 2nd, a daughter of Mr Houstoun
2 CONC  of Castle Steward, and 3rd, Helen Cathcart of Carlton and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT *(1.1) Sir Robert Adair (d. 1655) (q.v.);
2 CONT *(3.1) Rev. William Adair (d. 1684); minister of Ayr 1640-84;
2 CONT *(3.2) Anna or Marian Adair, m. William Houston of Killester. He inherited the Kinhilt estate and the castles of St. John and Dunskey from his father in 1608, but exchanged part of the property, including Dunskey, with 1st Viscoun
2 CONC t Montgomery, one of the leaders of the Plantation of Ulster, for lands at Ballymena (Antrim) in 1620. He died 4 November 1626
