1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/boards/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=723&p=surnames.adair
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Adair was the son of William ADAIR of KINHILT, and brother of Sir Robert ADAIR of Kinhilt and Ballymena.
2 CONT
2 CONT He (William ADAIR) married the widow of Robert CUNNINGHAM minister of Holywood.
2 CONT
2 CONT For 43 years William Adair had been a minister of Ayr, and he did not long survive his severance from the charge. He died in February, 1684, and was buried in the shadow of the Church which he had built "betwixt the twa laigh wind
2 CONC owes on the east syd of the isle." All through his public life he had been noted for his gift of prayer, and the monument which marks his resting-place represents him on his knees. His character, like his career, had come through 
2 CONC strange vicissitudes. Extreme ardour had given place to extreme caution. But it was lit up with heroism in the end. Nothing in his ministry became him like the leaving it. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Next year Alexander Gregorie was translated from St. Quivox to succeed Rev. William Adair. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://landedfamilies.blogspot.com/2013/04/23-adair-of-ballymena-castle-and.html?m=1
2 CONT
2 CONT William Adair (d.1626) of Kinhilt and Ballymena.  Eldest son of Ninian Adair (d. c.1606) of Kinhilt.  Made a denizen of Ireland, 1624.  He married 1st, Rosina, daughter of Sir Thomas McClellan of Bomby; 2nd, a daughter of Mr Houst
2 CONC oun of Castle Steward, and 3rd, Helen Cathcart of Carlton and had issue:
2 CONT *(1.1) Sir Robert Adair (d. 1655) (q.v.); 
2 CONT *(3.1) Rev. William Adair (d. 1684); minister of Ayr 1640-84;
2 CONT *(3.2) Anna or Marian Adair, m. William Houston of Killester. He inherited the Kinhilt estate and the castles of St. John and Dunskey from his father in 1608, but exchanged part of the property, including Dunskey, with 1st Viscoun
2 CONC t Montgomery, one of the leaders of the Plantation of Ulster, for lands at Ballymena (Antrim) in 1620. He died 4 November 1626.
2 CONT
