1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR JAMES MUIRHEAD OF LAUCHOPE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''James Muirhead, younger of Lauchope (1618 x 1622) James Muirhead, younger of Lauchop (1637) Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope (1654 x 1659) Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope (1659 x 1660) Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope (1
2 CONC 667 x 1671) Sir James Muirhead of Lauchop, knight (1671) Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope (post mortem 1677 x 1685)  Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope (post mortem 1693 x 1699)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Alexander Nisbet, writing in volume two of A System of Heraldry, Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope had the honour of knighthood conferred on him by James VI, King of Scots, in year 1617, or the year 1621. [https://arc
2 CONC hive.org/details/systemofheraldry02nisb/page/263/mode/1up Heraldry II: 263] It is supposed therefore, in view of his knightly rank, that he is the man of the same name who, according to the Scots Peerage, married Lady Margaret Som
2 CONC erville, the widow of Gilbert, Lord Somerville. Lord Somerville died in 1618, [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/26/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 26] and his widow is noticed as the wife of Sir James Muirh
2 CONC ead of Lauchope in a deed that was registered in the Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Lanark before 7 March 1622. [NRS: RS40/I/144] Nisbet believed that Jean Houston, but probably https://www.geni.com/people/El
2 CONC izabeth-Houston/6000000051481366123?through=6000000011336795578 , was Sir James's first wife, but since this lady married her husband before 31 May 1597 [https://archive.org/details/registrhttps://archive.org/details/registrummagn
2 CONC isi06scot/page/187/mode/1up RMS 1593-1608: 565] it might be supposed that she probably married the father of Sir James Muirhead of Lauchop, here treated, who died in October 1622. [NRS: C9/7/19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope, here treated, died intestate in May 1671. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Sir James Muirhead of Lauchop, knight, parish of Bothwell,
2 CONC  reference CC9/7/39]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 22 December 1671 the Testament Dative and Inventory of the deceased Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope was given up by his son Claud Muirhead of Lauchope. John Hamilton, fiar of Woodhall, acted himself as cautioner for Claud and
2 CONC  confirmation was granted to him on 10 February 1672. No provision was made for a surviving wife and it is supposed that Sir James was probably a widower at the time of his death. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary 
2 CONC Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Sir James Muirhead of Lauchop, knight, parish of Bothwell, reference CC9/7/39]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000180881644823 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000180881149821 Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Somerville/6000000180811869963?through=6000000042883987789 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/26/mode/1up The Scot
2 CONC s Peerage VIII: 26] They were married before 7 March 1622. [NRS: RS40/I/144]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Dalziel/6000000011336633715?through=6000000011336795578 She is noticed as his wife on 25 February 1654. [https://archive.org/details/scotspe
2 CONC eragefoun02pauluoft/page/411/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: p. 411, Note12, citing Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
