1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == CLAUD MUIRHEAD OF LAUCHOPE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Testament Dative and Inventory of his deceased Father ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 22 December 1671 the Testament Dative and Inventory of the deceased Sir James Muirhead of Lauchope was given up by his son Claud Muirhead of Lauchope. John Hamilton, fiar of Woodhall, acted himself as cautioner for Claud and
2 CONC  confirmation was granted to him on 10 February 1672. No provision was made for a surviving wife and it is supposed that Sir James may have been a widower at the time of his death. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary
2 CONC  Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Sir James Muirhead of Lauchop, knight, parish of Bothwell, reference CC9/7/39]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000180881644823 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000180881149821 Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted to Gavin Muirhead on 8 January 1685. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Claud Muirhead of Lauchop, parish of Bothwell, reference CC9/7/46
2 CONC ]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Claud Muirhead of Lauchope, here treated, died in November 1681, on or soon after 14 November 1681, the day upon which he made his last will and testament. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament 
2 CONC Testamentar and Inventory of Claud Muirhead of Lauchop, parish of Bothwell, reference CC9/7/46]'''
2 CONT
