2 CONT '''31 July 1629: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland which confirms possession of the lands and barony of Prestoun to Sir James Hammiltoun of Fingartoun, identified in the charter as the eldest lawful son of Sir John Hammilto
2 CONC un of Prestoun. The barony of Prestoun was to be held by Sir James in liferent, and in fee by his eldest lawful son son Robert Hammiltoun, and his lawful heirs by his future wife ANNAM HENRIESOUN.  Annam Henriesoun is identiified 
2 CONC in the charter as the third lawful daughter of Sir Thome Henriesoun of Chesters, one of the Senators of the College of Justice. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/499/mode/1up RMS 1620-33: charter number 1483
2 CONC ]'''
