1 NAME James /Fleming/
2 GIVN James
2 SURN Fleming
2 _MARNM Fleming
2 NICK James John
1 NAME James Fleming, of Boghall
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1591
1 DEAT
2 DATE OCT 1623
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 2. Hon James Fleming of Boghall (d. Oct 1623), mar. after 7 Nov 1612 Janet Brisbane, dau. of John Brisbane of Bishopston, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT # 1a. John Fleming of Boghall(dsp. after 22 Aug 1656)
2 CONT # 2a. James Fleming (dsp. bef. 24 May 1654)
2 CONT # 3a. Francis Fleming (d. after 1623)
2 CONT # 1a. Anna Fleming (d. after 1623)
2 CONT # 2a. Jean Fleming (d. after 1623)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Burke's:
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. James, of Boghall, who m. in 1612, Janet Brisbane, dau. of the Laird of Rishoptoun, and d. in 1622. His son, John, came of age, 1643. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT James had a charter of the lands of Boghall, Milltown, and Arretshole from his father on 10 April 1593. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations 
2 CONT # The Scots Peerage: Founded on Wood's Edition of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland, Containing an Historical and Genealogical Account of the Nobility of that Kingdom, with Armorial Illustrations (1904-1914), Paul , Sir Jam
2 CONC es Balfour, (9 volumes. Edinburgh: D. Douglas, 1904-1914), FHL book 941 D22p; FHL microfilms104,157-104,161., vol. 8 p. 547.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=K3MaAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA218&ots=iAyq4fjxj1&dq=john%20fleming%201st%20earl%20of%20wigton&pg=PA218#v=onepage&q=john%20fleming%201st%20earl%20of%20wigton&f=false A Genealogical History of the Dormant:] 
2 CONC Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct ... By Sir Bernard Burke, page 218 "Fleming - Earl of Wigton" also attached. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * https://histfam.familysearch.org//getperson.php?personID=I207650&tree=EuropeRoyalNobleHous
2 CONT * http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/wigtown1606.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT There is a hypothesis that our family descends from James and Janet Brisbane... and had sons: Alexander, Richard and our Thomas, these along with son John, are the ones who came to Virginia.   Source: Cousin Berthe Daniels of Kent
2 CONC , WA. James dates would work with this--also, since none of these sons could have inherited the title or estates, it would make sense for them to seek their fortunes in what was then the "new world". Some sources say that Thomas e
2 CONC migrated in 1616, some say he was born in 1616.
