1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Douglas,_1st_Duke_of_Queensberry Wikipedia Entry]
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=grI2AAAAIAAJ An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII]; by George Brunton, David Haig; 1832; Page 413
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT William Douglas was the First Duke of Queensberry and the third Earl of Queensberry. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William was born in 1637 in Drumlanrig, Dumfriesshire, Scotland. He was eldest son of James Douglas and Lady Margaret Stewart. He died in 1695. He was buried at Durisdeer Church, Dumfriesshire, Scotland. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William was the builder of Drumlanrig Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT WIlliam married Isabel Douglas. They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT James [1] William [1] George [1] Lady Anne [1] Ancestral File Number
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestral File Number: 1VFK-FC1. [2]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT This connection to the Douglas line may be an internet myth....
2 CONT
2 CONT www.facebook.com./jasonedwardkennedy
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT First Duke of Queensbury, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT William Douglas was the First Duke of Queensberry and the third Earl of Queensberry. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William was born in 1637 in Drumlanrig, Dumfriesshire, Scotland. He was eldest son of James Douglas and Lady Margaret Stewart. He died in 1695. He was buried at Durisdeer Church, Dumfriesshire, Scotland. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William was the builder of Drumlanrig Castle, which still stands.
2 CONT
2 CONT WIlliam married Isabel Douglas. They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT James [1]
2 CONT William [1]
2 CONT George [1]
2 CONT Lady Anne [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Douglas-1063#_note-Renton
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Duke of Queensberry PC  also 3rd Earl of Queensberry and 1st Marquess of Queensberry
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of James Douglas, 2nd Earl of Queensberry (before 1622 – 1671)
