1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LADY MARGARET DOUGLAS Lady Applegarth===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Lady Margaret Douglas. However, she was still alive on 13 July 1711, the date upon which Sir John Jardine of Applegirth registered a discharge in favour of his mother, [http
2 CONC ://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD472%2f19&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Margaret+Douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1720&di=n NRS: GD472/19] but she died before March 1627, the date upon which t
2 CONC he accounts for her funeral expenses were prepared. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD472%2f48&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Margaret+Douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1720&di=n National Re
2 CONC cords of Scotland, Papers of the Jardine family of Applegirth, reference GD472/48]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 January 1684: Signature of the lands of Applegirth granted to Margaret Douglas, widow of Sir Alexander Jardine. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f40%2f46&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&
2 CONC tp=n&k=Applegirth&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1687&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/40/46]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 February 1686: Precept of Poinding. Lady Margaret Douglas, Lady Applegirth against debtors. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD472%2f64&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Lady+Margaret+Dou
2 CONC glas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Jardine family of Applegirth, reference GD472/64]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 April 1686: Minute of Agreement between Dame Margaret Douglas, Lady Aplegirth and Robert Carruthers of Ramerskails to subscribe a bond of Corroboration and Wadset for 7,000 merks on the Estate of Apilgirth to and in favour o
2 CONC f Robert Carruthers. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD472%2f65&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Margaret+Douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1720&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of th
2 CONC e Jardine family of Applegirth, reference GD472/65]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 June 1686: Discharge. Lady Margaret Douglas, Lady Appilgirth, to Alexander Johnston, younger for £252 Scots. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD472%2f12&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=
2 CONC Applegirth&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1625&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Jardine family of Applegirth, reference GD472/12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''X 1686: Bonds, assignations, receipts and other papers concerning John Maxwell of Castlemilk and litigation with Lady Margaret Douglas, Lady Apelgirth and others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.a
2 CONC spx?reference=GD472%2f58&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Lady+Margaret+Douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Jardine family of Applegirth, reference GD472/58]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1687: Discharge by Andrew Johnstounes elder and younger of Lockerbie to Lady Margaret Douglas, Lady Apilgirth of a Decreet of the Lords of Council and Session (granted 22 February 1679) against Sir Alexander Jardine and others 
2 CONC concerning the away-taking from the lands of Milnbank 'twentie-four cowes with their followers and four oxen togither with three mears with foalls and twa horses all belonging to Robert Johnstane'. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov
2 CONC .uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD472%2f23&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Lady+Margaret+Douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Jardine family of Applegirth, reference GD472/
2 CONC 23]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 January 1687: Discharge by Lady Margaret Douglas, relict of the deceased Sir Alexander Jardan of Apilgirth, to John Maxwell of Castlemilk and Mr Alexander Forrester, minister at St Mungo, of a Bond of Corroboration for £222 
2 CONC 4/- Scots. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD472%2f58&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Lady+Margaret+Douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Jar
2 CONC dine family of Applegirth, reference GD472/58]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 April 1687: William Forrester, Edinburgh to Margaret Douglas, Lady Apilgirth concerning the 'apprysing against Lockerbie' and the general charge to enter heir raised by her son. Apologises for the delays in the legal process
2 CONC . [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD472%2f54&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Margaret+Douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1720&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Jardine family of
2 CONC  Applegirth, reference GD472/54]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 November 1687: Translation by Margaret Douglas, Lady Apilgirth of a bond by John Kirkpatrick for 1260 merks Scots, dated 1 and 31 December 1683. [http://catalogue.nhttps://www.geni.com/profile/language_chooser?tabs_id=tabs-a
2 CONC bout_me-543rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD472%2f23&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Lady+Margaret+Douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Jardine family of Appl
2 CONC egirth, reference GD472/23]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
