1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===AGNES FAWSYDE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Agnes Fawsyde is the daughter of George Fawsyde of the Ilk. She married Sir William Douglas of Kelhead and had issue. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/148/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 148]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Agnes Fawsyde died intestate before 1649, when her widowed husband was contracted to marry Jean Stuart. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/148/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 148]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Her Testament Dative and Inventory===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 29 January 1652. [National Records of Scotland Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Agnes Fawsyde sometime spouse to Sir William Douglas of Kelheid, reference CC8/8/65]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 December 1644: Extract Contract of Wadset by Gilbert Kirkwod [Kirkwood] of Pilrig to Col. William Douglas of Kelheid [Kellhead] and Agnes Fawsyd [Fallside], his spouse, of the lands and teinds of Pilrig, the Coumoun Mure of 
2 CONC the Cannogait [Canongate] with reservation, and 4 acres in Newheavin [Newhaven], with Back-Tack by the latter to the former. Registered in B. of C. & S. 16 [July 16]46. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/detail
2 CONC s.aspx?reference=GD69%2f37&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=fawsyd&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Balfour Family of Pilrig, Midlothian, reference GD69/37]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/148/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 148]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Douglas was the son of William Douglas, 1st Earl of Queensberry (died 1640) and Isobel (of Lothian) Kerr, daughter of the 1st Earl of Lothian. His brother was to become the 2nd Earl of Queensberry (died 1671), and through 
2 CONC a contract with him was infeft in Kelhead.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married first to Agnes, daughter of George Fawside of Fawside. Their son, Sir James Douglas of Kelhead (1639-1708) was made a Baronet of Nova Scotia in his father's lifetime.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Jean Stuart, daughter of Sir Robert Stuart, in 1649.
2 CONT
2 CONT # 2.	Sir William Douglas of Kelhead, Governor of Carlisle (d 1673) 	m1. Agnes Fawside (dau of George Fawside of Fawside).  
2 CONT ##A.	Sir James Douglas, 1st Bart of Kelhead (b 19.09.1639, d before 04.1708, 2nd son) 	m. (28.10.1667) Catherine Douglas (dau of James Douglas, 2nd Earl of Queensberry) 
2 CONT ##B.	Archibald Douglas (Colonel, 4th son)
2 CONT ###	i.	daughter
2 CONT ##C.	Mary Douglas 	m. (mcrt 28.01.1647) John Johnston of Wamphray (d 1656)
2 CONT ##	D.	Catherine Douglas (b 10.04.1638) 	m. Menzies of Stenhouse
2 CONT ##	E.	Sophia Douglas 	m. (1672) John Craill of Stevenstoun
2 CONT ##	F.+	other issue - William (dvp unm),
2 CONT ## Robert, 
2 CONT ##George (captain), 
2 CONT ##Isobel (bpt 24.10.1635), 
2 CONT ##Margaret (b 03.04.1637), 
2 CONT ## Sarah (b 17.11.1641)
2 CONT # m2. (1649) Jean Stuart (dau of Sir Robert Stuart of Schelinlaw)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source: [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/dd/douglas09.php Stirnet: Douglas 09]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.  WILLIAM6 DOUGLAS (William5, James4, William3, James2, William1) was born in 1618 in Dumfries-shire, Scotland. He died in 1673 in Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Agnes Fawside in 1637 in Scotland. She was born in 1618 in Scotland. She died in 1649 in Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Douglas and Agnes Fawside had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * JAMES7 DOUGLAS was born on 19 Sep 1639 in Scotland. He died in 1708. He married Catherine Douglas, daughter of James Douglas and Margaret Stewart in 1661. She was born in 1650 in Durisdeer, Dumfries-shire, Scotland.
2 CONT * ARCHIBALD DOUGLAS was born on 02 Jan 1643 in Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland. He died in 29 1729 in Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland.
2 CONT * GEORGE DOUGLAS was born in 1646 in Scotland.
2 CONT *15.   ROBERT DOUGLAS was born on 02 Jan 1643 in Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland. He died in 29 1729 in Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland. He married Harriet Ella Gifford in 1663 in Midlothian, Scotland. She was born in 1645 in Scot
2 CONC land.
2 CONT * WILLIAM DOUGLAS was born in 1637 in Dumfries-shire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source: < [http://www.thetintypeshop.com/family/Douglas/Surnames/DtoF/Douglas/kathrynpegelowgedcom_2012-03-09_2012-04-04_2012-08-18.pdf “Descendants of William Douglas”] > (2013) Page 4 of 178.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000198190049871&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source: Johnston, George Harvey, "The heraldry of the Douglases : with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees" (1907)  Page 23. < [https://archive.org/details/heraldryofdougla00john/
2 CONC page/23/mode/1up Archive.Org] >''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT >In 1647 was established that link which makes the Marquess of Queensberry the sole representative of this ancient family [of Fawside]. It was in that year that the Hon. "William Douglas of Kelhead (second son of Sir William Dougl
2 CONC as of Drumlanrig), who was afterwards first Earl of Queensberry, married Agnes, daughter of Fawsyde of Fawsyde, who, in Foster's Peerage, is described as a " member of an ancient family, which has been seated for four centuries at
2 CONC  Fawside dastle, in the parish of Tranent."
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source: “Notice of the Fawsydes of that Ilk.”  Proceedings of the Society, February 13, 1890.  < [http://www2.thesetonfamily.com:8080/information/Fawside.pdf PDF] > (Page 377) PDF page 8. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
