1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JAMES DOUGLAS OF KELHEAD Baronet===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/dd/douglas09.php#maxsp2 Stirnet: Douglas 09]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James Douglas, of Kelhead</strong>, 2d but 1st surv. s. and h. ap. of the Hon. Sir William Douglas, of Kelhead aforesaid, sometime (1647), Governor of Carlisle, by his 1st wife, Agnes, da. and h. of George Fawside, of Faw
2 CONC side, which William was 2d s. of William, 1st Earl or Queensberry [S.], was b. 19 Feb. 1639, and was v.p. cr. a Baronet [S.], 26 Feb. 1668,( b ) with rem. to the heirs male of his body. He suc. his father in the family estate, 167
2 CONC 3. He to. (contract 28 Oct. 1667) Catherine, 2d da. of his paternal uncle, James (Douglas), 2d Earl of Queensberry [S.], by his 2d wife, Margaret, da. of John (Stewart), 1st Earl of Traquair [S.]. He was living 8 Sep. 1705, but d.
2 CONC  before April 1708."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n285/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 266
