1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Douglas, 3rd of Mouswald, married Agnes Rome, daughter of John Rome of Dalswinton-Holm, and they had 10 children, two of whom suceeded to the title.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their eldest son, also James, married in 1654 Janet Laurie, but he died predeceasing his father without children. William, the second son, succeeded in about 1667 as 4th baron, but he died in 1670, also without children.
2 CONT
2 CONT The title then fell to the 3rd son, John, who became 5th baron of Mouswald. He too died without children. His brothers, Archibald and Robert had presumably died before him, because the title then fell, in 1692, to his niece, Eliza
2 CONC beth, Robert's daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT ————————
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.douglashistory.co.uk/history/families/douglas_of_mouswald.htm#.W3CIthZlDYU
2 CONT
2 CONT James Douglas of Mouswald, M.P., 1644-47, married in 1627 Agnes Rome,  and had : — 
2 CONT *(a) James (below)
2 CONT *(b) William Douglas of Mouswald, (b 1649, Cockpen) living 1663. (dsp?)
2 CONT *(c) John Douglas of Mouswald was retoured heir to his father 
2 CONT *(d) Robert Douglas, married and had a daughter Elizabeth, who on 9th February 1692 was served heir to her uncle George, and in same year to her uncle Archibald.
2 CONT *(e) Archibald Douglas.
2 CONT *(f) George Douglas.
2 CONT *(g) Nicolas Douglas James and his brother William, 28th February 1674, he was also again retoured to his father 21st November 1676. He resigned the lands of Mouswald to the Earl of Queensberry, 24th February 1674.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Douglas of Mouswald, married, 1654, Janet, daughter of Laurie of Maxwellton, and died in his father's lifetime, s.p.
2 CONT
2 CONT The above from " The Barony of Mouswald and its Barons," by John J. Reid, B.A., F.S. A.Scot. {Proceedings of the Society of Antiquaries of 1888-89).
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Sir Simon Carruthers, 8th of Mouswald (d 1504) married a daughter of Douglas of Drumlanrig, possibly the 4th Laird
2 CONT
