1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Elizabeth Semple:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p17794.htm#i177935
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cochrane of that Ilk was the son of John Cochrane of that Ilk and Elizabeth Sempill.[2] He married Elizabeth Montgomerie, daughter of Robert Montgomerie of Skelmorlie, circa 1579.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Cochrane, Renfrewshire, Scotland.[1] On 30 November 1556 he had a charter of the lands of Cochrane.[2] He added the Tower to his manor (and was then called Cochrane Castle).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Cochrane of that Ilk and Elizabeth Montgomerie
2 CONT *1. Elizabeth Cochrane+[1]
2 CONT *2. Janet Cochrane [2] 
2 CONT *3. Margaret Cochrane [2] d. c 1601
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct o
2 CONC r Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume IV, page 526.
2 CONT *2. Mosley, Charles, editor. Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes. Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003, page 1224. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT "Of that Ilk"
2 CONT
2 CONT * Cochrane, Thomas, "Autobiography of a Seaman", London: Richard Bentley, 1861
2 CONT * Paterson, James, "History of the County of Ayr: With a Genealogical Account of the Families of Ayrshire", Edinbugh: John Dick, 1852, Vol. II
2 CONT * Paul, James Balfour. "The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom", Edinburgh: David Douglas,1906, Vol.
2 CONC  III
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896980.0001.000/1:93?rgn=div1;view=fulltext
2 CONT
2 CONT XIII. WILLIAM COCHRAN of that ilk, who succeeded him,* and got charters under the great seal from queen Mary, of the lands and barony of Cochran, and several others, inter 1558 et 1560. He was a man of great sagacity, oeconomy and
2 CONC  prudence, and greatly adorned and beau∣tified the ancient seat of the family of Coch∣ran with large plantations and buildings. He married Margaret, daughter of sir Ro∣bert Montgomery of Skelmorly, in the shire of Ayr, by Mary his
2 CONC  wife, daughter of Ro∣bert lord Semple, by whom he had three daughters. Whether the two eldest (whose names are not come to our knowledge) had any successi∣on, we cannot pretend to determine; but he was succeeded by Elizabeth his 
2 CONC third daughter, as will be shown hereafter. William having no appearance of any male issue, made a resignation and entail of his whole estate, in favours of his daughter Eliza∣beth, and the heirs-male of her body, whom failing, to
2 CONC  several others particularly specified in the deed of entail, which is dated, anno 1593, any person so succeeding being oblig∣ed to carry the name and arms of Cochran, &c.
