1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ROBERT BOYD OF PORTINCROSS===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Testament Dative and Inventory===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 24 June 1634. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, Testament Dative of Robert Boyd of Portincross, parish of Kilbryde, reference CC9/7/26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''c. 1580: Marriage contract of Robert Boyd, son of Archibald Boyd of Portincross, and Jean Montgomery, daughter of Sir Robert Montgomery of Skelmorlie. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?referenc
2 CONC e=GD3%2f2%2f10%2f26&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=portincross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/2/10/26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from Paterson's History of Ayrshire===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The testament testamentar, laterwill, and inventar of the guidis and geir perteining to vmquhile hew boyde, sone lawfull to vmquhile Archibald boyde of portincross, burges of Irwen, quha deceist in ye moneth of October, the zei
2 CONC r of God Jai vi and ten zeiris, maid and gevin vp be his awin mouth in his awin dwelling hous in Irwen, ye xxvj day of October ye said zeir," &c. "Robert boyd of Portincross, Ard. boyde vnder ye hill," his brother, were witnesses 
2 CONC to this document". [https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyo02pateuoft/page/136/mode/1up History of the County of Ayr II: 136]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyo02pateuoft/page/n6/mode/1up History of the County of Ayr : with a genealogical account of the families of Ayrshire. By James Paterson. Vol. II (Thomas George Stevenson, Edinburgh, M.DCC
2 CONC C.LII.), 528 pp.]
