2 CONT 5 September 1593: Charter granted by Sir Robert Montgomery, elder of Skelmorlie in favour of Sir Robert Montgomery, younger his eldest lawful son and the heirs male to be lawfully gotten between him and Anna Scott, second lawful d
2 CONC aughter of Sir James Scott of Rossie, his future spouse; which failing to the heirs male lawfully gotten of the said Sir Robert Montgomery, younger his own body; which also failing to Sir Robert Montgomery, younger his nearest law
2 CONC ful heirs male and assignees whatsoever of the tenandry of Skelmorlie; reserving the granter's liferent of the lands of Skelmorlie and Lochransay; to hold of Alexander, Earl of Eglinton for payment of taxed ward duties [http://cat
2 CONC alogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f7%2f2%2f12&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=anna+scott&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglin
