2 DATE 14 JAN 1735
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===SIR HUGH MONTGOMERY OF SKELMORIE Baronet (formerly HUGH MONTGOMERY OF HARTFIELD)===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT 30 December 1715: Letter from Sir Robert Montgomerie of Skelmorlie, Bruntisland Castle, to his uncle Hugh Montgomerie of Hartfield, asking forgiveness for having married without latter's knowledge. (Fraser, i, 242). [http://catalo
2 CONC gue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f5%2f918&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+montgomerie+of+skelmorlie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Ea
2 CONC rls of Eglinton, reference GD3/5/918]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT 30 Jamuary 1716: Letter from Hugh Montgomerie of Hartfield, Glasgow, to Sir Robert Montgomerie of Skelmorlie: "I can have no further resentment about your marriage". [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.a
2 CONC spx?reference=GD3%2f5%2f922&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+montgomerie+of+skelmorlie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/5/922]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Hugh Montgomery, Baronet [S 1628] of Skelmorlie</strong>, which he purchased from his nephew, uncle and heir male, being 3rd son of the 3rd Baronet; was a merchant at Glasgow and sometime Provost of that city; M.P. th
2 CONC ereof [S] 1702-07 and [G.B.] 1707-08, being one of the Commissioners for the treaty of the Union [S]; Rector of the Univ. of Glasgow, 1724; succeeded to the Baronetcy in August 1731. He married (contract 26 August 1687) Lilias, da
2 CONC ughter of Peter Gemmel, Merchant and Baillie of Glasgow, by Christian, daughter of William Boyd of Portinscross. He died s.p. 14 January 1735, 'at his house' when the Baronetcy became dormant, but the estates devolved, under an en
2 CONC tail made in 1733, on his great niece and heir of line, Lilias, 1st daughter of the 5th Baronet."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n355/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 337
