1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir James Montgomery, Baronet [S 1628] of Skelmorlie</strong>, 1st son and heir; succeeded to the Baronetcy, 7 February 1684; was M.P. [S] of Ayrshire, 1689-93 (till unseated 28 April 1693 for not signing the assurance), 
2 CONC being one of the Deputies from the Parliament [S] to present the Crown to William and Mary. He, however, afterwards, though a Protestant, joined the Court of the exiled James II at St Germains. He married (contract 14 September 16
2 CONC 78) Margaret, 2nd daughter of James (Johnstone) Earl of Annandale [S], by Harriet, daughter of William (Douglas), 1st Marquess of Douglas [S]. He died in London, September 1694."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n355/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 336
