2 CONT http://www.carothers-carruthers.com/butterwhat.htm John Carruthers, 1st Baron Holmains, eldest son was named John, but he was killed in 1542 at the Battle of Solway Moss.  After Holmains' 1st wife, Blanche Murray, died in 1541, Ho
2 CONC lmains married Janet Jardine and named their 1st son John.  This son John was also the Parson of Little Dalton Kirk and was associated with David, the Earl of Crawford in 1581, when they set fire to the House of Ruthven to release
2 CONC  Adam Creichton, who had been incarcerated there.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.caronkin.ca/caron/27626.htm Janet Jardine  Born: Abt 1504, Cockpool, Dumfries, Scotland Marriage (1): Cuthbert Murray before 1528 in Dumfries, Scotland Marriage (2): John Carruthers 1st Baron of Holmains about 1541 in D
2 CONC umfries, Scotland Died: Aft 1542, Dumfries, Scotland Janet married Cuthbert Murray, son of John Murray and Unknown, before 1528 in Dumfries, Scotland. (Cuthbert Murray was born about 1480 in Cockpool, Dumfries-shire, , Scotland an
2 CONC d died before 16 Jan 1541 in Cockpool, Dumfries, Scotland.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet next married John Carruthers 1st Baron of Holmains, son of John Carruthers 4th Laird of Holmains and Unknown, about 1541 in Dumfries, Scotland. (John Carruthers 1st Baron of Holmains was born about 1485 in Holmains, Dumfries
2 CONC , Scotland and died on 19 Aug 1580 in Little Dalton Kirk, Dumfries, Scotland.)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Records of the Carruthers Family" note that Janet was seeing the Sheriff about terms of her late husbands will in June 1542.  
2 CONT
