1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Robert, of Kirkhouse</strong>, also styled of Crustanes; slain in 1583; for the crime Archibald Maxwell of Cowhill and William his son were tried and acquitted in 1605. His testament shows that his wife (who survived him)
2 CONC  was Nicolas, daughter of Charles Murray of Cockpule, and it names his eldest son William, his second son Charles, and a daughter Jane. It is probable, however, that the following five prosecuters of Maxwell of Cowhill for the sla
2 CONC ughter of Robert were all his sons."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft#page/126/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. III, page 127
