2 CONT
2 CONT Correction in likely birth year:
2 CONT
2 CONT Constraints
2 CONT
2 CONT After parents’ marriage (~1570) → Herbert born after ~1570
2 CONT
2 CONT Father died 16 March 1579; Herbert succeeded “in his minority” → Herbert born before 16 Mar 1579, and young enough to be under age at that point.
2 CONT
2 CONT Resulting birth window
2 CONT
2 CONT That gives:
2 CONT
2 CONT Herbert Maxwell (kirk.IX): born ~1571 to early 1579
2 CONT A practical working range is 1571–1578, with a “best guess” around 1574–1576.
2 CONT
2 CONT One important consistency check
2 CONT
2 CONT Your screenshot from BOC shows the father of Herbert (IX) as Bernard (VIII) (died 16 March 1579), not “John.” If you’re confident John + Marion are Herbert’s parents, then either:
2 CONT
2 CONT your numbering/name-label (“John”) doesn’t match BOC’s naming for the same person, or
2 CONT
2 CONT there’s a pedigree conflict that should be flagged in-text.
2 CONT
2 CONT But even if we keep your “married c.1570” constraint, the birth window above still stands as long as the “minor in 1579” fact is true.
