1 NAME Thomas /Erskine/ Master of Erskine
2 GIVN Thomas
2 SURN Erskine
2 NSFX Master of Erskine
2 _MARNM Erskine
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT OCT 1551
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir Thomas Erskine, Master of Erskine – Succeeded as Master after Robert's death. He held the abbacy of Dryburgh (1541–1547), concluded a treaty with England in 1551, and received sasine of Brotherstanes in October
2 CONC  1551. He likely died before his father. He married Margaret Fleming, widow of Lord Graham, but had no legitimate issue. His natural children included:
2 CONT *Adam Erskine – Commendator of Cambuskenneth.
2 CONT *Elizabeth Erskine – Natural daughter by Jonet Abernethy, married Robert Graham of Gartmore.
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/592/mode/2up James Balfour Paul, ed., ''The Scots Peerage'', vol. 5 (Edinburgh: D. Douglas, 1904), p609-12]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===THOMAS ERSKINE Master of Erskine===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Thomas, Master of Erskine, here treated, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Thomas-Erskine-Lord-of-Brechin/6000000002304363591 '''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/611/mode/1up Biographical Summary by The Scots Peerage]===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas, Master of Erskine after his brother's death. Before that date, from 1541 onwards to 1547, he held the office of Abbot or Commendator of Dryburgh. He concluded a treaty with England in June 1551.He had sasine, on 7 Octob
2 CONC er 1551, as Sir Thomas, Master of Erskine, of the lands of Brotherstanes, co. Berwick, sold to him by Sir John Home of Coldenknowes. He seems to have died soon afterwards, or at least before his father. He married (contract 30 Jan
2 CONC uary 1548-49) Margaret, daughter of Malcolm, third Lord Fleming, and widow of Robert, Lord Graham, who fell at Pinkie, but by her had no issue. He had a natural son Adam, Commendator of Cambuskenneth, and a daughter (by a Jonet Ab
2 CONC ernethy) Elizabeth, married (contract 29 January 1562-63) to Robert Graham of Gartmore, brother of John, Earl of Menteith. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/611/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: p. 611]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[http://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896390.0001.000/1:151?rgn=div1;view=fulltext Biographical Summary by The Peerage of Scotland]===
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Master of Erskine, who being a Nobleman of great Parts was imployed in several Embassies into England[c], whereby he won great Reputation to himself, and served his Country very faithfully. He married Margaret Daughter of M
2 CONC alcolm Lord Fleming[d]: But was taken away in the Flower of his Age, leaving no lawful Issue behind him[e].
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[http://www.thepeerage.com/p10923.htm#i109223 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Erskine, Master of Erskine1
2 CONT M, #109223, d. after 7 October 1551
2 CONT Last Edited=29 Dec 2011 Consanguinity Index=0.09%
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Erskine, Master of Erskine was the son of John Erskine, 5th Lord Erskine and Lady Margaret Campbell.2 A contract for the marriage of Thomas Erskine, Master of Erskine and Margaret Fleming was signed on 30 January 1548/49.1 
2 CONC He died after 7 October 1551, without legitimate issue.2
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Commendator to Dryburgh between 1541 and 1547.2 He was styled as Master of Erskine between 1547 and 1551.1 He held the office of Scottish Ambassador to England in 1551.2 Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealoy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ee/erskine01.php Stirnet: Erskine 01]
2 CONT
