1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''William Livingston''', 6th Lord Livingston was the son of Alexander Livingston, 5th Lord Livingston and Lady Agnes Douglas.1 He married Agnes Fleming, daughter of Malcolm Fleming, 3rd Lord Fleming and Janet Stew
2 CONC art, circa 1553. He died between October 1592 and November 1592.  He gained the title of 6th Lord Livingston.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Extract from The Scots Peerage (Volume VII) by Sir James Balfour Paul (Edinburgh 1910) page 439-443 (http://archive.org/details/cu31924092516222)
2 CONT
2 CONT He died between 18 October 1592, when his name appears in a family charter, and 29 November of that year. He married, about 1553, Agnes Fleming, second daughter of Malcolm, third Lord Fleming, by his wife Janet Stewart, an illegit
2 CONC imate daughter of King James iv. Whether Lady Livingston survived her husband has not been ascertained. Both are said to have been buried in Falkirk churchyard, and two recumbent figures near the family tomb are supposed to repres
2 CONC ent them. More probably, however, these belong to an earlier period. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Livingston had issue five sons and two daughters :—
2 CONT * 1. Alexander, first Earl of Linlithgow.
2 CONT * 2. John, who died young.
2 CONT * 3. Henry, who also died young.
2 CONT * 4. Sir George of Ogilface, married Margaret, believed to have been of the family of Innernytie, and died about 1616. From him descended the second family of Livingston of Westquarter and Bedlormie.
2 CONT * 5. Sir William of Culter, died 2 May 1607, buried at Dundrennan ; married Mary, daughter of Sir William Bailie of Lamington, and widow of Edward Maxwell, Abbot of Dundrennan. His son, William, married Helen Livingston, heiress o
2 CONC f Westquarter.
2 CONT * 6. Jean, married (contract 1 and 10 April 1575) to Alexander, fourtli Lord Elpliinston, and had issue. She died 15 September 1651.
2 CONT * 7. Margaret, married, first, in 1581, as his second wife, to Sir Lewis Bellenden of Auclinoul, Justice-Clerk ; and secondly, after 1591, to Patrick Stewart, Earl of Orkney who squandered all her property and left her to die in p
2 CONC overty.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Wikisource article on this William Livingstone==
2 CONT [http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Livingstone,_William_(DNB00) Wikisource]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
