1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===CUTHBERT MURRAY OF COCKPOOL===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/234/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: pp. 219-20]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "(398) <strong>Cuthbert Murray of Cockpool</strong>, died 1493. He was served heir to his father 1474, and is supposed to have built the Castle of Comlongan. He married, before 1460, Marjory Menzies, and had:
2 CONT * John (No. 399).
2 CONT * Mungo(No. 411).
2 CONT * Charles Murray.
2 CONT * Cuthbert Murray, died before 1521.
2 CONT * Gavin Murray, living 1504. 
2 CONT * George Murray, living 15 14.
2 CONT
2 CONT ARMS on Seal, 1477. Three stars within a Royal tres sure. Crest : A stag's head (Laing's Seals)."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/98/mode/2up The heraldry of the Murrays: with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees], by G. Harvey Johnston, 1910, 
2 CONC page 98, paragraph 398
2 CONT
2 CONT Cuthbert Murray was one of the commanders of Scottish Royalist forces at the Battle of Lochmaben Fair on on 22 July 1484.  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Lochmaben_Fair
