1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN MURRAY OF COCKPOOL===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/236/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: pp. 220-3]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "(399) <strong>Sir John Murray of Cockpool</strong>, died c. 1527. His lands in Dumfriesshire and Kirkcudbright were erected into the Barony of Cockpool 1509. He had issue :
2 CONT * Cuthbert (No. 400).
2 CONT * Patrick Murray, Tutor of Cockpool. Married Janet Campbell. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had also a natural son :
2 CONT * David (No. 406)."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/98/mode/2up The heraldry of the Murrays: with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees], by G. Harvey Johnston, 1910, 
