1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Curson-209
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was the second son of Walter Curson of Waterperry, Oxfordshire.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Thomas Cursson, clerk, Comptroller of the Queens Highness household" made his Will on 2nd May 1555. His wife Annys/Agnes was named as his executor and his brother Wyndsor was named as the Overseer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He bequeaths to his daughter Mary "all the lands that was given unto me by the Quenes highnes, and my own lands before to remain to my daughter Mary and her heirs" also "such stuff and goods that remain of mine at Waterpery to be 
2 CONC to the use of my daughter Mary Cursson as appeareth by a deed of gift of my mother's in my casket".
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate of his Will was granted 30th May 1555.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT # Francis Nichols. The English Compendium: Volume II (1761). Page 343.
2 CONT # https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/D954003; PROB 11/37/352; Will of Thomas Cursson, Clerk; Date: 30 May 1555
