1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT =Alexander Graham, 2nd Earl of Menteith=
2 CONT (c. 1475–c. 1537)  Graham appears in the records of Scotland as the Earl of Menteith in 1493. Likely the grandson of Malise Graham, it is of some debate whether this Earl Alexander was the son of Patrick Graham (Earl Malise's seco
2 CONC nd son) or was the son of Alexander Graham (Earl Malise's first son who died in 1471). Most evidence seems to show that Patrick Graham was the likely father. Prior to 1493 and after the death of Earl Malise Graham in 1490, he is r
2 CONC eferenced, but at that time he is only referenced as heir.[1] During the 15th century in Scotland, one was often termed an heir when the age of majority had not been reached. It is therefore likely that Alexander Graham, this seco
2 CONC nd earl, was born around 1475. Robbers from the Clan Gregor in the year 1533 stole 40 cows from him and his son William, Master of Menteith. He married Margaret Buchanan, daughter of Walter Buchanan of the Clan Buchanan, and had t
2 CONC wo sons and a daughter. He died between the 31st of January 1536 and the 27th of February, in 1537.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From the peerage.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Graham, 2nd Earl of Menteith1 
2 CONT M, #30675, 
2 CONT Alexander Graham, 2nd Earl of Menteith was born circa 1472.1 
2 CONT He was the son of Patrick Graham and Isabel Erskine.1 
2 CONT He married Margaret Buchanan, daughter of Walter Buchanan.1 
2 CONT He died (uncertain?) from 27 February 1536/37 to 16 May 1537.1
2 CONT He succeeded as the 2nd Earl of Menteith [S., 1427] in 1491.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Alexander Graham, 2nd Earl of Menteith and Margaret Buchanan
2 CONT
2 CONT # William Graham, 3rd Earl of Menteith+ d. c 1543/44
2 CONT #Marion Graham+2
2 CONT
