2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warriston Warriston (/wʌrˈɪsˈtən/ Wau-RIS-tən) is a suburb of Edinburgh, the capital of Scotland. It lies east of the Royal Botanic Garden in Inverleith. The name derives from Warriston House, a loc
2 CONC al mansion house demolished in 1966.[1] In July 1600 John Kincaid, the Laird of Warriston was murdered by his wife, Jean Livingstone a daughter of the Laird of Dunipace, her two female servants, and his stable hand. The women were
2 CONC  captured and sentenced to be burnt.[2]
2 CONT ##Ashford, The Lands of Warriston in The Book of the Old Edinburgh Club, New Series vol.3, Edinburgh 1994, p. 20
2 CONT ##John Duncan Mackie, Calendar State Papers Scotland, vol. 13 part 2 (Edinburgh, 1969), pp. 666–7.
2 CONT #Chronological map of Edinburgh showing expansion of the City from earliest days.  < [https://maps.nls.uk/view/74400069#zoom=5&lat=5554&lon=5191&layers=BT link] > 
