1 OCCU 5th Lord of Campbell; 4th Earl of Argyll, Knight
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} --------------------
2 CONT Archibald was calle "the Red" and was the 4th Earl of Argyll. Appointed by King James V Justice-General of Scotland and Master of the Kings Household. He was Mater of the Kings wine cellar in 1542. He fought with distinction at th
2 CONC e battle of Pinkie in 1547 and at the siege of Haddington in 1548. He was among the first peers to adopt Protestantism. In 1558, he wad again appointed to Justice-General by Queen Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT died between 21 August 1558 and 2 December 1558
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 5th Lord Campbell [S., 1445] in 1529.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 4th Lord Lorne [S., 1470] in 1529.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 4th Earl of Argyll [S., 1457] in 1529.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Justiciar [Scotland] on 28 October 1529.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Master of the Household on 28 October 1529.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Master of the King's wine cellar on 28 March 1542.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1543 the lands of of Muckart, Perthsire were bestowed on him for his services in the defence of the Church against heresies.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Justiciar of Bute in 1545.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Pinkie on 10 September 1547, where he commanded a body of Highlanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Siege of Haddington in 1548.
2 CONT
2 CONT After 1548 he was won over by English gold, and went over to the English side.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has an extensive biographical entry in the Dictionary of National Biography.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Castle Campbell (Castle Gloom)
