1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HUGH SOMERVILLE OF DRUM===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hugh Somerville of Drum is the second son of Hugh, Lord Somerville. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/334/mode/1up RMS: 928] His mother seems likely to be Eleanor Seton. [http://archive.org/stream/scotspe
2 CONC eragefoun08pauluoft#page/26/mode/2up The Scots Peerage VIII: 26-7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 April 1593: Charter by which Hugh, Lord Somerville, confirms that he has sold (vendidit) the lands of Gilmertoun, Drum and Gutteris, all located in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh, to his second son Hugh Somerville: "filio suo l
2 CONC egitimo secundogenito". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/334/mode/1up RMS: 928]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 June 1601: Charter by which Hugh Somerville of Drum and Margaret Hamilton, his spouse, with the consent of Gavin Hamilton of Raploch, confirm that they have sold to Mr. John Preston of Fentonbarns and his wife Lilie Gilbert, 
2 CONC the lands of Gutheris, with the mansion house thereof, and the lands of Drum and Gilmertoun, with the castle and manor of thereof, all located in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/pag
2 CONC e/454/mode/1up RMS: 1296]'''
2 CONT
