2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Colquhoun was born in 1573. He was the son of John Colquhoun 15th Laird of Luss
2 CONT
2 CONT This interesting surname is of Scottish locational origin from a place called Colquhoun in the former county of Aberdeenshire (now part of Grampian region), first recorded in the form of "Colghoun" in 1246. The name appears to der
2 CONC ive from the Gaelic "coil", "cuil", a nook, corner or "coill(e)" a wood plus "cumhann" narrow; hence "narrow corner or wood". Colquhoun is the name of a Scottish family descended from Umfridus de Kilpatrick, who acquired the lands
2 CONC  of Colquhoun in the reign of Alexander 11 (1214-1249). The surname is first recorded in the mid 13th Century. Vmfredus de Kelquon witnessed a confirmation charter by Robert 1 to Sir John Colquhoun (1308). About the middle of the 
2 CONC 14th Century Sir Robert Colquhoun married the heiress of Humphrey de Luss and thus became Lord of Colquhoun and Luss.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander married Helen Buchanan in 1595 [1] and died in 1617. [2] [3]
2 CONT
