2 CONT *   ?. William COLQUHOUN        1633-1675 ___________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_John_Colquhoun,_1st_Baronet
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1620, he married Lady Lilias Graham, eldest daughter of John Graham, Fourth Earl of Montrose, and elder sister of the Great Montrose,[5] which was what her younger brother, James Graham, 5th Earl of Montrose, came to be known, 
2 CONC in addition to being the Marquis of Montrose. In 1632 Sir John was accused of absconding his wife's sister, Lady Catherine Graham. It was alleged that he had used witchcraft and sorcery to accomplish this. As a fugitive he was exc
2 CONC ommunicated and his estates forfeited.[6] _____________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p24572.htm#i245712
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created 1st Baronet Colquhoun, of Luss [Nova Scotia] on 30 August 1625, with a special remainder to heirs male whatsoever.1 In 1632 a warrant was issued for his arrest on charge of abducting his sister-in-law, Katherine, th
2 CONC e life-rents of his estates being made over to Sir Robert Douglas of Spott, 1st and last Viscount Belhaven, but Sir John's brother Humphrey recovered the estates.1 ___________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Additional references
2 CONT *Chiefs of Colquhoun and their country. Volume 1 ... Fraser, William, Sir, 1816- 1898 [Author] Calhoun family.  Page xxv - xxvi [https://digital.nls.uk/histories-of-scottish-families/archive/96517274#?c=0&m=0&s=0&cv=30&xywh=-43%2C
2 CONC -385%2C2499%2C5189 link]
2 CONT *The Clan Colquhoun Journal, Vol. 2, Nbr. 2  *Sir John Colquhoun of Luss - Necromancer?", byJames Pearson 
2 CONT *The Clan Colquhoun Journal, Volume 5, Number 3, Autumn 2002, “Who Was William Cahoon?” (The United Kingdom Society) by Gary D. Calder.
2 CONT *Y DNA testing: https://www.familytreedna.com/public/calhoun?iframe=yresults William b 1632 in Hap'group R1b1a2 - Family A.  John of Luss b 1698 in Hap'group E1b1b1 - Regrouping is coming.  Retrieved 11 Sept 2019
2 CONT
