1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ADAM COLQUHOUN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adam Colquhoun is the son of Alexander Colquhoun of Luss and his wife Helen Buchanan. [https://archive.org/details/chiefsofcolquhou01fras/page/235/mode/1up The Chiefs of Colquhoun. Vol, I: p. 235] He is mentioned in his father'
2 CONC s last will and testament dated 16-17 May 1617. His father died on 23 May 1617. [https://archive.org/details/chiefsofcolquhou01fras/page/230/mode/1up Ibidem: p. 230]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian was the daughter of Lindsay of Bonneil and had two children. She married about 1621 and died before 1630. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband: Adam Colquhoun.  Adam is described as a Merchant of Dumbarton and the fifth son of Alexander XIV. [2] Adam was the father of two children, Robert XVI and a daughter, who married Thomas Buchanan, sixth of Carbeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT #Robert Colquhoun  (abt. 1622 - abt. 1666) Married his cousin Katherine McAuselan.  “It was in the person of this Robert Colquhoun that our branch of the family found its way to Ireland"[2]
2 CONT #Helen Colquhoun. (Abt 1625 - ). Married Thomas Buchanan.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT See comments under Discussion tab
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady, Christian Lindsay  
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: ABT 1603 Bonniel, , , Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: ABT 1629 , Dumbarton, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Gender: Female
2 CONT
2 CONT Family:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: ABT 1621 , Dumbarton, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Colquhoun, Adam  
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: ABT 1601 Dumbarton, , , Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: DEC 1634 Dumbarton, , , Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Gender: Male
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Lus, Sir_Alexander_Colquhoun_XV_& XVII of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Buchanan, Margaret Helen 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Colquhoun, Robert  
2 CONT
2 CONT Colquhoun, Helen  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam (did not)  live in Ireland on his fathers property. He inherited the property in 161 7 and in 1630 he transferred title to his son Robert. “He changed the spelling of name to Calhoun when he first went to Ireland.“ [No]  “Joh
2 CONC n C. Calhoun (U.S. Vice-President) of South Carolina's family line descends from Adam.“ [?]
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam married Lady-Christian Lindsay in 1621
2 CONT
