1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ANNABELL ERSKINE (aka ANNABELLAM ERSKYNE)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Annabella Erskine, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Adam-Erskine-Commendator-of-Cambuskenneth/6000000024539924967?through=6000000027691773518  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page
2 CONC /134/mode/1up RMS 1620-1633: charter number 398] It cannot be regarded as being certain but it seems quite likely, probable even, that her mother was https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Drummond/6000000179023896829?through=600000
2 CONC 0027691773518 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/85/mode/1up RMS 1609-1620: charter number 236]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Annabella Erskine, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-Buchanan-17th-of-that-Ilk/6000000020945892285?through=6000000027691773518 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/134/mode/1up RMS 1
2 CONC 620-1633: charter number 398]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 July 1604: Charter by which John Buchanan of that Ilk confirms, following upon a marriage contract dated 5 May 1602, that he has given a liferent from various lands to his wife, Annabellam Erskyne, daughter of Adam, Commenda
2 CONC tor of Cambuskenneth. Her father was alive on 5 May 1602, the date upon which he signed the marriage contract, but he probably died before 28 July 1604, the date upon which the Laird of Buchanan issued his charter. Annabella Ersky
2 CONC ne obtained a charter of confirmation under the Great Seal of Scotland on 24 December 1622. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/134/mode/1up RMS 1620-1633: charter number 398]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Printed Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1620-1633. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. (H. M. Ge
2 CONC neral Register House, Edinburgh, 1894), 1096 pp. including idices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://archive.org/stream/buchananbooklife00buchuoft#page/183/mode/1up EVIDENCE FROM THE BUCHANAN BOOK]===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Buchanan, who married Annabel Erskine daughter of Adam, Commendator of Cambuskenneth, son of the Master of Mar, had, (1) George, his successor, and (2) Walter Buchanan. This Sir John Buchanan was, says Auchmar, account
2 CONC ed the worst, if not the only bad one of all the Lairds of Buchanan, and by his frequent travels into foreign nations and other extravagances had involved his estate in such an immense debt that his grandson at first found it inco
2 CONC nvenient to enter as heir.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://archive.org/stream/cu31924028090698#page/n337/mode/1up EVIDENCE FROM STRATHENDERICK]===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''JOHN BUCHANAN of Buchanan had gift of the ward and non-entry of  all his estates since the death of his father, Sir George, dated, Perth, 28th March 1599. On 26th October 1602 he is retoured heir of his father Sir George Buchan
2 CONC an in Buchanan, and other lands, and in the same year he had a thirty-eight years tack of the whole teinds of Kilmaronock from his father-in-law, Adam, Commendator of Cambuskenneth, to him and his wife Annabel Erskine. By Annabel 
2 CONC Erskine he had at least two sons: (1) George; and (2) Walter, who was at Glasgow College 7th March 1620.''' 
2 CONT
