1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mariote 'Marjory' Stewart''' was born in Balvenie, Fifeshire, Scotland. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-10029640 John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-10029677 Eleanor Sinclair, Coun
2 CONC tess of Atholl]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariote married [https://www.geni.com/profile-60414238 Colin Campbell, 3rd of Glenorchy] in 1508 in Balvenie Castle, Dufftown, Banffshire, Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-38485928 Sir Duncan Campbell, 4th of Glenorchy]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-38485929 Sir John Campbell, 5th of Glenorchy]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-47512776 Colin Campbell, 6th of Glenorchy and Arkinglass]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34840423168 Mariota Campbell]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34840423186 Helen Campbell].  
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on July 26, 1529 in Isle of Lochtay, Perthshire, Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Wives and Daughters of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl - Part 1" (Brad Verity et al, May 15, 2014).  < [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/eq3_G4VOLiI/m/NhYosxelf7oJ soc.genealogy.medieval] >
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Mariote Stewart, married Colin Campbell, 3rd Laird of Glenorchy
2 CONT
2 CONT She is called sixth daughter of 2nd wife by DP, 4th daughter of 2nd wife by BEP, and listed as the 10th daughter in SP Atholl (1904).
2 CONT
2 CONT Most sources call this daughter 'Margery', but from her obit in the Chronicle of Fortingall, we know her name was 'Mariote', and that she died on 26 July 1529 [not 1524, as SP has it]:
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Obitus Mariote Stuart domine de Glenwrquhay xxvj die Julii apud Insulam de Lochtay, et sepulta in Finlark anno Domini mvxxviiij" https://archive.org/stream/blackbookoftaymo00inneuoft#page/120/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Gordon MacGregor in the Campbell of Glenorchy pedigree in his Red Book of Scotland series, updated just this year, Mariote (whom he calls 'Margery') Stewart and the 3rd Laird of Glenorchy had an elder daughter, 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Mariota Campbell, m. by 5 October, 1498, William Stewart, 2nd of Balindoran, (he was widow of Janet, daughter of Archibald Buchannan of Lettir, by whom he had issue) and had issue": http://www.redbookofscotland.com/sample%20fami
2 CONC lies/Campbell%20of%20Glenorchy.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT '''If Mariote Stewart had a daughter who in turn was married by 1498, Mariote would have to have been a daughter of the 1st Earl of Atholl by his 1st wife Margaret Douglas.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Disputed origins
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart and Eleanor Sinclair had two sons and nine daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Atholl, living 1520, and died before 1522, who married Janet Campbell (died about Candlemas 1545/6), daughter of Archibald Campbell, 2nd Earl of Arygll.
2 CONT # Andrew Stewart, Bishop of Caithness.
2 CONT # Jean (or Janet) Stewart, married by contract dated 31 August 1507, James Arbuthnott of Arbuthnott. He had a crown charter of the feudal barony of Arbuthnott 29 January 1507. He left a testament dated 7 March 1521, and died befor
2 CONC e 13 March 1521.
2 CONT # .Katherine Stewart, married Sir John Forbes, 6th Lord Forbes.
2 CONT # Elizabeth/Elspeth Stewart, married Sir Robert Innes 2nd of Innermarky.
2 CONT # Marjory Stewart, married Sir Colin Campbell, of Glenorchy.
2 CONT # Margaret Stewart, married Sir William Murray, of Castleton who was killed at Battle of Flodden Duke of Atholl
2 CONT # Elizabeth Stewart, married Alexander Robertson, of Strowan.
2 CONT # Elizabeth (or Isabel) Stewart, married John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Lennox
2 CONT # Jean Stewart, married Robert Gordon, Knt., of Pitlurg.
2 CONT # Margaret Stewart, married Robert Robertson younger, of Strowan.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Stewart,_1st_Earl_of_Atholl]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Mariote was the daughter of John Stewart of Balveny and Eleanor Sinclair. [1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Colin Campbell.[1][2] There were at least three children from this marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Duncan Campbell[3] 
2 CONT #     John Campbell[3] 
2 CONT #     Colin Campbell[3]  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
