2 TITL Balvenie Castle
2 NOTE https://www.historicenvironment.scot/visit-a-place/places/balvenie-castle/
3 CONT
3 CONT A wide ditch encircles this striking, curtain-walled castle. Built in the 1200s as the seat of the powerful earls of Buchan, the heavily fortified stronghold became an elegant lodging in the 1500s.
3 CONT
3 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balvenie_Castle
3 CONT
3 CONT Balvenie Castle is a ruined castle 1 km north of Dufftown in the Moray region of Scotland. 
3 CONT
3 CONT Originally known as Mortlach, it was built in the 12th century by a branch of the powerful Comyn family (the Black Comyns) and was extended and altered in the 15th and 16th centuries. .... . The Battle of Arkinholm in May 1455 saw
3 CONC  the defeat of this, the main Douglas line by an army loyal to James II. All of their lands and titles were forfeited to the Crown, including Balvenie Castle. King James divided up the estates among his supporters, which included 
3 CONC the Douglas Earl of Angus and provided Balvenie Castle to Sir John Stewart, who later became the first Earl of Atholl. 
