2 CONT # "The Campbell of Glenorchy Family Tree" < [https://www.nationalgalleries.org/art-and-artists/24093 nationalgalleries.org] > The original Lord Campbell, Duncan Campbell of Lochawe, is depicted reclining below an elaborately fruit
2 CONC ing cherry tree.  The trunk is decorated with portraits of Glenorchy lairds, with Colin Campbell (who commissioned the work) second from the top and his potential heir above. The surrounding roundels further document the genealogy
2 CONC . The ornate and heraldic quality reflects Jamesone’s training as a decorative painter and the rich colour scheme is typical of his oeuvre.
