1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Her parents are "traditionally" seen as https://www.geni.com/people/Colin-Campbell-1st-Lord-of-Glenorchy/6000000006444452295?through=6000000006147775259 and his 3rd wife, https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Stirling/6000000002955
2 CONC 134135?through=6000000006444452295.  However, the [http://redbookofscotland.co.uk/ ''Red Book of Scotland''] shows this Mariota Campbell as daughter of the 3rd of Glenorchy.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mariote Campbell''' Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-60414238 Colin Campbell, 3rd of Glenorchy] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-115269659 Mariote 'Marjory' Stewart]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariote married [https://www.geni.com/profile-76735118 William Stewart of Balquidder and Baldoran] before October 5, 1498. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-120420167 John Stewart, 1st of Glenbuckie]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34670504702 Walter Stewart, 3rd of Baldorran]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34840428161 Elen Stewart].  
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on August 12, 1537 in East Ayrshire, Scotland. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://rykbrown.net/TNG/getperson.php?personID=I18797&tree=BROWN
2 CONT
2 CONT Duncan Stewart (1739) says:
2 CONT
2 CONT >"William Stewart of Baldorran, married Marion [sic: Mariot] Campbell, daughter to Sir Colin Campbell of Glenurquhy, as appears by a charter in their favours, granted by Robert Menzies of Comrie, of the lands of Emyr-Crechan [sic 
2 CONC s/b Emyr-Crethane] and Croftyn-Terray, in the Earldom of Strathern and Shire of Perth, dated at Lochtay, the 5th of October 1498. This charter is confirmed by King James IV, the 25th of said month. By her, he had Walter and John, 
2 CONC who is a witness to several charters , and designed Johannes filius Guliemi Stewart de Baldorran, particularly in 1508, granted by Glenurchy. Of him is Glenbucky. William of Baldorran is said to have had another son, Andrew, of wh
2 CONC om Gartnafuaroe [sic - Andrew of Gartnafuaran was the brother of William, not his son.] Of these three brothers [sic] are most of the Stewarts of the South-west district of Perthshire descended, to the number at least 300 common p
2 CONC eople. <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT >Addenda - For Emyr-Crechan, read Emyr-Crethane. These lands were talzied [illegible] of Walter, and his lawful heirs, to John Stewart, his brother. There is one Andrew Stewart, witness to this charter, who, perhaps, might have be
2 CONC en Garnafuaroe's ancestor. The lands of Duchlass, in the lordship of Rosneth, and shire of Dumbarton, holden of the King in Feu, are confirmed to Walter Stewart, son of WIlliam Steart of Baldorran, and the lawful heirs-male of his
2 CONC  body, which failing to William Stewart's lawful heirs whatsoevr, pub arch lib 13, num 370. By what evidences I have [illegible] of Baldorran, it appears that the traditional account mentioned in the note of page 133 [referring to
2 CONC  the origin of the Stewarts of Gartnafuaran] is not well grounded." <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sir William married firstly by 1 May 1484, to Janet, daughter of Archibald de Buchannan,1st of Lettir, (she was widow of Robert Tosheoch, son of Andrew Tosheoch of Monzievaird, by whom she had no apparent issue), when they had a 
2 CONC charter from her father for the lands of Lettir, in the Lordship of Strathgartney.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Stewart_of_Baldorran
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Stewart (c.1440–c.1500), 2nd Laird of Baldorran, 1st Royal Bailie of the Crown lands of Balquhidder, was a fifteenth-century Scottish landowner, and founder of the Balquhidder Stewart clan. He was the grandson of James
2 CONC  Mhor Stewart who launched a failed bid for the Crown of Scotland in 1429. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stewart married twice. His first wife was Janet Buchanan, daughter of Archibald Buchanan of Lettir (in Strathyre). They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Janet Stewart (born c1475).
2 CONT #     Agnes Stewart (born c1477).
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife was Marion Helen Campbell, [SIC: MARIOTE] Of Glenorchy, daughter of Colin Campbell, '''1st of Glenorchy''', whom he married on 5 October 1498, and by whom he had three children:[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Walter Stewart, 3rd Laird of Baldorran, 2nd Bailie of Balquhidder, born c1480 in Baldorran, Campsie, Stirlingshire.
2 CONT #     John Stewart, 1st Laird of Glenbuckie, born c1485 in Baldorran, Campsie, Stirlingshire.
2 CONT #     Mariote Stewart, born c1490 in Baldorran, Campsie, Stirlingshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the portioning of Balquhidder which took place during the sixteenth century, the descendants of Sir William Stewart of Baldorran gained hereditary tacks of land. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Campbell-2596
2 CONT
2 CONT Marion was the daughter of Colin Campbell and Margaret Striveling.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married WIlliam Stewart before 5 Oct 1498.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.thepeerage.com/p1944.htm#i19436
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Colin Campbell, 1st of Glenorchy was the son of Sir Duncan Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell and Margaret Stewart.2 He married, firstly, Mariot Stewart, daughter of Sir William Stewart of Albany, before 1448.1 He married, secondly, 
2 CONC Janet Stewart, daughter of John Stewart, 2nd Lord Lorn and unknown wife (?), circa 1448.1 He married, thirdly, Margaret Robertson, daughter of Robert Robertson of Struan, after 1448.1 He married, fourthly, Margaret Stirling, daugh
2 CONC ter of Lucas Stirling, before 27 October 1467.1 He died circa September 1475.1 He was also reported to have died on 24 September 1480.3 He was buried on 26 September 1475.1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Colin Campbell, 1st of Glenorchy and Margaret Stirling
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Marion Campbell+4 d. bt 28 Apr 1530 - 23 Aug 1530.  Married 1)  Malise Graham, 1st Earl of Menteith 2) John Drummond
2 CONT #     George Campbell1
2 CONT #     Mariot Campbell1.  Married William Stewart of Baldoran before 1498.
2 CONT #     Helen Campbell+1.  She married, firstly, unknown MacEane of Ardnamurchan.1 She married, secondly, unknown MacLaine of Lochbuie.1 She married, thirdly, Iain MacGregor, 7th Chief of Clan Gregor, son of Evan MacGregor, after fi
2 CONC rst ravishing her.
2 CONT #     John Campbell, 1st of Lawers+4 d. 9 Sep 1513
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Descendants ofThe Duke of Albany From Duncan Stewart’s Genealogy
2 CONT https://www.chuckspeed.com/balquhidder/history/dstewart.html
2 CONT
2 CONT p.173               V. William Stewart of Baldorran. m. Marion, dau. of Sir Colin Campbell & Margaret, dau. of John, Last Lord Lorn. Living 25 Oct 1498.
2 CONT
2 CONT *                                     1. Walter, his successor.
2 CONT *                                     2. John of Glenbucky, of whom later. Living 1508.
2 CONT *                                     3. Andrew of Gartnafuaroe, of whom later.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "Wives and Daughters of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl - Part 1" (Brad Verity et al, May 15, 2014).  < [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/eq3_G4VOLiI/m/NhYosxelf7oJ soc.genealogy.medieval] >
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Mariote Stewart, married Colin Campbell, 3rd Laird of Glenorchy
2 CONT
2 CONT She is called sixth daughter of 2nd wife by DP, 4th daughter of 2nd wife by BEP, and listed as the 10th daughter in SP Atholl (1904).
2 CONT
2 CONT Most sources call this daughter 'Margery', but from her obit in the Chronicle of Fortingall, we know her name was 'Mariote', and that she died on 26 July 1529 [not 1524, as SP has it]:
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Obitus Mariote Stuart domine de Glenwrquhay xxvj die Julii apud Insulam de Lochtay, et sepulta in Finlark anno Domini mvxxviiij" https://archive.org/stream/blackbookoftaymo00inneuoft#page/120/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Gordon MacGregor in the Campbell of Glenorchy pedigree in his Red Book of Scotland series, updated just this year, Mariote (whom he calls 'Margery') Stewart and the '''3rd Laird of Glenorchy''' '''had an elder daughter''', 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Mariota Campbell, m. by 5 October, 1498, William Stewart, 2nd of Balindoran, (he was widow of Janet, daughter of Archibald Buchannan of Lettir, by whom he had issue) and had issue": http://www.redbookofscotland.com/sample%20fami
2 CONC lies/Campbell%20of%20Glenorchy.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT '''If Mariote Stewart had a daughter who in turn was married by 1498, Mariote would have to have been a daughter of the 1st Earl of Atholl by his 1st wife Margaret Douglas.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
