1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM RUTHVEN===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Competing Claims and Fake Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''First'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Peter Barns-Grahams has received a report which suggests that William Ruthven, here treated, may have settled in Sweden, but presently, for want of evidence, this claim cannot be verified. [https://www.stirnet.com/g
2 CONC enie/data/british/qr/ruthven2.php Stirnet: Ruthven 02] There was a man named William Ruthven who is noticed as a Colonel in Swedish service but the name of his father has not been statisfactorily identified. [https://archive.org/s
2 CONC tream/scotsinswedenbei00fiscuoft#page/48/mode/1up The Scots in Sweden, pp. 48 et seq.] Possibly he is the same person as Captain William Ruthven. [https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=1721 Universiry of St. Andrew
2 CONC s: Institute of Scottish Historical Studies]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Second'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''At least one pedigree published by MyHeritage claims that it was William Ruthven, the son of William, second Lord Ruthven, and Lady Janet Haliburton, who married Katherine Stewart and had four children, including a 
2 CONC son named Alexander. [https://www.myheritage.com/names/william_ruthven MyHeritage] This suggests that he was the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/William-Ruthven-of-Ballindean/6000000019003358643?from_flash=1&fsession_id
2 CONC =1580935843316&through=6000000057283946165 who was he son of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Ruthven-of-Ballindean/6000000058633692018?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1580936392441&through=6000000019003358643 and his wife https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/people/Agnes-Crichton/6000000004268676680?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1580936506529&through=6000000058633692018 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/102/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 102]'''</blockquote
2 CONC >
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Fake Pedigree Published by MyHeritage'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''William Ruthven, 1530 - 1599. William Ruthven was born in 1530, at birth place, to William Ruthven and Janet Ruthven (born Halyburton). William was born in 1502, in Huntington Hall, Ruthven Castle, Perthshire, Scotl
2 CONC and. Janet was born Circa April 19 1503, in Kynard, Perthshire, Scotland. William had 14 siblings: Lilias Drummond (born Ruthven), Katherine Campbell (born Ruthven) and 12 other siblings. William married Katherine Jean Ruthven (bo
2 CONC rn Stewart) circa 1568, at age 38. Catherine was born circa 1538. They had 4 children: Alexander Ruthven and 3 other children. His occupation was occupation. William passed away on month day 1599, at age 69 at death place. He was 
2 CONC buried at burial place. [https://www.myheritage.com/names/william_ruthven MyHeritage]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of Identity===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Ruthven, here treated, is the son of William, Lord Ruthven, and his wife Jonet Haliburton. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#page/260/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 260]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''With his brothers James, Henry, and Alexander, William Ruthven, here treated, was one of the heirs in remainder identified in a charter dated 10 June 1540 by which James V, King of Scots, confirmed that he had given various lan
2 CONC ds to William Ruthven of Ballandane. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/491/mode/1up RMS: charter number 2169 on p. 491]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Ruthven, here treated, is not mentioned in the list of heirs in remainder who are identified in the charter by which Jonet Haliburton, wife of William, Lord Ruthven, confirmed that she had given the lands of Ballindane 
2 CONC in the barony of Ballegirnoch and sheriffdom of Perth to William Ruthven of Ballindane. William already possessed the lands of Ballindane but he had resigned them into the hands of the superior, Jonet Haliburton, in order to obtai
2 CONC n a new grant which included his heirs in remainder. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/682/mode/1up RMS: charter number 2913 on pp. 682-83]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for William Ruthven, here treated. He was alive on 10 June 1540, when he and his brothers James, Henry and Alexander, were named as heirs in remainder to William Ruthven of Ball
2 CONC indean, but because he is not mentioned in William Ruthven of Ballandane's second charter, dated 8 May 1543, it has been suggested that: "he was probably dead" before this date. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#p
2 CONC age/260/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 260]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 June 1540: Charter by which James V, King of Scots, confirms that he had given various lands to William Ruthven of Ballandane. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/491/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regu
2 CONC m Scottorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 2169 on p. 491]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 May 1543: Charter by which James V, King of Scots, confirms that he had given various lands to William Ruthven of Ballandane. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/682/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum 
2 CONC Scottorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 2913 on pp. 682-83]'''
