2 CONT '''25 February 1625: Contract between Sir Duncan Campbell of Glenurquhie, kt, tutor of Katherine Campbell, his lawful daughter, on one part, and Patrick Campbell of Culdaris, on other part, whereby said Duncan `"for the better hel
2 CONC p and support of the said Katreine Campbell his dochter to ane honourabill mareage" binds himself to deliver to said Patrick before 1 May next to come, various great mares as specified; 50 in Auchinchalein and merkland of Glenking
2 CONC las, 50 in Glenlochae Albanoch, 24 in Glenlocha Urquhay and Coniniche, 2 in park of Finlarg, extending in all to sixscore six great mares, to be kept by said Patrick in steelbow, for the next nine years following. Cancelled by rem
2 CONC oval of the signature of granter. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f23%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+campbell+of+culdaris&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/23/13]'''
