1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARGARET TOSHEOCH===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Tosheoch was the daughter of Andrew and Elizabeth Tosheoch. In August 1581 (11th and 24th inst., at Ilanran, Stirlingshire, and Monzie, Perthshire, respectively), she contracted to marry Archibald Campbell the fourth s
2 CONC on of Colin Campbell, 6th of Glenorchy. She hadn't married as it was said she "digested the signature she had ripped off from her marriage contract" as she was unsatisfied marrying her future husband (according to a mention from 1
2 CONC 601). [http://redbookofscotland.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/Tosheoch-of-Monzievaird.pdf Red Book of Scotland]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Tosheoch, here treated, did afterwards marry Archibald Campbell, brother of Duncan Campbell of Glenorchy. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f149&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=
2 CONC n&tp=n&k=campbell+of+ardbeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD112/2/149]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 April 1602: Extract contract between Sir Duncan Campbell of Glenurquhay, kt. and Colin Campbell, his eldest son, on one part, and Archibald Campbell, brother of said Duncan, and Margaret Toscheoch, his spouse, on other part,
2 CONC  whereby said Archibald and Margaret surrender 3 merkland of Murlagan Moir, 10 merkland of Nether Larach (?Lanich), 4 merkland of Cortharmuik with forest, 4 merkland of Tirray, £3 land of Tulliche, £3 land of Dalgirdy, pertaining 
2 CONC to granter by reversion made to him by deceased Colin Campbell of Glenurquhay, his father, in sheriffdom of Perth, £6 land of Achinrear, 8 merkland of Lesmoir with chantry thereof, 10 merkland of Achlyne, 2 merkland of Contaliche,
2 CONC  4 merkland of Drumveik, lodging in burgh of Perth in Southgate on north side thereof, pertaining to granter as heir of deceased Mr Patrick Campbell, his brother, in said sheriffdom, maills and duties thereof, and all bairn's part
2 CONC  of goods, heirship etc., as heir of said Patrick or of Colin Campbell of Ardbeith, his brother, 13 April 1602. Reg. b of c and s, 20 July 16(torn). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1
2 CONC 12%2f2%2f149&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=campbell+of+ardbeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/149]'''
