2 DATE BEF 24 MAR 1632
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===COLIN CAMPBELL OF ARDBEITH===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sometime fiar of Glenorchy===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 June 1615: Precept of clare constat by Sir Duncan Campbell of Glenurquhay, kt., in favour of Colin Campbell of Ardbeith, as heir of deceased Colin Campbell of Ardbeith, granter's brother, his father, in 4 merkland of Dowinche
2 CONC , Stronnuo and Corrieantran in lordship of Glendochart, sheriffdom of Perth. With sasine, procuratory of resignation in favour of said Sir Duncan and Colin Campbell, his eldest son, fiar of Glenurchy, and instrument following, 8-1
2 CONC 0 June 1615. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f34%2f24&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=campbell+of+ardbeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the C
2 CONC ampbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/34/24]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 January 1617: Inhibition at instance of James Cheisholme of Cromlix on bond of provision 1 January 1617 in supplement of marriage contract between Jean, his sister, and Colin Campbell of Ardbeith. Reg. Particular Register of 
2 CONC Inhibitions Perth 29 November 1617. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f52%2f19&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=campbell+of+ardbeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Sc
2 CONC otland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/52/19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 December 1619: Obligation by Colin Campbell of Ardbeich, Balloch, as to writs of Kingart. Narrates that, with consent of Jean Chisholme, his spouse, and Sir James Chisholme of Cromlix, his brother-in-law, he had, by contract 
2 CONC dated at Dunblane and Balloch 2-20 November 1619 sold to Colin Campbell, fiar of Glenurquhay, his heirs male and assignees, the 8 merklands of Kingart, stewartry of Stratherne and sheriffdom of Perth. Binds himself to make availab
2 CONC le for judicial transumpt etc:- Extract Retour dated at Crieff 25 January 1610 as heir to late Colin Campbell of Ardbeich, his father, in Kingart, Ardbeich, Darrie etc, stewartry of Stratherne, sheriffdom of Perth. Sasine 6 March 
2 CONC 1616 (Patrick Drummond, notary) on precept from Chancery following on above retour. Procuratory by Colin Campbell of Ardbeich 19 December 1616 for resignation of 8 merklands of Kingart, 8 merklands of Ardbeichlorne, 4 merklands of
2 CONC  Darrie with mills etc to Crown for new grant to said Colin Campbell and Jean Chisholm in liferent, and heirs male etc. Instrument of resignation following thereon, 19 December 1616, Patrick Hamilton, notary. Great Seal charter 20
2 CONC  December 1616 in favour of Colin Campbell and Jean Chisholme and heirs male etc of 8 merklands of Kingart, 8 merklands of Ardbeich Lorne and 4 merklands of Darrie, with mills etc. Precept of sasine under Quarter Seal of 20 Decemb
2 CONC er 1616. Sasine 21 February 1617, Robert Muschet notary. Written by Thomas Rae, notary public, servant to Sir Duncan Campbell of Glenurquhy, and witnesses by him with John Campbell of Eddiramucky, Mungo Lokhart, servant to Colin C
2 CONC ampbell, fiar of Glenurquhay, Andrew Ogilvy, servant to granter, and James Campbell, fiar of Fintullich. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f6%2f48&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=c
2 CONC hisholme+of+cromlix&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/6/48]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 January 1620: Letters of inhibition at instance of Colin Campbell, fiar of Glenvruqhie, against Colin Campbell of Ardbeith. Narrates contract dated at Dunblane and Balloch 2-20 November 1619 by which, for sum of 5000 merks, s
2 CONC aid Colin Campbell of Ardbeith, with consent of Jean Chisholme, his spouse, and Sir James Chisholme of Cromlix, his brother-in-law, sold to said Colin Campbell of Glenvrquhie the 8 merklands of Kingarth, stewartry of Stratherne an
2 CONC d sheriffdom of Perth, and was to grant tack of said lands until entry of said Colin Campbell of Glenvrquhay with the superior. Seeks inhibition in implement of said contract. With executions. Inhibition reg. Perth Sheriff Court 1
2 CONC 8 February 1620. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f6%2f52&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=chisholme+of+cromlix&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of th
2 CONC e Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/6/52]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 February 1622: Charter by Colin Campbell of Ardbeith, Edinburgh, with consent of Jean Chisholme, his spouse, and Sir James Chisholme of Cromlix, to Archibald Campbell, brother of Sir James Campbell of Laweris, of 6 merklands 
2 CONC of Ardchalzie Eister in lordship of Glendochart, reserving his own liferent, in implement of contract made at Dunblane on 4 September 1621 and contract of present date. Written by Master David Ramsay, servant to Adam Lawtie, write
2 CONC r in Edinburgh. Witnesses: John Campbell of Innerzelvie, Master William Stirling, son of late Master William Stirling, rector of Aberfoyll, said Adam Lawtie and Masters David Ramsay and Andrew Patersone, his servants. [http://cata
2 CONC logue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f7%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=chisholme+of+cromlix&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Br
2 CONC eadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/7/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 January 1622: Charter by Colin Cambell of Ardbeithe, Dunblane, with consent of Jean Chisholme, his wife, and of Sir James Chisholme of Cromlix, knight, in favour of Archibald Cambell, brother of Sir James Campbell of Laweris,
2 CONC  in terms of agreement at Edinburgh 21 December 1622 of 6 merklands of Ardchalzie Eister in lordship of Glendochart, Perth-shire, holding from Sir Duncan Campbell of Glenurquhie and Colin Campbell, his son, reserving liferent. Wri
2 CONC tten by Alexander  Hervie, servant to Robert Alschunder, writer. Witnesses: Master James Campbell, son of Sir James Campbell of Laweris, John Blakwode, in Dunblane, Thomas Hambell, notary there, and Robert Muschet, notary in Monte
2 CONC the. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f7%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=chisholme+of+cromlix&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Fa
2 CONC mily, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/7/8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1632: Extract registered renunciation by Anna Campbell, Dunblane, daughter and heiress to late Colin Campbell of Ardbeiche with consent of Mungo Campbell, fiar of Laweris, Archibald Campbell, his uncle, Sir James Chish
2 CONC olme of Cromlix, and Walter Chisholme in Dunblane, her curators, and of Jean Chisholme, her mother, widow of Colin Campbell, and consent of Sir Colin Campbell of Glenwrquhy. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/d
2 CONC etails.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f6%2f53&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=chisholme+of+cromlix&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), referenc
2 CONC e GD112/2/6/53]'''
