2 CONT
2 CONT Married to William John Hall (1517-1560)
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hall was born 1513 in Durham, England and died about 1575 in Eidlecote, Warwickshire, England. He married Mary Stuartel aka Mary Stewart who was born 1513 in Durham, England and died circa 1570 in Warwickshire, England. Sh
2 CONC e was the daughter of Alexander Stewart (1493 - 1513) Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. John Hall was born 1534 Mirfield, Yorkshire, England. He was buried on Dec. 9, 1607
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. John William Hall was born 1535 in Mirfield, Yorkshire, England. He died in 1605 in Willesborough, Kent, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Francis Hall was born on July 23, 1540 in Mirfield, Yorkshire, England. He died in 1610
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. William Hall was born 1541 in Mirfield, Yorkshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Thomas Hall was born 1543 in Mirfield, Yorkshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. James Hall was born 1545 in Mirfield, Yorkshire, England
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Unclear if this is the correct line- no child named Wilhelmus Holloway referenced, but there was a "William Lee I Holloway" born to her in 1543 (1 of 13
2 CONT
2 CONT When Lady Mary Stewart was born in 1513, in Durham, Durham, England, her father, Sir Alexander Stewart 4th Lord of Dalswinton, was 32 and her mother, Elizabeth Kennedy of Blairquhan, was 41. She married William John Hall in 1538, 
2 CONC in Mirfield, Yorkshire, England, United Kingdom. They were the parents of at least 12 sons and 1 daughter. She died on 22 August 1570, in Yorkshire East Riding, England, United Kingdom, at the age of 57, and was buried in Rotherha
2 CONC m, Yorkshire, England.
