3 TIME 21:35:25
0 @I6000000070201223405@ INDI
1 NAME John /Wallace of Auchans and Dundonald/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Wallace of Auchans and Dundonald
2 _MARNM Wallace of Auchans and Dundonald
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 16 OCT 1572
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN WALLACE OF AUCHANS AND DUNDONALD===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''John Wallace of Auchans and Dundonald, here treated, was formerly known as John Wallace of Inchgotrig, He was the tutor of Craigie and the bailie principal of Kyle-Stewart'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Wallace of Inchgotrid, afterwards known as John Wallace of Dundonald, is noticed as tutor of Craigie on 22 April 1543, [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/569/mode/1up RMS, 1600-20: 1578] and then agai
2 CONC n on 3 July 1545. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f132&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+wallace&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1580&di=n NRS: GD8/132] He is noticed as Bailie Principal of
2 CONC  Kyle-Stewart on 10 February 1557.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f30%2f22&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Wallace+of+Dundonald&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD3/1/1/30/22]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Wallace of Auchans and Dundonald died before 16 October 1572, the date upon which his eldest son John was served as heir to his deceased father. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n308/mode/1up The Book o
2 CONC f Wallace. Volume I: 138]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Wallace of Dundonald married Katherine Kennedy, widow of William Lord Herries. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/740/mode/1up RMS, 1513-46: 3151] She must have died before 24 October 1573, by which d
2 CONC ate her husband had married for a second time. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/564/mode/1up RMS, 1546-80: 2149]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Wallace of Auchans and Dundonald married Agnes Stewart, daughter of Sir John Stewart of Minto and sister of Walter, Lord Blantyre. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n308/mode/1up The Book of Wallace: 138
2 CONC ] She and her husband had a charter for the lands of Burnesyd on 24 October 1573. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/564/mode/1up RMS, 1546-80: 2149]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 April 1543:  Charter issued by Master Thomas Huchesone, chaplain of the chapel of Saint Ninian of Dundonald, on 28 April 1543. By his charter Master Thomas confirmed that he has given a feu charter for the following lands to
2 CONC  JOHN WALLACE OF INCHGOTRIG,TUTOR OF CRAIGIE; viz. the five merk lands of Plewlands, the four merk lands of Gretriggs, the one merk lands of Gauriggs, the one merk lands of Holmes of Dundonald, together with the manse and glebe of
2 CONC  the chaplainry. His charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 28 April 1543. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/569/mode/1up RMS, 1600-20: 1578]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Before 28 January 1617 John Wallace, now of Dundonald, grandson and heir of the deceased John Wallace of Inchtogrig, quitclaimed and gave up any rights he may have had in this land.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 July 1545: Act, ordaining JOHN WALLACE, TUTOR OF CRAIGIE, as principal, Hugh Wallace of Carnweill, John Wallace of Meynfuid and Hugh Wallace in Aucharris, as cautioners to Robert Boyd of Kilmarnock, for resignation by him in 
2 CONC favour of the said JOHN of the £20 land of DUNDONALD and the sum of 900 marks. Dated at Ayr, 3 Jul 1545. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f132&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+walla
2 CONC ce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1580&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/132]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 July 1545: Charter which confirms possession of the lands of DUNDONALD to JOHN WALLACE, TUTOR OF CRAIGIE. Dundonald had previously resigned in favour of JOHN WALLACE by Robert Boyd in Kilmarnock, with the consent of his wife
2 CONC  Agnes Sommerville and his son Robert Boyd. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/737/mode/1up RMS, 1513-46: 3136]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 August 1545: Charter which confirms possession of the lands of DUNDONALD to JOHN WALLACE, TUTOR OF CRAIGIE, and his wife LADY KATHERINE KENNEDY, widow of William Lord Herries. The land is to be held by them in conjunct fee a
2 CONC nd liferent, and by their lawful male heirs in feu ferme, whom failing by JOHN WALLACE'S lawful heirs. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/740/mode/1up RMS, 1513-46: 3151]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 May1549: Extract decree (dated 6 Apr 1549) in the action at the instance of Robert, Lord Boyd of Kilmarnock, and his assignee, William, Lord Semphill, to the reversion of the lands of Previk, against Elizabeth Campbell, reli
2 CONC ct of William Wallace, warditor of Craigie, the late William, Earl of Glencairn, her spouse, for his interest, and John Wallace, her nephew, and the said WILLIAM [WALLACE, WARDITOR OF CRAIGIE] and JOHN WALACE, HIS TUTOR. The actio
2 CONC n is continued to the 23 May 1549. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f143&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+wallace&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boy
2 CONC d Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/143]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 March 1551-52: Letter of reversion by William Dalrimpill [Dalrymple] of Laucht to Jonet Dalrimpill, his "darrest sister", undertaking that if Marion, his sister, or her heirs shall succeed him in the £5 lands of Cameragane t
2 CONC hey shall resign them to the said Jonet or her heirs on payment of 500 merks on the high altar of the parish church of Aire [Ayr]. At Aire. Witnesses: David Craufurde [Crawford], brother to the laird of Kilburny [Kilbirnie], MASTE
2 CONC R ADAM WALLACE, BROTHER OF JOHN WALLACE, TUTOR OF CRAGY, Thomas Lamb, George Kessane [Kesson] and Master Gavin Ross, notary. Henry Prestoun [Preston], notary, signs for the granter. No witnesses' signatures. [Tag and seal missing.
2 CONC ] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD117%2f71&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+wallace&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1580&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cathcart Family of Ca
2 CONC rleton and Killochan, reference GD117/71]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 September 1557: Instrument of sasine following on GD3/1/1/30/21 in favour of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton as heir foresaid in the lordship and lands of Giffen. Baillie Edward Wallace of Sewalton, baillie depute of JOHN WALLACE OF 
2 CONC DUNDONALD, BAILLIE PRINCIPAL OF KYLE STEWART. Witnesses: Patrick Montgomery of Giffen, John Mur of Park and others. Hugh Dunlop, notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f3
2 CONC 0%2f22&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Wallace+of+Dundonald&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/30/22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 October 1573: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms possession of the forty shilling lands called Burnesyd, located in the parish of Dundonald in the Kyle-Stewart division of Ayrshire, to JOHN WALLACE OF DUNDONA
2 CONC LD and his wife AGNES STEWART. The land is to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent, and by their lawful male heirs in feu ferme, whom failing to John's heirs and assignees. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04sc
2 CONC ot/page/564/mode/1up RMS, 1546-80: 2149]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 March 1574-75: Duplicate of charter number 2149. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/640/mode/1up RMS, 1546-80: 2381]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 December 1575: Charter by John Wallace of Craigie, son and heir of deceased John Wallace of Craigie with the advice and consent of Hugh Wallace of Carnell, JOHN WALLACE OF DUNDONALD, Mr Michael Wallace de [C]rawfurd, his cur
2 CONC ators for their interest in implementation of a contract between himself with the consent of his curators and Lord James, Earl of Morton, Lord Dalkeith at Edinburgh and Ayr of sale and alienation in favour of Lord James of 40 merk
2 CONC  land of old extent of Thuristoun (Thurston), Wodhall (Woodhall) and Waddilie (Weatherley), 20 pound land of Thuristoun and Wodhall, 10 merk land of Woddilie in property and tenandry in the barony and sheriffdom of Renfrew by anne
2 CONC xation to hold in property and tenandry of the king as prince and stewart of Scotland. At Edinburgh and Ayr, 24th and 28th December 1575. Witnesses: William Wallace, my servant, Michael Wallace, and William Wallace, son of said Mi
2 CONC chael, Hugh Wallace, uncle, and Thomas Wallace, brother of said John Wallace of Dundonald and William Wallace in Tarbert and diverse others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f1386%
2 CONC 2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=wallace+of+dundonald&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Charters Relating to North Berwick and Thuristoun, East Lothian, reference GD1/1386/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n308/mode/1up The Book of Wallace by the Reverend Charles Rodgers, DD., LL.D. Volume I. (Grampian Club, Edinburgh, MDCCCLXXXIX), 305 pp., see pp. 138-45 for Wallace of Auch
2 CONC ans and Dundonald]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ww/wallace03.php Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Wallace03]'''
