1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===AGNES MURRAY===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It cannot be regarded as being certain but it seem likely that Agnes Murray, here treated, is the daughter of Sir John Murray of Cockpool. The name of Sir John's wife is not known. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun0
2 CONC 1pauluoft/page/239/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 223]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Agnes Murray, here treated, married Ninian Maculloch of Cardoness. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/239/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 223] She is noticed as his wife on 15 December 1505. [http://cata
2 CONC logue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f222%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Agnes+Murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y NRS: GD1/222/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Agnes Murray, here treated married James Kennedy of Blairquhan, She survived her second husbands and was alive in 1560. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/239/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 223]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 December 1505: Instrument of resignation by Alexander Makculloch of Myrtoun, Knight, as procurator from Ninian Makculloch of Cardyness [Cardoness] of his resignation in the hands of the King as superior of the 20 merkland of
2 CONC  Newtoun of Cardyness in the lordship of Cardyness and sherrifdom of Kirkcudbricht, for reinfeftment in favour of the said Ninian and of Agnes Murray his spouse conjunctly. Done in a chamber of the King's palace beside the monaste
2 CONC ry of Holyrood near Edinburgh Witnesses: James, Abbot of Dunfermlyne, Treasurer to the King, David, Abbot of Cambuskynneth, Thomas Boswell, Patrick Sinclair, George Bard, James Stewart, and James Jaklyne, with others. Notary: Patr
2 CONC ick Painter. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f222%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Agnes+Murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Mackculloch of Cardyness 
2 CONC resignation, Kirkcudbrightshire, reference GD1/222/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This charter was printed in [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/615/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfou
2 CONC r Paul, Advocate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1883), charter number 2901 on p. 616]
