2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Agnew-391
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick "8th Sherriff of Galloway, 1st Baronet of Lochnaw" Agnew Born 1578 in Leswalt, Wigtownshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Sir Andrew Agnew and Agnes (Stewart) Agnew
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Andrew Agnew [half], Alexander Agnew [half], Quentin Agnew [half], Jean Agnew [half] and Grizell Agnew [half]	
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Margaret (Kennedy) Agnew — married 1599 in Lochnaw Castle, Wigtownshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Andrew Agnew M.P., Agnes (Agnew) MacDowall, James Agnew, Alexander of Whitehills Agnew, Rosina (Agnew) Cathcart and Patrick Agnew Jr.	
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 29 Oct 1661 in Galloway, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick Agnew of Lochnaw, 1st Bt. was born circa 1578. He was the son of Sir Andrew Agnew of Lochnaw and Agnes Stewart. He married Margaret Kennedy, daughter of Sir Thomas Kennedy, Master of Cassillis and Elizabeth Makgill, ci
2 CONC rca 1598. He died in 1661 at Lochnaw, Wigtownshire, Scotland. He was buried at Old Church, Leswalt, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Kennedy and Sir Patrick Agnew of Lochnaw, 1st Bt.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Sir Andrew Agnew of Lochnaw, 2nd Bt. d. 1671
2 CONT
2 CONT    *  Lt.-Col. James Agnew3 d. b 1661
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Patrick Agnew, 1st of Sheuchan
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Lt.-Col. Alexander Agnew, 1st of Whitehills
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Agnes Agnew
2 CONT
2 CONT    *  Marie Agnew She married Hew MacDowall of Knockglass
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Rosina Agnew
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Elizabeth Agnew She married John Baillie, son of Alexander Baillie and Eupheme Vaus. They lived at Dunragit, Wigtownshire, Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was invested as a Knight before 1629. He was created 1st Baronet Agnew, of Lochnaw, co. Wigtown [Nova Scotia] on 28 July 1629.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the offices:
2 CONT
2 CONT     8th Hereditary Sheriff of Galloway between 1616 and 1649.
2 CONT     Sheriff of both Kirkcudbright and Wigtown in the 1650s, while Scotland was part of the Protectorate with England..
2 CONT     Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Wigtownshire [Scotland] between 1628 and 1633.
2 CONT     Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Wigtownshire [Scotland] in 1643, 1644, 1645 and 1647 
2 CONT
2 CONT When he died in 1661, he was succeeded by his eldest son, Andrew, who would also be returned as MP for Wigtownshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT     Cracrofts Peerage 
2 CONT
