1 NAME William Henry /Deane/
2 GIVN William Henry
2 SURN Deane
2 _MARNM Deane
1 NAME William Henry Dean of Dorchester and Maryland
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1600
2 ADDR
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1699
2 PLAC Dorchester, Dorset, , England
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DEAN William Henry; ENG>MD,USA; 1600-1700
2 CONT
2 CONT =DEAN=
2 CONT
2 CONT Searching for descendants of William Henry Dean who was  the owner and master of his own ship "Betty." He came from England to St. Mary's Maryland sometime before 1639. He was married to Elizabeth DAMPIER, who probably never came 
2 CONC to America as he was engaged in coastal shipping and may have returned to England on many occasions. He never owned land  and eventually returned to England permanently. Tradition has it that he was the father of fourteen children
2 CONC  of  whom only four are known to have come to America. Two of  his sons who did not come were ship builders in the service  of the British government. The sons who came to America were: Thomas, James, John and William.
2 CONT
2 CONT  -- 
2 CONT
2 CONT *  John Duling
2 CONT *  2698 E. Yucatan Ct.
2 CONT *  Grand Junction, CO 81506
2 CONT * jduling@wic.net
2 CONT
2 CONT William was a ship master of the ship "Betty" that sailed to St. Mary's, Maryland.  He may not have stayed in America and might have returned to England on the ship.
2 CONT
2 CONT links:
2 CONT * http://www.chambersheritage.com/images/wdeendsc.pdf
