1 NAME James /Dunbar/
2 GIVN James
2 SURN Dunbar
2 _MARNM Dunbar
1 NAME Sir James Dunbar of Mochrum, 1st Baronet
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1647
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1718
1 TITL sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR JAMES DUNBAR OF MOCHRUM Baronet ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 March 1691: Assignation by James Dunbar of Mochrum, spouse of Isobel Nicolsone, one of 3 daughters of deceased Sir Thomas Nicolsone of Carnock, one of 3 aunts and heirs portioners of deceased Thomas, lord Naiper, to chamberl
2 CONC ain of Carnock and Plean, of third part of rents and profits of lands and baronies of Carnock and Plean, in parish of St. Ninians, sheriffdom of Stirling, [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refere
2 CONC nce=GD110%2f701&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=isobel+nicolsone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1750&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Hamilton-Dalrymple Family of North Berwick, reference GD110/701]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Dunbar, of Mochrum, co. Wigtown, s. and h. of Thomas Dunbar, of Mochrum, by Christian, da. of Major James Ross, of Balneil, was served heir to his father, 29 June 1675; had a Great Seal charter of the Barony of Mochrum, 1
2 CONC  June 1677, and was cr. a Baronet [S.], as above, 29 March 1694, with rem. to heirs male of the body. He m. firstly, 11 Feb. 1679, Isabel, da. and eventually coheir of Sir Thomas Nicolson, 2d Baronet [S. 1637], of Carnock, by Marg
2 CONC aret, da. of Alexander [Livingstone], 2d Earl of Linlithgow [S.]. With her he acquired the estate of Plean, co. Stirling. He m. secondly, Jane da. of ( — ) Kennedy, of Miunnchen, but by her had no male issue. He d. 1718. [https://
2 CONC archive.org/details/cu31924092524408/page/n383/mode/1up Complete baronetage; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 364]'''
