1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Andrew Cathcart, here treated, was a merchant. According to Sir James Fergusson, he was taken prisoner by a French privateer in August, 1688, but was exchanged the following year. Fergusson suggested that he may
2 CONC  have been identical with https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Cathcart-merchant-in-Glasgow/6000000081319265007who who was suspected by the Kirk Session of Dailly in 1693 of fornication committed at Killochan. However, the relations
2 CONC hip proposed has not been proved. [https://aanhsorg.files.wordpress.com/2018/08/the-cathcarts-of-carleton-and-killochan.pdf The Cathcarts of Carleton and Killochan: 141]'''
