2 CONT had a liferent of the manor-place of Greenlaw and lands adjoining, and by whom he had issue :
2 CONT * 6. Mr. John, of Greenlaw, who married Nicolas, daughter of Robert Stewart of Ravenstone or Castle Stewart, second son of James, Earl of Galloway. He died intestate in January 1729, and Nicolas Stewart, as his relict executrix-da
2 CONC tive, and Grissell Gordon, his only daughter, executrix-dative qua nearest of kin, both decerned to him after edict dated 9 May 1729, were confirmed as such executors on 1 December in the same year.
2 CONT * 7. James, of the Welsh Fusiliers, in 1711 serving in  Flanders,1 and said to have died at Boreland of Balmaghie in 1752.2 He married Grizel, eldest or only daughter of William Gordon of Grange, and had issue female....
