1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John Sinclair, Lord Murkle</strong> (died 5 June 1755) was a Scottish judge...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...A son of John Sinclair, 8th Earl of Caithness and Janet Carmichael of the Hyndford family, he was admitted to the Faculty of Advocates on 7 February 1713. On 18 January 1721 he was appointed one of the Solicitors General for Sc
2 CONC otland. He was elevated to the bench on the death of Sir William Calderwood of Polton on 3 November 1733, with the judicial title Lord Murkle. He died in Edinburgh on 5 June 1755."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'John Sinclair, Lord Murkle', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 25 January 2012, 17:54 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=John_Sinclair,_Lord_Murkle&oldid=473191009> [accessed
2 CONC  12 November 2012]
2 CONT
