1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir James Stewart, Baronet [S. 1687], of Burray</strong>, 1st s. and h. ; suc. to the Baronetcy on the death of his father, in 1704. He m. Anne, 1st da. of David Carmichael, of Balmeady. He d. s.p. a prisoner, under suspi
2 CONC cion of high treason, in the new gaol, Southwark, 24 Aug. 1746, when the issue male of the grantee expired, and the Baronetcy became dormant. His widow d. 19 Jan. 1779. Will recorded 25 Sep. 1779, in the Commissariot Court at Edin
2 CONC burgh."
2 CONT
