1 TITL Reverend
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===REVEREND GEORGE GRAHAM (aka REVEREND GEORGE GRAHAME)===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bishop of Dunkeld and Orkney===
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://inchbrakie.tripod.com/abookofthegraemes/id31.html A Book of the Graemes] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 February 1689: Copy Renunciation and Abjuring of Episcopacy by Mr George Graham, sometime pretended Bishop of Orkney. Dated at Brecknes in Stromness. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refere
2 CONC nce=GD106%2f14&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/14]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>George Grahame</strong>, born 1565, second son of George G. of Inchbraike and Majorie, daugh. of Andrew Rollo of Duncrub; educated at Univ. of St Andrews; M.A. (1587); ord. to Clunie in 1589; trans. to Auchtergraven befor
2 CONC e 1595; trans. to Scone in 1601; promoted to Bishop of Dunblane Feb. 1603 (retaining the living of Scone); app. to Bishopric of Orkney 26th Aug. 1615; installed Oct. 1616; dep. by Glasgow Assembly 11th Dec. 1638, but disclaimed Ep
2 CONC iscopacy 11th Feb. following, thereby saving his estate of Gorthie in Perthshire and others in Orkney; retired to Edinburgh, and died before 19th Dec. 1643, the place and exact date being unknown. He marr. before 29th Jan. 1594-5,
2 CONC  Marion (died 10th April 1632), daugh. of Sir Robert Crichton of Eliock, Sanquhar, and had issue - David of Gorthie, served heir 17th June 1647; Patrick of Rothiesholm and Graemeshall, min. of Holm; Mungo, apprenticed to David Mur
2 CONC ray, merchant, Edinburgh, 18th June 1634, died 1645; Henry, writer; Catherine (marr., cont. 24th June 1618, Patrick Smythe of Braco), died 13th Oct. 1637; Elspet; Agnes (marr. Adam Bellenden of Stennis); Jean, born 1609, died 1623
2 CONC ; John of Breckness; James, merchant, Edinburgh, apprenticed to David Graham, merchant, Edinburgh, 15th Aug. 1638; Marjory (marr. (1) George Drummond of Blair; (2) George Drummon of Balloch; (3) Major James Stewart of Banchory); M
2 CONC argaret, or Marion (marr. 1630, William Henryson of Holland, North Ronaldsay); George, alive in 1654; Elizabeth (marr. James Scrimgeour of Kirkton)."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc00scot#page/352/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. VII, page 353
