2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Graham/6000000052738945259?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1484473599779&through=6000000044569241022
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Graham/6000000052739009200?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1484473751048&through=6000000044569241022
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bastard Child===
2 CONT
2 CONT James Graham had a bastard son by a lady named Elspet. His name was https://www.geni.com/people/Ichabod-Graham/6000000052749800133?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1484473075046&through=6000000044569241022
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 April 1649: Disposition by Robert, earl of Morton, to '''James Grahame, merchant, son of deceased George Grahame of Morsyde and Margaret Heart, his spouse,''' of Knarstane, Lingrow, Tofts, Warbuster and Hatstane, in parish of S
2 CONC t Ola. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f1666&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+heart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, ref
2 CONC erence GD150/1666]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT 30 December 1653: Assignation by Sir Alexander Inglis of Inglistoun, to '''James Graham, merchant burgess of Edinburgh,''' of the sum of 3000 merks, contained in Bond by Deceased Mr George Wynrahame, to the granter, of date 7 Octo
2 CONC ber 1643. and Bond of Corroboration by John Wynraham, of date 10 March 1653 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD122%2f2%2f194&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1570
2 CONC &dt=1670&di=y National Records of Scotland, reference GD122/2/194]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 January 1654: Translation by '''James Graham, merchant burgess of Edinburgh''' to Mr James Windrahame, portioner of Newtounleyis, of a Bond by the late Mr George Wynrame, to Sir Alexander Inglis of Inglistoun, for 3000 merks; o
2 CONC f date 17 Octerber 1643, also Bond corroborating the same, by John Wynram of Libbertoun, son to the deceased Mr George, of date 7 March 1653. and Assignation of said Bond by Sir Alexander Inglis, to the said James Graham, of date 
2 CONC 30 December 1653 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD122%2f2%2f199&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1570&dt=1670&di=y National records of Scotland, reference GD122
2 CONC /2/199]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 March 1656: Kirkwall. Bond of caution by George Heart, son of David Heart of Rusland, in favour of '''James Grham, merchant in Edinburgh, now resident in the sheriffdom of Orkney, sometime spouse to Margaret Heart,''' of the sum
2 CONC  of £155 contained in a bond by '''the said Margaret''' in favour of Captain John Wood, merchant in London, dated 4 June, 1655, and assigned by him to John Forrester, writer in Edinburgh on 7 February, 1656, if the said George sho
2 CONC uld be found liable for that sum by the Lords of Council and Session. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD190%2f2%2f213&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+heart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y N
2 CONC ational Records of Scotland, Papers of the Smythe Family of Methven, Perthshire, reference GD190/2/213]
