1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN GRAHAM OF BRECKNESS===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Graham of Breckness is the youngest son of George Graham, Bishop of Orkney, and his wife Marion Crichton. He was probably born in 1618. He died in Auggust 1666. [James M. Irvine, The Breckness Estate: A History of its Lair
2 CONC ds, Tenants and Farms, and Skaill House (James M. Irvine, 2009), pp. 32-46]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Graham of Breckness married Barbara Stewart. According to James M. Irvine, Barbara Stewart was the daughter of James Stewart of Graemesay and the great-great-granddaughter of Robert Stewart, Earl of Orkney [James M. Irvine
2 CONC , The Breckness Estate: A History of its Lairds, Tenants and Farms, and Skaill House (Pinted in Orkney for James M. Irvine by The Orcadian Limited, 2009), pp. 39 and 303] but it would appear that Irvine is mistaken. Barbara Stewar
2 CONC t was in fact the eldest daughter of Harry Stewart of Gramsay. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=barbara+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National 
2 CONC Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
