2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26-28 February 1645: Antenuptial contract of marriage between John Grahame of Brekness on one part, and Harry Stewart of Gramsay, James Stewart, fiar thereof, his eldest son and apparent heir, and Barbara Stewart, said Harry's 
2 CONC eldest daughter, on other part, whereby said John binds himself to infeft said Barbara in liferent in 3½d. land of old called kirkland in town of Utterstromness, 25d., half farthing land, (king's land and udal land,) in said town,
2 CONC  with three quoys there called Smiddiequoy, Larquoy and Mowatisquoy, 2d., half merk udal land in town of Innerstromness, ½d. udal land in Stannigar there, quoy of land there called Quoyboir, ½d. land of old called kirkland in town
2 CONC  of Quhom, 3 merk, fourth part merk and a settin mailing more of udal land there, ½d. land in town of Cairstane commonly called Conquesquoy, with manor place and house of Breknes in town of Utterstromnes, all in parish of Stromnes
2 CONC , reserving liferent, in return for 3000 merks scots; with charter de me and sasine following. Recorded in the Particular Register of Sasines for Orkney on 3 March 1645. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/detai
2 CONC ls.aspx?reference=GD217%2f11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=barbara+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 August 1645: Instrument of sasine propriis manibus by John Grahame of Breknes in favour of Barbara Stewart, his future spouse, sister of James Stewart, fiar of Gramsay, in 20 meils malt yearly from 24 merkland of Burwick and 
2 CONC 9 merkland of Soulsetter. A sasine in her favour was recorded in the Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Orkney on 20 August 1645. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD21
2 CONC 7%2f164&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=barbara+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/164]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 May 1646: Charter de me by John Grahame of Breknes, with consent of Barbara Stewart, his spouse, to Katherine, Margaret and Marjorie Sinclair, daughters of deceased Magnus Sinclair in Burwick, of 24 merkland of Burwick; with
2 CONC  sasine following. recorded in the Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Orkney on 4 June 1646. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f165&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ba
2 CONC rbara+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/165]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 October 1657: Contract of excambion between John Grahame of Breknes, with consent of Barbara Stewart, his spouse, on one part, and John Broun, eldest son and heir of Magnus Broun in Done in Utterstromnes, with consent of sai
2 CONC d Magnus and Isobel Beatoun, his spouse, mother of said John Broun, whereby said John Grahame dispones to said Magnus Broun in liferent and John Broun in fee, ½d. land in Cairstane called Conquesquoy, in excambion for 3 2/3 merk l
2 CONC and in 6 merk penny land called Leager in Uttertoun and 1 merkland in Quoy Fealtquoy in 6d. land of Fealtquoy there, ½d. land extending to a 2 merkland of udal land, one merkland called Cowplanes land, the other George Brounes mer
2 CONC k in Innerstromnes, ½ merkland in Innerstromnes wadset to said Magnus by Alexander Broun, said John Broun's ½d. land in Utterstromnes wadset by Patrick Beatoun to said Magnus, all within parish of Stromnes; with extract dispositio
2 CONC n, charter a me and sasine. Sasine recorded in the Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Orkney on 1 January 1658. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f15&st=1&tc=y&t
2 CONC l=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=barbara+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 April 1664: Charter a me by John Grahame of Breknes to Harry Grahame, his eldest son, and his heirs male, of 3½d. kirkland in town of Utterstromnes, 25d., half farthing king's land there, with 3 quoys of land called Smiddiqu
2 CONC oy, Larquoy and Mowatisquoy, 2d., ½ merk udal land in Innerstromnes, ½d. udal land in Stanneger there, quoy there called Quoyboir, ½d. kirkland in town of Quhome, 3¼ merk 1 settin mailing udal land there, manor place and house of 
2 CONC Breknes in Uttertoun, 3 2/3 merkland in 6d. land called Leager there, 1 merkland in Quoyfealtquoy in 6d. land of Fealtquoy there, ½d. land extending to a 2 merkland of udal land called Conplanes land and George Brounes merk in Inn
2 CONC erstromnes, all in parish of Stromnes, 24d. land of Suthirquoy, comprehending 8d. land of Gorn, 8d. land of Skaill and 8d. land of old called the Stonkland of Suthirquoy, with part of links called Langobak besouth the burn of Skai
2 CONC ll, 3d. land called Unigar, 1¾d. land called Hammer in Aithstoun (5 farthing king's land, 2 farthing udal), links of Sandwick, hill called Keirfeald, all in parish of Sandwick, reserving liferent of granter and Barbara Stewart, hi
2 CONC s spouse [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f255&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=barbara+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland,  Papers of the Scarth Family of 
2 CONC Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/255]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 April 1677: Extract discharge by Mr. Robert Honyman, only son of deceased Andrew, bishop of Orknay, with consent of Margaret Grahame, his spouse, to Harry Grahame of Brecknes, of all bairn's part due to said Margaret by dece
2 CONC ase of John Grahame of Brecknes, her father, or of Barbara Stewart, her mother. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f488&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=barbara+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&
2 CONC dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/488]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
