2 CONT Bio notes: Biography of Thomas Grove
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Grove was born in Halesowen c1783 and baptised there on 3 September 1783, the son of Samuel and Esther Grove [1][2]; at the time, Halesowen was an exclave of the County of Shropshire. For details of his connection with his 
2 CONC son Charles, see Charles Grove. His wife was named Sarah Ann, after whom her grand-daughter by Charles and Eliza Grove was named.  There are two marriages in the region recorded in the IGI of Thomas Grove to a Sarah in the few yea
2 CONC rs before 1816:
2 CONT -	Thomas Grove married Sarah Taylor in St. Philip, Birmingham, Warwickshire on 11 January 1803 [2]. This would have made him 19 or 20 at the time. NB The maiden name of Thomas Grove's mother was Taylor or Tayler.
2 CONT -	Thomas Grove married Sarah Holloway in St. Martin, Birmingham on 28 Feb 1814 [3]. This would have made Thomas about 30 at the time. NB. Thomas's brother, Josiah probably married Mary Holloway in 1799 - perhaps they were sisters.
2 CONT -	It is also possible that Thomas Grove married Sarah Taylor and that she died and he remarried, this time to Sarah Holloway.
2 CONT The marriage to Sarah Holloway in 1814 seems very likely as 3 baptisms are recorded for their children in Halesowen between 1815 and 1819 [4]. At this time, he is recorded as being a mason or bricklayer as were his brothers Edward
2 CONC  and Josiah [5]. He and his brother Edward are the two bricklayers recorded as living in High Street, Halesowen in the 1828, 1835 and 1844 Pigot Directories [6][7]. He presumably died some time after 1844 and is most likely buried
2 CONC  in Halesowen.
2 CONT
2 CONT A description of Halesowen in 1844 is described in the 1844 Pigot Directory [7].
2 CONT [1] IGI  www.familysearch.org accessed on 30/03/2006
