2 CONT COACHES & OMNIBUSES.
2 CONT To BIRMINGHAM, the Mail (from Stourbridge) calls at the New Inn, every evening at six, and a Coach, every morning at a quarter before ten - Jordan's Omnibus (from Kidderminster) calls at the Lyttelton's Arms, every morning (Sunday
2 CONC  excepted) at half-past eight - and another calls at Mr Trewollas', at the same hour.
2 CONT To KIDDERMINSTER, Jordan's Omnibus (from Birmingham) calls at the Lyttelton's Arms, every afternoon (Sunday excepted) at half-past five - and another calls at Mr Trewollas', at the same hour.
2 CONT To STOURBRIDGE, the Mail (from Birmingham) calls at the New Inn, every morning at half-past ten - and a Coach every evening at half-past seven.
2 CONT CONVEYANCE BY RAILWAY.
2 CONT The nearest Station to Hales Owen is Birmingham, seven miles distant, where the London and Birmingham, the Grand Junction, the Birmingham and Derby Junction, and the Birmingham and Gloucester Railways have their respective Station
2 CONC s.
2 CONT There are regular conveyances to Birmingham, as noticed in the preceding list of Coaches and Omnibuses.
2 CONT CARRIERS.
2 CONT To BIRMINGHAM, Thos. Knight, from his house, Birmingham street, every Monday, Thursday and Saturday - and Jos. Tildesley, from his house, Church street, every Tuesday, Thursday & Sat.
2 CONT To BROMSGROVE, Thos. Knight, from his house, Birmingham st, every Tuesday.
2 CONT To STOURBRIDGE, Joseph Tildesley, from his house, Church st, every Monday, Wednesday and Friday.
2 CONT CONVEYANCE BY WATER.
2 CONT To BIRMINGHAM, DUDLEY, TIPTON, STOURBRIDGE. &c.  Boats, pass through daily, and forward goods to all parts - Thomas Brewin, agent, Heywood wharf.
2 CONT
