1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marjorie (Margaret), daughter of Robert, duke of Albany, and 1st wife of Duncan Campbell, had children:
2 CONT # Celestine (who died young)
2 CONT # Archibald
2 CONT # Colin ''(See more on the About of husband Duncan.)''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT * From http://www.thepeerage.com/p10802.htm
2 CONT * F, #108012, d. before August 1432
2 CONT * Last Edited=7 Oct 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Marjorie Stewart was born before 1380. She was the daughter of Robert Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany and Margaret Graham, Countess of Menteith. '''(Sic: more likely a daughter of the 2nd wife, Muriel de Keith.  See below''')
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Sir Duncan Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell, son of Sir Colin Campbell of Lochow and Mariot Campbell. She died before August 1432.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Marjorie Stewart was also known as Marceline Stewart. Her married name became Campbell.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://groups.google.com/forum/m/#!topic/soc.genealogy.medieval/5RRnyv3b3nQ  	Fw: Robert Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany, 1340-1420, and dau. Lady Marjorie Stewart, 1380-1432] Leo van de Pass, 1/21/2008
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Burke's Peerage 1938, page 144, tells that Marjory's 
2 CONT parents-in-law married "sometime before 1 April 1387"
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Colin Campbell of Lochow and Margaret (Mariot ?) Campbell (Marjory's  in-laws) married before 1 April 1387 and had four sons and a daughter, the  second son Colin Campbell, 1st of Ardkinglass, according to G. Harvey  Johnston 
2 CONC in his "The Heraldry of the Campbells", page 105, married by Papal  licence in 1396<nowiki>-----------</nowiki>how young was Colin?
2 CONT
2 CONT To me it seems that Marjory's husband most likely was born 1387-1389, which  makes him at least seven or more years younger than his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT To me it seems that who is the mother of Marjoy depends on when she was  born, Aaron Parmenter quotes several times that she was born before 1380.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Graham, Countess of Menteith, the possible mother of Marjory,  according to CP VIII page 668 died between20 July 1372 and 4 May 1380. Her  parents married before 1334, and apparently she was born about 1339, .making  her 
2 CONC young enough to give birth "before 1380" to Marjory. On 20 July 1372 (I  presume) Margaret attended the contracting of a marriage, but what if she  died shortly after that? Making Marjory born about 1372? Makes Marjory  "possibly"
2 CONC  15 years older than her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Graham appears to have married her fourth husband Robert Stewart,  1st Duke of Albany, in 1361 and their (no doubt) first child Murdoch was  born about 1362. There were only three or four more children (daughters)  born. 
2 CONC Would they have been born between 1362 and "before 1380"?
2 CONT
2 CONT Muriella Keith and Robert Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany, received dispensation  to marry on 4 May 1380. and their son John, Earl of Buchan, CP Volume II  page 377 was born about 1380. This means that Marjory, is she has the same  mo
2 CONC ther, was born after 1380 which makes it possible to be much closer in age  to her husband Duncan Campbell, most likely born 1387-1389, especially as  Muriella Keith and Robert Stewart appear to have had five children (3 sons)  an
2 CONC d we do not know where Marjory would fit in.
2 CONT
2 CONT In all I am not as yet convinced that I have the wrong mother for Marjory.  If anyone can give better details, I will gladly change it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # [S01352] ~Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage and Knightage, London, 1938. page 145. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Birth date seen as 04/07/1397
2 CONT
