2 CONT
2 CONT ===SIR COLIN CAMPBELL OF GLENORCHY===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/353/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 231]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Sir Duncan Campell and his 1st wife, Margaret (Marjorie) Stewart (daughter of Robert Stewart, Duke of Albany, governor of Scotland)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 October 1439: Precis made by Dr Annie Dunlop, Florence, of a dispensation for marriage of Colin Campbell, kt, and Marion Stewart, who have been living together in fornication, ignorant of fact that they are related in second
2 CONC  and third, and third and fourth degrees of consanguinity and in the third and third degrees of affinity. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f25%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mari
2 CONC on+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), Marriage Contracts and Related Papers, reference GD112/25/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 October 1440: Charter by Isabella, duchess of Albany, countess of Levenax, Inchedavanow, to Colin Campbell, kt, laird of Glenurchay, by reason of his marriage to Marion Stewart, daughter of deceased Walter Stewart of Albany, 
2 CONC granter's son, of lands of Feorlyng More and Feorlyng Natara of Kangerlouch, and lands of Mame Beg and Mame More in granter's earldom of Levenax, sheriffdom of Dumbertane, to be held by said Colin and Marion and their legitimate h
2 CONC eirs, whom failing, to Andrew Stewart of Albany, kt, granter's grandson, son of said deceased Walter, with proviso that all thieves convicted there are to be hanged on the duchess's gallows at Faslane. Witnesses: Arthur Stewart, g
2 CONC ranter's grandson, Gilbert of Galbrathe, John Campbell and Alexander McYwyr, her relatives, sir John of Rosnethe, vicar of Luss, sir Gilbert McArthour, chaplain, Donald the clerk and sir Walter Bet, rector of Craginche. Seal entir
2 CONC e on tag. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f25%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Fa
2 CONC mily, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), Marriage Contracts and Related Papers, reference GD112/25/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 March 1448-49: Charter, de me, by John Stewart, lord of Lorne, in favour of John Campbell, kt., lord of Glenurquhay, in terms of contract of marriage between the latter and granter's daughter, JANET STEWART, in following lan
2 CONC ds; 5 merkland of Letterbean, ½ merkland between Lakans and Altmothle, with island of Incheconnon and all other islands annexed therto, the pennyland of Clarga and Blara, the pennyland of Corelarumayr, pennylands of Clucherach, Po
2 CONC ll Andnowych, Aeynyth, Lochacyleod, with the lake of Lochyleod, Drumnaschealga, Blaraneadyn, pennyland of Strying with its lake and islands, and the pennyland of Fynglann, in lordship of Lorne, sheriffdom of Perth. Witnesses: Alan
2 CONC  Stewart, granter's brother; Patrick Gregor of Stromnelachan; John [Johnson?] Campbell Ywar; Duncan (lord) Beane; David, Chanter of Lysmoyr; sir Gavin, curate of [Clachan] Dysert. At the castle of Glenurquhay. Granter's seal on ta
2 CONC g; good condition. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f75%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=janet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cam
2 CONC pbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/75/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 March 1448-49: Copy charter by John Stewart, lord of Lorne, to Colin Campbell, kt., laird of Glenurquhay, his relative, by reason of marriage of said Colin and JONET STEWART, granter's daughter, of 5 merkland of Letterbean, 
2 CONC with half merkland between LeakansumMar and river called Altmothle with island of Inchconnan and all other islands annexed, 1 pennyland of Elarge and Blara, pennyland of Corelarne, pennyland of Cluchich, pennyland of Poll Andowich
2 CONC , pennyland of Aeynyh Lochantyleod in loch of Lochtynleod, pennyland of Drunnaschealge and Blaranaedyn, pennyland of Stryng with its loch and islands, and pennyland of Fynglean, in lordship of Lorn, sheriffdom of Perth, at the cas
2 CONC tle of Glenurquhay. Witnesses: Alan Stewart, granter's brother, Peter McGregor of Sronmelachan, John Johnston, [wanting] Campbell, Ewar Duncanson, Duncan Vean, David, chanter of Lismore, and sir Gavin, curate of Dysart. [http://ca
2 CONC talogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f1%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadal
2 CONC bane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/1/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 November 1454: Letters by George (Lauder), bishop of Argyll, reciting apostolic letters of Pope Nicholas, 5 ides April 1454, a.r. 8, for marriage of Colin Campbell, kt., of Glenurquha, and JONET STEWART, daughter of John Ste
2 CONC wart, lord of Lorne, who are within the forbidden degrees of consanguinity. Witnesses: John Stewart, lord of Lorne, Colin Campbell, lord of Lochaw, sir James Lawdre, vicar of Kippen, Thomas Spens, rector of Lochfine, and sir Ninia
2 CONC n Morrison (Moritii). Seal almost entire, on tag. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f1%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=jonet+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records 
2 CONC of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/1/8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 December 1456: Instrument narrating that John Stewart, lord of Lorne, gave sasine, propriis manibus, to Colin Campbell, knight, of Gleanourchaye, and Jonet Stewart, his spouse, daughter of said John, in lands of Lettirvean a
2 CONC nd Vrailorne, 17 December 1456. Notary: David Ouchtour, priest, Dunblane diocese. Witnesses: George, bishop of Argyll, Colin Campbell, lord of Lochou, Donald McLachlan of that ilk, Maurice [McFadzen], treasurer of Argyll, Patrick 
2 CONC Laudor, vicar of Kippen and chaplain. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f37%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=colin+campbell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Sco
2 CONC tland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/37/1]'''
2 CONT
