2 CONT '''1573-1590: Charter of confirmation by King James VI of a charter by Torquil McCloyde of Lewis to Margaret Nyne Angus Mc Alexander his spouse in liferent, of one davach of the lands of Daweachenehard, two davachs of the lands of
2 CONC  Strathannort, a half davach of the lands of Chorre, a half davach of the lands of Achechall, in the lordship of Ross and shire of Inverness; also six davachs of lands in the lordship of Lewis, namely the 20 penny lands of Enge, t
2 CONC he 20 penny lands of Vollis, the 30 penny lands of Lochis, the 20 penny lands of Broagir, the 20 penny lands of Gallis, the 10 penny lands of Coldstaff on the north side of Lewis, in the lordship of Lewis and shire foresaid, all l
2 CONC ying in Cogache: to be held from the granter and his heirs, of the Crown, for rendering the services used and wont; under reservation of the said Torquil McCloyds liferent of the said lands. This charter contains a precept of sasi
2 CONC ne, and is dated at the Chanonry of Ross 12 October 1573, and the confirmation is dated at Holyroodhouse 28 July 1590. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD305%2f1%2f1%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&
