2 CONT '''21 January 1439-40: Precept of clare constat by Alexander de Ile, earl of Ross, lord of the Isles, in favour of John Ross, as heir of deceased Hugh Ross, his father, in lands of Balnagowan, Achavill, Gorry, Culcarne, Badcoll,  
2 CONC Moltvy, Petmodvoy, Estirallane, annualrent from Tarbart, and lands of the 2 Rareychis, Culnyss, Westray, Strathcaron, and Strathocale, Osbudule, Innercasly, Mullochy, in granter's earldom and sheriffdom of Inverness. Bailies: Geor
2 CONC ge Munro and Alexander McCullach. Tag, seal gone. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD297%2f180&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Balnagowan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Sc
2 CONC otland, J. & F. Anderson Collection, reference GD297/180]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 January 1456-57: Instrument narrating that John Ross, laird of Balnagowan, asked Alexander Sutherland, laird of Dunbeth, for a bond for £20 Scots from said Alexander, to which he agreed, and discharged the said John, though 
2 CONC he could not find the bond, whereupon the said John paid said Alexander for the wadset of the lands of Culyndoray and Moyblare, and asked for the charter of wadset to be returned to him; Alexander refused to do this until he was g
2 CONC iven another merk as maill, which John refused, so they agreed to deposit the charter with William Monilaw till the plea was settled. Notary: William Monilaw, priest, diocese of Ross. Witnesses: Sir Magnus Buge, rector of Olryk, S
2 CONC ir Thomas Colysone and Sir William Monilaw, chaplains of Tayne, Donald McTirissone and Christian of Fores, [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD199%2f16&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Balnago
2 CONC wan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ross Family of Pitcalnie, reference GD199/16]'''
