1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN STEWART Earl of Lennox ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stewart, Earl of Lennox, here treated, is the eldest son of Sir Alan Stewart of Darnley and his wife Catherine Seton. A date and place of birth has not been identified for him.  [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefou
2 CONC n05paul/page/348/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 348]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stewart, Earl of Lennox, here treated, died after 31 August 1495 and before 11 September 1495. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/349/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 349]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 May 1438: Indenture between Alexander Mongomry, knight, Lord of Ardrossane, and Alan Stewart, Lord of Dernlie, for the marriage of John Stewart, son and heir of the said Alan, and Margaret Mongomry, daughter of the said Alex
2 CONC ander; for which marriage the latter became bound to pay, in name of tocher, with the said Margaret, the sum of 600 merks Scots, and the said Alan became bound to infeft the said John and Margaret, in conjunct fee, in the 40 merk 
2 CONC lands of Dregarn and Dromley, etc. Dated at Houstoun. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f2%2f1%2f47&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alan+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National
2 CONC  Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/2/1/47]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 January 1511-12: Charter of confirmation by King James IV, as Stewart of Scotland, in favour of Matthew, Earl of Lennox confirming a charter by deceased Robert Stewart of Scotland, Earl of Strathearn, to the also deceased Si
2 CONC r John Stewart of Darnley of the lands of Crukisfu, Inchinnan and Parthickscot lying in the barony of Renfrew, and also disponing to Matthew, Earl of Lennox, all claim he had as King and Stewart of Scotland to the duties and profi
2 CONC ts of the said lands through recognition, nonentry or escheat, with the castle of Crukisfu, the Mains of Darnley and its mill, the lands of Dormontside, Nethertoun and old Cruxton [Crookston] extending to a £20 land of old extent 
2 CONC lying about the castle and manor place of Inchinnan with the park and yards thereof, the Mains of Inchinnan, lands of Whitehill, town of Inchinnan, Raschielie, Wrightland, Florish, Craigton and Garnerland with the commonties of th
2 CONC e same, extending likewise to a £20 land of old extent lying in the barony of Renfrew, to be held ward of the King. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f6%2f1%2f1&st=1&tc=y&
2 CONC tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=stewart+of+darnley&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/F/6/1/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/344 The Scots Peerage V: pp. 344-62 for Stewart, Duke of Lennox]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER.htm#MaldouenLennoxdied1251 Medieval Lands: Scotland, Earls]'''
2 CONT # '''[http://www.thepeerage.com/p10921.htm#i109207 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10921.htm#i109207 Biographical Summary from Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stuart, 1st Earl of Lennox was born before 1430. He was the son of Sir Alan Stuart of Darnley and Catherine Seton. He married Margaret Montgomerie, daughter of Alexander Montgomerie, 1st Lord Montgomerie and Margaret Boyd,
2 CONC  on 15 May 1438, by indenture, with both parties being underage. He died between 8 July 1495 and 11 September 1495. John Stuart, 1st Earl of Lennox gained the title of Lord Darnley. He gained the title of 1st Earl of Lennox.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER.htm#JohnStewartLennoxdied1495B Biographical Summary by Medieval Lands] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''JOHN Stewart, son of ALAN Stewart of Darnley & his wife Catherine Seton ([8 Jul/11 Sep] 1495).  Lord Darnley 1460.  Lord Darnley claimed the Earldom of Lennox in 1473, as the heir of Elizabeth daughter of Duncan Earl of Lennox,
2 CONC  whom he claimed (wrongly it appears) was the Earl's second daughter.  The claim was disputed by John Haldane of Gleneagles, whose wife was descended from Elizabeth's older sister Margaret, in whose favour the king and the Lords o
2 CONC f the Council found 12 Jan 1476.  However, a settlement was presumably reached as Lord Darnley eventually took his seat in the parliament of 1488 as Earl of Lennox. m (1438) MARGARET Montgomerie, daughter of ALEXANDER Lord Montgom
2 CONC erie & his wife Margaret Boyd of Kilmarnock. John & his wife had nine children.'''
2 CONT
