1 OCCU Commanded the right wing of the Scots army at the Battle of Flodden Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER.htm#MaldouenLennoxdied1251
2 CONT
2 CONT ===MATTHEW STEWART, EARL OF LENNOX===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of birth has not been identified for Matthew Stewart. Darryl Lundy's Peerage suggests that he was born between 1460 and 1470. [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10212.htm#i102119 Darryl Lundy's Peerage: Matthew Stuart
2 CONC , 2nd Earl of Lennox] This proposition fits well with the age suggested by the letter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirmed that he had given custody of Dumbarton Castle to Matthew and his father, where it would appear that 
2 CONC Matthew may have already reached the age of majority before 22 October 1488, that is before 22 October 1467. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/381/mode/1up RMSRS: 1794]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Matthew Stewart, Earl of Lennox, was killed at the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513. Thereafter, on 23 September 1513, his son John received a precept of sasine from the Scottish Chancery  as heir to his deceased father. [
2 CONC http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f6%2f2%2f10&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+stewart+earl+of+lennox&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD220/1/F/6/2/10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 October 1488: Letter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms that he has given custody of Dumbarton Castle to John Stewart, Earl of Lennox, and Matthew Stewart, his son and apparent heir. [https://archive.org/stream/regis
2 CONC trummagnisi02scot#page/381/mode/1up Registrum Magnii Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, charter number 1794 on p. 381]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 February 1489-90: Remission by King James III with consent of the estates of Parliament to Matthew Stuart, son and apparent heir to John Earl of Lennox, and his friends and followers for holding the castle of Dunbrettan [Dum
2 CONC barton] against the King. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%2f4%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+earl+of+lennox&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1471&dt=1513&di=y National Records of Sco
2 CONC tland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/F/5/4/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 May 1490: Indenture between John, Earl of Lennox and Matthew Stuart, his son and apparent heir, and Elizabeth Menteith, spouse of deceased John Napier of Merchiston as one of the heirs of the earldom of Levenax [Lennox] and 
2 CONC Archibald Napier, his son, whereby Elizabeth and her son discharge the Earl of Lennox of all intromissions with the earldom of Lennox and all right they might claim thereto, and therefore the Earl obliges himself to dispone to the
2 CONC m a quarter of the earldom lying together, and if a £5 land of that is granted to John Haldane of Gleneagles the Earl obliges him to grant them another £5 land just as good. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/d
2 CONC etails.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%2f4%2f10&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+earl+of+lennox&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1471&dt=1513&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), refer
2 CONC ence GD220/1/F/5/4/10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 May 1490: Instrument of sasine following on precept from chancery, 16[?26] May (1490), following on GD198/53, reciting letters of procuratory, 24 Feb. 1489/90, by Matthew Stewart, sheriff of Dunbertane [Dumbarton], son and a
2 CONC pparent heir of John, lord Dernly [Darnley], in favour of Umfra Culquhoun [Colquhoun], Robert Noble, younger, and John Akynross, as his deputes. Sheriff deputes Umfra Culquhoun [Colquhoun]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrso
2 CONC nlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f56&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+Matthew+Stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1460&dt=1490&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Haldane Family of Gleneagles, Perthshire, reference GD198/5
2 CONC 6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 June 1490: Charter of resignation by King James IV in favour of Matthew Stuart, son and apparent heir to John, Earl of Lennox, Lord Darnley, of the whole earldom of Lennox and lordship of Darnley called Crucksfu, the lands of
2 CONC  Galston with its pertinents, with the patronage of the churches and chapels belonging to the earldom, lying in the sheriffdoms of Dunbarton, Stirling, Ayr and Renfrew, to be held ward of the King, proceeding on resignation by Joh
2 CONC n, Earl of Lennox, reserving the liferent to the Earl and the liferent of a third part of the lands to Margaret Montgomery, his spouse, for her lifetime; dated at Linlithgow. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/
2 CONC details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%2f5%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+earl+of+lennox&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1471&dt=1513&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), refer
2 CONC ence GD220/1/F/5/5/1] This charter was printed in [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/411/mode/1up The Reguster of the Great Seal of Scotland]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 June 1490: Instrument by Matthew Stuart, son and apparent heir to John, Earl of Lennox, disputing the sasine given by the sheriff of Stirling to Robert Graham of Fintry at the principal messuage of Craigton called Fintry in 
2 CONC the sheriffdom of Stirling without reference to the earl as superior of the said lands. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%2f5%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+earl+of+le
2 CONC nnox&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1471&dt=1513&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/F/5/5/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 May 1493: Notarial copy of transumpt by John Anthony [di San Georgio,] bishop of Allessandria in Italy, at instance of master Alexander Menteth, clerk of Glasgow diocese, of papal letters or confessional on supplication of J
2 CONC ohn Stewart, earl of Lennox, Matthew Stewart, heir of Lennox, and their wives, that their confessor, might be able to absolve them from excommunication etc., and that they might have a portable altar. Witnesses: masters Bernardino
2 CONC  de Bertis, granter's secretary and chamberlain, and George Brown, canon of Dunkeld. Transumpt made by Gilbert Strathauchin, clerk of St Andrews diocese, and copied by Cuthbert Muligane, notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk
2 CONC /nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f6%2f1953&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+stewart+earl+of+lennox&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Mu
2 CONC niments), reference GD220/6/1953]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 August 1505: Instrument of sasine in favour of Matthew, Earl of Lennox, heir to Allan Stuart, Lord Darnley, his grandfather, in the lands of Ballincrofts [Ballencrieff?] with its mill, Balbardie, Inche Eston [Easter Inch] an
2 CONC d Tobane [Torbane], lying in the barony of Bathgate and sheriffdom of Renfrew, following on precept from Chancery dated 11 Jul 1505. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%
2 CONC 2f7%2f11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=allan+stuart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/F/5/7/11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 September 1513: Precept of sasine from Chancery directed to the sheriffs depute of Dunbartonshire for serving John Stewart, Earl of Lennox, heir to the deceased Matthew, Earl of Lennox, his father, who was killed in Northumb
2 CONC erland [at Flodden]; dated at Stirling. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f6%2f2%2f10&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+stewart+earl+of+lennox&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nati
2 CONC onal Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/F/6/2/10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10212.htm#i102119 Darryl Lundy's Peerage: Matthew Stuart, 2nd Earl of Lennox]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===NOTES===
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd Earl of Lennox. He married Elizabeth Hamilton Countess.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox was killed on 9 September 1513 while leading Scottish forces at the Battle of Flodden. [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Flodden Battle of Flodden]
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox (Bef. 5 May 1488-9 September 1513, Flodden) was a prominent Scottish nobleman. Stewart was the son of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Lennox, and Margaret Montgomerie, daughter of Alexander Montgomeri
2 CONC e, 1st Lord Montgomerie.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married firstly, on 13 June 1490, Margaret Lyle, daughter of Robert Lyle, Lord Lyle. On 9 April 1494, he married Elizabeth Hamilton, daughter of James Hamilton, 1st Lord Hamilton, and Mary Stewart, daughter of King James II of 
2 CONC Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stewart and Elizabeth Hamilton had six children: Mungo Stewart, Agnes Stewart, John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Lennox, Margaret Stewart, Elizabeth Stewart, and Catherine Stewart.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT G. E. Cokayne et al., eds. The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct, or Dormant. Reprint ed. (Gloucester, UK: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000).
2 CONT
