1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sir John Stewart, Seigneur d'Oison,''' b. bef. 1446, d. c. 1512.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John, Earl of Lennox, died after 31 August and before 11 September 1495.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had married Margaret (contract dated at Houstoun, 15 May 1438), eldest daughter of Alexander Montgomerie, Lord of Ardrossan, neither being then of lawful age, 
2 CONT
2 CONT and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. John, of Henriestoun, Seigneur d’Oison on the death of his brother William. …
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stuart, second Seigneur d'Oizon (1st Baron of Henriestoun), who was born circa 1472 and died in 1512. He, too, entered the French service, saving the life of his first cousin once removed General Bernard Stuart, Seigneur d'Au
2 CONC bigny, at the battle of Terina in Italy. John was the "Premier Homme d'Armes" of France 1505-8. He was twice married, first, to Maria Semple; and secondly to Anne de Monypenny, daughter and heiress of Alexander de Monypenny, Seign
2 CONC eur de Concressault. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com/books?id=-P4UAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA553&lpg=PA553&dq=James+Crawford+6th+Lord+of+Auchinames&source=bl&ots=_j_YhK2sNC&sig=VIVgqs6qlE-ZTsMVWQbQnYQvP64&hl=en&sa=X&ei=eBPpU94NlOKgBO21gqgG&ved=0CEQQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q=J
2 CONC ames%20Crawford%206th%20Lord%20of%20Auchinames&f=false age 553] of A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great Britain and ...By John Burke. "Patrick Crawfurd, of Auchinames, who m. a daughter of John Frazer, thi
2 CONC rd laird of Knock (by Margaret, his wife, only child and heiress of Sir John Stuart, of Glenderston, fourth son of John, first Earl of Lennox, grandson of the celebrated Sir John Stuart, Count Devereux, field-marshal of France), a
2 CONC nd had a son and successor ...."
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=338fAAAAYAAJ&lpg=RA1-PA243&ots=hy-ha4zoEe&dq=john%20stewart%20of%20henriestoun&pg=RA1-PA243#v=onepage&q=john%20stewart%20of%20henriestoun&f=false page 243] of the The London Quarterly Review.  
2 CONC "It is unknown whether William Stuart, Seigneur d'Oyzon in France, the third son of John, the first Earl of Lennox, left any issue.  John Stuart of Henriestoun, the next brother of the Seigneur d'Oyzon, left an only daughter, Marg
2 CONC aret, who married John Fraser of Kuvich, in Ayrshire, from whom there may be descendants."
2 CONT
