2 CONT '''6 April 1498: Precept of sasine from Chancery in favour of John Colquhoun of Luss and Elizabeth Stuart, his spouse, and longest liver of the two, in the £10 land of Garthsquyb and its mill lying in the earldom of Lennox and she
2 CONC riffdom of Dunbarton, following on charter under the great seal and John Colquhoun's own resignation. Dated 6 Apr in the 10th year of the King's reign. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=
