2 CONT ===BIOGRAPHICAL SUMMARY===
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart, second Earl of Athole, killed at Flodden in 1513.  He married Mary, daughter of Archibald Campbell, second Earl of Argyll) killed at Flodden), son of Colin Campbell, first Earl of Argyll (died 1493), son of Archibald
2 CONC  Campbell (died before his father), son of Sir Duncan Campbell (died 1453), by his wife, Marjory Stewart, daughter of Robert, Duke of Albany, Regent of Scotland (died 1420), son of Robert II (died 1390), son of Walter, Lord High S
2 CONC teward of Scotland, by his wife Marjory, daughter of Robert Bruce (died 1329).  By his marriage with Mary Campbell, John, Earl of Athole, had a daughter, Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Stewart,_2nd_Earl_of_Atholl BIOGRAPHICAL SUMMARY BY WIKIPEDIA]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born after 1475 to John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl and Eleanor Sinclair. He married Lady Janet Campbell, daughter of Archibald Campbell, 2nd Earl of Argyll, by Elizabeth Stewart. He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of At
2 CONC holl on 15 September 1512 at the death of his father. He fought in the Battle of Flodden Field on 9 September 1513. He was living in 1520, and died before 1522. His widow, Janet, died about Candlemas 1545-6.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Atholl (1507-1542).
2 CONT     Lady Janet Stewart married (1st) Alexander Gordon, Master of Sutherland; (2nd) Sir Hugh Kennedy, of Girvanmains; (3rd) Henry Stewart, Lord Methven; and (4th) Patrick, Lord Ruthven.[1]
2 CONT     Lady Helen Stewart, married (1st) John Lindsay, 5th Lord Lindsay of the Byres; (2nd) Thomas Moncur.
2 CONT     Lady Elizabeth Stewart, stated to have married Kenneth Mackenzie, 10th of Kintail.
2 CONT     Lady Jean Stewart (died 19 April 1522), married James Arbuthnot, 13th of Arbuthnott.
2 CONT     Lady Isabel Stewart, stated to have married James Hering, of Lethendy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/468/mode/1up
2 CONT p443-444 STEWART, EARL OF ATHOLL
2 CONT
2 CONT II. JOHN, second Earl of Atholl, succeeded his father. He is usually stated to have fallen at Flodden, but in reality he died after 1520, and before 1522. On 3 May 1522 his son was infeft as heir by a precept from chancery dated 4
2 CONC  January 1521-22. l He married Janet, daughter of Archibald Campbell, second Earl of Argyll, who survived him,2 and died about Candlemas 1545-46.3 Had issue :—
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. JOHN, third Earl.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Janet, married, first, about 1520, to Alexander Gordon, Master of Sutherland, eldest son of Adam Earl of Sutherland;4 secondly, before 1532, to Sir Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains; thirdly, before 1544, to Henry Stewart, Lord Methv
2 CONC en ; fourthly, in 1557, to Patrick, Lord Ruthven.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Helen, married to John, fifth Lord Lindsay of the Byres.She was married, secondly, to Thomas Moncur, a dependant, and died May 1577. Her son Patrick, Lord Lindsay, attempted to stop this marriage in January 1564.5
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Jean, married, August 1507, to James Arbuthnott of that Ilk.6
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Elizabeth, stated to have been married to Colin Mackenzie of Kintail.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Isabel, stated to have been married to James Hering of Lethendy.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. JOHN, third Earl of Atholl, born 6 October 1507,7 succeeded his father. He was famous for his great hospitality and his magnificent way of living, more like a sovereign prince than a subject.8 He died about November 1542, of 
2 CONC sickness contracted while with the King's army, before the battle of Solway.9 He married, first, Grizel, (laughter of Sir John Rattray of that Ilk ; 10 secondly, Jean or Janet, daughter of John, sixth Lord Forbes.11 She was marrie
2 CONC d to him less than six months before his death, and on that ground her service of terce was refused.12 She married, secondly, Alexander Hay of Dalgety ; and, thirdly,
2 CONT
2 CONT ''1 Sutherland Book. 2 Ibid., i. 96 n. 3 Acts and Decreets, xi. 67. 4 Fraser's Sutherland Book, i. 96. 5 St. Andrews Kirk Session Register, i. 230. 6 Arbuthnott Inventory, v. supra, p. 288. 7 Exch. Rolls, xv. 677. 8 Pitscottie, i.
2 CONC  337. 9 Acts and Decreets, i. ff. 361, 364 ; Seventh Report Hist. MSS. Com., App. 713. 10 Complete Peerage; Reg. Mag. Sig., 17 March 1537-38. » Macfarlane's Gen. Coll., ii. 214. 12 Acts and Decreets, i. ff. 508, 525''
2 CONT
2 CONT .as his first wife, William Leslie of Balquhain.1 He left issue : —
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. JOHN, fourth Earl.2
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Barbara, married, contract 20 May 1536, to James Menzies of that Ilk.3
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Isabel, married, before 25 March 1552, to William Stewart of Grandtully.4
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Margaret, married, before 19 February 1539, to John Grant, fourth of Freuchie. She died in 1555.5
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Helen, stated to have been married to Sir John Mac-farlane of that Ilk.6
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Jean, stated to have been the Joneta Stewart, relict in 1595 of John Otterburn of Redhall.7
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Daughter stated to have been married to the Laird of Balfour.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Daughter stated to have been married to the Laird of Balbednach8 or Wood of Balbegno.9
2 CONT
2 CONT ''1 Hist. Rec. of Family of Leslie, iii. 46. 2 Douglas inserts as second son Sir James Stewart of Balvany, but no evidence of him has been found. 3 Beg. of Deeds, ii. 353 ; Reg. Mag. Sig. 4 Fraser's Stewarts of Grandtully, Ixxv. 6
2 CONC  Fraser's Chiefs of Grant, i. 152. 6 Scot. Antiquary, xi. 9. 7 Reg. Mag. Sig. 8 Camden MS. 9 Douglas.'' 
2 CONT
