2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT After the decease of Sir John, a calamitous and almost ruinous contest arose between his younger sons and their brother-in-law, the Earl of Athol. Tradition affirms that the Earl, having married Sir John's only daughter, deemed hi
2 CONC mself entitled to a portion, at least, of the Rattray estate, and being a person of great power and authority, came, with a considerable body of men, took possession of the castle of Rattray, and carried off the family writs; whil
2 CONC e Patrick Rattray, the second son, totally unable to resist so potent a nobleman, retired to the castle of Craighall, winch he gallantly defended, and succeeded in holding, together with the lands of Craighall and Klnballoch; the 
2 CONC Athol family continuing to possess the greater part of the lands of Rattray. until they were evicted from them by an appraising, at the instance of Sir Robert Crichton, of Clunie, about the beginning of the seventeenth century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry, Volume 2, By John Burke, p. 1100
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Rattray was Knighted by King James IV in 1488. Appointed Bailie of Regality at Scone 1506. Killed at the Battle of Flodden in 1513. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >John Rattray *1479 Married Margaret Abercrombie. Died soldiering in Holland, leaving 2 daughters who were '''forcibly surrendered to the Earl of Atholl''' for upbringing and marriage into his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Grizel Rattray married '''John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Atholl,''' who murdered Patrick for the Rattray lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Patrick Rattray, 12th Laird of Kinballoch. Driven from Rattray Castle, he settled at KInballoch and began building Craighall. In 1553 he was murdered in his own chapel by his brother-in-law , the 3rd Earl of Atholl, who coveted R
2 CONC attrau lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sylvester Rattray of Craighall. In spite of hindrances from the Atholls, he eventually was served heir to his father and brither to the barony of Craighall and Kinballocxh. Married Marjorie d/o 3rd Lord Gray. Died 1554.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Dawn Stapylton-Adkins. James Rattray & His Descendants in South Africa 1822-1992, self-published, Cape Town, 1992
2 CONT
