2 CONT '''2 February 1590: Summons of Declarator of Recognition at the instance of Mr David Makgill of Cranston-riddell Advocate to our Sovereign Lord and Mr David Makgill younger of Cranston-riddell his son, against John now Earl of Cas
2 CONC sillis son and heir of Gilb. Earl of Cassillis who last deceased, who was son and heir of the also deceased Gilbert Earl of Cassillis immediate heretable tenant to the King and his predecessors, of the 20 pound land of Culean with
2 CONC  the manor place and mill thereof lying in the bailiary of Carrick, and holden by him of the King and his predecessors by service of ward and relief and also against John Lord Thirlestane Chancellor, John Lord Hamilton Sir Thomas 
2 CONC Lyon of Auldbar Knight Treasurer, Sir Patrick Vaus of Barnbarrock Knight, Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culean Knight, Thomas Kennedy of Bargany and John Kennedy of Blairquhan curators of the said John Earl of Cassillis for their interest
2 CONC  and also against Margaret, Giles, and Katharine Kennedys daughters and heirs of the deceased David Kennedy of Culean, Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains son and heir of the said Margaret Kennedy and Richard Kennedy in Largs husband of t
2 CONC he said Katharine Kennedy for their respective interests, bearing the said Mr David Makgill younger of Cranston-riddell being donator to and having a Charter from the King to him his heirs and assignees of the said 20 pound land o
2 CONC f Culean manor place and mill thereof and which had fallen in his highnesses hands by recognition through the alienation of the whole, or greater part thereof without licence or consent of his highness as the Charter of the said 2
2 CONC 0 pound land of Culean under the Great Seal in favor of the said Mr David Makgill younger, did bear, and therefore he had good and undoubted right and title to raise and insist in an Action of Declarator of Recognition before the 
2 CONC Lords of Council against the said John Earl of Cassillis as son and heir aforesaid and his said Curators and also against the other defenders above named prebended possessors of the said 20 pound land of Culean and all others havi
2 CONC ng or pretending to have interest therein, that is to say the said defenders to hear and see the said lands of Culean decerned by Decree of the said Lords to be recognosced to the King, and that the foresaid defenders or any of th
2 CONC em shall never be found hereafter to pretend right thereto by whatever infeftment right or security granted to them, but that the same are fallen to and ought to remain with his highness and his donator aforesaid in time coming. D
2 CONC ated and Signet at Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f991&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hugh+kennedy+of+girvanmains&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotla
2 CONC nd, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/991]'''
