2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis, was one of the Scots Commissioners appointed by the Parliament of 14 December 1557, and sent to France to negotiate Queen Mary's marriage with the Dauphin, and as such was party to the marriage-contr
2 CONC act at the Louvre on 19 April 1558, but was one of the commissioners who met with a mysterious death at Dieppe on their way home. They had refused to consent to the proposal that the Crown-Matrimonial of Scotland should be granted
2 CONC  to the Dauphin, and it is supposed they were poisened. The Earl is said to have died on 28 November 1558, but the exact date is not known, though it was reported in Scotland between 29 November and 5 December 1558. [https://archi
2 CONC ve.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/471/mode/1up/search/quintin+kennedy The Scots Peerage II: 471]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
