1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It is unclear which “Thomas Maclelland of Bombie” was her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Maclellan-of-Bombie/6000000017960235753?
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Marion was a daughter, possibly the eldest daughter of Gilbert Kennedy, 2nd Earl of Cassillis and his wife Lady Isabel Campbell. She was born in 1524.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Thomas McClelland of Bomby.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.kirkcudbright.co/historyarticle.asp?ID=116&p=19&g=4
2 CONT
2 CONT Gl.  Thomas Maclellan, of Bombie, who was killed in the high street of Edinburgh, 11 July. 1526, by the Barons of Drumlanrig, and Lochinvar, leaving a son, Sir Thomas Maclellan, of Bombie, who m. Helen, dau. of Sir James Gordon, o
2 CONC f Lochinvar, by whom he had a son,
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Sir THOMAS who succeeded him.He got a charter, under the great seal,* of all the lands that his father sir Thomas, and his grandfather sir William died possest of, do∣mino Thomae MacLellan de Bombie, &c. anno 1542. He married
2 CONC  Helen,* daughter of sir James Gordon of Lochinvar, by whom he had a son,
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896980.0001.000/1:149?rgn=div1;view=fulltext
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Sir THOMAS, who got charters un∣der the great seal,*Thomae MacLellan de Bom∣bie, of the lands of Plintoun, Blackmark, and several others, inter 1516 et 1520.
2 CONT
2 CONT This sir Thomas had the misfortune to be killed in the street of Edinburgh,* in a fami∣ly feud between him and his neighbours the barons of Drumlanrig and Lochinvar, in Ju∣ly 1526, leaving issue a son,
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Sir THOMAS who succeeded him.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT *Burke’s Peerage and Baronetage 1935 edition
2 CONT *Balfour Paul, Sir James. The Scots Peerage (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1904-1914); in 9 Volumes; Earl of Cassillis - Volume 2 pages 443-502 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/467 Archive.Org]
