2 DATE BEF 22 OCT 1574
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES KENNEDY OF UCHTILLUR===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/467 The Scots Peerage II: 467]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1560: Decree and Final sentence given and pronounced by Thomas Abbot of Glenluce, bearing his being chosen by James Kennedy of Ochterlour at request of Gilbert Earl of Cassillis, to decide about the heritable right of the lands
2 CONC  of Ochterlour and others, lying in the County of Wigton, belonging to the said James Kennedy, and that conform to his obligation dated at Mayboll 12th January then last 1560 and subsuming that having undertaken to decide in the m
2 CONC atter and having respect for the well and honour of the House of Cassillis and considering that James Kennedy having no heirs male of his body, but only two daughters and that Agnes Johnston his wife was not likely to have more ch
2 CONC ildren and also considering that he had and has great support and assistance yearly from the Earl (his brother's son) therefore ordains him to infeft the Earl and his heirs male in the lands of Ochterlour and 5 merk land of Stranr
2 CONC aer and Marscluvy - reserving his liferent and the liferent of the said Agnes Johnston his wife and decerns the Earl to dote his two daughters according to their rank at the sight of four landed gentlemen nearest of him to the Hou
2 CONC se of Cassillis [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f594&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+johnston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kenne
2 CONC dy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/594]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 August 1665: Contract between John, Earl of Montrose and John Graham of Knockdollian whereby the Earl assigns to [blank] on behalf of John Graham a letter of reversion granted by James Kennedy of Uchterluan and Agnes Johnsto
2 CONC n his spouse in favour of Walter Douglas of Ferguston for redeeming the lands of Stronyrair and Markslarrie lying in the sheriffdom of Wigtown, [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f
2 CONC 1%2fA%2f5%2f2%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+johnston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/A/5/2/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 October 1574: Discharge by John Kennide of Kirckmichall to Hew Kennedy of Uchtillure and Elizabeth Kennedy, his spouse, of 160 merks scots in complete payment of 1,400 merks as tocher of Agnes Kennedy due in marriage contrac
2 CONC t by deceased James Kennedy of Uchtillure and Agnes Johnston, his spouse, to said John, and Alexander Kennedy, his son and apparent heir. [Subscribed by granter] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?
2 CONC reference=GD109%2f2677&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+Kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y National Rcords of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire	1412-1965, reference GD109/2677]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 March 1579-80: Tack by Thomas, abbot of Glenclue, with consent of convent thereof, setting to his 'cusingnes' Elizabeth Kennedy of Uchtillur, daughter and successor of umquhile James Kennedy of Uchtillur, to Hew Kennedy her 
2 CONC son, the longer liver of them two, and said Elizabeth's heris, and assignees, The teind sheaves, teinds of lamb, wool, stirk, cheese, gryse, geese, hemp, lint, pasche fines, oblations and all other emoluments of the parsonage and 
2 CONC vicarage of the 5 merkland of Areowland of old extent, in the barony and parish of Glenluce and sheriffdom of Vigtoun, then and for long before possessed by said Elizabeth; and that for 19 years from Lammas 1579. Tack duty 5 merks
2 CONC  Scots. At said abbey 21 Mar 1579/1580. Witnesses, Gillbert Kennedy of Grycane-manis, Alexander Kennedy, son and apparent heir of Gilbert Kenneedy of Drumnellane, Richart Sanderson in Glenluce, Sir Herbert Andresone, vicar of Kelt
2 CONC oun, notary public. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2546&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+Kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Register Hou
2 CONC se charters, 1st series, reference RH6/2546]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 October 1590: Contract between John, Earl of Montrose and John Graham of Knockdollian whereby the Earl assigns to [blank] on behalf of John Graham a letter of reversion granted by James Kennedy of Uchterluan and Agnes Johnst
2 CONC on his spouse in favour of Walter Douglas of Ferguston for redeeming the lands of Stronyrair and Markslarrie lying in the sheriffdom of Wigtown, dated at Glasgow 24 Aug 1565, to which reversion the Earl had right by contract and a
2 CONC ssignation between him and the said Walter Douglas, and in this cause John Graham renounces in favour of the Earl all right and title to the lands of Easter and Wester Clobar in the barony of Mugdock and sheriffdom of Stirling, ex
2 CONC cepting only a liferent tack of Easter Clobar set to the said John by the deceased William, Earl of Montrose. At Mugdock.[http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f5%2f2%2f9&st=1&
2 CONC tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+johnston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/A/5/2/9]'''
