1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === John Campbell, Bishop of the Isles
2 CONT * Gender:	Male 
2 CONT * Birth:	circa 1514, Cawdor, Nairn, Scotland  
2 CONT * Death:	after 1600, Ardchatten, Argyll, Scotland  
2 CONT * Parents: Sir John Campbell, 1st of Calder and Muriel Calder of Cawder  
2 CONT * Partner: unknown  
2 CONT * Spouse: Isabel Lamont   
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Campbell and an unknown woman:
2 CONT #Alexander Campbell, Prior of Ardchattan 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Campbell and Isabel Lamont:
2 CONT #  Colin Campbell, of Inveresragan ( - Yes, date unknown)
2 CONT #  John Campbell, of Eriskay (Abt 1560 - Aft 15 Nov 1625)
2 CONT #  Margaret Campbell (Abt 1570 - Yes, date unknown)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bishop of the Isles
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bishop_of_the_Isles
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bishop of the Isles or Bishop of Sodor was the ecclesiastical head of the Diocese of the Isles (or Sodor), one of Scotland's thirteen medieval bishoprics. The bishopric, encompassing both the Hebrides and Mann, probably traces
2 CONC  its origins as an ecclesiastical unity to the careers of Olaf, King of the Isles, and Bishop Wimund.  In 1689, the Episcopacy was abolished in the Church of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT *1557–1560 x 1562	John Campbell (III.)	Scottish Gaelic: Eóin Caimbeul.
2 CONT * 1572–1592 x 1594	John Campbell (III.) (again)	Scottish Gaelic: Eóin Caimbeul.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prior_of_Ardchattan
2 CONT
2 CONT The Prior of Ardchattan (later Commendator of Ardchattan) was the head of the Valliscaulian, and then Cistercian, monastic community of Ardchattan Priory, Argyll. It was founded in 1230 by Duncan MacDougal, Lord of Argyll. In Apri
2 CONC l 1510 it was incorporated as a cell of Beauly Priory. It was annexed to the bishopric of the Isles in 1615. The following are a list of abbots and commendators:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT List of commendators
2 CONT
2 CONT * Neil Campbell, 1544
2 CONT * John Campbell (again), 1545–1580[1] "In 1558 John Campbell became Prior of Ardchattan, he was succeeded by his son Alexander in 1580, but during these troubled years of religious dissension the number of monks dwindled and the P
2 CONC riory become a private dwelling house."[2] Was Bishop of the Isles, 1557 x 1559-1560 x 1564
2 CONT * Alexander Campbell, 1580–1602
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
