1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Donald Campbell of Ardnamurchan</strong>, co Argyll, and also, by purchase, or Airds in that county, illegit. son or Sir John Campbell of Calder, 'being a man of considerable power and consequence, and the terror of t
2 CONC he district in which he lived'; was created a Baronet [S] 15 January, sealed 23 December 1628, but not recorded in the Great Seal Register [S], with rem. to heirs male whatsoever, and with a grant of, presumably, 16,000 acres in N
2 CONC ova Scotia, of which he had seizin in December 1628. He obtained a new enfeoffment of Airds and other his estates, 28 August 1643, with rem. to George Campbell, son of Sir John Campbell of Calder, the legit. son of his [the Barone
2 CONC t's] father. He married firstly, Jane, daughter of Colin (Campbell), 6th Earl of Argyll [S], by, presumably, his 2nd wife, Agnes, daughter of William (Keith), Earl Marischal [S]. He married secondly, Anne Campbell, illegit. daught
2 CONC er of the said Earl. He died s.p.m.s, 1651, when the Baronetcy became extinct, and the estate of Ardnamurchan passed to the Earls of Argyll [S], but that of Airds devolved, under the entail of 1643, to the abovenamed George Campbe
2 CONC ll."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n359/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 341-342
