1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MASTER NICOL CAMPBELL OF KEITHICK===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Master of Arts; Dean of Lismore Cathedral===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Master Nicol Campbell of Keithick is the bastard son of The Right Reverend Donald Campbell, Abbot of Cupar-Angus Abbey in Perthshire, Scotland. Letters of Legitimation were granted to him on 12 December 1543. [https://archive.o
2 CONC rg/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/697/mode/1up RMS: 2976]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 December 1543: REGINA &c., dedit literas legitimationis NICHOLAO CAMPBELL bastardo, filio naturali Donaldi C. xxix. 97. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/697/mode/1up RMS, 1513-46, charter number 2976]
2 CONC '''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 April 1559: Feu charter by Donald, abbot of Coupar, and convent thereof to Nicholas Campbell, Master of Arts, dean of Lismore, whom failing to David Campbell, his natural brother, of the lands of Dalwany and Craignaite with t
2 CONC he forest, privileges and pastures of Glenbrauchty, Glaswory and Glasworybog. Coupar. [Subscribed by abbot and chapter; common seal of chapter appended]. [514.52]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.asp
2 CONC x?reference=GD16%2f9%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Dalwany&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Airlie, reference GD16/9/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 July 1583: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/225/mode/1up RMS, 1580-93, charter number 730]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 March 1619: REX,— cum consensu &c. (208. 186.),— ratificavit cartam per quondam M. Nic. Campbell do Kethik, cum consensu quond. Katherine Drummound ejus sponse et quond. M. Walteri Lindsay de Hiltoun, factam quond. Joanni com
2 CONC . de Montrois, et quond. Domine Jeanne Drummound ejus conjugi, — de ipsius dimidetate terrarum de Wavdropertoun cum loco et mansione (per Jo. Forbes occupat.), vie. de Kincardin ; — Tenend. dictis com. de M. et Jeanne in conjuncta
2 CONC  infeodatione, et heredibus inter eos legit, procreatis, quibus deficientibus, heredibus et assignatis dicti com. quibuscunque, de rege pro uno den. albe firme ; — de data apud locum de Kincardin, 10 Maii 1586: [https://archive.or
2 CONC g/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/720/mode/1up RMS, 1609-20, charter number 1993]'''
2 CONT
