3 CTRY Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''''John, Master of Seton''''', married Christian Lindsay, daughter of (John, first) Lord Lindsay of the Byres. 
2 CONT The couple being related in the third and third degrees of consanguinity, a commission to grant dispensation for their marriage was given by Pope Pius II. to the Bishop of St. Andrews 20 January 1458-59. The Master predeceased his
2 CONC  father, and was buried in the parish church of Seton. His wife survived him, and was married secondly, before 19 July 1476, to Robert Cunningham, son and heir-apparent of Alexander, first Lord Kilmaurs, afterwards created Earl of
2 CONC  Glencairu. She died before 11 March 1496. By her the Master of Seton had three sons:
2 CONT 1. '''''George.'''''
2 CONT 2. ''John.'' He witnessed an indenture dated at Seton 7 April 1491, being therein designed brother-german
2 CONT of George, Lord Seton.
2 CONT 3. ''Alexander''. He witnessed a document on 20 November 1501, designed as brother-german of George, Lord Seton.
2 CONT 4. ''Margaret'', married to Robert, second Lord Lyle, and had issue a son named George.
2 CONT '''''Source: "The Scots Peerage" Vol 8, page 577.'''''
2 CONT
