2 CONT *From: https://histfam.familysearch.org//getperson.php?personID=I198925&tree=EuropeRoyalNobleHous __________________________
2 CONT *Earl of Nithsdale was a title in the Peerage of Scotland. It was created in 1620 for Robert Maxwell, 9th Lord Maxwell, with remainder to heirs male. He was made Lord Maxwell, Eskdale and Carlyle at the same time. The title of Lor
2 CONC d Maxwell had been created in the Peerage of Scotland in 1445 for Herbert Maxwell.
2 CONT *'''Some confusion in the numbering of the Lords Maxwell has arisen from the second Lord's surrender of his barony during his lifetime in favour of his son, who then pre-deceased him'''. Some authorities refer to the son only as "
2 CONC the Master of Maxwell", but he is more usually counted as the third Lord Maxwell.[4] The fourth Lord Maxwell was killed at the Battle of Flodden in 1513
2 CONT **          Lords Maxwell (1445)
2 CONT * Herbert Maxwell, 1st Lord Maxwell (d. c.1454)
2 CONT *''' Robert Maxwell, 2nd Lord Maxwell (d. c.1485)
2 CONT * John Maxwell, 3rd Lord Maxwell (d. 1484 dvp)
2 CONT * John Maxwell, 4th Lord Maxwell (c.1476–1513)
2 CONT * Robert Maxwell, 5th Lord Maxwell (1493-1546)
2 CONT * Robert Maxwell, 6th Lord Maxwell (d.c.1553)
2 CONT * Robert Maxwell, 7th Lord Maxwell (1551–1555), aged four years
2 CONT * John Maxwell, 8th Lord Maxwell (1553–1593), briefly the Earl of Morton, between 1581–1586
2 CONT * John Maxwell, 9th Lord Maxwell (1583–1613)
2 CONT * Robert Maxwell, 10th Lord Maxwell (1586–1646) (created Earl of Nithsdale in 1620)
2 CONT *From: Earl of Nithsdale http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Maxwell,_2nd_Lord_Maxwell ______________________________
