2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Born in Calderwood and passed in Bannockburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert (Maxwell) Maxwell IInd Lord Maxwell is a member of Clan Maxwell.
2 CONT On 13th January 1424/5, at Edinburgh, a feu charter was made by Thomas de Somerville, Lord of Carnwarth in Lanarkshire, to Robert de Maxwell, son and heir to Sir Herbert de Maxwell Knt., Lord of Carlaverock, and Jonete, daughter o
2 CONC f John Forestare, Lord of Corstorphine, of the lands of Libertoun in the barony of Carnwarth, which Sir Herbert has resigned. destination is to the male heirs legitimately procreated by Robert & Jonete, failing whom to the said he
2 CONC irs of Sir Herbert, failing whom to Amero de Maxwell brother of the said Herbert, etc.[1] This charter was doubtless concluded shortly after the marriage of Robert & Jonete.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert was the 2nd Lord Maxwell.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT Robert married Janet Forrester.[2] They had the five sons and one daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT John, Master, 3rd Lord Maxwell, married Janet Crichton[2]
2 CONT Thomas married Agnes Maxwell, heiress of Kirkconnel and Stewart of Kirkcudbright[2]
2 CONT David[2]
2 CONT Robert[2]
2 CONT Aymer[2]
2 CONT Christian[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.The Great Seal of Scotland, no.15, confirmed at Edinburgh, 4th February 1424/5.
2 CONT 2. 2.0 2.1 2.2 2.3 2.4 2.5 2.6 2.7 Sir William Fraser, The Book of Carlaverock (Edinburgh: unknown, 1873), p. 140-151, digital images, https://archive.org/stream/bookofcarlaverv100fras#page/140/mode/1up. Internet Archive (https://
2 CONC archive.org : accessed 30 October 2016).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT "Robert Maxwell, 2nd Lord Maxwell", The Peerage, http://www.thepeerage.com/p36497.htm#i364969
2 CONT "Robert Maxwell, 2nd Lord Maxwell1 
2 CONT M, #364969, d. between 22 April 1485 and 29 April 1486
2 CONT Last Edited=27 Oct 2014
2 CONT      Robert Maxwell, 2nd Lord Maxwell was the son of Herbert Maxwell, 1st Lord Maxwell and unknown daughter Herries.2 He married Janet Forrester, daughter of Sir John Forrester, 2nd of Corstorphine and Jean Sinclair, from 13 Janua
2 CONC ry 1424/25 to 4 February 1424/25.3 He died between 22 April 1485 and 29 April 1486.1
2 CONT      He held the office of Admiral and Warden of the Western Marches.4 He succeeded as the 2nd Lord Maxwell [S., 1445] circa February 1453/54.4
2 CONT Child of Robert Maxwell, 2nd Lord Maxwell and Janet Forrester
2 CONT John Maxwell, Master of Maxwell+1 d. 22 Jul 1484
