1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALAN MCILVANE OF GRIMMET===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alan Mcilvane of Grimmet is the son of Gilbert McIlvane of Grimmet. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f414&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=makilvan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS:
2 CONC  GD25/1/414]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1517: Retour of John Kennedy of Bennan as heir to his father George Kennedy of Bennan in the 6s 8d land of Bennan comprising the [blank] mains and coiff with the manor, the 21 merkland of [Ballecruchan, the 2 merkland of] Throw
2 CONC ag, the 6s 8d land of Lefnochtclare, with the office of "mair of fie" and serjeant of the bailiary of Carrik. At Knokcosshap near Gervane, in presence of Alexander Kennedy of Gervane [mains and Thomas Corry] of Kelwod, bailies-dep
2 CONC ute of Carrik. Assize: John Kennedy of Culzeane, knight, Fergus Kennedy of Knokdaw, Thomas [blank], Gilbert Kennedy of Kirkmichell, Fergus Kennedy of Drumnellane, Patrick [blank], John Eclis of that ilk, John Eclis of Kildonane, H
2 CONC ew Kennedy of [blank], [John Kennedy of Bard]rochat, Alan Mcilwane of Grummet younger, and James Mccoynill of Barneil[1]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&t
2 CONC p=n&k=mcilwane&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Family of Bennan and Finnarts, reference GD60/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 April 1532: Alan Makilwene served on assize. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/261/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter nu
2 CONC mber 1196 note 1 on p. 261]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 September 1541: Precept of Clare constat by Malcom Prior of Whitehorn and Convent thereof, for infefting Allan Makilvan as heir of the deceased Gilbert Makilvan his father, in the 25 shilling land of Grumetland, lying in the
2 CONC  parish of Colmonel and Earldom of Carrick - to be holden feu of the said prior and Convent and Convent and their successors. Witnesses - Gilbert Baird of Kilquhenzie and Gilbert and John Kennedys. Dated at Whitehorn. Signed by th
2 CONC e Prior, sub Prior and 12 monks. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f414&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=makilvan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Sctland, Papers of the
2 CONC  Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/414]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 May 1544: Charter by which Allani Mackilvene de Grumet confirms that he has given his son and heir apparent Gilberto Mackilvene, and his wife Jonete Corrie, the three merk land of old extent of Nether Grumet, the three merk l
2 CONC and of old extent of Grumet, and the six shilling eight penny land of old extent of Attiquin, to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent. Gilbert reserved his own liferent from the lands of Attiquin, and the liferent of his w
2 CONC ife Mariote Fergussoun from the twenty shilling land of Barquhois and the twenty shilling land of Garrigrum. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/758/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register
2 CONC  of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 3235 on p. 758]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 June 1544: Alan Makilwene served on assize. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/709/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter num
2 CONC ber 3035 note 1 on p. 709]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomaston_Castle THOMASTON CASTLE]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomaston Castle was originally built in the 13th century for a nephew of Robert The Bruce, and first owned by Alan McIlvaine (b. 1500 in Ayrshire) whose family supplied wine to the Earls Kennedy, owners of nearby Culzean Castle. 
2 CONC Upon his death, Thomaston passed to Patrick McIlvaine on his marriage to Isobel Kennedy, niece of the Earl of Cassilis.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Account===
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.macsoldpapermoney.com/TheMcIlvains.pdf The McIlvains]
2 CONT
2 CONT "The McIlvaines are a sept of the McBain/McBean Clan. The Clan Badge is a grey demi catamountain,
2 CONT salient, on his sinister foreleg a Highland targe, gules, and inscribed with the MacBain Clan Motto:
2 CONT 'Touch Not a Catt, Bot a Targe.'
2 CONT
2 CONT Allan McElwain/McIlvaine de Grumete, Laird of Grimet
2 CONT Born: around 1470 Ayrshire, Scotland
2 CONT Married: Marian Fergoussone in 1495
2 CONT Died: around 1545
2 CONT Parents: Gilberto Mcylveyne McIlvne McElwain Laird of Grummet & Attiquyne and Isabel Elizabeth Kennedy Lady of Grymmet & Attiquyne"
2 CONT [https://huntingformyroots.wordpress.com/2020/08/18/mcilvaine-family/]
