1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children of Sir John KENNEDY and Elizabeth MONTGOMERY:
2 CONT
2 CONT V.  John KENNEDY.  He was born about 1474, Culzean Castle, Maybole, Ayrshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Suggested as the person who appears on The Flodden Death-Roll under Lords: - "Culwen, Sir John Kennedy of Cullean?". (The Scottish Antiquary, or, Northern Notes and Queries Vol. 13, No. 51 (Jan., 1899), pp. 101-111) [https://www.j
2 CONC stor.org/stable/25516912]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Kennedy,_2nd_Lord_Kennedy John Kennedy (d 1508) His second wife was Lady Elizabeth Gordon, daughter of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly and Elizabeth Crichton, whom he married between 24 Aug
2 CONC ust 1467 and 12 August 1471. By her he had three sons and four daughters, including Janet Kennedy (c. 1480 – c. 1545) and Margaret Kennedy, wife of Andrew Stewart.
2 CONT *https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00311144&tree=LEO cites
2 CONT *Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage and Knightage, London, 1938. page 88 
2 CONT *http://mlloyd.org/gen/macomb/text/kennedy/kennedypedigree.htm
2 CONT *http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I18671&tree=CC cites
2 CONT *[S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Kennedy01: The Scots Peerage (Cassillis), Burkes Peerage 1 9 34 (Ailsa).
2 CONT *[S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Seton02.
2 CONT *https://www.maybole.org/history/surname/macilvean/of_carrick.htm
