2 CONT # +Isabella Margaret Campbell, b. 1490, Loudoun, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00221961&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Campbell of Loudoun, son of Sir George Campbell of Loudoun d. Aft 1492 and NN Kennedy, married Isobel Wallace, daughter of Thomas Wallace of Craigie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT The historie and descent of the house of RowallaneÃ‚Â by Sir William Mure, knight of Rowallan ; written in, or prior to 1657 Published 1825 by Printed for Chalmers and Collins in Glasgow The Scots peerage, Vol. V, page 494 links
2 CONT
2 CONT http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1323.htm#i39734 http://strengthyarbrough.familytreeguide.com/getperson.php?personID=I1965&tree=T1&PHPSESSID=91cec46dd0d347fcd9b1eaec61e3ddee http://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecc
2 CONC o/004896980.0001.000/1:159?rgn=div1;view=fulltext
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Sir HUGH, high sheriff of Air, who got charters under the great seal,*Hugoni Campbell de Loudoun, militi, of many lands and baronies, inter 1501 et 1507.
2 CONT
2 CONT This sir Hugh sat in the Scotch parliament when queen Mary's jointure was settled,*anno 1504.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Isabel, daughter of sir Thomas Wallace of Craigie,* by whom he had a son,
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Hugh, his heir,ÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â€ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â”and five daughÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚ÂˆÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â£ters.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Annabella, married, 1st, to sir Thomas Boswell of Auchinleck; 2dly, to sir John CunÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚ÂˆÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â£ningham of Caprington.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Helen, married to Laurence CrawÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚ÂˆÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â£furd of Kilbirny, ancestor of the viscount GarÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚ÂˆÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â£nock and earl of Crawfurd.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Isabel, married to Mungo Muir of RowÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚ÂˆÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â£allan.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Janet, married toÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â€ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â”Campbell of Cesnock.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Margaret, married to Thomas KenneÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚ÂˆÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â£dy of Bargeny.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died anno 1508, and was succeeded by his son,
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir HUGH CAMPBELL of Loudoun, high sheriff of Air,* who was possest of a vast estate, which appears by his charters under the great seal, inter 1580 et 1600.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a man of sine parts, and in great favour with king James VI. who appointed him one of the lords of his privy council,* created him a baronet and lord of parliament, by the title of lord Loudoun, the last day of June 1601.
2 CONT
2 CONT He afterwards got charters under the great seal,*Hugoni domino Loudoun, of many lands, inter 1612 et 1616.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 1st, Margaret, daughter of sir John Gordon of Lochinvar,* ancestor of visÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚ÂˆÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â£count Kenmure, by whom he had a son,
2 CONT
2 CONT George, master of Loudoun,ÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â€ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â”and three daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Juliana, married to sir Colin Campbell of Glenurchy, ancestor of the earl of BÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â€ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â¢eaÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚ÂˆÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â£dalbane.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Isabel, married to sir John Maxwell of Pollock,
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Margaret, married to John Kennedy of Blairquhan, Esq;.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 2dly, lady Isabel Ruthven, daughter of William earl of Gowrie, widow of sir Robert Gordon of Lochinvar, by whom he had two daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.ÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â€ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â”, married to sir William CunÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚ÂˆÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â£ninghame of Cunninghamhead.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.ÃƒÂƒÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â€ÃƒÂ‚Ã‚Â”, married to David Crawfurd of Kerse, Esq;.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 3dly, Margaret, daughter of sir David Home of Wedderburn, by whom he had no issu He died anno 1622, and was succeeded by his grand daughter Margaret, as will be shown hereafter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896980.0001.000/1:159?rgn=div1;view=fulltext
