1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JANET BORTHWICK===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It has been claimed that Janet Borthwick, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-William-Borthwick-of-Catcune-1st-of-Borthwick/6000000149648899862 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Janet Borthwick was granted a papal dispensation for her marriage to Sir Adam Borthwick of Hailes on 2 November 1411. [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalnote00hepb/page/n49/mode/1up Genealogical Notes: 23] According to St
2 CONC irnet, she was the daughter of Sir William Borthwick. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/hh4bz/hepburn1.php Stirnet: Hepburn]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/genealogicalnote00hepb/page/n5/mode/1up Genealogical notes of the Hepburn family. By Edward Hepburn. (Printed for Private Circulation, 1925), 51 pp. including index]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/hh4bz/hepburn1.php Stirnet: Hepburn 1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Borthwick was the daughter of Sir William Borthwick of Catcune and wife of Adam de Hepburn, Lord of Hailes in Haddingtonshire. They had a Papal Dispensation to marry dated 2nd November 1411.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT By her husband she had nine known children including John Hepburn, Bishop of Dunblane, and Sir Patrick Hepburn, 1st Lord of Hailes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Janet Borthwick (?)[1, 2]
2 CONT *Father: Sir William Borthwick, of Catcune,   d. Bef 1430 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT # Sir Adam Hepburn, of Hailes,   d. 1446  Children 	
2 CONT * +	1. Sir Patrick Hepburn, of Hailes, 1st Baron Hailes ,   b. Abt 1412,   d. Aft 6 Dec 1482  (Age ~ 70 years)
2 CONT * +	2. Margaret Hepburn
2 CONT * +	3. Elizabeth Hepburn
2 CONT * +	4. Agnes Hepburn
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # [S265] Colquoun_Cunningham.ged, Jamie Vans
2 CONT # [S285] London 1910. Alan Sutton, 1982, G E C, (London 1910. Alan Sutton, 1982)
2 CONT # [S281] Scottish Families, Gregory Lauder-Frost, (ABC Publications)	
2 CONT # [S01352] ~Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage and Knightage, London, 1938. 1326 
2 CONT # [S00058] The Complete Peerage, 1936 , Doubleday, H.A. & Lord Howard de Walden. VI 239 
