1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN MONTGOMERY OF HESSILHEAD formerly of CORSCRAIG===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to James Paterson, Sir John Montgomery of Hessilhead is the son of Hugh Montgomery of Hessilhead and his wife Janet Maxwell. [https://archive.org/stream/historyofcountyo01pateuoft#page/290/mode/1up History of Ayr I:  
2 CONC p. 290]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Flodden Death at Flodden]===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Montgomery of Hessilhead died on 9 September 1513, fighting under the Standard of James IV, King of Scots, at Flodden near Branxton in Northumberland, England.  [https://archive.org/stream/historyofcountyo01pateuoft#pa
2 CONC ge/290/mode/1up History of the County of Ayr: I:  p. 290]''' 
