2 CONT '''20 August 1485: Instrument of sasine given propriis manibus by Hugh, Lord Montgomery to Robert Montgomery as son and heir to deceased Sir William Montgomery, knight of the lands of Giffyn and Bar. Witnesses: John Montgomery of 
2 CONC Hethhed and others. John Moderuele, notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f30%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hethhed&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=n National Records of Sc
2 CONC otland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/30/5 ]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 April 1490: Letter of reversion granted by Sir John of Montgomery of Corscraig whereby he declares that although Hew, Lord Montgomery had sold to him the 4 merk land of old extent of Gyfnok, lying within the lordship of East
2 CONC wood, yet on the said Lord paying to him 100lib Scots upon the high altar of the Kirk of Eastwood, on 40 days warning he would give him regress to the said lands. Dated at Glasgow. Witnesses: Archibald, Earl of Argyll, and Lord Ca
2 CONC mpbell and others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f75&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corscraig&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgome
2 CONC rie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/10/75]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 June 1498: Precept directed from the chancery of James IV to James, Lord Hamilton, David Kennedy, knight, son and heir apparent of John, Lord Kennedy, James Campbell of Loudoun, Robert Montgumry of Giffen, John Montgomry of C
2 CONC orscrag, knight, Constantine Dunlop of that ilk, Lyon King of Arms, Ormonde Pursuivant, John Keir and Donald Malinny, messengers, and siller of them, as his sheriffs of Ayr for infefting Hugh, Lord of Montgumry in the said offices
2 CONC  conform to GD3/1/1/15/6 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f15%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corscrag&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the 
2 CONC Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/15/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 February 1499: Instrument of resignation by Hugh, Lord of Montgomery of his lands of Robertoun lying in the bailliary of Cunningham within the sheriffdom of Ayr in the hands of King James IV as Stewart of Scotland in favour o
2 CONC f Hugh, Lord of Montgomery and Elene Campbell, his spouse (both personally present and accepting) and the longest liver of them two in conjunct infeftment and the heirs lawfully procreated or to be procreated between them; whom fa
2 CONC iling to the heirs and assignees of the said Hugh, whomsoever. Done in the Royal Palace of Striveling. Witnesses: George, Abbot of Dunfermline, James, Abbot of Scone, Cuthbert, Lord of Kilmauris, John, Lord  Kennedy, Andrew, Lord 
2 CONC of Avandale, John, Master of Athole, William Dromond, John Montgomery of Corscrag, knight, Robert Montgomery of Giffin, Andrew Wod, William Sinclar, William Spishous, servants and doorkeepers of the royal chamber and others. Andre
2 CONC w Cuninghame, notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f52%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corscrag&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Mon
2 CONC tgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/52/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This deed is printed in Memorials of the Montgomeries II: p. 58]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 November 1500: Precept following on charter for infefting Hugh, Lord Montgomery in the foresaid lands. Dated at Corsle.Baillies Robert Montgomery of Giffing, John Montgomery of Corscraig, Alexander Montgomery of Braidstane, 
2 CONC John Crawfurd, Lord of Baichlian, John Montgomery, James Montgomery (brothers), german of the said Hugh, Lord Montgomery and others. Witnesses: John Kennedy of Culzane and others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatal
2 CONC ogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f35%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/10
2 CONC /35/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 February 1501: Procuratory of resignation granted by John Knox for resigning his 4 chalders of oatmeal and one pound of pepper which he uptook yearly at feast of Whitsunday and Martinmas in winter by equal proportions furth 
2 CONC of the said lands of Stane in the hands of King James IV in favour of Hugh, Lord Montgomery. Procurators John Knox, son and heir apparent of John Knox of that ilk, John Montgomery of Heslet, knight, John Montgomery, son and heir a
2 CONC pparent of George Montgomery of Skelmorlie, Andrew Wood and John Kinloch. Dated at Knok. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f64%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=heslet&ko=p&r=&
2 CONC ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/64/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 February 1501: Instrument of sasine following in precept of clare contstat in favour of Alexander Montgomery, son of Robert Montgomery of Giffen then deceased as heir to his father in the lands of Poldrait together with cert
2 CONC ain annualrents levied yrealy from certain tenements of land within the burgh of Linlithgow. Witnesses: Sir John Montgomery of Corss Crage, Robert Franceiss of Stane and others. John Maknakle, notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.
2 CONC gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f50%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, refe
2 CONC rence GD3/1/1/50/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 November 1501: Inquisition made at Grey in Giffin on 26 Nov 1501 before Hugh, Lord Montgomery and superior of Giffin, by John Montgomery of Corscrag, knight, John Blar of that ilk, Alexander Montgomery of Bradstan, Robert Ke
2 CONC r of Kerisland, Thomas Boyll of Ryissholm, Alexander Peten of that ilk, Andrew Craufurd of Badlane, Alexander Hamilton of Camsketh, Alexander Caulduell of that ilk, William Ros of Mungrenan, Gilbert Dunlop of Hawpland, John Montgo
2 CONC mery and James Montgomery, brothers german of Lord Montgomery; whereby it is found that Alexander Montgomery, son of Robert Montgomery of Giffen then deceased is heir of his father in the 33 merks of the land of old extent of Giff
2 CONC in together with the lands of Knokintyr and 50s annualrent to be levied yearly from the lands of Drumdow lying within the sheriffdom of Ayr; item in 25 acres of land of Poldreat lying within the territory of Linlithgow and sheriff
2 CONC dom of the same together with certain annualrents to be levied yearly from certain tenements of land within the burgh of Linlithgow which lands and annualrents were then valued at 135 merks and in the time of peace at 43 merks now
2 CONC  held of the said Hugh, Lord Montgomery as superior in capite for ward relief and marriage when they should happen and three suits of court at three head pleas yearly on the Greyhill of Giffin and had been in his hands through non
2 CONC entry, since the decease of the said Robert Montgomery 15 days before. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f30%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df
2 CONC =1500&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/30/6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This deed was printed in Memorials of the Montgomeries, Earls of Eglinton, II: p. 61'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1503: Tack granted by Margaret Blair, spouse to Robert Montgomery of Giffin and Lady of the Third Part of Giffin in favour of her beloved goodson, Alexander Montgomery of Giffin and his heirs of all her terce lands of Giffyn in
2 CONC  which Robert Montgomery, unquhile, her husband died vest and seised as of fee; and also of the lands which Dame Janet Houstoun had in conjunct fee and terce with entry on the 18th day of May 1503 for all the days of her life. Giv
2 CONC en under the seal of John Hamiltone, burgess of Glasgow because the said Margaret had no seal of her own. Witnesses: Sir John Montgomery of Corsecrag, knight, John Montgomery, brother german to Alexander Montgomery of Giffin and T
2 CONC homas of Ralston and others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f30%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Sco
2 CONC tland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/30/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This deed was printed in Memorials of the Montgomeries, Earls of Eglinton, II: p. 63.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 April 1505: Charter granted by James IV under his Great Seal on the narrative that notwithstanding the lands and lordship of Giffin, which had pertained to Hugh Lord Montgomery held by him of the King, as Stewart of Scotland
2 CONC  in capite, and the tenandries thereof then pertaining to the following parts, held by them heritably form the said Hugh, Lord Montgomery viz the lands of Giffin which had pertained to deceased Alexander Montgomery; the lands of H
2 CONC eichedis, Hesykedis and Bawgray which had pertained to John Montgomery, knight; the lands of Braidstane which had pertained to Alexander Montgomery; the lands of Ovirtooun which had pertained to Robert Ker; the lands of Begert Ram
2 CONC mysheid and Litilheichede which had pertained to Adam Mure, knight, and the lands of Rouchwod and Braidstane-Ward which had pertained to Robert Hamyll were recognosed in the hands of the King through the alienation of the greater 
2 CONC part thereof, made by the said Hugh, Lord Montgomery and his predecessors to their foresaid free tenants and their predecessors and by the lapse of year and day after this recognition and the said Hugh and all others having intere
2 CONC st thereto being lawfully cited by the Lords of the King's Council and their decree made thereupon that the foresaid lands and lordship ought to pertain to the King and his successors and the same possessed by him as his property 
2 CONC and to be disponed by him at his free pleasure in future times for ever; because the greater part had been alienated by Hugh and his predecessors to the said tenants and their predecessors without the licence, consent and confirma
2 CONC tion of the King and his predecessors; the foresaid lands and lordship being held of them as Stewarts of Scotland for the service of ward and relief as the said decree made thereupon by the said Lords more fully bore, nevertheless
2 CONC  the King considering the good faithful and gratuitous service done to him by his said cousin and that the said alienations were made for the greater part long before to the said foresaid tenants and their predecessors, possessors
2 CONC  thereof, he did nor desire that they should be dispossessed or disinherited but rather that by his present gift and new infeftment they should have more certain rights thereto; therefore he for himself, and his successors, Kings 
2 CONC and Stewarts of Scotland, heritably gave and confirmed to Hugh, Lord Montgomery, his heirs and assignees, the lands and lordship of Giffin with tenants, tenandries etc with full consent and licence to his said cousin and his heirs
2 CONC  to give, alienate and dispone the foresaid lands and lordship, in tenandries, free tenandries, or otherwise to the foresaid persons, who were tenants and possessors thereof without damage or peril of forfeiture for making the sai
2 CONC d alienation; to hold of the King and his successors, Kings and Stewarts of Scotland, in fee, heritage, property, superiority and tenandry for ever for services used and wont, and the said tenants to hold of the said Hugh and his 
2 CONC heirs. Witnesses: William, bishop of Aberdeen, Keeper of the Privy Seal, Archibald, Earl of Ergyle, Lord Campbell and Lorne, Master of the Household, Patrick, Earl of Bothuell, Lord Halis, etc Mathew, Earl of Levinax, Lord Dernlie
2 CONC , Alexander, Lord Home, Great Chamberlain, Andrew, Lord Gray, justiciary, James, Abbot of the monastery of Dunfermline, treasurer, and Master Gavin Dunbar, archdeacon of St Andrews, clerk register. Dated at Striveling in the 17th 
2 CONC year of his reign. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f30%2f11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers o
2 CONC f the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/30/11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 June 1505: Charter by which Hugh, Lord Montgomery, confirms to John Montgomery of Corscraigis, possession of the lands of Hessilheidis, Heicheid Major and Heicheid Minor, with Bawgra, together with the two merk land of Drumb
2 CONC owie in the lordship of Giffen. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi06scot#page/667/mode/1up The Register of the Great Seal of scotland, A.D. 1593-1607, charter number 1835 on p. 667]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    12
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 July 1509: Charter granted by Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Lord Montgomery and lord of the lordships of Ardrossan and Giffin in favour of his cousin, Patrick Montgomery, son and heir of his deceased cousin, Alexander Montgomery o
2 CONC f Giffin and his heirs male, etc; whom failing to Archibald Montgomery, brother german of the said Patrick and his heirs male etc; whom failing to Malcolm Montgomery, brother german of the said Patrick and Archibald, and his heirs
2 CONC  male etc; whom failing to Mathew Montgomery, brother german of the said Patrick and the heirs male etc; whom failing to Robert Montgomery, also brother of the said Patrick and the heirs male etc; whom failing to John Montgomery, 
2 CONC also brother german to the said Patrick, and his heirs male etc; whom all failing freely to return to the said Earl and his heirs of the whole of his lands of the lordship of Giffin with the tower and fortalice thereof and the Mil
2 CONC l of Heslet and the house and mill lead thereof, with all privileges belonging thereto, lying the barony of Kylestewart, within the sheriffdom of Ayr, the lands of Lochhous and Poldrait lying in the constabulary of Linlithgow with
2 CONC in the sheriffdom of Edinburgh, the lands of Knokuntyre and Knokmylne lying in the lordship of Kyle Regis, within the sheriffdom of Ayr, together with an annualrent of 50s Scots levied and taken yearly from the lands of Drumdow, l
2 CONC ying in the said lordship of Kyle Regis, and also all tofts crofts and particates of land lying within the burgh of Linlithgow and also all his annualrents within the said burgh, which lands had pertained to the deceased Alexander
2 CONC  Montgomery, holden by him of the said Earl in capite; and because the Earl's predecessors had alienated the greater part of the lands and whole lordship of Giffin, they had been recognosced from him as superior thereof and adjudg
2 CONC ed to the King as Lord Stewart of Scotland by decreet of the Lords of his Council and which the said Earl had relaxed and redeemed; to hold of him and his heirs for yielding of three suits of court at three head pleas to be held y
2 CONC early at the Grehill of Giffen together with wards, marriages and reliefs when they should happen; reserving always to him and his heirs the Grehill for the capital messuage which ought to contain 6 acres of land in length and bre
2 CONC adth and whenever residing therein to have free liberty of peat and turf and other foggage as the rest of those dwelling in the said lands have and grass for three cows in the common muir of Giffin.Dated at Castle of Eglinton. Wit
2 CONC nesses: John Montgomery of Corsecrag, knight, Cuthbert Montgomery of Skelmorlie, William Dunlop of Crag and others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f30%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n
2 CONC &tn=n&tp=n&k=john+montgomery&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/30/13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    13
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 May 1550: REGINA etc. dedit literas legitimimationis ROBERTO MONTGOMERY bastardo, filio naturali quondam Johannis M. de Hissilheid militis. xxx. 588. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/107/mode/1up Regis
2 CONC trum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-1580, charter number 458 on p. 107]''
2 CONT
