2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 April 1517: Instrument of resignation made by Thomas Hume, burgess of the burgh of Edinburgh and Janet Wod, his spouse in favour of Thomas Hume of Langshaw, knight of the lands of Crevauch lying in the lordship of Stewarton 
2 CONC and sheriffdom of Ayr which had been alienated to them by the said Thomas Hume; whereupon the said Thomas Hume and Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, Lord Montgomery asked instruments. Done in the house of the said Earl situated within the B
2 CONC urgh of Edinburgh, on the south side of the public street thereof [Written by] John Chapman, notary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f12%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hum
2 CONC e+of+langshaw&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/12/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 April 1517: Charter of vendition granted by Sir Thomas Hume of Langshaw, knight in favour of Hugh, Earl of Eglinton, his heirs and assignees of the lands of Crevauch therein described as extending yearly to 5 merks of land o
2 CONC f old extent, lying within the bailliary of Cunningham and sheriffdom of Ayr; to hold of him in feu for payment yearly of a penny Scots at the feast of Whitsunday on the ground of the said lands, in the name of feu farm if asked o
2 CONC nly. Dated at Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f12%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hume+of+langshaw&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers
