2 CONT '''17 April 1517: Obligation by Sir Thomas Hume of Langshaw to pay to Hugh, Earl of Eglinton the sum of 600 merks Scots in case he should be molested in the peaceable possession of the lands of Crevouch. Dated at Edinburgh. [http:
