2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 June 1576: Extract bond of caution by Henry, Lord Sinclair, as cautioner for Magnus Sinclair of Kynninmonth [Kinninmonth], to Andrew Bruce, son of umquhile Marion Bruce, spouse of said Magnus, of money received by Magnus on t
2 CONC he reversion to James Gib [Gibb] of Ballinkirk of sixteen part lands of Over Stintoun [Over Stenton] in regality of Dunfermline and sheriffdom of Fife and reversion to Thomas Scott of Abbotshall of annualrent on lands of Abbotshal
2 CONC l. Registered: B of C and S, 18 June 1576. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD164%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=andrew+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland
2 CONC , Papers of the Sinclair Family, Earls of Rosslyn, reference GD164/8]'''
