1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===KENTIGERN HUNTER OF HUNTERSTON (aka MUNGO HUNTER OF HUNTERSTON)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kentigern Hunter of Hunterston (aka Mungo Hunter of Hunterston) is the son of Robert Hunter of Hunterston. The name of his mother is not certainly known, although it seems quite likely, probable even, that he was the son of Jan
2 CONC et Montgomery. [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso45scotuoft#page/21/mode/1up Hunterston Papers: 21-2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to John Burke: "Mungo or Quintegern Hunter of Hunterston" fell at Pinkie on 10 September 1547. [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalheral02burk#page/501/mode/1up Commoners II: 501] It seems that this is wrong, howe
2 CONC ver, and that he was actually killed at the Battle of Falsyd (Falside), which took place on 9 September 1547. This is made clear by a precept of sasine made in favour of his son Robert dated 15 October 1548, where it is said that:
2 CONC  "the late Kentigern Hwntar of Hwntaristoun, father of Robert Hwntar, bearer of these presents, died last vest and seised as of fee at out faith and peace under our banner at the BATTLE OF FALSYD in all and whole the five merk lan
2 CONC ds of old extent of CAMPBELLTOUN." [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso45scotuoft#page/25/mode/1up Hunterston Papers: 25-8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kentigern Hunter of Hunterston married Marion Hamilton. The marriage contract is dated 1 August 1537. [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso45scotuoft#page/21/mode/1up Hunterston Papers: 21] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Hunter-of-Hunterston/6000000019818796996?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1531476237416&through=6000000019829799745
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Hunter-of-Abbotshill/6000000039285628910?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1531476345530&through=6000000019829799745
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 June 1536: Charter by which Robert Hunter of Hunterston confirms that he has sold the sixteen shilling eight penny land of old extent of Mekill Caldorwod in the barony of Kilbride and sheriffdom of Lanark, to James Hamilton, 
2 CONC brother of Robert Hamilton of Torrance, and Cristine Stewart. The charter was witnessed by Kentigerno Huntar and a number of others. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/354/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regu
2 CONC m Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 1590 on p. 354]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 May 1546: Charter by which the Queen confirms possession of the lands of Arnele-Huntar to Kentigerno Huntar of Huntarstoun and his wife Mariote Hammiltoun. Kentigern had previously resigned this land to the crown in order to
2 CONC  obtain a new grant in his name and in the name of his wife. The land was to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent, and by their lawfull male heirs, whom failing by Kentigerno's heirs.  [https://archive.org/stream/registrum
2 CONC magnisi03scot#page/761/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 3249 on p. 761]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso45scotuoft#page/n4/mode/1up M. S. Shaw, WS. for Lt.-General Sir Aylmer Hunter-Weston of Hunterston, Some Family Papers of the Hunters of Hunterston (Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh,
2 CONC  1925), 90 pp.]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalheral02burk#page/500/mode/1up A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland, enjoying territorial possessions or high official rank; but univested with 
2 CONC heritable honours, by John Burke, Esq., Vol. II (Henry Colburn, London, MDCCCXXXV), pp. 500-03 for Hunter of Hunterston]
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/hh4bz/hunter01.php Stirnet: Hunter 01]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Unatributed Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kentigern Mungo Huntar of Huntarstoune or of that Ilk  who married Marion, daughter of James Hamilton of Torrance county of Lanark and with  her was infeft in Easter Arneil on 1st August 1537 during his father's life time. He  
2 CONC succeeded his father in 1546, as appears from an instrument of sasine of the 8th May  of that year and in the same year, would seem to have been present with "Our Soverane  Ladyis oist and army convenit at Dumbartane the xi day of
2 CONC  July for asseging of the  Castle thereof", as the Register of the Privy Seal, contains a grant made to him of  "all gudis moveable quhilk pertinit to William Finlay in Dalry and Alexander Finlay  younger and now pertening to our 
2 CONC Soverane Lady be resoune of Eschete throw thair  tresonable remaining and abyding at hame fra our Soverane Ladyis oist and army."'''
