1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == NINIAN STEWART OF ARMALEISH ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sheriff of Bute and Arran; Captain and Keeper of the Royal Castle of Rothesay==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 August 1506: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms possession to Ninian Stewart, Sheriff of Bute, and his wife Jonete Dunlop, of one half of the lands of Nether Dunallide, and one half of the lands of Dullaride-
2 CONC Gilliemechell, together with the lands of Largilzane in the lordship of Bute and sheriffdom thereof. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/636/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2988]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/dd/dunlop01.php Stirnet: Dunlop 01]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/289/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 289]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ninian Stewart (Sheriff of Bute and Aran)'''
2 CONT * Birth: ABT 1476 in Ardmaleish, Isle of Bute, Scotland
2 CONT * Death: ABT 1539 in Rothesay Castle, Isle of Bute, Scotland
2 CONT * Father: James Stewart of Kilcattan b: ABT 1445 in Kilcattan, Isle of Bute, Scotland
2 CONT * Mother: unknown
2 CONT * Married: 1) unknown Campbell 2) Janet Dunlop 3) Elizabeth Blair
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd son
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices held:
2 CONT *  The office of Sheriff of Bute.
2 CONT *  He held the office of Sheriff of Arran.
2 CONT *  On 28 May 1490 he was retoured heir to Ardmaleish, Greenan, Mill of Kilcattan and Corrigillis estates.
2 CONT *  He held the office of Hereditary Captain and Keeper of Rothesay Castle in 1498
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://awtc.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=:2516992&id=I526140304&ti=5538 '''awtc.ancestry.com....''']; 
2 CONT * ID: I526140304
2 CONT * Name: Ninian STEWART OF BUTE
2 CONT * Given Name: Ninian
2 CONT * Surname: Stewart of Bute
2 CONT * Sex: M
2 CONT * Birth: Abt 1480 1
2 CONT * Marriage -1- Elizabeth BLAIR b: Abt 1480
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT NINIAN, the eldest son, succeeded, was sheriff of Bute, and got a new grant of the hereditary command of the castle of Rothesay, with a salary of 40 merks yearly, out of the feu-farms of Bute, Kintyre, Cowal, &c. upon which he got
2 CONC  a charter under the great seal,* from king James IV. anno 1502.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Ninian Stewart, Sheriff of Bute and Arran[1, 2]
2 CONT   1469 - 1538
2 CONT
2 CONT Suffix 	Sheriff of Bute and Arran  Birth 	1469  Gender 	Male  Died 	Bef 1538  		 	
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	James Stewart, Sheriff of Bute 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 	dau. Campbell 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 	 	1. James Stewart, Sheriff of Bute
2 CONT
2 CONT  	2. Robert Stewart, of Ambrismore
2 CONT
2 CONT  	3. Archibald Stewart, of Largilzane
2 CONT
2 CONT  	4. Alexander Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2 	Janet Dunlop 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 	Bef 10 Aug 1506  [2, 3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 3 	Elizabeth Blair 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 	Bef 15 Oct 1516  [1, 4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 	 	1. Ninian Stewart, of Largobroughton, Kildavanan and Kilcattan
