2 CONT Ninian" Stewart (James,1 John," King Robert II) was served heir to his father in 1490. He was made hereditary castellar of Rothsay by James IV in I4qS. He married (1) Campbell, and had four children; 
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Janet Dunlop. and had a son Archibald; and 
2 CONT
2 CONT (j) Elizabeth, daughter of Blair of that ilk.
2 CONT
2 CONT  From him sprang the Stewarts of Kilchattan. Ascog, Ballinstraid and Ballintoy, of whom is the Londonderry family (later). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 1 James : who succeeded [of John Lamond ; ancestor Stewarts of Ambrismore 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Robert : of Nether Kilmory. 1506, and Ambrismore. 1429; married a daughter 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 William : of Largivrechtan, 1506, and the south half of Cugach. 1535
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Janet ; married Ninian Bannatyne of Karnes but was divorced on account of 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 Archibald : of Largizean, ancestor of the Stewarts of Largizean [consanguinity 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Alexander : of Kildavanan; married Elizabeth Tait 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Ninian : of Nether Kilmory, 1531, and Largizean, 1548. He obtained Kilda- vanan from his father and purchased Kilchattan from his cousin James.1' He was granted Ambrismore in heritage in 1506 and exchanged his lands in Perthshir
2 CONC e for Kildonan and others in Arran,
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.com/books?id=ZxpWAAAAMAAJ&pg=RA1-PA30&lpg=RA1-PA30&dq=mary+campbell+married+ninian+stewart&source=bl&ots=MvmRDtl88y&sig=ACfU3U34um0yGcJpU1k5V0qnYuxtjTIGtw&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwi1qID5sM7gAhUF1oMKHbWYAYAQ6AEwBn
