1 NAME Gavin Blair, of Auldmuir
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1560 AND 1600
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT The parents of Ann Blair of Auldmuir were Gavin Blair of Auldmuir and his wife, Annabel Stewart.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Auldmuir Farm is situated roughly 1.5 miles west of Dalry and the former barony of Lynn, once owned by the Lynns of that Ilk. On 15 January 1622, Master Gavin Blair of Auldmuir was one of several witnesses to a charter for the Kir
2 CONC klands [church lands] of Eaglesham belonging to Alexander Montgomerie, Earl of Eglinton.''1/''
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Gavin's wife is revealed in a judicial ratification dated 8 December 1628 whereby "Annabel Stewart, designated spouse of Mr Gavin Blair of Auldmuir" ratified the disposition of a property in County Down, Ireland.''2/''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1643, Andrew Lynn gave investment in his Ayrshire properties “to Ann Blair, his future spouse, daughter of Gavin Blair of Auldmuir”.''3/''
2 CONT
2 CONT Then, on 2 May 1667, Gavin was described as deceased in a charter for lands belonging to the Earls of Eglinton, including "2 merk land and a half merk land of Kirkwood, all lying in the said bailliary of Cunningham, which had pert
2 CONC ained to the deceased Master Gavin Blair of Auldmuir".''4/''  However, even as late as 1729, Gavin was remembered as having owned "of old" "2 and half merk land of Kirkwood" in Stewarton Parish, Ayrshire.''5/''
2 CONT
