1 NAME Alexander /Cunningham of Montgreenan/ Commendator of Kilwinning
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN Cunningham of Montgreenan
2 NSFX Commendator of Kilwinning
2 _MARNM Cunningham of Montgreenan
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 14 NOV 1583 AND 22 JUN 1585
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALEXANDER CUNNINGHAM OF MONTGREENAN===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Commendator of Kilwinning Abbey===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Cunningham, here treated, is the only son of Alexander, Earl of Glencairn, and his second wife Janet Cunningham. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/241 The Scots Peerage IV: pp. 241-42]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Alexander Cunningham, here treated. He was alive on 14 November 1583, the date upon which he gave a feu charter for the eighteen shilling land of old extent of Rouchbank, an
2 CONC d other lands, including the five merk lands of Over and Nether Ardoch, to James Hamilton of Ardoch [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/200 RRS IV: 653] but he died before 22 June 1585, the date upon which Jam
2 CONC es VI, King of Scots, confirmed the charter he granted to John Culper of Bridgend-Wester [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/266 RRS IV: 838]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 May 1585: Licence by Alexander, commendator of Kilwinning and the convent thereof to Laurence Young. son and heir to John Young to sell the said lands (then called Blacklands) to any person or persons he should please. Dated 
2 CONC at Kilwinning. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f84%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+commendator+of+kilwinning&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotlan
2 CONC d, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/84/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 November 1586: Procuratory of resignation granted by John Lochrig for resigning the said lands in the hands of Alexander, commendator of Kilwinning and the convent thereof in favour of Thomas Essait. Dated at Irvine. [http:/
2 CONC /catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f3%2f9%2f11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+commendator+of+kilwinning&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montg
2 CONC omerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/3/9/11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 July 1592: Instrument of Seisin in favour of James Cunningham (son of late Alexander commendator of Kilwinning) (See GD39/1/121) in (the 8 merk land of Shaw) the 4 merk land of Bowieston and 5 merk land of Lambrochton, proce
2 CONC eding on a precept of clare constat by James Earl of Glencairn to the said James Cunningham as heir of Jean Cunningham his sister, daughter of Alexander commendator of Kilwinning. Witnesses to the precept, John Cunningham of Ross,
2 CONC  brother german of the Earl, Hugh Glen of Linthill and Robert Cunningham servitor to the Earl, dated at Finlayston 23 July 1592 (23 July 1592 was the last day of 25th Jas. VI. Do. 25 Jas. VI., 28 July 1592 was in 26 Jas) [http://c
2 CONC atalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f132&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=montgrenan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/132]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 October 1648: Disposition by William Cunynghame son lawful to [deceased Alexander C. of Montgrenan] commendator of Kilwining, to Jean Cunyngham daughter to deceased Mr. James C. of Monkgrennand my brother german without reve
2 CONC rsion of the 16 merkland of Powtoun. At Paisley. wit:- Robert Alexander writer in Paisley, James Alexander his son and John Whyte notary burgess of Paisley. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refer
2 CONC ence=GD138%2f1%2f299&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=montgrenan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland,Papers of the Stewart family, Earls of Galloway, reference GD138/1/299]'''  
