1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == GRIZEL CUNNINGHAM ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Grisillidi Cunynghame (1619) Dame Grizel Cunynghame (1626)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the Marquis de Ruvigny, Grizel Cunningham, here treated is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Blair-Lady-Mountgrenan/6000000181732397845?through=6000000181732967832 [https://archive.org/details/scotsp
2 CONC eeragefoun05paul/page/166/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 166]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Grizel Cunningham, here treated, married, https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Boyd-of-Bedlay/6000000109158603824?through=6000000181732967832 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/166/mode/1up The Scots Peerage
2 CONC  V: 166] They were contracted on 23 October 1603. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/boyd2.php Stirnet: Boyd 2] On 8 June 1619 she and her husband, under the guise of Sir Thomas Boyd of Bonschaw, had a charter for t
2 CONC he lands and barony of Stevenstoun in the Cunningham division of Ayrshire 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 June 1619: REX, - pro se et tanquam administrator etc.  (ut in carta 793), - cum consensu etc.  (211. 175.): - concessit D. THOME BOYDE de Bonschaw militi, et  Domine GRISILLIDI  CUNYNGHAME  ejus sponse terras  et  baroniam d
2 CONC e Stevinstoun, cum castro, molendinis, piscationibus, extenden. ad 20 librat. antiqui extentus  in proprietate, in parochia de Stevinstoun, balliatu de Cunynghame, vic.  Air ; - quas Wil. domlnus de  Kilmaris, cum  consensu Willel
2 CONC mi Cunynghame scribe donatoris sue eschaete et vitalis redditus, resignavit ; et quas  rex dictis  Tho. et Gris, de novo dedit, cum lacu de Stevinstoun ; et oniues incorporavit  in  liboram  baroniara  de Stevinstoun, ordinando  f
2 CONC ortalicium de S. alias Kerilaw principale fore messuagium: - Reseuvatis vitalibus redditibus Jacobo com. de Glencarne et Domino Agneti Hay ejus sponse: - Tenend. dictis Tho. et Gris. in  conjuncta infoodatione, et heredibus inter 
2 CONC eos legitime procreatis, quibus deficientibus, heredibus dicti Tho. et assignatis  quibuscunque, de Carolo principo: - Test. ut in aliis cartis etc.  xlix. 157.  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/738/mode/1u
2 CONC p RMS 1609-20: charter number 2034]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 June 1626: Rental of lands and barony of Stevinstoun, disponed by Sir Thomas Boyde of Benshaw with consent of Dame Grizel Cunynghame, his spouse. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference
2 CONC =RH15%2f28%2f189&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+boyde&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Cuningham of Cuninghamhead, reference RH15/28/189]'''
2 CONT
