1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===GABRIEL SEMPILL OF CRAIGBAIT (formerly GABRIEL SEMPILL OF CATHCART)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gabriel Sempill of Craigbait is the son of Gabriel Sempill of Cathcart and his wife Jonet Spreull. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft#page/533/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: p. 533-34]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 January 1550: Charter by which William Sempill of Craigbait confirms that he has sold to his brother german, Gabriel Sempill, and Gabriel's wife Margaret Lindsay, in conjunct fee and liferent, the five pound lands of old ext
2 CONC ent of Craigbait, in the parish of Kilbarchan and sheriffdom of Renfrew. The charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 25 February 1550-51. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/133/mode/1up Regis
2 CONC trum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-1580, charter number 586 on p. 133]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 January 1550:  Charter by which Gabriel Sempill of Cathcart confirms that he has sold to his brother german, William Sempill, the castle and fortalice of Cathcart, the castlelands and superiority of Cathcart, and various oth
2 CONC er lands located in the barony of Cathcart and sheriffdom of Renfrew. The charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 25 February 1550-51. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/133/mode/1up RMS: cha
2 CONC rter number 587 on p. 133]'''
