1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM SEMPILL OF CATHCART (formerly WILLIAM SEMPILL OF CRAIGBAIT)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Sempill of Cathcart is the son of Gabriel Sempill of Cathcart and his wife Jonet Spreull. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft#page/533/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: p. 533-34]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 January 1550: Charter by which William Sempill of Craigbait confirms that he has sold to his brother german, Gabriel Sempill, and Gabriel's wife Margaret Lindsay, in conjunct fee and liferent, the five pound lands of old ext
2 CONC ent of Craigbait, in the parish of Kilbarchan and sheriffdom of Renfrew. The charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 25 February 1550-51. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/133/mode/1up Regis
2 CONC trum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-1580, charter number 586 on p. 133]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 January 1550:  Charter by which Gabriel Sempill of Cathcart confirms that he has sold to his brother german, William Sempill, the castle and fortalice of Cathcart, the castlelands and superiority of Cathcart, and various oth
2 CONC er lands located in the barony of Cathcart and sheriffdom of Renfrew. The charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 25 February 1550-51. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/133/mode/1up RMS: cha
2 CONC rter number 587 on p. 133]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Books of the Town Clerks of Glasgow===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 August 1572: William Symple of Cathcart and Jonet Mungumry, his spouse, gave sasine propriis manibus to Gabriel Symple, their eldest son and apparent heir, and Margaret Spreull, his spouse, and l. l., of the 13s. 4d. land, ol
2 CONC d extent, called Brigholm of Cathcart, occupied by John Andersoun, lying in the barony and parish of Cathcart and shire of Renfrew, and that conform to the tenor of a charter. Reserving the liferent of the granters. Witnesses: Tho
2 CONC mas Spreull of Coldoun, Thomas Spreull, his son, George Allan, John Symple, son of the said William. [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsprotoc01renwgoog#page/n112/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols VI:  protocol number 1873 p. 96]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 April 1573: Gabriel Symple, son and apparent heir of William Symple of Cathcart, and Margaret Spreull,  spouses, produced a charter whereby William Symple of Cathcart granted to his son Gabriel the merk land of old extent cal
2 CONC led Palice of Cathcart, with the meadow called Kirkmedo, sometime occupied by q. Gabriel Symple of Cathcart; also the 20 s. land of old extent called the Litle Manis of Cathcart, occupied by John Thomsoun, junior; also 2 acres of 
2 CONC land occupied by John Hervy; also the 6s. 8d. land, old extent, tilled (manural) by John Hervy; also the 40d. land, old extent, occupied by John Wry; lying in the barony of Cathcart and shire of Renfrew. Charter sunscribed and sea
2 CONC led at Glasgow, 9 April 1573, in presence of Thomas Spreull of Coldoun, Thomas Spreull, his son, William Steward, son of John Steward of Bultreis, John Symple, son of the granter, and Mr. Henry Gibsoun, notary. Sasine fiven by Rob
2 CONC ert Symple (son of the Laird of Cathcart) as bailie in hac parte. Witnesses: Thomas Spreull of Coldoun, Gabriel Spreull, his son, Robert Maxuell, John Wry, John Young, and John Neilsoun. [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsprotoc
2 CONC 01robegoog#page/n14/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols VII: protocol number 1923 on pp. 2-3]'''
