2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 April 1500: Action of the King against Robert of Craufurd of Kilbirny, Marion of Creichtone, Lady of Kilbirny, Robert of Creichtone, John of Creichtone, and Sir Mungo Creichtone, chaplain, tutors testamrntar to the said Robe
2 CONC rt , to see it declated that the ward and marriage of the said Robert belong to the King by decease of Malcolm of Craufurd of Kilbirny, father of the said Robert, . . . . . [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=inu.3000004778445
2 CONC 3&view=1up&seq=563 Acta: 411]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 November 1500: Action by John, Lord Symple, against Robert of Craufurd of Kilbirny, son and heir of the deceased Malcolm of Craufurd of Kilbirny, Marion of Creichtone, Lady of Kilbirny, Robert of Creichtone, John of Creichto
2 CONC ne, and Sir Mungo Creichtone, chaplain, tutors to the said Robert Craufurd, . . . . . [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=inu.30000047784453&view=1up&seq=585 Acta: 433]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 February 1506-07: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms to Robert Craufurd in Kylbyrny possession of one half of the twenty merk land of old extent of Estir Grenok. The King's charter also confirms possession of
2 CONC  the remaining half of Estir Grenok to Robert and his wife Margrete Symple, which half is to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/654/mode/1up RMS  1424-1513: chart
2 CONC er number 3062]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=inu.30000047784453&view=1up&seq=7 Acta Dominorum Concilii. Acts of the Lords of Council in Civil Causes. Vol. II. A. D. 1496-1501. With some Acta Auditorum et Dominorum Concilii A.D. 14
2 CONC 62-1482. Edited by George Neilson, LL.D.,  and Henry Paton, M.A. (HMSO., Edinburgh, 1918), 588 pp. including index and errata]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General 
2 CONC Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), 1153 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
