2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1583: Charter under Great Seal confirming a charter (dated at Edinburgh 6th April 1585 (sic)) by Robert Grahame of Knokdoliane granting to John Grahame, his son and apparent heir and to Helen Kennedy, his future spouse
2 CONC , lawful daughter of Thomas Kennedy of Bargany and the survivor of them in conjunct fee and the heirs to be lawfully begotten betwixt them, whom failing to said John's heirs male whomsoever, in implement of a marriage contract dat
2 CONC ed [ ] in the £10 lands of Craig, £5 lands of Milanerdaill, 40 shilling lands called Ballaird and Altikaine, half merk land of Drumwachty (or Drumuauchtane), with mill and mill lands thereof, £10 lands of Auchindraine with manor p
2 CONC lace, mill and mill lands thereof, £10 lands of Ballachthrull (or Ballochtrule) and Corvar, 5 merk 10s lands of Tomlothre (or Tomlothie), Monunsioun and Balluig (or Moling), with manor, towers, fortalices, yards, orchards, tenants
2 CONC , tenandries and services of free tenants thereof all lyng in the earldom of Carrick, sheriffdom of Air. To be held a me of the King rendering therefor service ought and wont. Reserving to said Robert the liferent of Craig, Ballai
2 CONC rd, Altikane, Drumwachty, Auchindraine, Tomlothre, Monunsioun and Balluig, Ballachthoull and Corvar. With precept of sasine addressed to James McCornok. Witnesses to the confirmed charter Barnard Fergusson of Kilkerran, Simon Ferg
2 CONC usson, his son, Adam Hog and John Kennedy, servitors of Thomas Kennedy of Barganye Witnesses to the charter of Confirmamus (which contains a clause of novodamus), Colin, Earl of Argyll, Lord Campbell and Lorne, Chancellor and Jusi
2 CONC ce General, Patrick, Archbishop of St Andrews, Robert, commendator of Dunfermline, the King's secretary, Walter, commendator of Blantyre, Keeper of the Privy Seal, Alexander Hay of Eister Kennet, Clerk of the Rolls, Register and C
2 CONC ouncil, Lewis Bellenden of Auchnoule, knight, Justice Clerk, Robert Scott, Director of Chancery [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2660&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+kennedy&ko=p
2 CONC &r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/2660]'''
2 CONT
