2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 November 1592: Discharge and renunciation by Mr John Graham of Knokdoliane, lawful tutor to Robert Grahame, son liberal begotten between unquhile Robert Grahame of Knokdolian, his unquhile father and Elizabeth Sempill, his s
2 CONC pouse and as his lawful administrator in favour of Robert, Master of Eglinton (in consideration of 3200 merks Scots) of a yearly annualrent of 160lib Scots furth of the 5lib land Peacockbankis, corn milne thereof, the 4 merk land 
2 CONC of Overbordland, the lands of Quhitleyis, Galbrochhill, Auchentibbers, Littil Fulwode and Struthers all of old extent extending in whole to a 25 merk land lying in the parishes of Stewarton and Dunlop, Bailliary of Cunningham and 
2 CONC sheriffdom of Ayr and of another yearly annualrent of 36 bolls of oatmeal furth of the lands called Haning alea Lytillward, the lands called Stanyflatt and Benezaird and others and furth of the 10s land of Meirsyde, all of old ext
2 CONC ent lying in the parish and regality of Kilwinning, Bailliary of Cunningham and sheriffdom of Ayr. Dated at Irvine. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f49%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n
