2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 November 1592: Discharge and renunciation by Mr John Graham of Knokdoliane, lawful tutor to Robert Grahame, son liberal begotten between unquhile Robert Grahame of Knokdolian, his unquhile father and Elizabeth Sempill, his s
2 CONC pouse and as his lawful administrator in favour of Robert, Master of Eglinton (in consideration of 3200 merks Scots) of a yearly annualrent of 160lib Scots furth of the 5lib land Peacockbankis, corn milne thereof, the 4 merk land 
2 CONC of Overbordland, the lands of Quhitleyis, Galbrochhill, Auchentibbers, Littil Fulwode and Struthers all of old extent extending in whole to a 25 merk land lying in the parishes of Stewarton and Dunlop, Bailliary of Cunningham and 
2 CONC sheriffdom of Ayr and of another yearly annualrent of 36 bolls of oatmeal furth of the lands called Haning alea Lytillward, the lands called Stanyflatt and Benezaird and others and furth of the 10s land of Meirsyde, all of old ext
2 CONC ent lying in the parish and regality of Kilwinning, Bailliary of Cunningham and sheriffdom of Ayr. Dated at Irvine. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f49%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n
2 CONC &tn=n&tp=n&k=Elizabeth+Sempill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/49/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 April 1606: Disposition by Robert Grahme of Grougar, with consent of Margaret Montgomerie, his spouse, and William McKerrell of Hilhous, to Thomas Kennedy of Kirkhill and Agnes Kennedy, his spouse, of 50s. land of Pinbraid a
2 CONC nd Blakfardeine, part of £10 land of Craig in parish of Commonell. In dorso: note of resignation by said Robert, 31 December, 1607. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f672&st=1&tc=
2 CONC y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=grougar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/672]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 April 1606: Extract disposition by Robert Grahame of Growgar, with consent of Margaret Montgomerie, his spouse and William McKerrell of Hilhous, to David Kennedy of Corss and Janet Kennedy, his spouse, of 40s. lands of Polga
2 CONC rnokis, 20s. land of Over Preistoun, 10s. land of Quhytfardein, all part of £10 land of Craig, parish of Cammonell, and 20s. land of Mekleschallochtmuck, in parish of Girven. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/
2 CONC details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f673&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomerie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/673]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 June 1614: Discharge by Anna Graham, lawful daughter of the deceased Sir John Graham of Knockdolian having reached 21 years of age, in favour of John, Earl of Montrose as principal and Robert Graham of Gartmore as cautioner,
2 CONC  of the sum of 5000 merks which the Earl and Robert Graham had, by their bond dated at Glasgow 5 Nov 1607, obliged themselves to make forthcoming to her by Robert Graham of Grugar, now of Auchincloich, in full satisfaction of all 
2 CONC her rights through the decease of her father, Sir John or the decease of her grandfather, Robert Graham of Knockdolian, as one of their heirs portioners; discharging the said Earl and his cautioner of the said bond and the said Ro
2 CONC bert Graham of Auchincloich; at Glasgow. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f7%2f6%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+john+graham+of+knockdolian&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y N
2 CONC ational Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/A/7/6/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 June 1614: Discharge by Robert Graham of Auchincloich and Robert Graham his son with consent of his curators, in favour of John, Earl of Montrose as principal and Robert Graham of Gartmore as cautioner, of an obligation gran
2 CONC ted by them obliging them to cause Anna Graham, eldest lawful daughter of Sir John Graham of Knockdolian, upon reaching 21 years of age, to renounce (as one of the three heirs portioners of the said Sir John and Robert, his father
2 CONC ) in favour of the said Robert Graham of Auchincloich her right as heir foresaid, and granting them to have received the said renunciation from the said Anna Graham in the terms of the obligation; at Glasgow. [http://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f7%2f6%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+john+graham+of+knockdolian&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Duke
2 CONC s of Montrose, reference GD220/1/A/7/6/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 March 1617: Renunciation and discharge by Robert Graham younger of Auchinhowie with consent of his curators, in favour of John, Earl of Montrose, of the wadset right of the lands of Balmore, Sommerstoun and Malichen lying in
2 CONC  the parishes of Campsie and Kilpatrick, sheriffdoms of Stirling and Dunbarton, granted to the deceased Margaret Montgomery, mother to the said Robert, in liferent and to the said Robert himself in fee by the Earl, and set back by
2 CONC  them to the Earl by payment of the back tack duty of £1000 scots yearly, redeemable by payment of £10,000 for which Robert now grants receipt and declares the infeftment to be extinguished; at Glasgow. [http://catalogue.nrscotlan
2 CONC d.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f7%2f7%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=malichen&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD2
2 CONC 20/1/A/7/7/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 June 1617: Disposition and assignation by Robert Graham, younger of Auchincloich, eldest lawful son of Robert Graham, sometime of Grugar and now of Auchincloich and deceased Margaret Montgomery, his spouse, upon reaching the
2 CONC  age of 21 years, in favour of John Montgomery of Cocklebie, his uncle, of a wadset right for an annualrent of £1000 out of the lands of Balmore, Sommerstoun and Malichen, redeemable by payment of £10,000 after the said Robert rea
2 CONC ches the age of 22 years at two terms; to which he had right by virtue of a contract made between the said Margaret Montgomery, his mother, and the said Robert Graham of Auchincloich, his father, as administrator to him on the one
2 CONC  part and John, Earl of Montrose on the other part, dated at Edinburgh 25 Nov 1611. By which contract it is declared that John Montgomery of Cocklebie, his uncle, had in his name and on his behalf and his mother's, paid the said s
2 CONC um of £10,000 and therefore the said annualrent and sum of £10,000 was provided to the said Margaret in liferent and to him, the said Robert, in fee. This disposition and assignation is dated at Edinburgh, with a ratification at t
2 CONC he foot of it by John, Earl of Montrose, at whose instance the said Robert stood interdicted. The consent is dated at Kincardine 17 Jun 1618. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%
2 CONC 2fA%2f8%2f5%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=malichen&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/A/8/5/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 November 1617: Disposition and assignation by Robert Graham, younger of Auchincloich, eldest lawful son of Robert Graham, sometime of Grugar and now of Auchincloich and deceased Margaret Montgomery, his spouse, upon reaching
2 CONC  the age of 21 years, in favour of John Montgomery of Cocklebie, his uncle, of a wadset right for an annualrent of £1000 out of the lands of Balmore, Sommerstoun and Malichen, redeemable by payment of £10,000 after the said Robert
2 CONC  reaches the age of 22 years at two terms; at Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f8%2f5%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=malichen&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nationa
2 CONC l Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/A/8/5/3]'''
2 CONT
