2 DATE BEF 23 OCT 1652
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == WILLIAM ROSS Lord Ross ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Ross, Lord Ross, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/James-4th-Lord-Ross-of-Hawkhead/6000000000128209829?through=6000000021378202292 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Sempill/6000000002188110941?throug
2 CONC h=6000000021378202292 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/254/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 254]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Previous to his succession to the Peerage he was known as William Ross of Torphin, or as Sir William Ross of Muriston or Newriston. He was on the Committee of War for the county of Renfrew 26 August 1643 and  24 July 1644. [htt
2 CONC ps://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/257/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 257]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Ross, Lord Ross, here treated, is reported to have died in 1656. However, it would appear that this is wrong. He is certainly known to have died before 23 October 1652. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pau
2 CONC luoft/page/257/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 257] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD119%2f355&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lord+ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1648&dt=1656&di=n NRS: GD119/355]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Reords of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 July 1623: Contract between William Ross of Torphin and Thomas Whitefords, elder and younger. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f2%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+ross
2 CONC +of+torphin&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/2/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 June 1634: Discharge by Lyon King of Arms to Sir William Ross of Muirestown for his knighthood. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f7%2f129&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william
2 CONC +ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1652&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/7/129]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 March 1646: Letter from Sir William Ross of Muriston to Margaret, countess of Eglinton; the family of William Cumynge, one of her tenants, had occupied her barn while infected with plague and magistrates of Paisley are now a
2 CONC nxious to have it "cleansed". (Fraser, i, 146). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f5%2f383&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+ross+of+muriston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Re
2 CONC cords of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/5/383]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 October 1652: Discharge by George Lord Ross only son of the deceased William Lord Ross, with consent of Dame Helen Forrester his mother and his curators therein named, to Walter Lord Torphichen, of a Bond for 3000 merks Scot
2 CONC s over the lands of Torphynes in the barony of Calder. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD119%2f355&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lord+ross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1648&dt=1656&di=n National Reco
2 CONC rds of Scotland, Papers of Lord Torphichen, reference GD119/355]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
