0 @N6000000001783346875@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT 1537 Lady Janet Douglas Lyon (Lady Glamis) died - Falsely accused witch
1 CONT
1 CONT Falsely accused witch. Janet was the widow of John Lyon, the 6th Lord Glamis (c.1491 - 1528) and then married Archibald Campbell of Skipnish. However, she was also grand-daughter of Archibald Douglas, the 5th Earl of Angus (c.1449
1 CONC  - 1513), a relationship which caused her terrible demise at the hands of King James V (1512-42). In his purge of the Douglases, Janet was accused of being a witch, arrested with her new husband and imprisoned in a dark dungeon in
1 CONC  Edinburgh Castle. He escaped, but was killed in the process, while she was burned on Castlehill in Edinburgh.
1 CONT
1 CONT (http://www.geo.ed.ac.uk/scotgaz/timeline1599.html)
