0 @N6000000002187931959@ NOTE Gilbert Kennedy, 1st Lord Kennedy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Gilbert Kennedy, 1st Lord Kennedy (b. c.1406, d. after 6 March 1478/79) was a Scottish lord, the son of Sir James Kennedy the younger, of Dunure, and Lady Mary Stewart, daughter of King Robert III of Scotland.
1 CONT
1 CONT He had two children either out of wedlock or by an unnamed wife.
1 CONT
1 CONT Unnamed Kennedy 
1 CONT Elizabeth Kennedy (b. bef. 1425) 
1 CONT He married (1) Catherine Maxwell, daughter of Herbert Maxwell, 1st Lord Maxwell, circa 1440. They had two children.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children Catherine Kennedy (b. bef. 1444) 
1 CONT John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy (1454, d. bt 24 Jul 1508 - 13 May 1509) 
1 CONT He married (2) Isabel Ogilvy, daughter of Sir Walter Ogilvy of Lintrathen, after 1460.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT He held the office of Keeper of the Castle of Lochdoun.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was created 1st Lord Kennedy between 27 March 1457 and 20 March 1458.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1460 on the death of King James II, he was one of the six Regents of Scotland.
1 CONT
1 CONT He held the office of Constable of Stirling Castle in 1466.
1 CONT
1 CONT Peerage of Scotland 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT New Creation Lord Kennedy
1 CONT c.1457–c.1478 Succeeded by:
1 CONT John Kennedy 
