0 @N6000000003615880936@ NOTE Laurance (Lawrence) OLIPHANT 
1 CONT Given Name: Laurance (Lawrence)
1 CONT Surname: Oliphant
1 CONT NPFX: Sir
1 CONT Sex: M
1 CONT Birth: Abt 1439 in Aberdalgie, Gask, Perthshire, Scotland
1 CONT Death: 1499
1 CONT Change Date: 9 Jan 2002
1 CONT
1 CONT Father: John OLIPHANT b: Abt 1408 in Aberdalgie, Gask, Perthshire, Scotland
1 CONT Mother: Isabel Or Margaret OGILVY b: Abt 1420 in Auchterhouse, Angusshire, Scotland
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage 1 Isabel HAY b: Abt 1460
1 CONT Married: Abt 1472
1 CONT Change Date: 1 Jul 2003
1 CONT
1 CONT I. 1. LAURENCE OLIPHANT, of Aberdalgle, co. Perth, son and heir of Sir John OLIPHANT, of the same, by Margaret, daughter of Patrick OGILVY, of Auchterhouse, succeeded his father (slain at Arbroath) 23 January 1445/6. His wardship 
1 CONC and marriage were granted to Sir David Hay of Yester in 1450; and in 1450-51 he accompanied William, Earl of Douglas, on his journey through Flanders and France to attend the jubilee at Rome. He was created, certainly before 13 Ja
1 CONC nuary 1463/4, a Lord of Parliament as LORD OLIPHANT [SCT], under which title he sat in Parliament [SCT] 14 October 1467 and subsequently. He became Bailie of Inchaffray Abbey 25 January 1468/9, and of Elcho monastery for life 5 De
1 CONC cember 1470; a Lord of Council, 1469 to 1499, and sheriff of Perth, 1470-71. In December 1475 he was one of those appointed to implement the forfeiture of the Lord of the Isles; was a Lord Auditor, 1482; Commissioner to negotiate 
1 CONC and preserve the 3 years' truce with England, and to negotiate a marriage between James, Duke of Rothesay [SCT], and Anne, daughter of John, Duke of Suffolk, 1484; a Commissioner of Parliament to try Lord Crichton [SCT] in 1484 an
1 CONC d the Earl of Buchan [SCT] in 1488; a Lord of the Articles and a Commissioner to hold Parliament, both in October 1488; one of the King's Councillors in July 1489, and a member of the Secret Council in February 1489/90. In Novembe
1 CONC r 1489 he took part in the siege of Dunbarton Castle. He had English safe conducts on 26 February and 14 June 1491 as a member of Embassy proceeding to England, France, and Spain; and was Captain of Edinburgh Castle for 18 months 
1 CONC from 14 August 1492. He married, 1stly, before 20 May 1472, Isabel, youbgest daughter of
1 CONT William (HAY), 1st EARL OF ERROLL [SCT], by Beatrice, daughter of James (DOUGLAS), EARL OF DOUGLAS [SCT]. He married, 2ndly, Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Humphrey CUNINGHAME of Glengarnock, by whom apparently he had no issue. He die
1 CONC d between 1 February 1498/9 and 8 April 1500. His widow married, 2ndly, Sir John ELPHINSTONE of Airth. [CP 10:49-50]
