0 @N6000000002187896058@ NOTE Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell was the son of Adam Hepburn, Master of Hailes. Having been the Sherrif of Berwick, he succeeded his grandfather Sir Patrick Hepburn as Lord of Hailes (1482/1483).
1 CONT
1 CONT Hepburn took part in the rebellion against King James III, and is believed to be one of those directly responsible for the king's death. Under James IV he became Master of the King's Household, custodian of Edinburgh Castle and Sh
1 CONC erriff Principal of Edinburgh and Haddington, whilst his brother Adam was made Master of the Royal Stables.
1 CONT
1 CONT Patrick Hepburn was further appointed Great Admiral of the Kingdom on September 10, 1488, and became the Earl of Bothwell on October 17, 1488. Bothwell also acted as one of the plenipotentiaries sent to conclude the treaty for the
1 CONC  marriage of King James IV with Princess Margaret Tudor of England in October, 1501 and he stood proxy for the King at the ceremony of betrothal on January 25, 1502.
1 CONT
1 CONT Married twice, Bothwell died on October 18, 1508. His son, Adam became the next Earl of Bothwell.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT New Creation Earl of Bothwell
1 CONT 1488–1508 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Adam Hepburn
