0 @N6000000002187894165@ NOTE James Hamilton, 2nd Earl of Arran
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT James Hamilton, 2nd Earl of Arran (c. 1516–1575) was a Scottish Nobleman and the second son on James, 1st Earl of Arran.
1 CONT
1 CONT Through his mother, Hamilton was the great grandson of James II of Scotland and on the death of James V of Scotland he stood next in line to the Scottish throne after the baby Mary Queen of Scots, for whom he was appointed Regent.
1 CONT
1 CONT Initially a Protestant and a member of the pro-English party, in 1543 he was involved in negotiating the marriage of the Queen of Scots to the infant Prince Edward (the future Edward VI). Shortly after, however, he became a Cathol
1 CONC ic and joined the pro-French faction, consenting to the marriage of the Queen to the French Dauphin, later Francis II. In 1548, the Queen of Scots went to live in the French court. For his work on negotiating the marriage, Hamilto
1 CONC n was given the French title of Duc de Châtellerault.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1554, Mary of Guise, Mary Queen of Scots' mother, returned to Scotland to look after her daughter's interests there. Hamilton gave up the Regency on the condition that he would be next in line after Queen Mary, if she died chil
1 CONC dless. But Scottish succession had been secretly promised to France.
1 CONT
1 CONT Hamilton changed allegiance again in 1559, joining the Protestant 'Lords of the Congregation' to oppose the regency of Mary of Guise, and losing his French dukedom as a result. When Francis II died in 1560 Hamilton attempted, with
1 CONC out success, to arrange for his son James to marry the young widowed Queen Mary.
1 CONT
1 CONT His support swung between Mary and the 'Lords of the Congregation', depending on how he saw his advantage, but after Mary married Lord Darnley in 1565 he withdrew to his estates in France. In 1569, he returned to Scotland and was 
1 CONC imprisoned until, in 1573, he agreed to recognise Mary's infant James as the future King of Scotland.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT James Hamilton Earl of Arran
1 CONT 1529–1572 Succeeded by:
1 CONT James Hamilton
