1 CONT
1 CONT      George Douglas, 4th Earl of Angus was born before 1429.1 He was the son of William Douglas, 2nd Earl of Angus and Margaret Hay.1 He married Isabel Sibbald, daughter of Sir John Sibbald, before 1446.1 He died on 14 November 14
1 CONC 62.1 He was also reported to have died on 12 March 1462/63.2 He was buried in Abernethy, Perthshire, Scotland.1
1 CONT      George Douglas, 4th Earl of Angus succeeded to the title of 4th Earl of Angus [S., 1389] before 9 September 1446.1 He was a Commissioner to conclude a treaty with England in 1449.1 He held the office of Ambassador to England 
1 CONC in 1451.2 In 1454 he adherred to King James II during the Douglas rebellion, and was rewarded with large grants of lands of that family.1 He was a Commissioner to conclude a treaty with England in 1459.1 In 1460 he was accounted t
1 CONC he head of the party known as the 'Old Lords' during the minority of King James III.1 He fought in the Battle of Alnwick in 1462, where he obtained a victory over the English.1
1 CONT
