0 @N6000000002187894981@ NOTE Francis Stewart Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Francis Stewart Hepburn, 5th Earl of Bothwell (1563 - 1612) was a nephew of James Hepburn, the fourth Earl of Bothwell, and a grandson of James V of Scotland. He became the earl in 1587.
1 CONT
1 CONT A cousin of James VI of Scotland and I of England, it was alleged that they had a homosexual relationship with one another. At one stage he was Lord High Admiral of Scotland, but the king grew to distrust Hepburn, seeing him as a 
1 CONC potential rival (he was next in line for the throne after James).
1 CONT
1 CONT Hepburn felt that the beheading of Mary Queen of Scots should result in an invasion of England, a course of action his cousin, the king disagreed with. He was imprisoned for his activities in trying to advance such a course of act
1 CONC ion.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was accused of witchcraft and jailed for the crime in 1591. He was stripped of his land and titles for this crime. He attempted to capture Holyrood Palace in 1593 and took the king captive, making him promise to offer a pardon.
1 CONC  However, once pardoned Hepburn reverted to acting in the manner in which he previously had and in 1595 he had to flee Scotland and seek refuge in France.
1 CONT
1 CONT Hepburn died in 1612, in exile in Naples, Italy.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT James Hepburn Earl of Bothwell Followed by:
1 CONT Forfeit 
