0 @N6000000002188043087@ NOTE Archibald Campbell, 7th Earl of Argyll
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Archibald Campbell, 7th Earl of Argyll (c. 1575 – 1638), also called "Archibald the Grim", was a Scottish politician and military leader. He was the son of Colin Campbell, 6th Earl of Argyll, and converted to Roman Catholicism, al
1 CONC though in 1594 he had commanded royal troops in the Battle of Glenlivat against Catholic Rebels, especially the Gordons of Huntley. In 1619, he surrendered his estates to his son, Archibald Campbell. He was made a knight of the Go
1 CONC lden Fleece in 1624. His kinsman was William Alexander, 1st Earl of Stirling.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Reference
1 CONT Prebble, John: The Lion in the North, One Thousand years of Scotland's history, London, 1971 
1 CONT Judiciary Offices 
