1 CONT
1 CONT Schedule of Servants to Jaspar Farmar Senior as included in the inventory of his 
1 CONT Widow's Estate March, 1687.
1 CONT
1 CONT John Welsh - to serve me 4 years to commence at his arrival there, he to have at 
1 CONT ye expiration of his time a new suit of cloths with 50 acres of land according 
1 CONT to ye custom of ye country.
1 CONT
1 CONT John Billon ye same, Carigon.
1 CONT
1 CONT Daniel Berrin - ye two suits of cloths and land as the last.
1 CONT
1 CONT William Forest - for five years, at ye expiration of four, fifty acres of land 
1 CONT according to custom with a house to built on it my be and two suits of clothes 
1 CONT with 20 shillings of money,
1 CONT
1 CONT Ishmael Grube - for four years, to have land as aforesaid with five pounds in 
1 CONT money at ye expiration of the two first years.
1 CONT
1 CONT Edward Smout and his wife Elizabeth - for 4 years to have for the three last 
1 CONT years 50d a year with land according to the custom of the country with a new 
1 CONT suit of clothes.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jacob Prige - for four years to have the last three years 50d a year with land 
1 CONT according to ye custom of ye country.
1 CONT
1 CONT George Booth - is to serve for two years after his arrival in Pennsylvania 
1 CONT allowing him meat, drink, washing and lodging and cloths.
