0 @N6000000002187894746@ NOTE Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly1 (M)
1 CONT b. before 1435, #109564
1 CONT Pedigree
1 CONT Last Edited=29 May 2004
1 CONT
1 CONT      Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly was born before 1435. He was the son of Sir Alexander Seton and Elizabeth Gordon. He married, secondly, Elizabeth Crichton, daughter of Lord William Crichton.2
1 CONT       his name was legally changed to Alexander Gordon.3 He was baptised with the name of Alexander Seton.3 He gained the title of 1st Earl of Huntly.1
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Child of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly
1 CONT     Catherine Seton 1
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Children of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly and Elizabeth Crichton
1 CONT     Christian Gordon+
1 CONT     Lady Elizabeth Seton+ b. b 1451, d. 17 Apr 15001
1 CONT     George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly+ b. b 1455, d. 8 Jun 1501
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Child of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly and Egida Hay
1 CONT     Sir Alexander Gordon of Abergeldie+ b. b 1458, d. b Jan 15044
1 CONT
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Ex
1 CONC tinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 156. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
1 CONT    2. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VII, page 121.
1 CONT    3. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VI, page 675.
1 CONT    4. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 23. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
1 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
