0 @N6000000003043316863@ NOTE Notes from Sally Walmsley <Geniedash@bigpond.com>:
1 CONT In addition to Margaret [5865], also had sons Sir Bryce [d 1639] and John [who inherited from his nephew, ca 1646, and d 1662, succeeded by son William] and four other daus:
1 CONT  Isabell, m 1619 James Chalmers of Gadgirth; Anne, m 1633 Robert Boyd of Pitcon;
1 CONT  Janet, m 1636 Ninian Stewart of Ascog [see Burke's Commoners II 535]; Agnes, m 1640 William Shaw, provost of Newton.
1 CONT Bryce Blair of that Ilk was retoured heir to his father in the whole lands and barony of Blair on 10th April 1610.  By then, he was married to Annabell Wallace, of the Craigie family, whose arms were impaled with those of Blair ov
1 CONC er the main door of the house of Blair, dated 1617 (the house is a mile and a half south east of Dalry).  They had at least two sons, adn five daughters:-
1 CONT
1 CONT Sir Bryce Blair
1 CONT John Blair VIII
1 CONT Margaret Blair
1 CONT Issabell Blair
1 CONT Anne Blair was married in in 1633 to Robert Boyd of Pitcon, to continue our line
1 CONT Janet Blair
1 CONT Agnes Blair
